asurements of Ω and Λ from 42 High-Redshift\nSupernovae,\" Astrophysical Journal, Vol. 517, 1999, pp. 565-586.\n\n[54] Schwarzschild, B., \"High-redshift supernovae indicate that dark energy has been\nconstant for the past billion years,\" Physics Today, Vol. 60, 2007, pp. 21-25.\n\n[55] Riess, A. G., et al., \"New Hubble Space Telescope Discoveries of Type Ia\nSupernovae at z ≥ 1: Narrowing Constraints on the Early Behavior of Dark Energy,\"\nAstrophysical Journal, Vol. 659, 2007, pp. 98-121.\n\n[56] Astier, P., et al., \"The Supernova Legacy Survey: measurement of ΩM, ΩΛ and w\nfrom the first year data set,\" Astronomy and Astrophysics, Vol. 447, 2006, pp. 31-48.\n\n[57] Particle Data Group, \"Review of Particle Physics,\" Journal of Physics G: Nuclear and\nParticle Physics, Vol. 33, 2006, pp. 210-232.\n\n[58] Feynman, R. P., and Hibbs, A. R., Quantum Mechanics and Path Integrals,\nMcGraw-Hill Book Co., New York, 1965.\n\n[59] Feynman, R. P., Morinigo, F. B., and Wagner, W. G., Feynman Lectures on\nGravitation, edited by B. Hatfield, Addison-Wesley Publ. Co., Reading, MA, 1995.\n\n[60] Zee, A., Quantum Field Theory in a Nutshell, Princeton Univ. Press, Princeton,\n2003, Chap. VIII.1.\n\n[61] Calloni, E., et al., \"Gravitational effects on a rigid Casimir cavity,\" International\nJournal of Modern Physics A, Vol. 17, 2002, pp. 804-807.\n\n[62] Calloni, E., et al., \"Vacuum fluctuation force on a rigid Casimir cavity in a\ngravitational field,\" Physics Letters A, Vol. 297, 2002, pp. 328-333.\n\n[63] Bimonte, G., et al., \"Novel features of the energy-momentum tensor of a Casimir\napparatus in a weak gravitational field,\" Journal of Physics A: Mathematical and\nTheoretical, Vol. 41, 2008, 164056.\n\n[64] Bimonte, G., et al., \"Energy-momentum tensor for a Casimir apparatus in a weak\ngravitational field,\" Physical Review D, Vol. 74, 2006, 085011.\n\n[65] Bimonte, G., et al., \"Erratum: Energy-momentum tensor for a Casimir apparatus\nin a weak gravitational field,\