model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0e90e45ed3845bf2c696e2ebf7c0a976092688f70ef3edad12ead7ca29364345", "output_sha256": "0e90e45ed3845bf2c696e2ebf7c0a976092688f70ef3edad12ead7ca29364345", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T21:51:11.241646+00:00"}, {"id": "b869fd5353d5c853-p3", "card_id": "b869fd5353d5c853", "page": 3, "title": "DOW-UAP-D084, US Army-Flying-Saucer-Study_1949", "text": "COVER SHEET\nCOMBINED ROUTING-INFORMATION-FILING FORM\nPLANS & OPERATIONS DIVISION, GSUSA\n\n                                                    9nd15K\n\nDecimal Classification:    P&O 350.05 (24 Feb 49)                    geo\n\n                ← X 020 ID\n                ← X 360\n                ← X 471.94\n                                                    Suspense Date:\n\nSubject:  Evaluation Study of Phenomenon    Date  24 Feb 49    Origin: Executive Br, P&O ID\n(Flying Saucers)\n                                                                    ID\nDigest:\n\n\n\n\nAction:\n        Cmt #1 to D/ID\n\n\n\nReply required by:  None                        Executive        Branch\n\nTO:                                    Comments:\n  Control\n  European & Middle East\n  Far East & Pacific              Operations\n  Latin American\n  North American\n  Strategic Plans\n                                                Recommend Approval:\n  Policy                          Plans & Policy\n                                                  Branch Chief         Date__________\n                                                  Group Chief          Date__________\n                                        Concur:\n  Personnel                               Executive, P&O          File\n  Records                                 Deputy Director, AE      P/B\n  Implementing                            Deputy Director, P&O\n  Registered Documents                    Director, P&O\n  Asst Executive, P&O\n\n\nAction by Lt. Col. Peisinger\nSigned [signature]   Date  24 Feb 49             Dispatch          File\n\n                                                    CONFIDENTIAL\n25 FEB 1949                                                         AR NEAR  2\n\nNW 91369  [REDACTED]\nDocID 34748466  Page 3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "469116d8f1456d0752c21f0b67a9cb3f8612e2cd8ee0e270ae8183c6e23a51a9", "output_sha256": "469116d8f1456d0752c21f0b67a9cb3f8612e2cd8ee0e270ae8183c6e23a51a9", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T21:51:13.053746+00:00"}, {"id": "b869fd5353d5c853-p4", "card_id": "b869fd5353d5c853", "page": 4, "title": "DOW-UAP-D084, US Army-Flying-Saucer-Study_1949", "text": "Executive Br, P&O\nLt Col Peisinger/2944/eb\n24 Feb 49\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD:\n\n     1.  Conversations with the Chief of North Am Br and Office, Deputy\nDir P&O (AE) reveal that P&O has not received any evaluation of the flying\nsaucer type of phenomenon.  North Am Br feels that P&O, and themselves in\nparticular, have a direct interest in this phenomenon because, until it\nis properly evaluated, a possibility exists that this phenomenon may have\nforeign implication.\n\n     2.  Col Ligon, Intelligence Group, ID, suggests that this Division\nrequest ID to make a study on this whole subject insofar as it pertains\nto continental U.S.  ID will properly coordinate their efforts with the\nAF in this matter.\n\n     3.  ACTION:  Comment No. 1 to ID requesting evaluation study of\nphenomenon.\n\n     4.  COORDINATION:  ID - Lt Col Ligon, Ext 5509\n                        DD P&O (AE) - Lt Col Dawley, Ext 75303\n                        Exec, P&O - Col Guthrie, Ext 3465\n                        Ch, North Am Br - Col Goodell, Ext 3852\n                        PID - Lt Col Eyster, Ext 74341\n                              Ryan\n\nPID informed.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bebff801ba3bfe870a112d0e3cfd696c44af8457ffaa44db11b8c408d2242753", "output_sha256": "bebff801ba3bfe870a112d0e3cfd696c44af8457ffaa44db11b8c408d2242753", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T21:51:15.369055+00:00"}, {"id": "b869fd5353d5c853-p5", "card_id": "b869fd5353d5c853", "page": 5, "title": "DOW-UAP-D084, US Army-Flying-Saucer-Study_1949", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\nP&O 350.05 (24 Feb 49)          Evaluation Study of Phenomenon\nD/ID, GSUSA                D/P&O, GSUSA               24 Feb 49\n                                              Lt Col Peisinger/2944\n\n     1.  Reference is made to the following radios:\n\n          a.  CM IN 321, 2 Feb 49, from CO, Kirtland AFB, N. M., to Chief of Staff,\nUSAF, No. OSI-1-9C, 31 Jan 49;\n\n          b.  CM IN 1714, 8 Feb 49, from CO, AMC, Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio, to CO,\nFlight Service, No. AT-542, 7 Feb 49;\n\n          c.  CM IN 4712, 19 Feb 49, from CO, Kirtland AFB, N. M., to Chief of Staff,\nUSAF.\n\n     2.  Request that an evaluation study be made of the phenomenon referred to above\ninsofar as it concerns continental United States and that a copy of the study be\nfurnished to this Division.\n\n     FOR THE DIRECTOR OF PLANS AND OPERATIONS:\n\n\n                              /S/ B E Powell\n                         JOHN S. GUTHRIE, Colonel, GSC\n                         Executive, P&O\n\n\n\n\n\n          [ILLEGIBLE] ED 49  CO 33\n\n\n          6-8-0     CENSUS\n              DISPATCHED\n\n                                        CONFIDENTIAL\n\n                                                  COPY FOR R&O FILE\n                                                  2 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d82a89512544158e3d2e7c763fdffc9b1278c2b4341819f06ac9fc584b5c3447", "output_sha256": "d82a89512544158e3d2e7c763fdffc9b1278c