regon\n\n\n\n9. NAME OF [X] FATHER OR [ ] MALE GUARDIAN                  10. ADDRESS IF LIVING—IF DECEASED SO STATE\nNoah Frank NEWHOUSE                                         Portland, Oregon\n11. NAME OF [X] MOTHER OR [ ] FEMALE GUARDIAN               12. ADDRESS IF LIVING—IF DECEASED SO STATE\nEdith May RICHTER                                           Box 127, Garibaldi, Oregon\n\nIN THE EVENT THAT I AM NOT SURVIVED BY A SPOUSE OR ELIGIBLE CHILD I DESIRE THAT PAYMENT OF 6 MONTHS' DEATH GRATUITY BE MADE TO\nTHE RELATIVE SHOWN BELOW.  (The name of father or mother must be repeated if it is desired that he or she receive payment)\n\n13. FIRST NAME—MIDDLE NAME—LAST NAME          14. RELATIONSHIP          15. ADDRESS\n\nEdith May RICHTER                             Mother                    Box 127, Garibaldi, Oregon\n\n16. ALTERNATE RELATIVE                        17. RELATIONSHIP          18. ADDRESS\n\nDarrel Edwin NEWHOUSE                         Brother                   Rt 6, Box 756, Tacoma, Washington\n\n19. IN THE EVENT THAT I AM LISTED AS MISSING OR OTHER MILITARY CIRCUMSTANCES PREVENT ME FROM TRANSMITTING FUNDS TO MY DEPENDENTS, IT IS MY DESIRE THAT\nFIRST NAME—MIDDLE NAME—LAST NAME                                                    RELATIONSHIP\nNorma Isobel NEWHOUSE                                                               Wife\nADDRESS                                                                             RECEIVE EACH MONTH\n3581 S.E. Grant Court, Portland 15, Oregon                                          90                  PERCENT OF MY PAY\n\n20. I REQUEST THE FOLLOWING COMMERCIAL INSURANCE COMPANIES BE OFFICIALLY NOTIFIED IN CASE OF MY DEATH IN ACTIVE SERVICE\n          NAME OF COMPANY                              ADDRESS OF HOME OFFICE                              POLICY NO.\n\nPilot Life Insurance Company               Greensboro, North Carolina                                   321583\nCalifornia Western States                  Sacramento, California                                       399422\nNational Service Life Insurance            Veterans Administration, Wash., D.C.                         V-77-44-32\nGovernment Life Insurance                  Veterans Administration, Wash., D.C.                         K 948 857\n\n21. DESIGNATION OR CHANGE OF BENEFICIARY—SERVICEMEN'S INDEMNITY (PL 23, 82d Cong.)\n          (Does not operate as a designation or change of beneficiary of any insurance contracts issued by United States Government)\nALL PREVIOUS DESIGNATIONS OF PRINCIPAL AND CONTINGENT BENEFICIARIES, IF ANY, UNDER SERVICEMEN'S INDEMNITY ACT OF 1951, ARE HEREBY CANCELED, AND IT IS DIRECTED\nTHAT SAID INDEMNITY BE PAID TO:\n          NAME                                         RELATIONSHIP                    SHARE OR AMOUNT TO EACH BENEFICIARY\n\nNorma Isobel NEWHOUSE                                Wife                             100 per cent\n\n\n\n\nWITNESSED BY (Signature on all copies)                      SIGNATURE OF SERVICEMAN (Sign all copies)\nN. K. LUCAS\nG. L. LUCAS                                                 [Signature]\n\nGRADE OR RATE OF WITNESS          SERVICE NO.               DATE SIGNED\nLieutenant-USNR- R                290572                    30 March 1955\n\nDD  FORM  93                  Replaces DD Form 93, 1 Jul 50, which may be used.                         19—67492-1\n    1 FEB 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b30bbabc98969109f1b0af39cd144c86f10ff0d716185e78063b754cb55f3956", "output_sha256": "b30bbabc98969109f1b0af39cd144c86f10ff0d716185e78063b754cb55f3956", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:28:38.591099+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p12", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 12, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAV. S. AND A. FORM 913—REV.\nForm Prescribed by\nComptroller General, U.S.\nMay 17, 1945\n\nVOUCHER FOR REIMBURSEMENT\nFOR\nEXPENSES INCIDENT TO DEPENDENTS TRAVEL\nMAIL TO BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\nD. O. VOU. No. 143\nBU. VOU. No.\n\nTHE UNITED STATES, DR.\nPAID BY\n\nTO (PRINT) NEWHOUSE, Delbert C. CHIPMOT 177283\n(Last Name) (First) (Middle) (Rank or Rating) (File or Service No.)\n\nOFFICIAL ADDRESS Utility Squadron FIV\n\nNavy 943, c/o FPO, San Francisco, Calif C-1\n\nCERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENCE OF CHILDREN\n\nJUL 9 1954\n\nJ. G. HARPER\nSYMBOL 59043\n(For use of Paying Officer)\n\nAMOUNT\nDOLLARS | CENTS\n$ 109 20\n\nPAID BY CHECK No.\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\n109.20          J. G. HARPER, LT, SC, USN\n\nACCOUNTING CLASSIFICATION (For completion by Administrative Officer)\nAPPROPRIATION, LIMITATION\nOR PROJECT SYMBOL          APPROPRIATION TITLE\n\n1741453.18          029     74150\n                    22/31600\n\nFARE AUTHORIZED\nNot to exceed:\nFROM Oakland, Cal     TO Portland, Oregon\nRAIL 728 miles @15¢\nPULLMAN\nTOTAL $ PAID $109.20 CASH\n\nDelbert C. NEWHOUSE\n\nCERTIFICATION OF CLAIMANT (FILL IN ALL BLANKS BELOW WHERE APPLICABLE)\n\nPayment is requested for transportation for travel performed by the following, who were my dependents on the effective date of orders directing this change of station.\n\nNAME                    RELATIONSHIP          DATE OF BIRTH OF CHILDREN\nNorma I. NEWHOUSE       wife\nDelbert C. NEWHOUSE     son                   6/20/39\nAnne I. NEWHOUSE        daughter              9/14/40\n\n1948 Derby Street\nI certify that my dependents were located Berkeley, Calif               when orders directing detachment\n                                              (City and State)\nfrom my old permanent station were received, and departed from that place on (date) 6/12/54 and\n     3581 S.E. Grant Court\nand arrived at Portland, Oregon               on (date) 6/14/54        I further certify that my\n                (City and State)\ndependents traveled at my own expense, and that the child (children) named above is (are) the legitimate child (children) of the officer or man concerned. (IF CHILD (CHILDREN) IS (ARE) STEP OR ADOPTED, FILL IN CERTIFICATE ON REVERSE SIDE.)\n\nI certify that the travel covered by this claim represents the entire travel of all my dependents which has been or will be made on this change of station except as follows:\n\n*Reimbursement requested herein is (is not) in accordance with par. 3 of SecNav letter of 23 Dec. 1943.\n\n*I hereby designate Portland, Oregon                    as point to which transportation of dependents is desired.\nwhich will be the bona fide residence, and I certify that state with the dates shown, authorized.\nI certify that this account and schedule annexed are true and just in all respects, that payment thereof has been correctly, and that my statements of travel correctly reflect travel performed by my dependents, and at the places claimed and listed above I have actually established a bonafide residence for my dependents.\n\nSIGN\nORIGINAL \"PAYEE\"\nONLY          Delbert C. NEWHOUSE\n\nDATE                    RANK OR RATING CHIPMOT                U. S. N.\n*If applicable see Instruction 1.          16—44896-1          (Instructions on reverse side of form.)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8aff78acc9a0ee2de69dac8f2f582e3afbe6cb89bba7d0ac7df6d13e1a9458ed", "output_sha256": "8aff78acc9a0ee2de69dac8f2f582e3afbe6cb89bba7d0ac7df6d13e1a9458ed", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:28:45.772231+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p13", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 13, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. In the event this claim involves travel under secret or confidential orders, or orders from which the location of the old or new duty station is omitted for reasons of security, or under orders effecting assignment to or from sea duty or to or from a place to which dependents are not permitted to go, careful attention should be given to SecNav letter of 23 December 1944, particularly paragraphs 2, 3, 6 and 10.\n\n2. If your claim is not submitted under SecNav letter of 23 December 1944 (Instruction 1, above), the original and two certified copies of all orders involved, with all endorsements, must accompany claim.\n\n3. Claim should be prepared and forwarded to BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, Washington 25, D. C., in accordance with Article 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.\n\n4. CLAIM MUST BE SUBMITTED IN QUADRUPLICATE. The original is to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 912—Rev. and signed in ink on the face. Three copies (unsigned) to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 913—Rev.\n\n5. SECURELY STAPLE ALL PAPERS TOGETHER.\n\n6. The space below is to be used for any additional information by claimant which is necessary in settlement of this claim.\n\nI certify, except as noted hereon, that no prior claim has been presented by me or by any member of my family for the reimbursement for transportation of dependents as claimed herein and that my dependents traveled at my own personal expense as listed hereon and that no transportation in kind has been furnished with the exception of travel performed via government vessel from San Francisco, Calif to Guam, M.I.\n\nI further certify that my dependents were not authorized to travel to Guam, M.I. at the time I departed from my old permanent duty station due to the unavailability of housing. My dependents will travel [?] from the designated place to Guam, M.I. upon certification of housing by ComNavMarianas\n\nPayee's Signature\n\nCERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENCY OF CHILDREN\n(Note: To be used only for adopted or step children)\n\n_______ certify that _______ is (are) my (adopted) (step) child (children) and is (are) member(s) of my household; that said child is (children are) not possessed of property or income adequate for its (their) support and education; that it is (they are) not the beneficiary or beneficiaries, either directly or through others, of any trust or estate entitling it (them) to income adequate for its (their) support and education; that said child is (children are) in fact now and at all times solely dependent on me; that in all respects I maintain the child (children) at my own expense and from my own resources and am not reimbursed therefor directly or indirectly in any manner or form whatsoever; and that evidence of the child's (children's) dependency on me and my maintenance of it (them) has been filed with my pay accounts and is hereby made a part thereof. (See special requirements, Art. 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.)\n\nSIGNATURE\n\n☆U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE 16—44895-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f06eb4d66b5499ca400311a137055f296b933e46cd3d20cac44519962c360daf", "output_sha256": "339ec0659a39515f019380ecb514ad6e3ee825f967348913eadb9445d773a11b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:28:48.883961+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p14", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 14, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DATA SHEET TO ACCOMPANY CLAIM FOR\nREIMBURSEMENT FOR DEPENDENTS' TRAVEL\n\n(All entries to be made by the claimant in ink, in his own handwriting)\nThe following data is submitted in substantiation of my claim for reimbursement for travel performed by my dependents:\n\nMEMBER'S FULL NAME  Delbert  Clement  Newhouse  177283 CHPHOT\n              (First)    (Middle)    (LAST)    (Service No)(Rank/Rate)\n\nDUTY STATION  Utility Squadron FIVE              PHONE NUMBER 14-21282\n\nWIFE'S NAME  Norma Isobel Newhouse      Date of marriage  8/7/3606\n\nCHILDREN'S NAMES:        **RELATIONSHIP        DATE OF BIRTH\nDelbert Carroll Newhouse  Son                  6/28/3806\nAnne Lisbet Newhouse  Daughter                 3/14/4003\n_________________  ___________           ________________\n_________________  ___________           ________________\n\n** Step children or adopted children must be classified as such. Dependent parent\nmust be classified and claimed as such.\n\n\"I certify that my dependents were located at 1948 Derby St. Berkeley\n                                              Street Address,      City\nCalif.          when orders directing detachment from my old permanent station\n  State\nwere received, and departed from that place on  6/14/54          .\n                                                      Date\n** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** STRIKE OUT IF NOT APPLICABLE ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** **\nand arrived at (Point of Selection) 3581 SE Grant Court, Portland, Oregon on\n                                    Street Address,          City      State\n6/14/54 .         and departed from that place on                      .\n    Date                                                    Date\n** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** ** **\n\nand arrived at San Francisco, Calif on                   and departed there on\n                                            Date\n                   and arrived on Guam, M.I. on               Address on Guam\n     Date                                        Date\n_______________________________________________________\".\n   Complete address\n\n\"I certify that my dependents were last transported or reimbursed at Government expense for travel to  Oakland, Calif.              \".\n                                               City,          State\n\nNOTE:   This data sheet is to be presented to the disbursing officer with the original\n        and three certified copies of travel orders, with all endorsements.  The\n        \"Voucher for Reimbursement for Expenses Incident to Dependent Travel\" (NAV.\n        S. AND A. FORM 912 Rev.) will be signed when completely filled in. This\n        \"Data Sheet\" or the \"Voucher for Reimbursement for Expenses Incident to\n        Dependent Travel\" (NAV. S. AND A. FORM 912 Rev.) will not be signed in blank.\n\n        \"I further certify that all entries made above are in my own handwriting and\n        are true and correct; that I have read this completed data sheet and understand that any misrepresentation or concealment of material fact by me may\n        work a forfeiture of the claim and subject me to trial by court martial or\n        Federal District court and to penalties extending to five years imprisonment or $10,000. fine, or both\".\n\n                              D Newhouse\n                         (Signature of Claimant)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "52d44c53dc08bfa1cc78817364d675652a8626d56eda0a0913160f65d260cb7a", "output_sha256": "00e422afe4127ef468f5e57e94f91c2a87d36518b9540ac10bb24290fcf66651", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:28:52.203592+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p15", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 15, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAV. S. AND A. FORM 913-REV.\nForm Prescribed by\nComptroller General, U.S.\nMay 17, 1945\n\nVOUCHER FOR REIMBURSEMENT\nFOR\nEXPENSES INCIDENT TO DEPENDENTS TRAVEL\n\nMAIL TO BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\nD.O. VOU. No. ___ 143\nBU. VOU. No. ___\n\nPAID BY\nGUAM, M. I.\n\nTHE UNITED STATES, DR.\n\nTO (PRINT) [ILLEGIBLE] Delbert [ILLEGIBLE] G. [ILLEGIBLE] LTJG/23 [ILLEGIBLE]\n(Last Name) (First) (Middle) (Rank or Rating) (File or Service No.)\n\nOFFICIAL ADDRESS Utility Squadron Five\n\nNavy 943, c/o FPO, San Francisco, Calif.\n\nCERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENTS OF CHILDREN\n\nJUL 9 1954\n\nJ. G. HARPER\n(For use of Paying Officer)\n\nAMOUNT\nDOLLARS | CENTS\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\n109.20          J. G. HARPER, LT, SC, USN       