etachment\n                                                         (City and State)\nfrom my old permanent station were received, and departed from that place on (date)   29 September 1949\n\nand arrived at    Washington, D.C.              on (date)  30 September 1949    I further certify that my\n                     (City and State)\ndependents traveled at my own expense, and that the child (children) named above is (are) the legitimate child (children) of the officer or man\nconcerned.  (IF CHILD (CHILDREN) IS (ARE) STEP OR ADOPTED, FILL IN CERTIFICATE ON REVERSE SIDE.)\n\n     I certify that the travel covered by this claim represents the entire travel of all my dependents which has been or will be made on this\nchange of station except as follows:\n\n*Reimbursement requested herein is (is not) in accordance with par. 3 of SecNav letter of 23 Dec. 1943.\n\n*I hereby designate _______________________ as point to which transportation of dependents is desired.\n     I certify that this account and schedule annexed are true and just in all respects; that payment therefor has not been received; and that\nmy statements of travel correctly reflect travel performed by my dependents.\n\nSIGN\nORIGINAL  PAYEE    [ILLEGIBLE] Delbert C. Newhouse\n   ONLY              [ILLEGIBLE] Newhouse\n\nDATE                                    RANK OR RATING    Lieutenant                U. S. N.\n*If applicable see instruction [ILLEGIBLE]  1949         16—44896-1                (Instructions on reverse side of form.)\n\nD.O. VOU. No.  71907\nBU. VOU. No.\n\nPAID BY\n\nNO. 179\nNRAO, WASH.\n\nOCT 27 1949\n\nJ. E. LEWIS\nSYM 50-049\n(For use of Paying Officer)\n\nAMOUNT\nDOLLARS     CENTS\n$            40\n\nPAID BY CHECK No.\n[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4b7f2a0fe8f7073936440dcb3fd20b25e9a52ceb50347809482e35d6e08b325b", "output_sha256": "e420b96dbf2bbd77a0180931bc1b4b61117b496be65f256d63be6fbae2775788", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:09.091142+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p42", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 42, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF AERONAUTICS GENERAL REPRESENTATIVE, USN,\nREFER TO INITIALS          CENTRAL DISTRICT\nAND NO.          Wrig Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.\nLT/177283/1350\nRN:rn\nSerial: 9593                    27 September 1949\n\nFrom:  Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n                                                    Mileage Paid$47.68\n                                                    BuSandA(FO), Navy\nSubj:  Change of duty.                              Dept., Washington\n                                                    25, D. C.\nRef:   (a) BuPers (Pers 31B14) dispatch 261713Z of September 1949.  Oct 21, 1949\n                                                    N. L. Smith, LCDR\n1.  Reference (a) is transcribed and quoted herewith for compliance: SC, USNR\n                                                    Sym 533593, BU.VOU.\n   \"Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, 177283/1350, USN, when directed  No.    2790\n   by the Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central\n   District, you will regard yourself detached from duty in the Office\n   of the Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central\n   District, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, and from\n   such other duty as may have been assigned you; proceed to Washington,\n   D. C., and report to the Chief of the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy\n   Department, Washington, D. C. for duty. You are hereby authorized\n   to delay 15 days, provided no excess leave involved, in reporting\n   in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as leave.\n   Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station advised\n   of your address.  Qualifications: 161270; 124500.\"\n\n2.  Delivered.\n\n                              T. J. RAFTERY\n                              By direction of BAGR-CD.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nOrders received at 1330, 27 September 1949.\n\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.      Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\nLT/177283/1350\nRN:rn\nSerial: 9594                    29 September 1949\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT\n\nFrom:  Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n1.  Detached this date.\n\n                              T. J. RAFTERY\n                              By direction of BAGR-CD.\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY  D. C. Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f50c48a6b3015759943636d102176f2636b5eeb0d354a04570aade054c0c3d9", "output_sha256": "7d606c1dddf06c9a711a7d5864f9f8b69f8daac07761d413eb3055c3b88b5fda", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:12.521240+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p43", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 43, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF AERONAUTICS GENERAL REPRESENTATIVE, USN,\nREFER TO INITIALS          CENTRAL DISTRICT\nAND NO.          Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, O.\n  OO/NEWHOUSE,D.C.\n  LT/177283/1350\n  RN:rn\n  Serial:  9593                                    27 September 1949\n\nFrom:  Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.                  Mileage Paid 47.68\n                                                              BuSandA(FO), Navy\nSubj:  Change of duty.                                        Dept., Washington\n          