                    By direction of BAGR-CD.\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY  [ILLEGIBLE signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "219c7bf6de5c040ea40570ff17673d0cf224fe0e3ee9fab67cfe3ff1465022fd", "output_sha256": "afdd227baec0a95a0b1899481bb9f4bb0ad3f92e97a443d180b144448ee72b02", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:15.616015+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p44", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 44, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "US NAS, ANACOSTIA, [REDACTED]\n\n3 October 1949\nReceived for pay purposes this date.\nPay computed 9/30/49.\nPaid $200.00 NFR #71 and has been charged on man's pay record.\n\n                                          (J.W. Hillman by\n                              /s/ H. E. Nichols    H. E. Nichols, Deputy\n                                   J. W. HILLMAN LTJG SC USN\n                                   Symbol 531316\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                                                  PE-11\n                                             OO/NEWHOUSE, D.C.\n\n                                                  20 Oct 1949\n\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on BUPERS (Pers 31B14) disp 261713Z dtd Sep 1949\nFrom:  Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics\nTo:    LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubj:  Change of duty.\n\n1.   Reported this date for duty.\n\n                              /s/ J. L. Bettinger, Jr.\n\n                                   J. L. Bettinger\n                                   By Direction\n\n\n\n                    Left - Dayton, Ohio on 29 Sept. 1949\n                    Arrived - Wash., D. C. on 30 Sept. 1949\n                    Traveled via privately-owned vehicle.\n                    No Government transportation furnished.\n\n                              /s/ D. C. Newhouse\n    