D FOR USE UNDER PATENT 1,772,492       IBM 743499", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9e28104571aa7494b4fd29294cbeacf5f90eecf38c41790e7dee26f619e9439f", "output_sha256": "cdec8be1565233139c3c22276218a4b1758e04c0e95d6753c2ae8e5801a2743a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:21.177852+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p46", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 46, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/1350\n\n12 October 1949\n\n\n                                                    C-1\n\nDear Mr. Newhouse:\n\n     It is with very real personal regret that I inform\nyou of the Navy's inability to retain you on active duty in\nyour present temporary status during the fiscal year 1950.\n\n     This decision was made necessary solely because of\nunavoidable budgetary reductions in appropriations for the\nNavy, and a consequent mandatory reduction in the personnel\nceiling.  It is in no way to be construed as a reflection upon\nthe performance of your duties, and the Navy will not forget\nthat you gave unstintingly of time and effort.  I hope that you\nwill continue to serve the Navy where your support is needed\nas never before.\n\n     Your temporary appointment will be terminated on 31 December\n1949.  If you are eligible for retirement, and so desire, you\nshould submit your request to reach the Bureau at the earliest\npracticable date but not later than 10 November 1949.  If you do\nnot retire you may expect to be reassigned to another billet\nupon reversion.\n\n     Please be assured of the Navy's deep appreciation of your\nloyal and honorable service.\n\n                         Sincerely,\n\n\n                         J. W. ROPER\n\n\n                                        Finished File Pers-31B11\n\nLT Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\nBureau of Aeronautics\nDepartment of the Navy\nWashington 25, D.C.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c3bbccb4be50a9e6560423db579367aa2382f09734ba253aaa6fbe7a476d9304", "output_sha256": "c3bbccb4be50a9e6560423db579367aa2382f09734ba253aaa6fbe7a476d9304", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:22.843439+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p47", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 47, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                          IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                          Pers 362-mhl\n                                          177283\n\n16 MAY 19[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nFrom:    The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:      LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350.\n\nVia:     Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,\n         Central District,\n         Wright Field,\n         Dayton, Ohio.\n\nSubj:    Application for transfer to commissioned limited duty status;\n         action on.\n\nRefs:    (a) Your application for transfer to commissioned limited\n             duty status.\n         (b) BuPers Circular Letter 175-48.\n\n1. Your application for transfer to commissioned limited duty status\nhas been carefully considered by the Selection Board convened in April\n1949 by the Secretary of the Navy. I regret to inform you that your\nname was not included among those recommended for appointment. However,\nI wish to assure you that this decision is no reflection upon your performance of duty in the Navy; nor will it in any way affect your present\nstatus.\n\n2. The number of applicants desiring transfer to commissioned limited\nduty status has been far in excess of the number of appointments which\ncan be offered. Therefore, it was necessary for the Selection Board\nto recommend, from among eligible applicants, only those best qualified\nfor appointment. The decision in your case was made after a careful\nreview of your entire record and your qualifications as compared with\nthose of other applicants of your rank and classification or enlisted\nrating.\n\n3. The interest you have shown in pursuing a naval career represents\nan exemplary attitude of service and patriotism. The Navy is sincerely\nappreciative of your contribution toward maintaining the naval establishment at a high level of efficiency during the war, the demobilization period, and the continuing period of world unrest.\n\n\n                              T. L. SPRAGUE\n\n\n                                                    B-12060\n                              FINISHED FILE PERS [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d2c5e190c5dcb5a4b34129d29e9deaf535112c9f63cd549f62dc630049f2b26b", "output_sha256": "ab3e9f1d5ffb01cb08b4b45e707f4e249e609ae3b7bde096d007d3355e173d58", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:24.946135+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p48", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 48, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAV. S. AND A. FORM 913—REV.          VOUCHER FOR REIMBURSEMENT                    363[ILLEGIBLE]\nForm Prescribed by                              FOR\nComptroller General, U. S.      EXPENSES INCIDENT TO DEPENDENTS TRAVEL         D. O. VOU. No.— [ILLEGIBLE]  3325\nMay 17, 1945\n                                    TO BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, WASHINGTON 25, D. C.        BU. VOU. No.—\n\nTHE UNITED STATES, DR.                                                                        PAID BY\n                                                                                        J. A. REBENTISCH\nTO (PRINT)  NEWHOUSE,  Delbert   C.    Lt. USN    177263                               Symbol 540415\n           (Last Name)      (First)   (Middle)   (Rank or Rating)    (File or Service No.)   NCDO Great Lakes\n\nOFFICIAL ADDRESS  Office of Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,\n\n                  Central District, Wright Field, Dayton, Ohio\n\n                  CERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENTS OR CHILDREN                                  SEP 15 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                                                                                         J. SCOTT\n                                                                                (For use of Paying Officer)\n                                                                                         AMOUNT\n                                                                                  DOLLARS        CENTS\n\n                        MEMORANDUM\n\n                                                                               $            202 08\n202.08          J. SCOTT, Officer in Charge 52-527 PAID BY CHECK No.\n                                                                                          526944\n                By Alice C. Gibbons, Agent Cashier\n\nACCOUNTING CLASSIFICATION (For completion by Administrative Officer)              FARE AUTHORIZED\n APPROPRIATION, LIMITATION                                                FROM              TO\n    OR PROJECT SYMBOL          APPROPRIATION TITLE\n                                                                  RAIL\n  1790813         TRNP-1949   020    74130                        PULLMAN\n                                                                  TOTAL    $\n\n                    CERTIFICATION OF CLAIMANT (FILL IN ALL BLANKS BELOW WHERE APPLICABLE)\n    Payment is requested for transportation for travel performed by the following, who were my dependents on the effective date of orders\ndirecting this change of station.\n\n          NAME                                          RELATIONSHIP              DATE OF BIRTH OF CHILDREN\n\n  Norma Isabel Newhouse                                    Wife\n  Delbert Carroll Newhouse                                 Son                       6/26/38\n  Anna Lisbet Newhouse                                     Daughter                  3/14/40\n\n                                         at 412 Third St., NHA #1,\nI certify that my dependents were located _____ Honolulu 50, T.I. _________________ when orders directing detachment\n                                                    (City and State)\n\nfrom my old permanent station were received, and departed from that place on (date)  1 July 1948; Arrived Alameda\nCalifornia 16 July 1948; Departed Alameda, California 16 July 1948\nand arrived at  Dayton, Ohio              on (date)  24 August 1948.    I further certify that my\n                  (City and State)\ndependents traveled at my own expense from Alameda, California to Dayton, Ohio and that the child (children) named above is (are) the legitimate child (children) of the officer or man\nconcerned. (IF CHILD (CHILDREN) IS (ARE) STEP OR ADOPTED, FILL IN CERTIFICATE ON REVERSE SIDE.)\n\n   I certify that the travel covered by this claim represents the entire travel of all my dependents which has been or will be made on this\nchange of station except as follows:  No exceptions\n\n   *Reimbursement requested herein is (is not) in accordance with par. 13 of SecNav letter of 23 Dec. 1943.\n\n   *I hereby designate _________________________________ as point to which transportation of dependents is desired.\n   I certify that this account and schedule annexed are true and just in all respects; that payment therefor has not been received; and that\nmy statements of travel correctly reflect travel performed by my dependents.\n\nSIGN\nORIGINAL (PAYEE\nONLY                            Delbert C. Newhouse,\n\nDATE  1 Sept. 1948             RANK OR RATING  Lieutenant                    U. S. N.\n   *If applicable see Instruction 1.          10—44896-1                    (Instructions on reverse side of form.)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5b75f3efc39a283ccc7160a7c4c7ac0842efd100fe287e8e84809700a2d88367", "output_sha256": "6f0f729cb683b288553b26baae2e2fe4a4983a7bfb6a2b957df4115778c93a1e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:29.420949+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p49", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 49, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. In the event this claim involves travel under secret or confidential orders, or orders from which the location of the old or new duty station is omitted for reasons of security, or under orders effecting assignment to or from sea duty or to or from a place to which dependents are not permitted to go, careful attention should be given to SecNav letter of 23 December 1944, particularly paragraphs 2, 3, 6 and 10.\n\n2. If your claim is not submitted under SecNav letter of 23 December 1944 (Instruction 1, above), the original and two certified copies of all orders involved, with all endorsements, must accompany claim.\n\n3. Claim should be prepared and forwarded to BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, Washington 25, D. C., in accordance with Article 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.\n\n4. CLAIM MUST BE SUBMITTED IN QUADRUPLICATE. The original is to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 912—Rev. and signed in ink on the face. Three copies (unsigned) to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 913—Rev.\n\n5. SECURELY STAPLE ALL PAPERS TOGETHER.\n\n6. The space below is to be used for any additional information by claimant which is necessary in settlement of this claim.\n\nI certify except as noted hereon that no prior claim has been presented by me or by any member of my family for the reimbursement for the transportation of dependents as claimed herein and that no transportation in kind has been furnished therefor.\n\n                                        Delbert G. Newhouse,\n                                        Lt. USN.\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nCERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENCY OF CHILDREN\n(Note: To be used only for adopted or step children)\n\nI, _________________ certify that _________________ is (are) my (adopted) (step) child (children) and is (are) member(s) of my household; that said child is (children are) not possessed of property or income adequate for its (their) support and education; that it is (they are) not the beneficiary or beneficiaries, either directly or through others, of any trust or estate entitling it (them) to income adequate for its (their) support and education; that said child is (children are) in fact now and at all times solely dependent on me; that in all respects I maintain the child (children) at my own expense and from my own resources and am not reimbursed therefor directly or indirectly in any manner or form whatsoever; and that evidence of the child's (children's) dependency on me and my maintenance of (them) has been filed with my pay accounts and is hereby made a part thereof. (See special requirements, Art. 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.)\n\nSIGNATURE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "29b4d4fb692ff8006af8d8e8fe5dcb713e82b8998316fdcf9b5703ed414c4278", "output_sha256": "4ce4895d6777b3d948b934da5c11c26aa5887f6fc18d9683a45db00b53f5e787", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:32.118904+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p50", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 50, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "PERS 82-15\nREPORT OF BENEFICIARIES\nNAVPERS-601 (1-45)\n\n[X] OFFICER  [ ] ENLISTED          1 May 1948.\n                                        (Date)\n\n          NEWHOUSE              Delbert  Clement\n           (Last name)            (First)    (Middle)\n\n0177283                    LT              USN\n(File or service number)    (Rank or rate and classification)\n\nU. S. COMMANDER UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n                    (Ship or station STAFF ALLOWANCE).\n\nTo carry out the provisions of the acts approved 4 June 1920, 22 May\n1928, 12 May 1930, and 17 March 1941, and acts amendatory thereof\ndirecting the payment of 6 months' pay to the widow, children, or dependent\nrelative of any of the personnel on the active list of the Regular Navy, or\non the retired list when on active duty, or of any of the personnel of the\nNaval Reserve called or ordered into active naval service by the Federal\nGovernment for extended naval service in excess of 30 days, who dies\nof wounds or disease not the result of his or her own misconduct, I give\nbelow the name and address of my wife or husband and that of each of my\nchildren:\n\nMrs. Norma Isabel NEWHOUSE\n        (Full name of wife or husband ; if not married, so state)\n\n412 - 3rd St., NHA #1, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n                    (Address of wife or husband)\n\nDelbert Carroll NEWHOUSE                6-28-38\n    (Full name of child ; if none, so state)          (Date of birth)\nSame as above.\n                    (Address of child)\n\nAnne Lisbet NEWHOUSE                    3-14-40\n        (Full name of child)                    (Date of birth)\nSame as above.\n                    (Address of child)\n\n                                         (Date of birth)\n        (Full name of child)\n\n                    (Address of child)\n\nIn the event that I am not survived by a wife (or husband) or child, or\nin the event of their decease prior to payment and collection of the gratuity,\nI then designate the following person as my dependent beneficiary under\nthe act:*\n\nMrs. Vencl RICHTER\n              (Name in full)\n\nGen. Del. Gariboldi, Oregon.\n                  (Address)\n\nMother.\n              (Relationship)\n\nIn the event of the death of the above-named beneficiary before payment\nand collection of the gratuity, I then designate the following person as my\ndependent beneficiary under the act:*\n\n              (Name in full)\n\n                  (Address)\n\n              (Relationship)\n\n* The acts state that death gratuity must be paid to the surviving wife (or\nhusband) or children, if any. In the event of leaving no wife or children,\nit may then be paid to a designated dependent beneficiary. Every member\nof the service, whether married or not, should designate a beneficiary\n(and an alternate, in case of prior death of the primary beneficiary). Failure\nto make such designation may result in nonpayment of the gratuity.\nSuch designation does not affect payment to a surviving wife (or husband)\nor children.                                                      06-16—43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "88556907af0ba4a7fdd81ad248b582846a152f044e05c1132b1394749babe234", "output_sha256": "88556907af0ba4a7fdd81ad248b582846a152f044e05c1132b1394749babe234", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:35.243143+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p51", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 51, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "8\n\n I CERTIFY that I will inform the Bureau of Naval Personnel via my\ncommanding office, immediately of any changes in marital status, or con-\nditions of dependency, or of voluntary occupancy of public quarters by my\ndependents.\n\n I CERTIFY that there has been no change in condition of dependency\nbetween      1 May 1947                    and current date.\n             (Date of last report of beneficiaries)\n\n I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that the facts stated and disclosed in the\nforegoing are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n  Delbert C. Newhouse\n                    (Signature)\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this        1st\n\nday of        May              , 1948, I having authority\nto administer oaths\n              J. C. CRONIN                    CAPT.   M\n              (Signature)                     (Rank)\n\n\n                        INSTRUCTIONS\n\n   This form must be sworn to before an officer of the\nUnited States Navy authorized to administer oaths, or\nbefore a notary public.\n\n   The full names and addresses of the beneficiaries must\nbe stated carefully.  If a married woman, her own given\nname should be stated; thus: \"Mrs. Anna May Smith,\" not\n\"Mrs. John Smith.\"\n\n   This slip shall be made out and handled as follows:\n   Officer, Navy: Forward to Bureau of Naval Personnel.\n   Nurse: Forward to Bureau of Medicine and Surgery.\n\n   Enlisted men, Navy: In duplicate; one copy to Bureau\nof Naval Personnel, one copy secured inside service rec-\nord.  In cases of men entitled to money allowances for\nquarters for enlisted men with dependents, two additional\ncopies, bearing the required certificate, to the Disbursing\nOfficer.\n\n   New beneficiary slips shall be executed and forwarded\nas above in all cases of change in status of the grantor or\nin that of his or her beneficiaries.\n\n   In any event, payment will be made to the widow or\nchildren, if any, whether designated or not.\n\n   Normally casualty notification will be sent to all the\nbeneficiaries designated on this form.  If, by reason of\nunusual circumstances, other special arrangements are\ndesired, a statement should be attached setting forth\nfull instructions including full names, addresses, and\nrelationships.\n\n\n                         C6-16—43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d7329ff398d3f2068c608fda846a5eb7ecf715b68f6d7a83ac11047005ea7392", "output_sha256": "d53a3965f0e1a2b6ab735aa0af45a01c768f1d92d9dacf7f6b12cdac5fa61ccc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:39.302976+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p52", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 52, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Navy Department\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nWashington 25, D.C.\n\nPers 3216A  gm\nFile No: 177283\n\n23DEC1946          24DEC1946\n\nTo:          Lt. Delbert Clement Newhouse\n             Aviation Supply Depot\n             Pearl Harbor, Territory of Hawaii\n\nVia:\n\nSubject:     Claim for Settlement of Unused Leave, Return of.\n\nRef:         (a) Bupers-BuSandA Joint Letter, claims for unused leave.\n\n     1.      Your Claim for Settlement of Unused Leave is returned here-\nwith for the reason indicated below. After correction of the error\nindicated all papers should be returned to this Bureau for further action.\n\n     2.      Payment cannot be made on your claim as submitted for the\nfollowing reason:\n\n          Date of present continuous active duty apparently\n     incorrect. Check and resubmit claim.\n\n\n\n\n     3.      You are advised that your claim must be resubmitted prior\nto 1 September 1947, in order that payment may be made under the Armed\nForces Leave Act of 1946.\n\nBy Direction of the Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n\n                                        C.F. NELSON,\n                                        LT. (jg), USN,\n\n                                        Officer Performance Division.\n\n          Finished File Pers 3216A\n\n\n                                                              4647", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1813003838d834736e0eb872321119015bd06d56d4aec8f8533834c18d9bcc57", "output_sha256": "d4760edf79a2500e28e59324278f0efe3ac104ad9c04821865a20db80213f88f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:40.824186+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p53", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 53, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Finished File Pars 81512\n\nOO/Newhouse, D. C.\n(177283)mv\n\n29 November 1946.\n\nFrom:    Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo  :    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, U. S. Navy.\nVia :    Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\n         Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubj:    Orders - Additional duty.\n\nRef      (a) ComNavBase orders dated 25 September 1946.\n\n     1.  The additional duty assigned by reference (a) is\nhereby cancelled.  Continue present duty.\n\n\n\n                              E. W. HANSON\ncc:BuPers                                    Finished File Pars 81512\n    ComServPac(2)\n    Com 14\n    CO, RecSta, Pearl\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nEnd-1              NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR T. H.\n\n11 December 1946\n\nFrom:         Supply Officer in Command\nTo  :         LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, LINE, USN\n                                             Finished File Pars 81512\n     1.   Delivered\n\n\n\n                              E. E. BRIGHTON\n\n         Finished File Pars [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n         Finished File Pars 81512               Finished File Pars 81512", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6846e830e9b33ba5dbf835421d121f8136cef3b4e11781342c375ba05edbbdf5", "output_sha256": "6eaa18d3568f230dbbf39d741b834df6f99ca8be3d2140aa3777adb2a41d10c9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:42.596219+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p54", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 54, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "17 7283\n\n      In Reply Address\n      Comdr. FAW-3\n      Refer File No.\n\n                              AIR FORCE ATLANTIC FLEET\n                              FLEET AIR WING THREE\n\n      FAW3/P15\n      Serial 1622                              c/o Fleet Post Office,\n                                                New York, N.Y.,\n                                                29 October 1943.\n\n\n\nFrom:          The Commander Fleet Air Wing THREE.\nTo:            Ensign D. C. NEWHOUSE, Assistant Photographic\n               Officer, Naval Air Station, Coco Solo, C.Z.\nVia:           The Commanding Officer, Naval Air Station,\n               Coco Solo, C.Z.\n\nSubject:       Air Crew Insignia.\n\nReference:     BuPers C/L No. 173-43.\n\n          1.       Authority is hereby granted you to wear the Air\nCrew Insignia without stars.\n\n          2.       The records indicate that you served more than\nthree months as a regularly assigned member of the crews of\ncombatant aircraft while serving under my command at the\nNaval Air Station, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba during the first half\nof the year 1942.\n\n          3.       This letter shall be presented to a Ships' Service\nstore selling this insignia as your authority to purchase same.\n\n\n                                        G. E. Compo\n                                   G. L. COMPO.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEND-1  30 October 1943  NA10/P15\nTo:  Ensign D. C. Newhouse, Assistant Photographic Officer\n\n  1.  Delivered.\n\n                              R. P. Kauffman\n\n                         R. P. KAUFFMAN\n                         Commander, USN\n                         Commanding\n\nFINISHED FILE PERS 56", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "696b9ab6f26b8a67b378861f7482ac915b0b7a76f4e2748791b0f1261395698d", "output_sha256": "696b9ab6f26b8a67b378861f7482ac915b0b7a76f4e2748791b0f1261395698d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:44.596420+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p55", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 55, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CORRECTION SLIP\nNAVPERS-1668 (10-43)                              To   Tabulated Records Section\n                                                       Records Division\n                                                       Pers. 82233\n\nNAME                                                  FILE NO.\n   Newhouse, O.        C.                              177283\n\nITEM          SHOWN AS           SHOULD BE            PER ORDERS/ROSTER DATED\n\nPERMANENT\nDUTY\nSTATION        7460              NAS\n(Do not show                     Coco Solo             11-1-43\nTemporary or\nAdditional Duty\nStations)\n\nRANK           W.O.              6\n\nCORPS          Phot              2-    Interpreted . . . . . . . . .\n                                       File No.   . . . . . . . . .\n                                       Coded      . . . . . . . . .\nSIGNED         [ILLEGIBLE]  FINI  Punched L.E. REC[ILLEGIBLE].\n                    Status Officer Verified  . . . . . . . . . .\nSIGNED         Pers 315 [ILLEGIBLE]  Checked  . . . . . . . . .\n                    Detail Officer\n\n[Stamp: FINISHED FILE PERS 82233]\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n1. This form is to be used to indicate any changes which should be made in the roster\nof officer personnel.\n2. Information shown on this form will not be checked and the form should not be originated unless the information shown above under \"should be\" can be fully substantiated.\n3. This form should not be used to request replacement of missing or broken lineindex strips.\n\n                    DEC 4  1943\n\n47", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3c651c68ad0f5fa08639bc9295b4cefd52f14280aa84617c89fa7d879d56c863", "output_sha256": "fa77d1816d09bcc68d5d8a458db062eb9cf807cffbae38cac4b4914a04581adb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:46.405393+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p56", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 56, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283                                                    134 019\n\nWf\n\n                        NAVY DEPARTMENT\n                   BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                        WASHINGTON, D.C.\n\n         Pers-326 -FKB                              March 18, 1943\n\n\nMemorandum for Records and Statistics Division, Manual Files Section\n\n        It is requested that the Performance Division (Officer Personnel)\nbe furnished statement of service for the following enlisted man appointed to officer rank:\n\n                      NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n\n        Full name  NEWHOUSE, Delbert C.-To Photographer - 393-07-21\n        Date of birth JUNE 5, 1913\n        Place of birth Marcola, Oregon                    B\n        Home address (City and State)\n        Garibaldi, Oregon\n        Name and address of beneficiary (show date slip submitted)\n        Wife, Norma Isobel Newhouse, 1210-S.E., 37th Ave., Portland, Ore.(1-15-42)\n        Name and address of next of kin (if different)\n        Same\n        Fleet Reserve? No\n        Enlisted rating    CP(PA)\n        Date of last enlisted rating  8-1-1942.\n        Dates of enlistment, reenlistment, extension of enlistment, and\n      . discharge; time lost for any reason;  and Army or other service\n        which may be counted for pay or retirement.\n\n\nPers. 2332-1-mah                                      March 20, 1943.\n\nENLISTED                              DISCHARGED\n3-18-29 (National Guard)(Active)      1-25-1932\n1-24-1933\nExt.Enl.2 yrs.\n1-24-1937                             1-23-1939\n\n1-24-1939\n\n31  13\n32 - 1 - 25\n29 - 3 - 18    No Unauthorized Absences,\n2 - 10 - 18                         F.A. Van Slyke          appt Photg 9-1-42\n              8 31\n            42-8-4\n            33-1-24\n             9-7-7\n             1-10-8\n             12 5-15\n\n                            F. A. Van Slyke\n\n                                          42-8-31\n                                          42-8-4\n                                          12-5-15  T 2 S\n                                          30 13-16  P & D.\n\n                                                     FINISHED FILE PERS 323", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b67d8bcf8a3919a659fbd959746a2eedc90146f08145caf57d53eb6edb50b4c2", "output_sha256": "cf6a9e047e643aa852a44f52ae5b43827b90938e9410c57b91aa8d4b6115ba59", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:49.034195+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p57", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 57, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283 NG\n\n                                              FINISHED FILE PERS 3180\n\n25 September 1946\n\nFrom:          Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo :           Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, 0177283\n               Ensign Oley (n) Ratsep, SCS, USNR, 483558\n\nVia :          SOinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubj:          Orders - Additional duty.\n\n     1.     When directed by Supply Officer in Command, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., on 26 September 1946 you will\nreport immediately to the Commanding Officer, Enlisted Personnel,\nU. S. Naval Receiving Station, Pearl Harbor, T. H., for additional\nduty on a summary Court Martial Board.\n\n     2.          This is in addition to your regular duty.\n\n\n\n\n                              E. W. HANSON\n\ncc:\nBuPers(Clipper)\nComServPac(2)\nCom14\nCO,RecSta,Pearl\n\n                    NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR\n\n                    End  1     SEP 26 1946\n\n                    From:  Supply Officer in Command\n\n                    1.   Forwarded.    E. E. BRIGHTON\n                                       BY DIRECTION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "35bb20716e8acda840a7444b957cc5621ae45f209d340f84ef02e700a26d7325", "output_sha256": "8a391015ef91b53db4d3f69f75891e5e42f5b5e3110ad707d49123782caddf95", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:50.665443+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p58", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 58, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAV. S. AND A. FORM 550          MUSTERING OUT PAYMENT\n\n177283          NEWHOUSE          Delbert          C          LP LINE USN\n(File or service No.)          (Surname)          (First name)          (Initial)          (Rank or rating and branch of service)\n\n24 Sept. 46     Aviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor          60 Days or More\n(Date discharged or released from          (Activity from which discharged)          (Length of service—Enter (less than 60\n   active duty)                                                                              days) or (60 days or more))\n\nDoes service record show service outside of continental limits of United States or in Alaska? Enter Yes or No......... Yes\n\nCOMMANDING OFFICER'S CERTIFICATE:     Discharged for convenience of Government to\n                                        accept permanent appointment in U. S. Navy.\nI certify that the above-named person is being discharged\nor released from active duty, that such person is entitled to          K. A. GRAHN, SGInC\npayment under the MUSTERING OUT PAYMENT ACT OF          (Name and signature of officer authorized to sign in accordance\n1944, and that the above information is correct.                               with article 2025(2)NR)\n\nVETERAN'S CERTIFICATE:\n  I hereby certify that I have not made previous application          ADDRESS TO WHICH CHECK(S) ARE TO BE SENT:\nfor mustering-out payment under the MOP Act of 1944. I am               (Omit address if service is LESS than 60 days)\naware of the fact that making application more than once is a\ncriminal offense under the United States Criminal Code.                    PAID IN FULL\n\nHave you served outside the continental          Yes               Aviation Supply Depot\nlimits of United States or in Alaska?     (Enter Yes or No)     (Number)               (Street)\n\n[Signature of applicant: Delbert C. Newhouse]                         Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n(Signature of applicant)                                    (City)          (Zone)          (State)\n\n          DISBURSING OFFICER'S PAYMENT DATA          |     MUSTERING OUT PAYMENT DIVISION DATA\nLUMP SUM MOP $300.00\nPaid [ILLEGIBLE] on [ILLEGIBLE]     5,112          9/26/46\n                  (Public voucher)     (Check number)          (Date)\n\n                    D. P. SULLIVAN - 984673\n          (Type name and symbol No. of disbursing officer making initial payment)\n\n                              XXXXXXX TRIPLICATE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a35e0fbf6457783869013880b36bd184e048c4ff8a6690d2cc4413411aa9049f", "output_sha256": "a35e0fbf6457783869013880b36bd184e048c4ff8a6690d2cc4413411aa9049f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:53.265159+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p59", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 59, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "22 March 1956\n\nC-2\n\nFrom: CWO Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\nTo:   Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:  Commanding Officer, Naval Air Technical Training Unit, Naval Air\n      Station, Pensacola, Florida\n\nSubj: Orders; forwarding of\n\nRef:  (a) BuPers Manual Art C-5407(4)\n\nEncl: (1) One copy of basic orders with all endorsements thereto\n\n1.  In compliance with reference (a), enclosure (1) is forwarded herewith.\n\n\n                        DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE [signature]\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nNC/Pcola/(mag)\nP16-4/00                              2 2 MAR 1956\n[REDACTED]\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on CWO Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, ltr of 22 Mar 1956\n\nFrom: Commanding Officer, Naval Air Technical Training Unit, Naval Air\n      Station, Pensacola, Florida\nTo:   Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n                              H. M. GARVEY\nCopy to:                      By direction\nCNATECHTRA\n\n\nFinished File—Pers P11a.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "910b6097855516b00f5abed0eda49294b73ef20d51fde0792d0f5791e18d55e7", "output_sha256": "e4287119c520b961ecb283370846a13c1301ad16984f2c251e26d69f9155883a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:55.124984+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p60", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 60, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NC/Pncla/(mag)\nP16-4/00\n177283/8311\n\n                              21 March 1956\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on CO, VU-5 Orders ser 121 of 23 Jan 1956\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer; Naval Air Technical Training Unit, Naval Air\n       Station, Pensacola, Florida\nTo:    CWO4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\n1.  Reported for duty this date.\n\n\n                                   F. M. HALL\n                                   By direction\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEnclosure (1)\n\n\n                                        Finished File--Pers P1186", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "06bf54d4b0c9f49e790d653158b30e4bc1805ab589832fafe48a9fe21d01b445", "output_sha256": "06bf54d4b0c9f49e790d653158b30e4bc1805ab589832fafe48a9fe21d01b445", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:56.115856+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p61", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 61, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "VU-5/ACW:rbd\nP16-4/00\nSer: 185\n10 February 1956\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on CO, VU-5 Orders ser 121 of 23 January 1956\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron FIVE\nTo:    CWO4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\n1.  Detached this date.\n\n\n                              B. F. ROWE\n\nCopy to:\nCOMSIX\nCNATRA\nCNATECHTRA\nCOMSERVPAC\nCOMUTWINGPAC\nNATECHTRAU NAS PNCLA\nCOMAIRPAC\n\n\n\n\n                              CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n\n\n\n\n                                             Finished File--Pers File", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7410e2637086727b414e8ac133a38c1e9c2a17100a8d4291bdadc6f8d48dd0f9", "output_sha256": "7b1ac4bad4dbec862d367504a69eb0d7977c03c6d53d93a8b99959cf0035226e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:30:57.336026+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p62", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 62, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET          VU-5/ACW:kf\n          AIR FORCE                    P16-4/00\n     UTILITY SQUADRON FIVE             Ser:  121\n                                       23 January 1956\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron FIVE\nTo:    CWO4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\nRef:   (a) BUPERS msg 191325Z of January 1956\n\n1.  Reference (a) is quoted below for your information and compliance:\n\n     \"CWO W3 DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/8311 DIR DET ABT 15 FEB PROUS\n     ARPROREP NATECHTRAU NAS PNCLA DUTY X DELREPARUS THIRTY DAYS X\n     GOVTRANSDIRVAIL TWO COMLTRANS AUTH OUTUS WHERE GOVTRANS NOT AVAL X\n     TRAVCHAR 1761453.18 MPN 1956 OC 029 EXACCT 74120 BUCONTROL 22/31600\"\n\n2.  In accordance with reference (a), when directed by the Commanding Officer,\nUtility Squadron FIVE, about 15 February 1956, you will regard yourself detached\nfrom duty with Utility Squadron FIVE and from such other duty as may have been\nassigned.  You will proceed to a port in the United States and upon arrival\nfurther proceed and report to the Commanding Officer, U. S. Naval Air Technical\nTraining Unit, Naval Air Station, Pensacola, Florida for duty.\n\n3.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of thirty (30) days, provided\nno excess leave involved, in reporting in compliance with these orders, such\ndelay to count as leave, any portion of which may be taken prior to or after\narrival in the United States.\n\n4.  Travel via government transportation is directed outside the United States\nwhere available.  Class TWO priority is certified for travel via government air-\ncraft.  Commercial transportation authorized outside of the United States where\ngovernment transportation is not available.\n\n5.  Cost of this travel is chargeable to appropriation 1761453.18 MPN 1956,\nobject class 029, expenditure account 74120, Bureau Control 22/31600.\n\n6.  Immediately upon reporting, copies of these orders shall be forwarded to\nthe Chief of Naval Personnel in accordance with Art. C-5407(4), Bureau of\nNaval Personnel Manual.\n\n7.  You are hereby authorized to draw three (3) months advance pay.\n\n8.  Delivered.\n\n\n                              B. F. ROWE\n\nCopy to:\nCOMSIX/CNATRA/CNATECHTRA/COMSERVPAC/          CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY:\nCOMUTWINGPAC/NATECHTRAU NAS PNCLA/COMAIRPAC\n\n                                               Finished File--Pers Titol", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "efc533bc16a0a87fb07ca61fe0dbba7883ae6bdc9c1d994bf15d7e5ded2a3cb5", "output_sha256": "efc533bc16a0a87fb07ca61fe0dbba7883ae6bdc9c1d994bf15d7e5ded2a3cb5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:31:00.146313+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff4