2+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p74", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 74, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "TEMPORARY ADDITIONAL DUTY ORDERS\n12ND 4827\n                                    NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER\n                                      OAKLAND, CALIF.\nFROM\nCommanding Officer                                    SERIAL NO.\n                                                      T - 12\nTO\n   CEPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN (177283/6311)        ESTIMATED COST\n                                                      TRANSPORTATION  $ 42.00\nREF.                                                  PER DIEM          45.00\n  (a)                                                 MISCELLANEOUS       7.50\nENCL\n  (1)                                                         TOTAL    94.50\n\n[ ] UNDER THE BASIC AUTHORITY GRANTED IN THE REFERENCE/ENCLOSURE, YOU ARE HEREBY DIRECTED AS FOLLOWS:\n\n(1) On or about 7 September 1953 you will proceed to the place(s) designated below for temporary\nadditional duty, and upon completion thereof you will return to your station and resume regular duties.\n\nPURPOSE/PLACE(S)\n\n        Proceed to the Naval Ordnance Test Station, Inyokern, China Lake, California, for\n        temporary additional duty of approximately 5 days duration, to represent this\n        activity at a conference concerning photographic problems.\n\nYOU ARE AUTHORIZED TO [  ] OPERATE [  ] VARY, OMIT, REVISIT [  ] VISIT SUCH ADDITIONAL PLACES DEEMED NECESSARY\n(2) Travel in connection with these orders is authorized as follows:\n\n[ ] GOVERNMENT VEHICLE IS DIRECTED WHERE AVAILABLE.\n\n[ ] GOVERNMENT AIR IS DIRECTED WHERE AVAILABLE. CLASS                  PRIORITY IS CERTIFIED.\n\n[ ] WHERE GOVERNMENT TRANSPORTATION IS NOT AVAILABLE, TRAVEL VIA ANY ONE OR COMBINATION OF THE COMMON CARRIERS,\nRAIL/BUS/AIR, IS AUTHORIZED.\n\n[ ] PRIVATELY OWNED VEHICLE IS AUTHORIZED WITH NO ADDITIONAL EXPENSE TO THE GOVERNMENT.\n\n[ ] PRIVATELY OWNED VEHICLE WITH REIMBURSEMENT AT THE RATE OF SEVEN CENTS PER MILE FOR THE OFFICIAL DISTANCE\nTRAVELED, SUCH MODE CONSIDERED MORE ADVANTAGEOUS TO THE GOVERNMENT.\n\n(3) If temporary duty is to be performed at an installation of the uniformed services and government\nquarters are not utilized, and maximum per diem is claimed, you are directed to obtain a certification as to\nthe availability of government quarters (and mess for temporary duty under instruction or temporary duty\noutside the U.S.) from the installation commander or his designated representative.\n\n(4) The cost of this travel is chargeable as follows:\n\nAPPROPRIATION                                        ALLOT. NO.       EXPEND. ACCT.    OBJ. CLASS.\n         1741603.11 SWEEP                              11018             49140            022\nJOB ORDER                        DOCUMENT NO.\n  0402-1140                          105180\nALLOTTEE\n        Naval Supply Center, Oakland, California\nREMARKS\n\n                              NSC Oakland, Calif. Date    9/25/53\n                              Paid $    33.50   Per Diem for period  9/13/53 to\n                              9/16/53  (  4 days @ $5., 1 3/4 days @\n                              $9. less 2.25\n                              under BuVou #   997  Check #   73,216\n\nSIGNATURE (COMMANDING OFFICER)           V. E. LAUDERDALE,          DATE\n                                         T. EARLE HIPP              26 August 1953\nCopy to: BuPers\n                                                                    NAVY DPPO 12ND-TI-8007", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "49ffbd072204d92adc987d19262a4cfff9e1b8182dbd6342f757fdb7ef4a29e3", "output_sha256": "85ced9f0e15cf208e3eab2eba2ba74e26b396168fca488777517b2050043fa4c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:31:52.981182+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff4