tion to one copy of each set of basic orders with all\nthe day of return as a day of leave, except when such return is made   endorsements thereon, as required by BuPers Manual Article C-5407(4).\n\n                          U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE    16—52837-4", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4210647559240c3737e19a7e4081e984f1d09b6a89d443bd19858fecf7d6a644", "output_sha256": "ea7bdce04b55045b12a7165c072589329edf6e61ca459d363b8241aaba601240", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:32:03.130618+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p79", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 79, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER\nOakland 4, California\n\n11:TAM:jlm\n177283/8311\n19 AUG 1952\n\nT-4\n\n                                          C-2\nFrom:  Commanding Officer\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:  Temporary additional duty\n\n1.  Proceed on or about 20 August 1952 to the place indicated below for\ntemporary duty.  This is in addition to your present duties, and upon\ncompletion thereof you will return to your station and resume your\nregular duties.\n\n     To Naval Ordnance Test Station, Inyokern, California, for temporary\nadditional duty, of approximately 3 days duration, in connection\nwith photographic matters.\n\n2.  Travel via government transportation, including government air, is\ndirected where available.  Class THREE priority is certified.  Where\ngovernment transportation is not available, travel via any one, or\ncombination, of the common carriers RAIL/BUS/AIR is authorized; or at\nyour option travel via privately owned conveyance is authorized at no\nadditional expense to the government, if such travel can be accomplished\nin the allowed travel time by rail.\n\n3.  If temporary duty is to be performed at an installation of the uni-\nformed services, and government quarters are not utilized, and maximum\nper diem is claimed, you are directed to obtain a certification as to\nthe availability of government quarters from the installation commander.\n\n4.  Cost of this travel is chargeable to appropriation 1731803.11 Service\nWide Supply and Finance, expenditure account 45028, job order number\n04061110004, allotment 11018, object class 022, document no. 04-002,207,\nNSC Oakland.  The estimated cost is:  Transportation $60.00, per diem\n$27.00.\n\n\n                                        T. EARLE HIPP\n\nCopy to:\nBuPers\n\n          AUG 2 5 1952\n          MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\n          From: Air Traffic Control Office 12ND\n               San Francisco, California\n\n          No government air transportation available\n          San Francisco, California to Inyokern, Calif.\n          this date.\n\n                         A. E. JACOBSON\n                         CDR E BENZ\n                         Officer in Charge", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ba69f2338bb77d4b4c03dd0f5a5907e4e74b3367ffe473c3deb1ed0fe05a656f", "output_sha256": "ba69f2338bb77d4b4c03dd0f5a5907e4e74b3367ffe473c3deb1ed0fe05a656f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:32:05.511786+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p80", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 80, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORTED: USNOTS\nINYOKERN, CALIFORNIA\n1610  25 AUG 1952\n\nR. SMITH, YNC, USN\n\n\n\n\n        U. S. NAVAL ORDNANCE TEST STATION\n        INYOKERN, CHINA LAKE, CALIFORNIA\n\n                        29 August 1952\n\n        FIRST ENDORSEMENT\n\n        From:  COMMANDER\n        To:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\n        Subj:  Temporary Additional Duty\n\n        1.  Reported 25 August 1952.\n\n        2.  Detached 29 August 1952.\n\n        3.  Government quarters were available\n        while on this Station.\n\n        4.  Government subsistence was not available\n        nor furnished while on this Station.\n\n        5.  Government transportation was not available\n        from U. S. Naval Ordnance Test Station, Inyokern,\n        China Lake, California to Oakland, California.\n\n                        W. V. R. VIEWEG\n\n\n\n                        R. H. SOLIER\n                        By direction\n\n\n  2   End.                    AUG 29 1952\n                         NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER\n                         OAKLAND, CALIFORNIA.\n\n        1.  Reported this date.  Resume your regular\n        duties.\n\n\n                        F. A. FIELDING\n                        By direction\n\n                                              Finished File--Pers Billet", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dc362236ce028acfdb6cb79fcab74473a645dd46b2ffc64a6e6ce4b1f9ee801e", "output_sha256": "dc362236ce028acfdb6cb79fcab74473a645dd46b2ffc64a6e6ce4b1f9ee801e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:32:07.386102+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p81", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 81, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nNAVPERS-321 (REV. 1-50)\n\n                    READ CAREFULLY THE INSTRUCTIONS\n                           PRINTED BELOW\n\nTO: Chief of Naval Personnel                                                    DATE: 4 AUG 1952\n\nFROM (Commanding officer)                              SHIP OR STATION\n\n           Commanding Officer              Naval Supply Center, Oakland, California\n\n          In conformity with requirements of U. S. Navy Regulations, I report the following leave of absence taken by:\nNAME (Last)              (First)                (Middle)                   GRADE AND CORPS        FILE NO.\n\nNEWHOUSE    