ctivities, Yokosuka, on or about 1 December 1951, detached from duty as Assistant\nAviation Supply Officer and from such other duty as may have been assigned; proceed to\nthe United States and upon arrival further proceed and report to the Bureau of\nAeronautics, Navy Department, Washington, D.C. for temporary duty for a period of about\ntwo (2) weeks.  Upon completion of temporary duty and when directed by proper\nauthority, detached; proceed and report to the Commanding Officer, Naval Supply Center,\nOakland, California for duty.  Authorized to delay fifteen (15) days in reporting\nWashington, D.C. provided no excess leave involved, such delay to count as leave.\nKeep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new commanding officer advised of your leave\naddress.  Government transportation is directed outside the United States.  For travel\nvia government aircraft, class THREE priority is certified.  Travel chargeable to\nAppropriation 1721453.18 MPN: Expenditure Account 74110; Object Class 029.  Qualified:\n124555, 161270, 148200.\n\n3.  Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance with these orders, or any\nmodification thereto, you are hereby directed to forward to the Chief of Naval\nPersonnel, via your new commanding officer, a copy of these orders with all\nendorsements thereto, including the final reporting endorsement.\n\n4.  In accordance with ALNAV 41-50 you are authorized to receive three (3)\nmonths advance pay.\n\n5.  Delivered and detached.\n\n\n                              J.P. THEW\nCopy to:                      Chief of Staff\n  CO, NSC, Oakland\n\nOrders received for compliance at (Time)  _1320_  (Date) 29 NOV 1951\n\n\n        Certified a True Copy             D.C. NEWHOUSE\n        [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9a07180553616144fd07b5ef37e3d6b6bf59535b30ff78dd8f4a6e8a0043b5e6", "output_sha256": "ef242e79c8287a59365577