val Personnel                                          NAVAL SPEEDLETTER—\n    ATTN: Pers-B115j                                                  Permits dispatch or informal language.\n    Navy Department                                                   May be sent (1) with enclosures, (2) in\n    Washington 25, D.C.                                               a window envelope (size 8⅝\" x 3⅝\"),\n                                                                      if contents are not classified as confi-\n                                                                      dential or higher, (3) to both naval and\n                                                                      nonnaval activities.\n                                                                      Is packaged 500 sheets of white or of\n(Fold)                                                                one color: yellow, pink, or green.\n\n\n\n\n          REFER BUPERS ORDERS 30691 OF 1 NOVEMBER 1951 TO CHPHOT\n\n          DELBERT C NEWHOUSE USN X REQUEST MODIFICATION TO READ\n\n          QUOTE REPORT TO COMMANDING OFFICER NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER\n\n          OAKLAND CALIFORNIA FOR DUTY UNQUOTE VICE QUOTE REPORT\n\n          TO OFFICER IN CHARGE AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT NAVAL SUPPLY\n\n          CENTER FOR DUTY UNQUOTE X\n\n\n\n\n                              J. H. LILLIS\n                              LCDR SC USN\n                              Administrative Officer\n\n\nCOPY TO\n                                                             Finished File—[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\nADDRESS: Commanding Officer                                   ←—— SENDER'S MAILING ADDRESS\n         Naval Supply Center                                  Address reply as shown at left; or reply\n         Oakland 4, California                                hereon and return in window envelope\n                                                              (size 8⅝\" x 3⅝\"), if not classified as\n                                                              confidential or higher.\n                                                              CLASSIFICATION\n\n                                                              NONCLASSIFIED\n\n                                                                                        MINS STANDARD", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1adcf170837dfb76138efa18fa61974d6bb1d8a31316856dce43a1810ec282bb", "output_sha256": "bb33e1da41d4b4d9edc8d7e05aba7ca040442d59f9890272c7b1bc6c0101d975", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:32:59.805729+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p98", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 98, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/8311\n                                        Pers-B115j-AMB-1\n                                        1 November 1951\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n       Fleet Activities\n       Yokosuka, Japan\nVia:   Commander, Fleet Activities\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\n1.  When directed by the Commander, Fleet Activities, on or about 1 December 1951,\nyou will regard yourself detached from duty with the Fleet Activities, Yokosuka, Japan,\nand from such other duty as may have been assigned you; will proceed to a port in the\nUnited States and upon arrival further proceed to Oakland, Calif., and report to the\nOfficer in Charge, Aviation Supply Depot, Naval Supply Center, for duty.\n\n2.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of fifteen days (provided no excess\nleave involved) in reporting in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as\nleave.\n\n3.  Keep your old and new station advised of your address.\n\n4.  Travel via government transportation is directed outside the United States.\nClass TWO priority is certified for travel via government aircraft.\n\n5.  Cost of travel is chargeable to 1721453.18, MPN, expenditure account 74110,\nobject class 029.\n\n\nCopy to:\nOP 54\nOP 553\nComNavFE\nComTwelve          Upon reporting, forward to BuPers a\nCO,NSC,Oak         copy of these orders (Staff Corps\nComServPac (3)     Officers an additional copy to\nComNavBase,SFran   cognizant Bureau) via new Command-\nOiC,ASD,NSC, Oak   ing Officer with all endorsements.\n\n                                        L. T. DuBOSE\n\nJacket copy        \"QUAL\"\nPers B111s         124555\n     E111a         161270\n     B11183        148200\n     B115J\n\n                                        30691", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "142f361c9bdf4ecdfb9ed803b430504823f4ec2596748c7311d831349a1a7c1c", "output_sha256": "142f361c9bdf4ecdfb9ed803b430504823f4ec2596748c7311d831349a1a7c1c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:02.119344+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p99", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 99, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICER'S ORDER MEMORANDUM          OPNAV FORM 135-1 (REV. 4-51)\nTO: BU PERS (Att. Pers: B115)\n                                                                    29 OCT 1951\n1. It is requested that the below named person be issued orders as indicated:\n\nRANK    NAME (First)      (Middle Initial)      (Last)        CORPS\n                                                                X USN    FILE NO. & DESIGNATOR OR CLASS\nCHPHOT  Delbert           C.                    NEWHOUSE       □ USNR   177283/8311\n                                                               DATE      ORIGINATING PERS\nAT  Commander Fleet Activities                                           B1157\n    Navy No. 3923  Yokosuka, Japan\n    c/o F.P.O., San Francisco, California\n\nTYPE OF ORDERS                                    (Give Data)    DATE OUT BY    CONTRO