title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "IN REPLY ADDRESS\nCOMMANDANT\nTWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\nAND REFER TO\n\nOFFICE OF COMMANDANT\nTWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\nSAN FRANCISCO, 2, CALIFORNIA\n\n12th. ND 60t Hs\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert C.\nLt. USN\n177283\n\n                                    2nd Endorsement\n\n\nFrom:  The Commandant, Twelfth Naval District.\n\nTo:    Lt. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:  Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported 1 Sept. 1946 for transportation.\n\n2.  Detached this date.  You will proceed in accordance\nwith paragraph 5 and upon arrival at destination will\nreport for duty as directed in basic orders.\n\n3.  Via government air transportation.  Priority No. C 3\n\n4.  The Disbursing Officer, Headquarters 12th. Naval\nDistrict is authorized and directed to furnish you the necessary\ncommercial air transportation from San Francisco, California to\nHonolulu, T. H., via Pan-American Airways.  Excess baggage in\namount       pounds is authorized.  Priority No.      certified\nby Naval Air Priorities Office (NATS)\n\n5.  Vacated public quarters in BOQ this date.\n\n\n\n                         J. G. ANDREWS\n                    By direction of the Commandant\n\nCopy to:\n       BuPers.\n\n\n\n\nNAV 12 FORM 526", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ec355148e6bf7085bfe60de2dda254bdffc379db2e14538f57e073d25ef55e5a", "output_sha256": "57c5d41426dfbf5b1c1720cd2d3d270697fca0fd090c6e80667ca3a14c7db4bd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:12.619960+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p101", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 101, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE                                                    REPORT PERS-3-4\nNAVPERS-321 (REV. 1-49)\n                              READ CAREFULLY THE INSTRUCTIONS\n                                      PRINTED BELOW\nTO: Chief of Naval Personnel                                                   DATE:   19 June 1950\n\nFROM (Commanding officer)                          SHIP OR STATION\n                                                   U.S. Naval Photographic Center,\n   L.W. PARRISH, CDR., USN                         NAS, Anacostia, D.C.\n\n          In conformity with requirements of U. S. Navy Regulations, I report the following leave of absence taken by:\nNAME (Last)              (First)                (Middle)               GRADE AND CORPS        FILE NO.\n\nNEWHOUSE,         Delbert              Clement                   PHOT    USN           177283\n\nNOTICE: Complete either A or B; do NOT use both for same leave\nA. TOTAL NO. OF DAYS LEAVE          B. DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE        LEAVE CREDIT REMAINING AS\n   INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME___4___    OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS ___   INDICATED ON OFFICER'S LEAVE ___25___\n                                       (Total number of days, excluding preparation period of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel\n                                       time from old to new station via shortest usually\n                                       traveled route.)\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF                                                            DATED\n\n                                              C-2\n\n[Signature of officer who took leave]                              T.R. ODENATH, LT., USN\n                                                                   (Signature of commanding officer)\n                                                                   By direction\n\n                                         INSTRUCTIONS\n1. This report will be made at expiration of leave by the immediate    before 0900, in which case it shall not be counted as a day of leave.\nsuperior of the officer to whom the leave is granted and forwarded     This refers to leave taken when not detached from 