043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "08b3aed9701d6c65c5855b9ef27b2f39d1595837f6fd402d840bda2be23ba21c", "output_sha256": "3cc914a42c629893f73c493b35f6c4e1cff3f0f7465cc8f359639fd75abff4f9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:39.489812+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p112", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 112, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "U. S. NAVAL PHOTOGRAPHIC CENTER\n                    U. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\nNPC31/P16-3/OO/LWP:rts        ANACOSTIA, D. C.\n\n9 October 1950\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on BuPers ords ser 21865 dated 4 October 1950\n\nFrom:      Commanding Officer\nTo  :      CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\n1.  Delivered.\n\n\n\n                              L. W. PARRISH\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT      U. S. NAVAL PHOTOGRAPHIC CENTER\n                              U. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\n                                  ANACOSTIA, D. C.\n\n21 OCT 1950\n\n\nFrom:      Commanding Officer\nTo  :      CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\n1.  Detached this date.\n\n2.  There were no public quarters available for assignment to you and therefore\nit was necessary for you to procure quarters at your own expense.\n\n\n\n                              L. W. PARRISH\n\nNOV 26 1950\n                                    CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\nDISTRICT STAFF HEADQUARTERS             DOnewhouse\n    TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n    SAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA\n\n         Third End.\n    Reported this date for transportation.\n    You are hereby directed to report to\n    CO, Naval Station, Treasure Island,\n    for assignment of quarters in BOQ.\n\n              A. T. JACOBSON\n              By direction of the Comdt.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ca4116ce215d4ab64c1e3e38554fd71d27467a9bd6173a162ae44ab9df0a15ff", "output_sha256": "ec87df5ea416ee3fd94c950d119b74a3a29eb8116226c0a322499ed3929b837b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:41.389445+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p113", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 113, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/8311\nPers-B115j-rgw-1\n4 October 1950\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n       Naval Photographic Center\n       Naval Air Station\n       Anacostia, Washington, D.C.\nVia:   Commanding Officer\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\n1.  When directed by your commanding officer in October 1950, you will regard yourself detached from duty at the Naval Photographic Center, Naval Air Station, Anacostia, Washington, D.C., and from such other duty as may have been assigned you; will proceed to San Francisco, Calif., and report to the Commandant, Twelfth Naval District, for transportation to Barbers Point, T.H., and upon arrival report to the Commanding Officer, Naval Air Station, for duty.\n\n2.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of ten days (provided no excess leave involved) in reporting at San Francisco, Calif., in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as leave.  Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel advised of your address.\n\n3.  Travel via government transportation is directed outside the United States. Class TWO priority is certified for travel via government aircraft.\n\n4.  Cost of travel is chargeable to 1711453.18, MPN 1951, expenditure account 74110, object class 029.\n\nCopy to:\nCNART\nOP 54\nComPRNC\nComTwelve\nComFourteen\nComServPac (3)\nCO NAS, BarbersPt, TH\nComNAB, FourteenthNavDist\n\n                                                          J. W. ROPER\n\nJacket copy        \"QUAL\"        Upon reporting, forward to BuPers a\nPers B111s         124559        copy of these orders, (Civil Corps\n    B1183          161270        Officers an additional copy to\n    E111a          148200        cognizant Bureau) via new Command-\n    B115j                       ing Officer with all endorsements.\n\n                                                          21865", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "44f0abb69db26d7eb3070260347bc1c26c0182fe93c2acacb849a48ab8d19e06", "output_sha256": "6cf0102f625d32f1c2176d062ee06d11047ea39912f89a460178a7bd52b16573", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:43.552267+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p114", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 114, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/8311\nPers-B115J-rgw-1\n4 October 1950\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n       Naval Photographic Center\n       Naval Air Station\n       Anacostia, Washington, D.C.\nVia:   Commanding Officer\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\n1.  When directed by your commanding officer in October 1950, you will regard yourself detached from duty at the Naval Photographic Center, Naval Air Station, Anacostia, Washington, D.C., and from such other duty as may have been assigned you; will proceed to San Francisco, Calif., and report to the Commandant, Twelfth Naval District, for transportation to Barbers Point, T.H., and upon arrival report to the Commanding Officer, Naval Air Station, for duty.\n\n2.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of ten days (provided no excess leave involved) in reporting at San Francisco, Calif., in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as leave.  Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel advised of your address.\n\n3.  Travel via government transportation is directed outside the United States. Class TWO priority is certified for travel via government aircraft.\n\n4.  Cost of travel is chargeable to 1711453.18, MPN 1951, expenditure account 74110, object class 029.\n\nCopy to:\nCNART\nOP 54\nComPRNC\nComTwelve\nComFourteen\nComServPac (3)\nCO NAS, Barbers Pt, TH\nComNAB, Fourteenth Nav Dist\n\n                                                    J. W. ROPER\n\nJacket copy    \"QUAL\"     Upon reporting, forward to BuPers a\nPers B111s     124559     copy of these orders, (Chief Corps\n     B11183     161270     Officers an additional copy to\n     E111a      148200     cognizant Bureau) via new Commanding Officer with all endorsements.\n\n                                                    21865", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6ce1970af364ba3084f180f1c66649858795c3341e49f130f5ee60642d627cd5", "output_sha256": "0f38f408600dabe40a4a815b1f6ab2fd69da4e22cf7272f1898ca809c08aabb5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:33:46.246093+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p115", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 115, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Op-541C5/Hm\nOFFICER'S ORDER MEMORANDUM          OPNAV-54-109 REV. 4-50\nTO: BU PERS (Att. Pers: B115)                    Vne eW              19 SEP 1950\n1. It is requested that the below named person be issued orders as indicated.\n\nRANK    NAME (First)       (Middle Initial)        (Last)         CORPS\nCPHOT   Delbert            [ILLEGIBLE] C.          NEWHOUSE                  X USN        FILE NO. & DESIGNATOR OR CLASS\n                                                                  □ USNR       177283/8311\nAT Naval Photographic Center, Naval Air Station,                  DATE         ORIGINATING PERS\nAnacostia, Washington, D.C.                                       9-29         B11-7\n\nTYPE OF ORDERS                                    (Give Data)    DATE OUT BY  CONTROL NUMBER\n□ FIRST      X CHANGE      □ APPROVAL    □ COTA                  10-6         021865\n  ORDERS       OF DUTY       OF ACTION\n\n□ ORDCAN     □ ORDCOR      □ UNDELIVE