69163315f5ff40", "page": 123, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF AERONAUTICS GENERAL REPRESENTATIVE, USN,\nREFER TO INITIALS          CENTRAL DISTRICT\nAND NO.       Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n  00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.\n  LT/177283/1350\n  RN:rn\n  Serial: 9593                              27 September 1949\n\nFrom:  Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\nSubj:  Change of duty.                                          C-2\n\nRef:   (a) BuPers (Pers 31B14) dispatch 261713Z of September 1949.\n\n1.  Reference (a) is transcribed and quoted herewith for compliance:\n\n    \"Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, 177283/1350, USN, when directed\n    by the Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central\n    District, you will regard yourself detached from duty in the Office\n    of the Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central\n    District, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, and from\n    such other duty as may have been assigned you; proceed to Washington,\n    D. C., and report to the Chief of the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy\n    Department, Washington, D. C. for duty.  You are hereby authorized\n    to delay 15 days, provided no excess leave involved, in reporting\n    in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as leave.\n    Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station advised\n    of your address.  Qualifications: 161270; 124500.\"\n\n2.  Delivered.\n\n                              T. J. RAFTERY\n                              By direction of BAGR-CD.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nOrders received at 1330, 27 September 1949.\n\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.      Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\nLT/177283/1350\nRN:rn\nSerial:  9594                             29 September 1949\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT\n\nFrom:  Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,  Central District.\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n1.  Detached this date.\n\n                              T. J. RAFTERY\n                              By direction of BAGR-CD.\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY    D. C. Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "69461d25818637999d773de18b47627cc1aa77dcd2ce5262517cce1cee5a726d", "output_sha256": "e6d156b4862a87e31a53bda0dc58f9af769375e995e3a580c81682344d76c0c7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:34:31.399720+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p124", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 124, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "PE-11\nOO/NEWHOUSE, D.C.\n\n20 Oct 1949\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on BUPERS (Pers 31B14) disp 261713Z dtd Sep 1949\n\nFrom: Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics\nTo:   LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177285/1350\n\nSubj: Change of duty.\n\n1. Reported this date for duty.\n\n                              J. L. Bettinger\n                              By Direction\n\n\n\n\nCertified a True Copy\nD. C. Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "43568a75be21e4648ac723d9fbaad84a5360ab7c0d4eec41b7f203bc408bf12a", "output_sha256": "df4717cee21905a9e9fe57a8931e83b2cbfcbab7bb5e5e78f6b58012fac8c4bc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:34:32.325941+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p125", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 125, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE                                                    REPORT PERS-3-4\nNAVPERS-321 (REV. 1-49)\n                              READ CARE