                                   30 June 1949\n              1949 JUL 7   08:39\n\nFrom:         The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:           LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n              Office of Bureau of Aeronautics General Repre-\n                sentative, Central District,\n              Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\n              Dayton, Ohio.\n\nVia:          Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,\n              Central District.                    C-2\n\nSubject:      Temporary additional duty.\n\n1.  On or about 5 July 1949, you will proceed to the following places\nfor temporary duty in connection with aeronautical matters:\n\n        Rochester, N.Y.,\n        Binghamton, N.Y.,\n        Baltimore, Md.\n\n2.  You are authorized to omit or revisit any of the above mentioned\nplaces and to vary the above itinerary as may be deemed necessary.\n\n3.  This is in addition to your present duties and upon the completion\nthereof you will return to Dayton, Ohio and resume your regular duties.\n\n4.  Travel via government aircraft is directed where available.  Class\nTWO priority is certified.\n\n5.  You will be reimbursed on a per diem basis while absent from your\nstation in accordance with Par. 4153, NTI.\n\n\nCC: BuAer                                    T. L. SPRAGUE\n\nJacket Copy\nPers-3118\n     316\n     3118\n     3118-F(BuAer)\n                                             T-11117\n\n                                        Finish File Pers-3118F", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ea7211f3f58cccfd16a926b9c9462c3fb4a8a270d17c7c2747afc206e2f01ed5", "output_sha256": "63dcfac47cb97bfcbc421402a9f8c87ba9e60f8f85bb863613457451ffac8138", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:35:08.684634+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p140", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 140, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy,