ary the above itinerary as may be deemed necessary.\n\n3.  This is in addition to your present duties and upon the completion\nthereof you will return to Dayton, Ohio and resume your regular duties.\n\n4.  Travel via government aircraft is directed where available.  Class\nTWO priority is certified.\n\n5.  You will be reimbursed on a per diem basis while absent from your\nstation in accordance with Par. 4153, NTI.\n\n\nCCs: BuAer\n\nJacket Copy                              T. L. SPRAGUE\nPers-3118\n     316\n     3118\n     3118-F(BuAer)\n                                         T-11117", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d2bc86a46a2e7f15711ab29378bbfb4b40727cde0f65defc4b161365c1cc0cbb", "output_sha256": "148b718fef8d101bb61f0e64cd3b91fc016c91b05c4383d9e9207f3d4b9c0033", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:35:36.806401+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p151", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 151, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "TEMPORARY TRAVEL O[REDACTED] REQU[REDACTED]     via BAGR[REDACTED] D\nNAVPERS-1863 (REV. 8-48)\n\nTO:  The Chief of Naval Personnel.                                    DATE    24 June 1949\n\nIT IS REQUESTED THAT TEMPORARY TRAVEL ORDERS BE ISSUED AS INDICATED:\nBUREAU OR OFFICE\n\n     Bureau of Aeronautics\nNAME (Last)              (First)                    (Middle initial)     RANK AND CORPS     FILE NO.     DESIGNATOR OR\n                                                                                                           CLASSIFICATION\n     Newhouse, Delbert C                                                  LT, USN            177283        1350\nDUTY STATION OR TEMPORARY DUTY STATION (Where officer is to be addressed)  A 713\n     BAGR/CD, Dayton, Ohio\nIS OFFICER NOW ON TEMPORARY DUTY          IF YES, REFERENCE ORDERS\nON PER-DIEM BASIS?\n               [