ve,\n               Central District\n\nSubject:       Temporary additional duty.\n\n1. On or about 8 March 1949 you will proceed to Washington, D. C.\nfor temporary duty in connection with Aeronautical matters.\n\n2. This is in addition to your present duties and upon the comple-\ntion thereof you will return to Dayton, Ohio and resume your regular\nduties.\n\n3. Travel by government air is directed where available.\n\n4. For travel by naval transport aircraft, Class THREE priority\nis hereby certified.\n\n5. Where government air is not available, commercial air is au-\nthorized where necessary to expedite completion of this duty.\n\n6. You will be reimbursed on a per diem basis while absent from\nyour station in accordance with Par. 4153, NTI.\n\n7. Subject travel was essential at this time, and the length of\ntime consumed in administrative channels prevented written orders\nfrom being issued prior to your departure.\n\n(Confirming telephoned instructions\n    of 7 March 1949.)\n\nCC: BuAer\n\nJacket Copy                    T. L. SPRAGUE\nPers-3118\n     3118\n     3118-F(AER.)\n     316\n                               T-3859", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c95cd9a044bc00785150851e18d60a7ed234d0d5975c41c161f3b72f4b17c996", "output_sha256": "9953c4afff576fe67c4e98ebb772f155f048202f24b17ed445743b67ea462197", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:05.415284+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p162", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 162, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "TEMPORARY TRAVEL ORDER REQUE[REDACTED] via\nNAVPERS-1863 (REV. 6-47)              BAGR, CD[REDACTED]\n\nTO:  The Chief of Naval Personnel.                         DATE  7 March 1949\n\nIT IS REQUESTED THAT TEMPORARY TRAVEL ORDERS BE ISSUED AS INDICATED:\nBUREAU OR OFFICE\n\nBureau of Aeronautics, Navy Dept. Wash. DC\nNAME  (L