ING ANY TRAVEL TIME    07          OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS ______\n                    (Total number of days, excluding preparation period of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel\n                    time from old to new station via shortest usually\n                    traveled route.)\n\nLEAVE CREDIT REMAINING AS\nINDICATED ON OFFICER'S LEAVE\nRECORD (NAVPERS-329)          44\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF                              DATED\n\nBAGR-CD                                   26 Nov 48\n\nD. C. Newhouse                            Henry J. Bowker, By direction\nD. C. NEWHOUSE                            HENRY J BOWKER, By direction\n(Signature of officer who took leave)          (Signature of commanding officer)\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. This report will be made at expiration of leave by the immediate\nsuperior of the officer to whom the leave is granted and forwarded\nimmediately to the Chief of Naval Personnel. Care must be taken to\ninsure that correct number of days leave are reported.\n2. The day of departure from station or duty counts as a day of duty;\nthe day of return as a day of leave, except when such return is\nmade before the regular hour for forenoon quarters on board ship or\nfor beginning work at a shore station. This refers to leave taken when\nnot detached from ship or station (see Article 1727, Navy Regulations).\n3. In cases of authorized delay counting as leave, this form is to be\nsubmitted in addition to one copy of each set of basic orders with all\nendorsements thereon, as required by BuPers C/L 44-47.\n\nU. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE     16—52637-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c7c34cffdafb0b0667cc227c901c61ff2c7851c63021ac3f548f0257b881c63e", "output_sha256": "44385027f1d7b3b27bd3673c4981989f851eb6c2c87ffaabe83f9a0fc3d02635", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:11.811972+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p164", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 164, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/1350\nPers-3118-LEN-2\n\n17 January 1949\n\nFrom:        The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:          LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n             Office of Bureau of Aeronautics General\n               Representative, Central District,\n             Wright Patterson Air Force Base,\n             Dayton, Ohio.\n\nVia:         Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative.\n\nSubject:     Temporary additional duty.\n\n1.  On or about 11 January 1949 you will proceed to Washington, D.C.\nfor temporary duty in connection with photographic and policy\nconference.\n\n2.  This is in addition to your present duties and upon the completion thereof you will return to Dayton, Ohio, and resume your regular\nduties.\n\n3.  Travel by government air is directed where available.\n\n4.  For travel by naval transport aircraft Class THREE priority is\nhereby certified.\n\n5.  You will be reimbursed on a per diem basis while absent from your\nstation in accordance with Para. 4153, NTI.\n\n6.  Subject travel was essential at this time, and the length of time\nconsumed in administrative channels prevented written orders from\nbeing issued prior to your departure.\n\n(Confirming telephoned instructions\n  of 11 January 1949)\n\nJacket Copy\npers-3118\n     3118-F (BuAer)                    T. L. SPRAGUE\n     3118\n     311D                              T-692", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "560a32fcd0a683d664347fa16a62eced987946544348f62d4a37a4c143237d38", "output_sha256": "d3d2378a085ce006f7b909fc2219c7ddaeaafccdbb38d8489cbbd798883b9328", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:13.919475+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p165", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 165, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Na