IC & POLICY CONFERENCE\n\n                                                              FINISHED FILE PERS-31454\n\n\nIT IS NECESSARY THAT I RECEIVE ORDERS NOT LATER THAN (HOUR)             (DATE)\nIS AIR TRAVEL TO BE DIRECTED? (Check mode(s) of travel)\nX  where available\n   Government Air    (PRIORITY    3    )          Commercial Air\n\nESTIMATED COST TRANSPORTATION                             HOW OFFICER WILL TRAVEL:\n\nESTIMATED COST PER DIEM                   $11.00               Government Air\n\nMISCELLANEOUS (TAXI, TIPS, ETC.)\n                                                                                       JAN 1 2 1949\n           TOTAL                          $11.00\n\nREMARKS:\n\n                                                    C.T.A.  11 JAN 1949\n\n\nREQUESTED BY                             SECTION                             ROOM      EXTENSION\nMr. L. J. Finnerty                       Military Personnel Branch            3910      3294\n\nSIGNED (1)                               SIGNED (2)                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nFORWARDED/APPROVED BY\n[ILLEGIBLE]\n                              U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE   16—37704-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "68a296df5f2cf7dac08ba99ae6146339b40f33a36d18966df86aba364281cc9f", "output_sha256": "9e51d7c35f6c1ebf2260511fbdad9ff4103440a14f41301234bda3f6577ef795", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:16.859789+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p166", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 166, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICER FORM                    Aviation Supply Depot\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement  LT  17728  Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n     (Claimant's name in full)          (Rank)        (File No.)        (Duty Sta.)\nFrom:\nTo  :    Officer-in-Charge, Terminal Leave Disbursing Office.\nVia :    (1) Disbursing Officer\n         (2) Commanding Officer\n         (3) Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers 3216A)\n\nSubj :   Claim for settlement for accrued leave.\n\nRefs :   (a) Armed Forces Leave Act 1946.\n         (b) BuPers Circular Letter 193-46.\n\n1.  In accordance with the provision of reference (a) I hereby submit claim for accrued leave\ndue me, if any.\n\n2.  To the best of my knowledge and belief I have had leave in the amounts and during the fiscal\nyears since 1 July 1939 as indicated below:\n\n    No. of Days         Fiscal Year         No. of Days         Fiscal Year\n    XXX                 XXXXX               12                  1946\n    30                  1943                4                   1947\n    35                  1945\n\n3.  In accordance with the provisions of reference (b) I have computed that my total leave credit\non 31 August 1946 was... 110 ....... days. It is requested that the Chief of Naval Personnel verify [REDACTED]\n[REDACTED] the above total leave credit and by endorsement of this letter so inform the addressee.\n\n4.  I entered into present continuous active duty as a commissioned or warrant officer on\n[REDACTED] 1 September 1942.\n\n5.  On 31 August 1946, I was serving in the rank of......... Lieutenant .........................\n\n6.  I have (had) had enlisted service since 8 September 1939 and I have (not) appended hereto as\nan enclosure a statement of such service together with supporting documents. I have not submitted any other claim for settlement for accrued leave.\n\n                                                    D.C. Newhouse\n                                                    Signature of Claimant\nEnd 1\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\nFrom: Disbursing Officer......... Pearl Harbor, T. H. ..................\n                                        (Ship or Station)\nTo  : Officer-in-Charge, Terminal Leave Disbursing Office.\nVia : Commanding Officer.\n\n1.  The rate of pay of the above claimant on 31 August 1946 was $..9.583 ...... per day.\n2.  He was receiving subsistence allowance at the rate of        $..1.40 ...... per day.\n3.  His rate of rental allowance was                             $..3.00 ...... per day.\n\n         Finished File Per 3216A          D.F. SULLIVAN ENS.(SC)USN   584673\n                                          Signature of D. O.          Symbol No.\nEnd 2\n                                                    NOV 25 1946\nTo :    Officer in Charge, Terminal Leave Disbursing Office.\nVia:    The Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers 3216A).\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n        15 APR 1947                       K. A. GRAHN, CDR SC USN\n                                          Commanding Officer\nEnd 3\nTo :   Officer-in-Charge, Terminal Leave Disbursing Office.\n\n1.  Examination and verification of the claimant's record indicated that on 31 August 1946, he\nhad a total of...... 39 ... days accrued leave standing to his credit for his officer services.\n\n                                          LOUIS E. DENFELD\n\n14ND-GEN-35\nPH—10-10-46—17,500", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bfc4cb346592f82a1738e7b3d8f446e5c2087e8e738d0a32cdb7e092a30b3041", "output_sha256": "fa734dbe0e59ca799a9dd9d31c8751b2f2219eb5f62ad36b9fbf2edf35073306", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:20.377222+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p167", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 167, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "(FORM FOR OFFICERS WITH PRIOR ENLISTED SERVICE)\n\nName .... NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement .......................... Officer File No. 177283..\n\n1.  I had enlisted service subsequent to 7 September 1939 in a branch of the Armed Forces of the\nUnited States as follows:\n\n          Date of Enlistment              Branch of Service                    Enlisted Serial No.\n\n          24 January 1939                U. S. Navy......                       393 07 21..........\n\n          ...........................     ..............................         ..........................................\n\n          ...........................     ..............................         ..........................................\n\n2.    During the above period (a) of service I had leave as follows:\n\n          Days of leave           Fiscal Year             Days of leave              Fiscal Year\n\n          ....19.........         ..........1940           ......................     ......................\n\n          ..................      ..................         ......................     ......................\n\n          ..................      ..................         ......................     ......................\n\n          ..................      ..................         ......................     ......................\n\n3.    During the above period (a) of service I was AWOL, AOL or in confinement as a result of\nsentence of a court martial...........0............days.\n\n4.    (a) I was appointed a commissioned or warrant officer directly from enlisted status on........\n1 September 1942........\nOr\n4.    (b) I was discharged from....................................., on..............................., at which\n                                              Branch of Service\ntime my enlisted rank or rating was......................................., and I was appointed a commissioned\nor warrant officer on................................\n\n5.    At the date of my discharge, or appointment (as indicated in 4 (a) or (b) above) I was (was\nnot) serving in one of the first three pay grades.\n\n6.    If the statement above is in the affirmative I did (did not) have a dependent.\n\n7.    I attach the following documents: Acceptances of appointments as PHOT, USN;\n                                              ENS, USN; LTJG, USN; and LT, USN.\n8.    I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I am the person who served in the Armed Forces under the name stated above and that the foregoing statements are true and correct to the best of my\nknowledge and belief.\n                                                                      D. C. Newhouse\n                                                                      Signature of Claimant\nSubscribed and sworn to before me on.......NOV 25 1946...............................\n\n                                                                      K.A.Grahn\n                                                                      Officer Authorized to\n                                                                        administer oaths.\n(After completing this form attach it securely to the Officer Claim Form.)  K. A. GRAHN, CDR SC USN\n\nEnd-1.                                                NOV 25 1946\n\nTo:         Officer in Charge Terminal Leave Disbursing Office.\n\nxxxxxxxxExamination of the claimant's enlisted service record shows that on the date described the\ndate of appointment as shown in paragraph (a) above he was serving in the rate of xxxxxxxxxx\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx in the service for pay purposes xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx Service record of LT NEWHOUSE\ncannot be examined; record forwarded to BuPers at           K.A.Grahn\ntime of NEWHOUSE'S discharge from permanent en-            .............................\nlisted status to accept permanent appointment                    Commanding Officer\nPH-10-10-46-5,6 as Chief Photographer on 25 Sept 1946.   K.A.GRAHN, CDR SC USN", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c009a0da3f0a77b02a9e058c1dbe0384da21a2b46e5d7f497701fa2599e6355b", "output_sha256": "41360e2b5bf7182bfc5267651c12beedac9b51f82c19b0c7e3a2ab92975dd96a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:23.866919+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69