ST DESPATCH ORDERS.\n\nREQUESTED BY                         SECTION                          ROOM        EXTENSION\n    Mr. Geo J. Finnerty           Military Personnel Branch           3910          3294\n\nSIGNED (1)                           SIGNED (2)              [signature]\n\nFORWARDED/APPROVED BY\n\n                        U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE  16—37704-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "371360a250e650901724a9aee16183f4f18657c8110183d8db63c6af1a868a94", "output_sha256": "d872402e342685d9562d7bed7dd78af0c4e52e6b42d9f0e4c53b06556579542a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:46.758921+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p178", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 178, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nFU/FF12/P16-4/00/60:wn          Air Force\n                    UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial:  82-48                                          1 July 1948.\n\nFrom:          The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :          Lieutenant\n                    Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, 0177283/1350, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:       Change of Duty.\n\nReference:     (a) BuPers disp. 221305Z of June 1948.\n\n     1.     Reference (a) is quoted, for information and compliance:\n\n     LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/1350 DIRDET ABOUT 1 JULY PROREP BUAER\n     NAVY DEPT TEM ABOUT 2 WEEKS X COMPLETION DIRDET PROREP BAGR\n\n     CENTRALDIST WRIGHT PATTERSON AIRFORCE BASE DAYTON OHIO DUTY\n     REPLTR COMBINE X DELREP 15 DAYS WASH DC PROVIDED NO EXCESS\n\n     LEAVE INVOLVED XX XX XX\n\n     2.     You will proceed immediately and report to the Commandant\nof the FOURTEENTH Naval District for transportation for yourself and\nyour dependents to a port in the United States.  Upon arrival you will\nproceed and carry out the orders contained in paragraph one above or any\nmodification thereto.\n\n     3.     Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station\nadvised of your address.\n\n     4.     Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance with these\norders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed to forward to\nthe Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new Commanding Officer, a copy of\nthese orders, complete with all endorsements thereto, including the final\nreporting endorsement.\n\n     5.     Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                                        J. C. Cronin\nCopy to:                                J. C. CRONIN.\n     CNO (OP-54)\n     BuPers (Pers 31163)\n     BuAer\n     ComNINE\n     ComAirPac\n     ComServPac\n     BAGR, Central District Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n     ComFOURTEEN.    CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c1551a14469b9fea6c0bef92ddbf76d78b87fd2db5f0fa564c7f87989887a894", "output_sha256": "89627b236e1903653ac45f924e9c87f346f51ec7e0bc980dc5ca14c7229f9f2e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:49.074073+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p179", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 179, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OC/Newhouse, D.C.\n(177283/1350)\n\n13 July 1948\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on\nComUtWingPac orders\nSerial 82-48 dated\n7-1-48.\n\nFrom:          Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo  :          Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:       Change of duty.\n\n     1.        You reported for transportation on 2 July 1948.\n\n     2.        Travel by government air is directed outside the continental limits of the United States.  For travel via Military Air\nTransport Service Aircraft, Class THREE priority is hereby certified.\n\n     3.        Detached this date.  Report immediately to the Booking\nOffice, MATS Terminal, Hickam Field, for air transportation.\n\n\n\n                         S. S. MURRAY.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "86b2be78788cd2c82a095daf570fb9457c687d58497f802aa03c902229c184f8", "output_sha256": "e03d9276b943230c38e962ba4e32211621a30fc86d2f4ce332f010f4224147cc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:50.291554+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p180", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 180, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE-2                THIRD ENDORSEMENT on ComAirWingPac         11 August 1948\nCO/NEWHOUSE,D.C.        orders Serial 82-48 dated 7/1/48\n\nFrom:           Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:             LT Delberta C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubject:        Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported this date for temporary duty.\n\n\n                                        C. H. Holt\n                                        By Direction\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                            C-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8f7a4faa934f6e81abb6be570fed6601b6508aabcf539a1c227e193be126602b", "output_sha256": "4cebeb4f460237761f3010f15701bbea8dc066a54b90c5dce8bfb769396717d4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:51.431629+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p181", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 181, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF AERONAUTICS GENERAL REPRESENTATIVE, USN\nREFER TO INITIALS                    CENTRAL DISTRICT\nAND NO.                         WRIGHT FIELD, DAYTON, OHIO\n\nMLS:mls\n\n                                              Finished File Pers 311S83\n\n26 August 1948\n\nFrom:      Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350.\nTo  :      Chief of Naval Personnel.\nVia :      Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\n\nSubj:      Compliance with Orders - Reporting of.\n\nRef :      (a) BuPers disp 221305Z/JUNE 48, as modified by BuPers ser\n               6717, dtd 18 Aug 48.\n\n1.   The Chief of Naval Personnel is hereby furnished a certified copy\nof reference (a), containing all endorsements thereto including the final\nreporting endorsement.\n\n2.   By copy of this letter, the Commandant, NINTH Naval District is in-\nformed of my reporting for duty with the Bureau of Aeronautics General Repre-\nsentative, Central District.\n\n                                         D. C. NEWHOUSE.\n\nENGL: (HW)\n1. CertCy of ref(a), w/all\n   ends thereto incl final\n   reporting endorsement.\n\nCopy to:\n  Com9 (OffDistrOff)\n  w/1 cy ref (a).\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE, D.C./                                               End-1\nLT/177283/1350/USN\nMLS:mls   7904                                          AUG 27 1948\n\nFrom:      Bureau of Aeronautics Representative, Central District.\nTo  :      Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n1.   Forwarded.\n\nBy direction of BAGR-CD:                     M. LUKE,\n\nCopy to:\n  Com9 (OffDistrOff)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3bb4b7eeb14393a03ebbdd2ff51bbac1ebe671ec07e71bc21c43ce2b7ee1cb6b", "output_sha256": "3bb4b7eeb14393a03ebbdd2ff51bbac1ebe671ec07e71bc21c43ce2b7ee1cb6b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:54.046844+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p182", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 182, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE-2                    FOURTH ENDORSEMENT on ComUtWingPac              13 August 1948\n00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.             orders Serial 82-48 dated 7/1/48\n\n\nFrom:           Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:             LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubject:        Change of Duty.\n\n1.  Detached this date from temporary duty.\n\n\n\n                                        /s/  C. H. HOLT\n                                             By direction\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nJN-177283/1350\nEnd-5                        21 August 1948                  ASO Phila., 11, Pa.\nTo:      LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n1.       Reported 19 August 1948; temporary duty completed 21 August\n1948.  No government quarters available or assigned you at this station.\n\nBy direction of Supply Officer-in-Command:\n\n                                        /s/ E.R. BRITT\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE, D.C./           24 AUGUST 1948                          End-6\nLT/177283/1350/USN\n\nFrom:    Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo :     Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n1.   Reported this date.  No government quarters or messing facilities are\navailable at this station.\n\n                                        M. LUKE,\n                                        By direction.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nI hereby certify that travel performed in accordance with these orders was by privately\nowned vehicle as follows:\n\nDeparted Washington, D.C.  1000, 8/18/48.    Arrived Philadelphia  2100 8/18/48.\nDeparted Philadelphia, Pa  1230, 8/21/48.    Arrived Dayton, Ohio  1030 8/24/48.\n\nI further certify that no Government transportation or transportation requests were furnished\nme for use in performing travel in compliance with these orders.\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY             D. C. NEWHOUSE.\n[signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "df468fdb6d64721fd0a4bb7c4df50599c43d386cabe05b5935dc48216cd1c934", "output_sha256": "df468fdb6d64721fd0a4bb7c4df50599c43d386cabe05b5935dc48216cd1c934", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:56.738595+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p183", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 183, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/1350\nPers-31167-PAB-1\n\n18 August 1948\n\nFrom:                The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:                  LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n                     Bureau of Aeronautics,\n                     Navy Department.\n\nVia:                 BuAer (2).\n\nSubject:             Modification of orders.\n\n1.  Your dispatch orders 221305 June 1948 are modified in that when directed by the\nChief of the Bureau of Aeronautics, you will regard yourself detached from temporary\nduty in the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, will proceed immediately to\nPhiladelphia, Pa., and report to the Supply Officer in Command, Naval Aviation Supply\nDepot for temporary duty for a period of about two days in the Aviation Supply Office,\nNaval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.\n\n2.  Upon completion of this temporary duty you will carry out the remainder of your\nbasic orders.\n\n\nCC: ComNine (2)\nCNO (OP-54)\nSupOfComd, NASD, Phila, Pa.\nBAGR, Central Dist, Wright Patterson,                    T. L. SPRAGUE\n  Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n\n\nJacket copy\nPers-3118\nPers-82233\nPers-3118-F                                          6717\nPers-31167", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e51f5d3b574b988e0e2facfaca295de31db61ee1d740708f0ff4cfc681700c84", "output_sha256": "2a8efd9cf3ce4b7b820c5afa838304c29712b3966d2e38f184135af96188f58b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:58.441681+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p184", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 184, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE-2                    THIRD ENDORSEMENT on ComUtWingPac          11 August 1948\nCO/NEWHOUSE,D.C.            orders Serial 82-48 dated 7/1/48\n\nFrom:           Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:             LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubject:        Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported this date for temporary duty.\n\n\n\n\nARRIVED CONT. U.S. at Alameda, California 16 July 1948.\n\n\nLeft Alameda  16 July 1948\n\nArrived Washington, D.C.  11 August 1948\n\nNo Government transportation furnished.\n\n                    /s/ D.C. Newhouse.\n                        (Officer's Signature)\n\n\nTravel was performed by privately owned automobile.\nAuthority ALNAV 613-46.  No government Transportation\nfurnished.\n\n                    /s/ D.C. Newhouse.\n                        Signature of Officer.\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[signature] D.C. Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cabcea65f7eca2ec06ac66285d2b21feb30704328d0281c6e991a2d1b66230c2", "output_sha256": "f831e6b044905bf1e466003f3782e592baacba67ecef034d22fd949905b86c1d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:36:59.790034+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p185", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 185, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\nAir Transport Squadron TWO\nNAS, Alameda, California\nArrived NAS, Alameda, California aboard\nFlight JUL 16 1948 date 2216\nat 1330 PST\n\n          /s/ Tetwenas\n          Air Transport Officer\n\n\nMEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT          17 July 1948\n\nArrived San Francisco, California\nProceeding this date, via privately owned automobile, to carry out basic orders.\n\n                    /s/ H. C. NEWHOUSE,\n                        Lt., USN.\n\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\nD. C. Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6787b155a79b313c26db345fdf9438d5bd1e933ce8ee97dee5b2f1f3f67bfc7f", "output_sha256": "6787b155a79b313c26db345fdf9438d5bd1e933ce8ee97dee5b2f1f3f67bfc7f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:00.763901+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p186", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 186, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "00/Newhouse, D.C.\n(177283/1350)\n\n13 July 1948\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on\nComUtWingPac orders\nSerial 82-48 dated\n7-1-48.\n\nFrom:          Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo:            Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:       Change of Duty.\n\n     1.        You reported for transportation on 2 July 1948.\n\n     2.        Travel by government air is directed outside the con-\ntinental limits of the United States.  For travel via Military Air\nTransport Service Aircraft, Class THREE priority is hereby certified.\n\n     3.        Detached this date.  Report immediately to the Booking\nOffice, MATS Terminal, Hickam Field, for air transportation.\n\n\n                              S. S. MURRAY.\n\n\nMATS SPACE CONTROL CENTER, HONOLULU\n     ENDORSEMENT JUL 13 PAID  DATE          CHECKED IN ATC FOR FLITE!\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT, 14th NAVAL DISTRICT\nREPORTED, PROCEED BY AIR TRANSPORTATION ASSIGNED\nTO  WO  AIR PRIORITY 3D\nCERTIFIED TRANSPORTATION FURNISHED VIA MATS\nTRIP 2216 ON 15 JUL 1948\n               J.B. CANNON\n               By direction\n\n\nHEADQUARTERS 12TH NAVAL DISTRICT PR #47\nPAID $225.-, DATE 7/17/48\nR. R. PRENTICE, Comdr. (SC) USNR. 56-310\n\n               K.D. TAYLOR, Deputy\n               For R.R. PRENTICE, COMDR (SC) USNR 56-310", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0445cc1ab06a54c4f94b7cfc74db686ee3dddc5f012237ee3ad130477f8e5cf2", "output_sha256": "6c9794f588707934d3764fc2be22c3fbae3bf5aecaf00707812224863025cef5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:03.796969+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p187", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 187, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "2 - JUL 1948\n[ILLEGIBLE] Endorsement\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT\n14TH NAVAL DISTRICT, PEARL HARBOR, T. H.\nRequested for transportation this date.\n\n                    THOS. H. BINFORD\n                         By direction\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMATS SPACE CONTROL CENTER, HONOLULU\n         ENDORSEMENT JUL 13 1948 DATE\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT, 14th NAVAL DISTRICT\nREPORTED, PROCEED BY AIR TRANSPORTATION ASSIGNED\nTO   WC   AIR PRIORITY #3D\nCERTIFIED TRANSPORTATION FURNISHED VIA MATS\nTRIP 2216 on 15 JUL 1948\n                    J.B. CANNON\n                    By direction\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[SIGNATURE]\n\n                                          BuS&A Wash 25 D.C.\n                                          Mileage Pd $242.16\n                                               August 17 1948\n                                          VoNo\n                                          P.L. BARENSFIELD, JR.\n                                          LT, SC, USN, Symbol #55914\n                                                    1138\n\n\n                                          BuS&A Wash 25, D.C.\n                                          Paid $14.00\n                                          Subs Tpn Acct Exp\n                                          Aug 17 1948\n                                          Per Diem From 7/15 to 7/16/48\n                                          P.L. BARENSFIELD, JR, LT SC USN\n                                          SYMBOL # 55914         1139\n\n\n                                          MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\n                                          Air Transport Squadron TWO\n                                          NAS Alameda California\n                                          Arrived NAS Alameda, California\n                                          aboard flight 16 JUL 1948  2216\n                                          at __________ PST\n\n\n                                                Air Transport Officer", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3d0572b8fbbebd56a9f8ed4f9f83169c78b575b1a09dbd17afd595050cdc156a", "output_sha256": "21f11231949e9b9f4cf658fb88232901268b51f3a8ceb07920b0b37be3bbfbb4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:05.975174+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p188", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 188, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nFU/FF12/P16-4/00/60:wn          Air Force\n                    UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial:  82-48                                              1 July 1948.\n\n\nFrom:         The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :         Lieutenant\n                   Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, 0177283/1350, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:      Change of Duty.\n\nReference:    (a) BuPers disp. 221305Z of June 1948.\n\n          1.       Reference (a) is quoted, for information and compliance:\n\n          LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/1350 DIRDET ABOUT 1 JULY PROREP BUAER\n          NAVY DEPT TEN ABOUT 2 WEEKS X COMPLETION DIRDET PROREP BAGR\n          CENTRALDIST WRIGHT PATTERSON AIRFORCE BASE DAYTON OHIO DUTY\n          REPLTR COMBINE X DELREP 15 DAYS WASH DC PROVIDED NO EXCESS.\n\n          LEAVE INVOLVED XX XX XX\n\n          2.       You will proceed immediately and report to the Commandant\nof the FOURTEENTH Naval District for transportation for yourself and\nyour dependents to a port in the United States.  Upon arrival you will\nproceed and carry out the orders contained in paragraph one above or any\nmodification thereto.\n\n          3.       Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station\nadvised of your address.\n\n          4.       Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance with these\norders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed to forward to\nthe Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new Commanding Officer, a copy of\nthese orders, complete with all endorsements thereto, including the final\nreporting endorsement.\n\n          5.       Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                                                  J. G. Cronin\nCopy to:                                          J. C. CRONIN.\n     CNO (OP-54)\n     BuPers (Pers 31163)\n     BuAer\n     ComNINE\n     ComAirPac\n     ComServPac\n     BAGR, Central District Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n     ComFOURTEEN.     CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "27082363ee13b377029f94ff380c72fce7303d944d532d43b3732789e5f5954a", "output_sha256": "91f8869fa1cab7bc9a233a34616a56096be037efd31ba2a40564c402f9b6ee03", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:08.375357+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p189", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 189, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "WILL CAL\n\nOFFICER'S ORDER MEMORANDUM\nNAVPERS-1152 (REV. 6-45)\n\nFILE NO.          NAME (PRINT)    (last)              (first)          (middle initial)    RANK        CLASSIF.    ☑ U.S.N.\n177283/1350        NEWHOUSE         DELBERT              C               LIEUT               □ U.S.N.R.\n\n□ FIRST          □ CHANGE OF      □ WAIVER OF          □ APPROVAL                          □ CONFIRMING\n  ORDERS           DUTY             PHYS DEFECTS          OF ACTION\n\n☑ ORDERS OF  22 JUNE 48    