a your new Commanding Officer, a copy of\nthese orders, complete with all endorsements thereto, including the final\nreporting endorsement.\n\n     5.      Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                                        J. C. Cronin\n\nCopy to:                               J. C. CRONIN.\n     CNO (OP-54)                FINISHED FILE PERS-3118?\n     BuPers (Pers 31163)\n     BuAer\n     ComMINE\n     ComAirPac\n     ConServPac\n     BAGR, Central District Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n     ComFOURTEEN.\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5b38d3fd2c79fc16f55a7d7eca990584ad170c70675bb15824bc95ab1cc59aa1", "output_sha256": "5b38d3fd2c79fc16f55a7d7eca990584ad170c70675bb15824bc95ab1cc59aa1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:14.711992+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p191", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 191, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAV. S. AND A. FORM 913—REV.\n          Form Prescribed by\n     Comptroller General, U. S.\n          May 17, 1945\n\n                              VOUCHER FOR REIMBURSEMENT\n                                           FOR\n                    EXPENSES INCIDENT TO DEPENDENTS TRAVEL                D. O. VOU. NO.    3375\n                    MAIL TO BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, WASHINGTON 25, D. C.    BU. VOU. NO.\n\nTHE UNITED STATES, DR.                                                      J. A. RHEPBYIISCH\nTO (PRINT)  NEWHOUSE,   Delbert   C.   Lt.   USN   17725              Symbol 540415\n            (Last Name)           (First)    (Middle)        (Rank or Rating)      (File or Service No.)    NCDO Great Lakes\nOFFICIAL ADDRESS   Office of Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,\n                                                                              SEP 15 194[?]\n                   Central District, Wright Field, Dayton, Ohio\n                         CERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENCY OF CHILDREN\n                                                                        J. SCOTT\n                                                            Symbol 52-527\n                                                            (For use of Paying Officer)\n                                                                AMOUNT\n                                                            DOLLARS        CENTS\n\n                    MEMORANDUM\n\n                                            FINISHED FILE PERS 811\n\n202.08              J. SCOTT, Officer in Charge 52-52  PAID BY CHECK NO.\n                    By Alice C. Gibbens, Agent Cashier      526944\n\nACCOUNTING CLASSIFICATION (For completion by Administrative Officer)              FARE AUTHORIZED\n APPROPRIATION, LIMITATION          APPROPRIATION TITLE              FROM              TO\n   OR PROJECT SYMBOL                                               RAIL\n                                                                 PULLMAN\n  1790813         TRNP-1949   020    74130                        TOTAL    $\n\n                    CERTIFICATION OF CLAIMANT (FILL IN ALL BLANKS BELOW WHERE APPLICABLE)\n\nPayment is requested for transportation for travel performed by the following, who were my dependents on the effective date of orders\ndirecting this change of station.\n\n          NAME                                          RELATIONSHIP          DATE OF BIRTH OF CHILDREN\nNorma Isabel Newhouse                                      Wife\nDelbert Carroll Newhouse                                   Son                    6/26/38\nAnne Lisbet Newhouse                                       Daughter               3/14/40\n\n                              at 412 Third St., NHA #1,\nI certify that my dependents were located      Honolulu 50, T.H.              when orders directing detachment\n                                          (City and State)\nfrom my old permanent station were received, and departed from that place on (date)   1 July 1948; Arrived Alameda\nCalifornia 16 July 1948; Departed Alameda, California 16 July 1948\nand arrived at   Dayton, Ohio                      on (date)   24 August 1948.   I further certify that my\n        from Alameda, California to Dayton, Ohio\ndependents traveled at my own expense and that the child (children) named above is (are) the legitimate child (children) of the officer or man\nconcerned. (IF CHILD (CHILDREN) IS (ARE) STEP OR ADOPTED, FILL IN CERTIFICATE ON REVERSE SIDE.)\n\nI certify that the travel covered by this claim represents the entire travel of all my dependents which has been or will be made on this\nchange of station except as follows:   No exceptions\n\n*Reimbursement requested herein is (is not) in accordance with par. 3 of SecNav letter of 23 Dec. 1943.\n\n* I hereby designate _____________________________ as point to which transportation of dependents is desired.\n\nI certify that this account and schedule annexed are true and just in all respects; that payment therefor has not been received; and that\nmy statements of travel correctly reflect travel performed by my dependents.\n\nSIGN\nORIGINAL  1PAYEE ___________________________\nONLY                    Delbert C. Newhouse,\nDATE    1 Sept. 1948              RANK OR RATING    Lieutenant\n*If applicable see Instruction 1.      10—44890-1              (Instructions on reverse side of form.)    U. S. N.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1f47e257094f149cf19f20ab8b8522d9e7a2051f58f3b150422afa10775db7a6", "output_sha256": "ebe12ebe0b3f99f9bb1f6cb02d6c45a6eb3ab6073a50c0f9b2616a3dc7bc3eb3", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:18.556295+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p192", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 192, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. In the event this claim involves travel under secret or confidential orders, or orders from which the location of the old or new duty station is omitted for reasons of security, or under orders effecting assignment to or from sea duty or to or from a place to which dependents are not permitted to go, careful attention should be given to SecNav letter of 23 December 1944, particularly paragraphs 2, 3, 6 and 10.\n\n2. If your claim is not submitted under SecNav letter of 23 December 1944 (Instruction 1, above), the original and two certified copies of all orders involved, with all endorsements, must accompany claim.\n\n3. Claim should be prepared and forwarded to BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, Washington 25, D. C., in accordance with Article 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.\n\n4. CLAIM MUST BE SUBMITTED IN QUADRUPLICATE. The original is to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 912—Rev. and signed in ink on the face. Three copies (unsigned) to be on NAV. S. and A. Form 913—Rev.\n\n5. SECURELY STAPLE ALL PAPERS TOGETHER.\n\n6. The space below is to be used for any additional information by claimant which is necessary in settlement of this claim.\n\nI certify except as noted hereon that no prior claim has been presented by me or by any member of my family for the reimbursement for the transportation of dependents as claimed herein and that no transportation in kind has been furnished therefor.\n\n                    Delbert O. Newhouse,\n                    Lt. USN.\n\nCERTIFICATE OF DEPENDENCY OF CHILDREN\n(Note: To be used only for adopted or step children)\n\nI, _________________ certify that _________________ is (are) my (adopted) (step) child (children) and is (are) member(s) of my household; that said child is (children are) not possessed of property or income adequate for its (their) support and education; that it is (they are) not the beneficiary or beneficiaries, either directly or through others, of any trust or estate entitling it (them) to income adequate for its (their) support and education; that said child is (children are) in fact now and at all times solely dependent on me; that in all respects I maintain the child (children) at my own expense and from my own resources and am not reimbursed therefor directly or indirectly in any manner or form whatsoever; and that evidence of the child's (children's) dependency on me and my maintenance of it (them) has been filed with my pay accounts and is hereby made a part thereof. (See special requirements, Art. 2513, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.)\n\n_________________________\nSIGNATURE\n\n☆ U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE    16—44895-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "14563d6c7f73e7819acf2b4f69e2dcb42964e73c04a0817c9675d346a760c19d", "output_sha256": "37f2340431e9734c1e02808f9883f8ac82f55fd9267e659837b2bb6705c9af2e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:21.212020+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p193", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 193, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nFU/FF12/P16-4/00/60:wn          Air Force\n                        UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\nNAVY ACCOUNTS DISBURSING OFFICE\nGREAT LAKES, ILLINOIS\n     Serial: 82-43                                    1 July 1948.\nTRANS. OF DEPENDENTS\nFrom _____________ From: ___________  The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nAmount $________                       Lieutenant\nOn Bu. Vou. No.__:         J. SCOTT    Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, 0177283/1350, U.S. Navy.\nDate__________              (SC) USN\n              Subject: LT. Change of Duty.\n\n     Reference:     (a) BuPers disp. 221305Z of June 1948.\n\n          1.     Reference (a) is quoted, for information and compliance:\n\n     LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/1350 DIRDET ABOUT 1 JULY PROREP BUAER\n     NAVY DEPT TEN ABOUT 2 WEEKS X COMPLETION DIRDET PROREP BAGR\n\n     CENTRALDIST WRIGHT PATTERSON AIRFORCE BASE DAYTON OHIO DUTY\n     REPLTR COMMINE X DELREP 15 DAYS WASH DC PROVIDED NO EXCESS\n\n     LEAVE INVOLVED XX XX XX\n\n          2.     You will proceed immediately and report to the Commandant\n     of the FOURTEENTH Naval District for transportation for yourself and\n     your dependents to a port in the United States.  Upon arrival you will\n     proceed and carry out the orders contained in paragraph one above or any\n     modification thereto.\n\n          3.     Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station\n     advised of your address.\n\n          4.     Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance with these\n     orders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed to forward to\n     the Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new Commanding Officer, a copy of\n     these orders, complete with all endorsements thereto, including the final\n     reporting endorsement.\n\n          5.     Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                                              J. C. Cronin\nCopy to:                                   J. C. CRONIN.\n     CNO (OP-54)\n     BuPers (Pers 31163)\n     BuAer\n     ComNINE\n     ComAirPac\n     ConServPac\n     BAGR, Central District Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n     ComFOURTEEN.  CERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fcd99346a0095a970c1816ea058c9b3c4d4bac5b743b271d55b064aa803b9986", "output_sha256": "393702ea45aa709ff8bd643ea2dc496d363480e2045ba7cf4a747f2fad688b20", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:23.791101+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p194", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 194, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "2 - JUL 1948  [REDACTED]  Endorsement\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT\n14TH NAVAL DISTRICT, PEARL HARBOR, T. H.\nReported for transportation this date.\n\n                    THOS. H. BINFORD\n                         By direction\n\n\nNATS SPACE CONTROL CENTER, HONOLULU\n        ENDORSEMENT JUL 13 1947 DATE\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT, 14th NAVAL DISTRICT\nREPORTED, PROCEED BY AIR TRANSPORTATION ASSIGNED\nTO WC  AIR PRIORITY 3D\nCERTIFIED TRANSPORTION FURNISHED VIA NATS\nTRIP 2216 ON 15 JUL 1948\n                    J.B. CANNON\n                      By direction\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[signature]\n\n        BuS[REDACTED]sh 25 D.C.\n        Mileage[REDACTED]d 242.16\n              August 17 1948\n        VoN\n        P.L. BARENSFIELD, JR,\n        LT, SO, USN, Symbol #55914\n                          1138\n\n        BuS&A Wash 25, D.C.\n        Paid $14.00\n        SubsTpnAcctExp\n        Aug 17 1948\n        Per Diem From  7/15 to 7/16/48\n        P.L. BARENSFIELD, JR, LT SO USN\n        SYMBOL # 55914          1139\n\n        MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\n        Air Transport Squadron TWO\n        NAS Alameda California\n        Arrived NAS Alameda, California\n        aboard flight 16 JUL 1948  2216\n        at ____________ PST\n\n\n                    Air Transport Officer", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7971bcc5df0deac7978dc406d0303962a657c8cc36ae60efa45c51313e49cbf5", "output_sha256": "da46deab72f1ddf6e69e1c6bdc3fe30bf205edff90a1bd90f8fd7723733899de", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:25.728097+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p195", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 195, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CO/Newhouse, D.C.\n(177283/1350)\n\n13 July 1948\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on\nComUtWingPac orders\nSerial 82-48 dated\n7-1-48.\n\nFrom:          Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo  :          Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:       Change of duty.\n\n          1.        You reported for transportation on 2 July 1948.\n\n          2.        Travel by government air is directed outside the continental limits of the United States.  For travel via Military Air\nTransport Service Aircraft, Class THREE priority is hereby certified.\n\n          3.        Detached this date.  Report immediately to the Booking\nOffice, MATS Terminal, Hickam Field, for air transportation.\n\n\n                              S. S. MURRAY.\n\n\nNATS SPACE CONTROL CENTER, HONOLULU\n      ENDORSEMENT JUL 13 PAID  DATE        . CHECKED IN ATC FOR ELITE!\nOFFICE OF THE COMMANDANT, 14th NAVAL DISTRICT              D\nREPORTED, PROCEED BY AIR TRANSPORTATION ASSIGNED\nTO   WC   AIR PRIORITY 3D  .\nCERTIFIED TRANSPORTATION FURNISHED VIA NATS\nTRIP 2216 ON 15 JUL 1948\n                    J.B. CANNON\n                    By direction\n\n\nHEADQUARTERS 12TH NAVAL DISTRICT PR #47\nPAID $225.=, DATE 7/17/48\nR. E. PRENTICE, Comdr. (SC) USNR. 56-310\n\n            K.D. TAYLOR, Deputy\n            For R.E. PRENTICE, COMDR (SC) USNR 56-310\n                    JL\n\nUSNAS Anacostia, D.C.\nPaid $210 this date.\n\nJ. W. HILLMAN, LTJG, SC, USN, Symbol 531316\nBy H.E. NICHOLS Dept\n\n8/9/48\nPRM 30", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "af2ef2334e16321975a81d5fe3076f12b6de37ef55d473be186f9c890e60a33e", "output_sha256": "15c099a8abd8c8242b00e1ac08fb45ffd6f14551553e3db3012fa18463c23099", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:27.862430+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p196", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 196, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\nAir Transport Squadron TWO\nNAS, Alameda, California\nArrived NAS, Alameda, California aboard\nFlight JUL 16 1948 date 2216\nat 1330 PST\n\n          /s/ Tetwenas\n          Air Transport Officer\n\n\nMEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT          17 July 1948\n\nArrived San Francisco, California\nProceeding this date, via privately owned automobile, to carry out basic orders.\n\n                         /s/ D. C. NEWHOUSE,\n                              Lt., USN.\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "598a035c376151b688c5d34e1615c7512d3e1a9aeb2cec44fb2f5a9b48639b89", "output_sha256": "299f8b1ab58e05fe19e8f2034a74e2a536ba967b180ca7b837c7db09ac0458c0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:28.838828+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p197", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 197, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE-2          THIRD ENDORSEMENT on ComUtWingPac        11 August 1948\nOO/NEWHOUSE,D.C.  orders Serial 82-48 dated 7/1/48\n\nFrom:         Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:           LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubject:      Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported this date for temporary duty.\n\n                                        C. H. Holt\n                                        By Direction\n\n\nARRIVED CONT. U.S. at Alameda, California 16 July 1948.\n\n\nLeft Alameda  16 July 1948\n\nArrived Washington, D.C.  11 August 1948\n\nNo government transportation furnished.\n\n                    /s/ D.C. Newhouse.\n                        (Officer's Signature)\n\n\nTravel was performed by privately owned automobile.\nAuthority ALNAV 613-46.  No government transportation\nfurnished.\n\n                    /s/ D.C. Newhouse.\n                        Signature of Officer.\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[handwritten signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e836f947a756a4c7bb8e1e6c99e9e9e0008ebca9351101deef5cc305dc780939", "output_sha256": "653a25cf2bdddfb89e0f318287f4ed0690dba1a3a674440ccfb4c967e89bdb17", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:30.380088+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p198", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 198, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/1350\nPers-31167-PAB-1\n\n18 August 1948\n\nFrom:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:            LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n               Bureau of Aeronautics,\n               Navy Department.\n\nVia:           BuAer (2).\n\nSubject:       Modification of orders.\n\n1. Your dispatch orders 221305 June 1948 are modified in that when directed by the\nChief of the Bureau of Aeronautics, you will regard yourself detached from temporary\nduty in the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, will proceed immediately to\nPhiladelphia, Pa., and report to the Supply Officer in Command, Naval Aviation Supply\nDepot for temporary duty for a period of about two days in the Aviation Supply Office,\nNaval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.\n\n2. Upon completion of this temporary duty you will carry out the remainder of your\nbasic orders.\n\nCC: ComNine (2)\nCNO (OP-54)\nSupOfComd,NASD,Phila,Pa.\nBAGR,CentralDist,WrightPatterson\n  Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n\nJacket copy\nPers-3115\nPers-82233\nPers-3118-F\nPers-31167\n\n                                              T. L. SPRAGUE\n\n                                              J. SCOTT USN\n                                              LT. (SC)\n\n                                    6717", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a50f052d9edbf18d83cf1318cc3e7104a7dede762aed5688835b59428207a6ea", "output_sha256": "ede10da28b4e8dbfca0438da5bba8be23383e801f2632f0a7c3e8ad48e064068", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:32.214223+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p199", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 199, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE-2                    FOURTH ENDORSEMENT on ComUtWingPac              18 Aug.\n00/NEWHOUSE,D.C.            orders Serial 82-48 dated 7/1/48\n\nFrom:           Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:             LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n\nSubject:        Change of Duty.\n\n1.  Detached this date from temporary duty.\n\n\n                                            /s/  C. H. HOLT\n                                                 By direction\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nJN-177283/1350\nEnd-5                           21 August 1948                  ASO Phila., 11, Pa.\nTo:     LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350\n1.      Reported 19 August 1948; temporary duty completed 21 August\n1948.  No government quarters available or assigned you at this station.\n\nBy direction of Supply Officer-in-Command:\n\n                                            /s/ B.R. BRITT\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE, D.C./          24 AUGUST 1948                          End-6\nLT/177283/1350/USN\n\nFrom:    Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo  :    Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n1.   Reported this date.  No government quarters or messing facilities are\navailable at this station.\n\n\n                                            M. LUKE,\n                                            By direction.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nI hereby certify that travel performed in accordance with these orders was by privately\nowned vehicle as follows:\n\nDeparted Washington, D.C.  1000, 8/18/48.    Arrived Philadelphia  2100 8/18/48.\nDeparted Philadelphia, Pa  1230, 8/21/48.    Arrived Dayton, Ohio  1030 8/24/48.\n\nI further certify that no Government transportation or transportation requests were furnished\nme for use in performing travel in compliance with these orders.\n\n\n\n                                            D. C. NEWHOUSE.\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n[signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f7d6047b4983f894e9d085d8276d02211bb0c1c45a04015749a8537bf145c7c6", "output_sha256": "f7d6047b4983f894e9d085d8276d02211bb0c1c45a04015749a8537bf145c7c6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:34.793745+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p200", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 200, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nNAVPERS-321 (REV. 6-47)\n\n                                    READ CAREFULLY THE INSTRUCTIONS\n                                           PRINTED BELOW\nTO:  Chief of Naval Personnel                                                          DATE:  11 Aug. 1948\n\nFROM (Commanding officer)                                    SHIP OR STATION\n\n     Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics                           BuAero., Navy Dept. Washington, D. C.\n\n              In conformity with requirements of U. S. Navy Regulations, I report the following leave of absence taken by:\nNAME (Last)              (First)              (Middle)                    RANK AND CORPS          FILE NO.\n\n     NEWHOUSE             Delbert              C.                          LT, USN                 177283/1350\n\nNOTICE: Complete either A or B; do NOT use both for same leave\nA. TOTAL NO. OF DAYS LEAVE          B. DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE          LEAVE CREDIT REMAINING AS\n   INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME ___        OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS  9     INDICATED ON OFFICER'S LEAVE  51\n                                        (Total number of days, excluding preparation period of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel\n                                        time from old to new station via shortest usually\n                                        traveled route.)\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF                         Finished File Pers 3016A DATED\n\n     ComUtWingPac orders Serial 82-48                                      1 July 1948             C-2\n\n________________________                                                ________________________\n  (Signature of officer who took leave)                                   (Signature of commanding officer)\n\n                                            INSTRUCTIONS\n1. This report will be made at expiration of leave by the immediate    made before the regular hour for forenoon quarters on board ship or\nsuperior of the officer to whom the leave is granted and forwarded     for beginning work at a shore station.  This refers to leave taken when\nimmediately to the Chief of Naval Personnel.  Care must be taken to    not detached from ship or station (see Article 1727, Navy Regulations).\ninsure that correct number of days leave are reported.                 3. In cases of authorized delay counting as leave, this form is to be\n2. The day of departure from station or duty counts as a day of duty;  submitted in addition to one copy of each set of basic orders with all\nthe day of return as a day of leave, except when such return is        endorsements thereon, as required by BuPers C/L 44-47.\n\n                          U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE    16—52637-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "625a0fe8cd43f3dce68d5d7d139b629ffdf6a694529c67c01a4513b7e552bd6c", "output_sha256": "588e30289f46bd7911976f80717a8a34df88d054b009727e67457755b5864d60", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:37.275025+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p201", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 201, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/1350\nPers-31167-PAB-1\n\n18 August 1948\n\nFrom:                The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:                  LT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n                     Bureau of Aeronautics,\n                     Navy Department.\n\nVia:                 BuAer (2).                                C-2\n\nSubject:             Modification of orders.\n\n1. Your dispatch orders 221305 June 1948 are modified in that when directed by the\nChief of the Bureau of Aeronautics, you will regard yourself detached from temporary\nduty in the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, will proceed immediately to\nPhiladelphia, Pa., and report to the Supply Officer in Command, Naval Aviation Supply\nDepot for temporary duty for a period of about two days in the Aviation Supply Office,\nNaval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.\n\n2. Upon completion of this temporary duty you will carry out the remainder of your\nbasic orders.\n\n\n\nCC: ComNine (2)\nCNO (OP-54)\nSupOfComd, NASD, Phila, Pa.\nBAGR, Central Dist, Wright Patterson,                    T. L. SPRAGUE\n  Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n\nJacket copy\nPers-3118          Shipped for Armed Million\nPers-82233         Pers 31167\nPers-3118-F\nPers-31167         8 - 18 - 48\n\n                   P.B.R.\n\n\n\n                              Upon reporting, forward to BuPers a\n                              copy of these orders. (Staff Corps\n                              Officers an additional copy to\n                              cognizant Bureau) via new Command-\n                              ing Officer with all endorsements.\n\n                                                           6717", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0aa9928271306b56a0a05dfdff22c6b33146039a425f76eb9a0ea412312655a7", "output_sha256": "7fea5fed1a49f2d3eb717ee6bbb1d5a0e1fde50f5d8ad568c3d81777087a969c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:39.273946+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p202", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 202, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nFU/FF12/P16-4/00/60:wn          Air Force\n                    UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial:  82-48                                          1 July 1948.\n\nFrom:         The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :         Lieutenant\n                  Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, 0177283/1350, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:      Change of Duty.\n\nReference:    (a) BuPers disp. 221305Z of June 1948.\n\n        1.        Reference (a) is quoted, for information and compliance:\n\n    LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/1350 DIRDET ABOUT 1 JULY PROREP BUAER\n    NAVY DEPT TEN ABOUT 2 WEEKS X COMPLETION DIRDET PROREP BAGR\n\n    CENTRALDIST WRIGHT PATTERSON AIRFORCE BASE DAYTON OHIO DUTY\n    REPLTR COMMINE X DELREP 15 DAYS WASH DC PROVIDED NO EXCESS\n\n    LEAVE INVOLVED XX XX XX               Finish File   Pers-31163\n\n        2.        You will proceed immediately and report to the Commandant\nof the FOURTEENTH Naval District for transportation for yourself and\nyour dependents to a port in the United States.  Upon arrival you will\nproceed and carry out the orders contained in paragraph one above or any\nmodification thereto.\n\n        3.        Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station\nadvised of your address.\n\n        4.        Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance with these\norders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed to forward to\nthe Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new Commanding Officer, a copy of\nthese orders, complete with all endorsements thereto, including the final\nreporting endorsement.\n\n        5.        Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                  Finish File    Pers-31163          J. C. Cronin\nCopy to:                                          J. C. CRONIN.\n    CNO (OP-54)\n    BuPers (Pers 31163)\n    BuAer                                    Finish File    Pers-31163\n    ComMINE\n    ComAirPac\n    ComServPac\n    BAGR, Central District Wright Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n    ComFOURTEEN.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8033db6ef6af0682562e1267301e66cd3279dac37baac45dfd1308585e6e9852", "output_sha256": "8033db6ef6af0682562e1267301e66cd3279dac37baac45dfd1308585e6e9852", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:41.779990+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p203", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 203, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NA    COMMUNICATION SYSTE\n\nDRAFTED BY                    FILE Nr.              ROOM Nr.         EXT. Nr.\nPERS 31163 RLR 1              177283/1350                            71302\nRELEASED BY                   CODE/SECT. Nr.        DATE\nCAPT ALLEN SMITH JR                                 21 JUNE 1948     1005\n\n                    Please leave this space clear\n\n                                                              3163\n\n\nFROM: BUPERS WASHN D. C.          221305              PRECEDENCE\n                              (date/time group) (GTG)\nTO:          COMUTWINGSPACFLT\n                                                      □ PRIORITY\n\nINFO:        COMAIRPAC\n             COMSERVPAC                               □ ROUTINE\n             BAGR CENTRALDIST WRIGHT PATTERSON AIR\n             FORCE BASE DAYTON OHIO                   XX[REDACTED]IGHT\n             COMNINE\n                                C-2                  UNLESS CLASSIFIED\n                                                      RESTRICTED\n\n                                                      WILL BE CLASSIFIED\n                                                      PLAIN\n\n          