d for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nSHIP OR STATION COMMANDER UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET          DATE 20 March 1948\n\nFROM: The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet,\n                                    COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: {REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n         {REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n\n         IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME    NEWHOUSE           Delbert          Clement              FILE NO. 0177283\n            LAST                FIRST              MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS    LT, 1350, U.S.Navy                              SIGNAL NO. 16046\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF   ComUtWingPac                                     DATED    2 March 1948\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n      (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME________  TEN (10) days\n\n(B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n    TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n    EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n    VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE.................................  __________\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE                    EXPIRING DATE\nLeave credit remaining as indicated on Officer's Leave Record, 31 days.\n                              SIGNED ONIA B. STANLEY, Jr., CDR, USN,\n                                     By direction COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n     1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n     2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n     3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.                                        16—33335-2   U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ae8c99f783234dcee41528d30c54d512b1557c010ed06141cee8fd47afd1523e", "output_sha256": "1065aa804f4160e6127e3c40cbb97a14cc983fab0c244d27100b4592fed352fb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:51.190517+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p206", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 206, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UTILITY SQUADRON NINE\nCARE OF FLEET POST OFFICE\nSAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA\n\nVU9/P16-4/00/rwb\n\nSerial: 79\n\n                                        26 January 1948\n\n\n\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT to\nComAirPac Orders serial\nT-194-48 dated 7 January\n1948.\n\n\n\n\nFrom:          The Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron NINE.\nTo  :          Lieutenant Delbert G. NEWHOUSE, 0177263/1350, USN.\n\nSubject:       Temporary Additional Duty.\n\n     1.        You reported for temporary additional duty in\nUtility Squadron NINE on 19 January 1948.\n\n     2.        Temporary additional duty completed this date.\nCarry out your basic orders.\n\n\n\n                                        A. G. NEAL\n\n\ncc:  BuPers\n     ComAirPac\n     ComUtWingPac", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "84bf76058e0de8e9b37ac35bd096c834c2f1021bc57c7ac53454d64afdc82275", "output_sha25