I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME        NEWHOUSE              Delbert        Clement              FILE No.  0177283\n              LAST                  FIRST          MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS    LT, U.S. Navy                              SIGNAL No.:  16046\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF    ComUtWingPac                                    DATED  9 December 1947\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n    (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME              SEVEN (7) days\n\n    (B) DELAY, COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n    TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n    EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n    VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE....................................  —\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE                             EXPIRING DATE\nLeave credit remaining as indicated on Officer's Leave Record, 40 days.\n\n              SIGNED   J. C. CRONIN, CAPT., U.S.N.,\n                       Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n    1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULA-\nTIONS).\n    2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n    3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.\n                                                                  16—33335-2   U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f8ed3c66586ce4d46be2d0a724dbaf4e19c5d82e3fe129fa79e0caeddc8904b", "output_sha256": "b048fba756ad518c6c6a724588e0b378e28e8c024cd2913817b051c9a8b723f7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:37:56.463813+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p209", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 209, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "FF12-5/P16-3/00\n611-ms\n\n                    COMMANDER AIR FORCE\n                UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n\n\n                    T-194-45          7 January 1945\n\n\nFrom:         Commander Air Force, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :         Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, AVN, U.S. Navy, (117263).\n\nVia :         Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nSubject:      Temporary Additional Duty.\n\n     1.       When directed by the Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet\nin January, 1945, proceed to the command indicated below for temporary duty\nin connection with inspection and operation of photographic laboratories.\nThis is in addition to your present duties and upon completion thereof you\nwill return and resume your regular duties.\n\n                    Utility Squadron NINE and detachments\n\n     2.       You are authorized to omit or revisit any of the above\nmentioned commands or vary the itinerary as may be deemed necessary.\n\n     3.       Travel by government air is directed.  For travel via Naval\nTransport Aircraft, Class II priority is hereby certified.\n\n     4.       An excess of forty (40) pounds baggage is authorized while\ntraveling by air.\n\n     5.       A per diem of $7.00 will be allowed while absent from your\nstation, in accordance with paragraph 4153, U. S. Navy Travel Instructions.\n\n\n\n\n                              J. D. PRICE.\n\nCopy to:\n     BuPers\n\n\n\n                                                  Finished File Pers 310F\n                       