n□ Prorep  □ Delrep\n3. TO                                                                             FOR\n                                                                                  □Tem  □Duty  □Staff  □Duffy\n\n                                                                                  □Tem-  □Duins  □Furas\n                                                                                   Ins            by\nTRANS:                                                                            AS:\nPER DIEM    REMARKS\n□\n                          FINISHED FILE PERS-31152\n             15885\n\n                                          G. J. Frauenheim\n                                          By Direction\n\n\nCno-op-54\n\n           INFORMATION ADDRESSEE(S)              MAIL   MGM   AMGM   DISP.\n Comdt 14 N.D.\n Com air Pac\n\nDATE  10-13-47   PERS. NO. 31167   DETAIL OFFICER  Hough   EXT. 7803   DATE OUT BY 10-13-47\nNAVAER-1145 (REV. 9-45)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0dd9734d46833018e0607793fad76c1b72d8410b05ddf2d841bb8f189065f726", "output_sha256": "4479b10581106e7ba295755b61275b96f7f0cf05d74c91c1e51133405aaaca88", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:03.864638+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p212", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 212, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OC/Newhouse, D. C\n(177283/1100)\n\nSerial No. 15809\n\n14 October 1947\n\nFrom:        The Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo:          Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LTML, U. S. Navy.\nVia:         (1) Commander, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n             (2) Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\n                 Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubject:     Change of duty.\n\nReference:   (a) Bureau dispatch to Com 14, 131707Z of Oct.\n             1947.\n\n     1.      Reference (a) is quoted for your information and\ncompliance:\n\n     \"LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE LINE 177283 WHEN DIRECTED BY THE SUPPLY\n     OFFICER IN COMMAND NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER PEARL HARBOR TH IN OCTOBER\n     1947 DETACHED FROM DUTY AT THE NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT NAVAL\n     SUPPLY CENTER PEARL HARBOR TH AND FROM SUCH OTHER DUTY AS MAY\n     HAVE BEEN ASSIGNED X PROCEED AND REPORT TO THE COMMANDER AIR FORCE\n     US PACIFIC FLEET FOR DUTY X A DELAY OF FIFTEEN DAYS IN REPORTING\n     IN COMPLIANCE WITH THESE ORDERS IS AUTHORIZED X PROVIDED NO EXCESS\n     LEAVE IS INVOLVED X DELAY TO COUNT AS LEAVE X KEEP BUREAU AND\n     NEW STATION ADVISED OF ADDRESS X\"\n\n     2.      Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance\nwith these orders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed\nto forward to the Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new commanding\nofficer a copy of these orders complete with all endorsements thereto,\nincluding the final reporting endorsement.\n\n\n                                   THOS. H. BINFORD,\n                                   By direction.\n\nCC: Papers\n    CNO (OP 54)\n    ComServPac\n    ComAirPac\n    Com N.B 14th", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "81e97d4a29934d2260d2ee4442b360e7ac7aa7d541fc5552acb4706121936edb", "output_sha256": "81e97d4a29934d2260d2ee4442b360e7ac7aa7d541fc5552acb4706121936edb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:05.901479+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p213", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 213, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\n                    Aviation Supply Depot\nSHIP OR STATION  Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H.     DATE    17 October 1947\n\nFROM:  Supply Officer in Command\n                              COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n         REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n\n     IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME      NEWHOUSE,          Delbert            C.                   FILE No. 177283\n              LAST                FIRST              MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS  Lieutenant, USN                                      SIGNAL No.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF                                                       DATED\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n\n     (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME              Two          G-2\n\n     (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n          TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n          EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n          VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE.....................................\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE    0815 - 10/14/47              EXPIRING DATE  2115 - 10/16/47\n\nLeave credit as indicated on\nOfficers Leave Record, [REDACTED] days.                SIGNED\n             48                                                H. J. P. FOLLI\n                                                                    COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n     1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n     2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n     3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.                                   16—33335-2    U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1850b700211f03dc982e5fa6082cfda7f9734c5385c379272f42f0f1df9ac06e", "output_sha256": "fc9428b453bf998560c8df1450d4694f011afe3f0d7996e6136e83e11d2a00c4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:08.707694+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p214", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 214, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "23 October 1947.\n\nFrom:        Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, LINE, U. S. Navy,\n             (0177283).\nTo   :       The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nVia  :       The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nSubject:     Compliance with orders - Report of.\n\nReference:   (a) BuPers CircLtr 44-47\n\nEnclosure:   (A) Orders of subject officer with FIRST, SECOND,\n                 THIRD, AND FOURTH endorsements thereto.\n\n     1.     In accordance with reference (a), enclosure (A) is\nforwarded herewith.\n\n                                   Delbert C. NEWHOUSE.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nFU/FF12/P16-4/00/          UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n60:ac                           Air Force\n                         UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial: 1240                                    OCT 24 1947\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT:\n\nFrom:        The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo   :       The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n     1.      Forwarded.\n\n                                   J. C. CRONIN.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8fe98a4224ca8906a0