ACIFIC FLEET\n                              Air Force\n                        UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial: 092-47\n\n                                        23 October 1947.\n\nFOURTH ENDORSEMENT on\nCom-14 Orders Serial\n15809 dated 10-14-47.\n\n\nFrom:          The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :          Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, LINE, U.S. Navy,\n                    (0177283).\n\nSubject:       Change of Duty.\n\n        1.      You reported this date for duty on the Staff of the\nCommander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\n\n\n\n                                        J. C. CRONIN.\n\nCopy to:\n        CNO (OP-54)\n        ComServPac\n        Com-14\n        ComNAB 14ND\n        ComNavBase Pearl\n        ComFair, West Coast\n        ComAirPac", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2c80aa246d62eec750ca4df127cb28817b7332ead4d029aee563ee8b8ec815b7", "output_sha256": "e350e08b008e5b185eed1848d78b8c6c3dc0a5bddbdb20a6248742ddc5141294", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:13.105238+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p217", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 217, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "COMMANDER AIR FORCE\nUNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n\nFF12-5/P16-4/00\n611-sn\n\n\n\nTHIRD ENDORSEMENT on\nCom-14 Orders Serial\n15809 dated 10-14-47.                    23 OCT 1947\n\n\nFrom:          Commander Air Force, Pacific Fleet.\nTo  :          Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, Line, U.S. Navy, (177283).\n\nSubject:       Change of Duty.\n\n          1.   You reported to Commander Air Force, Pacific Fleet on 23\nOctober 1947.  You will proceed immediately and report to Commander Utility\nWing, Pacific Fleet for duty on his staff.\n\n          2.   No transportation is necessary in the execution of these\norders.\n\n\n\n\nCopy to:                                    J. D. PRICE.\n          CNO (OP-54)\n          ComServPac\n          Com-14\n          ComNAB 14ND\n          ComNavBase Pearl\n          ComFairWestCoast", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c03fc9540d4a2452fafbd9c139777b27f3ace96f2a073e2207fdb0ebe971792a", "output_sha256": "c03fc9540d4a2452fafbd9c139777b27f3ace96f2a073e2207fdb0ebe971792a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:14.341320+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p218", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 218, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OO/NEWHOUSE D C                    NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR, T. H.\n(177283)                           FNB-2 on Com14 Ords Ser 15809 dtd 14 Oct 47\n\n22 October 1947\n\nFrom:   Supply Officer in Command\nTo  :   Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, U. S. Navy\n\nSubj:   Change of Duty\n\n1.      Delivered and detached this date.\n\n\n                              W. V. FOX\n\ncc:\nCNO (OP 54)\nComServPac\nComAirPac\nComNAB 14HD\nCom14\nComNavBase Pearl", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7e48ef34eba55999b4ead3a3401a5d4b6a1b0ec2d684f5dcdb086917bf00bf69", "output_sha256": "7e48ef34eba55999b4ead3a3401a5d4b6a1b0ec2d684f5dcdb086917bf00bf69", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:15.507199+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p219", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 219, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "15443\n\nCO/HENHOUSE, D. C.\n(177283)60B/gft\n\n15 Oct 1947\n\nEncl-1 on ComIA orders\nSer 15809 dtd 14 Oct 47.\n\nFrom:        Commander, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo  :        Lieutenant Delbert C. HENHOUSE, Line, U. S. Navy\nVia :        Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\n             Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubj:        Change of Duty\n\n     1.      Forwarded for compliance when directed by the\nSupply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor,\nT. H., in October 1947.\n\n\n\n\n                         E. W. HANSON\n\n\n\n\ncc:  CNO (OP 54)\n     Comservpac\n     ComAirPac\n     ComNAB 14ND\n     ComIA", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e8a2e35e5d83bb7a7349fb1634c6daa04d6a58a2e99db58b150cbcfab6f9cd0c", "output_sha256": "3cb44ec6f48c818e84d50738e6d58fae1a6f957c168a56f1695c9053a1f596e7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:16.865894+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p220", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 220, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OC/Newhouse, C.\n(177283/1100)\n\n                                                           15443\n\nSerial No. 15809\n\n14 October 1947\n\nFrom:        The Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo:          Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LTJG, U. S. Navy.\nVia:         (1) Commander, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n             (2) Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\n                 Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubject:     Change of duty.\n\nReference:   (a) Buers dispatch to Com 14, 1317072 of Oct.\n                 1947.\n\n     1.      Reference (a) is quoted for your information and\ncompliance:\n\n     \"LT DELBERT C NEWHOUSE LINE 177283 WHEN DIRECTED BY THE SUPPLY\n     OFFICER IN COMMAND NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER PEARL HARBOR TH IN OCTOBER\n     1947 DETACHED FROM DUTY AT THE NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT NAVAL\n     SUPPLY CENTER PEARL HARBOR TH AND FROM SUCH OTHER DUTY AS MAY\n     HAVE BEEN ASSIGNED X PROCEED AND REPORT TO THE COMMANDER AIR FORCE\n     US PACIFIC FLEET FOR DUTY X A DELAY OF FIFTEEN DAYS IN REPORTING\n     IN COMPLIANCE WITH THESE ORDERS IS AUTHORIZED PROVIDED NO EXCESS\n     LEAVE IS INVOLVED X DELAY TO COUNT AS LEAVE X KEEP BUPERS AND\n     NEW STATION ADVISED OF ADDRESS X\"\n\n     2.      Immediately upon reporting for duty in compliance\nwith these orders, or any modifications thereto, you are hereby directed\nto forward to the Chief of Naval Personnel, via your new commanding\nofficer a copy of these orders complete with all endorsements thereto,\nincluding the final reporting endorsement.\n\n\n                                        THOS. H. BINFORD,\n                                        By direction.\n\ncc: Bupers\n    CNO (OP 54)\n    ComServPac\n    ComAirPac\n    Com N.B 14HD", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0ec25567fc1840de286689239de8cfc01aa228f1b8dde16d6d3403ce4ddd8470", "output_sha256": "0ec25567fc1840de286689239de8cfc01aa228f1b8dde16d6d3403ce4ddd8470", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:18.966250+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p221", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 221, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\n                    Aviation Supply Depot\nSHIP OR STATION_   Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor          DATE  1 August 1947\n\nFROM:     SUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\n                              COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n         [ILLEGIBLE] ABSENCE OR ABSENCE.\n\n         IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME          NEWHOUSE,          Delbert          Clement          FILE NO.  177283\n               LAST               FIRST             MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS    Lieutenant, USN                               SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF                                                  DATED\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n      (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME           Ten\n\n      (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n          TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n          EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n          VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE....................................\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE    21 July 1947                   EXPIRING DATE     31 July 1947\n\nLeave credit remaining as indicated\non Officers Leave Record, 25 days      SIGNED    H. E. F. FOLEY\n                                                           COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n   1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n   2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n   3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.\n                                                                    16—33385-2    U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fbd360d5a6e2b69cd2a88e617342e31a70ba0ac4bda5bef861ea1c71b17f2dff", "output_sha256": "7e227b9717dccab8e0da5332b8bdf889e2920d882efcfda743b2beeb10352088", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:21.756632+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p222", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 222, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF BENEFICIARIES                    7\nNAVPERS-601 (1-45)\n[X] OFFICER    [ ] ENLISTED         1 May 1947\n\nNEWHOUSE          Delbert        Clement\n  (Last name)          (First)        (Middle)\n\n177283                    Lt., USN\n(File or service number)      (Rank or rate and classification)\n\nU.S. Aviation Supply Depot, NSC, P.H., T.H.\n                    (Ship or station)\n   To carry out the provisions of the acts approved 4 June 1920, 22 May\n1928, 12 May 1930, and 17 March 1941, and acts amendatory thereof\ndirecting the payment of 6 months' pay to the widow, children, or dependent\nrelative of any of the personnel on the active list of the regular Navy, or\non the retired list when on active duty, or of any of the personnel of the\nNaval Reserve called or ordered into active naval service by the Federal\nGovernment for extended naval service in excess of 30 days, who dies\nof wounds or disease not the result of his or her own misconduct, I give\nbelow the name and address of my wife or husband and those of each of my\nchildren:\n\n            Norma Isobel Newhouse\n        (Full name of wife or husband; if not married, so state)\n\n        412  3rd St., NHA#1, Honolulu, T.H.\n                    (Address of wife or husband)\n\n        Delbert Carroll Newhouse          6/28/38\n        (Full name of child; if none, so state)      (Date of birth)\n\n        412  3rd St., NHA#1, Honolulu, T.H.\n                      (Address of child)\n\n        Anne Lisbet Newhouse              3/14/40\n             (Full name of child)              (Date of birth)\n\n        412  3rd St., NHA#1, Honolulu, T.H.\n                      (Address of child)\n\n____________________________              ________________\n        (Full name of child)                    (Date of birth)\n\n____________________________\n                (Address of child)\n\n  In the event that I am not survived by a wife (or husband) or child, or\nin the event of their decease prior to payment and collection of the gratuity,\nI then designate the following person as my dependent beneficiary under\nthe act:*\n\n            Edith May Richter\n                  (Name in full)\n\n            G.D., Garibaldi, Oregon\n                     (Address)\n\n            Mother\n                  (Relationship)\n\n  In the event of the death of the above-named beneficiary before payment\nand collection of the gratuity, I then designate the following person as my\ndependent beneficiary under the act:*\n\n____________________________\n              (Name in full)\n\n____________________________\n                 (Address)\n\n____________________________\n               (Relationship)\n\n  *The acts state that death gratuity must be paid to the surviving wife (or\nhusband) or children, if any. In the event of leaving no wife or children,\nit may then be paid to a designated dependent beneficiary. Every member\nof the service, whether married or not, should designate a beneficiary\n(and an alternate, in case of prior death of the primary beneficiary). Failure\nto make such designation may result in nonpayment of the gratuity.\nSuch designation does not affect payment to a surviving wife (or husband)\nor children.                                        06-16-43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "13b19f7c73b6fcca288f13aebc948350be32ea8ee5041923639d75b5b42a658a", "output_sha256": "9b9af60d79e29b71c35d0a4568f755c0358e050785e7cc90c00d092d7655d4e2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:26.284715+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p223", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 223, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "8\n\nI CERTIFY that I will inform the Bureau of Naval Personnel via my commanding officer immediately of any changes in marital status, or conditions of dependency, or of voluntary occupancy of public quarters by my dependents.\n\nI CERTIFY that there has been no change in condition of dependency between _________________________ and current date.\n         (Date of last report of beneficiaries)\n\n• I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that the facts stated and disclosed in the foregoing are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n          [Signature: D.C. Newhouse]\n                    (Signature)\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this  28th\n\nday of    April          , 1947, I having authority\nto administer oaths.\n\n   [Signature: K.A. Grahn],    Cdr, SC, USN\n        (Signature)                   (Rank)\n\n\n                        INSTRUCTIONS\n\n   This form must be sworn to before an officer of the\nUnited States Navy authorized to administer oaths, or\nbefore a notary public.\n\n   The full names and addresses of the beneficiaries must\nbe stated carefully. If a married woman, her own given\nname should be stated; thus: \"Mrs. Anna May Smith,\" not\n\"Mrs. John Smith.\"\n\n   This slip shall be made out and handled as follows:\n   Officer, Navy: Forward to Bureau of Naval Personnel.\n   Nurse: Forward to Bureau of Medicine and Surgery.\n\n   Enlisted men, Navy: In duplicate; one copy to Bureau\nof Naval Personnel, one copy secured inside service record. In cases of men entitled to money allowances for\nquarters for enlisted men with dependents, two additional\ncopies, bearing the required certificate, to the Disbursing\nOfficer.\n\n   New beneficiary slips shall be executed and forwarded\nas above in all cases of change in status of the grantor or\nin that of his or her beneficiaries.\n\n   In any event, payment will be made to the widow or\nchildren, if any, whether designated or not.\n\n   Normally casualty notification will be sent to all the\nbeneficiaries designated on this form. If, by reason of\nunusual circumstances, other special arrangements are\ndesired, a statement should be attached setting forth\nfull instructions including full names, addresses, and\nrelationships.\n\n\n          U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE     c6-16—43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "50d3a729ff3f54bb23246cc306ad3e545de12b09c307531a39c0da4b1ef1d775", "output_sha256": "fb0a01a61bc0cb701b38c44da9268dc854d158bf3b57c6da7e32282773ca1141", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:28.736936+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p224", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 224, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Address Reply to\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\nand refer to:\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                      Naval Supply Center\n                       Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n19 November 1946\n                                                          C-1\n\nFrom:  LT Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN (177283)\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nAttn:  Pers-3122\nVia:   Supply Officer in Command\n                                                          LAP-\nSubj:  Retention on Active Duty in Commissioned Status    6/48\n\nRef:   (a)  AlNav 588-46\n       (b)  My Acceptance and Oath of Office, 25 September 1946\n\n1.  It is requested that I be retained on active duty in a\ncommissioned status until 30 June 1948 or longer.\n\n2.  By reference (b) I accepted a permanent appointment as\nChief Photographer, USN, and acknowledged receipt of notice\nof appointment to the rank of Lieutenant in the Navy for\ntemporary service.\n\n\n                              D. C. Newhouse\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nP16-3/00\nNT4-93(3:KAG:nlw)\n\nSerial: 4763                              1 9 NOV 1946\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nAttn:  Pers-3122\n\n1.  Forwarded, recommending approval.\n\n                                               Pers 31266\n                              K. A. GRAHN\n\ncc:  Com-14 (Officer Personnel Section)\n     SOinC NSC PH\n                                               FINISHED FILE\n                                               PERS 82232\n\n\n\n\nForm No.-NSC-43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3db41477dd1a5be7105a0e68a6f6beed39ba1f0474fddeaef34d297713ddbd45", "output_sha256": "f48b6eb9b6e9289eaf901c345bf534813cb9d50d56c989c5557a98469aaa0c63", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:30.662882+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p225", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 225, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Address Reply to\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\nand refer to:\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                       Naval Supply Center\n                        Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n19 November 1946\n\n\nFrom:  LT Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN (177283)\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nAttn:  Pers-3122\nVia:   Supply Officer in Command\n\nSubj:  Retention on Active Duty in Commissioned Status\n\nRef:   (a)  AlNav 588-46\n       (b)  My Acceptance and Oath of Office, 25 September 1946\n\n1.  It is requested that I be retained on active duty in a\ncommissioned status until 30 June 1948 or longer.\n\n2.  By reference (b) I accepted a permanent appointment as\nChief Photographer, USN, and acknowledged receipt of notice\nof appointment to the rank of Lieutenant in the Navy for\ntemporary service.\n\n\n\n\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nP16-3/00\nNT4-93(3:KAG:nlw)\n\nSerial:  4763                              19 NOV 1946\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nAttn:  Pers-3122\n\n1.  Forwarded, recommending approval.\n\n\n\n\n                              K. A. GRAHN\n\ncc:  Com14 (Officer Personnel Section)\n     SOinC NSC PH\n                                                FINISHED FILE\n                                                 PERS 82232\n\n\nForm No.-NSC-43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3b7ea9b132e25aa50fc2bcca6419ca6141c5262e0c1cddc53233b600513de47a", "output_sha256": "3b7ea9b132e25aa50fc2bcca6419ca6141c5262e0c1cddc53233b600513de47a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:32.606617+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p226", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 226, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Co/Newhouse, D.C.                    NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR, T.H.\n(177283)\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on ComLA Ords          26 February 1947\nserial 5014 dtd 25 Feb 1947\n\nFrom:      Supply Officer in Command\nTo :       Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\nVia :      SOinC, Aviation Supply Depot\n\nSubj:      Authorization to travel.\n\n     1.    Delivered.\n\n\n                              E. R. BRIGHTON\n                              By direction\n\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComNavBase\n    ComLA", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "79c7b808f9e25f2b2d9c9ce8a2b95521178484a09b40cd6777dd1a0d023c3d08", "output_sha256": "0fb906613e0e814d5dd3b0e836470ad545d5b2b57c8ef0d60b2950eb8213a466", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:34.564923+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p227", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 227, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Address Reply to\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\nand refer to:\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                       Naval Supply Center\n                       Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n\n                                              4 April 1947\n\n\n                              V/c.\n\nFrom:  Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN (177283)\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers 3216A), Navy\n       Department, Washington 25, D.C.\n\nSubj:  Claim for Unused Leave, Request for information concerning\n\n1.  On 25 November 1946 my claim for unused leave\nwas forwarded to the Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers\n3216A) by my commanding officer.  In January 1947\nthe claim was returned for correction of minor\nerrors; required corrections were made, and all\npapers were returned to the Bureau of Personnel\nthe same month.\n\n2.  To date I have not been advised by BuPers either\nthat my claim has been forwarded to the Terminal\nLeave Disbursing Office or that further correction\nof the claim is necessary.  Information concerning\naction taken by the Bureau in processing the claim\nwould be appreciated.\n\n\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\n15 April 1947                              [ILLEGIBLE] File Pers 3216A\n\n\nForm No.-NSC-43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "974eea9e1c40c8adad1106f8f6ab468bfa522259eda14abc6f3b1783aaa5ad6f", "output_sha256": "d0367d4e7e88692e2f6012f430a8c680daa2fea18ccdec6bc0a56891deb09de7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:36.195493+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p228", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 228, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Address Reply to\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\n    and refer to:\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                       Naval Supply Center\n                       Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n\n                                          4 April 1947\n\n\nFrom:  Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN (177283)\n  To:  Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers 3216A), Navy\n       Department, Washington 25, D.C.\n\nSubj:  Claim for Unused Leave, Request for information\n       concerning\n\n1.  On 25 November 1946 my claim for unused leave\nwas forwarded to the Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers\n3216A) by my commanding officer.  In January 1947\nthe claim was returned for correction of minor\nerrors; required corrections were made, and all\npapers were returned to the Bureau of Personnel\nthe same month.\n\n2.  To date I have not been advised by BuPers either\nthat my claim has been forwarded to the Terminal\nLeave Disbursing Office or that further correction\nof the claim is necessary.  Information concerning\naction taken by the Bureau in processing the claim\nwould be appreciated.\n\n\n                         D. C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nForm No. NSC-43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "de13b335b420b4cc71e4684ba55604b8edaa3b91813099b5c6ca8edb80eafbcf", "output_sha256": "1284f3f09a23919283b14064acdba7948841b049fb8e051810358c8150e5e6b0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:37.714557+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p229", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 229, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CC/Newhouse, D. C.\n(177283)\n\nSerial No. 314\n\n2 February 1947\n\nFrom:    The Commandant, Fourteenth Naval District.\nTo  :    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U. S. Navy.\nVia :    ScinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H.    C-1\n\nSubj:    Authorization to travel.\n\n1.       When directed by the Supply Officer in Command, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., on or about 28 February 1947,\nyou are authorized to proceed to the island of Maui, T. H., and\nupon arrival report to the Commanding Officer, Naval Air Station,\nKahului, Maui, T. H., for temporary duty in connection with\nprocessing Naval Air Station requisitions backlog. This is in\naddition to your present duties, and upon completion thereof,\nand when directed by the Commanding Officer, Naval Air Station,\nKahului, Maui, T. H., return to your station and resume your\npresent duties.\n\n2.       Except where other means of authorized travel are equally\nor more expeditious, travel by government air is directed and is\nnecessary for the successful accomplishment of an essential or\nemergency mission. For transportation via Naval Air Transport\nService aircraft, Class THREE priority is hereby certified.\n\n3.       No expense to the government is authorized in the execution\nof this authorization. In case you do not desire to bear this expense\nyou will regard this authorization as revoked.\n\n\n\n                                        J. I. HALL, JR.\n\ncc:  Rulers\n     Comdt., NavBase, Pearl\n\n\n\n                              FINISHED FILE PERS 3161", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c2af942f1f448bf0b7fa77d0212878ca40b0ee8a04cc7e6eab5c8b7e33d9dcda", "output_sha256": "450bdb8840acc06228caf910b1cf230c80ca2371d5342c4d1824196f5a05014d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:39.543187+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p230", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 230, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OO/Newhouse, D.C.                    NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR, T.H.\n(177283)\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on Com14 Ords          26 February 1947\nserial 3014 dtd 26 Feb 1947\n\nFrom:    Supply Officer in Command\nTo  :    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\nVia :    SOinC, Aviation Supply Depot\n\nSubj:    Authorization to travel.\n\n     1.    Delivered.\n\n\n                                   E. E. BRIGHTON\n                                   By direction\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComNavBase\n    Com14\n\n* - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nOO/Newhouse, D.C.               AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT, PEARL HARBOR, T.H.\n(177283)\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on Com14 Ords         27 February 1947\nserial 3014 dtd 26 Feb 1947\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\n\nSubj:  Authorization to travel\n\n1.  Delivered.\n\n\n                                   K. A. GRAHN\n\ncc:  BuPers\n     ComNavBase\n     Com14\n     SOinC, NSC PH\n\n\n                                             FINISHED FILE PERS 3163", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1c9ffe8f2e160fb336f59db9dbf557805e881c39061265e5d4ab6b9d61174599", "output_sha256": "1c9ffe8f2e160fb336f59db9dbf557805e881c39061265e5d4ab6b9d61174599", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:42.211842+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p231", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 231, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "7283\n\nNA114/P16-4/00          U. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\nON3/WHH/esa             KAHULUI, MAUI, T. H.\n\n                                        C-2\n                                    Mc823\n\nEnd-3    28 February 1947.\nFrom:    The Commanding Officer.\nTo :     Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U. S. Navy.\n\nSubj:    Authorization to travel.\n                                        11 MAR 1947\n1.       Reported for temporary additional duty this date.\n\n2.       Temporary additional duty completed this date.  Carry out\nremainder of basic orders.\n\n\n                        T. J. HEDDING.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEND-4 on Com14 Ords serial              AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n3014 dtd 26 Feb 1947                         PEARL HARBOR\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command           28 February 1947\nTo:    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U. S. Navy\n\n1.  Returned from temporary additional duty this date.\n\n\n                        K. A. GRAHN\n\ncc:  BuPers\n     ComNavBase\n     Com14\n     SOinC NSC PH", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dd5bedbe6427ba71e907759adea5129c66bf6280006947d7c385750afcb4e69d", "output_sha256": "dd5bedbe6427ba71e907759adea5129c66bf6280006947d7c385750afcb4e69d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:43.961564+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p232", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 232, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BNP 321 REVISED F[ILLEGIBLE]  943\n\nREPORT OF LEAVE OR ABSENCE  See Instructions Below\n\nShip or Station  Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Phila., Pa Date  25 April 1946\n\nFrom:     Supply Officer in Command\n                        Commanding Officer\n\nTO:       Bureau of Naval Personnel, Navy Department\n\nSUBJ:     REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n          REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n\n          In conformity with requirements of U. S. NAVY regulations, I report\nthe following leave of absence taken by:\n\nNAME       NEWHOUSE          Delbert          C          File No.    177283\n           Last              First            Middle\n\nRANK AND CORPS    Lieut. USN                       SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF   SOinC 1st endorsement            DATED   11 April 1946\n\nNOTE:     Use either (A) or (B).  DO NOT use both for same leave.\n\n  (A)     LEAVE: Total number of days, including any travel time    2 Days\n\n  (B)     Delay counting as leave or leave between stations.\n          Total number of days, excluding preparation period\n          of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel time\n          from old to new station via shortest usually traveled\n          route.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInsert inclusive dates to agree with number of days leave.\nSee instructions below.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE  16 April 1946             EXPIRING DATE   17 April 1946\n\n                                                        W. D. SAMS.\nBy direction of SOinC:                     SIGNED  Lieut. SC USN\n                                                   Military Personnel Officer\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n        The day of departure from station or duty counts as a day of duty;\n        the day of return as a day of leave.  This refers to leave taken when not\n        on ship or station (See ARTICLE 1727, Navy Regulations).\n\n        For authorized delay counting as leave, this form should\n        be used in addition to the B-slip Form.\n\n        This report should be made at expiration of leave by the immediate\n        commanding officer from the leave is granted and forwarded\n        to the Department (Bureau of Naval Personnel).  Care\n        should be taken that correct number of days leave is reported and\n        correct inclusive dates reported.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8dca67ad4a1ea259a004b570359eb11047e8c5e131afef1f557f712e7a4c6e79", "output_sha256": "c5244f1201648bb0b7ea8ba959abf961f23042aa88c7aba7c2c51123ca95aa4d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:46.475099+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p233", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 233, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Standard Form No. 1012a—Revised\nFORM APPROVED BY U. S.\nCOMPTROLLER GENERAL, U. S.\nJuly 19, 1937 (Amended Aug. 27, 1941)\nGeneral Regulations No. 88\n\nVOUCHER FOR PER DIEM AND/OR REIMBURSEMENT OF\nEXPENSES INCIDENT TO OFFICIAL TRAVEL\n\nD. O. Vou. No. 278-47\nBureau No.\n\n(Statement of account must be completely filled in by payee prior to signature, and there must not be any erasure or alteration unless initialed or signed by him)\n\nGeneral Accounting Office\nPREAUDIT\nCertified for payment in the\nsum of $\nCOMPTROLLER GENERAL OF\nTHE UNITED STATES\nBy\n\nU. S. NAVY DEPARTMENT\n(Department, bureau, or establishment)\nTHE UNITED STATES, Dr., To Delbert C. Newhouse, Lt.\n(Payee) SC, USN\nAviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor.\n(Address)\nOfficial Headquarters c/o FPO San Francisco, California\n(Address)\nDomicile Residence\n(For use of Postal Service only)\n\nPAID BY\nPEARL HARBOR\n(804)\n23 DEC 1946\nC. E. SULLIVAN\n(For use of Paying Office)\n\nAMOUNT\nDOLLARS CENTS\n\nFOR PER DIEM in lieu of subsistence, mileage for privately owned motor vehicle, and/or REIMBURSEMENT\nof travel and other expenses paid by me in the discharge of official duty from August 21, 1946,\nto Nov. 27, 1946, as per itemized statement within, under authority No. FILE 3161-JMO-1A, dated August 7,\n1946, copy of which is attached,* or has been previously furnished with voucher No., paid\n19, by\n(Name of disbursing officer)\n$ 254.32\n\n(Payee will NOT use this space)\nDifferences\n\nAccount verified correct for $\n(Signature or initials)\n\nFINISHED\nOFFICERS\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nACCOUNTING CLASSIFICATION (For completion by administrative office)\n\nAPPROPRIATION, LIMITATION\nOR PROJECT SYMBOL | APPROPRIATION TITLE | LIMITATION OR PROJECT AMOUNT | APPROPRIATION AMOUNT\n\n1770813 | TRNP 1947 74110 | $ | $254.32\n\nALLOTMENT SYMBOL | AMOUNT | ENCUMBRANCE LIQUIDATED | COST ACCOUNT Symbol | COST ACCOUNT Amount | OBJECT OF EXPENDITURE Symbol | OBJECT OF EXPENDITURE Amount\n\n$\n\n$\n\n$\n\nPaid by { Check No., dated, 19, for $ on Treasurer of the United States\n          in favor of payee named above.\n         { Cash, $254.32, on 23 Dec, 1946 SIGN ORIGINAL ONLY Delbert C. Newhouse, Lt. SC, USN\n(Signature of payee)\n\n*If there was no prior authority state circumstances which rendered securing prior authority impracticable. 16—23954-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0e119e0e29aa81d80902980fc0741ac97f0e3cdebdd830a0e52a23af7da3d7db", "output_sha256": "e3e755e91915ffe7ffb56b73cdb5779e12674867dbf4ed0fb626f3647442298d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:49.888076+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p234", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 234, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "ITEMIZED SCHEDULE OF TRAVEL AND OTHER EXPENSES\n\n1. Date and hour of departure from official headquarters ----------------------------------------- ----------------\n                                                                                    (Date)              (Hour)\n2. Give duty status on first day of voucher period:\n   *Arrived at ----------------------------------- on ----------------------------------, 19------,\n   for temporary duty for approximate period -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n   Approximate date of return to official headquarters ----------------------------------------, 19------\n3. †State authorized per diem in lieu of subsistence, $------------------\n4. †State authorized allowance for actual subsistence expenses: Not to exceed $----------------- per day.\n5. Where for traveler's personal convenience or through the taking of leave there is interruption of travel, deviation\n   from the direct route, or where traveler delays at a place other than post of duty, a statement showing the facts\n   should appear on the voucher.\n\n*If authority provides for travel to more than one point, time of arrival and departure from each should be stated in the body of the account in chronological order.\n†If more than one rate of allowance is authorized, full statement of application of each rate must be given in some convenient place on this voucher.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDATE  |                    CHARACTER OF EXPENDITURE                    | SUB- |        AMOUNT        | NOTATIONS\n1946  |              (To be itemized by the day and fully explained)    | VOU. |---------------------|  (Payee must not\n      |                                                                 | NO.** | SUBSISTENCE | OTHER |  use this column)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nReimbursement for cost of transportation of my dependents\nwife and children on permanent change of duty from Aviation\nSupply Depot, Phila Pa. to Aviation Supply Depot, P.H.\n\nI certify that Norman I. Newhouse is my lawful wife, and\nthat Delbert Carroll Newhouse, and Anne Lisbet Newhouse,\nage 8 and 6 years, male and female born June 25, 1938\nand March 14, 1940 are my legitimate children.\n\nI, Delbert C. Newhouse certify that Delbert Carroll Newhouse\nand Anne Lisbet Newhouse are my legitimate children, will\nbe 9 and 7 years of age at next birthday, and are members\nof my household; that said children are not possessed of\nproperty or income adequate for their support and education;\nthat they are not the beneficiary, either directly or\nthrough others, of any trust or estate entitling their\nincome adequate for their support and education; that\nsaid children are in fact now and at all times solely\ndependent on me; that in all respects I maintain the\nchildren at my own expense and from my own resources\nand am not reimbursed therefor directly or indirectly in\nany manner or form whatsoever, and that evidence of the\nchildren's dependency upon me and my maintenance of them\nhave been filed with my pay accounts and is hereby made\na part hereof.\n\nI certify that the location of my dependents named herein\non August 7, 1946 the date I received my orders was\nPhiladelphia, Pa.\n\nTravel of dependents named herein was made from Phila\nPa. to San Francisco, California.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c32a13c640a2c87dc45dc7eef84ebd112ed3c3f9982812da44fe7aba10f0b66f", "output_sha256": "8170b98fab7e9a2dc2d131f4f34d3382124e08d7fe9956092178d2f990f98631", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:52.841903+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p235", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 235, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Departed:    Phila Pa. on August 21, 1946\nArrived:    Garibaldi, Oregon on Aug. 27, 1946\n             ( Privately owned automobile )\n\nDeparted:    Garibaldi, Oregon on Nov. 26, 1946\nArrived:     San Francisco, Calif. on Nov. 27, 1946\n             ( Commercial transportation )\n\nPhiladelphia Pa. to San Francisco, California - 3079 miles\n v. 27    (O.M.T. TM 14-510 page 356-)\n     3079 miles - - - - - - - @ 4¢ per mile                          127.16\n     3079 miles - - - - - - - @ 2¢ per mile                           63.58\n     3079 miles - - - - - - - @ 2¢ per mile                           63.58\n                    TOTAL CLAIMED:    $254.32\n\nAbove travel was performed by private conveyance and\ncommercial transportation.\n\nI certify that all travel performed by my dependents\nwas at my own expense, no portion thereof being made\nby Government conveyance or transportation requests.\n\nThe reimbursement requested herein is in accordance\nwith paragraph 3 of the Secretary of the Navy's\nLetter of 23 Dec. 1943.\n\nI hereby designate San Francisco, California as the\npoint to which travel is desired.\n\nI hereby certify that the above account is just and\ntrue in all respects and that the penalties for\npresenting a false claim are known to me.\n\nI certify, except as noted hereon, that no prior\nclaim has been presented by me or any member of my\nfamily for the reimbursement for transportation of\ndependents as claimed herein that no transportation in\nkind has been furnished therefor.\n\n\n                    Delbert C. Newhouse\n                       Lt. SC, USN\n\n\nTOTALS (to be carried forward to continuation sheet, if necessary)\n\nTOTAL AMOUNT OF VOUCHER (not to be used when totals are carried forward to continuation sheet)\n\n**When subvouchers required by regulations were not obtained, state fully the circumstances showing reason for omission.                                    16-23054-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c0ba56edbea3fb31747c90d1d758b110f0ea3f8ead0b0b2291d6c280a12f307e", "output_sha256": "1d6c54f03f572a9a88d4755cb81123e1e3e953cbfef311879594088fd43df7bc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:55.376211+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p236", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 236, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "STATEMENT OF TRAVEL PERFORMED FOR WHICH REIMBURSEMENT IS NOT CLAIMED\nBY TRAVELER\n\nDATE OF\nTRAVEL | NO. OF TRANS-\nPORTATION\nREQUEST OR\nSPEEDOMETER\nREADING | FROM— | TO— | VIA\n(Kind of carrier\nor vehicle)* | CLASS OR\nMILEAGE† | AMOUNT\n\n[Table body is blank/empty with bleed-through text from reverse side, not legible]\n\n*Railroad, steamship, airplane, bus, etc.\n†Abbreviate class of service or accommodations used. Railroad: F, first class; I, intermediate class; M, mixed class; O, coach; P, Pullman accommodations; DR, drawing room;\nCP, compartment; BR, bedroom; SOS, single occupancy section; SEC, section; LB, lower berth; UB, upper berth; S, seat. By other mode: Number of miles traveled.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. The provisions of the travel regulations [REDACTED] must be strictly observed in order to avoid suspensions [REDACTED] and disallowances in the accounts.\n2. When more space is required [REDACTED] ization of the account, use continuation sheets [REDACTED] standard forms 1012b—Revised and\n1012c—Revised) and fasten together [REDACTED] left-hand corner.\n3. As many copies of the approved [REDACTED] orandum voucher may be made as required for [REDACTED] erative purposes.\n\nU. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE 16—23954-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "916f95902d7b5745b3128842d42b3bf1d49168026b361159860bc5c5b3ca4c6f", "output_sha256": "a6772849a7e14eee3c5357f0925f4e4618fad839ea12eebe243faeb865c3ad47", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:38:57.318144+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p237", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 237, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply address not [REDACTED]\nsigner of this letter, but    NAVY DEPARTMENT\nBureau of Naval Personnel,    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nNavy Department, Wash. 25, D.C.  WASHINGTON 25, D.C.\nRefer to No. 177283\n                                              [ILLEGIBLE] Depot\n                               12/23/46\n                          Paid [ILLEGIBLE] Per Diem dependent\n                          In Amount of $[ILLEGIBLE] PV#278-47\n                          From: 8/21/46 [ILLEGIBLE] 32\n                          To: 11/27/46\nPers-3161-JMJ-1A                        [Signature] D. F. Sullivan\n                                         D. F. SULLIVAN\n7 August 1946                            ENSIGN SC, USN\n\nFrom:        The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:          Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n             Aviation Supply Depot,\n             Philadelphia, Pa.\n\nVia:         Supply Officer in Command.\n\nSubject:     Change of duty.\n\n    When directed by the Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply\nDepot, you will regard yourself detached from duty at the Aviation\nSupply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa., and from such other duty as may\nhave been assigned you; will proceed to San Francisco, Calif., and\nreport to the Commandant, Twelfth Naval District, for first available\ntransportation to Pearl Harbor, T.H., and upon arrival report to the\nCommandant, Fourteenth Naval District, for duty at the Naval Aviation\nSupply Depot, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n2. You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of five days in\nreporting at San Francisco, Calif., in compliance with these orders\nsuch delay to count as leave.\n\n3. Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel advised of your address.\n\n\n                              /s/ LOUIS DENFELD\n                              LOUIS DENFELD  F.W.B.\n\nCC:\n  ComFour.\n  ComTwelve.\n  CNO (OP512).\n  ComFourteen.\n  ComServPac (2).\n  SupOfComd, NavAviationSupDep,\n    Pearl Harbor, T.H.                        11909\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nStamped on face of Basic Letter:        Certified to be a True Copy\n\nU.S. Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.   [Signature] D C Newhouse\n\n             19 AUG 1946\nAdvanced _____ months pay $300.00 which has been\ncharged on my rolls.\n             /s/ W.D. WRIGHT, Lt. (jg) (SC) USN\n                 Disbursing Officer", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ce92945bd1b10ce7d4da981689ba306f6df3961a0eeb298173da3f3600134924", "output_sha256": "b2f398c311d083e92bb7e027f3ec98b3cbdabf33ac8fc0047966962bd81ce6d4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:01.260687+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p238", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 238, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Stamped on face of Basic Letter:\n\nD-AO---12th N.D. San Francisco, Calif. 9/3/46\nPaid mileage or per diem $238.31    04222-47\nFrom Philadelphia, Pa. To San Francisco, Calif.\n\n          /s/ R E Pel, Deputy\n     For R. E. PRENTICE, COMDR.(SC) USNR 56-310\n\nNOTICE TO ALL OFFICERS ON CHANGE OF STATION\nIn view of the extreme housing shortage in\nall shore establishments it is considered\nhighly inadvisable to move families until\nsuch time as the officer in question has\nreported for duty and obtained suitable\nquarters for his family.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nJacket No. 177283\nEnd-1                    19 AUG 1946          NASD, Phila., Pa.\n\nTo:       Lieut. Delbert C. Newhouse, USN.\n\n1.        Delivered. Detached.\n\nBy direction of SOinC:\n                              /s/ J. A. SINCOCK\n                                  J. A. SINCOCK\n                          Military Personnel Officer\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n18 SEP 1946              DISTRICT STAFF HEADQUARTERS\n                          TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n                          SAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA\n\n                         ________Endorsement\n\n               Reported this date for transportation.\n               You are hereby assigned public quarters in BOQ.\n\n                    /s/ W.L.TAYLOR\n                        W.L.TAYLOR\n                    By direction of the Comdt.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                                             Certified to be a True Copy\n\n                                             Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "14ddd86de2ed3dffcb8914c13a9169dfd1dced8aa59f7ebdcae0568f729acab5", "output_sha256": "7623fa588be96c3360b363e08a292e4d05e1f4d061c20cd4f36f44b9ce0ea8ad", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:03.662549+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p239", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 239, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Office of Commandant\n       TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n       San Francisco 2, California\n\n12th. ND 60tHs\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert C.                    SEP 8 1946\nLt. USN\n177283                                  2nd Endorsement\n\nFrom:   The Commandant, Twelfth Naval District.\nTo:     Lt. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:   Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported 1 Sept. 1946 for transportation.\n\n2.  Detached this date.  You will proceed in accordance with paragraph 3\nand upon arrival at destination will report for duty as directed in basic\norders.\n\n3.  Via government air transportation.  Priority No. C3\n\n4.  The Disbursing Officer, Headquarters 12th. Naval District is authorized\nand directed to furnish you the necessary commercial air transportation from\nSan Francisco, California to Honolulu, T.H., via Pan-American Airways.  Excess baggage in amount      pounds is authorized.  Priority No.     certified\nby Naval Air Priorities Office (NATS)\n\n5.  Vacated public quarters in BOQ this date.\n\n                              /s/ W. L. TAYLOR\n                              W. L. TAYLOR\n                         By direction of the Commandant\n\nCopy to:\n     BuPers.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                         MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\n\n              From:          COMMANDING OFFICER  VR-4\n              To:            Newhouse\n              TRANSPORTATION VIA NAVAL AIR TRANSPORT\n              SERVICE FURNISHED FROM THIS STATION\n\n              TO:       HHL\n              8 Sept 46  /s/ Lt. Cdr. Hawley   Ca\n                              BY DIRECTION\n\n              ARRIVED AT Hon   AT 0825 9/9/46\n\n                    /s/ Lt.(jg) Clements\n                         Signed by ATO   OHG\n\n                                        Certified to be a True Copy\n\n                                        d cnewhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "85fd70281e805ba41d43aa3d374463c7cc3a83823c43cc29ca65aa340725b310", "output_sha256": "41b8ec859d8a6288ff93e9f38805b8efd8665287da81c2c7491c3c4a70caf2df", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:05.949167+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p240", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 240, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "O/Newhouse, D.C.      [REDACTED]4th Naval District, Pearl Harb[REDACTED]H.\n  177283)\n\nEnd-3    Date: 9 SEP 1946\nTo:      Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, U.S. Navy.\nSubj:    Change of duty.\n\n        Reported this date.  You will further report to the Commandant, U.S. Naval\nBase, Pearl Harbor, T.H., for duty at the Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n\n                              /s/ A. A. KNOTEK\n                                  A. A. KNOTEK\n                                  By direction.\n\nc: BuPers\n   ComServPac\n   CNO (op 512)\n   FRO San Fran\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEnd-4      9 September 1946\nFrom:      Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\nTo:        Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, USN.\nSubj:      Change of duty.\n\n   1.      Reported this date.  Further report to Supply Officer in Command,\nNaval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H. for duty at the Naval Aviation Supply\nDepot, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n                              /s/ E. W. HANSON\n                                  E. W. HANSON\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran\n    Com 14\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEnd-5  (on BuPers 3161-JMJ-1A      Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n       dtd 7 Aug 1946)\n\n9 September 1946\n\nFrom:    Supply Officer in Command\nTo:      LT Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, USN\nVia:     SOinC, Aviation Supply Depot, NSC\n\nSubj:    Change of Duty\n\n   1.    Reported this date.  You will further report to the Supply Officer\nin Command, Aviation Supply Depot, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\nfor duty.\n                                           Certified to be a True Copy\n                              /s/ T. M. NEECE\n                                  T. M. NEECE   D C Newhouse\n                                  By direction", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d14ed5ead9bc82da67d0728ded83bea359c6bcaec1bc8c66ffec3cac9e3658e5", "output_sha256": "e62433c4ecee53fff7895d667948841bf440c4d71b3f8ad76c1c858e67fbde9a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:08.691946+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p241", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 241, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "END-6                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT, PEARL HARBOR\n\n9 September 1946\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    LT Delbert C Newhouse LINE USN\n\n1.     Reported this date.\n\n                         /s/ G. M. BRYDON\n                             G. M. BRYDON (  )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                         Certified to be a True Copy\n\n                         D C Newhouse", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "905cb8bca5fc4219f2757b6a5d4e0654499fbc42c95e2e79f3775dbf1f0966ac", "output_sha256": "905cb8bca5fc4219f2757b6a5d4e0654499fbc42c95e2e79f3775dbf1f0966ac", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:09.529562+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p242", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 242, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "S. and A. Form 33\n(Revised May 1941)\n\nAPPLICATION FOR TRANSPORTATION FOR DEPENDENTS\n(See Art. 2505-3 Navy Travel Instructions)\n                                    Aviation Supply Depot,  20 Sept., 1946\n                                    U.S. Pearl Harbor, T.H.,\nFROM: LT D C NEWHOUSE, LINE                              , U.S.N.\nTo:  Bureau of Naval Personnel          Via: Commandant, Fourteenth Naval Dist.\nEnclosures: Three certified copies of orders of BuPers\n           Original and two\n         dated 7 August 1946        , detaching me from duty at (on) NASD Philadelphia\n                    (If change of home yard (port) execute certificate on reverse of this form)\n         and ordering me to permanent duty at (on) ASD Pearl Harbor\n\n1. It is requested that transportation be furnished the following, who were my dependents on the effective date of\nabove orders:\n         Name                 Relationship         Date of birth of        †Location of dependents when\n                                                      children              orders were received\n   Norma I. Newhouse           Wife                                    6148 Oxford Ave.,\n                                                                        Philadelphia, Pa.\n   Delbert C. Newhouse         Son                  6/28/38\n   Anne L. Newhouse            Daughter             3/14/40\nAddress of dependents    Garibaldi, Oregon - c/o Mrs. V. Richter\nFrom San Francisco, Cal. to Pearl Harbor, T.H.        via\nWith stopover at                          (Name place; as, Chicago, 4 days)\nPullman or stateroom accommodations  Stateroom\n                                                 (\"lower berth,\" \"stateroom,\" etc.)\nApproximate time travel is to begin   First available\n\n2. I certify that the [XX] children named above [XX] are my  Legitimate                          [XXX] children\n                                                                  (Legitimate—step—adopted) †\nwill be  9 and 7        years of age, respectively, at next birthday, and [XXXXXXX] are members of my household; that said\n[XXX]\nchildren are not possessed of property or income adequate for [XX] their support and education; that [XXX] they are not the beneficiary,\nor beneficiaries, either directly or through others, of any trust or estate entitling [XX] them to income adequate for [XXX] their support\nand education; that said [XXXXX] children are in fact now and at all times solely dependent on me; that in all respects I maintain the\n[XXX]\nchildren at my own expense and from my own resources and am not reimbursed therefor directly or indirectly in any\nmanner or form whatsoever; *and that evidence of the [XXXXX] children's dependency upon me and my maintenance of [XX] them has\nbeen filed with my pay accounts and is hereby made a part hereof.\n   3. I further certify in the case of my dependent mother that she is in fact dependent on me for her chief support, that\nshe resided with me as a member of my household while at my last permanent duty station, and that an affidavit of evidence\nof dependency, filed                                      , has been accepted by the General Accounting Office for pay purposes.\nI further certify that there has been no change in the conditions of dependency since last filing of affidavit of dependent\nmother.\n   4. I certify that                                                                                    is (are) the child (children)\n                                         (Stepchild—stepchildren)\nof                                                           , who is on this date living, and my lawful wife.\n                         (Name of mother)\n   5. If transportation is furnished as requested above, to a place other than my new duty station, I hereby waive additional transportation for the dependents named herein.\n   6. I certify that I have not made application for transportation for the dependents named in paragraph 1 on this change\nof station except as follows:\n\n   7. I hereby authorize the checking of my personal pay account for any excess cost involved due to transportation furnished in excess of that authorized at Government expense; and hereby agree to accept such checkage in lieu of cash payment prior to issuance of transportation requests.\n                                                                  D.C. Newhouse\nAPPROVED:                                                         (Signature of applicant)\n                                              , U. S. N., Commanding.\n   Approval of commanding officer is required in all cases where it is impracticable or impossible for the applicant to attach original orders.\n                                                                                            13 DEC 1946\n                          OPEC—TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT                    , 19\nThe transportation requested above has been furnished as described on the reverse hereof.\nNo Government transportation available. Furn on USS GEN. RANDALL on 11/27/46.  No rail tran.\nfurn.                                [Signature]\n                                     FOR: A.E. [ILLEGIBLE] (SC) USNR      , U. S. N.\n\n*In the case of officers drawing rental and subsistence allowance with dependents including a wife this clause may be omitted.\n†If adopted children of enlisted men attach authenticated copy of adoption papers signed under seal by the clerk of the court having jurisdiction,\nto be forwarded to the Bureau of Supplies and Accounts. If such copy has been forwarded on a previous change of station reference to such evidence should be furnished.\n  *When orders are received while the dependents are temporarily absent from the old station a statement will be furnished showing necessity for\ndependents returning to the old station prior to proceeding to the new station.                                            File 8