H., in connection with photography.\n\n\n                                    /s/ A. A. KNOTEK\n                                        A. A. KNOTEK\n                                        By direction.\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nInd-4     9 September 1946\nFrom:     Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\nTo:       Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, USN.\nSubj:     Change of duty.\n\n  1.      Reported this date.  Further report to Supply Officer in Command,\nNaval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H. for duty at the Naval Aviation Supply\nDepot, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n                                    /s/ E. W. HANSON\n                                        E. W. HANSON\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran\n    Com 14\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nInd-5 (on BuPers 3161-JMJ-1A       Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n      dtd 7 Aug 1946)\n\n9 September 1946\n\nFrom:     Supply Officer in Command\nTo:       LT Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, USN\nVia:      SOinC, Aviation Supply Depot, NSC\n\nSubj:     Change of Duty\n\n  1.      Reported this date.  You will further report to the Supply Officer\nin Command, Aviation Supply Depot, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\nfor duty.                                       Certified to be a True Copy\n\n                                    /s/ T. M. NEECE\n                                        T. M. NEECE\n                                        By direction\n                                                        Finished File 819", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c625aeb15afa464d325a46bb30fe43a68c385145a0a18d09f5d82085af3c4dfc", "output_sha256": "8cfb9e9680a6a8ae7643eddef3a8369c63584b25a15c6cc97d8e2bb3df323685", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:22.915714+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p245", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 245, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Office of Commandant\n          TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n        San Francisco 2, California\n\n12th. ND 60tHs\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert C.                          SEP 8 1946\nLt. USN\n177283                                         2nd Endorsement\n\nFrom:   The Commandant, Twelfth Naval District.\nTo:     Lt. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:   Change of duty.\n\n1.  Reported 1 Sept. 1946 for transportation.\n\n2.  Detached this date.  You will proceed in accordance with paragraph 3\nand upon arrival at destination will report for duty as directed in basic\norders.\n\n3.  Via government air transportation.  Priority No. C3\n\n4.  The Disbursing Officer, Headquarters 12th. Naval District is authorized\nand directed to furnish you the necessary commercial air transportation from\nSan Francisco, California to Honolulu, T.H., via Pan-American Airways.  Excess baggage in amount     pounds is authorized.  Priority No.    certified\nby Naval Air Priorities Office (NATS)\n\n5.  Vacated public quarters in BOQ this date.\n\n                              /s/ W. L. TAYLOR\n                                  W. L. TAYLOR\n                         By direction of the Commandant\n\nCopy to:\n     BuPers.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                       MEMORANDUM ENDORSEMENT\n\n              From:          COMMANDING OFFICER  VR-4\n              To:            Newhouse\n              TRANSPORTATION VIA NAVAL AIR TRANSPORT\n              SERVICE FURNISHED FROM THIS STATION\n\n              TO:       HHL\n              8 Sept 46  /s/ Lt. Cdr. Hawley   Ca\n                              BY DIRECTION\n\n                                                  Certified to be a True Copy\n              ARRIVED AT Hon   AT 0825 9/9/46\n                                                  D Newhouse\n\n              /s/ Lt.(jg) Clements\n                   Signed by ATO   OHG\n\n                                                    Finished File 812", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a0752b06d1f6c9eb38507d33fe84b94e20670591e87e1bf50202a612f80eec61", "output_sha256": "035a042fd5ceac4b0d3fdcf3d48d1b6288c2b0b8447c852b01c0c90a6a809400", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:25.288013+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p246", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 246, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Stamped on face of Basic Letter:\n\nD-AO----12th N.D. San Francisco, Calif. 9/3/46\nPaid mileage or per diem $238.31  04222-47\nFrom Philadelphia, Pa. To San Francisco, Calif.\n\n          /s/ R E Pel, Deputy\n  For R. E. PRENTICE, COMDR.(SC) USNR 56-310\n\n\nNOTICE TO ALL OFFICERS ON CHANGE OF STATION\nIn view of the extreme housing shortage in\nall shore establishments it is considered\nhighly inadvisable to move families until\nsuch time as the officer in question has\nreported for duty and obtained suitable\nquarters for his family.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nJacket No. 177283\nEnd-1                    19 AUG 1946          NASD, Phila., Pa.\n\nTo:      Lieut. Delbert C. Newhouse, USN.\n\n1.       Delivered. Detached.\n\nBy direction of SOinC:\n                              /s/ J. A. SINCOCK\n                                  J. A. SINCOCK\n                          Military Personnel Officer\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n18 SEP 1946             DISTRICT STAFF HEADQUARTERS\n                          TWELFTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n                         SAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA\n\n                              Endorsement\n\n          Reported this date for transportation.\n          You are hereby assigned public quarters in BOQ.\n\n                         /s/ W.L.TAYLOR\n                             W.L.TAYLOR\n                         By direction of the Comdt.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                                              Certified to be a True Copy\n                                              D C Newhouse\n                                              [ILLEGIBLE] File m[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0cda36376a28ec558f10bc0c4c414dd8d053f01de99ee7fff291b77b6fb213c0", "output_sha256": "57b0cd3921bdf58782e411a5614c831c422363be912a9cfc13128d07264110fb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:27.534302+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p247", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 247, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply address not the\nsigner of this letter, but        NAVY DEPARTMENT\nBureau of Naval Personnel,      BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nNavy Department, Wash. 25, D.C.   WASHINGTON 25, D.C.\nRefer to No. 177283\n\nPers-3161-JMJ-1A\n\n7 August 1946\n\nFrom:        The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:          Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n             Aviation Supply Depot,\n             Philadelphia, Pa.\n\nVia:         Supply Officer in Command.\n\nSubject:     Change of duty.\n\n1.  When directed by the Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply\nDepot, you will regard yourself detached from duty at the Aviation\nSupply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa., and from such other duty as may\nhave been assigned you; will proceed to San Francisco, Calif., and\nreport to the Commandant, Twelfth Naval District, for first available\ntransportation to Pearl Harbor, T.H., and upon arrival report to the\nCommandant, Fourteenth Naval District, for duty at the Naval Aviation\nSupply Depot, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n2.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of five days in\nreporting at San Francisco, Calif., in compliance with these orders\nsuch delay to count as leave.\n\n3.  Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel advised of your address.\n\n\n                              /s/ LOUIS DENFELD\n                                  LOUIS DENFELD  F.W.B.\n\nCC:\n  ComFour.\n  ComTwelve.\n  CNO (OP512).\n  ComFourteen.\n  ComServPac (2).\n  SupOfComd, NavAviationSupDep,\n    Pearl Harbor, T.H.                            11909\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n  Stamped on face of Basic Letter:                Certified to be a True Copy\n\n  U.S. Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.    DNewhouse\n\n                    19 AUG 1946\n  Advanced _____ months pay $300.00 which has been\n  charged on my rolls.\n                    /s/ W.D. WRIGHT, Lt. (jg) (SC) USN\n                        Disbursing Officer", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c77a8048d76d13c9962adb2475e31e6ff5ea66baa2a89596cf5ee1036d0f81b8", "output_sha256": "03f0e625bf25129d9ffa418d39b6a4a88446ab33587d02e077028987bb46d842", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:29.979851+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p248", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 248, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Address Reply to\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\nand refer to:\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                       Naval Supply Center\n                       Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n20 September 1946\n\n\nFrom:        NEWHOUSE, Delbert C., 177283, LT, LINE, USN\nTo:          Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:         (1)  Supply Officer in Command\n             (2)  Commandant, FOURTEENTH Naval District\n\nSubject:     Transportation of Dependents; Request for\n\nReference:   (a)  District C/L 88-45\n\nEnclosures:  (A)  S&A Form 33 in quadruplicate\n             (B)  Certified Copies of orders\n\n1.  Forwarded herewith is my request for transportation of\nmy dependents to this station.\n\n2.  I expect to remain on duty in this area for at least six\nmonths from this date.\n\n3.  I have obtained quarters for my dependents and myself in\nthe Ex-Dispensary, Junction Area, Aviation Supply Depot,\nPearl Harbor.\n\n                              Delbert C. Newhouse\n                         DELBERT C NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT                              20 September 1946\n\nFrom:        Supply Officer in Command\nTo:          Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:         Commandant, FOURTEENTH Naval District\n\n1.  Forwarded, recommending approval.\n\n2.  The conditions enumerated in paragraph (2) of reference\n(a) have been met.\n\n                              K. A. Grahn\n                         K. A. GRAHN\n\n\n\n\nForm No.-NSC-43                                      Finished File 319", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1817297ab1b05e08c147da8919a59cfcd77f218d942d63f8689a707dc886c82c", "output_sha256": "1817297ab1b05e08c147da8919a59cfcd77f218d942d63f8689a707dc886c82c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:31.885938+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p249", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 249, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "cancel\n9/30/46BF\n\n                              OFFICE OF COMMANDANT\n                    14th NAVAL DISTRICT, PEARL HARBOR, T. H.\n                         NAVY NUMBER 128 (ONE TWO EIGHT)\n                              c/o Fleet Post Office\n\n\n\n\nSerial: D-4773\n\n\n23 September 1946\n\nEndorsement TWO on\nNEWHOUSE, D. C. LT.,\nLINE, USN, 1tr dtd 20\nSeptember 1946 to BuPers\n\nTo    :       Commandant, 12th Naval District.\n\n        1.       Forwarded approved in accordance with BuPers\ndispatch 272100 November 1945, under category: -\n\n                              \"A\"\n\n\nBy direction of the Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n\n                              J. L. Hall, Jr.\n\n                              J. L. HALL, Jr.\n\n\n\ncc:   AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT, SUPPLY OFFICE (NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER) PEARL\n\n                                                        Finished File 813", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2a6b6db087862fd58094bb4fd323ca51012e78903ea7e16e0de4e1cce9d324b0", "output_sha256": "d3a04204ea171319e8decdc46ec3db04b4c6b1d1ef1b72ef37cb07d47c469700", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:33.221336+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p250", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 250, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283\n\nm1°\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nEND-6                          AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT, PEARL HARBOR\n\n9 September 1946\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    LT Delbert C Newhouse LINE USN\n\n1.  Reported this date.\n\n\n                              G M BRYDON\n\ncc:  BuPers\n     Com14\n     ComNavBase\n     ComServPac\n     CNO (Op 512)\n     FRO SanFran\n     SOinC NSC PH\n\n\n                         FINISHED FILM PERS #195", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "22892a2f57bc46a7933a59658f7d0f79bd2b2d8dfcbe46f8ad1f163f56c49397", "output_sha256": "3ffe74e3645043f25dd58d923c9274a61f3742d87a9cefc8926b9a625d5e43ca", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:34.265987+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p251", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 251, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OO/Newhouse, D. C.     14th Naval District, Pearl Harbor, T. H.     1/316\n(177283)\n\n               9 SEP 1946\n\nEnd-3  Date:\nTo :   Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, U. S. Navy.\nSubj:  Change of duty.\n\n1.       Reported this date.  You will further report to the Commandant, U. S. Naval\nBase, Pearl Harbor, T. H., for duty at the Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., in connection with photography.\n\n\n\n\n                                                    A. A. KNOTEK,\n                                                    By direction.\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    FBO NY 128\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1843d15de403f52345feb3ed0d8645bebfea7a673b647adc5069307116edd70e", "output_sha256": "d821e0749c440740e8ba1667add5ccf1bc1740b394100ea1add47d381e66b361", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:35.456602+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p252", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 252, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nSHIP OR STATION  Aviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor  DATE  9 December 1946\n\nFROM:          Comdr. Karl A. GRAHN, SC, USN (81449)\n                              COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:   BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: { REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n           REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n\n     IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME  NEWHOUSE          Delbert          Clement          FILE NO.  177283\n           LAST               FIRST             MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS   LT LINE                              SIGNAL NO.  - - -\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF  CO End-1 to Request for Leave       DATED  25 Nov 46\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n\n  (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME         Four\n\n  (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n      TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n      EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n      VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE.................................  ___________\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE   3 December 1946       EXPIRING DATE   6 December 1946\n\n                                         SIGNED  [signature]\n                                                    COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n     1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n     2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n     3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.                                           16—33335-2   U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "63cd097d9a85e01fefed08254c1b595fa921fbcbb28cdca314f5458fe3ae361d", "output_sha256": "27749016c2dcfc27c40e0cb5e15a0d221f3d6883153ddd1be53446dbc65d2176", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:38.195694+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p253", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 253, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 322\n(Revised April, 1943)\n\nB                    FINISHED FILE PERS-3216\n\nREPORT OF COMPLIANCE WITH ORDERS\n(See notes below)\n\nAviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor          9 September 1946\n              (Ship or Station)                                    (Date)\nFrom LT D C NEWHOUSE LT(LINE) USN                    File No. 177283\n              (Typewrite or print rank and name)\nTo: BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL,\n        Via Commanding Officer.\nSubject: Report of compliance with orders.\nReference: (a) Order No. Pers-3161-JMJ-1A dated 7 August          , 1946\n              issued by BuPers\n\n1. Reference (a) was received on    19 August          , 1946\n      [was detached from\nI [xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]    NASD, Philadelphia\n   [xxxxxxxxxx]\non                         19 August                              , 1946\n                                (Date of detachment)\n\n   [xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]\nI [reported]              Aviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor\n   [xxxxxxx]\non                         9 September                            , 1946\n                                (Date of reporting)\n\n2. (a) I sailed from United States to duty outside continental limits thereof on 9 Sept.    ,\n   1946  (this item to be inserted only if applicable).           (Date of sailing)\n\n   (b) I arrived in United States from duty outside continental limits thereof on              ,\n                                                                   (Date of arrival)\n   19      (this item to be inserted only if applicable).\n\n\n                                    [Signature] D C Newhouse\n                                              (Signature)\n[Signature] G. M. Brydon\nForwarded by GEORGE M BRYDON    CAPT SC USN Supply Officer in Command\n\nNOTE (a).—It is a matter of special importance to officers' records that this form be made out with care and accuracy and forwarded to the Bureau of Naval Personnel promptly. In the case of aviation and staff corps officers, a copy marked DUPLICATE should also be forwarded.\n        (b).—In cases of delay counting as leave, the forwarding of this form does not dispense with the requirement of forwarding Form BNP 321 (Report of Leave of Absence), which should be forwarded in addition to this form.\n\nU. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE   16—20071-4", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "816ba82a1076a80ce8f7a0fa87ab5cf672b9d5aa9b46fa369336b56ccdd72f2a", "output_sha256": "1eccf6a11304e8cffd64da70bf07f4eb4d2efa422efdcfafce6fb9ad3a2ffc17", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:42.256628+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p254", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 254, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CO/Newhouse, D. C.          14th Naval District, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n(177263)\n                                                                    3/5\n                    9 SEP 1946                                      316\nEnd-3  Date:\nTo :    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, U. S. Navy.\nSubj:   Change of duty.\n\n1.       Reported this date.  You will further report to the Commandant, U. S. Naval\nBase, Pearl Harbor, T. H., for duty at the Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., in connection with photography.\n\n\n\n\n                                                    By direction.\n\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    FBC NY 128\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEnd-4    9 September 1946\nFrom:    Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo  :    Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, LINE, USN.\nSubj:    Change of duty.\n\n    1.   Reported this date.  Further report to Supply Officer in Command,\nNaval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H. for duty at the Naval Aviation\nSupply Depot, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., in connection with\nphotography.\n\n\n                                                    E. W. HANSON\ncc: BuPers\n    ComServPac\n    CNO (Op 512)\n    FRO San Fran\n    Com 14\n\n                                          [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "49addce2baee140b8e97e706f0a6af4e72499995d54c80a2dfc7b83a5b31192c", "output_sha256": "c9b3afc53ed612b7609d0e1c700a3ec6f2e914b09bee3971d60b68e26999e663", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:44.279754+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p255", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 255, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "6b\n2/314\n\n25 September 1946\n\n\nFrom:          Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo :           Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, 0177283\n               Ensign Oley (n) Hatsep, SCS, USNR, 0483558\n\nVia :          SCinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubj:          Orders - Additional duty.\n\n     1.        When directed by Supply Officer in Command, Naval\nSupply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H., on 26 September 1946 you will\nreport immediately to the Commanding Officer, Enlisted Personnel,\nU. S. Naval Receiving Station, Pearl Harbor, T. H., for additional\nduty on a summary Court Martial Board.\n\n     2.        This is in addition to your regular duty.\n\n\n\n\n                              E. N. HANSON\n\ncc:\nBuPers (clipper) ✓        NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, PEARL HARBOR\nComServPac(2)\nComl4                     End—  SEP 26 1946\nCO,RecSta,Pearl\n                          From:  Supply Officer in Command\n\n                          1.     Delivered.\n\n                                              E. E. BRIGHTON\n                                              BY DIRECTION\n\n\n                    FINISHED FILE PERS [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4c60372499834ca749b611adb744db828c3b093c5504808387fe725826b11666", "output_sha256": "7787c6ae3e067f191cf57f955fce2dd8df1b21a1ae05b68351126a47814b698e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:45.897917+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p256", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 256, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "c\n315\n316\n\n25 September 1946.\n\nFrom:      Commandant, U. S. Naval Base, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo :       Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, 0177283.\n           Ensign Oley (n) Ratsop, SCS, USNR, 0483558.\nVia :      SOinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\nSubj:      Orders - Additional duty.\n\n     1.    When directed by Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\nPearl Harbor, T. H. on 26 September 1946 you will report immediately to the\nCommanding Officer, Enlisted Personnel, U. S. Naval Receiving Station, Pearl\nHarbor, T. H. for additional duty on a summary Court Martial Board.\n\n     2.    This is in addition to your regular duty.\n\n\n\n\n                              E. W. HANSON\n\ncc:\n   BuPers (clipper)\n   ComServPac (2)\n   Com 14\n   CO, RecSta, Pearl", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0a4efb136444e6a9aa2b0cfcb550c50cf44007a337e6d636d79d95b2b43f029c", "output_sha256": "65189647e2592789ab86f3164cc6abdaf1830e2dabe216b7541f4756bd304cf0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:47.245880+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p257", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 257, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 393\n(Rev. December 1942)\n\nBENEFICIARY SLIP\n\nName  NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n            (Name in full, surname to the left)\n\nSerial No.  177283\n              (File number, not signal number)\n\nStation  Naval Aviation Supply Depot\n                    (Name)\n\nPhiladelphia 11, Penna.    19 May 1945\n      (Place)                        (Date)\n\nUnder the provisions of the Act approved May 22, 1928, as extended by\nthe Act of March 17, 1941, directing the payment of 6 months' pay to the\nwidow, children, or dependent relative of any of the personnel on the\nactive list of the Regular Navy, or on the retired list when on active\nduty, or of any of the personnel of the Naval Reserve called or ordered\ninto active naval service by the Federal Government for extended naval\nservice in excess of 30 days, who dies of wounds or disease not the result\nof his or her own misconduct, I give below the name and address of my\nwife and that of each of my children:\n            (See instructions on reverse side)\n\nMrs. Norma Isobel Newhouse\n      (Full name of wife ; if not married, so state)\n\n6841 Oxford Ave., Philadelphia 11, Pa.\n                  (Address of wife)\n\nDelbert Carroll Newhouse  28 June 1938\n  (Full name of child ; if none, so state)          (Date of birth)\n\n              Same as wife.\n                  (Address of child)\n\nAnne Lisbet Newhouse  14 March 1940\n  (Full name of child)                             (Date of birth)\n\n              Same as wife.\n                  (Address of child)\n\n************************\n  (Full name of child)                              (Date of birth)\n\n\n                        (Address of child)\n\nIn the event of my leaving no widow or child or of their\ndecease before payment is made, I then designate as my\nbeneficiary under the said act the following relative, my\n\n                  Mother\n                (Relationship)\n\nMrs. Edith May Newhouse Richter\n              (Name in full)\n\nP.O. Box 225, Garibaldi, Oregon\n                    (Address)\n\n\n\n*\n\n\n\n* If the beneficiary named above is your father, mother, brother, or\nsister, you need not fill in these three lines. If the beneficiary is a\nmore distant relative, such as a grandparent, state briefly wherein de-\npendency exists, such as \"allotments registered,\" \"monthly contributions\nby Government check,\" indicating amounts and regularity thereof.\n\n                        [OVER]                    16—82303-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7691f00a96ee85208764ea953e4c2c843de1652e1381a6cd269a20b25d5ed4b6", "output_sha256": "68297e18d6c415ec3d59c245db198af86cf56f2edafb0570424a2a36ce4d77b8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:49.868438+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p258", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 258, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In the event of the death of the above-named beneficiary\nbefore payment is made, I then designate as my beneficiary\nunder said act the following relative, my\n\n                    Brother\n                (Relationship)\n\n        Darrell Edwin Newhouse\n                (Name in full)\n\n        P.O. Box 225, Garibaldi, Oregon\n                    (Address)\n\n\n\n  *\n\n\n\n* In case of relatives more distant than your parent or brother or\nsister, state briefly wherein dependency exists, indicating amounts and\nregularity thereof.\n\n\n    I CERTIFY that I will inform the Bureau of Naval Per-\nsonnel immediately of any changes in marital status or\nconditions of dependency.\n    I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that the facts stated and\ndisclosed in the foregoing are true to the best of my knowl-\nedge and belief.\n\n                    Delbert C. Newhouse\n                        (Name)\n\n            Lieut.(jg)          , U. S. Navy,\n                (Rank)          [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this  22nd\n\nday of     May              , 1945, I having author-\nity to administer oaths.\n\n            William R. Turner  Lieut USNR\n\n\n                        INSTRUCTIONS\n\n    This form must be sworn to before an officer of the United States Navy\nor Marine Corps authorized to administer oaths, or before a notary\npublic.\n    The full names and addresses of the beneficiaries must be stated care-\nfully.  If a married woman, her own given name should be stated; thus:\n\"Mrs. Anna May Smith,\" not \"Mrs. John Smith.\"\n    This slip shall be made out and handled as follows:\n    Officer, Navy: Forward to Bureau of Naval Personnel.\n    Officer, Marine Corps: Forward to Commandant, Marine Corps.\n    Nurse: Forward to Bureau of Medicine and Surgery.\n    New beneficiary slips shall be executed and forwarded as above in all\ncases of change in status of the grantor or in that of his or her bene-\nficiaries.\n    In any event, payment will be made to the widow or children, if any,\nwhether designated or not, but not to a mother or other relative unless\ndesignated.\n\n            U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE   16—32303-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6fed68e9db6169a93131430f3da4cc013761678d8f4cce51f4cb9fa537409395", "output_sha256": "ada725817147ec8237242ffdf162c3827aa0714b1932abd6fbb4b0d2b4a66a5b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:52.166405+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p259", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 259, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "FILE No. 177283\n\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n(Name of officer; surname first)\n\nEnsign, USN\n(Rank and corps)\n\n19 August 1944\n(Date)\n\nIf your status has changed from \"no dependents\" to \"dependents\"\n(or vice versa) since last report, indicate by √ in this space □\n\nREPORT OF DEPENDENTS UNDER ACT\nOF JUNE 10, 1922\n\nNOTE.—The Act of June 10, 1922, defines the term \"dependent\"\nas a lawful wife, unmarried children under 21 years of age, or the\nmother of an officer provided she is in fact dependent on him for\nher chief support.)\n\nNumber      3\n\nMother      Yes\n           (Yes or No)\n\nWife        Yes\n           (Yes or No)\n\nAge and sex of each child under 21 years of age:\n  Male  -  6 yrs.\n\n  Female  -  4 yrs.\n\n\n\n\nGPO  16—33831-2\n\n\nBENEFICIARY SLIP\n\nName NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n          (Name in full, surname to the left)\n\nSerial No. 177283\n           (File number, not signal number)\n\nShip or\n  station        NAS\n                (Name)\n\nCOCO SOLO C Z     19 August 1944\n                          (Date)\n\nUnder the provisions of the Act approved May 22, 1928, as extended by the Act of March 17, 1941, directing the payment of 6\nmonths' pay to the widow, children, or dependent relative of any\nof the personnel on the active list of the Regular Navy, or on the\nretired list when on active duty, or of any of the personnel of the\nNaval Reserve called or ordered into active naval service by the\nFederal Government for extended naval service in excess of 30\ndays, who dies of wounds or disease not the result of his or her\nown misconduct, I give below the name and address of my wife\nand that of each of my children:\n(See instructions on reverse side)\n\nNO CHANGE SINCE LAST REPORT\n     (Full name of wife; if not married, so state)\n\n\n                    (Address of wife)\n\n\n(Full name of child)           (Date of birth)\n\n\n                    (Address of child)\n\n\n(Full name of child)           (Date of birth)\n\n\n                    (Address of child)\n\n\n(Full name of child)           (Date of birth)\n\n\n                    (Address of child)\n\nIn the event of my leaving no widow or child or of\ntheir decease before payment is made, I then designate as my beneficiary under the said Act the following relative, my\n\n                    (Relationship)\n\n\n                    (Name in full)\n\n\n                    (Address)\n\n*If the beneficiary named above is your father, mother, brother,\nor sister, you need not fill in these three lines. If the beneficiary\nis a more distant relative, such as a grandparent, state briefly\nwherein dependency exists, such as \"allotments registered,\"\n\"monthly contributions by Government check,\" indicating amounts\nand regularity thereof.\n                    [OVER]      16—33831-2\n\n\n                              177283\n                    File No.\n\n              REPORT OF NEXT OF KIN\n\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n     (Name of officer, surname first)\n\n      19 August 1944\n           (Date)\n\nAny change since last report:\n\n           X YES or NO\n\n(Strike out one; if no change, do not fill out remainder of this\nreport.)\n\n\nName of next of kin\n\n\n                              (Relationship)\n\nPermanent residence:\n\n  Street and No.\n\n  City or town\n\n  State\n\nEmergency address:\n\n  Street and No.\n\n  City or town\n\n  State\n\n\n                              (Signature)\n\n\n                              (Rank and corps)\n                                        GPO  16—33831-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "02465543a3fba5db13d4cc8c48c19f8c662b7f7bb2403b205d3dc4118d8c9fb2", "output_sha256": "d91e503352e69ca2767df3f196f8c0f72ddbb35ec7a5e43aeafae4ab47ecbd1a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:56.002906+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p260", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 260, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "FILE No. 177283\n\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n        (Name of officer ; surname first)\n\nEnsign, USN\n        (Rank and corps)\n\n6-30-44\n        (Date)\n\nREPORT OF DEPENDENTS UNDER ACT\n        OF JUNE 10, 1922\n\n(NOTE.—The Act of June 10, 1922, defines the term \"dependent\"\nas lawful wife, unmarried children under 21 years of age, or the\nmother of an officer provided she is in fact dependent on him for\nhis support.)\n\nNumber  Three\n\nMother  No\n             (Yes or No)\n\nWife   Yes\n           (Yes or No)\n\nAge and sex of each child under 21 years of age:\n\n6 yrs. - male\n\n4 yrs. - female\n\n\n\n\nGPO  16—33831-1\n\n---\n\nFILE No.  177283\n\nBENEFICIARY SLIP\n\nName  NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n              (Print name, surname to the left)\n\nNAS, Coco Solo, C.Z.          6-30-44\n           (Place)                         (Date)\n\nAny change since last report:\n        YES or NO\n(Strike out one ; if no change, do not fill out remainder of this\nreport.)\n\nUnder the provisions of the Act of June 4, 1920 (41 Stat. 824),\nas amended by the Act of May 22, 1928 (45 Stat. 710 ; U. S. C.\nTitle 34, Sec. 943), as further amended by Public Law 16, 77th\nCongress, approved March 17, 1941, directing the payment of six\nmonths' pay to the widow, children, or dependent relative of any\nofficer, enlisted man, or nurse, on the active list of the regular\nNavy or regular Marine Corps, or on the retired list when on\nactive duty, or officer, aviation cadet, midshipman, nurse, warrant\nofficer, or enlisted man of the U. S. Naval Reserve called or\nordered into active naval or military service by the Federal Gov-\nernment for extended naval or military service in excess of 30\ndays, who dies of wounds or disease not the result of his or her\nown misconduct, I give below the name and address of my wife\nand that of each of my children:\n\n(Full name of wife ; if not married, so state)\n\n(Address of wife)\n\n(Full name of child ; if none, so state)\n\n(Address of child)\n\n(Full name of child ; if none, so state)\n\n(Address of child)\n\n(Full name of child ; if none, so state)\n\n(Address of child)\n\nIn the event of my leaving no widow or child or of\ntheir decease before payment is made, I then desig-\nnate as my beneficiary under the said act the follow-\ning dependent relative, my—\n\n(Relationship)\n\n(Name in full)\n\n(Address)\n\n*State briefly wherein dependency exists, such as \"allotments\nregistered,\" \"monthly contributions by Government check,\" etc.\n                        (OVER)\n                                    16—33831-1\n\n---\n\nREPORT OF NEXT OF KIN\n\nFILE NO.: 177283\n\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n        (Name of officer, surname first)\n\n6-30-44\n        (Date)\n\nAny change since last report:\n\n        YES or NO\n\n(Strike out one ; if no change, do not fill out remainder of this\nreport.)\n\nName of next of kin\n\n(Relationship)\n\nPermanent residence:\n\n        Street and No.\n\n        City or town\n\n        State\n\nEmergency address:\n\n        Street and No.\n\n        City or town\n\n        State\n\n(Signature)\n\n(Rank and corps)\n\nGPO  16-33831-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "19c18ea5a7a3e73448d3a92f4c4818b71a07ea74f670eefc871638cc0549bc85", "output_sha256": "c3372ce58fba2196d47dab0fc352a8bca3ed2309a7f0138c6b9ff6682e892e28", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:39:59.841618+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p261", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 261, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n(Name of officer; surname first)\n\nEnsign\n(Rank and corps)\n\n12/31/43\n(Date)\n\nREPORT OF DEPENDENTS UNDER ACT OF\nJUNE 10, 1922\n\n(Note: Act of June 10, 1922, defines the term \"dependent\" as lawful wife, unmarried children under 21 years of age, or the mother of an officer provided she is in fact dependent on him for her chief support.)\n\nNumber