event of my leaving no widow or child or of\nt[REDACTED] decease before payment is made, I then designate\nas my beneficiary under the said act the following\ndependent relative, my\n\n                    (Relationship)\n\n                    (Name in full)\n\n                    (Address)\n\n\n*State briefly wherein dependency exists, such as \"allotments registered,\" \"monthly contributions by Government check,\" etc.\n               (OVER)          16—22799-1\n\n\nREPORT OF NEXT OF KIN\n\nNewhouse, Delbert Clement\n         (Name of officer, surname first)\n\n              2-14-43\n               (Date)\n\nAny change since last report:\n\n               YES or NO   First Report\n\n(Strike out one; if no change, do not fill out remainder of this report)\n\nName of next of kin: ----------------------------------------\n\nNorma Isobel Newhouse\n\n              Wife\n           (Relationship)\n\nPermanent residence:\n\nStreet and No. 1210 S.E. 37th Avenue\n\nCity or town  Portland\n\nState -------- Oregon\n\nEmergency address:\n\nStreet and No. ....... Same as above\n\nCity or town -------------------------------------------\n\nState -------------------------------------------\n\n         Delbert C. Newhouse\n                    (Signature)\n\n         Photographer (Demps.), U.S.N.\n                    (Rank and corps)          16—22799-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7740bf735c1745269c44292a6752a4f6e279e5e828ed7127b4c086d8135b89d6", "output_sha256": "962d712878877987e67da1b50dfa3abe2146befbeed35cc1f24c3b9578b0588c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:06.881088+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p263", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 263, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In the event that payment cannot be made to the above-named dependent relative, I then designate as my beneficiary under the said act the following dependent relative, my\n\n-------------------------------------------\n(Relationship)\n\n-------------------------------------------\n(Name in full)\n\n-------------------------------------------\n(Address)\n\n[REDACTED]\n\n[REDACTED]\n\n* State briefly wherein dependency exists.\n\nI do solemnly swear (or affirm) that the facts stated and disclosed in the foregoing are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nDelbert Clement Newhouse\n(Name)\n\nPhotographer (Temp)_______, U. S. Navy.\n(Rank)\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me, this 14th\n\nday of February _____________, 1943, I hav[REDACTED]\nauthority to administer oaths.\n\nJ. R. LITCHFIELD\n\n[REDACTED]\n\nCommander, USNR\n\nCommanding Officer.\n\n══════════════════════════════════════\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nThis form must be sworn to before an officer of the United States Navy or Marine Corps authorized to administer oaths, or before a notary public.\n   The full names and addresses of the beneficiaries must be stated carefully. If a married woman, her own given name should be stated; thus: \"Mrs. Anna May Smith,\" not \"Mrs. John Smith.\"\n   New beneficiary slips shall be executed and forwarded as above in all cases of change of status of the grantor or in that of his or her beneficiaries.\n   In any event, payment will be made to the widow or children, if any, whether designated or not.\n\n☆  U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE : 1942     16—22709-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "43cbd0e195471000569e0f163db486501cd83f8aaf38851971c199f1b6c4e743", "output_sha256": "e59439b0a5ebad0b26a76e3a0cf9583c51749e8cec444767c079432705991558", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:08.823318+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p264", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 264, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nSHIP OR STATION Aviation Supply Depot, Pearl Harbor DATE 9 September 1946\n\nFROM: [REDACTED] Supply Officer in Command\n                    COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:   BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: [REDACTED]\n         REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n\n         IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME  NEWHOUSE      Delbert       Clement                    FILE No. 177283\n          LAST           FIRST          MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS  LT LINE                                       SIGNAL No. 16132\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF  BuPers Pers-3161-JMJ-1A                      DATED  7 August 1946\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n\n   (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME\n\n   (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n       TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n       EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n       VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE.................................  Four Days\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW:\n\nCOMMENCING DATE  29 August 1946             EXPIRING DATE  1 September 1946\n\n                                            SIGNED  G M BRYDON CAPT SC USN\n         FINISHED FILE PERS-3216                        COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n   1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n   2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n   3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.                16—33335-2   U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8b8ddca0f50edb3203909f58355dfddd2b8a402624ae6b5cde23d47481de58d9", "output_sha256": "f6ac09f35874531c9997fa3d900c8c79c88140e6af94afda17a86b558e2482bb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:11.612092+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p265", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 265, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CROSS REFERENCE SHEET\n\nName or subject                                    File 177283\n\nNewhouses, D. C. Lt.\n\nFrom:  AVSUPJEP PEARL                    Date  8/3/46\n\nTO:    BUPERS\n\n032222Z RE BUPERS PERS-3145-JG-1D 19 Jul 46 ORDER G PHOT J. P. MALITO TO THIS DEPOT\nFOR DU. INDICATIONS ALSO RECVD THAT --- RECENTLY AT NASD PHILA ALSO IN PROCESS TRANSF\nTO ASD PEARL AS PHOTO OFFCR. CHF PHOT E. J. HAIRR RPTD ON 20 JULY FR NAS KANEOHE\nUNDER COM14 ORDERS 20374 dtd 17 JUL. BUREAU ADVISED OF THIS APPARENT DUPLICATION FOR\nAPPROPRIATE ACTN.\n\n8/8/46 BUPERS TO AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT PEARL HARBOR.\n091537 REFUR 032222. ORDERS PHOT MALITO USN CANCELLED. --- ORDERED FR NASD PHILA.\n\n\nSEE FILE NUMBER................443964..................\n\nGENERAL FILES, BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n\n\n\n\n\nNAVPERS-2109 (7-33)                                                          (P)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ff6eb8521f783df415dcb140b7fd94096f7e7e918500505d3cf9ea15621ca653", "output_sha256": "973390cf42942591d5bd46696a834e9c2a777f0c36604c8b58db503f603bb531", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:13.387983+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p266", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 266, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BNP 321 REVISED FEB. 1943\n\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE  See Instructions Below\n\nShip or Station Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Phila., Pa. Date  16 August 1946\n\nFrom:    Supply Officer in Command\n                    Commanding Officer\n\nTO:      Bureau of Naval Personnel, Navy Department\n\nSUBJ:    REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n\n         In conformity with requirements of U. S. NAVY regulations, I report\nthe following leave of absence taken by:\n\nNAME      NEWHOUSE         Delbert          C          File No.  177283\n           Last             First          Middle\n\nRANK AND CORPS  Lieut. USN                            SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF  SOinC 1st endorsement              DATED   12 August 1946\n\nNOTE:    Use either (A) or (B). DO NOT use both for same leave.\n\n  (A)    LEAVE: Total number of days, including any travel time  3 Days\n\n  (B)    Delay counting as leave or leave between stations.\n         Total number of days, excluding preparation period\n         of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel time\n         from old to new station via shortest usually traveled\n         route.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInsert inclusive dates to agree with number of days leave.\nSee instructions below.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE  13 August 1946          EXPIRING DATE  15 August 1946\n\nBy direction of SOinC:\n                                                   J. A. SIMCOCK\n                              SIGNED  Lt. Cdr. SC(S) USNR\n                                      Military Personnel Officer\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1.   The day of departure from station or duty counts as a day of duty;\nthe day of return as a day of leave.  This refers to leave taken when not\ndetached from ship or station (See ARTICLE 1727, Navy Regulations).\n\n2.   In cases of authorized delay counting as leave, this form should\nbe submitted in addition to the B-slip Form.\n\n3.   This report will be made at expiration of leave by the immediate\nsuperior of the Officer to whom the leave is granted and forwarded\nimmediately to the Navy Department (Bureau of Naval Personnel).  Care\nmust be taken to insure that correct number of days leave is reported and\ncorresponds with the inclusive dates reported.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f7acbd60023a073d9ef7c23340523df947f6bf457c7b09a436d63a54c701568", "output_sha256": "6e01a8d41ee76d6004e4fa867524846e88773ce8e54345091ba22197a1d61b6e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:15.707844+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p267", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 267, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply address not the signer of this\nletter, but Bureau of Naval Personnel,\nNavy Department, Washington 25, D. C.\nRefer to No.\n\n           177283\n\nPers-3161-JMJ-1A\n\n                        NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\n               BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                    WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n\n7 August 1946\n\n\nFrom:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:            Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n               Aviation Supply Depot,\n               Philadelphia, Pa.\n\nVia:           Supply Officer in Command.\n\nSubject:       Change of duty.\n\n1. When directed by the Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply\nDepot, you will regard yourself detached from duty at the Aviation\nSupply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa., and from such other duty as may\nhave been assigned you; will proceed to San Francisco, Calif., and\nreport to the Commandant, Twelfth Naval District, for first available\ntransportation to Pearl Harbor, T.H., and upon arrival report to the\nCommandant, Fourteenth Naval District, for duty at the Naval Aviation\nSupply Depot, Pearl Harbor, T.H., in connection with photography.\n\n2. You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of five days in\nreporting at San Francisco, Calif., in compliance with these orders,\nsuch delay to count as leave.\n\n3. Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel advised of your address.\n\n\n\nCC:\n  ComFour.\n  ComTwelve.\n  CNO (OP512).\n  ComFourteen.\n  ComServPac (2).\n  SupOfComd, NavAviationSupDep,                    LOUIS DENFELD\n    Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n\n[SIGNATURE]\n\n                    TO ALL OFFICERS ON CHANGE OF [ILLEGIBLE]\n                    In view of the extreme housing shortages in\n                    all shore establishments it is considered\n                    highly inadvisable to move families until\n                    such time as the officer in question has\n                    reported for duty and obtained suitable\n                    quarters for his family.\n\n                                                             11909", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1d9bc80a391c04bce5987e7a97a6c1a0ba64e1c1f909eefc22edf4861b3d1217", "output_sha256": "a8b295c1cd42008e100e7da70bca5d76128a56fac999e2738808454c3b0b1923", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:17.867250+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p268", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 268, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Op-512-RMS\n\n                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n              OFFICE OF THE CHIEF OF NAVAL OPERATIONS\n                       WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\nTo:    Bu Pers (Att. Pers 316)                                              31 JUL 1946\n\n1. It is requested that the below named person be issued orders as indicated below:\nFILE No.        NAME          (last)              (first)       (middle-initial)    RANK      CLASSIF.       U.S.N.\n 177283         NEWHOUSE,     Delbert     C.                      Lieut.    USN        U.S.N.R.\n                                                                                          L  PLAIN X\n☐ ORDERS OF_____            ☐ UNEXECUTED PORTION                ☐ STUDENT              R  AIR\n                               ORDERS OF____                       AVIATOR CLAUSE\n                                                                                          D  BGM\n☐ LETTER                    ☐ DISPATCH                          ☐ FLYING CLAUSE         I  NL\n                               (time-group)____\n                                                                                          S  DEF.\n☐ CANCELED    ☐ MODIFIED    ☐ CORRECTED    ☐ REPEATED           ☐ TECHNICAL OBSERVER\n                                              FOR COMPLIANCE                              ROU-\n☐ DETACHED                                                FROM                          TINE\n☐ HEREBY   X WHEN    ☐ ON OR              ☐ Tem  X Duty  ☐ Tem Ins ☐ Du Ins  ☐ Staff  ☐ Du Fly  A\n             DIRECTED   ABOUT\n                                                                                          T  PRIOR\n☐ WHEN                                       AS:\n  RELIEVED (BY)                                                                          C  RESTR.\n☐ UPON          SO in C    ☐ UPON DISCHARGE\n  REPORTING (OF)              TREATMENT                                                  H  CONF.\n\nAT Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa.\nPROCEED X Prop  ☐ Pr Delrep  ☐ Pr Olmrop  ☐ Report    X  Delrep         FOR\n                                              on    five (5) days    ☐ Tem  X Duty  ☐ Staff  ☐ Du Fly\n1. TO Commandant,\n        Fourteenth Naval District                                      Tem-\n                                                                   ☐ Ins   ☐ Du Ins  ☐ Tur as by\n                                                               (at) Naval Aviation Supply\nTRANS:                              ☐ Dir Dot  Comp  Depot, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n☐ Prop    ☐ Do Lrop                          Bir Dot  FOR in connection with photo.\n2. TO                                                            ☐ Tem   ☐ Duty  ☐ Staff  ☐ Du Fly\n\n                                                                ☐ Tem-\n                                                                  Ins   ☐ Du Ins ☐ Tur as\n\nTRANS:                              ☐ Dir Dot  Comp  AS:\n☐ Prop    ☐ Do Lrop                          Bir Dot  FOR\n3. TO                                                           ☐ Tem   ☐ Duty  ☐ Staff  ☐ Du Fly\n\n                                                                ☐ Tem-\n                                                                  Ins   ☐ Du Ins  ☐ Tur as by\n\nTRANS:                                                          AS:\nPER DIEM    REMARKS\n☐\n                                                              Charles C. Gold\n\n                                                             CHARLES C. GOLD\n                                                             By Direction\n\n                              11909\n\n\n                    INFORMATION ADDRESSEE(S)                   MAIL    MGM    AMGM    DISP.\n  By S 1 Y\n\n\nDATE          PERS. NO.        DETAIL OFFICER                  EXT.          DATE OUT BY\n 8/1/46       3/6/           Whittedly                          7803     8/7/46\nNAVAER-1145 (REV. 9-45)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "801fd7d31ba15b7456d568f9b8b30b0479cee8212d20d2b26d455dc9b0ed93db", "output_sha256": "13f1c20e93782d87aa93ed52f2094f4fd0238dc648bc18f8ddaf29913e7a020e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:22.534798+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p269", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 269, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply address not the signer of this\nletter, but Bureau of Naval Personnel,\nNavy Department, Washington, D. C.\n  Refer to No.\n         Pers-3214\n         177263-mmr\n\n                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n             BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                   WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                                          FOR PEACE\n                                                            OF\n                                                          MIND—\n                                                          BUY\n                                                        SAVINGS\n                                                        BONDS\n\n2 3 AUG 1946\n\nFrom:        The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nTo:          Lt. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\nVia:         SupOfCom, NASD, Oxford Ave. & Martin's Mill Rd., Phila.\n\nSubj:        Application for Transfer to the Regular Navy - Action on.\n\nRefs:        (a)  Your Application for Permanent Appointment in the\n                  U.S. Navy.\n             (b)  BuPers Circular Letter 288-45 (Revised).\n\n1.  The Selection Board, convened by the Secretary of the Navy to\nrecommend Naval Reserve and Temporary USN officers for appointment as\ncommissioned officers and warrant officers in the Regular Navy, has\nconsidered your application for transfer, and I am pleased to inform\nyou that this Board has recommended you for permanent appointment in\nthe Regular Navy as a commissioned warrant officer.\n\n2.  This notification is for informational purposes only, in order to\nadvise you of the action taken by the Selection Board on your application.\nOf additional interest to you is the fact that the President has signed\nPublic Law #347, which provides the necessary legislation to effect the\ntransfer of officers to the Regular Navy.\n\n3.  Upon confirmation by the Senate the appointments of officers to the\nRegular Navy will be issued to the service in a circular letter published\nin the Navy Department semi-monthly bulletin.  If you are on inactive\nduty you will be notified of your appointment including instructions for\nacceptance.  In the event that you fail to receive this notification from\nthe Bureau of Naval Personnel and you find your appointment published in\nthe semi-monthly bulletin you may contact the nearest Naval District\nCommandant for instructions and acceptance of appointment.\n\n\n\n\n                    [signature]\n\nCC:\n  Pers 31.           FINISHED FILE Pers-3214\n\n\n                              S/ T. L. SPRAGUE\n                          Rear Admiral Louis Denfeld\n                          Vice Admiral, U. S. N.\n                          The Chief of Naval Personnel\n                          Acting\n\n                                                              C-73156", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "978747c9753dcf70c241350f9d35dd221ff42887c05c3ea3ebeefec8e9469609", "output_sha256": "74bdf5dec13c8fd71a5a33b4baacb6aac4d3cd6ca62f28e0ab1e8a398f9b66cb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:25.145904+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p270", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 270, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REPORT OF BENEFICIARIES                    7\nNAVPERS-601 (1-45)\n\n[X] OFFICER  [ ] ENLISTED          5 June 1946\n                                        (Date)\n\n         NEWHOUSE              Delbert          Clement\n          (Last name)            (First)          (Middle)\n\n         177283                   Lieut. USN (T)\n    (File or service number)    (Rank or rate and classification)\n\nU. S.     NASD Philadelphia, Pa.\n                    (Ship or station)\n   To carry out the provisions of the acts approved 4 June 1920, 22 May\n1928, 12 May 1930, and 17 March 1941, and acts amendatory thereof\ndirecting the payment of 6 months' pay to the widow, children, or dependent\nrelative of any of the personnel on the active list of the Regular Navy, or\non the retired list when on active duty, or of any of the personnel of the\nNaval Reserve called or ordered into active naval service by the Federal\nGovernment for extended naval service in excess of 30 days, who dies\nof wounds or disease not the result of his or her own misconduct, I give\nbelow the name and address of my wife or husband and that of each of my\nchildren:\n\n              Norma Isobel Newhouse\n         (Full name of wife or husband; if not married, so state)\n\n              6148 Oxford Avenue, Phila., Pa.\n                      (Address of wife or husband)\n\nDelbert Carroll Newhouse                    6/28/38\n      (Full name of child; if none, so state)          (Date of birth)\n\n                   Same as above\n                    (Address of child)\n\nAnne Lisbet Newhouse                        3/14/40\n         (Full name of child)                      (Date of birth)\n\n                   Same as above\n                    (Address of child)\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n         (Full name of child)                      (Date of birth)\n\n\n                         (Address of child)\n\n   In the event that I am not survived by a wife (or husband) or child, or\nin the event of their decease prior to payment and collection of the gratuity,\nI then designate the following person as my dependent beneficiary under\nthe act:*\n\n              Mrs. Edith M. Richter\n                    (Name in full)\n\n              Garibaldi, Oregon\n                       (Address)\n\n                       Mother\n                    (Relationship)\n\n   In the event of the death of the above-named beneficiary before payment\nand collection of the gratuity, I then designate the following person as my\ndependent beneficiary under the act:*\n\n              Darrell Edwin Newhouse\n                    (Name in full)\n\n              Garibaldi, Oregon\n                       (Address)\n\n                       Brother\n                    (Relationship)\n\n  *The acts state that death gratuity must be paid to the surviving wife (or\nhusband) or children, if any. In the event of leaving no wife or children,\nit may then be paid to a designated dependent beneficiary. Every member\nof the service, whether married or not, should designate a beneficiary\n(and an alternate, in case of prior death of the primary beneficiary). Failure\nto make such designation may result in nonpayment of the gratuity.\nSuch designation does not affect payment to a surviving wife (or husband)\nor children.\n                                                    e6-16—43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6ee75a5e50d87c866c66d16667508fac370819a6e8d8db4e66a6044e1aa228b9", "output_sha256": "6ee75a5e50d87c866c66d16667508fac370819a6e8d8db4e66a6044e1aa228b9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:28.823619+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p271", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 271, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "8\n\n   I CERTIFY that I will inform the Bureau of Naval Personnel via my\ncommanding officer immediately of any changes in marital status, or con-\nditions of dependency, or of voluntary occupancy of public quarters by my\ndependents.\n\n   I CERTIFY that there has been no change in condition of dependency\nbetween ________1 May 1945________ and current date.\n              (Date of last report of beneficiaries)\n\n   I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that the facts stated and disclosed in the\nforegoing are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n         D C Newhouse\n                    (Signature)\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this______7th___________________\n\nday of ______June_________, 19_46_, I having authority\nto administer oaths.\n\n   E G Willelston Lt(jg) USN\n         (Signature)              (Rank)\n\n\n                        INSTRUCTIONS\n\n   This form must be sworn to before an officer of the\nUnited States Navy authorized to administer oaths, or\nbefore a notary public.\n\n   The full names and addresses of the beneficiaries must\nbe stated carefully.  If a married woman, her own given\nname should be stated; thus: \"Mrs. Anna May Smith,\" not\n\"Mrs. John Smith.\"\n\n   This slip shall be made out and handled as follows:\n   Officer, Navy: Forward to Bureau of Naval Personnel.\n   Nurse: Forward to Bureau of Medicine and Surgery.\n\n   Enlisted men, Navy: In duplicate; one copy to Bureau\nof Naval Personnel, one copy secured inside service rec-\nord.  In cases of men entitled to money allowances for\nquarters for enlisted men with dependents, two additional\ncopies, bearing the required certificate, to the Disbursing\nOfficer.\n\n   New beneficiary slips shall be executed and forwarded\nas above in all cases of change in status of the grantor or\nin that of his or her beneficiaries.\n\n   In any event, payment will be made to the widow or\nchildren, if any, whether designated or not.\n\n   Normally casualty notification will be sent to all the\nbeneficiaries designated on this form.  If, by reason of\nunusual circumstances, other special arrangements are\ndesired, a statement should be attached setting forth\nfull instructions including full names, addresses, and\nrelationships.\n\n\n                     c6-16—43177-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f2296a60c19fdcd7dbd008d406c9df5a47909bdc2bd703e830720eee00ff9a35", "output_sha256": "f89cc50851889f133cb1f8335cbdd7ca63dbcba9a05626c52e5eb1059a225e80", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:31.298900+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p272", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 272, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BNP 321 REVISED FEB. 1943\n\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF A[REDACTED]NCE  See Instructions Below\n                    Naval Aviation Supply Depot\nShip or Station    Philadelphia, Pennsylvania              29 December 1945\n\nFrom:    Supply Officer in Command\n                    Commanding Officer\n\nTO:      Bureau of Naval Personnel, Navy Department\n\nSUBJ:    REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n         REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n\n         In conformity with requirements of U. S. NAVY regulations, I report\nthe following leave of absence taken by:\n\nNAME      NEWHOUSE           Delbert            C          File No.  177283\n          Last               First              Middle\n\nRANK AND CORPS    Lieut.(jg) USN                    SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF    SOinC 1st endorsement              DATED   21 November 1945\n\nNOTE:    Use either (A) or (B). DO NOT use both for same leave.\n\n  (A)    LEAVE: Total number of days, including any travel time    10 Days\n\n  (B)    Delay counting as leave or leave between stations.\n         Total number of days, excluding preparation period\n         of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel time\n         from old to new station via shortest usually traveled\n         route.\n\nInsert inclusive dates to agree with number of days leave.\nSee instructions below.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE   12 December 1945         EXPIRING DATE   21 December 1945\n\n                    FINISHED FILE PERS-3216        W. D. SAMS\n\nBy direction of SOinC:              SIGNED   Lieut. SC USN\n                                             Military Personnel Officer\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1.   The day of departure from station or duty counts as a day of duty;\nthe day of return as a day of leave.  This refers to leave taken when not\ndetached from ship or station (See ARTICLE 1727, Navy Regulations).\n\n2.   In cases of authorized delay counting as leave, this form should\nbe submitted in addition to the B-slip Form.\n\n3.   This report will be made at expiration of leave by the immediate\nsuperior of the Officer to whom the leave is granted and forwarded\nimmediately to the Navy Department (Bureau of Naval Personnel). Care\nmust be taken to insure that correct number of days leave is reported and\ncorresponds with the inclusive dates reported.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a334f09c261f925e89d35316fbd4d7e6197ee20a6c06e6fb75147c8bd43cd059", "output_sha256": "59ce659bcf1e47bc7009618c4133ae939b0b04f38d44a08cc8c80b594a6f5ae5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:33.656021+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p273", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 273, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "IN REPLY ADDRESS\nAVIATION SUPPLY OFFICER\nNAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\nPHILADELPHIA 11, PA.\n\n                                                          22134\n\n                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n             NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n               OXFORD AVENUE AND MARTIN'S MILL ROAD\n                       PHILADELPHIA 11, PA.\n                     AVIATION SUPPLY OFFICE\n\n\n                                        T-845\n25 January 1946\n\nFrom:    The Supply Officer-in-Command.\n\nTo:      Lieutenant (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, JR-177283,\n           Naval Aviation Supply Depot,\n           Oxford Avenue & Martin's Mill Road,\n           Philadelphia 11, Pa.\n\nSubject:  Temporary Additional Duty.\n\n     1.  Proceed to the place (or places—in the order given) indicated below, for temporary\nduty.  This is in addition to your present duties and upon the completion thereof, you will\nreturn to your station and resume your regular duties:\n\n             On or about 28 January 1946, to the Deputy Chief of\nNaval Operations, Navy Dept., Washington, D. C., regarding problems\nconcerning photo materials.\n\n     2.  A per diem of $7.00 in lieu of subsistence will be allowed\nwhile absent from station in accordance with Article 2501-4(d)\nU. S. Navy Travel Instructions.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                        E. D. FOSTER\n                                        Rear Admiral SC USN\n                                        Supply Officer-in-Command\n\n\n\n\nCopies to:\n   BuPers\n   ComFour", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f22e4b56ed4fe9f0fa0456e2ebba0627643da7c05da7e7d1c368351a04d9f331", "output_sha256": "9d48376a7894bed20c99f5f7f1c881362f34c1277f04d2f41a20eb819c5b21cb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:35.383504+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p274", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 274, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NASD Form #153\n\nBNP 321 REVISED FEB. 1943\n\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE  See Instructions Below\n\n                    Naval Aviation Supply Depot,\nShip or Station Phila., 11, Pa.          Date  22 February 1945\n\nFROM:      Supply Officer-in-Command\n                    Commanding Officer\n\nTO:    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT          15250\n\nSUBJECT:   REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE\n           REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE\n\n    In conformity with requirements of U.S. NAVY regulations, I\n\nreport the following leave of absence taken by:\n\nNAME    NEWHOUSE, DELBERT C.               FILE NO.   177283\n        LAST        FIRST       MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS Lt.(jg) USN                 SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF   SOinC 1st End.          DATED    6 February 1945\n\nNOTE:  Use either (A) or (B), DO NOT use both for same leave.\n\n    (A) LEAVE:  total number of days, including any travel time\n\n                                                         5 days\n\n    (B) Delay counting as leave or leave between stations:\n        Total number of days, excluding preparation period\n        of 4 days and excluding allowance for travel time\n        from old to new station Via shortest usually\n        traveled route", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d9031e32cacea7e3bac2e7317c1e57484cd427e8c996984301521c1db668fee8", "output_sha256": "3abe3c5ee580007f86ece13acc94094e6bd0db967a555e74a71e5e7a9853ba92", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:36.994370+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p275", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 275, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "ADDRESS REPLY TO\nCOMMANDANT\nFOURTH NAVAL DISTRICT\nAND REFER TO NO.\n\n00\n                        FOURTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n                         DISTRICT STAFF HEADQUARTERS\n                              BUILDING NO. 4\n                        NAVY YARD, PHILADELPHIA 12, PA.\n\n                                                    24 November 1944.\n\n                         4ND    T—12218\n\n\nFrom:    The Commandant, Fourth Naval District.\n\nTo  :   Lieutenant, junior grade, Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, (JN 177283),\n         Naval Aviation Supply Depot,\n              Oxford Avenue & Martin's Mill Road, Philadelphia 11, Pa.\n\n\n\nVia  :  Supply Officer in Command, Naval Aviation Supply Depot,\n         Oxford Avenue & Martin's Mill Road, Philadelphia 11, Pa.\n\nSubject: Temporary Additional Duty.\n\n\n     1.  Proceed to the place (or places—in the order given) indicated below, for temporary duty.\nThis is in addition to your present duties and upon the completion thereof, you will return to your station\nand resume your regular duties:\n\n        On or about 24 November 1944, to the Bureau of Aeronautics,\nPhotographic Division, Navy Department, Washington, D.C., to attend a\nconference.\n\n     2.  Reimbursement will be on a per diem basis in accordance with\nALNAV 80.\n\n\n\n\n                                                    M. F. DRAEMEL\n\nCopies to:\n  Bupers\n  BuAer\n                                                    FINISHED FILE PERS-1820\n\nPhila. Na. Yd.—11961—6-10-44—30,000 over 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8a636633e4df5431c4fc76b5b017491c5f00153c0e85a98dbe8b5f16ef0b0063", "output_sha256": "40c1a2ee4b01441177208af9846b58c3bdfe1ca5e7d94ce9bd9d44866a63f5cc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:38.756666+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p276", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 276, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BNP 323\n(Revised April 1943)\n\n                                    B\n\n              REPORT OF COMPLIANCE WITH ORDERS\n                           (See notes below)\n\nNaval Aviation Supply Depot, Phila., Pa.    9/13/44\n              (Ship or Station)                          (Date)\nFrom:  Lieut.(jg) Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.   File No.  177283\n              (Typewrite or print rank and name)\nTo: BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL,\n         Via Commanding Officer.\nSubject: Report of compliance with orders.\n                            024605              31 July,\nReference: (a) Order No. __________ dated __________________, 1944\n                  issued by Bureau of Naval Personnel\n\n1. Reference (a) was received on ____6 September________, 1944.\n    |was detached from |\n  I |was discharged from| U.S. Naval Air Station, Coco Solo, Canal\n    |completed          |                                          Zone\n  on ______________________6 September,_________________________, 1944.\n                                (Date of detachment)\n\n    |assumed command of |\n  I |reported           | Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Phila., Pa.\n    |arrived            |\n  on ______________________13 September,_________________________, 1944.\n                                (Date of reporting)\n\n2. (a) I sailed from United States to duty outside continental limits thereof on _______________,\n                                                                                  (Date of sailing)\n        19______ (this item to be inserted only if applicable).\n\n   (b) I arrived in United States from duty outside continental limits thereof on  9/7/44      ,\n                                                                                  (Date of arrival)\n        19______ (this item to be inserted only if applicable).\n\n\n                                          D.C. Newhouse\n                                    ______________________________\n                                              (Signature)\n\nForwarded by  E. M. CRONIN, Capt(SC) USN - Acting Supply Officer\n                                              in Command.\n\nNOTE (a).—It is a matter of special importance to officers' records that this form be made out with care\nand accuracy and forwarded to the Bureau of Naval Personnel promptly.  In the case of aviation and staff\ncorps officers, a copy marked DUPLICATE should also be forwarded.\n        (b).—In cases of delay counting as leave, the forwarding of this form does not dispense with the\nrequirement of forwarding Form BNP 321 (Report of Leave of Absence), which should be forwarded in\naddition to this form.\n                        U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE   16—29671-3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9b4aedbd4f7758d398a9a3d490c8a0b64bf24c57ff40de8bd504b433729c61c3", "output_sha256": "7383d28effa451e98f590476c3a258ae48ea6ff441d1495b7d4f820c629d7617", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:41.348059+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p277", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 277, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 321—Revised July 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nSHIP OR STATION  NAS, COCO SOLO, CANAL ZONE          DATE  21 August 1944\n\nFROM:    COMMANDING OFFICER\n                              COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:   BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n         XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n\n         IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME  NEWHOUSE,        Delbert          Clement            FILE NO.  177283\n        LAST              FIRST             MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS    Ensign    USN                            SIGNAL No.  13749\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF  NAS COCO SOLO, CANAL ZONE               DATED  6/26/44\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n\n   (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME              30\n\n   (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n      TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n      EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n      VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE...............................  ----\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE    16 July 1944       EXPIRING DATE        15 August 1944\n\n                                      SIGNED  T. DURFEE, Comdr., USNR.\n                                                    COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE.  THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.\n                                            16—33335-2    U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3ce54eeebc78d2493f4fe1a1840e50d2afed7e74f7ea652dd98bf3cbf3d60c43", "output_sha256": "d6f73f0289a03fc83a0fc65d14745cf23e6786bdc5938482650f7ce9ab447dbc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:44.107336+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p278", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 278, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177285\nPers-3163-DMB-5\n\n                                        31 July 1944.\n\n\nFrom:           The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nTo:             Ens. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n                Naval Air Station,\n                Coco Solo, C. Z.\n\nVia:            ComFifteen.\n\nSubject:        Change of duty.\n\n1.  When directed by the Commandant, Fifteenth Naval District,\nupon the reporting of your relief Lieutenant (jg) James T. Griffin,\nA-V(S), USNR, you will proceed to a port in the United States,\nvia first available government transportation, including air,\nand upon arrival further proceed to Philadelphia, Pa., and report\nto the Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply Depot, for\nduty, reporting by letter to the Commandant, Fourth Naval District.\n\n2.  You are hereby authorized to delay for a period of twenty\ndays in reporting in compliance with these orders, such delay\nto count as leave.\n\n3.  Keep the Bureau of Naval Personnel and your new station\nadvised of your address.\n\n4.  The attention of the Supply Officer in Command, Naval\nAviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia, Pa., is invited to the\nfact that you have been trained in photographic supply.\n\n5.  The Secretary of the Navy has determined that this employment\non shore duty is required by the public interests.\n\n\n\nCC:                             RANDALL JACOBS.\n  CNO (Op 32).\n  CO, NAS, Coco Solo, C. Z.\n  SupOfinComd, AvSupDepot,\n    Philadelphia, Pa.\n  ComFour.\n\n                                                024605\n\n                    Jacket copy\n                    Pers 82233\n                    Pers 3101\n                    Pers 102\n                    Pers 3163", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "752be854f9c97bc3184e738b8591f360830e9512cbdd59029c70874c73dab9ca", "output_sha256": "242b9e9ed53e561239724e64b9eac8ae717aa80de189e2fe47dce4c8f91016b9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:46.166324+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p279", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 279, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply refer to Initials\n    and No.\n\nOp-32-B1-CAN[REDACTED]    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n00/NEWHOUSE, D.C.  OFFICE OF THE CHIEF OF NAVAL OPERATIONS\n                        WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n\n                           29 JUL 1944\n\n        From:     The Chief of Naval Operations.\n        To:       The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n        Subj:     Ensign Delbert C. Newhouse, USN, #177283\n                  Change of duty - Request for, via Com 15\n\n1.  It is requested that Ensign Newhouse be detached from duty\nUS Naval Air Station, Coco Solo, when directed upon reporting of\nrelief (Lt.(jg) James T. Griffin, A-V(S), USNR.) and ordered\nto proceed (with twenty (20) days' delay) and report to the Supply\nOfficer-in-Command, Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia,\nPennsylvania for duty. by ltr Com 4\n\n2.  It is requested that a paragraph be added to subject officer's\norders stating that he has been trained in photographic supply.\n\n\n                                          A. O. Preil (\n                                          By Direction\n\n\n        Lt.(jg) Noyes\n        28 July, 1944\n        Leona Monk\n\n        Detail B1\n                        FINISHED FILE PLEASE SIGN\n                                        JUL 29 1944\n\n                                        3163 frey\n                                        air ltr\n                                        Out 7/31\n\n\n                          024605", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4c3d63c2013af7472d3fc258b4e397e609385bd3e1bccd9d2e5df6f3f2e3be67", "output_sha256": "ca000b1760af1c3f58e87cddd532244d41b8e8d21bc1a907b02fdc7222475be2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:47.965783+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p280", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 280, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283\n                    5th Endorsement on\n                    Request for leave, dated 25 Mar. 1943.\n                                          NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                                          DEPARTMENT\n                                          RECEIVED\n                                          177283\n                                          1943 MAY 22 PM 12 00\n\n                    PORT DIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nP16-3               Naval Transportation Service\nGWDD/jas/1jc        Eleventh Naval District\nSerial B-SP-15433   242 West Seventh Street\n                    San Pedro, California.\n\n                              18 May, 1943.\n\nRESTRICTED\n\nFrom:           The Port Director (NTS), San Pedro.\nTo  :           Photographer Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, U.S. Navy.\n\nSubject:        Orders.\n\nReferences:     (a)\n                (b)\n\n     1.         Reported, 18 May, 1943.\n\n     2.         You will proceed immediately to the S/S.\nU.S.S. CAMERIA  for transportation to 15th Nav. Dist.  Upon\nArrival at that destination you will report to the nearest\nNaval activity for further instructions.\n\n     3.         During the period covered by this endorsement\nthere were no Government quarters available for assignment to\nyou and none were assigned.\n\n     4.         The contents of these orders are to be con-\nsidered confidential and are not to be disclosed to other than\nproper Naval authorities.           FINISHED\n\n                                          G. W. D. DASHIELL\n\nCopy to:\n  BuPers (Air mail)\n  Comsowespec (Air mail)\n  Com 12 ND\n  PD 12 ND\n  Com Fifteen (Air mail)\n\n8  10  22  23  24  31  32  36  62  211  215  222  885\n\n                                          NOTED\n                                          PERS-23231", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a653afd95796a6e7ad8cf5d3411d168a4f8b9fecac6a6e63f4743e2726b3da04", "output_sha256": "e753c024245896382ed42e308b060c1e14bd3927319dcf6d073b182cf0f7b4e2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:49.978145+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p281", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 281, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "P16-4/00                    OFFICE OF                           BUR. OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                    THE NAVAL DISTRICT COMMANDANT              NAVY DEPARTMENT\n                              NAVY 121                              RECEIVED\n                         FLEET POST OFFICE\n                           NEW YORK, N.Y.                    1943 JUN 4  PM 3  35\n\n                                                June 1, 1943\nFrom:        The Commandant Fifteenth Naval District\nTo  :        Photographer\n             Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\n\nVia:\n\nSubject:     Change of duty.\n\n     1.      Upon the receipt of these orders and when directed\nby the proper authority you will consider yourself relieved of\nyour present duties and all other duties that may have been\nassigned you.\n\n     2.      You will report to Commanding Officer Naval Air Station\nfor such duty as he may assign.\n\n\n\n                                               S. C. MC CORMICK,\n                                               By direction.\n\ncc:\n     Bupers\n\n                    FINISHED FILE PERS 323\n\n                                                    6083\n\n\n\n\n15 ND.\n\n\n                                               NOTED\n                                           PERS-22931\n\n1    6    10    22    23    24    [ILLEGIBLE]    32    36    62    211    215    222\n\n     \"X\" out and init[ILLEGIBLE] over your encircled Pers. No. before releasing", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4d72fe3a6389689ec58131c0b95d7a102839cd5e7776b68c93cfa6d41f5d0edd", "output_sha256": "043ef7dc5e97ac88fc8d07a98546e0b6c7e5809b54852cad13460eb8687fea1a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:51.623511+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p282", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 282, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283\nBNP 321 REVISED FEB. 1943\nREPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nSHIP OR STATION Hdqtrs. 15th Naval District.          DATE May 27, 1943.\n\nFROM: The Commandant, Fifteenth Naval District.\n                    COMMANDING OFFICER\nTO:    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL, NAVY DEPARTMENT\n\nSUBJECT: {REPORT OF LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n          {REPORT OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OF ABSENCE.\n\n        IN CONFORMITY WITH REQUIREMENTS OF U. S. NAVY REGULATIONS, I REPORT THE FOLLOWING LEAVE OF ABSENCE\nTAKEN BY:\n\nNAME NEWHOUSE,     Delbert          C.              FILE NO.\n          LAST          FIRST           MIDDLE\n\nRANK AND CORPS  Photographer, USN.                  SIGNAL NO.\n\nUNDER ORDERS OF Comdt.15th N.D. P18-1/00/EFA/bwj(60) DATED  3/23/43\n\nNOTE: USE EITHER (A) OR (B).  DO NOT USE BOTH FOR SAME LEAVE.\n\n   (A) LEAVE: TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, INCLUDING ANY TRAVEL TIME    Thirty (30)\n\n   (B) DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE OR LEAVE BETWEEN STATIONS:\n       TOTAL NUMBER OF DAYS, EXCLUDING PREPARATION PERIOD OF 4 DAYS AND\n       EXCLUDING ALLOWANCE FOR TRAVEL TIME FROM OLD TO NEW STATION\n       VIA SHORTEST USUALLY TRAVELED ROUTE................  ..................\n\nINSERT INCLUSIVE DATES TO AGREE WITH NUMBER OF DAYS LEAVE.  SEE INSTRUCTIONS BELOW.\n\nCOMMENCING DATE  April 17, 1943.         EXPIRING DATE   May 16, 1943\n\n                    Finished USNR Register File\n                                        SIGNED S.C. MCCORMICK, By direction.\n                                                    COMMANDING OFFICER\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n   1. THE DAY OF DEPARTURE FROM STATION OR DUTY COUNTS AS A DAY OF DUTY; THE DAY OF RETURN AS A DAY OF\nLEAVE. THIS REFERS TO LEAVE TAKEN WHEN NOT DETACHED FROM SHIP OR STATION (SEE ARTICLE 1727, NAVY REGULATIONS).\n   2. IN CASES OF AUTHORIZED DELAY COUNTING AS LEAVE, THIS FORM SHOULD BE SUBMITTED IN ADDITION TO THE\nB-SLIP FORM.\n   3. THIS REPORT WILL BE MADE AT EXPIRATION OF LEAVE BY THE IMMEDIATE SUPERIOR OF THE OFFICER TO WHOM\nTHE LEAVE IS GRANTED AND FORWARDED IMMEDIATELY TO THE NAVY DEPARTMENT (BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL).\nCARE MUST BE TAKEN TO INSURE THAT CORRECT NUMBER OF DAYS OF LEAVE IS REPORTED AND CORRESPONDS WITH THE\nINCLUSIVE DATES REPORTED.\n                                                    16—33335-1    U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "71de7009138b1b9b8ce2bb5ef7c118a2ad32fbb0f7a62c7f35bfe3a8195d90bf", "output_sha256": "6875269c4aff968b4f86030df90cab7df58bc4a25b86e3d0c91e82daf858a81e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:54.490980+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p283", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 283, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REFER TO No.\n\nP15-4/00/HFH/bmm                    OFFICE OF\n                        COMMANDANT FIFTEENTH NAVAL DISTRICT              177283\n                                    BALBOA, CANAL ZONE          1943 FEB 15 PM 5 30\n\n\n          N.I.                                        January 23, 1943\n\n                                                            12001501\n                                                        15NO BALBOA-HGTS\nFrom:       The Commandant\nTo:         Photographer\n            Newhouse, D. C., USN\nVia:        Officer-in-Charge Outlying Bases\nSubject:    Change of duty\n\n     1.     Upon the receipt of these orders and when directed\nby your Commanding Officer you will consider yourself relieved of\nyour present duties and all other duty assigned you; will report\nvia such government transportation including air as may be\narranged to Balboa, Canal Zone.\n\n     2.     Upon arrival Balboa, Canal Zone report to the\nCommandant Fifteenth Naval District for duty with the Officer-in-\nCharge District Photographic Activities.\n\n\n                                              H. C. McCORMICK\n                                              By direction\n\ncc:\n  BuPers ✓\n\n                    V30015O1\n\n        Robinson - P3V41          P3211\n                  ack.\n\n1  1/6  6 10  10 22  22 23  23 24  24     32 32 36    62  6    215  222 222  232\n\nFINISHED FILE PERS 283                                              GL\n                                                              NOTED PERS 283", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e534b93235c9570f244c9cc3aa440ac5f1a21781185f3fac449fab9b0c531b56", "output_sha256": "a6caeed316d001afad583db2a233a1dde5182ef7c2a66d6a75a09fe8f785ba6d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:56.308456+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p284", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 284, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "QR/F18-1/CO/EFA/DWj/(60)  SECOND ENDORSEMENT\nHdqtrs., 15th Naval District, Balboa, C. Z.    March 23, 1943.\n\nFrom:          The Commandant, Fifteenth Naval District.\nTo:            Photographer Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, U.S.N.\n\nVia:           The Co-ordinator of Photographic Activities,\n               Fifteenth Naval District (Division Officer).\n\nSubject:       Leave of absence - request for.    1943 MA.    177383\n\n     1.        Return granted.  Arrangements for return transportation should be made immediately upon arrival in the United States.\n\n     2.        For security of information, the Commander in\nChief, United States Fleet, directs that personnel on leave should\nnot participate in a press conference or talk to reporters or talk\nover the radio, except after consultation with and clearance of the\nsubject matter by a Public Relations Officer of the Navy or Marine\nCorps.\n\n\n                                   T. S. KING,\n                                   Chief of Staff.\ncc:BuPers. ✓\n\n\n\n\n                                        FINISHED FILE PERS 31954\n\n1  6  10  22  25        01   52  30   02  211  215  222  252\n\n\"x\" out and initial        your corrected Pers. No. before releasing", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dd80a2d37b73d178e17caa608556a80e7ae0294e67644bdf88f65f0b69e884fa", "output_sha256": "4f8a75fab67dabc66ce81ea2fc446e585a03c622661d00f5690f59fe4cf04e5e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:40:58.817927+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p285", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 285, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REFER TO No.\n\n                    OFFICE OF\n             COMMANDANT FIFTEENTH NAVAL DISTRICT\n                    BALBOA, CANAL ZONE\n\n\n                                        March 25, 1943\n\n\nFrom:       Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S.N.\nTo  :       The Commandant, Fifteenth Naval District.\nVia :       The Co-ordinator of Photographic Activities,\n            Fifteenth Naval District (Division Officer).\n\nSubject:    Leave of Absence - request for.\n\n\n     1.     It is requested that I be granted thirty (30) days leave\nin the United States to begin on or about April 15, 1943.\n\n     2.     I have been on duty outside the United States since November 16, 1940 and have had no leave since March, 1940.\n\n     3.     On October 25, 1939 I was transferred from the Naval Air\nStation, Sitka, Alaska to Patrol Squadron Forty-five at the Naval Air\nStation, San Diego, California.  This squadron was redesignated VP Squadron Fourteen and I was transferred from there on November 16, 1940 to\nthe Naval Air Station, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba where, on August 10, 1942,\nI received orders to report to the Commandant Fifteenth Naval District\nfor assignment to duty.\n\n     4.     If this request be granted, my address while in the\nUnited States will be:\n\n                         1210 S.E. 37th Avenue,\n                         Portland, Oregon\n\n     5.     I am not a member of any court or board.\n\n\n                                   Delbert C. Newhouse FILEPERS 31954\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - FINISHED - - - - - -\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT          The Office of the\n                    CO-ORDINATOR OF PHOTOGRAPHIC ACTIVITIES\n                         Fifteenth Naval District\n\n                                        March 25, 1943\n\n     1.     Forwarded recommending approval.\n\n\n                                   H.E. SHEFFERS", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "57e8ec7bffc3c5025133aac8b2ea3cfc9bf1db93088a9347fa1bfbe1480913db", "output_sha256": "5f1b8e2d51016e34953cb37316967267481ad49bb7f2307138a47c0d954edf15", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:01.008983+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p286", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 286, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "REFER TO No.\n\nP16-4/00/RPR/le                    OFFICE OF\n                    COMMANDANT FIFTEENTH NAVAL DISTRICT      177283\n                              BALBOA, CANAL ZONE              1943 FEB 22 AM 9 30\n\n                                        T-495\n\n                                                    February 17, 1943.\n\n\nFrom:          The Commandant.\nTo  :          Photographer\n                 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\nSubject:       Temporary additional duty.\n\n          1.       On or about February 2, 1943 you will proceed from\nU.S. Naval Base, Santa Elena, Ecuador, to Quito, Ecuador, for\ntemporary additional duty in connection with making photographs\nas may be necessary of the source of food supply of the base.\n\n          2.       This is in addition to your regular duties and upon\nthe completion thereof, you will return to your station and resume\nyour regular duties.\n\n          3.       A per diem of $6.00 in lieu of subsistence is\nauthorized while in an air travel status and away from your station\nin the execution of these orders.\n\n          4.       Transportation will be via government aircraft.\n\n\n                                              C.H. Isello\n                                        D. E. CUMMINGS,\n                                              Acting.\n\n(Confirming written\n  orders of C.O. Santa\n  Elena Bay, dated January                DT- 36753\n  26, 1943.)\n\n\n| 6   10   22   23   24   31   32   36   62   211   215   222\nBarrera\n        \"B\" out end [ILLEGIBLE]              [ILLEGIBLE] before releasing\n\n                                        Finished File De[ILLEGIBLE]\n                                             MAR 13 1943", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8693c399fb18e52526301fd5d26b7c6bdc329c1408ee691ff4d8b8b4622c6fd7", "output_sha256": "44a45293845ac2739f1682705c2481d2abb8648d03dba9afa37a7b15c55aa3ec", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:02.890580+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p287", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 287, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NB125/P16-4/00/dcn\n\n                              U.S. NAVAL BASE,\n                           Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador,\n                              January 26, 1943.\n\n\nFrom:          The Commanding Officer.\nTo :           Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S.N.\n\nSubject:       Temporary Additional Duties.\n\n        1.     Upon receipt of these orders and when directed by proper\nauthority you will proceed via Military Aircraft, on an inspection tour of\nthe Quito, Ecuador area, to inspect and make such photographs as may be\nnecessary of the source of food supply of this base.\n\n        2.     You are authorized $6.00 per diem for necessary expenses\nwhile on this inspection.\n\n        3.     Upon completion of this inspection you will return to this\nbase and continue with your regular duties.\n\n\n                                        J. R. LITCHFIELD\n                                        Commander, USNR\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nFirst Endorsement.          Office of the Naval Attache,\nOO/N.S.Salinas                  Quito, Ecuador\n                                4 February 1943.\n\nFrom: U. S. Naval Attache, Quito, Ecuador.\nTo  : Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S.N.          7-c  Issue\n\n      1. Reported. Upon completion of temporary duty carry out the remainder\nof your orders.\n\n                                        Robert S. Black, Jr.\n                                        Assistant.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT                U.S. NAVAL BASE,\n                               Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador,\n                                  February 12, 1943.\n\nFrom:    The Commanding Officer.\nTo:      Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S.N.\n\n        1.     In compliance with the above orders you departed this base at\n0700 February 2, 1943.\n\n        2.     You returned to duty this date.\n                                        Finished File-Detail-Blnca\n                                        MAR 13 1943\n                                        J. R. LITCHFIELD", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4149d2c51c7c8b1295749d8d51481160fce0d75062cdde9b581fb9aeed524f87", "output_sha256": "4149d2c51c7c8b1295749d8d51481160fce0d75062cdde9b581fb9aeed524f87", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:05.238137+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p288", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 288, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICER'S\nSELECTION BOARD JACKET\n\n(1)  PHOTO – CERTIFICATES – COMMISSIONS\n         A.  PHOTOGRAPH\n         B.  BIRTH\n         C.  CITIZENSHIP\n         D.  EDUCATION-TRAINING\n         E.  COMMISSIONS\n         F.  APPOINTMENTS\n         G.  ACCEPTANCES\n         H.  WAIVERS\n         I.  OATHS OF OFFICE\n         J.  CLASSIFICATION CHANGES\n\n(2)  CITATIONS – AWARDS – DISCIPLINE\n\n(3)  REPORTS – TRANSCRIPTS – APPLICATIONS\n         K.  PERSONAL BIOGRAPHY\n         L.  STATEMENTS OF SERVICE\n         M.  REPORTS OF PHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n         N.  REPORTS OF MEDICAL SURVEYS\n         O.  APPLICATION FOR COMMISSION\n         P.  NOTICE OF SEPARATION\n         Q.  REQUESTS FOR CHANGE OF DUTY\n\n(4)  MISCELLANEOUS CORRESPONDENCE\n         (STAMPED: \"SELECTION BOARD\")\n\nSEPARATED\n\n\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0320e3a60d03116e1b4adf92820002587f6fe3916247aecaf51960136d16f607", "output_sha256": "0320e3a60d03116e1b4adf92820002587f6fe3916247aecaf51960136d16f607", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:06.655163+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p289", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 289, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "U.S. NAVAL RECEIVING STATION\n       U.S. NAVAL STATION\n  SAN DIEGO 36, CALIFORNIA\n\n                                                         991/GHH:rb\n                                                         1900\n                                                         31 March 1960\n\nTHIRD ENDORSEMENT on BUPERS ORDS 021081 of 29 February 1960\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, U.S. Naval Receiving Station, San Diego 36, California\nTo:    CHPHOT W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\nSubj:  Orders relieving you of all active duty incident to your retirement on\n       1 April 1960\n\n1.  Reported 25 March 1960.\n\n2.  Government quarters and messing facilities were available to you but not to your\ndependents, if any.\n\n3.  Physical examination incident to your retirement not required in accordance with\nArticle C-10409, BuPers Manual.\n\n       31 March 1960                              B.C. LUSHBOUGH, LT, MC, USNR\n\n4.  As verified by your officer leave record (NavPers 329), your earned leave credit\ncomputed through the effective date of retirement is sixty (60) days.\n\n5.  Detached 31 March 1960, you will regard yourself released from all active duty\neffective 2400 this date at which time you are transferred to inactive duty on the\nRetired List of the U.S. Navy with the rank of Lieutenant but with retired pay based\non the rank of Chief Photographer W-4.\n\n6.  You have stated that upon release from active duty, your home address, the place\nat which you may be reached at any time by orders or other official communications\nwill be 652 Burkham St., El Cajon, California.\n\n7.  Inform the Chief of Naval Personnel and the Commandant of the Naval District in\nwhich your home address as set forth above is located of any change in such address.\nSuch notification also shall be forwarded to the U.S. Naval Finance Center (Special\nPayment Division), Cleveland 15, Ohio in order that your retired pay check may not\nbe delayed, due to incorrect address.\n\n\n                                                    G. H. HANSELL Jr.\n                                                    By direction\n\nCopy to:\nBUPERS - DATPROBR\nDNI\nCOM - 11\n\n                         Attached Files, Pers 19233\n\n                                                              APR 0 6 1960", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "705816ed9d39e5f3e931fcbaee71620f2c23e8c41b8e99690ef188b09fda8dd1", "output_sha256": "8fb0a9e5eb58d161e97ee06d444bd373479dc1474e841f362594e38c039e34d5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:09.010322+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p290", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 290, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "PACIFIC FLEET PHOTO-TRIANGULATION GROUP\n U. S. NAVAL STATION, BOX 144\n SAN DIEGO 36, CALIFORNIA\n\n                                          PFPTG:RWJ:gt\n                                          1320\n                                          Ser: 44\n                                          25 March 1960\n\n\nFrom: Officer in Charge, Pacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group\nTo:   CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj: Orders relieving you of all active duty incident to your\n      retirement\n\n1. Detached this date. You will report immediately to the Commanding\nOfficer, U.S. Naval Receiving Station, San Diego, California for temporary\nduty in connection with your retirement processing.\n\n2. No expense to the government is authorized in the execution of these\norders.\n\n\n                         ROBERT W. JOHNSON", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3f05a4f3e068880a514865f71ab7c238b16b7f5cf3e75904d0ceaa2e488bb7f0", "output_sha256": "3f05a4f3e068880a514865f71ab7c238b16b7f5cf3e75904d0ceaa2e488bb7f0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:10.300314+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p291", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 291, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "PFPTG:RWJ:BS\n1821\nSer: 39\n14 March 1960\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT\n\nFrom: Officer in Charge, Pacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group\nTo:   CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\n1. Delivered.\n\n\n                              ROBERT W. JOHNSON", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9d78e45277b45f687ab22ea41b222464367b026c1e22e9a17065ee85482e320e", "output_sha256": "9d78e45277b45f687ab22ea41b222464367b026c1e22e9a17065ee85482e320e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:11.090535+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p292", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 292, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/8311\nFFS-1:NI:rle\n1321\n8 March 1960\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on BUPERS Orders 021081 of 29 Feb 1960\n\nFrom:  Commander Training Command, U. S. Pacific Fleet\nTo:    CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\nVia:   Officer in Charge, Pacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group\n\nSubj:  Orders relieving you of all active duty incident to your\n       retirement\n\n1.  Readdressed and forwarded for delivery.\n\n2.  When directed by the Officer in Charge, Pacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group on 31 March 1960, you will proceed and carry out your basic\norders.\n\n\n                              T. M. FLECK\n                              Chief of Staff", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2ea36c60283f264e94eb9c0a7ab1588b5a8d8b8cae78c823535b4e35af87d211", "output_sha256": "8ccd6e1b89793161525bb3e9fd2476ee3f60ac294a4e062c49b3e8e2868e46fd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:12.302752+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p293", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 293, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "IMPORTANT: Forward only this copy to BuPers\nupon reporting to final destination. Include\nall endorsements. (See Art. C-5407 (4)\nBuPers Manual)\n\n                                                177283/8311\n                                                Pers-B721-cbc-2\n                                                29 February 1960\n            AIRMAIL\n\nFrom: Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:   CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n      Pacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group\n\nVia:  Commander, Training Command, Pacific Fleet\n\nSubj: Orders relieving you of all active duty incident to your retirement\n\nRef:  (a) Sections 1 and 5, Chapter 14, BuPers Manual\n      (b) BuPers Instruction 1811.1A\n\n1.  Your request to be transferred to the retired list was approved by the Secretary\nof the Navy, effective 1 April 1960.\n\n2.  When directed by your commanding officer on 31 March 1960 you will regard\nyourself detached from all duties which may have been assigned you and will proceed\nto your home of selection.  You will regard yourself relieved of all active duty in\nthe Navy effective at 2400 on date of detachment.\n\n3.  On 1 April 1960 you will be transferred to the retired list with the rank\nof Chief Photographer, W-4 pursuant to the provisions of Title 10,\nU.S. Code, Sections 1293, 1315 and 1371.\n\n4.  It having been determined that you served satisfactorily in the rank of\nlieutenant you are hereby advanced, effective 1 April 1960\nto the rank of lieutenant on the retired list and with the retired pay based on\nthe rank of Chief Photographer, W-4, pursuant to the provisions of Title 10, U.S.\nCode, Section 6151 as amended.\n\n5.  Attention is invited to references (a) and (b) concerning general information\naffecting the retirement of officers.\n\n6.  If you are hospitalized at any time during the period preceding the date of your\nretirement, you should advise the Chief of Naval Personnel by message concerning the\ndiagnosis, prognosis, and probable period of hospitalization.\n\n7.  You will not be required to take a new physical examination unless a material\nchange in your physical condition has occurred subsequent to your recent retirement\nphysical examination.\n\n8.  It is requested that you report your mail address in accordance with Article\nB-2206 (7), Bureau of Naval Personnel Manual.\n\n9.  Accounting data 1701453.2218  030  22/31600.140\n\n10.  Enter in item 11c, DD Form 214:  BuPers ltr Pers-B721-cbc-2 of 29 February 1960,\n569, Voluntary retirement after twenty years' service - Warrant Officer - 10 USC 1293.\n\nCopy to:              Jacket copy\nNAVFINCEN CLEVE SPD (2)  Pers-B74\n                          B812    B115\n                          B721    B1314\n                          B52 (2)         021081      W. R. SMEDBERG, III", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b58bf1759fa97c2c7eec1b8fbff8b60a983a564130a733cb4ea618bfc00136a1", "output_sha256": "d8a4e99fc7a3ed28d51e9f16ddffecaa5e99db01b3dc1ef05612b241c01b81f2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:15.339669+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p294", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 294, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 2259 (Rev. 1-59)          OFFICER DESIGNATOR CODE CHANGE                    S-1\n\n60-6170                                                    DATE    30 June 1960\nTHE DESIGNATOR CODE OF THE OFFICER NAMED BELOW WAS APPROVED FOR CHANGE:\nNAME (Last, in caps)              (First)              (Middle)       RANK          FILE NO.\n\nNEWHOUSE,                    Delbert              C.             LT           177283\nCHANGED FROM                     CHANGED TO\n                                     1353                    USNR          X USN  Ret\n\n\n     APPROVAL RECOMMENDED BY\n\n     RELEASE APPROVED BY\n\n X   EFFECTIVE  4-6-60 per orders of 2-29-60 per jacket review\n\n     PER\n\n\nCOPIES TO:\n  FINISHED FILE\n  QUALIFICATIONS FILE\n                                                   J. E. HOLLAND\n                                                   (Officer Designator Section)\n                                                   Pers B765\nGPO  16—74534-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d0aa6e62c442eb554ddf7db564a384487819fe5fdf0e8ed2774aa35ddaf62e8f", "output_sha256": "d0aa6e62c442eb554ddf7db564a384487819fe5fdf0e8ed2774aa35ddaf62e8f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:16.588204+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p295", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 295, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "S-1\n\n\n177283/8311\nPers-B721-cbc-2\n29 February 1960\n\nAIRMAIL\n\nFrom: Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo: CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\nPacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group\n\nVia: Commander, Training Command, Pacific Fleet\n\nSubj: Orders relieving you of all active duty incident to your retirement\n\nRef: (a) Sections 1 and 5, Chapter 14, BuPers Manual\n(b) BuPers Instruction 1811.1A\n\n1. Your request to be transferred to the retired list was approved by the Secretary\nof the Navy, effective 1 April 1960.\n\n2. When directed by your commanding officer on 31 March 1960 you will regard\nyourself detached from all duties which may have been assigned you and will proceed\nto your home of selection. You will regard yourself relieved of all active duty in\nthe Navy effective at 2400 on date of detachment.\n\n3. On 1 April 1960 you will be transferred to the retired list with the rank\nof Chief Photographer, W-4 pursuant to the provisions of Title 10,\nU.S. Code, Sections 1293, 1315 and 1371.\n\n4. It having been determined that you served satisfactorily in the rank of\nlieutenant you are hereby advanced, effective 1 April 1960\nto the rank of lieutenant on the retired list and with the retired pay based on\nthe rank of Chief Photographer, W-4, pursuant to the provisions of Title 10, U.S.\nCode, Section 6151 as amended.\n\n5. Attention is invited to references (a) and (b) concerning general information\naffecting the retirement of officers.\n\n6. If you are hospitalized at any time during the period preceding the date of your\nretirement, you should advise the Chief of Naval Personnel by message concerning the\ndiagnosis, prognosis, and probable period of hospitalization.\n\n7. You will not be required to take a new physical examination unless a material\nchange in your physical condition has occurred subsequent to your recent retirement\nphysical examination.\n\n8. It is requested that you report your mail address in accordance with Article\nB-2206 (7), Bureau of Naval Personnel Manual.\n\n9. Accounting data 1701453.2218 030 22/31600.140\n\n10. Enter in item 11c, DD Form 214: BuPers ltr Pers-B721-cbc-2 of 29 February 1960,\n569, Voluntary retirement after twenty years' service - Warrant Officer - 10 USC 1293.\n\nCopy to: Jacket copy\nNAVFINCEN CLEVE SPD (2) Pers-B74\nB812 B115\nB721 B1314\nB52 (2) 021081 W. R. SMEDBERG, III", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a3c973abb92e4a495d82178c991f9bb3852e0ceeacf1ec0be5005acb5ef8c85b", "output_sha256": "797ce3236182854232c6e75745c2866436d8b84bbed7def8608abf61952df50a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:19.424331+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p296", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 296, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICERS ORDER MEMORANDUM                    NAVPERS 1152 (Rev. 5-59)\nRANK          NAME (First, Middle Initial, rd)                    CORPS        USN        FILE NO./DESIGNATOR\nCHPHOT W4    Delbert C. M HOUSE                                   USNR       177283/8311\nAT   Pacific Fleet Photo-triangulation Group                DATE              ORIGINATING PERS\n     Fleet Camera Group Pacific                               24 Feb 60         B721\nVIA  Contraper\nLETTER ORDERS              MESSAGE ORDERS                          DATE OUT BY        CONTROL NO.\n  PLAIN       XXX   AIR      DEFERRED      ROUTINE      PRIORITY     29 Feb            021081\nTYPE OF ORDERS\n  CHANGE                  NEW            RECALL        RECALL        APPROVAL        AUTHORI-\n  OF DUTY      X   RAD    APPT.                        & RAD         OF ACTION       ZATION\n  ORDCAN       ORDCOR     ORDMOD         CONTREAT\n                                                       ISSUED BY\n  UNDELORDCAN  UNORDCAN   FURORDMOD    