                                 S-1               552\n                                                             7b\n                                   Pers-B52-MOA/cg\n                                   177283/8311\n\n                                             11 FEB 1960    B5\n                                                            89°\nTHIRD ENDORSEMENT on ltr of CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN,\n                    dated 5 January 1960\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    Secretary of the Navy\n\nSubj:  Transfer to the Retired List of:\n       Chief Photographer, W-4 Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, U. S. Navy\n\nRef:   (a) SECNAVINST 1811.3A\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n2.  The request submitted in basic letter does not fall within any of\nthe criteria of sub-paragraph 4.a. of reference (a).  However, its\napproval would not be contrary to the best interests of the Service.\n\n3.  Pursuant to the foregoing and sub-paragraph 4.b. of reference (a),    B1141c\nI recommend that the attached request of subject named officer to be         [signature]\ntransferred to the retired list of officers of the Navy after completing\nmore than twenty-seven years' service be approved, effective 1 April 1960,\nand that he be transferred to the retired list in his present grade, or\nsuch other grade as he may be entitled to on date of retirement, in\naccordance with the provisions of U. S. Code, Title 10, Sections 1293,\n1315 and 1371.\n\n\n                                                              B[?]21\n                                                              [signature]\n\n                         ALMON E. LOOMIS\n                         Deputy Chief of Naval Personnel\n                                                              [checkmark]\n\n\n\n                                                              [initials]\n\n\n                                                              [initials]\n\n\n                    Finished File B52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1b6488857621456c14011756c0e24285121e0301ee0f55cf36bf9fdda1aaa8d2", "output_sha256": "31994f337413d9cb7f662b610977188b226a8b21a1272cf947c602d45e0dc78e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:27.051332+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p298", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 298, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Pers-B52-HOA/1mm S-1\n177283/8311\n5 February 1960\n\nMEMORANDUM TO PERS-B63a\n\nSubj: CHPHOT, W-4, Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN\n\n1. The official record of the subject indicates he held a higher temporary\ngrade in the U.S. Navy. It is requested that a determination be obtained\nfrom the Secretary of the Navy as to the highest rank or grade in which the\nsubject is deemed to have satisfactorily served. The subject's retirement\nis scheduled to be effective 1 April 1960.\n\n\n\n                              H. C. ANSON, JR.\n                              LCDR, USN\n                              Head, Non-Disability Retirement Branch\n\n\nTOTAL ACTIVE SERVICE:\n\n\n30 yrs. effective 1 March 1960\n\n\nPresent Duty Station:\n\nOfficer in Charge\nPacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group Headquarters\nU. S. Naval Station\nSan Diego 36, California\n\n\n\n\n                         Finished File Pers-B83", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e6814301a216fa08ea5c91b38ea5802ea23419fb45c5db0ab114d44d5285c55a", "output_sha256": "dc2bb2fc39ce6852ae57d7838d3b50df8723f483621f98f27e81c4b08e4e4dc5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:28.402044+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p299", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 299, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nOFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                                    S-1\n\n                                          177283/8311\n                                          12 FEB 1960\n\nFrom:  Secretary of the Navy\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nSubj:  Determination of highest federally recognized rank satisfactorily\n       served\n\nRef:   (a) 10 USC 6151, as amended\n\n1. Pursuant to reference (a), I have determined the highest grade and\nrank in which Delbert C. Newhouse has satisfactorily served to be that\nof lieutenant.\n\n                         W. B. Franke\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                    Finish File Pers B52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3507a9096c4144f98a2285a56964216070a585e7163967802ba78f578c065afb", "output_sha256": "a0b0a2743b76729e3d607ebc9d9bda0b9f5caf8ea146205e22328816547dcaca", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:29.525845+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p300", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 300, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nWASHINGTON 25, D.C.\n\n                                          IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                          Pers-B52-HOA/cg\n                                          177283/8311\n\n                                          11 FEB 1960\n\nTHIRD ENDORSEMENT on ltr of CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN,\n                dated 5 January 1960\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    Secretary of the Navy\n\nSubj:  Transfer to the Retired List of;\n       Chief Photographer, W-4 Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, U. S. Navy\n\nRef:   (a) SECNAVINST 1811.3A\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n2.  The request submitted in basic letter does not fall within any of\nthe criteria of sub-paragraph 4.a. of reference (a).  However, its\napproval would not be contrary to the best interests of the Service.\n\n3.  Pursuant to the foregoing and sub-paragraph 4.b. of reference (a),\nI recommend that the attached request of subject named officer to be\ntransferred to the retired list of officers of the Navy after completing\nmore than twenty-seven years' service be approved, effective 1 April 1960,\nand that he be transferred to the retired list in his present grade, or\nsuch other grade as he may be entitled to on date of retirement, in\naccordance with the provisions of U. S. Code, Title 10, Sections 1293,\n1315 and 1371.\n\n\n                    [signature]\n\n\n                    ALMON E. LOOMIS\n                    Deputy Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n\n\n\n\nfinished File B52          APPROVED SECNAV_______ 19 FEB 1960", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4df810710eee27162d525520ae2c8fc00dd00770c4840452c3ef209469352eaa", "output_sha256": "90ac3419c4b37d2ef6041513b24a3aa4e73fcdad18833b8aa473d938cdd19e1a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:31.484642+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p301", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 301, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "09 096L NW 9 F\n\nFF8-1:N1:jdw\n1800\nSer: 58\n8 JAN 1960\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on CHPHOT W-4 Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\nltr of 5 January 1960\n\nFrom: Commander Training Command, U. S. Pacific Fleet\nTo: Secretary of the Navy\nVia: Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nSubj: Retirement from Active Duty; request for\n\n1. Forwarded, recommending approval.\n\n\nT. M. Fleck\nChief of Staff\n\n\nCopy to:\nOIC PACFLT PHOTO-TRIANGULATION GRU\nCHPHOT W-4 D. C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\n\n\nFinished File B52\n2              APPROVED SECNAV  10 FEB 1960", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "235425be3c2b4828dec2deec