9-19T17:41:47.770069+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p305", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 305, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "fee\nS-1\nDEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\nIN REPLY REFER TO\nPers-B52-HOA/1mn\n177283/8311\n5 February 1960\n\nFrom: Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nTo: CHPHOT, W-4, Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nVia: Officer in Charge\nPacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group Headquarters\nU. S. Naval Station\nSan Diego 36, California\n\n\nSubj: Voluntary Retirement\n\nRef: (a) BuPers Instruction 1811.1A\n\nEncl: (1) Navy Guide for Retired and Fleet Reserve Personnel\n\n1. This is to acknowledge receipt of your letter of 5 January 1960 in\nwhich you have requested voluntary retirement effective 1 April 1960. \nYour request is being processed for 1 April 1960.\n\n2. Your attention is invited to the requirements set forth in subparagraph 3k\nof reference (a) regarding a retirement physical examination. Your request\ncannot be forwarded to the Secretary of the Navy for approval until a report\nof such examination is received. If you have forwarded a report of pre-\nretirement physical examination or a certified copy thereof to Pers-B52, please\ndisregard this paragraph.\n\n3. This acknowledgment is not to be construed as being an indication of approval\nof your retirement, as such action is at the discretion of the Secretary of the\nNavy. Appropriate orders will be issued effecting your transfer to the Retired\nList upon approval of your request by the Secretary of the Navy. It would be\nadvisable to exercise caution in making commitments in anticipation of voluntary\nretirement until you are in receipt of retirement orders.\n\n4. You are advised that, with certain exceptions, retired officers including\nwarrant officers of the Regular Navy are prohibited from holding a civilian\nposition or office with the Federal Government when either the retired pay or\nthe rate of compensation fixed for the civilian position or office amounts to\n$2500 or more per annum. Your specific attention is invited to the information\nconcerning the Dual Employment Statute, the Dual Compensation Statute,\nand the conflict-of-interest restrictions of private employment activities,\ncontained in Chapters 1 and 2 of Part Eight of enclosure (1).\n\n\n\nH. O. ANSON, JR.\nCopy to: By direction\nPers-B11h1c\nNAVPERS 2527 (REV 12-58)\nGPO 870257\n\nFinished File B52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0b8a4b788f76a39b114ec0aacdda225c9fe87f3c0c3bd4b36b0166b42e5e923f", "output_sha256": "5fb15aa6d25cc79fd58c4880790ff467f886448a11d8afade0ea082f40333c98", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:50.408058+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p306", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 306, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Form approved by Comptroller General, [ILLEGIBLE]\nApril 26, 1950\n                                                                    S-1\n                                              *See Art. B-2305 BuPers Manual\n\nREPORT PERS-82-79          INDIVIDUAL ORDER TO ADJUST PAY RECORD\n\n1. LEAVE RATIONS OR LOSS OF PAY DUE TO ABSENCE                           HOUR          DATE\n\n☐  WITH LEAVE: AOL OR AWOL          ☐  WITHOUT LEAVE:\n   period, if any, excused as unavoidable     Not excused as unavoidable     DEPARTURE _________  ___________\n\n                                              LEAVE OR LIBERTY EXPIRED\n☐  WITH LEAVE: AOL period, if any,   ☐  OVER LIBERTY:    RETURNED TO NAVAL\n   not excused as unavoidable             Not excused as unavoidable   JURISDICTION _________  ___________\n\nCredit leave rations and/or check pay in accordance with current directives\n\n2. CHANGE RATE: TO ______________________________ FROM ______________________________\n 