 applicable. Only one item shall be completed on each page prepared.\n\nItem 8. (Miscellaneous Pay Orders.) This item may be used to authorize credit of pay for diving duty, salvage and footage dives, duty at a Submarine Escape Training Tank, Navy Deep Sea Diving School or Navy Experimental Diving Unit, and such other items of pay as may subsequently be authorized. Entries in item 8 will be made in the following form:\n\n1. Diving Duty: \"Entered on diving duty --------------------------------- Duty terminated --------------------------------\n                                    (Date)                                                              (Date)\n\nQualified as ------------------------------------------------- Diver, lapsing --------------------------------------------\"\n                        (Designation)                                                         (Date)\n\nand, if applicable, \"Assigned Experimental Diving Unit.\"\n\n2. Salvage and Footage Dives:\n\n          Types of Dive                              Date          Hours—Minutes          Number of Feet\n  (Salvage or Footage—List separately)\n\n----------------------------------------------------------  ----------------  -----------------------  -----------------------\n\n----------------------------------------------------------  ----------------  -----------------------  -----------------------\n\n----------------------------------------------------------  ----------------  -----------------------  -----------------------\n\n3. Duty at Navy Deep Sea Diving School or Navy Experimental Diving Unit: \"Assigned to (or terminated) duty\n\ninvolving training of divers at ------------------------------------------ on ------------------------------------------------.\n                                        (Sub. Esc. Trng., etc.)                              (Date)\nDuty terminated ------------------------------------.\"\n                           (Date)\n\n4. Duty at Submarine Escape Training Tank: \"Assigned to diving duty involving training of personnel in methods\n\nof escape from submerged submarine at ----------------------------------------------- on --------------------------------\n                                                                (Activity)                                        (Date)\nDuty terminated ----------------------------------.\"\n                           (Date)\n\nThe first page used will be numbered 1 in block provided beside the page number and subsequent pages numbered 2, 3, 4, etc.\n\n\nThis page supersedes a portion of the entries included on old forms, page 9U, NavSandA-518; page 9V, NavSandA-517; page 9W, NavSandA-516; page 9X, NavSandA-515; page 9T, NavSandA-519.\n\n\n                                          Page 7\n                                                                                        U. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7bbe7985fe4f221ad203482e6dd330f2b73499f3937b90077d92c861a40abf99", "output_sha256": "7bbe7985fe4f221ad203482e6dd330f2b73499f3937b90077d92c861a40abf99", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:57.250669+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p308", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 308, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "1 DEC 1955   S-1\n\nFrom:  CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:   Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron FIVE\n\nSubj:  Code of Conduct for Members of the Armed Forces of the United States\n\nRef:   (a) SECNAV INSTRUCTION 1610.1\n\n1.  In accordance with reference (a), the following statement is submitted:\n\n   \"I fully understand the Code of Conduct for Members of the Armed Forces\n   of the United States; and if I become a prisoner of war, I will do\n   everything in my power to measure up to its standards.\"\n\n                    DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - VU-5/ACW:rlp\n                                                       P20\n                                                       Ser:  1478\n                                                       1 DEC 1955\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron FIVE\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n                    B. F. ROWE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "96b99e97f2137c2176a61dd4a674f8580184b6df4e1264aa2aa5ed861170878b", "output_sha256": "96b99e97f2137c2176a61dd4a674f8580184b6df4e1264aa2aa5ed861170878b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:41:58.673494+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p309", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 309, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "INSTRUCTIONS:                    96089-50\n  USE TYPEWRITER OR PRINT IN INK\n  ORIGINAL TO THE CHIEF OF NAVAL PERSONNEL                Date: 13 July 1955\n  WHITE COPY TO APPOINTEE; PINK COPY TO COMMANDING OFFICER\n  YELLOW COPIES TO DISBURSING OFFICER\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, Utility Squadron FIVE\n\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n              (Name)                        (File No./Designator)\n\nSubj:  Appointment as Chief Warrant Officer W-4\n\nRef:   (a) Commission or SecNav letter Pers-B1311-eg  dated  28 June 1955   .\n\n1.  By physical examination conducted on  13 July            , 1955  you were found\nphysically fit for continuation on active duty and, therefore, physically qualified\nfor subject promotion.\n\n2.  Subject appointment, authorized by reference (a), is delivered herewith.\n\n                                              B. F. ROWE\n                                              (Signature)\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nI,   Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311                  , having been\n\n[X]permanently  [ ] temporarily appointed a Chief Warrant Officer W-4  [X]USN  [ ]USNR,\nto rank from the  15th  day of   June       , 1955 , do accept such appointment.\n\n    Having accepted the appointment indicated above, I do solemnly swear (or affirm)\nthat I will support and defend the Constitution of the United States against all\nenemies, foreign and domestic; that I will bear true faith and allegiance to the\nsame; that I take this obligation freely, without any mental reservation or purpose\nof evasion; and that I will well and faithfully discharge the duties of the office\non which I am about to enter:  So help me God.\n\n                                    Delbert Clement Newhouse\n                                    (Signature of appointee in full)\n\n    Subscribed and sworn to before me this  13th  day of   July        , 1955 .\n                                    Hamilton G. Park Jr., LCDR\n                                    Hamilton G. PARK, Jr., LCDR\n                                    (Signature and rank of witnessing officer)\n\n\n      Effective Date: 15 June 1955\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nFrom:   Utility Squadron FIVE                        13 July 1955\n              (Commanding Officer)                         (Date)\n\nTo:     The Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers-B1312)\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n                                              B. F. ROWE\n                                              (Signature)\n                                         FINISHED FILE PERS B812\n                                                        A51118", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "74662b15a803757784be906f67b2c098343b19d50a5dc60e89c7e2eb618d25de", "output_sha256": "accf32621980584dcf4da99d5932671943284062acb21c688234fb66e1080ef7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:01.637267+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p310", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 310, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\n                    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                        WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n                                                          S-1\n                                              IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                              Pers-B1311-\n                                                          eg\n                                              177283/8311\n\n                                              28 JUN 1955\n\nFrom:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nTo:      Commanding Officer\n         Utility Squadron 5\n         FPO, San Francisco, Calif.\n\nSubj:    CWO, W-4, Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n         Promotion of\n\nRef:     (a) Warrant Officer Act of 1954\n\nEncl:    (1) Appointment\n         (2) Delivery, Acceptance and Oath of Office Form\n\n1.  Enclosure (1) is authority for the promotion of subject officer.\n\n2.  Prior to delivery of enclosure (1) the commanding officer must\ndetermine that subject officer is mentally, morally and professionally\nqualified to perform the duties of the grade indicated therein, and\nthat he meets the physical qualifications prescribed below.\n\n3.  If subject officer's health record indicates that he has undergone\nan annual physical examination within the four months preceding receipt\nof this letter, and no disqualifying defects were noted, he is to be\nconsidered physically qualified for promotion and the appointment may be\ndelivered.\n\n4.  If subject officer has not had an annual physical examination within\nthe above stated time, or if he has had an examination wherein disqualifying\ndefects were noted, the commanding officer shall direct him to report to a\nmedical officer for physical examination for promotion.  The physical standards shall be the same as those for retention on active duty.  The findings\nof the medical officer should read, \"is (or is not) physically qualified for\ncontinuation on active duty and for promotion to the grade of Chief Warrant\nOfficer W4\".  Report of this physical examination will be made to the Chief\nof the Bureau of Medicine and Surgery on Standard Form 88.\n\n5.  In the event the commanding officer should determine that subject officer\nis not mentally, morally or professionally qualified or, if he is not physically qualified for promotion, enclosure (1) shall be returned to the Chief\nof Naval Personnel, Attn:  Pers B1311, with a report of the circumstances.\n\n\n\n                              B. T. MORRISON\n                              By direction\n\n\nA28238", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "62824f7576187f22463a626c01ebb5ff6e3ddaa25dad4da25c152eff16aa68b1", "output_sha256": "c272fdc74c4ee3d114324ecc0fb1e04c9bc87287cd82f22d4ed26d6472df5ef8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:04.123893+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p311", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 311, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "28 JUN 1955\n\nKNOW YE, that reposing special trust and confidence in the Patriotism, Valor,\n\nFidelity and Abilities of DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE        I do\n\nappoint him, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate,\n             a Chief Warrant Officer, W-4\n\n                    UNITED STATES NAVY\n\n\nto rank as such from the    fifteenth      day of      June nineteen\n\nhundred and    fifty-five\n\n\n\n              THIS IS A SKELETON DOCUMENT FOR FILE\n              AND RECORD PURPOSES OF THE ARMED\n              FORCES TYPE COMMISSION ISSUED TO THE\n              ABOVE NAMED OFFICER.\n\n\n\n                                        Finished File Pers B1311 /s/\n\n\n\n\n                        twenty-second              June\nDone at the City of Washington, this         day of\n                              fifty-five\nin the year of our Lord one thousand nine hundred and seventy-ninth and of the\nIndependence of the United States of America the one hundred and\n\n                         By the President\n\nRegistered:\n\n\n  B. T. Morrison                              C. S. THOMAS\n_________________________                    _________________________\nFOR THE CHIEF OF NAVAL PERSONNEL             SECRETARY OF THE NAVY\nEffective: 15 June 1955\n\n                       File No. 177283                   A 5723", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "56a9e6169749c8290308f039e9b827d5f7e18c4f61e5472ee431f021f69a90c1", "output_sha256": "efacbdb9095211f23955fed928e3f1585a8a0397226bb05a89db6efabf2b9df5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:05.792528+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p312", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 312, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "3ND-NCCC-1C                                                    TELEPHONE MAIN 5-4500\n\n                  U. S. NAVAL CORRESPONDENCE COURSE CENTER    IN REPLY REFER TO:\n                              BUILDING \"RF\"                   NCCC/P11-1/00\n                            U. S. NAVAL BASE                  HSB:et\n                          BROOKLYN 1. NEW YORK\n                                                              13 June 1951\n\nFrom:  Officer in Charge\n\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n       Box 11-H, Navy #3923\n       c/o FPO, San Francisco, Calif.\n\n\nSubj:  Correspondence Course in Uniform Code of Military Justice\n                          NavPers 10971; completion of\n\n1.  In recognition of having furthered your proficiency in\nthe naval service by the successful completion of the subject\ncorrespondence course on 26 May 1951 with a mark of\n4.0, the U.S. Naval Correspondence Course Center, on behalf\nof the Chief of Naval Personnel, takes pleasure in transmitting this Letter of Satisfactory Completion.\n\n2.  A copy of this letter will be placed on file in your\nofficial record.\n\n\n\n                                        HUGH S. BROWN\n\n\nCopy to:\n→ BuPers (Pers E221)\n\n   Commander, Fleet Activities,\n   Navy # 3923, c/o FPO,\n   San Francisco, Calif.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9a746f090101e33474537b31e0898c6047f3bf844c3791862cdb5e56b924e686", "output_sha256": "093cb24ef56e0ffd4867cc01ec0dc58d7651586c7856cd902749ea8c2ad9df75", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:07.652666+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p313", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 313, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\nIN REPLY REFER TO\n\nPers-3215-arr\n177283/1100\n\n\n14 December 1949\nFrom:    The Chief Of Naval Personnel\n\nTo:\n              Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U. S. Navy\n\nVia:      Chief of the Bureau of Aeronautics\n              Navy Department\n              Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\nSubj:     Initial Distribution of Warrant Officers and Chief Warrant Officers\n              in Pay Grades prescribed by Career Compensation Act of 1949.\n\nRef:      (a) AlNav 97 of 12 October 1949\n\n1.  You were initially assigned as of 1 October 1949 in accordance with\nreference (a) to pay grade W-3 in your permanent status as a commissioned\nWarrant Officer.  Accordingly, upon reversion to your permanent status\nyou will be entitled to receive the pay and allowances of a commissioned\nWarrant Officer in pay grade W-3\n\n\n                                          James H. Curran\n                                          By direction.\n\n\n\n\n16 DEC 1949\n\n\nFINISHED W FILE PERS-3215[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "46cc8989380ff83e9852c830383f203cd45db7d846871f0deed4182c1d193e8d", "output_sha256": "cb4404228ba235dd04d6c3cec88992593b5e9a9ce5d79a95eb6313d37656b14b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:09.058344+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p314", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 314, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "TEMPORARY PROMOTIONAL ACTION TAKEN PURSUANT TO PUBLIC LAW 381, 80TH CONGRESS:\n\nFILE NO.        NAME                    CLASS    RANK      DATE OF RANK\n\n\n\n177283  NEWHOUSE DELBERT C   LAP-  LT      4  01   46\n\n\n\n\n\n                              210-47\nAFFIRMED IN ALNAV. NO. ______\n\n                                                    S-1\nCONTINUED IN ALNAV NO. ______", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "26b4e9e802ce649d15d7eba550337bb7cc3071f1eaaec9de0d30b91b84ad323f", "output_sha256": "26b4e9e802ce649d15d7eba550337bb7cc3071f1eaaec9de0d30b91b84ad323f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:09.888714+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p315", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 315, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS - 1782  (REV. 3-45)\n\n                    STATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT\n\n\nFILE NUMBER  |              NAME               |  CLASS  |APPOINTED TO|\n             |                                 |         |            |\n\nDATE OF APPOINTMENT  |  DATE OF RANK  |  CIRC. LTR.  |  ALNAV.  |    NUMBER    |    DATED\n                     |               |              |          |              |\n\nSubject to the conditions stated below, the above individual was appointed by the President to the rank indicated\nabove, for temporary service.\n\nIn the event all stated conditions be met, the appointment (unless expressly declined) is to be regarded for all purposes\nas having been accepted on the date made, without formal acceptance or oath of office, as provided in Section 5 of an\nAct of Congress approved June 30, 1942, (Public No. 639 — 77th Congress).\n\n\nCONDITIONS UNDER WHICH APPOINTMENT WOULD NOT BE EFFECTED:\n\n     1.   Physical disqualification.\n     2.   Withheld by commanding officer.\n     3.   Declined.\n     4.        (a)   Under treatment in hospital;\n               (b)   On sick leave;\n               (c)   Missing;\n               (d)   Prisoner of war.\n\n\nNOTE:  The effectiveness of this appointment must be verified by other correspondence in the officer's correspond-\n       ence jacket unless notation appears hereon indicating appointment not effected.\n\n\n\n\n          FINISHED FILE\n        OFFICER PROMOTION\n            SECTION\n\n\n                    STATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "53a457eb23da2f140a9f43fdc9424d41485590c9f520cddcbb5fbd16eeaed042", "output_sha256": "dbef6da65cd5a2bbf54f36f93fb910b2b30f84bac8d783689c51db5040c1ee18", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:11.642593+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p316", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 316, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "b9\n\nAddress Reply to                                              ROUTING\nSUPPLY OFFICER IN COMMAND\n        and refer to:                                    Pers-32173\n                                                              32152\n                     AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT                  32173A\n                       Naval Supply Center              8 OCT 32171A 73\n                       Pearl Harbor, T. H.\n\n        ACCEPTANCE AND OATH OF OFFICE FOR PERMANENT APPOINT- 3216\n        MENT IN THE NAVY, PURSUANT TO THE AUTHORITY CON- FILE PERS-3216\n        TAINED IN BUPERS CIRCULAR LETTER NO. 182-46\n\n\n                                       25 September 1946\n\nFrom:  Lt. Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, LINE, USN (177283)\nTo:    The Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:   Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply Depot, Pearl\n       Harbor, T.H.\n\n1.  I, Delbert Clement Newhouse, having been appointed Chief\nPhotographer in the U. S. Navy, to rank from  - - - - -\ndo hereby accept such appointment, and do solemnly swear (or\naffirm) that I will support and defend the Constitution of the S-1\nUnited States against all enemies, foreign and domestic; that\nI will bear true faith and allegiance to the same, that I take\nthis obligation freely, without any mental reservation or pur-\npose of evasion; and that I will well and faithfully discharge\nthe duties of the office on which I am about to enter.  So help\nme God.\n\n\n                              Delbert Clement Newhouse\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this twenty-fifth day of\nSeptember 1946.\n\n\n                              K. A. GRAHN\n                              Supply Officer in Command\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n              ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF NOTICE OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT\n                         IN THE U. S. NAVY\n\n1.  I hereby acknowledge receipt of notice of appointment to\nthe rank of Lieutenant in the Navy, for temporary service, to\nrank from 1 April 1946 as made by the President and effective\nfrom the date of the above acceptance and oath of office.\n\n2.  This temporary appointment has not and will not be declined\nby me.\n\n\n                    FINISHED FILE PERS-3216\n\n\nForm No.-NSC-43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6fe8bee067965b7f99d9f99e59ffca52518c6c3594092726b6090b981b80d7c6", "output_sha256": "6fe8bee067965b7f99d9f99e59ffca52518c6c3594092726b6090b981b80d7c6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:13.989467+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p317", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 317, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "- 2 -\n\n3. Two (2) certified copies of this acknowledgment and the above\nacceptance and oath of office are being furnished by me to the\nDisbursing Officer carrying my accounts.\n\n                              Delbert Clement Newhouse\n                              Delbert Clement Newhouse\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n     I hereby certify that I have been in a continuous active duty\nstatus since 1 October 1945.\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nEND-1               AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT, PEARL HARBOR\n\n25 September 1946\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n                              K. A. GRAHN\n\n          FINISHED FILE PERS-3216", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3fabce9285e2db1b43ffef9f400a5c0611c777426f8991fc73fe651dde8d4b91", "output_sha256": "3fabce9285e2db1b43ffef9f400a5c0611c777426f8991fc73fe651dde8d4b91", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:42:15.314916+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p318", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 318, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "S-1\n\n[REDACTED] C. [ILLEGIBLE]\nPRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF [REDACTED]A,\n\n177283\nMAY 1947\nMAY 13 1947\n\nTo All Who Shall See These Presents, Greeting:\n\nKnow Ye, that, reposing special Trust and Confidence in the Patriotism, Valor,\nFidelity, and Abilities of . . . Delbert C. Newhouse . . . . . . . . . .\nI have nominated, and, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate, do ap-\npoint him a Chief Photographer in the Navy to rank with but after . .\nEnsign . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . in the service of the\nUNITED STATES. He is, therefore, carefully and diligently to discharge the\nDuties of . a Chief Photographer . . . . . . . . . . by doing and per-\nforming all Manner of Things thereunto belonging. And I do strictly charge\nand require all Officers, Seamen and Marines, under his Command, to be obedi-\nent to his Orders as . a Chief Photographer . . . . . . . . . . . . . .\nand he is to Observe and Follow such Orders and Directions, from time to time,\nas he shall receive from me, or the future PRESIDENT of the UNITED STATES of\nAMERICA, or his Superior Officer set over him, according to the Rules and\nDiscipline of the Navy. This Commission to continue in force during the\npleasure of the President of the United States for the time being.\n\n                    Done at the City of Washington, this 31st day\n                    of . . . July . . . . . . in the year of our Lord\n(L.S.)              one thousand nine hundred and . . forty-six . . . .\n                    and of the Independence of the United States the one\n                    hundred and . . seventy-first . . . .\n\nBy the President:              . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .\n                               . . . James Forrestal . . . . . .\n\n                               Secretary of the Navy.\n\n                    (The lowest number of\nRegistered No. . . .(same date takes rank\n\n. . . . W. J. Stewart . . . . . . . .\n          Registrar", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bf887ba43c9473f58547467c329b6debf03800d6b33ea9591bcb94a8593e977c", "output_sha256": "760c09c6691f5c27a9c0858407d5063f2aaa6d13ace392d7184add