, "text": "2/10/43        4      Staff, Com    ATL    Dist Photo\n  6/1/43               15ND                  Activities\n6/15/42        8      ABNB, Santa  ATL    Photo Offr\n  2/10/43              Elena Bay\n                       Ecuador\n\n1/23/33\n  6/15/42              Continuous Enlisted Status\n\n\n\n\n(1.) If not USNA give designation; I. E. LXR,—Ex–Reserve; L–XT,—Ex–Temp. appointment US\n(2.) Exact dates preferred.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6afa53d62375f1d220051e8972e9fa909bfdf944bdd29ef35fefd5a4a17c5cd7", "output_sha256": "3a9f46748a8012d9b493a33cec810f9ac56d79f0b8d9e7a7549d7e1bd5357fe8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:46.324400+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p354", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 354, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply refer to Initials\n    and No.\n\n                        NAVY DEPARTMENT\nOp-541C2/efb   OFFICE OF THE CHIEF OF NAVAL OPERATIONS\nWASHINGTON, D. C.      WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\nSerial: 2220 P54\n\n177283\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on\nltr from LT D. C. NEWHOUSE,                  22 DEC 1949\nUSN dtd 23 November 1949\n\nFrom:        Chief of Naval Operations\nTo  :        Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers-31B).\n\nSubject:     Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse; information\n             concerning termination of temporary appointment\n\n     1.      Forwarded for appropriate action.\n\n                              Ray C Needham\n\n                         RAY C. NEEDHAM\n                         BY DIRECTION\n\n\n                                        S-3\n\n\n\n\n\n        Finished File Pers-31B11              Finished File Pers-31B11\n                                                     [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4f46f44467fb56c21e793b228d7f1275f14218a4811a672a7d1eaa24cd27cd5b", "output_sha256": "c8480e20a97ba17db8a72a83914df18c28fc104ae74ccb67429c727f38921434", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:47.676482+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p355", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 355, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Op-54102/efb\nOO-NEWHOUSE, D. C.\nSerial:2220 P54\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on\nltr from LT D. C. NEWHOUSE,                    22 DEC 1949\nUSN dtd 23 November 1949\n\nFrom:          Chief of Naval Operations\nTo  :          Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers-31B).\n\nSubject:       Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse; information\n               concerning termination of temporary appointment\n\n          1.   Forwarded for appropriate action.\n\n\n\n                                        RAY C. NEEDHAM\n                                        BY DIRECTION\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n      Finished File Pers-31B11\n\n                                   Finished File Pers-31B11", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d3845a68b12ceec1628492248ce55ec27cb7ad280c771c733fa793f9cbb0dd3f", "output_sha256": "047a9a5a54a6df62fa348df8ce82ae9416513755233d341566e690b3993aeb48", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:48.728932+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p356", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 356, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PE\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on letter from Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN/\n177283/1350 dated 23 November 1949.\n\n                                                219593\n\n                                                1 9 DEC 1949\n\nFrom:  Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics.\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel.\nVia:   Chief of Naval Operations (Op-54).\n\nSubj:  LIEUTENANT DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE; information concerning termination\n       of temporary appointment.\n\n1.  Forwarded for consideration.\n\n2.  During the period 27 August 1948, to 29 September 1949, while on\nduty at the Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central Dis-\ntrict Headquarters, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio,\nLieutenant Newhouse served as Bureau of Aeronautics liaison officer\nwith the Air Materiel Command in matters relating to procurement of\nphotographic items under the single-service purchase assignment which\nwas awarded to the Air Force by the Department of Defense.\n\n3.  On 10 August 1949, the Head of the Procurement Branch of the\nPhotographic Division was ordered to sea duty and it became necessary\nto obtain a suitable relief.  Lieutenant Newhouse was ordered to this\nduty in the Bureau of Aeronautics because of his exceptional qualifications and recent experience in procurement procedures gained while on\nduty at Air Materiel Command Headquarters, Dayton, Ohio.  He is now\nserving as Head of the Procurement Branch, Photographic Division, during\nwhich time his services have been entirely satisfactory.\n\n                         T.C. Lonnquest\n\n                              T. C. Lonnquest\n                              Rear Admiral, U.S.N.\n21185                         Deputy and Assistant Chief of Bureau\n\nFinished File Per-31811                    Finished File Per-31811", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d1357e1a3d9fcfc1c4e2d8c062d394e81667f9ad2f736a87b902b80c5dcd8542", "output_sha256": "22a25a6d1919836eb1eec3b1a5c1bcb56abd975626eb5bb78d4eba87ca90f06a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:50.744853+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p357", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 357, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "5. Other pertinent matter in my correspondence file includes:\n\n     (a) A report of scores for college degree:\n\n          Aptitude  English  History  Math  Science  Total\n\n            99        94       93      81     97      98     219593\n\n          Possible scores range from 01 to 99.\n\n     (b) A notation that I am physically and educationally qualified\nfor transfer to regular Navy in permanent rank.\n\n     (c) A Certificate of Satisfactory Service dated 25 August 1948.\n\n     (d) The following memorandum:\n\n          \"MEMO                                    4 May 1948\n\n          To:  Operations (a) Sub-board (Cdr. Moore)\n\n          The enlisted record of Newhouse, Delbert C., cannot be\n          located.  Consideration for selection will have to be based\n          on his officer record only.\n\n                                        /s/  G. F. Dalton\n                                             Recorder\"\n\n6.  Within my specialty I have been consistently ordered to duty of\never increasing responsibility from Photographic Officer of Naval\nAir Stations; through Photographic Liaison Officer of Naval Aviation\nSupply Depots; Staff Photographic Officer, Commander Utility Wings,\nPacific; Staff Photographic Liaison Officer, Bureau of Aeronautics\nGeneral Representative, Central District with the U.S. Air Force at\nWright-Patterson Air Force Base; to my present assignment as Head,\nMaterial Procurement Branch under the Director, Photographic Division\nof the Bureau of Aeronautics.\n\n7.  While I appreciate the many problems which were faced by the Bureau\nof Naval Personnel and the Robinson Board in listing personnel to revert,\nit appears that reference (b), the governing directive, was not followed\nin my case.  On these grounds it is requested that my case be re-examined.\n\n\n                              DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\nFinished File Pers-31B11                        Finished File Pers-31B11\n\n                                   2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "db7141bf9fcb642831e5f4f018d6886c9e9e8b08aed0e26b974fde5a3b4cf5dd", "output_sha256": "db7141bf9fcb642831e5f4f018d6886c9e9e8b08aed0e26b974fde5a3b4cf5dd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:52.776195+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p358", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 358, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nBUREAU OF AERONAUTICS\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.                    IN REPLY REFER TO\n\n\n                                        23 November 1949\n\nFrom:  Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, USN/177283/1350\nTo:    Chief, Bureau of Naval Personnel\nVia:   Chief, Bureau of Aeronautics\n\nSubj:  Information concerning termination of temporary appointment\n\nRef:   (a) BuPers ltr 177283/1350 dtd 12 Oct 1949\n       (b) BuPers C/L No. 148-49 dtd 15 Sept 1949\n\nEncl:  (1) Transcripts of portions of representative fitness reports\n\n1.  I received reference (a) on 25 October 1949 notifying me that my\ntemporary appointment as lieutenant would terminate on 31 December 1949.\n\n2.  Reference (b) published the policy for the priority of reversion\nof temporary officers and asserted that it was highly desirable that\nreductions be effected on a logical basis, considering both the best\ninterests of the service and the most equitable consideration of the\ntemporary officers concerned.  Paragraph 2(d) stated that temporary\nofficers, permanent commissioned warrant, would be reverted in ascending\norder of retirement dates.\n\n3.  After receipt of reference (a), I have made a careful examination\nof my correspondence and fitness report files in the Bureau of Naval\nPersonnel.  Material of a possibly adverse nature was disclosed by\nthis examination in that an officer's fitness report dated 29 February\n1948 was checked in the unfavorable box and was signed by Captain J.\nC. Cronin, USN, then Commander Utility Wings, Pacific.  A partial\ntranscript thereof is appended hereto as Exhibit \"A\" of Enclosure (1).\nThis was my first report from this command and covered the period from\n23 October 1947 to 29 February 1948.  I was transferred from the command on 1 July 1948 and a transcript of section 12 of my next and final\nfitness report from Captain Cronin is appended hereto as Exhibit \"B\"\nof Enclosure (1).\n\n4.  The balance of all my fitness reports have ranged from above average\nto superior and, almost without exception, have recommended retention\nin temporary rank, transfer to regular commissioned rank, and promotion\nwhen eligible.  Exhibits \"C\" through \"G\" to Enclosure (1) are submitted\nas being truly representative of my fitness as an officer.\n\n        Finished File Pers-31311                    Finished File Pers-31311", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "145cb3841ad98647476722fceb88444a4ecfad3fe31fbf597c933521bec801a7", "output_sha256": "5d2a86ad8d5c8569b1a45717e4f3a26df3757f67dc7184327f6a670a9d1a7496", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:55.328199+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p359", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 359, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PH-3\n\nENCLOSURE (1)\n\nExhibit \"A\"        29 February 1948        Captain J. C. Cronin, USN\n\n12. \"Unfavorable.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse is a reserved, cheerful, and generally likeable officer.\nHe is having a most difficult time adjusting himself to staff duty.\nHe is judged competent in the technical aspects of photography, but\nhis performance of his administrative duties in both the photographic\nand operational departments is below average. It is felt that his\ndeficiency is principally due to his background and lack of experience\nin administration. He is making a sincere effort to correct this\ndeficiency. He is not yet fitted for promotion.\n\n\nExhibit \"B\"        1 July 1948        Captain J. C. Cronin, USN\n\n12. \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse is a quiet, reserved, and likeable officer. He has had\na difficult time adjusting himself to his duties on this staff, but\nhe has earnestly endeavored to do so. If his experience in naval\naviation had been wider, it is believed he would have performed his\nduties better. He has performed his technical duties as Photographic\nOfficer well. His performance of administrative duties, both as\nPhotographic Officer and as Assistant Operations Officer, has improved\nduring the period of this report. He is not yet fitted for promotion.\n\n\nExhibit \"C\"        19 August 1946        Admiral E. D. Foster, SC, USN\n\n12. \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse has carried out his duties as Photographic Liaison Officer\nin a manner which has reflected credit on this Depot. He has a confident\nand quiet manner and excellent military conduct. His screening of\nphotographic requests and handling of photographic problems has displayed an initiative and thoroughness which is most desirable for an\nofficer in his particular billet. Lt. Newhouse is recommended for promotion when due and for commissioned rank in the regular Navy.\n\n\n\n\nFinished File Pers-31B11                    Finished File Pers-31B11", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3da84b0b37c9eea16d9c110a94575866feca54aa94ca4ffe4579736d158680d0", "output_sha256": "31e7f0035d99b207a204ee5379de80c6710cdcda8395522d226ea6bf5e177be9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:57.465835+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p360", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 360, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PH-3\n\n                    ENCLOSURE (1)\n\nExhibit \"D\"          13 March 1947          Cdr. K.A. Grahn, Jr., SC, USN\n\n12.  \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse has shown a superior grasp of photographic supply details,\nsound judgment, foresight, devotion to duty and thoroughness in his\nprimary duty as photographic officer.  He carries out his depot duties\nas well as liaison with, and assistance to, ComAirPac and CinCPac with\ntact and efficiency, and is firm in administering photographic supply\ndoctrine in this area.  As Administrative Officer he is in charge\nof over 35 civilians and acts as division officer for 40 enlisted men,\nperforming both assignments very well.  His personal and military\ncharacteristics are the highest, he is recommended for promotion when\neligible.\n\n\nExhibit \"E\"\nRear Admiral C.W. Fox, SC, USN    23 May 1947    Cdr. E.R. Joshua, Jr., SC, USN\n\n12.  \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse possesses a sound grasp of supply procedures and has\nexerted a beneficial influence in this area in carrying out instructions\nof the Chief of Naval Operations, Chief, Naval Photographic Services.\nHis judgment is sound and mature; he shows consistent devotion to duty\nand is thoroughly reliable and loyal.  Performance of his collateral\nduty has been uniformly efficient.  His personal and military character-\nistics are excellent, and he is recommended for retention of present\ntemporary rank and for promotion when eligible.\n\n\nExhibit \"F\"\nRear Admiral C.W. Fox, SC, USN    22 October 1947   Cdr. H.J.P. Foley, Jr., SC, USN\n\n12.  \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse's performance of duty has continued to be excellent and\noutstanding.  In addition to a sound grasp of area and service-wide\nphotographic supply procedures, he possesses mature judgment and a\nhigh order of devotion to duty.  He is willing to accept responsibility\nand completes assignments with interest and dispatch.  His personal and\nmilitary character is excellent, and he has been recommended for a\nlimited service commission in his present rank.  He is recommended for\npromotion when eligible.\n\n             Finished File Pers31B11                    Finished File Pers31B11\n\n                                    2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "636d5402a87bf9c75fba6788d94d26328697ef58d98e6919ab6db592d75aa164", "output_sha256": "5d4d19dd8b468b1a9b870215523716138496e321a385c27d12d8a31a963dc84a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:43:59.825980+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p361", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 361, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Aer-PH-3\n\nENCLOSURE (1)\n\nExhibit \"G\"     29 September 1949    Rear Admiral L.M. Grant, USN\n\n12.  \"Satisfactory.\"\n\nLt. Newhouse is a loyal, capable officer.  He carries out the liaison\nwork on Single Department Procurement of photographic materials effectively\nand in a manner reflecting credit to the Navy.  He is tactful, cooperative,\nand has effectively handled numerous problems arising in this joint\ndepartment undertaking.  He is alert in keeping the Bureau of Aeronautics\nadvised on U.S. Air Force Research and Development projects.  Lt.\nNewhouse's personal and military character is excellent, and he is\nrecommended for promotion and continuation on duty in a commissioned\nstatus.\n\n\n\n\nFinished File Pers-31B11                    Finished File Pers-31B11\n\n3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8142dec33d64ba314c492b6a0470ae685c0b66bfb3c4ac961dfaa23b11d19076", "output_sha256": "c95d8f5a88fd03ec8d82c023e92fbb367014f9103ce1f6a7766517f192f94094", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:01.045784+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p362", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 362, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "LAST NAME          (Initials)          RANK AND CORPS     FILE No.      N. A. CLASS    PRESENT STATION        PRESENT DUTIES\nNEWHOUSE,     D.        C.        LT    USN          177283        OR DESIG.(1)   BAGR-CD, Dayton        Photo. Liaison\n                                                                    LAP\nOFFICER'S DATA CARD          NAVPERS-340 (Rev. 7-46)     DATE OF PRESENT RANK:   1 April 1946\nNOTICE:  This card to be submitted directly to Bureau of Naval Personnel annually (on 1 August), and when any significant changes in data occur.  Naval aviators submit to DcNo.\n         It is required of all commissioned and warrant officers.  Officers qualified in submarines or currently serving in submarine force organization submit this form in dupli-\n         cate.  All other officers submit only one copy.          PLEASE TYPE OR PRINT\n\nDATE REPORTED PRESENT    DATE OF BEGINNING PRESENT TOUR OF—     IS CHANGE OF PRESENT     IF YES, STATE WHEN AND DUTY DESIRED\nSTATION                  SEA                                    DUTY DESIRED?\n                         DUTY\n24 August 1948           SHORE  24 August 1948                  □ YES    X NO                            3-1446\n                         DUTY                                                                   FILE - RIORDAN\n\n                                        DETAIL DESIRED FOR NEXT DUTY\n\n                    SEA AND/OR ADVANCED BASE                                                    SHORE\n                                                                                               (Give four choices)\n          LOCALITY              KIND OF DUTY              TYPE SHIP\n\n1. Pacific Fleet           1. Photographic          1. CV or CVB              1. NAS Alameda, California\n2. West Coast              2. Photographic          2. Photo Squadron         2. NAS San Diego, California\n3.                         3.                       3.                        3. NASD, NSD, Oakland, California\n4.                         4.                       4.                        4. Navy Dept. (BuAero/CNO) Wash., D.C.\n\nPRESENT HOME ADDRESS                                                           PRESENT HOME TEL. No.\n               1820 Stratford Pl., Springfield, Ohio                                        #4-4936\n\nSPECIAL QUALIFICATIONS (Do not use code numbers):                 MARITAL STATUS              DEPENDENTS\n                                                                                             (Show age and sex of children)\nOperational Photography; Photographic Supply &                   X MARRIED          1. Norma I. NEWHOUSE, (wife)\nProcurement Naval School of Photography 1935.                    □ SINGLE           2. Delbert C.    \"    M-11\n                                                                                    3. Anne L.       \"    F-9\nLANGUAGE QUALIFICATIONS\n               None                                                                 4.\n\nREMARKS:                                                                          DATE CARD SUBMITTED:  1 August 1949\n          Permanent Rank:  Chief Photographer\n                                                                  SIGNATURE: D.C. Newhouse\n\n                              DO NOT WRITE IN SPACE BELOW\n\nOCCUPYING AUTHORIZED BILLET FOR:     TO BE RELIEVED o/a                         SLATED FOR:\n                                      BY                    , PRESDU\n         (Rank)                                                                                    REPORT PERS-3-14    16—49165-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a6a1f95417f63ae0d38db45dcf49625b3aafc569da62410104073f2afa99b949", "output_sha256": "6b662b5e47738a1d7c64c02f578f9a254a29e0bbc2b77b145e9a76204f228287", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:04.360268+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p363", "card_id": "ca6