aude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "298de5436c266518cca9789e8d4c6bfd9016979226908805dd9994edf054cd8e", "output_sha256": "a3aae4631f8229b4d376f408d56b49a5088df58bbf6f04904f3854bbb095b710", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:07.016800+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p364", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 364, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "SECNAV\n\nPers-32150-mjr\n177203/1350\n\n\n\n2 1 NOV 1949\n\nFrom:    Secretary of the Navy.\nTo:      Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, U.S. Navy.\n\n\nVia:     Chief of the Bureau of Aeronautics,\n         Navy Department,\n         Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\nSubj:    Termination of Temporary Appointment\n         as a Lieutenant.\n\n1.  In view of the reduction in the officer personnel strength\nof the Navy, the President terminates your temporary appointment\nas a Lieutenant in the Navy, effective 31 December 1949.\n\n2.  You will revert to your permanent status as a Chief Photographer.  The designator assigned you in this grade is 8311.\n\n\n                              For the President:\n\n                         FRANCIS P. MATTHEWS\n\n\n                              Secretary of the Navy.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "117a68e0805e113f22129fea88d70ffaea92ebe3cf301bb8f1d6b6ae2c02810a", "output_sha256": "c309168f7b9d0d4fb06ae904ab3b34b1dffc8ebdab4df2a2cc83e59bdff5cbf9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:08.266189+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p365", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 365, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Pers-8234-JAB\n\n                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n               BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                  WASHINGTON 25, D.C.\n\n31 Oct 1949\n\nFrom:  The Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    BuSandA, Officers' Accounts Division\n       Room 0202, Navy Department, Code F.O.\n       Washington 25, D.C.\nAttn:  Miss Watt\nSubj:  Base Pay Entry Dates.\n\nRef:   (a) Your recent requests.\n\n1.  In accordance with reference (a) Base Pay Entry Dates for the following\nlisted officers are forwarded herewith:\n\n        079591  INGALLS, Charles E., Jr.       LCDR   USN   10-11-37\n        522740  FICHTER, William F.            ENS    USNR   9-20-45\n        413154  HOWARD, William D.             LTJG   USNR  10-21-42\n        177283  NEWHOUSE, Delbert C.           LT     USN    3-16-30\n\n\n                                          M. M. ANGAS\n                                          By direction\n\n\n        Total 4\n\n\n\n\n                         FINISHED FILE 8234", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a1ac8b28fab75836d581dccca32706211b39f5c4619cb5dc29f8f0468c737eb7", "output_sha256": "77f84d568ec3d2c525fd194897340b710a293d6ebb52b83eb822da121a6415a2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:09.762362+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p366", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 366, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVY DEPARTMENT\n     Refer to:          BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nPers-3622 -rws         WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n   177283\n\n\n                                              1 1 FEB 1949\nFrom:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:            Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350.\n\n\nVia:           Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative,\n               Central District,\n               Wright Field,\n               Dayton, Ohio.\n\n\nSubj:          Application for commission as Limited Duty Officer;\n               Acknowledgment/Information regarding.\n\nRefs:          (a)  Your application for commission in Limited Duty Status.\n               (b)  BuPers Circ Ltr No 175-48.\n\n1.   Receipt is acknowledged of the (original) (duplicate copy) of reference (a).\nDefects, if any, are noted below.  It is requested that action be expedited and\npapers returned to the Bureau of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-362) if indicated:\n\n(x )  No defects.\n\n(  )  Application and all substantiating documents returned for completion in the\n      form shown in reference (b).\n\n(  )  Application incomplete.  Forward following document(s) immediately:\n      (  )  Fitness report form.\n      (  )  NavMed Form H-8 (report of physical examination).\n      (  )  Signed sworn statement for Detailed Information Sheet.\n      (  )  Commanding Officer's verification of statements in application in accordance with paragraph 11(e) of reference (b), and enclosure (B) thereto.\n\n(  )  Individual documents returned for correction or completion as follows:\n      (  )  Fitness report form returned for completion accordance paragraph 11(c)\n            and/or 11(d) of reference (b).\n      (  )  Fitness Report form returned for proper signature (s).\n\n(  )  Application will not be considered by the Selection Board and is filed without\n      action by reason of ineligibility due to:\n      (  )  Insufficient service (less than 10 years' active Naval service).\n      (  )  Overage ( cannot complete 30 years' service prior to attaining age 55).\n      (  )  Ineligibility as indicated in paragraph 8(b) of reference (b).\n\n(  )  Not eligible for rank requested.  Refer paragraphs 8 and 9 reference (b);\n      application in Bureau has been corrected accordingly, and will be considered\n      by Board for appointment in the rank for which eligible unless withdrawn by\n      written request.  The highest rank for which eligible is ________________.\n\n(  )  Other:\n\n\n                              -1-               FINISHED FILE PERS 362", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d5d1295ee2f8284b3120df2ffe4b8620660265cb903787423c2086c85c64ead8", "output_sha256": "c6bf8dbcef3fe369b8adaac3e9b29a449afa6047da811b5fed32eeca763f07ce", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:12.448591+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p367", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 367, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "2.    Attention of officers is invited to the fact that the special fitness report,\nsubmitted with the application, is an additional report for the use of the Selection Board and will not be filed in the officer's fitness report record.  This\nperiod must be included in the regular fitness reports submitted in accordance with\ncurrent instructions.\n\n\n                                        A. ZIMM\n                                    By direction.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "51bd87fe7df186f8a3651386b33f3c398dee7cfbce00f77ed316963b794eb08d", "output_sha256": "30c781b89790e93ef614ec00872b157913c23752bad17e6f756fe294ed009e63", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:13.183511+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p368", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 368, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DETAILED INFORMATION IN SUPPORT OF APPLICATION FOR COMMISSION IN LIMITED DUTY STATUS\n\n(a) NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement\n\n(b) Rank: Lieutenant.  File #: 177283/1350.  Form of appointment:  Lieutenant, Unrestricted.\n    Date of rank: 1 April 1946.\n\n(c) Not applicable.\n\n(d) Highest enlisted rating held: CPhoM.     Service #: 393 07 21.\n\n(e) through (i) are not applicable.\n\n(j) Date and place of birth: 5 June 1913; Marcola, Lane County, Oregon.\n\n(k) Detailed computation of service:\n\n        ENLISTED            WARRANT           COMMISSIONED\n                                                                    Total\n    Enlisted  Discharged    From      To       From       To        Service\n\n    1/24/33   1/23/39                                              06-00-00\n    1/24/39   6/24/42                                              03-05-01\n    Photographer          6/25/42   6/14/43                        00-11-20\n    Ensign                                   6/15/43   8/31/44    01-02-17\n    Lieutenant (jg)                          9/1/44    3/31/46    01-07-00\n    Lieutenant                               4/1/46    12/31/48   02-09-00\n    Time lost due to SKMC, NPDI, AOL, AWOL.................................NONE\n    Net active naval service as of 1 January 1949.........................15-11-08\n\n(l) Present station and description of duties:\n    Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\n    Assistant Director, Procurement Division for Photographic Procurement and\n    Developmental Engineering.\n\n(m) From October 1947 to July 1948.          Rank: LT\n    Staff, Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n    Duties:  Photographic Officer, Assistant to Staff Operations Officer and\n             Photographic Officer of Fleet Air Photographic Laboratory operated\n             by Commander, Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n    From September 1946 to October 1947      Rank: LT\n    NASD, Pearl Harbor, T.H.\n    Duties:  Receipt, storage and issuance of photographic materials. Administration of Naval and civilian personnel and duties as Recreation Officer;\n             Training Officer; Voting Officer; Fire Prevention Officer; Member\n             Survey Board; Member General Court Martial Board, and Summary Court\n             Martial Board, Naval Base, Pearl Harbor.\n    From September 1944 to September 1946    Rank: LT & LTJG\n    NASD, Philadelphia, Pa.\n    Duties:  Receipt, storage and issue of photographic materials.\n    From June 1943 to September 1944         Rank: LTJG, ENS & PHOT\n    NAS, COCO SOLO, C.Z.\n    Duties:  Administration and operation of photographic laboratory.\n\n                                    DEC 2 2 RECD\n\n                                                          LT(jg)-OPA", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0d5f8f6cd935b8648c3ab34641f83665d4cf52a135bfca50f44f55359a1a3ef6", "output_sha256": "acf3f79adf95c1ee8acddd39424b5e3b2a10940ef271471c6da3b689a17d7c05", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:16.232973+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p369", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 369, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DETAILED INFORMATION IN S[REDACTED]ORT OF APPLICATION FOR COMMISSION IN LIMITED DUTY STATUS\n\n(m) (Continued).\n\n     From February 1943 to June 1943.          Rank: PHOT\n     Staff, Commandant FIFTEENTH Naval District.\n     Duties:  Coordination of District photographic activities.\n     From August 1942 to February 1943.         Rank: PHOT & CPhom\n     Advanced Base \"GAMMA\", later designated as USNavBase, Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador.\n     Duties:  Administration of the Ordnance Department and duties as Photographic\n              Officer, Athletic Officer, and Welfare Officer.\n     From November 1940 to August 1942.         Rate: CPhom & PhomM1\n     NAS, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.\n     Duties: Administration and operation of photographic laboratory, production\n             of aerial photographic maps and aerial and ground photography.\n     From June 1939 to November 1940.          Rate: PhomM1\n     Patrol Squadron FOURTEEN (Redesignated from VF-45).\n     Duties:  Aerial and ground photography.\n     From April 1936 to June 1939.             Rate: PhomM1, 2, & 3.\n     NAS, San Diego, California.\n     Duties: Aerial and ground photography.\n     From December 1935 to April 1936.         Rate: PhomM3\n     Bombing Squadron ONE-B.\n     Duties:  Aerial and ground photography.\n     From June 1935 to December 1935.          Rate: PhomM3 & S1.\n     NAS, Pensacola, Florida.\n     Duties:  Under instruction at Naval School of Photography.\n     From November 1934 to June 1935.          Rate: S1\n     Scouting Squadron THREE-B.\n     Duties:  Photographic Striker.\n     From June 1933 to November 1934           Rate: S1 & S2\n     Flag Unit, Commander Aircraft Battle Force.\n     Duties:  Yeoman Striker.\n     From January 1933 to June 1933            Rate: S2 & AS\n     Naval Training Station, San Diego, California.\n     Duties:  Recruit Training.\n\n(n) Special naval qualifications and naval service schools attended:\n     1.  Naval School of Photography, NAS Pensacola, Florida.\n\n(o) Awards, decorations, and medals:\n     1.  Good Conduct Medal.\n     2.  American Defense, w/Base Clasp.\n     3.  World War II Victory Medal.\n     4.  Air Crew Insignia.\n\n(p) Civilian Education.\n     1. Graduate of High School (12 years), Garibaldi, Oregon, 1931.\n     2. Enrolled in the University of Kansas at Lawrence, Kansas, in September 1931,\n        and withdrew in December of the same year.\n     3. Completed United States Armed Forces Tests of General Education Development,\n        College Level at the Navy Yard, Philadelphia, in June, 1946, with average\n        percentile score of 98+.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9e144ad93ba045d3313c007a0311348454c74966687efc107585b22e2ef2d24a", "output_sha256": "d98e02984aeae80c6d0aad95a093fc229411ffbd16f61f616bc36b0b57f3e980", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:19.260061+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p370", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 370, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DETAILED INFORMATION IN SUPPORT OF APPLICATION FOR COMMISSION IN LIMITED DUTY STATUS\n\n(q) Eligible for rank of Lieutenant (junior grade). Lowest rank acceptable is\n    Lieutenant (junior grade).\n\n    I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that all statements made in this application\nand any additional statements pertaining thereto are entirely true and complete to\nthe best of my knowledge and belief:\n\n                              Delbert C. Newhouse\n                         DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE.\n\n     Subscribed and sworn to before me this  6  day of December 1948. I have\nauthority to administer oaths.\n                                   Henry J. Bowker\n                              HENRY J. BOWKER,\n                              Lieutenant Commander,\n                              U.S. Naval Reserve.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "20aac813bbf4446be6cf3ea43793e1b66f0c6ebd2df2a93a16a77cc0d8060c3a", "output_sha256": "bacf05a370d18b14efe84a958a84c8ab5e6366fb3eb84de41dc81e3c9851351a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:20.654006+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p371", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 371, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF AERONAUTICS GENERAL REPRESENTATIVE, USN\nREFER TO INITIALS                    CENTRAL DISTRICT\nAND NO.                         WRIGHT FIELD, DAYTON, OHIO\nDCN:mls\n\n\n29 November 1948\n\nFrom:     Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/1350.\nTo  :     The Chief of Naval Personnel (attn: Pers-362).\nVia :     Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\n\nSubj:     Application for a commission in limited duty status.\n\nRefs:     (a) BuPers C/L #175-48.\n          (b) BuPers C/L #174-47, (Corrected).\n          (c) BuPers C/L #104-48.\n          (d) Public Law #381-80th Congress.\n\nEncls:    (A) Detailed information in support of application for commission\n              in limited duty status.\n          (B) Special report of fitness, present duty.\n\n1.   In accordance with references (a) through (d), I hereby apply for a\npermanent commission as Lieutenant (junior grade), in LINE, Aviation; Aviation\nOperations.\n\n                                        Delbert C. Newhouse\n                              DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n00/NEWHOUSE, D.C./                                        END-1\nLT/177283/1350/USN\nMLS:mls    12973                                     DEC 2 1 1948\n\nFrom:     Bureau of Aeronautics General Representative, Central District.\nTo  :     The Chief of Naval Personnel (attn: Pers-362).\n\nEncl:     (C) NavMed H-8.\n\n1.   Forwarded.\n\n2.   It is believed that Lieutenant NEWHOUSE is specially qualified for the\nLimited Duty Status requested, and that he will, if selected, carry out the\nduties pertaining thereto in a creditable manner. The Commanding Officer, therefore, recommends Lieutenant Newhouse's selection.\n\n3.   Items of Enclosure (A) have been verified from applicant's record on board.\n\n                                        L. M. Grant\n                              L. M. GRANT.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6ea5e902f34c09f7ec8850e5c57c0ad55773e7146450ef2a78a1e1392c495115", "output_sha256": "82205dc3b010024292adc60adb03d7cf7fef3053729be528f4abb39691c6a180", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:23.034715+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p372", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 372, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVMED II-8 (Rev. 5-45)          PAGE N[REDACTED]\n\n               MEDICAL HISTORY\n\nSURNAME\n               NEWHOUSE\nCHRISTIAN NAME(S)\n          Delbert    Clement\nRANK OR RATE                    FILE OR SERVICE NO.\n     LT        USN             0177282\nBIRTHPLACE                     BIRTH DATE\n          Ore.                 6-5-13\n\n     STATE NAME OF PLACE—DATE EACH NEW ENTRY\n\n-NAS, Columbus, Ohio\n-12-1-48\n-Examined this date in accordance with\n-BuPers C.L. 175-48 and found physically\n-qualified for retention in the regular\n-Navy. It is the opinion of this\n-Medical Officer that this officer will\n-be physically and psychologically\n-qualified to perform all duties in his\n-work at sea and on foreign shore.\n-Further that he may reasonably be ex-\n-pected to remain physically qualified to\n-serve out the expected length of duty\n-in his rank.\n\n\n                    [signature]\n               W. A. BUTCHER\n               CDR (MCR) USNR birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday birthday\n\n\n                                        16-44869-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "599db023d9360d837eaa8cef09f49dcbfe73f5acff51ad44b10462ee70d2818c", "output_sha256": "5f43f88f2bb82f5f8fceed32842dfd6c530201bd103fb31042283fdf3ad3030d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:24.712621+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p373", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 373, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICERS BEING REPORTED ON to fill out Sections 1 through 5. Sign all three pages in the lower left hand corner.\nREPORTING OFFICER to fill out Sections 6 through 12. Sign all three pages in the lower right hand corner.\n\nOFFICER'S F