Delbert C. Newhouse\ncorrect                    ________________________\n  cert.                       Delbert C. Newhouse\n                                 (Signature)\n\n                                            532886", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a2fa1bb707c70229e36e24533cf9978be1dfebc8559c7341107a7b69d18d6d93", "output_sha256": "08641e27125de9945ba6011229b1be26bf5754439aa1d385340d928712aefa0b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:57.313029+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p377", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 377, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "2 2 SEP 1948\n\n\n\n        End-1  Pers 8272\n        From:  Chief of Naval Personnel        PERS 8272\n        To:    Chief of Bureau of Supplies and Accounts\n               Central Pay Accounts Division\n               Cleveland, 15, Ohio\n        1.     Verified and found to be correct.\n        By direction of Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n\n\n\n                              I. J. MAYNARD,\n                              Director, Misc. Rec. Div.\n                              [ILLEGIBLE] Activity", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "539f8553f720167d34d20ae9aa9f64e729643b76d5e42c76c3accb7c3e1968ed", "output_sha256": "d51f886d3830bfa652c19ca5772920c0c6feabcc10c7ccf9d744e9bf8a0404a9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:44:58.213643+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p378", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 378, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NASD FORM #17\n                    U. S. NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n   177283            NAVY #128 (ONE TWO EIGHT)                    3/15/47\n(File No.            FLEET POST OFFICE                            (Date)\n                    SAN FRANCISCO, CALIF.\n\nFrom:    NEWHOUSE, DELBERT C              LT.         USN.\n         (Name in full,                  Rank    Class    Desig.\n\nTo:      Disbursing Officer  NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, NAVY #128\n\nSubj:    Statement of Service.\n\nRef:     (a) Pay Readjustment Act of 16 June 1942, as amended\n         (b) ALNAV 200 - 44                                    S-3\n\n1.       In accordance with references the following officer's certificate\nof service for longevity pay purposes is submitted. It is requested that my\npay account be adjusted accordingly.\n\n Organization          Total Service        Time Lost          Net Time\n                    From        To        From      To     Years   Mos.   Days\n\nNational Guard En  3/18/29   1/25/33                          2      10      8\nU.S.N. Enlistment  1/24/33   8/31/42                          9       7      7\nU.S.N.Comm(Temp)   9/1/42    9/24/46                          4       0     24\nU.S.N.Comm(Perm)   9/25/46   3/15/47                          0       5     21\n\n\n\n\nTOTAL SERVICE FOR PAY PURPOSES --------------------------------  15     22     60\n                                       17 Years\n\n2.       I certify the above to be a true and correct statement of my prior\nservice. In the event of any errors I authorize the checkage of my pay account\nto adjust any overpayment resulting therefrom.\n\n                                            Delbert C Newhouse\n                                               (Signature)\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n(For Disbursing Officer)\n     Completed last 3 years' period of service   15 years 3/15/45\n     Total Service for Pay Purposes              17 years 3/15/47\n\n     Correct lest                                R.F. SULLIVAN\n     7-18-48                              Signature          Symbol No.\n     [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b756c062667f5cfcd01ac6bd1ab07bc09f3706615de2241297e9918c7577447a", "output_sha256": "f50ab1d4cc7b3779329e18007f38f7d30a714e215051192f8ddb3f37733cb5b9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:00.668086+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p379", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 379, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "15 JUL 1948\n\nEnd-1 Pers 8272\nFrom: Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:   Chief of Bureau of Supplies and Accounts\n      Central Pay Accounts Division\n      Cleveland 13, Ohio\n1.    Verified and found to be correct.\nBy direction of Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n\n\n\n                  I. J. MAYNARD,\n                  Director, Misc. Rec. Div.\n                  Records Activity", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f5b1cf4cd60af9de465a3f4a40bd3dda35e86ee6c51a5a74176b04c58da8b385", "output_sha256": "9b0db6de3f368b4e0789cf20d97e6c847ba35f4aa4fa380629b8d2ecc277ca8b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:01.642971+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p380", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 380, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In reply address not the signer of this\nletter, but Bureau of Naval Personnel,\nNavy Department, Washington 25, D. C.\n\nRefer to No. Pers-362-fh\n         177283\n\n                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n              BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                   WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                                        for PEACE\n                                                          OF\n                                                         MIND-\n                                                          BUY\n                                                        SAVINGS\n                                                         BONDS\n\nFrom:  The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:    LT DELBERT CLEMENT NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n                                                    7 JUL 1948\n\n                                                              P\nVia:   Commander Air Force,                                 2622\n       U.S. Pacific Fleet,\n       c/o Fleet Post Office,          S-3\n       San Francisco, California.\n\n\nSubj:  Application for transfer to commissioned limited duty status;\n       action on.\n\nRefs:  (a) Your application for transfer to commissioned limited\n           duty status.\n       (b) BuPers Circular Letter 175-47.\n\n1.  Your application for transfer to commissioned limited duty status\nhas been carefully considered by the Selection Board convened by the\nSecretary of the Navy.  I regret to inform you that your name was not\nincluded among those recommended for appointment.  However, I wish to\nassure you that this decision is no reflection upon your performance\nof duty in the Navy; nor will it in any way affect your present status\nor preclude your making application and being considered by subsequent\nselection boards.\n\n2.  The number of applicants desiring transfer to commissioned limited\nduty status has been far in excess of the number of appointments which\ncan be offered.  Therefore, it was necessary for the Selection Board\nto recommend, from among eligible applicants, only those best qualified\nfor appointment.  The decision in your case was made after a careful\nreview of your entire record and your qualifications as compared with\nthose of other applicants of your rank and classification or enlisted\nrating.\n\n3.  The interest you have shown in pursuing a naval career represents\nan exemplary attitude of service and patriotism.  The Navy is sincerely\nappreciative of your contribution toward maintaining the naval estab-\nlishment at a high level of efficiency during the war, the demobiliza-\ntion period, and the continuing period of world unrest.\n\n\n                                        T. L. SPRAGUE\n\n\n                                                              A-17154", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "019b0d2c01287e3f71e5ff80fb69c00dce21f3984dbdf6394ae32662ce24202b", "output_sha256": "5c807f4567ae3795ceaa4fbcd4f565ad467314abfc22957a34f5ae456c8c2d52", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:04.051156+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p381", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 381, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "attach to\napplication\n                         17 March 1948\n\nFrom:        Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, (Chief Photographer),\n             USN, 177283.\nTo:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nVia:         The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nSubject:     My Application for a Commission in Limited Duty Status;\n             Rank for which Eligible.\n\nReference:   (a) BuPers ltr Pers-3622-dmm 17283/1100 of 5 March 48.\n             (b) My request for modification of subject application\n                 forwarded by ComUtWingPac 1st end. P14-2 ser 62 of\n                 17 Jan 48.\n\nEnclosure:   (A) Certified copy of ref (b).\n\n     1.      Enclosure (A) is forwarded in reply to reference (a).\n\n     2.      I do desire to be considered for a lower rank than now\nheld, but not less than lieutenant (junior grade).\n\n                         Delbert C. Newhouse\n                         DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n                    UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nFU/FF12/P14-2/(60:rs)        Air Force\n                    UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\nSerial:      261\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT:              2 0 MAR 1948\n\nFrom:        The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n     1.      Forwarded.\n\n                         Onia B. Stanley Jr.\n                         ONIA B. STANLEY, JR.\n                         By direction.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "53f5108f49184044eba21a02b8f4ecef77517ce17746f84b90727d11cf8ed6b3", "output_sha256": "2a416fe5694a9889a33d8636d40b57716bae1aa9667408390abaac4e5ba32b12", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:05.916524+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p382", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 382, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In Reply Refer to          UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n  FU/FF12/P14-2                    Air Force\n  60:Sr               UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\n. Serial:  62                                    17 January 1948\n\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT to:\nLT D.C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\nltr request dtd 16\nJanuary 1948.\n\nFrom:          The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\nTo:            The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31).\n\nSubject:       Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\n     1.        Forwarded.\n\n\n\n\n                              J. C. CRONIN\n\nCopy to:\n     LT NEWHOUSE.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n\n  D.C. Newhouse                          ENCLOSURE ( )\n\nForm No. UTWING-20", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "406a3fe5f553d2f804f951654ad3af2a9abebe9d75a98822fc857500a1d3234b", "output_sha256": "502fe65c2faeece872b1b36c642acd7226d055246d86f9a2f912549d4b497873", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:07.081770+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p383", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 383, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\nJN 177283                    Air Force\n                    UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\n                                                  16 January 1948.\n\nFrom:          Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, (Chief Photographer),\n               USN, 177283.\nTo:            The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31).\nVia:           The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nSubject:       Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\nReference:     (a) SOinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H. ltr\n                   NT4-9/P17/00/021/CF ser 10583 of 31 Oct 1947.\n               (b) BuPers C/L No. 175-47.\n               (c) BuPers C/L No. 245-47.\n\n     1.        Reference (a) forwarded my request for transfer to\ncommissioned limited-duty status.\n\n     2.        Due to the change in paragraph 4, second sentence of\nreference (b) effected by reference (c), it is requested that paragraph\n2 (1) of my request for commissioned limited-duty be changed to read:\n\"I do desire to be considered for a lower rank than now held, but not\nless than lieutenant (junior grade).\"\n\n\n                                        DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE,\n                                        Lieutenant, U. S. Navy.\n\n     I do solemnly swear that all statements made in this request for\nmodification of application are entirely true and complete to the best\nof my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n                                        DELBERT CLEMENT NEWHOUSE.\n\n     Subscribed and sworn to before me this sixteenth day of January\n1948.  I have authority to administer oaths.\n\n\n                                        A. E. MARDEN,\n                                        Lieutenant, U. S. Navy.\n\n\nCERTIFIED TO BE A TRUE COPY\n  D. Newhouse                                ENCLOSURE (1)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7649b8cb258c1e8db68ef29f707a0737c32297195d9c7aec65e37ffdd285115a", "output_sha256": "78f704c8515dab682cc7d764e1a5b55debeb0a6272f007091d4f2071bdbcf042", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:09.137775+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p384", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 384, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Pers-3622-dmm\n177283/1100\n\n                                        5 - MAR 1948\n\n\n\nFrom:   The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:     LT. Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN.\n\n\nVia:    Supply Officer in Command\n        Aviation Supply Depot\n        Naval Supply Center\n        Navy 128, c/o Fleet Post Office\n        San Francisco, California\n\n\nSubj:   Your application for a commission in limited-duty\n        status; Rank for which eligible.\n\nRefs:   (a) Your application for a commission in limited-\n            duty status.\n        (b) BuPers Circ.Ltr. No. 174-47 as modified by\n            BuPers Circ.Ltr. No. 245-47.\n        (c) BuPers Circ.Ltr. No. 175-47.\n\n1.  By careful review of reference (a) and your records in the\nBureau, it has been determined that the lowest rank which you\nhave indicated will be acceptable is higher than the highest\nrank for which you are eligible in accordance with reference\n(b).  The highest rank for which you are eligible is LTJG.\n\n2.  The provisions of reference (c) require determination by\nthe applicant of his eligibility, however, in order to protect\nyour interests, it is assumed that you have misinterpreted\nreferences (b) and (c).  Therefore, your application will be\nsubmitted to the Selection Board for consideration for appoint-\nment to the highest rank for which you are eligible.\n\n3.  If you desire to be considered for a lower rank as well as\nthat given above, or to withdraw your application, you are\ndirected to submit a signed statement to that effect.\n\n\n\n\n                        G. F. DALTON,\n                        By direction.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3b7d4864eb32dde88f1c9c66c9c28b54b62b9b3d4f5524d47c54f17676b21bd9", "output_sha256": "3b7d4864eb32dde88f1c9c66c9c28b54b62b9b3d4f5524d47c54f17676b21bd9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:11.036657+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p385", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 385, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "*PHOTO                    NAVY DEPARTMENT\n177285 1M                BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                              WASHINGTON 25, D. C.              11 DEC 1947\n\nFrom:        The Chief of Naval Personnel. 177285.\nTo:\n\nVia:         Supply Officer in Command,\n             Aviation Supply Depot,\n             Naval Supply Center,\n             Navy 128, c/o FPO, San Francisco, Calif.\n\nSubj:        Application for Commission as Limited Duty Officer; Receipt of.\n\nRef:         (a) BuPers Circular Letter No. 175-47.\n\nEncl:        (A)\n\n                              xxxxxxxxxxxxx\n1. Receipt is acknowledged of the (original) (advance copy) of your application\nfor commission as limited duty officer.\n\n2. The following defects, as checked below, are noted:\n\n(    ) None.\n\n(    ) Fitness Report was not received with your application.  Your Commanding\n       Officer is requested to comply with reference (a), paragraphs 2(b)(2)\n       and 2(b)(3), and forward the completed fitness report to the Bureau of\n       Naval Personnel (attention Pers-311M).\n\n(    ) Fitness Report is returned herewith for completion in accordance with\n       reference (a), paragraphs 2(b)(2) and 2(b)(3).  Your Commanding Officer\n       is requested to complete or correct and return the fitness report as\n       soon as possible to the Bureau of Naval Personnel (attention Pers-311M).\n\n(    ) NavMed Form H-8 (report of medical officer's examination), as required\n       by reference (a), paragraph 2(c), was not received with your application.\n       Your Commanding Officer is requested to forward a signed copy of this\n       form to the Bureau of Naval Personnel (attention Pers-311M).\n\n(    ) Others\n\n\n\n                                                          A. ZIMM\n                                                       By direction.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a1e4023d3c3d2d48667c3a8d81f69b33dc5977d065ac987d3b6ebe150aa9de94", "output_sha256": "1b5d33e10bba209317e2c3c0dbca91c0a4d41b74d7f25a9efd389e7d61813231", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:13.125443+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p386", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 386, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "8\n3 11M\n\nEND-1 on Lt. Newhouse's\nltr dated 17 October 1947\n\n\n22 October 1947\n\n\nFrom:  Supply Officer in Command, Aviation Supply Depot,\n       Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor\nTo:    The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31).\nVia:   Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor\n\nSubj:  Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n\n\n\n                         H. J. P. FOLEY\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nNT4-9/P17/00              END-2 on LT D. C. Newhouse, USN ltr dtd\n021                                17 Oct 47\n\nCF  10583\n3 1 OCT 1947\n\nFrom:      Supply Officer in Command, Naval Supply Center,\n           Pearl Harbor, T. H.\nTo:        Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31)\n\nSubj:      Transfer to Commissioned Limited Duty Status\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n\n\n                         G. L. THOMAS\n                         By direction\n\ncc:\nComAirPac", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4f221617e1242f0c18e49bb1a190c58691c7d575ba66fface86fd724cc5a7824", "output_sha256": "5a1757f88c89db2f9f98a97ae9e1a07dc3fb13d1d2f654947e1c9459beb2f34f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:15.082648+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p387", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 387, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "JN 177283\n17 October 1947\n\n          (g) Cont'd.\n               (5) Naval Air Station, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.  Chief in Charge\n                   of Photographic Laboratory.  November 1940 to August 1942.\n               (6) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Scouting Force, Patrol Squadron\n                   Fourteen (Redesignated from VP-45).  Senior Photographer,\n                   June 1939 to November 1940.\n               (7) U. S. Naval Air Station, San Diego, Calif.  Photographer.\n                   April 1936 to June 1939.\n               (8) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Battle Force, Bombing Squadron\n                   One-B.  Photographer.  December 1935 to April 1936.\n               (9) Naval Air Station, Pensacola.  Under instruction at\n                   Naval School of Photography.  June 1935 to December 1935.\n               (10) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Battle Force, Scouting Squadron\n                   Three-B.  Photographer striker.  November 1934 to June\n                   1935.\n               (11) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Battle Force, Flag Unit.  Yeoman\n                   striker.  June 1933 to November 1934.\n               (12) Naval Training Station, San Diego, Calif.  Under recruit\n                   training.  January 1933 to June 1933.\n\n          (i) Graduate of Naval School of Photography at Naval Air Station\n              Pensacola, Florida.\n          (j) Good Conduct Medal, American Defense Campaign ribbon with\n              overseas star, American Theater campaign ribbon, World War II\n              Victory Medal, and Air Crew Insignia.\n          (k) Graduated from twelfth grade at Garibaldi High School, Garibaldi,\n              Oregon in 1931.  Enrolled at the University of Kansas, Lawrence,\n              Kansas in September 1931 and withdrew from the University in\n              December of the same year.\n              Completed the United States Armed Forces Tests of General\n              Educational Development, College Level at the Navy Yard,\n              Philadelphia in June 1946 with the average percentile score\n              of 98.4.\n          (l) I do not desire to be considered for a lower rank than now held\n              which is that of lieutenant.\n\n                                        D. C. NEWHOUSE\n                                        Lieutenant, U. S. Navy\n\n     I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that all statements made in this application\nand any additional statements pertaining hereto are entirely true and complete\nto the best of my knowledge and belief.\n                                        Delbert Clement Newhouse\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this  17  day of  October  1947.\nI have authority to administer oaths.\n\n                                        D. E. PARRISH\n                                        LT., SC, USN\n\n                              -2-", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6352ef5004ddef1c53663eb533b0ebaef287521038c7c9e4ecb6d242b0a6f7b0", "output_sha256": "f953fbb231ae404d2a67b9a371e8ba02954b7f4332cd6e02f49978ae26cf8504", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:18.887208+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p388", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 388, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "JN 177283\n\n                                        17 October 1947\n\nFrom:      Lieutenant Delbert C. Newhouse, (Chief Photographer), USN, 177283.\nTo  :      The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31).\nVia :      The Supply Officer in Command.\n\nSubj:      Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\nRef :      (a) BuPers Circular Letter No. 175-47.\n\nEncl:      (A) Certificate of physical fitness.\n           (B) Special Report of Fitness.\n\n     1.    In accordance with reference (a), I hereby apply for a permanent\ncommission in the United States Navy in a limited-duty status.\n\n     2.    The following information is submitted:\n\n           (a) Age 34, born 5 June 1913 at Marcola, Oregon.\n           (b) Does not apply.\n           (c) First enlisted 23 January 1933.\n           (d) 14 years, 11 months and 7 days total active duty.\n           (e) 1 April 1946 appointed to rank of lieutenant for temporary\n               service pursuant to authority contained in AlNav No. 150-47.\n           (f) Reported 9 September 1946 to Aviation Supply Depot, Naval\n               Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, for duty as Photographic Liaison\n               Officer with the collateral duties of: Military Personnel\n               Officer; Recreation Officer; Training Officer; Voting Officer;\n               Savings Bond Officer; Examining Board; Survey Board and\n               Summary Court Martial Board.\n           (g) Chief Photographer's Mate, Aviation, all aerial photographic\n               operations including aerial mapping with single and multiple\n               lens cameras and motion picture photography.\n           (h) (1) N.A.S.D., Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.  Photographic\n                   Liaison Officer and Officer in Charge, Photographic\n                   Materials.  September 1944 to September 1946.\n               (2) NAS, Coco Solo, C. Z.  Photographic Officer.  June 1943\n                   to September 1944.\n               (3) Commandant Fifteenth Naval District.  Assistant to Officer\n                   in Charge District Photographic Activities.  February 1943\n                   to June 1943.\n               (4) Advanced Base \"GAMMA\" later designated as U. S. Naval\n                   Base, Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador.  Gunnery Officer with\n                   the collateral duties of (1) Photographic Officer, (2)\n                   Athletic Officer, (3) Educational Officer, (4) Welfare\n                   Officer.  August 1942 to February 1943.\n\n                              -1-", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fcd227b123023dd7f82e449e29b6c9f587c31a71cc3478f0a4a48d10b56a84e3", "output_sha256": "63814a164338e0d8b4bc81628369a0c0915e7d1af750788ced5e25f4785cc3c6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:21.521114+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p389", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 389, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "4 May 1948\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nTo:    Operations (a) Sub-Board (CDR MOORE)\n\nThe enlisted record of NEWHOUSE, Delbert C.,\ncannot be located.  Consideration for selection\nwill have to be based on his officer record only.\n\n\n                         G. F. DALTON,\n                         Recorder.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "95aff4f694159a7f7ce117e0c4a5a1ac26e8357fa579a13f675921b7251905f5", "output_sha256": "95aff4f694159a7f7ce117e0c4a5a1ac26e8357fa579a13f675921b7251905f5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:22.294522+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p390", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 390, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVMED H-8          Page ___________________\n     (1943)\n          MEDICAL HISTORY\n               ________\n\nNEWHOUSE,          (Surname)     177283\nDelbert    Clement\n               (Christian name(s))\nBorn: Place Marcola, Ore.              Date 6-5-13\n     STATE NAME OF PLACE        DATE EACH NEW ENTRY\n\nU.S. Naval Air Station, (ASD)\nPearl Harbor, T.H.\n20, October 1947\nRef.: BuPers C/L 175-47, NDB, 15, Sept.,\n                                       1947.\n     This Officer is considered to be\nphysically qualified to perform full\nduty at sea and on foreign shore in a\nLimited Duty Officer status and meets\nthe standards for original officer\nappointment, (Part II, MMD) and if commissioned, the applicant could reasonably\nbe expected to remain physically qualified.\n\n                    N.L. YOOD, CDR(MC)USN\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                    ☆   GPO   16-9017-1\n\n          ENCLOSURE (A)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e16a06819454cf53bd8947086058d76017431002106453de0c90ff2c106b842c", "output_sha256": "54963b8680e9bf1664f7ee4c9a5b186e6a53942245f49e00f027e82465171e69", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:23.673240+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p391", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 391, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Page _______________\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n________\n\nSTATE NAME OF PLACE     DATE EACH NEW ENTRY\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n--------------------------------------------------------------------