S               YES  X NO                        to the officer for statement.\n    HIS EFFICIENCY?\n12. Give here a clear, concise appraisal of the officer reported on and his performance of duty, including any worthy of special mention. Include recommendations as to promotion. Any state-\n    ments of unsatisfactory performance, ability, character, or conduct must be referred to the officer for statement. Statements of a constructive nature which refer to minor imperfections or lack of\n    qualifications do not require reference to the officer for statement; e.g., \"This officer was a little slow in getting started but is now making good progress\" or \"This officer is well qualified in his\n    present duties but has had no experience at sea\" would not be unsatisfactory in nature.\n\n              Check one of these boxes — I CONSIDER THIS REPORT TO BE  X SATISFACTORY  □ UNFAVORABLE  □ UNSATISFACTORY\n\n    Lt. Newhouse's performance of assigned duties in the command has been uniformly\n    excellent.  He is a mature officer.  He possesses all of the qualities indicative of\n    a desirable officer -- loyalty, initiative, intelligence, industry and tact coupled\n    with a high standard of personal and military conduct.  Of the considerable number\n    of temporarily commissioned officers with whom I am acquainted, I consider him to be\n    definitely outstanding.\n\n    Lt. Newhouse is highly recommended for commission as a limited duty officer.\n\n\nSIGNATURE OF OFFICER REPORTED ON (applies only to Sections 1 through 5)    SIGNATURE [ILLEGIBLE] (If additional space is needed attach extra sheet)    Has this report been\n                                                                                                                                                          shown or referred to\nD.C. Newhouse                                    H.[ILLEGIBLE] Foley                                                                                  □ officer reported o