3080035de87414c8552a5ae673fff11e1b67523d1362f36896c74453361", "output_sha256": "b8ae53080035de87414c8552a5ae673fff11e1b67523d1362f36896c74453361", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:57.167332+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p394", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 394, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In Reply Refer to                    UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n                                              Air Force\n          FU/FF12/P14-2          UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n          60:Sr\n\n          Serial:\n                    62\n                                                        17 JAN 1948\n\n          FIRST ENDORSEMENT to:\n          LT D.C. NEWHOUSE, USN,\n          ltr request dtd 16\n          January 1948.\n\n          From:          The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n          To:            The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn: Pers-31).\n\n          Subject:       Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\n            1.           Forwarded.\n\n\n\n                                        J.C. CRONIN.\n\n          Copy to:\n            LT NEWHOUSE.\n\nForm No. UTWING-20", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1bc87d2f23207bcee4af9f2d6b52b2fa87231e9db63d45e166c7aa4feb4f6fb2", "output_sha256": "17fcda70052dc7be096dc6618fb9c84bb46f5f08b4c5de44d6c3d3b24a3221de", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:45:58.323585+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p395", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 395, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "In Reply Refer to          UNITED STATES PACIFIC FLEET\n   JN 177233                        Air Force\n                         UTILITY WING, PACIFIC FLEET\n\n                                              16 January 1948.\n\nFrom:        Lieutenant Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, (Chief Photographer),\n             USN, 177233.\nTo:          The Chief of Naval Personnel (Attn:  Pers-31).\nVia:         The Commander Utility Wing, Pacific Fleet.\n\nSubject:     Transfer to Commissioned Limited-Duty Status.\n\nReference:   (a) SOinC, Naval Supply Center, Pearl Harbor, T.H. ltr\n                 NT4-9/P17/00/021/CF ser 10583 dtd 31 Oct 1947.\n             (b) BuPers C/L No. 175-47.\n             (c) BuPers C/L No. 245-47.\n\n        1.        Reference (a) forwarded my request for transfer to\ncommissioned limited-duty status.\n\n        2.        Due to the change in paragraph 4, second sentence, of\nreference (b) effected by reference (c), it is requested that paragraph\n2 (1) of my request for commissioned limited-duty be changed to read:\n\"I do desire to be considered for a lower rank than now held, but not\nless than lieutenant (junior grade).\"\n\n\n                              Delbert C. Newhouse\n                         DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE,\n                         Lieutenant, U. S. Navy.\n\n\n        I do solemnly swear that all statements made in this request for\nmodification of application are entirely true and complete to the best\nof my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n                              Delbert Clement Newhouse\n                         DELBERT CLEMENT NEWHOUSE.\n\n\n        Subscribed and sworn to before me this sixteenth day of January\n1948.  I have authority to administer oaths.\n\n\n                              A. E. Marden\n                         A. E. MARDEN,\n                         Lieutenant, U. S. Navy.\n\n\nForm No. UTWING-20", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "134b8d45959c65aed0e4691e9b6887e05b78d9329a2d9baeb390a8fbf421f04b", "output_sha256": "ea2562d7412a2be93ab38d1afd4060312e9985a35394655c7b158dc75c42cae6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:00.443707+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p396", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 396, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICER SELECTION TEST\n\nReport of scores for:\n\nName                    NEWHOUSE DELBERT C                    S-3\n\nService Number          177283          COLLEGE DEGREE\n\nSection of Test    APTITUDE    ENGLISH    HISTORY    MATHEMATICS    SCIENCE    TOTAL SCORE\n\nPercentile Score      99          94         93           81            97          98\n\n\n                                                    NAVY TEST RESEARCH UNIT\n                                                         Princeton, N. J.\nAPR 30 1946\n\n              (See reverse side for explanation of scores)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "53b23f0a061868c906674bb48bb942fd6951c9dc815f5ecf5c6e20fe2bb858aa", "output_sha256": "53b23f0a061868c906674bb48bb942fd6951c9dc815f5ecf5c6e20fe2bb858aa", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:01.384471+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p397", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 397, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "EXPLANATION OF SCORES\n\n1. The scores are given in percentiles. The percentile scores run from 01 to 99 and indicate the percent of candidates receiving a lower score. Thus, if a candidate has a percentile score 63, 63 percent of the candidates taking the test made a lower score and 37 percent had the same or a higher score.\n\n2. It should be noted that the total score percentile is not an average of the percentiles for the sections, but indicates a candidate's relative standing on the basis of his total test score. Candidates with a generally high record on the test will have a percentile on the total score that is higher than the average of their percentiles on the sections. Similarly, candidates with a generally low record on the test will have a lower percentile on the total score than the average of their section percentile scores.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f43076ef25b6c69cd2cb54612eef600e839ab53f8bbe94a75be1e76056298d04", "output_sha256": "f43076ef25b6c69cd2cb54612eef600e839ab53f8bbe94a75be1e76056298d04", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:02.491524+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p398", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 398, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BRIEF SHEET-TRANSFER TO U.S. NAVY\nNAVPERS-2965 (11-45)\nNAME (Last)          (First)          (Middle)     FILE NO.      CORP-- CLASSIF.     RANK          [  ]USN\n\nNEWHOUSE    DELBERT    CLEMENT  177283                              LT.j.g.     USNR\n\nI. INCOMING CHECK OFF                                                         APPLICATION CODE\n1. APPLICATION RECEIVED WITHIN 6 MOS. OF DATE OF INACTIVE DUTY\n\n[  ] YES          [  ] NO          [✓] NOT APPLICABLE\n\n[✓] SIGNATURE                    [  ] THROUGH DISTRICT COMMANDANT\n                                                                              C PHOT/COMM/L\n2. (Check One)               3. LOCAL BOARD ACTION\n[✓] CO                [  ] NOT           [✓] RECOM-          [  ] NOT\n    RECOMMENDATION         RECOMMENDED         MENDED               RECOMMENDED\n\n4.\n[✓] FORM Y              [  ] NAVMED AV-1 (Duplicate)     [  ] SWORN AND SUBSCRIBED STATEMENT    REMARKS\n    (Duplicate)                                               BY APPLICANT RE DEFECTS\n\n[✓] SIGNATURES          [✓] CHEST X-RAY                  [  ] CURRENT BLOOD KAHN\n    BY MED. OF.             (Within 6 Months)\n\n5.\n[✓] FITNESS REPORT WITH    (Except officers who apply while on terminal leave,    CHECKED BY          DATE\n    SPECIAL NOTATION        inactive duty or after resignation)                    a.f.   