UTY STATION\n                                              [ILLEGIBLE stamp]                  [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n                                                                                                        (P)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6ee17780bc7fa609a6f7425f9f4e33aed6bbe6f93681d3847955d047424eb5ab", "output_sha256": "24866cff31e5ae2736bdcf373dc75b5bbea901ea74244c2bc4f6b9796cc7b1e0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:06.130327+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p399", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 399, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "1   4\n\n                                        LOCAL BOARD\n                                        NAVAL BASE, PHILA., PA.\n                                        5 April 1946\n\n   Ref: End. to:  Lt. (jg) Hewhouse's ltr. dated 29 March 1946\n\nTo:   Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nSubj: Lieut. (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, USN(T)\n      Request for transfer to U. S. Navy.\n\nRef:  (a) ComFour ltr. A17-31 of 13 December 1945.\n      (b) BuPers Circ. Ltr. No. 288-45 (Revised) of 15 November.\n      (c) BuPers Circ. Ltr. No. 303-45.\n      (d) Nav Act 36-46.\n      (e) Applicant's request for permanent commission in the\n          U. S. Navy dated 27 August 1945.\n\n  1.  A board consisting of:\n\n            Captain Dennis L. Francis, USN, member;\n            Commander William R. Miller, USN, member;\n            Commander Frank G. Law, USN, member;\n            Lieutenant Leslie T. Bukstel, CD, USNR, recorder;\n met at the Naval Base, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, at 0900\n on 5 April 1946 in compliance with reference (a).\n\n  2.  The board personally reinterviewed the applicant and submits the following comment:\n\n(a) He does not possess the educational requirements.\n\n(b) He will be given the general background and mental capacity test.\n\n(c) He does not meet the requirements as to age.\n\n(d) He meets the other requirements of BuPers Circ. Ltr. 288-45\n    (revised), BuPers Circ. Ltr. 303-45.\n\n(e) He has had sea duty.\n\n  3.  The board forwards this request as a modification of the\noriginal request dated 27 August 1945.  It is noted that the applicant\nis average and does not meet the educational requirements.  He\nwill be given the general background and mental capacity test.\n\n             10 APR REC'D         [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n                                  DENNIS L. FRANCIS\n                                  Captain, USN\n                                  Senior Member, Acting", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "649508543e9e762cf8fd7b3bb64d5e6fa990445aa41dcad1438f0b40d0723404", "output_sha256": "37dc9af0e167b9f7cbde3eb4d77bff66afd37974f5c93a16f4913043683261b7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:08.620680+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p400", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 400, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "End-2                    3 April, 1946               Naval Base Station\n                                                     Philadelphia, 12, Pa.\n\n\nTo:       The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nVia:      Local Board to Consider Applicants for Transfer of\n          Reserve and U.S.N. (Temporary) Officers to the Regular\n          Navy. (Captain F. H. Dean, U.S.N., Senior Member).\n\nSubj:     Lieutenant (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, USN(T).\n          Supplemental application for transfer to Regular Navy.\n\nRef:      (a)  Applicant's Request for Permanent Commission\n               in the U. S. Navy dated 27 August 1945.\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\nBy direction of ComFour:\n\n                                        E. H. MOLLISON\n                                Special Asst. to Asst. Chief of Staff\n                                        for Personnel", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f46d0f89d05134edc4c6827053d05ec112959dbe32e1118b7960a47dfadb3e7e", "output_sha256": "f46d0f89d05134edc4c6827053d05ec112959dbe32e1118b7960a47dfadb3e7e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:09.796523+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p401", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 401, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Jacket No. 17728[?]\nEnd-1          1  APR 1946          NASD, Philadelphia, Pa.\n\nTo:      BuPers\n\nVia:     (1) ComFour (Local Board)\n         (2) DCNO (Air) Op-512\n\n1.  Forwarded, recommending approval.\n\n\n                              R. M. HUMES\n                         ADMIN. EXEC. ASSIST.\n                              By direction", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7bb5547e889696cabc76c73dea43e7d5d6d1b3d06bd6bcb26bf700f0c08d7369", "output_sha256": "7bb5547e889696cabc76c73dea43e7d5d6d1b3d06bd6bcb26bf700f0c08d7369", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:10.637090+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p402", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 402, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "IN REPLY ADDRESS\nSUPPLY OFFICER\nNAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\nPHILADELPHIA 11, PA.\n\n                        NAVY DEPARTMENT\nJN 177283          NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                   OXFORD AVENUE AND MARTIN'S MILL ROAD\n                          PHILADELPHIA 11, PA.\n                          SUPPLY DEPARTMENT\n\n        29 March 1946\n\nFrom:       Lieutenant (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, USN (T).\nTo:         The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nVia:        (1) SOIC\n            (2) ComFour (Local Board)\n            (3) CNO, Op53\n\nSubj:       Appointment to Commissioned Rank, U. S. Navy -\n            Request for.\n\nRef:        (a) BuPers C/L 288-45, dated 1 October 1945 and\n                ALNAVS 202, 206 and 207-45.\n            (b) Applicant's Request for Permanent Commission\n                in the U. S. Navy, dated 27 August 1945.\n            (c) NAVACT 136-46.\n\n1.  This supplements and modifies reference (b) in that I request to\nbe considered for appointment as Photographic Specialist as authorized\nby reference (c).\n\n2.  A brief summary of my experience leading to qualification in the\ntechnical phases of photographic development work follows:\n\n        (a) Over twelve years experience in Naval Photography.\n        (b) Installation and operation of photographic laboratories\n            at NAS, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba and Naval Advanced Base,\n            Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador.\n        (c) Redesign, installation of changes and operation of\n            photographic laboratory at NAS, Coco Solo, C. Z.\n        (d) Duty as Photographic Liaison Officer representing\n            the Chief, U. S. Naval Photographic Service, at\n            NASD Philadelphia, Pa.\n\n3.  Recommendation on reference (b) by the Local Board was appointment\nas permanent commissioned warrant officer in the grade of Chief\nPhotographer due to my inability to meet educational requirements for\ncommissioned rank as set forth in reference (a).  It is further requested\ntherefore that I be permitted to take the required qualification test.\n\n4.  If found ineligible for commissioned rank I do wish to be considered\nfor commissioned warrant officer as Chief Photographer as recommended by\nthe Local Board on reference (b).", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e82d05f870dcd96b621accb2e2b1bd9c8f66717f81ad599ea5170e7f14b5dfde", "output_sha256": "e82d05f870dcd96b621accb2e2b1bd9c8f66717f81ad599ea5170e7f14b5dfde", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:13.022698+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p403", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 403, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "- 2 -\n\n5. I do solemnly swear that all statements made in this application\nand any additional statements pertaining hereto are entirely true and\ncomplete to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n                                        D. C. Newhouse\n                                        D. C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\n\nPhiladelphia,\nPennsylvania\n\n\nSubscribed and sworn to before me this    1st    day of April 1946.\nI have authority to administer oaths.\n\n\n                                        W. D. Sams\n                                        W. D. SAMS\n                                        Lieut. (SC), USN", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d97b27410ac5f44daa64ffe9515ec4ccd64100db59a2c3cdf9241a60de669511", "output_sha256": "cfd1fdb8f6e6417bf97851d1de80fbfffa91c32b367c64b40d1f8d190faeca44", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:14.163167+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p404", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 404, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BOARD OF MEDICAL EXAMINERS\nNAVY DEPARTMENT\nWASHINGTON, D.C.\n16 Jan 1946\n\n1.  The Board met at 10:00 A.M. this date, pursuant to an order appearing on the reverse hereof.\n\n2.  The Board convened for the consideration of the physical examination of Lieut. (jg) Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN (177283).\n\n3.  The recorder read the precept.  The Board and recorder were duly sworn.\n\n4.  The Board, having reviewed the report of physical examination mentioned above and the medical records on file in the Bureau of Medicine and Surgery, considers that this officer meets the physical standards for appointment in the U. S. Navy.\n\n5.  We, the undersigned members, therefore, certify that the officer of the case referred to in paragraph 2 is physically qualified for appointment in the U. S. Navy.\n\nL. G. Bell          CAPT.,\nL. G. BELL,         COMDR. (MC)USN\nSenior Member\n\nF. E. Chatard\nF. E. CHATARD,      COMDR. (MC)USN\nMember and Recorder\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nBUMED RP PEH          (ENDORSEMENT)\n\nDate:     16 Jan 1946\n\nTo:       BuPers\n\nSubj:     Record of Proceedings of a Special Board of Medical Examiners.\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n2.  The findings of the Board are approved.\n\nBy direction of the Chief, BuMed:\n\n\n                              C. A. BALL, CAPT. (MC) USN\n\nBUMED-722 (Rev. 11-45)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "58f248c700d1038cfe5357ddc364e298738e810db50869ce4fb600dd7a42ccfe", "output_sha256": "58f248c700d1038cfe5357ddc364e298738e810db50869ce4fb600dd7a42ccfe", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:16.194071+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p405", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 405, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Senior Member                              Member and Recorder\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nBUMED RP PEH                    (ENDORSEMENT)\n\nDate:        16 Jan 1946\n\nTo:          BuPers\n\nSubj:        Record of Proceedings of a Special Board of Medical Examiners.\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n2.  The findings of the Board are approved.\n\n\nBy direction of the Chief, BuMed:\n\n\n                                        C. R. BALL, CAPT. (MC) USN\n\n\nNAVMED-722 (Rev. 11-45)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7269a2034d5e62bf82e59fc01e1dc4dca0351ae11772b12a289974f226059e88", "output_sha256": "7269a2034d5e62bf82e59fc01e1dc4dca0351ae11772b12a289974f226059e88", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:17.243537+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p406", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 406, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVY DEPARTMENT\n             BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n71763                    Washington 25, D.C.\nPers-3176(3191)pmd-2A\n\n26 December 1945\n\nFrom:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nTo:            Captain Luther G. BELL,\n               Medical Corps, USN,\n               Bureau of Medicine and Surgery,\n               Navy Department.\n\nVia:           The Chief of the Bureau of Medicine and Surgery.\n\nSubject:       Precept convening a board of medical examiners.\n\nReference:     (a) SecNav 1st endorsement dated 17 November 1943.\n\n1.  In accordance with the authority vested in me by reference (a), a\nboard of medical examiners for the purpose of acting upon reports of\nphysical examinations of officers of the U. S. Naval Reserve and the\nU. S. Marine Corps Reserve for appointment in the regular Navy and\nMarine Corps, is hereby ordered to convene at the Bureau of Medicine and\nSurgery, Navy Department.\n\n2.  The board will consist of yourself as president and of the following\nnamed officers as members.\n\n                    Captain Clifford P. POWELL, MC, USN,\n                    Commander Gerald W. HURST, MC, USN,\n                    Commander Joseph C. PLACAK, Jr., MC, USNR,\n                    Commander Ferdinand E. CHATARD, MC, USN,\n                    Lieutenant Commander Arthur F. GARDNER, MC, USN, Ret.,\n                    Lieutenant Commander Daniel R. KOHLI, MC, USN.\n\n3.  Lieutenant Commander Daniel R. KOHLI, MC, USN, will act as recorder.\n\n4.  Any two or more members may act in any one case and the junior member\nwill act as recorder in the absence of the designated recorder.\n\n5.  The board of medical examiners convened by BuPers letter Pers-3176\n(3191) gv-2A dated 2 November 1945 is hereby dissolved.\n\n\n                                        LOUIS DENFELD\n\n\nCertified a true copy:\n\n\n /s/ Daniel R. Kohli\n    Lt. Comdr. (MC), USN\n    Member and Recorder", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "09ea358455293db245919a07c69953851f6027ae0bd7c4fcb5befb2a67c84ffa", "output_sha256": "dd56189160c6a47aeae7b87013c7e80cb3e9c9ab4256b271731b83a7e193344b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:19.551238+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p407", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 407, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NYPhil\n                                        19 September 1945\n\nEnd-2  on ltr. from Lieut. (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse (T), USN, 177283,\n       dtd. 27 August 1945.\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\nSubj:  Lieutenant (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, (T), USN, 177283, -\n       Request for Transfer to U. S. Navy.\n\nRef:   (a) ComFour ltr. A17-31 of 22 August 1945.\n       (b) ALNAV 202, 206 and 207 of August 1945.\n\nEncl:  (A) Report of Physical Examination.\n       (B) Fitness Report.\n\n1.   A board consisting of:  Captain Wyatt Craig, U. S. Navy, senior\nmember; Captain John M. Hoskins, U. S. Navy, member; Commander William\nR. Miller, U. S. Navy, member; and Lieutenant (jg) Adolph (N) Rosset,\nU. S. N. R., recorder; met at the Navy Yard, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania,\nat 0900, 19 September in compliance with reference (a).\n\n2.   The board personally interviewed Lieutenant (jg) Newhouse and\nsubmits the following comment:\n\n     (a) He very favorably impressed the board.\n     (b) He is physically qualified as shown by enclosure (A).\n     (c) His experience has been almost entirely in photography.\n     (d) He has the necessary qualification as to age.\n     (e) He has had overseas duty but no shipboard duty during the\n         present war.\n     (f) He meets the other requirements of ALNAVS 202, 206 and 207.\n\n3.   This officer is recommended for a commission as a Chief Photographer in the regular Navy.\n\n\n                                        Wyatt Craig\n                                        Wyatt Craig\n                                        Captain, U. S. N.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "489c10067fcaa3de94b2aaf2e8c0fe28fe268a2892cb6f1320183924ddfcf298", "output_sha256": "6b61a911705924f122234f6d0a370ba04122f78a551279bedff481c71ab050f8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:21.677977+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p408", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 408, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Jacket No. 177283\nEnd-1                                                    NASD, Philadelphia, 11, Pa.\n10 SEP 1945\n\nTo:          BuPers\n\nVia:         ComFour (Local Board)\n\nSubj:        Permanent Commission in the United States Navy - Application\n             for.\n\n1.           Forwarded, approval recommended.\n\n2.           Lt. (jg) Newhouse has been attached to this activity from Sept. 13,\n1944 to the present date. During this period he has demonstrated initiative\nand a keen interest in his duties. Lt. (jg) Newhouse has applied himself thoroughly\nand has shown outstanding ability in his technical specialty. His personal\nand military character is excellent.\n\n\n                              E. D. FOSTER\n\n                         E. D. FOSTER\n                         Rear Admiral (SC) USN\n                         Supply Officer-in-Command", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a02b54860d4425da8385930136e49a8a03e25173045c9f675525a045ef9c064b", "output_sha256": "1b9868921597991689010637e898c67f213f6c0959a7409f433e4fd5ffd0ee76", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:22.869010+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p409", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 409, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "JN 177283\n27 August 1945\n\n     (g) Cont'd.\n          (4) Advanced Base \"GAMMA\" later designated as U. S. Naval\n              Base, Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador.  Gunnery Officer with\n              the collateral duties of (1) Photographic Officer, (2)\n              Athletic Officer, (3) Educational Officer, (4) Welfare\n              Officer.  August 1942 to February 1943.\n          (5) Naval Air Station, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.  Chief in\n              charge of Photographic Laboratory.  November 1940 to\n              August 1942.\n          (6) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Scouting Force, Patrol Squadron\n              Fourteen (Redesignated from VP-45).  Senior Photographer,\n              June 1939 to November 1940.\n          (7) U. S. Naval Air Station, San Diego, Calif.  Photographer.\n              April 1936 to June 1939.\n          (8) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Battle Force, Bombing Squadron\n              One-B.  Photographer.  December 1935 to April 1936.\n          (9) Naval Air Station, Pensacola.  Under instruction at\n              Naval School of Photography.  June 1935 to December 1935.\n          (10) U. S. Fleet, Aircraft Battle Force, Scouting Squadron\n              Three-B.  Photographer striker.  November 1934 to June\n              1935.\n          (11) U. S. Fleet, Commander Aircraft Battle Force (FLAG DIV.)\n              Yeoman striker.  June 1933 to November 1934.\n          (12) Naval Training Station, San Diego, Calif.  Under recruit\n              training.  January 1933 to June 1933.\n     (h) Graduate of Naval School of Photography at Naval Air Station,\n         Pensacola, Fla.\n     (i)(1) Good Conduct Medal.\n         (2) American Defense campaign ribbon with one star.\n         (3) American Theater campaign ribbon.\n     (j) Graduated from twelfth grade at Garibaldi High School, Garibaldi,\n         Oregon 1931.\n         Enrolled at the University of Kansas, Lawrence, Kansas in Sept.\n         1931 and withdrew from the University in December of the same\n         year.\n     (k) Have had no civilian business or professional experience.\n\n\n                              D. C. Newhouse\n                              D. C. NEWHOUSE\n\n\nPhiladelphia\nPennsylvania\n\n     Subscribed and sworn to before me this 31st day of August 1945.\n\n\n                              J. A. NOBLE, LT. SC(S) USNR,\n                              Military Personnel Officer.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8c3694e552fa642b0bc7d1f0cf1ffb2e2d60cdfa97ec503eddbfdff1bdb7f5f4", "output_sha256": "abeafd30dba5e64895aabb7d28227991fec2af4e4d96564eb9f4f50b7ce65aca", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:25.561081+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p410", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 410, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CORRESPONDENCE (IN DUPLICATE)\nSHOULD BE ADDRESSED TO THE\nSUPPLY OFFICER-IN-COMMAND, NOT\nTO SIGNER OF THIS LETTER, AND\nREFER TO NO.\n\nJN 177283\n\n                    NAVAL AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                    OXFORD AVENUE & MARTIN'S MILL ROAD\n                         PHILADELPHIA 11, PA.\n\n\n     27 August 1945\n\n     From:      Lieutenant (jg) Delbert C. Newhouse, USN (T)\n     To:        The Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n     Via:       (1) SOIC, NASD\n                (2) ComFour\n\n     Subj:      Permanent Commission in the United States Navy -\n                Application for\n\n     Ref:       (a) ALNAV 207\n\n\n     1.   In accordance with the provisions of reference (a), I hereby\n     make application for permanent commission in the United States Navy.\n\n     2.   The information requested by reference (a) follows:\n\n          (a) Age - 32, born 5 June 1913 at Marcola, Oregon.\n          (b) Does not apply.\n          (c) Reported for active duty as apprentice seaman 24 January 1933.\n          (d) Appointed lieutenant (junior grade) 1 September 1944 by ALNAV\n              for temporary duty.\n          (e) Present duty is Naval Aviation Supply Depot, Philadelphia,\n              Pennsylvania, in the capacity of Bureau of Aeronautics\n              Representative and Technical Advisor in Photography to\n              the Supply Officer in Command.  My duties as Assistant\n              to the Officer in Charge of the Photographic Unit (Storage\n              Division) include administration of the unit in receipt,\n              stowage, and issue of photographic materials.  This unit\n              handles its own invoicing and correspondence, combining\n              the regular functions of Stock Control and Issue Divisions.\n          (f) Operational photography and photographic supply.\n          (g) (1) NASD, Philadelphia, Penna.  Reported for duties described\n                  in paragraph (e) above on 13 September 1944.\n              (2) NAS, Coco Solo, C. Z.  Photographic Officer from June 1943\n                  to Sept. 1944.\n              (3) Commandant Fifteenth Naval District.  Assistant to Officer\n                  in Charge District Photographic Activities.  February 1943\n                  to June 1943.\n\n\n                                    -1-", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "935926fec363477717bb6e2ac4f3d790aab786965d4f1a5999243adc3ff7563d", "output_sha256": "935926fec363477717bb6e2ac4f3d790aab786965d4f1a5999243adc3ff7563d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:27.939314+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p411", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 411, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NMS Form Y\n(1939)\n\n                              REPORT OF PHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n                                                    TRANSFER TO REGULAR NAVY & PER-    Date of examination    28 August 1945\n\nPlace of duty    NASD, PHILA., PA.                    Place of examination    NASD, PHILA., PA.\n\nName    NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement  177263        Rank    Lt.(jg)        Corps    USN\n              (Surname first, Christian names in full)\nPlace of birth    Oregon                                    Date of birth    6-5-13\n\nFamily history    Irrelevant\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHistory of illness or injury    Mumps, Influenza, Measles. Fracture of left clavicle and scapula,\nAppendectomy 1930.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHead and face    Normal\n\n     Eyes: Pupils (size, shape, reaction to light and distance, etc.)    Round, equal, react to L & A\n\n          Distant vision Rt.    18    /20, corrected to    20    /20 by    Lenses\n\n                           Lt.    18    /20, corrected to    20    /20 by    Lenses\n\n          Binocular vision    ---              Color perception    Normal AOP 1940\n               (Without lenses—Recorded only when visual defects exist)        (State edition of Stilling's plates used)\n          Disease or anatomical defects    None\n\nEars: Hearing Rt. Watch    40  /40\"   Coin click  20  /20'   Whispered voice    15  /15'   Spoken voice    15  /15'\n\n               Lt. Watch    40  /40\"   Coin click  20  /20'   Whispered voice    15  /15'   Spoken voice    15  /15'\n\n          Binaural    ---  /15'.   Disease or defects    None\n               (Spoken voice)\nNose    Normal\n                    (Disease or anatomical defect, obstruction, etc.  State degree)\nSinuses    Normal\n\nTongue, palate, pharynx, larynx, tonsils    Normal\n\nTeeth and gums (disease or anatomical defect):    Normal\n\n     Missing teeth    #17, 32\n                        (List numbers)\n     Nonvital teeth    No. 9\n                        (List numbers)\n     Periapical disease    None\n                              (Degree)\n     Marked malocclusion    No\n                                  (Yes or no)\n     Lack of serviceable occlusion    No\n                                        (Yes or no)\n     Pyorrhea alveolaris              None\n                          (Degree)\n     Teeth replaced by bridges    None\n                                    (List numbers)\n     Meets dental requirements    Yes\n                                    (Yes or no)\n     Dentures              None\n                    (Description)\nGeneral build and appearance    Medium\n                                    (State whether slender, medium, or heavy, and postural abnormalities)\nTemperature    98.6                    Chest at expiration    39\n\nHeight    73\"                          Chest at inspiration    43\n\nWeight    198                          Circumference of abdomen at umbilicus    35\n\nRecent gain or loss, amount and cause    None\n\nSkin, hair, and glands                          Normal\n\nNeck (abnormalities, thyroid gland, trachea, larynx)    Normal\n\nSpine and extremities (bones, joints, muscles, feet)    Normal\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                                                                              M. Hovsepian\n                                                                           M. HOVSEPIAN, (DC) LT.USNR\n                                                                              (Signature of dental examiner)\n\n                                                                                                        16—11249", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8f50a1d31bd1fa3ba8a069dd9e9a6e4c6baab5e8f503090c978a2ff0717b4a20", "output_sha256": "296be0bfb13fb7705ba58428a76a9bbc6cbbfd462b6df27c6dbc1853f4144639", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:31.353262+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p412", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 412, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Thorax (size, shape, movement, rib cage, mediastinum) _________________ Normal\n\n  Respiratory system, bronchi, lungs, pleura, etc. _____________________ Normal\n\nCardio-vascular system ______________________________________________ Normal\n    Heart (note all signs of cardiac involvement) _________________ Normal\n\n    Pulse: Before exercise _____ 88 ___________________  Blood pressure: Before, S ___120______ D ___80_______\n      After exercise ___ 108 _____________________       Three minutes after, S __110___, D __80____\n                                                         (Manual of the Medical Department par. 1520(6))\n      Three minutes after ___ 96 __________________\n    Condition of arteries __________ Normal _____________  Character of pulse ___ Full & Regular ____________\n    Condition of veins _____________ Normal _____________  Hemorrhoids _________ None ____________________\nAbdomen and pelvis (condition of wall, scars, herniae, abnormality of viscera) _____________ Appendectomy 1930\n\nGenito-urinary system ___ Normal\n    Urinalysis: Sp. gr. ___1.024_______, alb. ___Neg._________, sugar ___Neg.__________, microscopical ___==\n    Venereal disease _______ None\nNervous system ________ Normal\n                                        (Organic or functional disorders)\n    Romberg ______________ Negative _____________________  Incoordination (gait, speech) ____ Normal\n    Reflexes, superficial ___ Normal _______, deep (knee, ankle, elbow) ________ Normal ____________ Tremors None\n    Serological tests (when required) _______ Not required\n    Abnormal psyche (neurasthenia, psychasthenia, depression, instability, worries) ___________ None\n\nSmallpox vaccination { Date last vaccination __ 9-21-42\n                     { Reaction ________ Immune                    Typhoid prophylaxis { Number of courses _______ Two\n                                                                                        { Date of last course ______ 2-18-38\nRemarks on abnormalities not otherwise noted or sufficiently described above _________ None\n\nSummary of defects ___ Defective vision both eyes 18/20, corrected to 20/20, NCD.\n\nIs the individual fit to perform active duty at sea or on foreign service?  (If not, state limit of duty) ____ Yes\n\nFindings and recommendations (as per Courts and Boards, when necessary) ___ Examined and found physically\nqualified for transfer to regular Navy and permanent rank.\n\n                                          A. H. Vaughn\n                                 A. H. VAUGHN, LT. COMDR. (MC) USNR\n                                          P. R. Cronlund\n                                 P. R. CRONLUND, LT. (MC) USNR\nRemarks or endorsement ___\n\nINSTRUCTIONS: Be definite in statement and specific in recommendation. All abnormal conditions shall be given diagnostic titles as listed in Navy\nNomenclature. The original only shall be forwarded direct to the Bureau of Medicine and Surgery except in cases of personnel of the Naval Reserve when\nthe original and one copy shall be forwarded via the Commandant. Regarding preliminary examinations for the Naval Academy, see paragraph 1403, and\nfor color perception, paragraph 1428, Manual of the Medical Department, U. S. Navy. The spoken voice (ordinary conversation) shall be recorded in all\ncases of defective hearing. In recording, the numerator of the fraction shall be the distance at which Snellen's 20-foot test letters can be determined\nand the denominator, 20.\n                                                                                                              16—11249", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5936509fab21e9a9c78faae83d6bf88247180abacbb61ae2673ee25b28938b54", "output_sha256": "8eb03be1fbc7849b05fa0a18a71baecaa1a2e359551a807a29ccc030fef70437", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:34.740508+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p413", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 413, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "1/7283\nPers-3271-TLG\n\n4 February 1947.\n\n\nTo:          General Accounting Office,\n             Claims Division,\n             Washington 25, D.C.\n\nSubject:     Lieut. Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN - statement of service\n             for use in connection with claim for longevity pay purposes.\n\nReference:   (a) GAO ltr., Claim No. 2303893-SH, dtd 12 Dec 46.\n\n1.  The following is a statement of subject officer's service as shown by\nthe records of this Bureau:\n\n               OREGON NATIONAL GUARD (ACTIVE).\n               18 Mar 29  Enlisted.\n               25 Jan 32  Honorably discharged.\n\n               (Underage - 18 years 5 June 1931).\n\n               U. S. NAVY.\n               24 Jan 33  Enlisted, USN.\n               1  Sep 42  Photographer (tempo.), USN.\n               15 Jun 43  Ensign (tempo.).\n               1  Sep 44  Lieut. (jg) (tempo.), USN.\n               1  Apr 46  Lieut. (tempo.).\n               Continuous service to date.\n\n               No record of time lost.\n\n2.  It is requested you contact Lieutenant Newhouse for the activities to\nwhich attached during the period in question.\n\n\nBy direction of the Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n\n                              M A Robertson\n                              Lieut. USNR\n                              Officer Performance Div.\n\n\n\n                         FINISHED FILE COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ee45f9e580e00a1c447e9e233518fbfe6c4c0c194fb9cf816b6314e38f16b02b", "output_sha256": "ee45f9e580e00a1c447e9e233518fbfe6c4c0c194fb9cf816b6314e38f16b02b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:46:36.742205+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p414", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 414, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "GENERAL ACCOUNTING OFFICE\n           WASHINGTON 25\n\n         NAVAL HISTORY\n\nCLAIMS DIVISION\nIN REPLY PLEASE QUOTE\n\n2303893\n                                                    DEC 1 2 1946\n\nNavy Department,\nBureau of Naval Personnel,\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\n     It is requested that information as checked below be furnished relative to:\n\nNewhouse        Delbert         O        177283      Lt. USN\n  Last Name      First Name    Initial   Service No.  Rank/Rating\n\n[X] Statement of Service.  [X] Transcript of Service  2/11/43 - 6/30/44\n\n[X] Please show all credited dates ships or stations from\n2/11/43 - 6/30/44 for longevity purposes.\n\n\n                                              Sam Harvey\n                                           For Chief of Section\n\nNavy Department,\nBureau of Naval Personnel.            Washington, D. C. ___________________\n\n     Returned to General Accounting Office, Claims Division, with information that:\n\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n              ENLISTED                        DISCHARGED\n  Date      Place Accepted         Date       Place          Unauthorized Absences\n\n\n\n\n                              FINISHED FILE