acket.\n    One-Officer concerned.                       THOMAS DURFEE\n    One-Com15\n\n                                        NOTED PERS 32152", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a4e1808ceddb70562489674b272530d3916a6c00619a19a2313f0afd6baf6a63", "output_sha256": "2e85d27dd612a680f8fd5ece925cb36d90303e8817e1adff2eb11faa9e22df89", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:08.403958+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p434", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 434, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS-1782(3-44)\nSTATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT\n\n[ ] OFFICER FILE     [ ] ENLISTED FILE                    REGISTERED NO. 861\nNAME                                                       APPOINTED TO\n\n  Delbert C. Newhouse                177283                    LT.(jg)\nDATE OF APPOINTMENT  | DATE OF RANK  |              | NUMBER | DATED\n  1 Sept.'44         | 1 Sept.'44    | [ ] CIRCULAR LETTER  [ ] *LNAV   169   1 Sept.'44\n\nSubject to the conditions stated below, the above individual was appointed by the\nPresident to the rank indicated above, for temporary service.\n\nIn the event all stated conditions be met, the appointment (unless expressly declined)\nis to be regarded for all purposes as having been accepted on the date made, without\nformal acceptance or oath of office, as provided in Section 5 of an Act of Congress\napproved June 30, 1942, (Public No. 639 - 77th Congress).\n\nCONDITIONS NECESSARY TO EFFECTUATION OF APPOINTMENT:\n  1.  Physical qualification.\n  2.  Delivery of appointment by commanding officer.\n  3.  Not declined.\n  4.  Not: (a) under treatment in hospital;\n           (b) on sick leave;\n           (c) missing;\n           (d) prisoner of war.\n\n================================================================================\n\nNOTE:  The effectiveness of this ap