nder treatment in hospital;\n           (b) on sick leave;\n           (c) missing;\n           (d) prisoner of war.\n\n\nNOTE:  The effectiveness of this appointment must be verified by other correspondence in the officer's\n       correspondence jacket unless notation appears hereon indicating appointment not effected.\n\n\n\n\n\n                         Finished File Pers-32152\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA32034                   STATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0ec4d1dee38b37d986ddce65c05ff2f8d2e504ae85ce8e4381e1c1bd7117fcd7", "output_sha256": "0ec4d1dee38b37d986ddce65c05ff2f8d2e504ae85ce8e4381e1c1bd7117fcd7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:12.044945+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p436", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 436, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "55-212\n\nBUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\nNAVY DE[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNA10/P17-2/00                    U. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\n                                  Coco Solo, Upham, C.Z.\n177283                            Navy 1955\n                                  c/o Fleet Post Office\n              1943 JUL  9  PM 1:  New York, N.Y.\n                                  6 July 1943\n\nFrom:        Ensign Delbert C. Newhouse, U. S. Navy.\nTo:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\nVia:         The Commanding Officer.\n\nSubject:     Acknowledgement of notice of Temporary Appointment.\n\n          1.     I hereby acknowledge receipt of notice of my appointment\nto the rank of    Ensign              in the regular Navy,\nfor temporary service made by the President on 15 June 1943.\n\n          2.     Notice of this temporary appointment was made by my\nCommanding Officer pursuant to the authority contained in BuPers C/L\n96-43.\n\n          3.     This temporary appointment has not and will not be\ndeclined by me.\n\n          4.     Two (2) certified copies of this letter are being furnished\nby me to the Disbursing Officer carrying my accounts in order that my pay\nmay be adjusted accordingly.\n\n\n                                   Delbert C. Newhouse\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -Delbert C. Newhouse- - - - - - - - -\nNA10/P17-2/00           FIRST ENDORSEMENT      U. S. Naval Air Station,\n                                               Coco Solo, Upham, C. Z.\n                                               Navy 1955\n                                               c/o Fleet Post Office,\n                                               New York, N.Y.\n\n\nFrom:        The Commanding Officer.\nTo:          The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n          1.     Forwarded.\n\nCopy to:\n     Com15                                     R. P. Kauffman\n                                          R. P. KAUFFMAN\n\n| 1   6   10   22   23   24  (31)  3[ILLEGIBLE]  36   62   211   215   222   1[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\"X\" out and initial over your encircled Pers. No. before rele[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nFINISHED FILE PERS 3161", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f9fcd0a26a5f7abd8cc248e42ed05ca29440518a503ce4265fc56916bc3d8ece", "output_sha256": "f9fcd0a26a5f7abd8cc248e42ed05ca29440518a503ce4265fc56916bc3d8ece", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:14.455852+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p437", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 437, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS-1782\nSTATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT\n\n☑ OFFICER FILE     □ ENLISTED FILE                              REGISTERED NO. 133\nNAME                                    Appointed to\n\n   NEWHOUSE, Delbert C.          177283                         Ensign USN\nDATE OF APPOINTMENT  | DATE OF RANK  |                    | NUMBER  | DATED\n   15JUN'43          |  15JUN'43     | ☑ CIRCULAR LETTER  □ ALNAV | 96 - 43 | 15JUN'43\n\nSubject to the conditions stated below, the above individual was appointed by the\nPresident to the rank indicated above, for temporary service.\n\nIn the event all stated conditions be met, the appointment (unless expressly declined)\nis to be regarded for all purposes as having been accepted on the date made, without\nformal acceptance or oath of office, as provided in Section 5 of an Act of Congress\napproved June 30, 1942, (Public No. 639 - 77th Congress).\n\nCONDITIONS NECESSARY TO EFFECTUATION OF APPOINTMENT:\n   1.   Physical qualification.\n   2.   Delivery of appointment by commanding officer.\n   3.   Not declined.\n   4.   Not: (a) under treatment in hospital;\n             (b) on sick leave;\n             (c) missing;\n             (d) prisoner of war.\n\n\n         THE EFFECTIVENESS OF THIS APPOINTMENT MUST BE VERIFIED BY\n         OTHER CORRESPONDENCE IN THE OFFICER'S CORRESPONDENCE JACKET\n         UNLESS NOTATION APPEARS HEREON INDICATING APPOINTMENT NOT\n                           EFFECTED.\n\n\n\n\n                         FINISHED FILE PERS 326\n                    STATEMENT OF TEMPORARY APPOINTMENT", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f6e18ad567abc49026aae4eb945c4f0b8c8f10616d8ba343201fada4ee3d8b88", "output_sha256": "d599e4f4739c8a4a7abb9875b8366e1df1f5880dfdca85a96c5c1ac930a7cde2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:16.376462+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p438", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 438, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "U. S. NAVAL BASE\n        Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador\n        October 15, 1942\n\n                              BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                              NAVY DEPARTMENT\n                              RECEIVED\n\nFrom:      Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\nTo:        The Bureau of Naval Personnel.          177283\n                                                NOV 6  PM 2 01\nSubject:   Acceptance of Appointment to the Rank of 1942\n           Photographer, USN for Temporary Service.\n\nReference: (a)  Commanding Officer, U. S. Naval Base\n                Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador letter of\n                October 15, 1942.\n           (b)  BuNavPers. C/L No 127-42 of September 1, 1942\n\n     1.    By reference (a) I was informed by my Commanding Officer\nthat I had been appointed by the President of the United States on September\n1, 1942 to the rank of Photographer, USN for temporary service to rank from\nJune 15, 1942, in accordance with reference (b).\n\n     2.    I have this date accepted this appointment.\n\n                                   Delbert C. Newhouse\n                                   Delbert C. Newhouse\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT to          U. S. NAVAL BASE          October 15, 1942\nPhotographer D.C.              Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador\nNewhouse, USN to BuPers\nof October 15, 1942\n\n\nFrom:      The Commanding Officer.\nTo:        The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n     1.    Forwarded.\n\n                                   J. R. Litchfield\n                                   J. R. LITCHFIELD\n\n\n                                             Finished - File\n          Finished - File                    Registrar (Appointments)\n          Registrar (Directory)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7d9813737c55d069e2e3acc6f8efb518ec55b69340132c78b8db71f91eb7d625", "output_sha256": "bb4542b4ce7311370e163f30c45e570938f061e3e509d2ae0cad698f9d79c72a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:18.403072+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p439", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 439, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "U. S. NAVAL BASE\nSanta Elena Bay, Ecuador\nOctober 15, 1942\n\n\nFrom:          Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, USN\nTo:            The Bureau of Naval Personnel.\n\nSubject:       Acceptance of Appointment to the Rank of\n               Photographer, USN for Temporary Service.\n\nReference:     (a)  Commanding Officer, U. S. Naval Base\n                    Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador letter of\n                    October 15, 1942.\n               (b)  BuNavPers, C/L No 127-42 of September 1, 1942\n\n     1.        By reference (a) I was informed by my Commanding Officer\nthat I had been appointed by the President of the United States on September\n1, 1942 to the rank of Photographer, USN for temporary service to rank from\nJune 15, 1942, in accordance with reference (b).\n\n     2.        I have this date accepted this appointment.\n\n\n                                        Delbert C. Newhouse\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT to          U. S. NAVAL BASE          October 15, 1942\nPhotographer D.C.              Santa Elena Bay, Ecuador\nNewhouse, USN to BuPers\nof October 15, 1942\n\n\nFrom:          The Commanding Officer.\nTo:            The Chief of Naval Personnel.\n\n     1.        Forwarded.\n\n\n                                        J. R. LITCHFIELD\n\n\n\n               Finished - File\n               Registrar (Directory)\n\n\n                                        Finished - File\n                                        Registrar (Appointments)\n                                        [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e88b6139c7ffda152c628e337f445ec46144edbea3fd7d6dfd93c59d46f008ab", "output_sha256": "ec640786a1f462bd87d10e53489721b147b44c40c020261af96f237cb055db46", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:20.243536+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p440", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 440, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "ELECTION OF OPTIONS UNDER THE UNIFORMED SERVICES CONTINGENCY OPTION ACT OF 1953\nNAVPERS 591 (NEW 9/53)\nNAME (Last)          (First)          (Middle)     SERVICE NUMBER     RANK OR RATING     USN     USNR\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement                           177283             CHPHOT             X\nPERMANENT ADDRESS                        STATUS                    NO. YEARS SERVICE COMPLETED FOR PAY\n                                  CHECK APPROPRIATE SQUARE          PURPOSES\nMrs. Vencl Richter               REGULAR        RESERVE\n                                             ACTIVE      INACTIVE\n Garibaldi, Oregon                           DUTY        DUTY           24\n                        x                                          MEMBER'S BIRTHDATE\n                                                                        6/5/13\n\n X    I DO NOT DESIRE TO RECEIVE REDUCED RETIRED PAY IN ORDER TO PROVIDE AN ANNUITY FOR MY DEPENDENTS.\n\nI ELECT THE FOLLOWING OPTIONS: (NOTE: YOU MAY SELECT OPTION 1 OR 2 OR 3 AND YOU MAY COMBINE OPTION 4 WITH THE ONE SELECTED,\nOR YOU MAY SELECT OPTIONS 1 AND 2 AND YOU MAY COMBINE OPTION 4 WITH EITHER OR BOTH. HOWEVER, THE COMBINED TOTAL OF OPTIONS ELECTED CANNOT EXCEED 50% OF REDUCED RETIRED PAY.)\n\n      OPTION 1    1/8 [ ]                    1/4 [ ]                              1/2 [ ]\n                  OF MY REDUCED RETIRED PAY PAYABLE TO OR ON BEHALF OF MY WIDOW UNTIL HER REMARRIAGE OR DEATH.\n\n      OPTION 2    1/8 [ ]                    1/4 [ ]                              1/2 [ ]\n                  OF MY REDUCED RETIRED PAY PAYABLE TO OR ON BEHALF OF MY SURVIVING CHILD OR CHILDREN UNMARRIED AND UNDER 18 YEARS OF AGE AND SURVIVING CHILD OR CHILDREN UNMARRIED AND OVER 18 YEARS OF AGE INCAPABLE OF\n                  SELF SUPPORT BECAUSE OF BEING MENTALLY OR PHYSICALLY INCAPACITATED.\n\n      OPTION 3    1/8 [ ]                    1/4 [ ]                              1/2 [ ]\n                  OF MY REDUCED RETIRED PAY PAYABLE TO OR ON BEHALF (A) OF MY SURVIVING WIDOW UNTIL HER REMARRIAGE OR\n                  DEATH AND (B) THEREAFTER TO MY SURVIVING CHILD OR CHILDREN UNMARRIED AND UNDER 18 YEARS OF AGE AND\n                  SURVIVING CHILDREN OVER 18 YEARS OF AGE AND INCAPABLE OF SELF SUPPORT BECAUSE OF BEING MENTALLY OR\n                  PHYSICALLY INCAPACITATED.\n\n      OPTION 4    NO FURTHER DEDUCTIONS SHALL BE MADE FROM MY RETIRED PAY COMMENCING WITH THE FIRST DAY OF THE MONTH\n                  FOLLOWING THAT IN WHICH THERE IS NO BENEFICIARY ELIGIBLE TO RECEIVE AN ANNUITY UPON MY DEATH. I DESIRE\n                  THIS OPTION TO BE COMBINED WITH OPTION NUMBER(S)_______________ CHECKED ABOVE.\n                                                                    (insert numbers)\n\nIMPORTANT: If any of the above options is elected the following information must be furnished:\nFULL NAME OF SPOUSE                                                                        DATE OF BIRTH OF SPOUSE\n\nFULL NAME OF WIFE PRIOR TO MARRIAGE\n\nPLACE OF MARRIAGE          (City)               (County)              (State)             DATE OF MARRIAGE\n\nHAVE YOU BEEN PREVIOUSLY MARRIED?    IF YES, GIVE DATE AND CITY, COUNTY, AND STATE OF DISSOLUTION OF EACH FORMER MARRIAGE AND\n                                     STATE WHETHER BY DEATH, ANNULMENT OR DIVORCE\n     [ ] YES     [ ] NO\n\nHAS YOUR SPOUSE BEEN PREVIOUSLY      IF YES, GIVE DATE AND CITY, COUNTY, AND STATE OF DISSOLUTION OF EACH FORMER MARRIAGE AND\nMARRIED?                             STATE WHETHER BY DEATH, ANNULMENT OR DIVORCE\n     [ ] YES     [ ] NO\n\nIMPORTANT: If either option 2 or 3 is included in your election, furnish required information below concerning legitimate child or children:\n          NAME OF EACH CHILD                    DATE OF BIRTH              INDICATE IF STEPCHILD OR ADOPTED CHILD\n\n\n\n\n\nI understand that during any period subsequent to my transfer to Fleet Reserve or retirement in which I am not receiving retired or retainer\npay, I shall be required to deposit with the United States Treasury the amount that would have been withheld from my retired pay under\nthe Options elected had I been receiving such retired pay, and if I fail to make such deposit I consent to checkage of such undeposited amounts,\nplus accrued interest upon being restored to a pay status; and that if I do not combine option 4 with the option selected, deductions will be made\nfrom my retired pay despite the fact that all beneficiaries predecease me or become ineligible for annuity benefits; and that in the case of retired\nmembers, election of any of the options provided is irrevocable. I certify the above information to be complete and accurate.\n\n                              Signature  D C Newhouse\n                                                    (Sign original and all copies)\n  Finished File Pers E-241    Subscribed and sworn to before me this  last    day\n                              of   March    19 67\n  NOTED TABULATED RECORDS\n                                    Virgil a Starr Phero USN\n                                                    (Signature and Title of Attesting Officer or Notary)\n☆ G. P. O.: 1953-273402          FOR DISTRIBUTION INSTRUCTION SEE NO. 7 ON REVERSE  (ORIGINAL)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4568f5f1f5a5a033c50ec09098df0e8ce7e67b711960edbdae0cd09ba992c5c3", "output_sha256": "d4e186a3403cc580bdbdaaa28d1ecad16d7c538688dd43e71d6edbadb64f4e42", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:29.251187+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p441", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 441, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "05 APR 1954\n\n\nINFORMATION AND INSTRUCTIONS CONCERNING THIS ELECTION FORM\n(For Nonretired members)\n\n1.    It is desired that all members with 17 years service creditable for basic pay purposes, active or inactive, either decline or elect to provide certain annuities for their dependents under the provisions of the Uniformed Services Contingency Option Act of 1953 (Public Law 239-83rd Congress). If you desire to receive a reduction in the retired pay which you may subsequently receive, thereby providing an annuity for your dependents, you must elect the desired option(s) not later than 30 April 1954 or prior to completion of 18 years service creditable for basic pay purposes, whichever is later. The terms of the election may be modified or revoked prior to retirement, but any modification or revocation will not be effective if you retire within five years from the date of such modification or revocation.\n\n2.    If you do not desire to receive reduced retired pay to provide an annuity for your dependents, check the square opposite \"I do not desire to receive reduced retired pay in order to provide an annuity for my dependents\" on the face of this form, sign all copies of the form and return it to the Bureau of Naval Personnel, Washington 25, D. C. You may subsequently elect to be covered by this Act, provided you submit such election to the Bureau of Naval Personnel, Washington 25, D. C., not later than 30 April 1954 or prior to completion of 18 years service creditable for basic pay purposes, whichever is later.\n\n3.    If you desire to receive reduced retired pay to provide an annuity for your dependents, fill out the form completely checking desired option(s); all copies must be signed and notarized or attested.\n\n4.    If either Option 2 or 3 is elected, it is required that all eligible children be named.\n\n5.    It should be noted that, under Option 3, all benefits are paid to the widow until her death or remarriage and thereafter in equal shares to or on behalf of the surviving children remaining eligible at the time the payment is due. Consequently, if it is desired that children of a former marriage receive payments concurrently with the widow, Options 1 and 2 should be elected.\n\n6.    In indicating the place of dissolution of a former marriage, please include the city, county and state.\n\n7.    The triplicate of this form is to be retained by you for your personal file. For active duty personnel, the original will be forwarded to the Bureau of Naval Personnel, Washington 25, D. C., and the duplicate is to be filed in your personnel jacket at your station of duty. For members in the reserve components, the original and duplicate will be forwarded to the Bureau of Naval Personnel, Washington 25, D. C.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2881719974c0b3be2850ef0f109e055657988f1b94638e3b7ed61013decdfde6", "output_sha256": "da55503dfa103b806269d7d9a875b235659f78d7e95e7f2178bf729c2ae971de", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:31.934555+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p442", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 442, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Navy offs. RD 3[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nVETERANS ADMINISTRATION\nREQUEST FOR INFORMATION\n\n1. TYPE OF CLAIM\nOriginal\n[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n2. SEPARATION FORMS ON FILE     3. DATA REQUESTED\n☐ YES   ☒ NO          ☒ SERVICE   ☒ MEDICAL   ☐ DENTAL   ☐ OTHER\n\n4. TO\n☐ ARMY   ☒ NAVY   ☐ AIR FORCE   ☐ MARINE CORPS   ☐ COAST GUARD   ☐ NATIONAL GUARD (Army)   ☐ NATIONAL GUARD (Air)   ☐ OTHER (Specify)\n\n5A. NAME AND ADDRESS OF VA REQUESTING OFFICE          5B. ORIGINATING UNIT          6. CLAIM NO.\nFROM   VARO                                            3044/211                    C-22312461\n        1380 S. Sepulveda Blvd\n        Los Angeles, Calif   90073                                               7. INSURANCE NO.\n\n8. LAST NAME - FIRST NAME - MIDDLE INITIAL (Under which served)     9. ALL SERVICE NOS.\nNEWHOUSE, DELBERT CLEMENT                                           #% 393 07 21   #11/283\n\n10. DATE OF BIRTH          11. PLACE OF BIRTH          12. DATE OF DEATH\n6/5/13                     Marcola, Oregon\n\n13. DATE ENTERED      14. DATE SEPARATED      15. CHARACTER OF           16. LAST GRADE, RATE OR\n    ACTIVE DUTY           FROM ACTIVE DUTY        SEPARATION OR DISCHARGE    RANK, AND ORGANIZATION\nA.  1/2/33            3/21/60                  Unk                         Lt\nB.\nC.\n\n17. ALLEGED DISEASE     18. DATES OF        19. PLACES OF          20. ORGANIZATION AT\n    OR INJURY               TREATMENT           TREATMENT              TIME DISEASE OR INJURY\n                                                                       WAS INCURRED\nA.  Arthritis           1957               Navy Hosp N.[ILLEGIBLE]  [ILLEGIBLE]\nB.  Arthritis           1960 - 1964        Navy Hosp San Diego Calif\nC.\n\n21. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION REQUESTED\n        Please furnish all active duty dates\n    and type of discharge and nature of injuries for\n    Complete separation at any time prior to 3-21-60?\n\n22. DATE                23. SIGNATURE AND TITLE OF VA OFFICIAL\n  4 21 64               F. B. WILLIAMS, Adm [ILLEGIBLE] Officer                    [ILLEGIBLE]481\n                                                                                    RR:gn\nENDORSEMENT - VERIFICATION BY SERVICE DEPARTMENT (Check applicable box(es))\n☐ AVAILABLE REQUESTED     ☐ ITEMS 8 & 9, AND 12 THROUGH 15     ☒ ITEMS 8 & 9, AND 12 THROUGH 15\n  RECORDS FORWARDED           VERIFIED CORRECT                     VERIFIED CORRECT, EXCEPT:\n\nVia:  BUMED                                              Pers E24-RAD-cjb\n8.  Officer No. 177283\n13A.  1-24-33    15C. Hon\nB.  1-24-39      D.  Hon\nC.  8-1-42       16.  CWO, W-4\n14A. 1-25-33\nB.  8-31-42           Subject officer was eligible