dith May Richter               P.O. Box 127           Mother\n                                                                  Garibaldi, Oregon\n                                                                  304 Labor Temple\n                                  Darrel Edwin Newhouse           Tacoma 3, Washington   Brother\n\n                                  Noah Frank Newhouse             Tacoma, Washington     Father\n\n17. BENEFICIARY OR BENEFICIARIES\nFOR UNPAID PAY AND ALLOWANCES (P. L. 147, 84th Congress). PERCENT OF SHARES\nMUST TOTAL 100 PERCENT.  100%  %  Norma Isobel Newhouse           652 Burnham St.,       Wife\n                                                                  El Cajon, California\n                          %\n\n18. PERSON TO RECEIVE ALLOTMENT OF PAY IF MISSING OR      PERCENT OF\nUNABLE TO TRANSMIT FUNDS.  100%    Norma Isobel Newhouse           652 Burnham St.,       Wife\n                                                                  El Cajon, California\n\n19. INSURANCE POLICIES IN FORCE INCLUDING USGLI AND NSLI (Agencies to be notified in case of death in active service)\nFULL NAME AND ADDRESS OF COMPANY          ADDRESS OF OFFICE RECEIVING PAYMENT OR HOME OFFICE        POLICY NO.\n\nNational Service Life             Veterans' Administration,                               V774432\nInsurance\nGovernment Life Insurance         Munitions Building, Washington 25, D.C.                  K948857\n\n20. SERVICE ORGANIZATION AND ADDRESS OF DESIGNATOR                                         DATE SIGNED\nPacific Fleet Photo-Triangulation Group, at San Diego California        24 August 1959\n\n21. SIGNATURE OF WITNESS                  22. SIGNATURE OF DESIGNATOR\nC. F. REINHOLZ, LTJG, USNR               Delbert C. Newhouse\n\nDD FORM\n1 Dec 56  93-1    Previous Editions are obsolete.\n                  For Navy, Marine Corps, and Coast Guard use: Will be used in lieu of DD Form 93.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "313fa6f303703b4de9e3859894a15959a0502b9774eff290c7e8d43fbc7e59c0", "output_sha256": "68c39b79b583c1eb427759e46229bad63eeed599c1cc910d0554666f4cede0e6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:43.157902+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p444", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 444, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "INSTRUCTIONS\n\n(Items for which no instructions are printed below are self-explanatory)\n\nIF NECESSARY, CONTINUE ANY ITEM IN \"REMARKS\" BUT SPECIFY THE PARTICULAR ITEM BEING CONTINUED.\n\nAll items of this form MUST be completed and MAINTAINED CURRENT by all officers and enlisted personnel in accordance with the following: NAVY—BuPers Manual, Art. B2312; MARINE CORPS—Par. 4019, PRAM; U. S. COAST GUARD—Personnel Manual, Par. 13–B–14.\n\nIn the event you, the designator, should die, the persons or agencies named in items 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, and 19 will be notified unless item 15 shall indicate a person or persons NOT to be notified.\n\nShould you become critically or seriously ill, or incapacitated to the extent that you cannot notify them, the persons named in items 10, 11, 12, 13, and 14 will be notified unless item 15 shall indicate a person or persons NOT to be notified.\n\nPayment of any benefits and disposition of remains in case of death shall be in accordance with applicable law.\n\nItem 10.—Enter full name and address of wife or husband. For wife, use given names, for example, \"Marion Elizabeth Dawson.\" If the designator is single, divorced, or widowed, so state.\n\nItems 12 and 13.—The term \"Father\" and/or \"Mother\" shall be interpreted to include \"natural,\" \"step,\" \"adoptive\" and person who stood in \"loco parentis\" to the designator for a period of not less than 1 year at any time prior to designator's entry upon active service.\n\nItem 14.—In the event that there is no other adult next of kin other than those named in items 10, 12 and 14, you may name a friend here. However, if a friend is named, he or she must be so identified.\n\nItem 14a.—Enter under this item, the names of those persons who are in fact actually receiving more than 50 percent of their support from the designator. The information thus furnished shall be used in connection with other determinations of dependency under existing or future laws.\n\nItem 16.—Enter the name, address, and relationship of beneficiary (or beneficiaries) whom you desire to receive the 6 months' death gratuity in the event you are not survived by a spouse or eligible child(ren). The succession of eligible survivor's as set forth in the \"Servicemen's and Veterans' Survivor Benefits Act,\" P. L. 881–84th Congress, is as follows: (1) Spouse; (2) Children (without regard to their age or marital status) in equal shares; (3) Parents or brothers or sisters (including those of halfblood and those by adoption), when so designated; (4) Parents in equal shares; or (5) Brothers and sisters (including those of halfblood or those by adoption) in equal shares.\n\nNOTE:\nThe payment to either category (4) or (5) is in the event that a designation is not made under category (3).\nThe term \"parents\" includes \"natural parents,\" \"stepparents,\" \"adoptive parents\" and persons who stood in \"loco parentis\" to the designator for a period of not less than 1 year at any time prior to the designator's entry upon active service.\n\nItem 17.—Enter name and address of the beneficiary or beneficiaries whom you desire to receive any unpaid pay and allowances (Arrears of Pay) due you at the time of death. There are no restrictions on who may be designated as a beneficiary or beneficiaries to receive unpaid pay and allowances and once a designation has been made it is binding until superseded by the completion of a later DD Form 93–1.\n\nItem 18.—The \"Missing Persons Act\" provides that pay and allowances continue to accrue to the pay account of any service member for the period he is missing or captured and may be paid to the dependents for support. This item reflects your desires and is used as a guide in the disposition of your pay. Allotments to dependents and insurance companies initiated prior to entering a missing status are continued in effect unless unusual circumstances indicate changes.\n\nItem 21.—The person assigned, by the commanding officer, the responsibility for interviewing the designator will, upon completion of the form, witness the designator's signature and sign in block 21.\n\nDISPOSITION INSTRUCTIONS\n\nU. S. NAVY: Original to BuPers, Washington 25, D. C.\n          Duplicate—File in Service Record at duty station.\n               See BuPers Instruction 1085.25 of 27\n               May 1953.\nU. S. MARINE CORPS: See Par. 4019, PRAM.\nU. S. COAST GUARD: See Personnel Manual, Par. 13–B–14.\n\n\nEntry of other useful information in connection with emergency data such as location of will, safety deposit boxes, etc., if applicable, should be made under \"Remarks.\"\n\n\nREMARKS:\n\n\n\n\nU. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE: 1957 O·F—411267", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8efc59b0af2badce16b90c6857e889062daea99934565c46509369c7201422cf", "output_sha256": "b3a05f6bddae22f4b0b8b89759f364014149939225de1da362feecd6dbf0f386", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:49.101407+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p445", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 445, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "C-1\n\n                                          Blbc1\n                                          FT\n\n                    Pers-Blbc1js        Blbc\n                    177283/8311\n                                          B\n                    7 April 1959\n                                          B115\n                                          1&8R\n                                          all\n                                          Blba\n\n\nMy dear Senator Morse:\n                                                              B1\nThis is in further reply to your inquiry of 31 March 1959 concerning\nChief Warrant Officer Delbert C. Newhouse, United States Navy.\n                                                              Blbc\nPresent plans are to detach Mr. Newhouse from the USS ESSEX (CVA-9)    FT\nin July of this year and to transfer him to the Fleet Camera Party,\nPacific at San Diego, California.  Earlier detachment of Mr. Newhouse\nis not feasible due to the unavailability of a qualified replacement    1623\nofficer.\n\nYour interest in this matter is appreciated, and it is hoped that the\nforegoing information may be of service to you.\n\nBy direction of Chief of Naval Personnel:\n\n                              Sincerely yours,\n\n\n\n                              F. J. Brush\n                              Captain, USN\n                              Director,\n                              Officer Distribution Division\n\nHonorable Wayne Morse\nUnited States Senate          Encl: (1) Ltr. fm Mrs. D. C. Newhouse\nWashington 25, D. C.                      dtd 17 March 1959.\n\n                              Originated by:  LCDR F. C. Turner, USN\nCopy to:                                      Pers Blbc1, x42075\nPers Blbc\nPers B115\nNaval Liaison Office\nJacket                        Finished File Pers Blbc", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "84eca06f52fd4375c57da01f4bdea1b2326866bee33a145b9c9830e1defaa046", "output_sha256": "132aa4596dcf1809bb6b787094fef44cdce8fca4d817ce654ad850eb872cc2dc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:51.017748+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p446", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 446, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVAL LIAISON OFFICE TO THE CONGRESS\nROOM 313B OLD HOUSE OFFICE BLDG.\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                                    B14c\n\n                        2 April 1959\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:  Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nATTENTION:\n\nSUBJECT:      NEWHOUSE, Delbert C., CWO, USN; request for duty on\n              the West Coast for last year in service\n              (NOTE DATE OF SHIPS CRUISE)\n\n1.  The attached correspondence has been referred to this office by\n\nSenator Wayne Morse of Oregon.\n\n2.  It is requested that your office reply in duplicate direct to the\n\nSenator, and return to him all enclosures except his letter, if any.\n\nPlease furnish this office with a copy of your reply.\n\n3.  The Senator has been advised of this referral to the NAVY\n\nDEPARTMENT.\n\n                                        Respectfully yours,\n\n\n                                        E. J. NEWBOULD\n                                        Commander, USN\n\nEncl: 1.  Trans chit dtd 31 Mar 59\n\n      2.  Ltr fm Mrs. Delbert C. Newhouse dtd 17 Mar 59\n\n      3.\n\nmlk\n                        3434\n                                APR 2  59\n                              BUREAU OF NAVAL\n                              PERSONNEL          E-29424", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "aca57501de3aa8296898b94b2089e174c7a9e718b1a67dc8f222bbd879a2a0a6", "output_sha256": "ded33a102845506ad29995cd8ded90c960c0bac7b2cae53aa892391491d518e3", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:52.608543+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p447", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 447, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "United States Senate\n\nMarch 31, 1959\n\n\n\nRespectfully referred to\n\nCommander E. J. Newbould\nNavy Liaison Office\n\nwith thanks for such favorable consideration as\n\nthe communication herewith submitted warrants,\n\nand for a report thereon, in duplicate to\n\naccompany return of inclosure.\n\n                    By direction of\n\n                    Wayne Morse\n\n                                        U.S.S.\n\nEncl. re CWO D. C. Newhouse - who would\nlike to be stationed on West Coast for last\nyear of duty. Newhouse's ship scheduled to\nleave April 15, so early consideration would\nbe appreciated.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f6fb67443c32f4062b9ea0e0d48047f02893ad904955528df467451ef913fe1b", "output_sha256": "d1fb842e5a152315c976460deb3ecd8a18c18ba47fe12a8efc44931678e99e12", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:53.592710+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p448", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 448, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "SHIP OR STATION\n                        U.S.S. ESSEX (CVA-9)\n\n                    Imperium Neptuni Regis\n\nGibraltar                                        Suez Canal\n12 Feb., 1958                                    28 Aug., 1958\n\n                    19 November, 1958\n\n        The U.S.S. ESSEX (CVA-9) bound\n    South on a return voyage from Formosa\n    to Mayport, Florida, via the Cape of\n    Good Hope and southern latitudes; there-\n    fore, be it remembered that said vessel,\n    and officers, and crew, have been inspec-\n    ted and passed on by his Imperial Majesty,\n    Neptunus Rex and his Royal Staff and each\n    found worthy to be membered as a trusty\n    Shellback and having been duly initiated\n        into the Ancient Order of the Deep.\n\n                                                        To Formosa\n\n            Also be it known that said\n        man participated in operat-\n        ions off the coast of\n        Lebanon from 15 July to\n        21 August, 1958 while          Qualified Shellback\n        providing air coverage          15 Oct., 1958\n        for United States\n        troops landed to\n        maintain order by\n        request of the\n        Lebanese Government.\n\nE.C. Monaghan\nE.C. MONAGHAN\nCHSHIPCLK, USN\nOfficer Personnel Officer\n\n                Rio De Janeiro\n\n                                                    From Formosa\n\n                        Cape of Good Hope\n                         25 Oct., 1958\n\nNAME (Last, first, middle)                    RATE      SERVICE NO.      BRANCH AND CLASS\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert C.                          CWO       177283           USN", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "82d2ee97e2575a76c9f9938d1ba47961fb2833476471fdcc98abacd94677c2ce", "output_sha256": "82d2ee97e2575a76c9f9938d1ba47961fb2833476471fdcc98abacd94677c2ce", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:55.443213+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p449", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 449, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Pers-E24-TLB:ems\n177283/8311\n25 Nov 1957\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    CHPHOT Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\n\nVia:   Commanding Officer\n       Naval Air Technical Training Unit\n       U. S. Naval Air Station\n       Pensacola, Florida\n\n\nSubj:  Home of Record; change of\n\nRef:   (a) Your ltr of 12 Nov 1957 with CO'S end NC/Pncla/(mag) Pl of\n           14 Nov 1957\n\n1.  As requested by reference (a), the records of this Bureau have been\nchanged to show your home of record to be Garibaldi, Oregon, effective\nthis date.\n\n\n\n\n                         V. E. ARMSTRONG\n                         By direction", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e284417e5a801012bd8113cd1b57436564c1993509c4e5df69e7b227adabc702", "output_sha256": "e284417e5a801012bd8113cd1b57436564c1993509c4e5df69e7b227adabc702", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:47:56.563884+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p450", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 450, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "177283/8311\n12 November 1957\n\nFrom:  CWO, W-4, Delbert Clement NEWHOUSE, USN  REC'D PERS E241\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\nVia:   Commanding Officer, Naval Air Technical Training Unit, Naval Air\n       Station, Pensacola, Florida          NOV 1957\n\nSubj:  Change of home of record; notification of\n\nRef:   (a) Article B-2206, BuPers Manual\n\n1.  This change of address is submitted as authorized in paragraph (2)\nof reference (a).\n\n2.  My home of record is changed as follows:\n\n             From:  208 Bryant Road, Navy Point\n                    Pensacola, Florida\n\n             To:    c/o Mrs. Vinel Richter\n                    Garibaldi, Oregon\n\n3.  It is requested that the records of the Bureau be changed accordingly.\n\n                    Delbert Clement Newhouse\n                    DELBERT CLEMENT NEWHOUSE\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n                                                     NC/Pncla/(mag)\n                                                     P1\n\n                                          14 NOV 1957\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, Naval Air Technical Training Unit, Naval Air\n       Station, Pensacola, Florida\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n1.  Forwarded.\n\n                    J. B. Doster\n                    J. B. DOSTER\n                    By direction\n\n\n                                          Finished File Pers-E241\n                                          [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffd