            for execution.\n\n\n                              DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\nDEPARTED: NAV STA/AIR, N.A.S. PENSACOLA, FLA.\n\nTIME                          DATE\n\n          OFFICER - OF - THE - DAY\n\n\n\n\n\n                    Finished File--Pers B1164", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "838d54134519dc7af6e1881e75540f437d7b3154e3ba70a5550a7f4657744ed1", "output_sha256": "80d7006a39fe164b4526fdb4d63a167902ede9a2867376086d9e57ec3672a3be", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:48:28.444250+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p461", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 461, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVAL AIR TECHNICAL TRAINING UNIT\nU. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\nPENSACOLA, FLORIDA\n\n                                                NC/Pensacola/(mag)\n                                                P16-4/00\n                                                177283/8311\n                                                13 November 1957\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer\nTo:    CWO, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nSubj:  Change of duty\n\nRef:   (a) BuPers msg #050915Z of Nov 1957\n\n1.  Reference (a) is quoted and transcribed herewith for your information and\ncompliance:\n\n     \"CHPHOTO W4 DELBERT C NEWHOUSE 177283/8311 DIRDET IN DEC PROPORICH\n     USS ESSEX CVA 9 ARREPCOVES X DELREP 10 JAN 1958 X VERCATEBURRS X TRAVCHAR\n     1781453.18 MPN 1958 OC 029 EXACTT 74120 BUCONTROL 22/31600\"\n\nTranscribed:  When directed by your Commanding Officer in December 1957, you\nwill regard yourself detached from duty with the Naval Air Technical Training\nUnit, Naval Air Station, Pensacola, Florida, and from such other duty as may be\nassigned you; will proceed to the port in which the USS ESSEX (CVA-9) may be\nand upon arrival report to the Commanding Officer of that vessel for duty.\n\nYou are authorized to delay until 10 January 1958, provided no excess leave is\ninvolved, in reporting in compliance with these orders, such delay to count as\nleave.  Keep your old and new station advised of your address using Form NavPers\n3036.  Since reimbursement for travel is based on travel required due to location of vessel or fleet command indicated above on the date of expiration of\ndelay, it is important to verify the location on that date.\n\nTravel is chargeable to appropriation 1781453.18, MPN 1958, object class 029,\nExpenditure Account 74120, Bureau Control 22/31600.\n\n2.  You are authorized to draw up to three months advance pay in the execution\nof these orders.\n\n3.  Delivered.\n\n\n                                   J. B. DOSTER\n                                   By direction", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2982d4b113afa8df18dc4f176a26363b793ae3786cf4544cf628a406734d14b4", "output_sha256": "db6600018cfbe3941e7265d729d3cba161a7cbe37240e78ab4dfefc446f2911e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:48:30.897210+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p462", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 462, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVAL COMMUNICATION SYSTEM                    PLACEMENT REVIEWED BY:\n\nDRAFTED BY                    FILE NR.                EXT. NR.\nPER3-Bb1129-AW-1              177283/8311             43296\nRELEASED BY                   CODE/SECT. NR.          DATE                    Bb1129\nCAPT G F SMALE                                        4 NOV 1957 1040\n\n                    Please leave this space clear\n\n\n\n\nFROM:    BUPERS                        05 09157               PRECEDENCE\n                                  (date/time group) (GCT)\nTO:      ENDENXXXN NATECHTU NAS PNCLA                         □ PRIORITY\n\n                                                             