x (CVA-9), with\nrank of CW 0-4/8311 during the\nLebanon operation.\n\n                        Delbert C. Devhouse\n\n                        652 Burnham St.\n                        El Cajon, Calif. 92021\n\n\n\n\nFinished File Pers E248 rdt", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cc792dd1f4841382ac265d367df61c0cad5d827ceb94f29db2a21fe1b72bab12", "output_sha256": "cc792dd1f4841382ac265d367df61c0cad5d827ceb94f29db2a21fe1b72bab12", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:02.659881+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p469", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 469, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "S-2\n\n                                    CVS9/JFH:jh\n                                    Code 11\n                                    Ser:\n                                         527\n                                    MAR 1 0 1961\n\nSECOND ENDORSEMENT on COMNAVAIRLANT ltr CNAL 334 of 2 Sep 1960\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVS-9)\nTo:    CWO-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\nSubj:  Commander Naval Air Force, U. S. Atlantic Fleet Ship\n       Department Excellence Insignia\n\n1.  Delivered. A copy of the basic letter and endorsements thereto\nwill be made a part of your official record.\n\n\n                              S. S. SEARCY, Jr.\n\nCopy to:\nBUPERS (With Basic Ltr and 1st End)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cb0c3be2b8b20d473441a5e35f1a3ae0c3bbc1a3587467cd6445d6f2421a0ca7", "output_sha256": "e8fa650a6f95f0243f4bf126a1cce34e858043c50df8e6b99a88f1d57dbd0a40", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:03.881803+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p470", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 470, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "FB2-18/002/rr\n5060\nSerial: 368\n11 September 1960\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT on COMNAVAIRLANT ltr CNAL 334 of\n2 SEP 1960\n\nFrom:   Commander Carrier Division EIGHTEEN\nTo:     Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVS-9)\n\nSubj:   Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet Ship\n        Department Excellence Insignia; award of\n\n1.  Forwarded with congratulations.\n\n2.  Commander Carrier Division EIGHTEEN takes pleasure in\ncommending the Commanding Officer and personnel of the Operations\nDepartment for the outstanding performance of duties which earned\nthis coveted award.\n\n\n                        F. L. ASHWORTH\n\n\n2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cc4dcd5e4450c8edfb14d134c45205c3cc59d360265e886b3b65c2d7c284b42f", "output_sha256": "cc4dcd5e4450c8edfb14d134c45205c3cc59d360265e886b3b65c2d7c284b42f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:04.923069+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p471", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 471, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "HEADQUARTERS\nCOMMANDER NAVAL AIR FORCE, U. S. ATLANTIC FLEET\nU. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\nNORFOLK 11, VIRGINIA          CNAL-334\n\n                                        2 SEP 1960\n\n\nFrom:  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet\nTo:    Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVS-9)\nVia:   Commander Carrier Division EIGHTEEN\n\nSubj:  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet Ship Department\n       Excellence Insignia; award of\n\nRef:   (a) OPNAVINST 3590.4A, Subj: Awards for intratype battle efficiency\n           competition and insignia to denote excellence in certain\n           weapons and operations\n\n1.  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet takes pleasure in\ncertifying the Operations Department of the USS ESSEX (CVS-9) as standing\nfirst in the CVA class ship during fiscal year 1960.\n\n2.  The Commanding Officer is congratulated on the exemplary performance\nof the ESSEX's Operations Department.\n\n3.  The ESSEX is authorized to display the Operations Department Excellence\nInsignia in accordance with reference (a).\n\n4.  Suitable entries will be made in the personnel records of the officers\nand men of the ESSEX who materially contributed to the earning of this\naward.  The Commanding Officer is requested to forward a copy of this\nletter to the command of those personnel formerly serving on board during\nfiscal year 1960, who significantly contributed to the winning of this\naward.\n\n\n                         W. L. REES", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "767063dcd9364af9c2b85594dc5f18f197f3e66e9940a9c3bc896a1956d97b55", "output_sha256": "767063dcd9364af9c2b85594dc5f18f197f3e66e9940a9c3bc896a1956d97b55", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:06.585544+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p472", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 472, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "HEADQUARTERS\nCOMMANDER NAVAL AIR FORCE, U. S. ATLANTIC FLEET\nU. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\nNORFOLK 11, VIRGINIA          CNAL-334\n\n                              2 SEP 1960\n\n\nFrom:  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet\nTo:    Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVS-9)\nVia:   Commander Carrier Division EIGHTEEN\n\nSubj:  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet Ship Department\n       Excellence Insignia; award of\n\nRef:   (a) OPNAVINST 3590.4A, Subj: Awards for intratype battle efficiency\n           competition and insignia to denote excellence in certain\n           weapons and operations\n\n1.  Commander Naval Air Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet takes pleasure in\ncertifying the Operations Department of the USS ESSEX (CVS-9) as standing\nfirst in the CVA class ship during fiscal year 1960.\n\n2.  The Commanding Officer is congratulated on the exemplary performance\nof the ESSEX's Operations Department.\n\n3.  The ESSEX is authorized to display the Operations Department Excellence\nInsignia in accordance with reference (a).\n\n4.  Suitable entries will be made in the personnel records of the officers\nand men of the ESSEX who materially contributed to the earning of this\naward.  The Commanding Officer is requested to forward a copy of this\nletter to the command of those personnel formerly serving on board during\nfiscal year 1960, who significantly contributed to the winning of this\naward.\n\n\n                         [signature]\n\n                         W. L. REES", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2354d276d39af569a771f36c038594e32f4d4e14ffb79ec3a273c721f35436e0", "output_sha256": "2354d276d39af569a771f36c038594e32f4d4e14ffb79ec3a273c721f35436e0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:08.336591+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p473", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 473, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "U.S.S. ESSEX (CVA-9)\nFLEET POST OFFICE\nNEW YORK, NEW YORK\n\n                                                    IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                                    CVA9/1650/CSW/meh\n                                                    Code 01\n                                                    10 March 1959\n\n\n\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVA-9)\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\nSubj:  CWO4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, 177283/8311\n       correspondence in the case of\n\nEncl:  (1) Copy of CO ESSEX ltr CVA9/CSW/deb Code 01 of 13 Nov 1958\n\n1. Enclosure (1) is forwarded herewith for inclusion in the record of\nsubject officer as indicated in paragraph 5 thereof.\n\n                              T. W. SOUTH II\n\n                              C. S. WALLINE\n                              By direction", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "95ca58071ec7c1478308e7aa5a0f9013f08fbb5b7ae3c5e708eef5260f17ac1b", "output_sha256": "c6ab999341f7e5bc5900236660bdc5d7e17f1fbed578c490e590b673b0eb2b99", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:09.591748+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p474", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 474, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "USS ESSEX (CVA9)          CVA9:CSW:deb\n     Fleet Post Office          Code 01\n     New York, New York\n\n                                    13 NOV 1958\n\n\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer, USS ESSEX (CVA9)\nTo:    All Hands, USS ESSEX (CVA9)\n       Commander, Air Task Group 201\n\nSubj:  Commendation for Operations performed during\n       Mediterranean and WesPac Deployment\n\n1.  The Commanding Officer is in receipt of many complimentary\ncommunications concerning the outstanding performance of ESSEX\nand Air Task Group 201 during the period 2 February to\n17 November 1958.\n\n2.  During this period ESSEX and her embarked Air Group served\nas a striking unit of the Sixth Fleet in Mediterranean waters,\nand her aircraft provided initial and sustained air support\nfor U. S. Marine landings in Lebanon from 15 July to August\n1958.  These operations, under wartime conditions, were per-\nformed by the men of ESSEX and ATG 201 with an outstanding\ndegree of professional skill and devotion to duty.\n\n3.  Following this, ESSEX was deployed on an emergency basis\nto the Far East, where air operations in support of U. S.\nNational policy during the Formosa crisis were conducted in\nthe same outstanding manner.\n\n4.  Indicative of the performance of ESSEX and her Air Group\nare the following excerpts from various communications\nreceived:\n\n     a.  In a letter of March 28, 1958, RADM N. S. HENDERSON,\nO.B.E., RN, Vice Naval Deputy, Supreme Headquarters, Allied\nPowers Europe who was on board observing operations, stated....\n\"But above all I took away an impression of a quietly effi-\ncient ship with a very lively crew, all of whom seemed keen\nand interested in the job.  I was deeply impressed....\"\n\n     b.  From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"AM DELIGHTED WITH A\nRECENT LETTER RECEIVED FROM COMMANDING OFFICER TENCH REPORT-\nING THE OUTSTANDING TREATMENT ACCORDED TENCH AND SEA ROBIN\nBY YOU WHILE IN COMPANY DURING YOUR RECENT VISIT TO PALMA X\nIT IS TRULY HEART WARMING TO LEARN OF THE WHOLEHEARTED\nCOOPERATION AND MUTUAL SUPPORT BETWEEN UNITS OF THE SIXTH FLT X", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "57d8339a0cf299c9276ad111383b814db0ee966d36b50ff015cb7c3c29725f8a", "output_sha256": "0341c00366195a1391dd4c28a9716d64d2f8ad5483be426a06589402115e97a2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:11.964245+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p475", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 475, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CVA9:CSW:deb\n        Code 01\n\nALSO MENTIONED WAS THE PUNCTILIOUS MANNER IN WHICH HONORS WERE\nRENDERED ON THE OCCASION OF AN INFORMAL VISIT BY COMMANDING\nOFFICERS OF TENCH AND SEA ROBIN X WELL DONE X SIGNED VADM\nBROWN\"\n\n     c. From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"I LIKE THE WAY YOU\nAPPRECIATED THE SITUATION CMM GOT GOING EARLY AND REACHED\nOUT TO DO A SUPERIOR JOB YESTERDAY X THERE CERTAINLY ISN'T\nANY FIRST AND SECOND TEAM IN MY CARRIERS X WELL DONE TO YOU\nAND ALL YOUR BOYS X SIGNED BROWN\"\n\n     d. From Commander Task Force Sixty....\"IT WAS A GRAND\nPERFORMANCE ON SUCH SHORT NOTICE X BOX SEATS IN YANKEE\nSTADIUM FOR SATURDAYS DOUBLE HEADER TO ALL CONCERNED X\nRADM ANDERSON\"\n\n     e. From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"CONGRATULATIONS ON\nWHAT I HAVE COME TO EXPECT AS A ROUTINE BUT HIGHLY POLISHED\nPRECISION PERFORMANCE ON THE PART OF THE WORLDS GREATEST\nFLYERS X SIGNED BROWN\"\n\n     f. From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"THIS MESSAGE FOR ALL\nHANDS X PROBABLY NO GROUP OF PEOPLE IN THE WORLD TODAY IS\nMORE CALM THAT THE MEN WHO SAIL AND FIGHT THE SHIPS OF THE\nSIXTH FLT X THIS IS AS IT SHOULD BE X WITH A MINIMUM OF NOISE\nAND LOST MOTION THE FLEET HAS AGAIN SWUNG INTO ACTION WITH\nQUIET DECISIVENESS X LESS THAN SEVENTY TWO HOURS AGO, ON\n15 JULY, THE SCATTERED 75 SHIPS OF THE FLEET WERE ENJOYING\nLIBERTY IN PORTS SEPARATED BY AS MUCH AS 1900 MILES X THIS\nMORNING, 18 JULY, MORE THAN 5000 COMBAT READY MARINES ARE IN\nLEBANON, OUR AIR HAS BEEN PARADED OVER JORDAN AND THE WHOLE\nOF THE FLEET IS IN THE BEST POSITION TO SUPPORT OUR MARINES\nOR TO CARRY OUT ANY OTHER ASSIGNED TASK X YOU WILL RECALL\nTHAT WITHIN A VERY FEW HOURS OF WORD FROM THE PRESIDENT, OUR\nCOMMANDER IN CHIEF, THE FIRST BATTALION OF MARINES WAS LANDED\nUNDER COVER OF NAVAL GUNS AND CARRIER BASED AIRCRAFT X THESE\nFACTS BEAR WITNESS TO OUR READINESS, OUR PLANNING AND OUR\nTRAINING X THEY TESTIFY TO OUR FLEXIBILITY AND MOBILITY AS A\nFIGHTING FORCE X NONE OF THESE ARE THINGS FOR WHICH WE CAN\nCONGRATULATE OURSELVES FOR THEY ARE THE THINGS WHICH EVERYONE HAS A RIGHT TO EXPECT OF US DASH OUR HALLMARK AND OUR\nREASON FOR BEING X HOWEVER, I BELIEVE WE CAN AND SHOULD CONGRATULATE OURSELVES ON THE FACT THAT A WORLD WHERE SO MANY\nHAVE TO SERVE BY STANDING AND WAITING, THE PRIVILEGE HAS\nFALLEN TO US TO BE OF REAL USE IN A TIME OF REAL NEED X\nSIGNED BROWN\"", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "999d0e16446fc16a7eab1922f9aad797bf89c81c65dffc815bc818215f12cd35", "output_sha256": "5694177864f24a8b99ea001e2e79a50dfd97048ae2221912dc3e570d5a19b3b7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:15.483125+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p476", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 476, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CVA9:CSW:deb\n                                        Code 01\n\n        g.  From Commander Task Force Sixty....\"ON THIS SEVENTH\nDAY OF ROUND THE CLOCK OPERATIONS I NOTE HOW SUPERBLY YOU\nHAVE MET YOUR SCHEDULE X NINETY EIGHT POINT TWO PER CENT\nIS SOMETHING TO BE PROUD OF X JOE D MAGGIO GOT ONE HUNDRED\nTHOUSAND FOR BATTING THREE FIFTY\"\n\n        h.  From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"I AND MEMBERS OF MY\nSTAFF HAVE HAD AN OPPORTUNITY THE LAST FEW DAYS TO OBSERVE\nYOUR OPERATIONS CLOSE AT HAND, WHICH WE HAVE WANTED TO DO\nFOR SOME TIME X WE WERE IMPRESSED BOTH WITH THE QUALITY OF\nYOUR AIR OPERATIONS AND THE SPIRIT OF THE CREW X I HAVE NEVER\nRECEIVED ANYTHING BUT \"CAN DO\" FROM ESSEX AND I NOW KNOW\nWHY X YOUR PERFORMANCE DURING THE LEBANON OPERATIONS HAS\nADDED LUSTRE TO THE ALREADY FAMOUS RECORD OF A FAMOUS SHIP X\nA TIP OF THE BROWN HAT TO ONE AND ALL X SIGNED VADM C R\nBROWN\"\n\n        i.  From Commanding Officer USS BOSTON (CAG-1)....\"YOUR\nFLYING TAXIES HAVE BEEN TERRIFIC X THE SERVICES YOU HAVE\nGIVEN US AT THE DROP OF A HAT IS VERY SINCERELY APPRECIATED X\nHEINZ X\"\n\n        j.  From Commander Sixth Fleet....\"PERSONAL TO THE CAPTAIN\nAND ALL HANDS X I TOO WISH YOU WERE LEAVING THE MED THROUGH\nTHE STRAITS OF GIBRALTAR X NO ONE KNOWS BETTER THAN I DO THAT\nYOU HAVE WORKED HARD AND WELL AND DESERVE TO GO HOME FOR A\nREST X BUT THERES A JOB TO BE DONE AND I HOPE SOME DAY YOU\nWILL LOOK BACK AND FEEL LUCKY AND PROUD THAT YOU WERE AMONG\nTHE VERY FEW PEOPLE IN THE WORLD WHO AT A CRITICAL TIME REALLY\nDID DO SOMETHING TO HELP KEEP PEACE IN THE WORLD X AND IF YOU\nHAVE TO THROW A PUNCH, I KNOW YOU CAN DO IT WITH THE BEST OF\nTHEM X THERE ISN'T ANY ONE ON THE SIXTHFLT TEAM THAT I WOULD\nRATHER HAVE REPRESENT US OUTSIDE THE MED X YOU HAVE BEEN A\nSHARP CAN DO SHIP FROM THE START X GOOD LUCK AND GOD BLESS\nYOU X SIGNED BROWN\"\n\n        k.  From Commander in Chief, U. S. Atlantic Fleet to\nESSEX and others....\"COMMANDER IN CHIEF U.S. ATLANTIC FLEET\nREGRETS THE NECESSITY OF YOUR TEMPORARY DEPARTURE FROM THE\nATLANTIC FLEET BUT APPRECIATES YOUR READINESS AND ABILITY TO\nHANDLE ANY SITUATION WORLD WIDE X WE WILL WELCOME YOU BACK\nWHEN THE SITUATION CLARIFIES X SIGNED ADM JERAULD WRIGHT\"\n\n        l.  From American Legation U. S. Naval Attache, Cairo,\nEgypt....\"SUEZ TRANSIT ESSEX AND UNITS COMDESRON 10 ON\n28 AUGUST CHARACTERIZED BY SMARTNESS AND EFFICIENCY X\nEGYPTIAN NATIONALS AND MEMBERS DIPLOMATIC CORP WHO OBSERVED\nESSEX GREATLY IMPRESSED X LARGE NUMBER AIRCRAFT ABOARD\n\n                                3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "491bbc19ab563b34536f6c1029447cb4e8ef8d31b174a383a929e528274abde0", "output_sha256": "0d5eb3eed94856149589ffd0cb94700422617b5896325e40f06072351e9ffc2c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:18.868462+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p477", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 477, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CVA9:CSW:deb\n                                                      Code 01\n\nCAUSED MUCH COMMENT X MUSIC BY SHIPS BAND AND PLAYING OF\n'I'LL SEE YOU IN MY DREAMS' ON DEPARTURE SUEZ WAS 'MASBOUT'\nWHICH IN ARABIC MEANS JUST RIGHT\"\n\n     m. From Chief of Naval Operations to ESSEX and others\n....\"THE EXPEDITIOUS AND EFFICIENT MANNER IN WHICH ALL ARRANGEMENTS WERE COMPLETED ON 28 AUG, TOGETHER WITH THE SMART\nSEAMANLIKE TRANSIT OF SUEZ CANAL BY ESSEX AND DESTROYERS\nUNDER COMDESRON 10 IS DESERVING OF HIGHEST CREDIT TO ALL CONCERNED X WELL DONE X ARLEIGH BURKE\"\n\n     n. From Commanding Officer, USS CHARA (AKA58)....\"MSG\nCAPT X IT HAS BEEN A REAL PLEASURE TO WORK WITH SUCH A SMART\nSHIP X JOHN\"\n\n     o. From Commander Naval Base, Subic Bay, Philippines....\n\"IT WAS A PLEASURE TO HAVE YOU VISIT US HERE AT SUBIC X THE\nCONDUCT, COOPERATION, AND APPEARANCE OF YOUR SHIPS COMPANIES\nWERE MOST OUTSTANDING X COME SOON AGAIN X RADM KEITH SENDS\"\n\n     p. From Commander Carrier Division Six to Commander Naval\nAir Force, U.S. Atlantic Fleet....\"MANY THANKS FOR YOUR WELCOME X IT IS MY PRIVILEGE TO HAVE BROUGHT HOME A SEASONED\nSHIP AND A SPLENDID AIR GROUP WHICH NAVAIRLANT CAN BE PROUD X\nI REGRET ESSEX IS NOT WITH US BUT REPORTS FROM MY FRIENDS OUT\nWEST SAY SHE IS WORTH ANY TWO PACFLT CARRIERS PUT TOGETHER X\nRADM ANDERSON\"\n\n     q. From Commander Task Group Seventy Seven point Four\n....\"IT HAS BEEN A PLEASURE TO HAVE HAD YOU WITH US X I HAVE\nBEEN VERY IMPRESSED WITH YOUR GET UP AND GO ATTITUDE THIS\nAPPLIES PARTICULARLY TO THE AIR GROUP X FINEST OPERATION I\nHAVE SEEN IN A LONG TIME X GOOD LUCK AND A PLEASANT TRIP HOME X\nRADM SOUTHERLAND\"\n\n     r. From U.S. Navy Liaison Officer, Singapore....\"YOUR\nBRIEF VISIT TO SINGAPORE CONSIDERED OUTSTANDING IN ALL RESPECTS X FINE APPEARANCE OF SHIPS AND MEN CMM EXEMPLARY CONDUCT ASHORE CMM ENTHUSIASTIC COOPERATION WITH ALL ORGANIZATIONS CMM ESPECIALLY AS REGARDS VISITING YOU PROVIDED TO\nCROSS SECTION OF LOCAL COMMUNITY CMM WAS NOTED THROUGHOUT\nAMERICAN CONSULATE AND BRITISH AND LOCAL COMMUNITY X AMERICAN\nCONSUL GENERAL CONCURS YOUR VISIT ENHANCED ESTEEM AND PRESTIGE\nOF OUR NAVY AND COUNTRY IN SINGAPORE AND JOINS ORIGINATOR IN\nBEST WISHES FOR PLEASANT CRUISE AND HAPPY HOME COMING\"\n\n\n\n                    4", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "053247c040c0640929eb999d0e1e44d564d6096cd76b72788d8fecafcfc66bc4", "output_sha256": "2af8fe43f5fdeba7e31ee34491dc2e2b03111d6314e10ceac1e2873001de33b5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:22.214680+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p478", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 478, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "CVA9:CSW:deb\nCode 01\n\n     s.  From Senior Officer Royal Ceylon Navy....\"IT WAS A\nPLEASURE TO HAVE HAD YOUR SHIPS HERE X GOODBYE AND GOOD\nLUCK TO ALL\"\n\n     t.  From American Legation, U. S. Naval Attache,\nColombo, Ceylon....\"CONGRATULATIONS ON THE EXCELLENT IM-\nPRESSION AND OUTSTANDING CONDUCT OF YOUR MEN AND OFFICERS\nWHILE IN COLOMBO X WE CONSIDER OURSELVES FORTUNATE IN HAV-\nING SHIPS OF YOUR HIGH CALIBER VISIT US X GOOD LUCK AND\nGOD SPEED ON YOUR PRESENT VOYAGE.\"\n\n     u.  From Commander in Chief, U. S. Atlantic Fleet....\n\"ON YOUR RETURN TO LANTFLT QUOTE A WELL DONE UNQUOTE FOR\nYOUR CLEAR DEMONSTRATION OF READINESS AND MOBILITY X BEST\nWISHES FOR A SPEEDY HOMEWARD VOYAGE AND A LONG AWAITED\nREUNION WITH YOUR FAMILIES\"\n\n5.  I commend ALL HANDS in ESSEX and CATG 201 for their\noutstanding performance during this period, and have direct-\ned that a copy of this document be inserted in the official\nrecords of the personnel concerned.\n\n                    T. A. CHRISTOPHER\n\n\n\n\n                         5", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "17f74e8ffbd1e48778796af8eb1e871bcbb84ca285d4e860831ff13326c793f3", "output_sha256": "299251bccea37d6f20dbfe45b6c7b894fed0d523bef74b29f6409478a6f4b399", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:23.767433+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p479", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 479, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "S-2\n\n                    USS ESSEX (CVA-9)\n                    Fleet Post Office\n                    New York, New York          CVA9/P15\n                                                11:ECM:jc\n\n                                                2 JUN 1958\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer\nTo:    CHPHOT, W-4, Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\n\nSubj:  National Defense Service Medal and Korean Service Medal\n\n1.  Delivered.\n\n\n                                    E. C. MONAGHAN\n                                    By direction\n\nCopy to:\nBUPERS", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a643eb22172d90a5200fa09cc2806ccf08a6e3d1e534ac865b4c1131697bdd74", "output_sha256": "a643eb22172d90a5200fa09cc2806ccf08a6e3d1e534ac865b4c1131697bdd74", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:24.794222+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p480", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 480, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\n                    BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL\n                         WASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n                                                          IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                                     Pers E24-IH:mjs\n                                                     177283/8311\n                                                     10 Dec 1956\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Personnel\nTo:    CHPHOT W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN\n\nVia:   Commanding Officer\n       Naval Air Technical Training Unit\n       U. S. Naval Air Station\n       Pensacola, Florida\n\nSubj:  Awards; information concerning\n\nRef:   (a) Your ltr of 29 Oct 1956 with 1st end\n\nEncl:  (1) (SC) Three Medals\n\n1.  In reply to reference (a), the following information is furnished:\n\n         AWARDS              |Eligible|Forwarded|  Not   |Previously|Authorization\n  Complete award adjudication|        |  under  |Eligible| issued   |to purchase\nx Awards requested           |        |separate |(See    |(See      |(See Note #3)\n                             |        | cover   |Note #1)|Note #2)  |Price of medal\n\nGood Conduct Medal-1937      |   x    |    x    |  #4    |          |\n\n\n\nAmerican Defense Service Medal|\n   Fleet Clasp    Base Clasp  |\nAmerican Campaign Medal       |   x    |    x    |        |          |\nEuropean-African-Middle Eastern|\n       Campaign Medal         |\nAsiatic-Pacific Campaign Medal|        |         |   x    |          |\nWorld War II Victory Medal    |\nNavy Occupation Service Medal |        |         |   x    |          |\n   Asia Clasp    Europe Clasp |\nChina Service Medal           |\nNational Defense Service Medal|   x    |(Not available for issuance)  |\nKorean Service Medal          |   x    |(Not available for issuance)  |\nUnited Nations Service Medal  |   x    |    x    |        |          |\n\n                              V. E. ARMSTRONG\n                              By direction\n\n\n(See applicable notes on reverse side)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7152961aafc44737ec99712b1ce0263401d1805961fc55e782861c291dd10566", "output_sha256": "7152961aafc44737ec99712b1ce0263401d1805961fc55e782861c291dd10566", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:27.011754+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p481", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 481, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "#1  Since the records of the Bureau fail to show that you are eligible for\nthe award(s), it is suggested that if you have substantiating evidence to\nverify your eligibility for the medal(s) and will forward this evidence to\nthe Chief of Naval Personnel, further consideration will be given to your\nrequest.\n\n#2  You are advised that the Bureau is without authority to issue more than\none medal to each recipient unless the original medal was lost, destroyed or\nrendered unfit for use without fault or neglect on the part of the person\nto whom it was awarded.  Therefore, it is requested that you submit to the\nChief of Naval Personnel a statement as to whether the loss of your medal(s)\nwas due to no fault or neglect on your part.  Upon receipt of this information,\nfurther consideration will be given to your request.\n\n#3  In the event you should desire to purchase the medal(s) from the\nSuperintendent, U.S. Mint, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, you may use this\nletter as your authorization.  The prices listed include $.25 per medal for\npostage and handling.  This is payable by postal money order or certified\ncheck to the Treasurer of the United States.\n\n#4  You are authorized to wear two bronze stars in lieu of the Second and Third\nGood Conduct award.  Clasps for subsequent awards of the Good Conduct Medal are\nno longer issued nor authorized.\n\n                                                                    A75505", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ae7a936bd56fd8f7340302572aa4ea49ea2c8969b73c7f8d99ea6985c8707279", "output_sha256": "3a35e61e47d075b61533efc4aef3bd6c081a826e6ff4fa9b45de30d9ec1086c7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:28.595925+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p482", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 482, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "BUREAU OF NAVAL PERSONNEL          X-3d\n     DISCHARGED ENLISTED PERSONNEL RECORDS BRANCH\n              9700 PAGE BOULEVARD\n            ST. LOUIS 14, MISSOURI     IN REPLY REFER TO:\n                                       Pers-E374/RAP/md\n                                       393 07 21\n                                       3 Dec 1956\n\n[REDACTED]\n\nFrom: Head, Branch SEVEN\n      Enlisted Services and Records Division\n\nTo:   Head, Correspondence and Services Branch (Pers-E24)\n\nSubj: NEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement, 393 07 21, ex-CPhoM, USN\n      Eligibility for awards earned during enlisted service\n\nEncl: (1) Copy of your spdltr of 14 Nov 56\n\n1. The records of the Bureau reveal that subject officer earned the\nfollowing awards for his enlisted service as indicated by