                                          REC'D PERS E241\n\n                                                    NOV 05 1956\n\n                                        29 October 1956\n\n\nFrom:  CHPHOT, W-4 Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283/8311\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel (Pers E24)\nVia:   Commanding Officer\n\nSubj:  Medals; request for\n\n1.  It is requested that I be issued the following medals:\n\n              √ Good Conduct Medal with 2 bars\n              √ Korean Service Medal\n              √ American Campaign Medal\n              √ Asiatic-Pacific Area Campaign Medal\n              √ Japanese Occupation Medal\n              √ United Nations Service Medal\n              √ National Defense Medal (For Korea)\n\n393-07-21\n\n2.  The above medals were previously issued to me but were lost in\ntransit between duty stations and was due to no fault or neglect on my\npart.\n\n                              Delbert C. Newhouse\n                              DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\nFIRST ENDORSEMENT                              31 OCT 1956\n\nFrom:  Commanding Officer\nTo:    Chief of Naval Personnel\n\n1.  Forwarded.  CHPHOT NEWHOUSE's current service record shows that he is\nauthorized the above medals.\n\n                              F. M. Hall\n                              F. M. HALL\n                              By direction\n\n\n                                        Finished File Pers-E24a\n                                                      dm", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1eced62a659f2a35a66cb64eb2a0503ba5d21f1a36b56efc54d7a7ca92b632d2", "output_sha256": "01b13148db1919c4b8e2b20171abdc6a2e9b0acbf846930c72838e109fe14848", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:49:32.825126+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p484", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 484, "title": "DOW-U