tanding officers I    great value to the         cally effective officer                               (Adverse)\n          know                      service\n(a)                                 X\n(b)       2                         13                         1                          —                         —\n\n17. COMMENTS. In this section it is important that the outstanding characteristics of the officer, and any weaknesses which seriously affect his performance of duty, be reported. The appraisal should be concise and concrete in terms of specific examples of performance from which the more general factors can be inferred. The appraisal will justify the marks assigned in items 14, 15, and 16, above. In addition, the appraisal should include outstanding qualifications in any field such as the following: administration, planning, logistics, electronics, new weapons, and in dealing with the public in personal or official contacts. This space must not be left blank.\nCWO NEWHOUSE is a very competent and well informed officer whose performance as\nPhotographic Officer of this command has been commendable. He controls his men and his\nfacilities very effectively, always meeting the demands placed on his section and\nworking in harmony with all departments on the ship. He is the type of officer who,\nwhen given a task to perform, does it with no questions asked, quietly and efficiently.\nDuring the period of this report very heavy work loads have been imposed on the photo\nlab in conjunction with air operations, public relations and miscellaneous requirements.\nThese have been met with promptness and outstanding quality because of the excellent\nadministration of section by CWO NEWHOUSE. CWO NEWHOUSE is a very likeable and congenial\nofficer who is respected by both juniors and seniors alike. His bearing, deportment and\ndress have been outstanding.\n\n18. NAME, GRADE, AND FILE NUMBER OF REPORTING OFFICER. OFFICIAL STATUS RELATIVE TO OFFICER REPORTED ON.\nT. A. C