b)                                               1\n\n17. COMMENTS. In this section it is important that the outstanding characteristics of the officer, and any weaknesses which seriously affect his performance of duty, be reported. The appraisal should be concise and concrete in terms of specific examples of performance from which the more general factors can be inferred. The appraisal will justify the marks assigned in items 14, 15, and 16, above. In addition, the appraisal should include outstanding qualifications in any field such as the following: administration, planning, logistics, electronics, new weapons, and in dealing with the public in personal or official contacts. This space must not be left blank.\n\nCWO4 NEWHOUSE has performed and carried out his duties as Assistant Fleet Air Photographic Officer in an excellent manner.  His devotion to duty as a naval officer in the field of photography sets an example for personnel in his specialty to follow.  He maintains and generates a high degree of morale among the men with whom he works.  His past experience and excellent knowledge of photography has been a great help both to the personnel and to the efficient operation of the Lab.  He has a pleasant and radiant personality.\n\n\n18. NAME, GRADE, AND FILE NUMBER OF REPORTING OFFICER. OFFICIAL STATUS RELATIVE TO OFFICER REPORTED ON.\nB. F. ROWE, CDR, USN  83860/1310          Commanding Officer\n                                                                                          16—70109-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "761f40fdd2afe8692a19e078720980506b5e49f762ac319aae1b96d2d86c1fd4", "output_sha256": "23667aac313ea8d524016a7bd901780ada4fef48b496115206eb931c8787c2fc", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:53:08.219876+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p528", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 528, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record fo