sal should include outstanding qualifications in any field such as the following: administration, planning, logistics, electronics, new weapons, and in dealing with the public in personal or official contacts. This space must not be left blank.\nCHPHOT NEWHOUSE has performed his assigned duties in a satisfactory manner. He is fairly well versed in his technical specialty and has maintained high requirements of workmanship of personnel in the Photographic Division. Through a continuing maintenance program he has maintained the laboratory in an excellent material condition and, as noted in paragraph 20, has also improved the state of material readiness of photographic equipment.\n\n\n\n18. NAME, GRADE, AND FILE NUMBER OF REPORTING OFFICER. OFFICIAL STATUS RELATIVE TO OFFICER REPORTED ON.\nB. F. ROWE, CDR, 083860/1310.  Commanding Officer.\n\n                                                                                                    10-70109-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "37033690f35924a7aa491ef609a533eade827e3d9cf1c47e34fa6c60e4a209b3", "output_sha256": "d5bd595457b58cc1f983fe6fd9654830c949631b733391c6361645b8f4cc5890", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:53:52.493962+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p534", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 534, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "19. In comparison with other officers of his grade and approximate length of service or approximate length of duty assignment, to what degree has this officer exhibited the following qualities?\n\n(a) PROFESSIONAL KNOWLEDGE (Consider the requirements of his various duty assignments and compare them to his professional knowledge.)\n\nNOT OBSERVED | Has exceptional knowledge of his duty assignments. Extremely well informed. | Has excellent knowledge of most phases of his duty assignments. Is well informed on