ot observed, so state.\n\nCHPHOT NEWHOUSE has a sound knowledge of the workings of the Photographic Supply System and, during the period of this report, he has used this knowledge to good purpose. He evaluated the material condition of the photographic equipment and has raised the state of material readiness by replacing obsolete and worn items.\n\n\n21. (a) As a general rule, officers should not be shown their fitness reports by the reporting seniors unless the report contains adverse matter. An adverse report must be referred to statement pursuant to Article 1701-(8) Navy Regulations. His statement should be attached to this report.\n\n(b) Has the officer reported on seen this report? YES □  NO X\n\n22. DATE FORWARDED    11 January 1955.    23.    [Signature of reporting officer]\n\n24.\n(Signature of regular reporting senior if report is concurrent)\n\nU. S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE   16—70109-1\n\n25 JAN 1955", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c27905531f68013e31e84c2f40b92966bfd6cd3252f39dc58e400856b334a72e", "output_sha256": "71639d9e7b2a8c9bb96fe6b2921b9823c8d38d96fc0531d63647e707ca8bcc47", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:53:57.494801+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p535", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 535, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "SEP 17 1954 C\n\nNAVPERS-310 (REV. 3-54)                    REPORT ON THE FITNESS OF OFFICERS\n\nTHE OFFICER REPORTED ON WILL FILL IN THE FIRST ELEVEN SECTIONS:\n1. NAME (Last)          (First)              (Middle)        2. GRADE    3. USN (R)   4. DESIGNATOR   5. FILE NO.\nNEWHOUSE           Delbert              Clement         CHPHOT      USN          8310            177283\n\n6. SHIP OR STATION                                                              7. DATE REPORTED PRESENT DUTY STATION\nUtility Squadron FIVE (VU-5)              