evelopments. Comment on observed skill in dealing with the public in personal or official contacts. Any mental, moral, or physical weaknesses which\nmight affect his efficiency, or failure to meet qualifications normally expected of an officer of his grade and designation should be indicated. Any adverse\nentry made in any part of the report must be explained in this paragraph. This space must not be left blank.\nCHPHOT Newhouse has performed his duties in an outstanding manner.  The use of his\ntechnical knowledge and experience in the administration and control of photographic\nsupplies and equipment has successfully assisted the Aviation Supply Depot in the per-\nformance of its mission.  He has been particularly effective in interpreting Bureau\nphotographic policies.  His loyalty and cooperation inspire subordinates to a high\nrate of efficiency and morale.  CHPHOT Newhouse is dependable and conscientious.  His\nquiet manner gains the respect of all with whom he works.  He is recommended for pro-\nmotion.\n\n\n12. NAME, GRADE, AND FILE NUMBER OF REPORTING OFFICER.  OFFICIAL STATUS RELATIVE TO OFFICER REPORTED ON.\n  T. EARLE HIPP, RADM SC USN 15943      Commanding Officer\n\n                                                                                          o9-10—63343a-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c5523a3e71c6cc87ecb1989a400ce907a70e442089e904fa030209b28c9c801a", "output_sha256": "d54bc8d2ecbcecac51dc18f4207630ad7caba628d55e2bfecefb144708ca5b3c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:54:50.165042+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p542", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 542, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "13. TO WHAT DEGREE HAS THE OFFICER REPORTED ON EXHIBITED THE FOLLOWING QUALITIES?\n\n                          NOT        OUTSTANDING        EXCELLENT        AVERAGE     