      (Last)              (First)              (Middle)          Grade    USN(R)    Designator    File No.\n         NEWHOUSE              Delbert              Clement           CHPHOT      8311      177283\n2. SHIP OR STATION                                                  DATE REPORTED PRESENT DUTY STATION\n Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, Washington, D.C.              26 December 1951\n3. PERIOD OF REPORT                   OCCASION FOR REPORT                        TYPE OF REPORT\n FROM 11/30/51  To 2/2/52         Semi-       Detachment of      Detachment        Con-\n                                  annual ___  Reporting Senior ___  of Officer _X_  Regular ___  current ___  Special _X_\n4. REGULAR AND ADDITIONAL DUTIES. List all duties assigned, including watches. List courses of study or instruction carried on. After each item insert\nin parentheses number of months this reporting period.\n\nEnroute Fleet Activities, Yokosuka, Japan, to Bureau of Aeronautics  11/30/51 to 12/26/51\nRef: BuPers dispatch orders: Pers B115J-2117472, Nov. 1951\nTemporary duty - Photographic Division, Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, Washington\nD.C. from 12/26/51 to 2/2/52\n5. PROFICIENCY IN FOREIGN LANGUAGES, STATING WHICH ONES AND ABILITY THEREIN\n\n\n\n                                                          D C Newhouse\n                                                   (Signature of officer reported on)\n\nFOLLOWING TO BE FILLED IN BY THE REPORTING OFFICER:\n6. EMPLOYMENT OF COMMAND DURING PERIOD OF THIS REPORT\n\nBureau of Aeronautics, Navy Department, Washington, D.C.\n7. REFERENCE HERE AND APPEND COPY OF ANY COMMENDABLE OR ADVERSE REPORTS ON THIS OFFICER RECEIVED DURING THE PERIOD OF THIS REPORT\n\nNone\n\n8. PERFORMANCE. Assign marks on a scale\nof 0 to 4.0 on the appropriate qualifications\nlisted, and on any other significant quali-\nfication, on which observation has been suf-\nficient to justify marking. \"PRESENT AS-\nSIGNMENT\" must always be marked where\nany other marks or comments relative to\nperformance are made. A mark below 2.5\nconstitutes an adverse entry.             PRESENT\n                                          ASSIGNMENT . . . 3.9____   ABILITY TO COMMAND ____________   AS STAFF OFFICER . ____________\n\n                                          AS EXECUTIVE OR                        As ____________\n                                          DIVISION OFFICER . ____________   WATCH OFFICER . ____________   IN ADMINISTRATION . 3.9____\n                                                                            TECHNICAL COMPETENCE\n                                          SHIP HANDLING . ____________     in Photography 4.0____________\n                                                                                (State specialty)\n9. CONSIDERING THE POSSIBLE REQUIRE-\nMENTS OF WAR, INDICATE YOUR ATTITUDE\nTOWARD HAVING THIS OFFICER UNDER YOUR    PARTICULARLY DESIRE Y   BE PLEASED         BE SATISFIED          PREFER NOT\nCOMMAND. WOULD YOU                       TO HAVE HIM? ____X____  TO HAVE HIM? ______  TO HAVE HIM? ______  TO HAVE HIM?\n                                                                                                              (Adverse) ____________\n10. IN COMPARISON WITH OTHER OFFICERS\nOF HIS GRADE AND APPROXIMATE LENGTH OF\nSERVICE, HOW WOULD YOU DESIGNATE THIS\nOFFICER?          OUTSTANDING ________  EXCELLENT __X__   ABOVE            AVERAGE __________   BELOW\n                                                           AVERAGE __________                     AVERAGE __________\n11. COMMENTS. Give in this space a concise appraisal of the officer reported on. Comment on any outstanding characteristics of value to the naval service,\nincluding ability to command and outstanding qualifications in any field such as administration, planning, logistics, electronics, new weapons, or new\ndevelopments. Comment on observed skill in dealing with the public in personal or official contacts. Any mental, moral, or physical weaknesses which\nmight affect his efficiency, or failure to meet qualifications normally expected of an officer of his grade and designation should be indicated. Any adverse\nentry made in any part of the report must be explained in this paragraph. This space must not be left blank.\n\nCHPHOT Newhouse has been on temporary duty at the Bureau of Aeronautics, Navy\nDepartment, for briefing, prior to assuming the duties of Photographic Technical\nOfficer at the Aviation Supply Depot, Naval Supply Center, Oakland. During this\nperiod he has also assisted materially in setting up the procedures whereby the\nBureau of Aeronautics could assume Purchase and inventory control of microfilm\nequipment and related supplies.\n\nHe is of excellent military and personal character. CHPHOT Newhouse is highly\nrecommended for promotion when due.\n\n\n\n\n\n12. NAME, GRADE, AND FILE NUMBER OF REPORTING OFFICER. OFFICIAL STATUS RELATIVE TO OFFICER REPORTED ON.\nMurlin W. Alley, CDR, USN, 79137, Acting Director, Photographic Division, BuAer\n                                                                                           c9-16—G3848a-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cc509d5101a90b1e2b933231e2cfc83bd9d62d890bcb44116572fa6482f43502", "output_sha256": "dc06841e8f59f30056ece5d627a913fdf43902e6478d4ad14c85c5fe61297039", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T17:55:44.207640+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p548", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 548, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "13. To What Degree Has the Officer Reported on Exhibited the Following Qualities?\n\n                              | NOT      | OUTSTANDING                | EXCELLENT                  | AVERAGE                    | UNSATIS-\n                              | OBSERVED |                   