conduct must be referred to the officer for statement. Statements of a constructive nature which refer to minor imperfections\n    or limitations and which do not constitute an unsatisfactory report. For example: \"This officer was a little slow in getting started but is now making good progress,\" or \"This officer is well\n    qualified in his present duties but has had no experience at sea\" would not be unsatisfactory in nature.\n\n           Check one of these boxes -- I CONSIDER THIS REPORT TO BE ☒ SATISFACTORY  ☐ UNFAVORABLE  ☐ UNSATISFACTORY\n\nLT. Newhouse is a loyal, capable officer.  He carries out the liaison work on Single\nDepartment Procurement of Cameras and Photographic materials effectively and in a manner\nreflecting credit to the Navy.  He is tactful, cooperative, and has effectively handled\nnumerous problems arising in this joint department undertaking.  He is alert in keeping\nthe BuAer advised on USAF Research and Development projects.  LT. Newhouse's personal\nand military character is excellent and he is recommended for promotion and continuation\non duty in a commissioned status.\n\n\nSIGNATURE OF OFFICER REPORTED ON (Applies only to Sections 1 through 5)    SIGNATURE OF REPORTING OFFICER (If additional space is needed attach extra sheet)    Has this report been ☒ Yes\n                                                                                                                                                                    shown or referred to\n  Delbert C. Newhouse                                                             L. M. Grant                                                                      officer reported on?  ☐ No\n\nWhen completed remove carbon paper, forward Pages 1 and 2, not detached, to BuPers.  Retain Page 3 for \"Officer's Qualification Record Jacket.\"\n                                          PAGE 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd