ved, and likable officer.  He has had a difficult\ntime adjusting himself to his duties on this staff, but he has earnestly endeavored to\ndo so.  If his experience in naval aviation had been wider, it is believed he would have\nperformed his duties better.  He has performed his technical duties as Photographic Officer\nwell.  His performance of administrative duties, both as Photographic Officer and as Assistant\nOperations Officer, has improved during the period of this report.  He is not yet fitted for\npromotion.\n\n\n                                                         (If additional space is needed attach extra sheet)\nSIGNATURE OF OFFICER REPORTED ON (Applies only to Sections 1 through 5)   SIGNATURE OF REPORTING OFFICER     Has this report been\n                                                                                                               referred to officer   Yes\n  [signature]  Newhouse                                              [signature] Cronin                        officer reported on?  [X] No\n\nWhen completed remove carbon paper, forward Pages 1 and 2, not detached, to officers. Retain Page 3 for \"Officer's Qualification Record Jacket.\"\n                                          PAGE 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f1e9ebbe3ea869f2f2bcdaa97f6fbb1403fe766a62a7384174b28a7254153096", "output_sha256": "97372071ddbdfc7d696ecfcd6cb17fca70081b1a08f5187cf7383ac45f3542c9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:00:12.197204+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p562", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 562, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OFFICER'S FITNESS REPORT\nNAVPERS-310A (REV. 6-45)\nPLEASE TYPE THIS FORM\nIf no typewriter is available use ink but be sure all copies are legible.\n\n20                                DATE 29 February 1948\n\n1. NAME (last)   