ge, Photographic and Photo-Lithographic\n     materials in a satisfactory manner during the period of this report.  He\n     has shown considerable initiative in assuming responsibility for administrative\n     details of this Division and he has demonstrated an outstanding ability in his\n     technical specialty.  Lieut. (jg) Newhouse's personal and military character\n     is excellent and he is considered qualified for promotion to the next higher\n     rank when due.  He is also recommended for a permanent commission in the\n     regular Navy.  This report has been shown to Lieut. (jg) Newhouse.\n\nSIGNATURE OF OFFICER REPORTED ON (Applies only to Sections 1 through 5)    SIGNATURE OF REPORTING OFFICER              HAVE YOU\n                                                                                                                          READ\n                                                                                                                          THE ATTACHED\n   [Signature: Newhouse]                              [Signature]                                                         INSTRUCTION\n                                                                                                                          SHEET? YES\nWhen completed remove carbon paper, forward Pages 1 and 2, not detached, to BuPers. Retain Page 3 for \"Officer's Qualification Record Jacket\".\n                                              PAGE 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "45ca9ca7c22f71036e687c977754e1ff293953669c07bf4fe27ee53baf2741e9", "output_sha256": "5390630195d469fe7adbbb2c5d1b6328e176969226a3eafc522573635f3926d2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:04:08.890710+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p571", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 571, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "OF