 Newhouse has been technical advisor on all matters pertaining to photographic material\n    and has a complete knowledge of his specialty.  He has an outstanding military and personal\n    character and is considered well qualified and recommended for promotion when due.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                               (If additional space is needed attach extra sheet)\nSIGNATURE OF OFFICER REPORTED ON (Applies only to Sections 1 through 8)    SIGNATURE OF REPORTING OFFICER                  HAVE YOU READ\n                                                                                                                              THE ATTACHED\n    [signature]                                                                  [signature]                                  INSTRUCTION\n                                                                                                                              SHEET?  Yes\n         When completed remove carbon paper, forward Pages 1 and 2, not detached, to BuPers. Retain Page 3 for \"Officer's Qualification Record Jacket\".\n                                                             PAGE 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "30a8c47254ce858b3f9b7eeb9db963e3326b454e158342d3da7cd7b5c32e2262", "output_sha256": "2b048448e954337a7ac3965d5392a22aee51728cdfea8c5821e2d6dbdda30ec5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:04:32.706120+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p572", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 572, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "Refer to File No.\n\nNA10/P20-2/00\n  1619\n\n                                    U. S. NAVAL AIR STATION\n                                           Coco Solo\n                                    Upham, Canal Zone\n7 September 1944\n                                              BUR\n                                         NAVY DEPARTMENT\n                                           RECEIVED\n                                    1944 SEP 15 PM 3 11\n\n                    8-32\n\nFrom:    CO\nTo:      BuPers\n\nSubj:    Lt. (jg) Delbert C. NEWHOUSE, USN, 177283 - Fitness report\n         covering period 7-1-44 to 8-19-44\n\nRef:     (a) Navy Regs. Article 137.\n\n1.  In accordance with reference (a), it is requested that subject\nfitness report be extended to include the period 8-20-44 to 9-6-44.\n\nBy direction of Commanding Officer:\n\n                              G. GOULDRUP", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4058faa065046d109d17eff47bbef9ea925665450aeb92eedf003e9b4dd363aa", "output_sha256": "4058faa065046d109d17eff47bbef9ea925665450aeb92eedf003e9b4dd363aa", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:04:33.997968+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p573", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 573, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 311\n(Rev. 8-43)\n\n(TO BE USED ONLY FOR OFFICERS ON SHORE DUTY)\n\nREPORT ON THE FITNESS OF OFFICERS\n\n(To be submitted in accordance with Section 5 of Chapter 2, U. S. Navy Regulations, 1920, and Bureau of Naval Personnel Manual,\nArticle C—1006)\n(Before making out this report read latest Bureau of Naval Personnel circular letter on the subject of fitness reports)\n\nThe following four questions to be made out by the officer reported on:\n                                          SEP - 2 1944                    File No. 177283\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement                          Rank Ensign                    , U. S. N.\n              (Surname first)\nStation    NAS COCO SOLO C Z               Period from 1 July 1944    to  6 Sept. 1944\n         (Aviation units enter naval station to which attached)                          19 August 1944\n                                                                              (See attached form)\n\n1. Regular duties ........ Photographic Officer.\n\nAdditional duties .................................................................................................\n                    (After each duty insert in parentheses number of months this reporting period)\n2. Present address of { wife (if married) 1031 S.E. 16th Ave., Portland, Oregon.\n\n                        next of kin (if unmarried) ...........................................................................\n(Indicate above the best address at which the Bureau of Naval Personnel may communicate with the wife or next of kin in an emergency.\nThe above address does not relate to the usual residence (home) which is maintained in the Bureau. See Art. 135 (2), U. S. N. R., 1920.)\n\n3. Proficiency in foreign languages, stating which ones, and ability therein ........ None.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n4. My preference for next duty is—\n\n   (a) Sea ...... Fleet Air Wing ...............................  Fleet ........ Pacific ........................................................\n\n   (b) Shore ...... NAS ............................................  Location .... West Coast\n                                                                 Delbert Clement Newhouse\n                                                                              (Signature)\n\nFollowing to be made out by Reporting Officer:\n\n5. Reporting Officer: Name ........... R.P. KAUFFMAN .....................................  Rank .......... CAPTAIN ................., U. S. N.\n\n6. Reporting officer's official status relative to officer reported on ................... COMMANDING OFFICER\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n7. Assign marks on scale of 0—4 in appropriate subdivisions given below, and any other qualification on which observation has been\n   sufficient to justify marking.\n              (Staff officers to be marked with respect to required duties. Mark below 2.5 constitutes an unsatisfactory report)\n\n   Present assignment ........... 3.6 ........  Ability to command ............................  As executive or division officer ......... 3.5 ........\n\n   As deck watch officer ............................  In administration ............ 3.6 ......\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n8. Has the work of this officer been reported on either in a commendatory way or adversely during the period of this report? If so,\n   state the subject, reference numbers, and substance of report. Clip copy to report. Comply with U. S. Navy Regulations, Arti-\n   cle 137 (11), with respect to commendatory reports. Any adverse comment constitutes an unsatisfactory report.\n\n                                              No.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n9. Considering the possible requirements in war, indicate your attitude toward having this officer under your command. Would you—\n              (An affirmative entry in item (4) constitutes an unsatisfactory report)\n\n   (1) Particularly desire to have him? ..............  (2) Be pleased to have him? ..............  (3) Be satisfied to have him? ..............\n                                                                                   X\n   (4) Prefer not to have him? ..............\n\n10. Has he any weaknesses—mental, moral, physical, etc.—which adversely affect his efficiency? (If \"Yes,\" give details.)\n              (An implied or stated defect constitutes an unsatisfactory report)\n\n                                              No.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16—33531-8                                                                                                                    (OVER)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ee177cc5e3acaadebbf0dafd8533064ce18e09b2e5563f3ddcfa595be7c258fa", "output_sha256": "ee177cc5e3acaadebbf0dafd8533064ce18e09b2e5563f3ddcfa595be7c258fa", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:04:37.784100+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p574", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 574, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "11. To what degree has he exhibited the following qualities? (See instructions in latest Bureau of Naval Personnel circular letter on\n    the subject of fitness reports.)\n\nIntelligence\n                                                    X\n(With reference to the fac-  Exceptionally quick-witted;  Grasps essentials of a situ-  Understands normal situa-    Slow of comprehension; un-\nulty of comprehension;       keen in understanding.        ation quickly.                tions and conditions.        imaginative.\nmental acuteness.)\n                                        X\nJudgment\n(With reference to a dis-    Unusually keen in estimat-   Can generally be depended     Fair judgment in normal      Frequently draws wrong\ncriminating perception by    ing situations and reach-     on to make proper deci-       and routine things.          conclusions.\nwhich the values and re-     ing sound decisions.          sions.\nlations of things are men-\ntally asserted.)                                    X\nInitiative\n(With reference to con-      Exceptional in ability to    Able to plan and execute      Capable of performing rou-   Requires constant guidance\nstructive thinking and re-   think, plan, and do things   missions on his own re-       tine duties on own respon-   and supervision in his\nsourcefulness; ability and   without waiting to be told   sponsibility.                 sibility.                    work, or evades responsi-\nintelligence to act on own   and instructed.                                                                   bilities.\nresponsibility.)\n                                                    X\nForce\n(With reference to moral     Strong, dynamic.              Strong.                       Effectual under normal and   Less than normal.\npower possessed and ex-                                                                   routine circumstances.\nerted in producing re-\nsults.)                                             X\nLeadership\n(With reference to the fac-  Inspires others to a high de- A very good leader.           Leads fairly well.           A poor leader.\nulty of directing, con-      gree by precept and ex-\ntrolling, and influencing    ample.\nothers in definite lines of\naction.)                             X\nMoral Courage\n(With reference to that      Exceptionally courageous.     Courageous to a high degree.  Fairly courageous.           Timid.\nmental quality which im-\npels one to carry out the\ndictates of his confidence\nand convictions fearlessly.)\n                             X\nCooperation\n(With reference to the fac-  Exceptionally successful in  Works in harmony with         Cooperates fairly well.      Not cooperative.\nulty of working harmoni-     working with others to a     others.\nously with others toward     common end.\nthe accomplishment of\ncommon duties.)\n                                        X\nLoyalty\n(Fidelity, faithfulness, alle- Unswerving in allegiance:   A high sense of loyalty.      Reasonably faithful in the   Inclined to be disloyal.\nglance, constancy — all      frank and honest in aid-                                    execution of his duty.\nwith reference to a cause    ing and advising.\nand to higher authority.)               X\nPerseverance\n(With reference to mainte-   Determined, resolute.         Constant in purpose.          Fairly steady.               Inclined to vacillate.\nnance of purpose or un-\ndertaking in spite of ob-\nstacles or discourage-\nment.)                                              X\nReactions in emergencies\n(With reference to the fac-  Exceptionally cool-headed    Composed and logical in his   Fairly logical in his actions Inclined to be disconcerted.\nulty of acting instinc-      and logical in his actions   actions in difficult situa-   in general.\ntively in a logical man-     under all conditions.         tions.\nner in difficult and un-\nforeseen situations.)\n                                        X\nEndurance\n(With reference to ability   Capable of standing an ex-   Can perform well his duties   Of normal endurance.         Less than normal.\nfor carrying on under        ceptional amount of phy-      under trying conditions.\nany and all conditions.)     sical hardships and strain.\n                                        X\nIndustry\n(With reference to per-      Extremely energetic and in-  Thorough and energetic.       Reasonably energetic and     Indolent; lazy.\nformance of duties in an     dustrious.                                                  industrious.\nenergetic manner.)\nMilitary bearing and neat-\nness of person and dress\n                                                    X\n(With reference to dignity   Exceptional.                  Very good.                    Fair.                        Unmilitary and untidy.\nof demeanor, correctness\nof uniform, and smart-\nness of appearance.)\n\n12. In comparison with other officers of his rank and approximate length of service, how would you designate this officer? Out-\n    standing ............ Excellent ............ Above average ...X.... Average ............ Below average ............\n\n                                        REMARKS\n13. Is this officer professionally qualified to perform ALL the duties of his grade? Yes ..X.... No ............ If deficient in any\n    particular, comment is required. Give in this space a clear, concise estimate of this officer's personal and military character, his\n    fitness for promotion, and duty performed worthy of special mention, and any information which might be of value to the Depart-\n    ment in making assignments to duty. A check opposite \"No,\" except for inexperienced Ensigns, or a statement that performance\n    of duty is clearly unsatisfactory constitutes an unsatisfactory report. A statement of minor deficiencies either in character or\n    performance of duties constitutes an unfavorable report. (THIS SPACE IS NOT TO BE LEFT BLANK.)\n\nThis officer has wide experience in photography, much of it while he has\nbeen in the Navy but with additional background from civil life. He has\nextensive Navy service and is familiar with naval procedure. He is a\nsteady, orderly, practical type of average intelligence but his dependable\nand conscientious performance and his administrative qualities are above\naverage. He can be trusted with responsibility. He has a sturdy physique\nand a healthy common-sense outlook that fit him for any kind of duty, and\nis excellent material for an eventual rank in the regular Navy. Recommended\nfor promotion when due.\n\n\n                                                        SEP 27 1950\n\n\n14. An unsatisfactory report must have statement of officer reported on attached; an unfavorable report requires that officer reported\n    on has been informed of his deficiencies either verbally or in writing. Has this been done? ............ What improvement, if any,\n    has been noted? ..............\n\n                                                        R.P. KAUFFMAN\n                                                             (Signature)\n                    (Do not write in unruled portion of this space)                                         16-53531-2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f7abbfa0e194e1f572640722f66c134f7fae2359ef665a8d8b617cdcd26b264f", "output_sha256": "2c36e2cb48fba8dbeeac9bed93316347c5e0e1903a55161227bf4653e8103be0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:04:49.296143+00:00"}, {"id": "ca69163315f5ff40-p575", "card_id": "ca69163315f5ff40", "page": 575, "title": "DOW-UAP-D104, Final Personnel Record for Newhouse, Delbert C., U.S. Navy, 1957", "text": "NAVPERS 311\n(Revised February 1943)                    (TO BE USED ONLY FOR OFFICERS ON SHORE DUTY)\n\n                        REPORT ON THE FITNESS OF OFFICERS\n        (To be submitted in accordance with Section 5 of Chapter 2, U. S. Navy Regulations, 1920, and Bureau of Naval Personnel Manual,\n                                                    Article C—1007)\n              (Before making out this report read latest Bureau of Naval Personnel circular letter on the subject of fitness reports)\n\nThe following four questions to be made out by the officer reported on:\n                                                                                              File No. 177283\n\nNEWHOUSE, Delbert Clement          -4 JUL 1944     Rank  Ensign                              , U. S. N.\n                              (Surname first)\nStation Naval Air Station, Coco Solo, C.Z.              Period from  1-1-44       to  6-30-44\n                   (Aviation units enter naval station to which attached)\n\n1. Regular duties  Photographic Officer (6)\n\n   Additional duties  Naval Censor(6); Audit Board A.O.C.(5); Aviation Examining Board(4)\n                                    (After each duty insert in parentheses number of months this reporting period)\n\n2. Present address of { wife (if married)  Garibaldi, Oregon\n\n                       { next of kin (if unmarried)\n              (Indicate above the best address at which the Bureau of Naval Personnel may communicate with the wife or next of kin in an emergency.\n              The above address does not relate to the usual residence (home) which is maintained in the Bureau. See Art. 135(2), U. S. N. R., 1920.)\n\n3. Proficiency in foreign languages, stating which ones, and ability therein  None\n\n\n4. My preference for next duty is—\n\n   (a) Sea Photographic Squadron                    Fleet  Pacific\n\n   (b) Shore  N.A.S.                               Location  Tillamook, Oregon\n                                                              D C Newhouse\n                                                                        (Signature)\n\nFollowing to be made out by Reporting Officer:\n\n5. Reporting Officer: Name       R. P. KAUFFMAN                    Rank       Captain              , U. S. N.\n\n6. Reporting officer's official status relative to officer reported on  Commanding Officer\n\n7. Assign marks on scale of 0—4 in appropriate subdivisions given below, and any other qualification on which observation has been\n   sufficient to justify marking.\n              (Staff officers to be marked with respect to required duties. Mark below 2.5 constitutes an unsatisfactory report)\n\n   Present assignment  3.6          Ability to command  3.5      As executive or division officer  3.5\n\n   As deck watch officer                