t in making assignments to duty. A check opposite \"No,\" except for inexperienced Ensigns, or a statement that performance\n    of duty is clearly unsatisfactory constitutes an unsatisfactory report. A statement of minor deficiencies either in character or\n    performance of duties constitutes an unfavorable report. (THIS SPACE IS NOT TO BE LEFT BLANK.)\n\nThis officer has wide experience in photography of all types, much of it while he has been in the\nNavy but with additional background from civil life. He has extensive Navy service and is\nfamiliar with naval procedure. He is a steady, orderly, practical type of average intelligence\nbut his dependable and conscientious performance and his administrative qualities are above\naverage. He can be trusted with responsibility and will run a good department without supervision.\nHe has a sturdy physique and a healthy common-sense outlook that fit him for any kind of duty.\nHe should be kept in the photographic field and is excellent material for eventual promotion to\npermanent commissioned rank in the regular Navy.\n\n14. An unsatisfactory report must have statement of officer reported on attached; an unfavorable report requires that officer reported\n    on has been informed of his deficiencies either verbally or in writing. Has this been done? ............. What improvement, if any,\n    has been noted? -------------------------------------------------------\n\n                                               R. P. Kauffman\n                                     R. P. KAUFFMAN          (Signature)\n                        (Do not write in unruled portion of this space)                              16-33831-1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "287556f3c785f0bce175db97c5305d99631772dfc4e1feab05240cc34ca4cc76", "output_sha256": "1cdda4fb3fe305a309f93e7f346494469f4e3bf1007ccbd0ce53f2254772acf9", "generated_at": "