Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM                                    Record Preview\n                                                                                    Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n   Document View    XML                                                             USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                                                                                    Declassified on: 20 March 2026\n\n                                    [REDACTED]\n\n   IIR - Intelligence Information Report                                                           O Print      X Close\n\n   —Core Metadata—\n\n   IIR NUMBER:                                    3024(i)\n   COLLECTOR                                                 COLLECTOR NAME                    COLLECTOR NUMBER\n                                                  AFSOC A2OX - MOTHERSHIP                6500\n\n   OVERALL CLASSIFICATION:           [REDACTED]\n   PRIMARY KEY                                    50005165458\n   VERSION NUMBER                                 1\n   ORIGINATING SYSTEM NAME                        1.4(c)\n   ORIGINATING SYSTEM ID\n   LAST MODIFICATION SYSTEM:\n   CREATE DATE                                    2022-04-27T13:29:17.651Z\n   LAST CHANGE DATE                               2022-04-27T13:18:21.087040000+00:00\n   MESSAGE FROM ADDRESS:                          1.4(c)  WASHINGTON DC//AFSOC HURLBURT FLD FL/AFSOC//\n   DTG                                            271329ZAPR22\n   DATE                                           2022-04-27Z\n   TITLE:                    [REDACTED]            1.4c                    Multiple Unidentified Aerial Phenomenon\n                                                  Observed Maneuvering Erratically and In Formation Over Gulf of Oman During AC-130 Gunship\n                                                  Live Fire Training on 8 September 2021 - Attachment\n\n   SUMMARY:                  [REDACTED]            On 8 September 2021 a USSOF AC-130 Gunship observed approximately 25 instances of UAPs\n                                                  while conducting a live fire exercise in the Gulf of Oman. The UAPs were observed as cold\n                                                  orbs flying at lower altitudes between 250 to 1300 MPH in different formations as well as\n                                                  maneuvering aggressively. UAPs also appeared to react to the aircraft firing its main\n                                                  cannon.\n\n   TARGET:                                        Portion Mark:    U\n\n                                                  Country:         OM\n\n                                                  Non State Entity:\n\n   TOPICS:                                        Portion Mark:  U\n                                                  NIPF          FMCC\n                                                                TECH\n\n   IFC/ICC                                        IFC150B\n                                                  IFC220L\n                                                  IFC150A\n\n   KEYWORD\n   NHCD ID:\n   USCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061           Approved for Release to AARO                    03/26/26   000001\n                                         (b)(6)\n                                                                                                                     1/7", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3a56b6a8e9e45bbf966f78485365e1059ea221825b49430698303720e877095f", "output_sha256": "3a56b6a8e9e45bbf966f78485365e1059ea221825b49430698303720e877095f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:03.278548+00:00"}, {"id": "d973d98ce1f1f852-p2", "card_id": "d973d98ce1f1f852", "page": 2, "title": "DOW-UAP-D101, Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM                                    Record Preview\n         IIR DOI:                                    2021-09-08Z                              Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                                                                                              USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n         REQUIREMENT NUMBER:                         NTRI200AJ002421                         Declassified on: 20 March 2026\n         SOURCE:              Classification         Source Identifier         Source Description         Context Statement\n                                          (U/[REDACTED]          1.4c                                      (S//NF) Source had direct access to\n                                                                                                            the reported information via the conduct of official duties.\n                                                                              1.4(c),130b                  Source was aware information would\n                                                                                                            be provided to the US government.\n\n         MESSAGE:                          [REDACTED] INITIAL OBSERVATION. On 8 September 2021 a United States Special Operations\n                                          Forces (USSOF) AC-130 Gunship was conducting live fire training in the Gulf of Oman in the\n                                          vicinity of (IVO) //MGRS: 40REN68[1.4a]3[1.4a]/ during period of darkness. The AC-130 first\n                                          observed Unidentified Aerial Phenomenon (UAPs) when the aircraft dropped a\n                                          water-activated flare to use as a mock target. The AC-130 entered an orbit around the\n                                          flare and the Combat Systems Officer (CSO) conducted collateral scans with the aircraft's\n                                          Electro Optical/Infrared (EO/IR) sensor IVO the flare. When the CSO slewed the sensor in\n                                          IR mode back to the flare they observed two approximately four-foot diameter cold orbs\n                                          between 0 to 20 feet above the surface of the water stationary over the flare for\n                                          approximately 15 seconds. After those 15 seconds passed, the CSO pulled the trigger\n                                          firing the aircraft's 105mm cannon. Immediately upon pulling the trigger, during the\n                                          slight delay between trigger pull and the cannon's recoil, the CSO observed the pair of\n                                          UAPs rapidly fly away from the flare and out of the sensor feed without changing\n                                          altitude.\n                                          [REDACTED] SUBSEQUENT OBSERVATIONS. The AC-130 crew observed approximately 25 instances of\n                                          UAPs viewed in IR as cold orbs in both white-is-hot and black-is-hot mode during the\n                                          sortie. Two UAPs were observed flying in a loose but coordinated formation increasing and\n                                          decreasing altitude like a wave while maneuvering around, over, and under each other in a\n                                          manner similar to how dolphins playfully swim in a pod. (SOURCE COMMENT: They [The UAPs]\n                                          knew they were flying together). UAPs were also separately observed flying in a formation\n                                          of three and separately observed flying erratically and maneuvering aggressively. The\n                                          attached videos depict a smoothly slewing EO/IR sensor or a stationary EO/IR sensor with\n                                          multiple UAPs darting around the sensor feed. The AC-130's crew attempted to save\n                                          entirety of the EO/IR footage of the UAP observations but the aircraft's Digital Video\n                                          Recorder (DVR) inexplicably failed and the video data became corrupted.\n                                          [REDACTED] ESTIMATED SPEED. The CSO calculated the UAP's approximate speeds using the\n                                          aircraft's TACTOOL and clocked their maximum observed maneuvering speed at 1300 miles per\n                                          hour (MPH) and the UAPs minimum observed maneuvering speed at 250 MPH. No means of\n                                          propulsion were observed.\n\n         COMMENT:                         [REDACTED])          1.4c               is the tag line for AFSOC personnel conducting          1.4c\n                                          debriefing.\n                                          (U/[REDACTED] This IIR was coordinated with USDAO Muscat and SOCCENT J2X without comment.\n                                          (U) Source A is available for recontact about information in this report.\n                                          (U/[REDACTED] Geographic coordinates were derived from AC-130 sensor feed GPS data.\n                                          (U/[REDACTED] requests concerning foreign disclosure and release of the information contained\n                                          in this report should be sent to the AFSOC FDO at          3.5c, (b)(6)\n                                          Include the justification, serial number, subject line of the report and the proposed\n                                          request in the initial correspondence.\n                                          (U/[REDACTED] IIR Evaluations and Source Directed Requirements regarding this report are\n                                          highly encouraged to assist in assessing collection efforts and requirements. Evaluations\n                                          and Source Directed Requirements can be created using [1.4(c)]\n                                                    3.5c, (b)(6)          Any questions concerning this report should be\n\nUSCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061               Approved for Release to AARO                                          03/26/26   000002\n         3.5c, (b)(6)                                                                                                                          2/7", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d97291b1fbf087efb61e4f5cc81edc4a8534043f97d31a1ee02f40eca140f9d9", "output_sha256": "a0d92e8d94ea62257d42327f316135a7fd76e71284e166a0397c21e932be2000", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:12.277662+00:00"}, {"id": "d973d98ce1f1f852-p3", "card_id": "d973d98ce1f1f852", "page": 3, "title": "DOW-UAP-D101, Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM                                          Record Preview\n                                    directed to:          3.5c, (b)(6)          Please reference IIR number along with  Reclassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                                    any final product or brief the IIR information was utilized.                    USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                                                                                                                    Declassified on: 20 March 2026\n      FULL MESSAGE TEXT:             R 271329Z APR 22\n                                    FM  1.4(c)  WASHINGTON DC//AFSOC HURLBURT FLD FL/AFSOC//\n                                    TO AFIAA AMHS BOLLING AFB DC\n                                    AFSOC HURLBU