 UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM\n\n                                          Record Preview\n                    HQDA DIR G2X WASHINGTON DC\n                    JAC MOLESWORTH RAF MOLESWORTH UK\n                    JAC MOLESWORTH UK\n                    JICCENT MACDILL AFB FL\n                    JOINT STAFF WASHINGTON DC\n                    JPRA FT BELVOIR VA\n                    JWAC DAHLGREN VA\n                    NASIC WRIGHT PATTERSON AFB OH\n                    NCTC WASHINGTON DC\n                    NGA WASHINGTON DC\n                    NGIC INTEL OPS CHARLOTTESVILLE VA\n                    NGIC SRD FT GEORGE G MEADE MD\n                    ONI WASHINGTON DC\n                    PENTAGON WASHINGTON DC\n                    USASOC INTEL CTR FT BRAGG NC\n                    USCENTCOM CCJ2 MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USCENTCOM CCJ3 MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USCENTCOM JOC MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USSOCOM J2 INTEL MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USSOCOM J3 OPERATIONS DIRECTORATE MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USSOCOM J5 STRATEGY PLANS AND POLICY MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USSOCOM JTF DEPLOYED\n                    USSOCOM SOFM MACDILL AFB FL\n                    USSTRATCOM INTEL DIRECTORATE OFFUTT AFB\n                    INFO 1.4(c)      WASHINGTON DC\n                    CIA WASHINGTON DC\n                    S-E-C-R-E-T//NOFORN\n                    QQQQ\n                    SERIAL: (U)      1.4c\n                    DATE OF PUBLICATION: 271329Z APR 22\n                    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n                                          US Air Force\n                              INFORMATION REPORT, NOT FINALLY EVALUATED INTELLIGENCE\n                    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n                    COUNTRY OR NONSTATE ENTITY: (U) Oman (OMN)\n                    SUBJECT: (S//NF)      1.4c                              - Multiple\n                    Unidentified Aerial Phenomenon Observed Maneuvering Erratically and\n                    In Formation Over Gulf of Oman During AC-130 Gunship Live Fire\n                    Training on 8 September 2021 - Attachment\n                    DATE OF INFORMATION: (U) 08 SEP 2021\n                    CUTOFF: (U) 08 Sep 2021\n                    SUMMARY: (S//NF) On 8 September 2021 a USSOF AC-130 Gunship observed\n                    approximately 25 instances of UAPs while conducting a live fire\n                    exercise in the Gulf of Oman. The UAPs were observed as cold orbs\n                    flying at lower altitudes between 250 to 1300 MPH in different\n                    formations as well as maneuvering aggressively. UAPs also appeared to\n                    react to the aircraft firing its main cannon.\n                    SOURCE NUMBER A: (U//FOUO)      1.4c\n                                        1.4(c), 130b\n                    CONTEXT A: (S//NF) Source had direct access to the reported\n                    information via the conduct of official duties. Source was aware\n                    information would be provided to the US government.\n                    WARNING: (U) THIS IS AN INFORMATION REPORT, NOT FINALLY EVALUATED\n                    Approved for Release to AARO\n\nUSCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061                                                    03/26/26   000004\n                                                                                                    4/7\n        3.5c,(b)(6)\n\n                    Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                    USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                    Declassified on: 20 March 2026", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2d0c4075abf5599da19c14233e4174181524b699a6f5b59f5c5da27263b8ca3c", "output_sha256": "879bf51c69a764c396f016fc750b720fd359bf0ce90950c1f83c52b4dfc8a54f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:21.202652+00:00"}, {"id": "d973d98ce1f1f852-p5", "card_id": "d973d98ce1f1f852", "page": 5, "title": "DOW-UAP-D101, Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM\n\n                                                Record Preview\n                     INTELLIGENCE REPORT CLASSIFIED SECRET//NOFORN.      Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                     TEXT: (U)                                                      USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                     [REDACTED] INITIAL OBSERVATION. On 8 September 2021 a United States classified on: 20 March 2026\n                     Special Operations Forces (USSOF) AC-130 Gunship was conducting live\n                     fire training in the Gulf of Oman in the vicinity of (IVO) //MGRS:\n                     40REN681.4d 31.4d/ during period of darkness. The AC-130 first\n                     observed Unidentified Aerial Phenomenon (UAPs) when the aircraft\n                     dropped a water-activated flare to use as a mock target. The AC-130\n                     entered an orbit around the flare and the Combat Systems Officer\n                     (CSO) conducted collateral scans with the aircraft's Electro\n                     Optical Infrared (EO/IR) sensor IVO the flare. When the CSO slewed\n                     the sensor in IR mode back to the flare they observed two\n                     approximately four-foot diameter cold orbs between 0 to 20 feet above\n                     the surface of the water stationary over the flare for approximately\n                     15 seconds. After those 15 seconds passed, the CSO pulled the trigger\n                     firing the aircraft's 105mm cannon. Immediately upon pulling the\n                     trigger, during the slight delay between trigger pull and the\n                     cannon's recoil, the CSO observed the pair of UAPs rapidly fly away\n                     from the flare and out of the sensor feed without changing altitude.\n                     [REDACTED] SUBSEQUENT OBSERVATIONS. The AC-130 crew observed\n                     approximately 25 instances of UAPs viewed in IR as cold orbs in both\n                     white-is-hot and black-is-hot mode during the sortie. Two UAPs were\n                     observed flying in a loose but coordinated formation increasing and\n                     decreasing altitude like a wave while maneuvering around, over, and\n                     under each other in a manner similar to how dolphins playfully swim\n                     in a pod. (SOURCE COMMENT: They [The UAPs] knew they were flying\n                     together). UAPs were also separately observed flying in a formation\n                     of three and separately observed flying erratically and maneuvering\n                     aggressively. The attached videos depict a smoothly slewing EO/IR\n                     sensor or a stationary EO/IR sensor with multiple UAPs darting around\n                     the sensor feed. The AC-130's crew attempted to save entirety of the\n                     EO/IR footage of the UAP observations but the aircraft's Digital\n                     Video Recorder (DVR) inexplicably failed and the video data became\n                     corrupted.\n                     [REDACTED] ESTIMATED SPEED. The CSO calculated the UAP's approximate\n                     speeds using the aircraft's TACTOOL and clocked their maximum\n                     observed maneuvering speed at 1300 miles per hour (MPH) and the UAPs\n                     minimum observed maneuvering speed at 250 MPH. No means of propulsion\n                     were observed.\n                     COMMENTS: 1. (Field Comment) (S//NF)[          1.4c          ]is the tag line\n                     for AFSOC personnel conducting[   1.4c   ]debriefing.\n                     2. (U/[REDACTED] This IIR was coordinated with USDAO Muscat and SOCCENT\n                     J2X without comment.\n                     3. (U) Source A is available for recontact about information in this\n                     report.\n                     4. (U/[REDACTED] Geographic coordinates were derived from AC-130 sensor\n                     feed GPS data.\n                     5. (U/[REDACTED] Requests concerning foreign disclosure and release of\n                     the information contained in this report should be sent to the AFSOC\n                     FDO at[          3.5c, (b)(6)          ]Include the justification,\n                     serial number, subject line of the report and the proposed request in\n                     the initial correspondence.\n                     6. (U/[REDACTED] IIR Evaluations and Source Directed Requirements\n                     regarding this report are highly encouraged to assist in assessing\n                     collection efforts and requirements. Evaluations and Source Directed\nUSCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061     Requirements can be created using [1.4(c)]                    03/26/26   000005\n                     Approved for Release to AARO\n3.5c, (b)(6)                                                                                                           5/7", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ce1629a9f0313f18f23b7271796ae460b79aaf0fec6454965a479190838240af", "output_sha256": "13aff038da9ffdc58460f229785f81424291d38c0b03e2e06793788d741321e2", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:27.132800+00:00"}, {"id": "d973d98ce1f1f852-p6", "card_id": "d973d98ce1f1f852", "page": 6, "title": "DOW-UAP-D101, Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM                                    Record Preview\n\n                              3.5c,(b)(6)          Any questions concerning this  Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                    report should be directed to:        3.5c,(b)(6)             USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                    Please reference IIR number along with any final product or brief the declassified on: 20 March 2026\n                    IIR information was utilized.\n                    ATTACHMENTS: (U) To follow - 1 ATTACHMENTS,\n                    1. Video, 8 September 2021 UAP[REDACTED], Powerpoint containing six\n                    embedded videos of 8 September 2021 UAPs captured via AC-130\n                    (SECRET//NOFORN).\n                    TOPIC: (U) FMCC; TECH.\n                    FUNCTIONAL CODE: (U) IFC150B; IFC220L; IFC150A.\n                    REQUIREMENT: (U) NTRI200AJ002421.\n                    MGT CODE: (U) BG; BK; RD; DF; DG.\n                    INSTR: (U) U.S. NO.\n                    PREP: (U)      3.5c, (b)(6)\n                    JOINT REP: (U) None.\n                    DATE OF ACQUISITION: (U//[REDACTED]) 20220407; USA, Cannon AFB, New Mexico\n                    POC: (U//FOUO) Direct all questions to AFSOC A2H, Hurlburt Field FL\n                    at SVOIP  3.5c, (b)(6)   or TSVOIP 3.5c,(b)(6) or email to\n                         3.5c, (b)(6)\n                    WARNING: (U) THIS IS AN INFORMATION REPORT, NOT FINALLY EVALUATED\n                    INTELLIGENCE REPORT CLASSIFIED SECRET//NOFORN.\n                    ===========================DISSEMINATION===========================\n                    AGENCY: (U) Central Intelligence Agency (CIA); Defense Intelligence\n                    Agency (DIA); Defense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA); Department of\n                    Defense; Federal Aviation Administration (FAA); National Aeronautics\n                    and Space Administration (NASA); US Air Force; US Army; US Marine\n                    Corps; US Navy.\n                    U.S. MISSION: (U) None.\n                    MILITARY: (U) Air Force; CENTCOM; SOCOM; Navy; Army; Marine Corps.\n                    STATE/LOCAL: (U) None.\n                    ===========================CLASSIFICATION===========================\n                    CLASSIFIED BY: AFSOC A2OH\n                    DERIVED FROM: DO SCG JUL 2017\n                    DECLASSIFY ON: 50X1-HUM\n                    [REDACTED]\n                    #0000\n\nCOLLECTION MANAGEMENT CODE:                         BG\n                                                     BK\n                                                     RD\n                                                     DF\n                                                     DG\n\nU.S. CITIZEN:                                        U.S. NO\n\n                              Classification                                    Instruction\n\nREPORTER:\n                                                     1.4c\n\n—Extended Metadata—\n\nPUBLIC NOTE:\nINTERNAL NOTES:\nBE NUMBER:\nLATITUDE/LONGITUDE:\nUSCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061          Approved for Release to AARO                    03/25/26   000006\n                              3.5c,(b)(6)                                                                          6/7", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6a0539f52df85c06ba135d1abab4f1dd35cb90461fe74aa6e825361b4bef8ecf", "output_sha256": "ae412aac50fb637a6f97793d4df625542ee0d008491f9649158ca657ac400c21", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:30.561275+00:00"}, {"id": "d973d98ce1f1f852-p7", "card_id": "d973d98ce1f1f852", "page": 7, "title": "DOW-UAP-D101, Intelligence Information Report, Unresolved UAP Report, Gulf of Oman, 2021", "text": "6/1/22, 11:23 AM                                    Record Preview                    Declassified by MG Richard A. Harrison\n                                                                                         USCENTCOM Chief of Staff\n                    Latitude              Longitude                                      Declassified on: 20 March 2026\n\n        UTM:\n        ENCL NOTE:\n\n\n                                              [REDACTED]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        USCENTCOM MDR 26-0049 to MDR 26-0061          Approved for Release to AARO                    03/26/26   000007\n                                        3.5c, (b)(6)\n                                                                                                                    7/7", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fb4dc6aa70c201b70c8ccdc7175fa560cd4d4f2b835b28d4d429411d32bc111c", "output_sha256": "f94a5b5715bb64a6b5db73da012775559389f8f9086ee202dfde0d81997bb579", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:04:32.211239+00:00"}, {"id": "d983745c9c3a4709-p1", "card_id": "d983745c9c3a4709", "page": 1, "title": "FBI-UAP-D010, FD-302-71, “Northeastern Orb Sighting,” 2026", "text": "FD-302 (Rev. 5-8-10)\n\n                                    - 1 of 2 -                                    OFFICIAL RECORD\n\n\n                           FEDERAL BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION\n\n\n\n                                                                    Date of entry  [REDACTED]\n\n\n      [REDACTED] On [REDACTED]                    [REDACTED]  was interviewed along with\n[REDACTED]          , [REDACTED]          , at [REDACTED]    [REDACTED]   [REDACTED]   [REDACTED]        .\nAfter being advised of the identity of the interviewing agents and the\nnature of the interview, [REDACTED]                          provided the following\ninformation:\n\n      On [REDACTED]  [REDACTED] , [REDACTED]      arrived home in the evening around 9:15pm.\nOnce parking in the driveway, [REDACTED]      noticed a ball of light through [REDACTED]\nwindshield which was yellow and about the size of a basketball. Upon exiting\nthe vehicle, [REDACTED]      saw a second ball of light which was larger and about\nthe size of a beach ball. The objects were behind a row of trees, which have\nsince been taken down but in front of a section of trees between [REDACTED]\nproperty and [REDACTED]  neighbor's property behind the home. [REDACTED]      was able to\nlook at the lights without strain or discomfort on [REDACTED]  eyes. [REDACTED]\nstated that [REDACTED]  has not had any health issues or concerns since seeing these\nobjects.\n\n[Agent Note: Based on where [REDACTED]      was standing, the objects were\napproximately 30 yards away and 20-30 feet above the ground].\n\n      [REDACTED]; Upon seeing the lights, [REDACTED]  came outside to view the objects as\nwell. Both [REDACTED]      and [REDACTED]  observed the objects move laterally to their\nleft, passing behind a tree approximately 36 yards away, at the same height,\ncontinuing behind a neighbor's house and beyond a tree that was\napproximately 75 away. It was at this point where [REDACTED]      stated that [REDACTED]\nsaw one orb going into the other orb before disappearing abruptly.\n\n      [REDACTED] [REDACTED]  stated that a few weeks after this event, [REDACTED]  saw several white\norbs travel over [REDACTED]  house from the west to the east. These white orbs were\ntraveling much higher in altitude than the prior red orbs.\n\n      [REDACTED]  In 1987, [REDACTED]  stated that [REDACTED]  had witnessed something strange off of\n[REDACTED]          ; [REDACTED]  in [REDACTED]          [REDACTED]  near power lines. [REDACTED]  saw a red light\ncircling around itself at night described it like the front end of Kit from\n\n\n                                    [REDACTED]\n\nInvestigation on  [REDACTED]          at  [REDACTED]                    United States (In Person)\n\n[REDACTED]                                    ,  [REDACTED]          ,  [REDACTED]\nFile #  [REDACTED]                                                       Date drafted  [REDACTED]\n\nby  [REDACTED]\n\nThis document contains neither recommendations nor conclusions of the FBI. It is the property of the FBI and is loaned to your agency; it and its contents are not\nto be distributed outside your agency.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7a7ec857f77d1a22f3b34eb536c3d10ce226f14a17dd7b07549a05317d966d0f", "output_sha256": "1ab69a336a5b6eb77f526f6646d4792d14c6125b180433f2a8f2b9be33de6d2c", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:07:19.639779+00:00"}, {"id": "d983745c9c3a4709-p2", "card_id": "d983745c9c3a4709", "page": 2, "title": "FBI-UAP-D010, FD-302-71, “Northeastern Orb Sighting,” 2026", "text": "FD-302a (Rev. 5-8-10)\n\n                              [REDACTED]\n\n          [REDACTED]    Interview of [REDACTED]\nContinuation of FD-302 of [REDACTED]                          , On [REDACTED]  , Page  2 of 2\n\n   the TV show Knight Rider. [REDACTED] saw the object hover and then land near the\npower station. Since then [REDACTED] stated that [REDACTED] has always been interested in\nthe topic of UAP.\n\n     [REDACTED] Attached to this interview were photos taken by Agents at the\npermission of [REDACTED] [REDACTED].\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                              [REDACTED]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8c337543a4a4195ef107909c448f91c090182eab2251a67401a876ff01925b32", "output_sha256": "5c4f63a0ed8c0d139ce7b7c51ded8110e7956ac53fbc82a8967cbfab6c39175b", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:07:20.707333+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p1", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 1, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "DECLASSIFIED\nAuthority:\nNND 57563\n\nAFOIN/Maj Gen Cabell/mcm/9613/3 Nov 48\n\nSECRET\n\n3 NOV 1948\n\nSUBJECT: Flying Object Incidents in the United States\n\nTO: Commanding General, Air Materiel Command\n Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n Dayton, Ohio\n\n 1. By letter dated 30 December 1947 from the Director of\nResearch and Development, Headquarters USAF, your Headquarters\nwas required to establish Project \"SIGN\". A 680\n\n 2. The conclusion appears inescapable that some type of\nflying object has been observed. Identification and the origin\nof these objects is not discernible to this Headquarters. It is\nimperative, therefore, that efforts to determine whether these\nobjects are of domestic or foreign origin must be increased until\nconclusive evidence is obtained. The needs of national defense\nrequire such evidence in order that appropriate countermeasures\nmay be taken.\n\n 3. In addition to the imperative need for evidence to permit\ncountermeasures, is the necessity of informing the public as to\nthe status of the problem. To date there has been too little data\nto present to the public. The press, however, is about to take it\ninto its own hands and demand to be told what we do or do not know\nabout the situation. Silence on our part will not long be acceptable.\n\n 4. Request immediate information as to your conclusions to\ndate and your recommendations as to the information to be given\nto the press. Your recommendation is requested also as to\nwhether that information should be offered to the press or withheld until it is actively sought by the press.\n\n BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n HQ. USAF\n 4-NOV 1948\nP105530 MAIL BRANCH\n\n C. P. CABELL\n Major General, USAF\n Director of Intelligence, Office of\n Deputy Chief of Staff, Operations\n\nOFFICE SYMBOL | 1. AFOIR | 2. AFOI1 | 3. AFOIN | 4. | 5.\nGRADE AND\nSURNAME OF | [ILLEGIBLE] | [ILLEGIBLE] |\nCOORDINATING | [ILLEGIBLE] | [ILLEGIBLE] | C. P. CABELL |\nOFFICERS | G.S. Harris Jr. | | Maj. Gen., USAF |\n\n[REDACTED]\n10-20242-2 U.S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "433994547bae01314c804e3e6f22b6f2484ebe0e1e0c0bcea7b5d5e76931b76d", "output_sha256": "a4b9bc09b3eff975d85b528d163b99bc49b5a5c8aceeeec901d508ac0fa3d564", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:38.318253+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p2", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 2, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "See TS-2-3931          AFOIN/Maj Gen Cabell/mcm/5613/2 Nov 48    3 Nov 48\nfor Cover Sheet +\n   M/R\n\n\n                              8 NOV 1948\n\n\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Flying Object Incidents in the United States\n\nTO:       Commanding General, Air Materiel Command\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Dayton, Ohio\n\n                    classified files\n          1.  By letter dated 30 December 1947 from the Director of\nResearch and Development, Headquarters USAF, your Headquarters\nwas required to establish Project \"SIGN\".\n\n          2.  The conclusion appears inescapable that some type of\nflying object has been observed.  Identification and the origin\nof these objects is not discernible to this Headquarters.  It is\nimperative, therefore, that efforts to determine whether these\nobjects are of domestic or foreign origin must be increased until\nconclusive evidence is obtained.  The needs of national defense\nrequire such evidence in order that appropriate countermeasures\nmay be taken.\n\n          3.  In addition to the imperative need for evidence to permit\ncountermeasures, is the necessity of informing the public as to\nthe status of the problem.  To date there has been too little data\nto present to the public.  The press, however, is about to take it\ninto its own hands and demand to be told what we do or do not know\nabout the situation.  Silence on our part will not long be accept-\nable.\n\n          4.  Request immediate information as to your conclusions to\ndate and your recommendations as to the information to be given\nto the press.  Your recommendation is requested also as to\nwhether that information should be offered to the press or with-\nheld until it is actively sought by the press.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                         /s/ C P Cabell\n                         Cmd, Air Materiel\n                                          Command\n                         C. P. CABELL\n                         Major General, USAF\n                         Director of Intelligence, Office of\n                           Deputy Chief of Staff, Operations\n                                          Dispatched\n                                          11-4\nNote: C/S #1, 2, 3 + 4 are TS                        Gaining.\nTS 2-3931, and are filed\nin TS Central file bin a cy of this ltr", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "27d979887f391dd74b955023e994cad80075c38d1bc882ab3edcd71a805d82db", "output_sha256": "38843802d8ad43bf8397319326ed1d18eff6a1ef1d7d5a7a3f78515e1c23cc48", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:40.737970+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p3", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 3, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "11-214\n\nSECRET\n\nDEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\nHEADQUARTERS UNITED STATES AIR FORCE\nWASHINGTON\n\n3 NOV 1948\n\n\nSUBJECT: Flying Object Incidents in the United States\n\nTO:     Commanding General, Air Materiel Command\n        Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n        Dayton, Ohio\n\n\n        1.  By letter dated 30 December 1947 from the Director of\nResearch and Development, Headquarters USAF, your Headquarters\nwas required to establish Project \"SIGN\".\n\n        2.  The conclusion appears inescapable that some type of\nflying object has been observed.  Identification and the origin\nof these objects is not discernible to this Headquarters.  It is\nimperative, therefore, that efforts to determine whether these\nobjects are of domestic or foreign origin must be increased until\nconclusive evidence is obtained.  The needs of national defense\nrequire such evidence in order that appropriate countermeasures\nmay be taken.\n\n        3.  In addition to the imperative need for evidence to permit\ncountermeasures, is the necessity of informing the public as to\nthe status of the problem.  To date there has been too little data\nto present to the public.  The press, however, is about to take it\ninto its own hands and demand to be told what we do or do not know\nabout the situation.  Silence on our part will not long be accept-\nable.\n\n        4.  Request immediate information as to your conclusions to\ndate and your recommendations as to the information to be given\nto the press.  Your recommendation is requested also as to\nwhether that information should be offered to the press or with-\nheld until it is actively sought by the press.\n\n        BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                        C.P. Cabell\n\n                        C. P. CABELL\n                        Major General, USAF\n                        Director of Intelligence, Office of\n                        Deputy Chief of Staff, Operations\n\n\n                T-73017\n\nSECRET\n\n238", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b1ddfeff2dd8437b56c60732dad9e0ff03b4d8fcdac87451f8a964bf73c0e5c9", "output_sha256": "b1ddfeff2dd8437b56c60732dad9e0ff03b4d8fcdac87451f8a964bf73c0e5c9", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:42.983504+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p4", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 4, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "[Document appears to be the reverse/back side of a page, showing mirror-image bleed-through text from the front side. The text is not directly legible as printed content on this side. Visible elements include what appears to be a date stamp reading '1960 NOV 5' and a time stamp '09:37' visible in mirror image near the top, and at the bottom mirror-image text reading 'MEMORANDUM' and 'JOINT VIA STATE GWICK / SARAJEVO COMM' and 'GROSS VIA THE DEPARTMENT']", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b1ceae8d77670b9336ff39a551cf2f44d152a75c0d069254ecb91350f9b59616", "output_sha256": "b1ceae8d77670b9336ff39a551cf2f44d152a75c0d069254ecb91350f9b59616", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:44.300344+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p5", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 5, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COVER SHEET                    L-1078\n\na. *RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          b. CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                    DATE:\n\n                         TYPE:                    RESTRICTED\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n                                                        SUSPENSE\n\n                                                   DATE _______________\n\n                                                   ASGD BY ____________\n\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT    28 OCT 1948    ~~~         No.  DIN-  12935\n\nc.                  SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n                                                   DATE _______________\n\n                                                   NO. ________________\n\n\n\n\n\n             (Use other side this sheet for additional remarks)\n\nd.  TO    BR.    TO          TO    DIV.    TO          TO      DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN          UP          DOWN          UP          DOWN               UP\n         OIP-PP\n         OIP-FL  _____  }    _____ AFOIP _____  }      _____ ASST EXEC _____\n         OIP-SP\n\n  X      OIR-CO  [signature]\n         OIR-DD                                          _____ ASST EXEC _____\n         OIR-AA  _____  }    _____ AFOIR _____\n         OIR-SR\n         OIR-RC  _____                                  _____ EXECUTIVE _____\n\n\n         OAI-OA  _____\n         OAI-DA  _____  }    _____ AFOAI _____          _____ DIR/INT _____\n         OAI-AE  _____\n         OAI-AF  _____\n         OAI-SV  _____\n\n\n         PERS\n         M & R   _____  }    _____ ADMIN _____\n         B & F   _____\n         CABLE\n\n_____    ......  _____\n_____    ......  _____       X  Action\n_____    ......  _____\n                             √  Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR    29 OCT 1948          f.  DISPATCH          FILE  [ILLEGIBLE]\n    ACTION ASGD TO   GDO    DATE              DISPATCHED BY  Garwig    TO   EG-\n    SIGNED  [signature Leavitt]  DATE 15-11-48  DATE DISPATCHED  11-15-48   AMC\n\nAFOIN FORM 4\n22 SEP 48          PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.           9-1748, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bdde5036f7b84c30df1a32e7f902eccb998c489d1260d1629c09918657d45e0d", "output_sha256": "bdde5036f7b84c30df1a32e7f902eccb998c489d1260d1629c09918657d45e0d", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:48.582528+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p6", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 6, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g. TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE _______________\n\n                                                    NO. ________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nh. TO:                                              DATE _______________\n\n                                                    NO. ________________", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3450cb6491676fdfd854ba4d92983a895a39e2666f1946e892cebb66c592b3d8", "output_sha256": "3450cb6491676fdfd854ba4d92983a895a39e2666f1946e892cebb66c592b3d8", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:49.258417+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p7", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 7, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "See TS-2-3931\nfor Cover Sheet SECRET\nF MR of B561c\n\n                                                    8 Nov 48\n\nBasic ltr fr Hq USAF, 3 Nov 48 to CG, AMC, \"Flying Object Incidents in\n    the United States\"\n\n                    1st Ind                    MCIAT/ABD/amb\n\nHq AMC, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio. 8 Nov 48\n\nTO: Chief of Staff, United States Air Force, Washington 25, D. C., ATTN:\n        AFOIR\n\n        1. In attempting to arrive at conclusions as to the nature of unidentified flying object incidents in the United States, this Command has made\na study of approximately 180 such incidents. Data derived from initial reports have been supplemented by further information obtained from check\nlists submitted by mail, from interrogations of other field agencies, and\nby personal investigation by personnel of this Command in the case of incidents that seem to indicate the possibility of obtaining particularly\nsignificant information.\n\n        2. The objects described fall into the following general classification groups, according to shape or physical configuration:\n\n            a. Flat disc of circular or approximately circular shape.\n\n            b. Torpedo or cigar shaped aircraft, with no wings or fins visible\nin flight.\n\n            c. Spherical or balloon shaped objects.\n\n            d. Balls of light with no apparent form attached.\n\n        3. Some of the objects sighted have definitely been identified, upon\nfurther investigation, as weather or upper air scientific balloons of some\ntype. A great many of the round or balloon shaped objects indicated in\nparagraph 2c above are probably of the same nature, although in most cases,\ndefinite confirmation of that fact has been impossible to obtain.\n\n        4. Some of the objects have been identified as being astrophysical\nin nature. For example, in daylight sightings, the planet Venus has been\nreported as a round, silvery object at extremely high altitude. Action is\nbeing taken to obtain the services of a prominent astrophysicist as a consultant, to study all of the incidents to determine whether some can be\nidentified as meteors, planets or other manifestations of astral bodies.\n\n        5. Arrangements for accomplishing a study of the psychological problems\ninvolved in this project are being made in coordination with the Aero-Medical\nLaboratory at this Headquarters. The possibility that some of the sightings\nare hallucinations, optical illusions or even deliberate hoaxes has been considered.\n    Filz - 6Jan 48\n    Maj Jones                    F1-\n\n                                    2\n\n                               SECRET\n\n                                                              T-73017", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5219608f55ad93201965ff40115f4505637b9bb5e0c17e3065142926d0fdf3bb", "output_sha256": "e3e7e0eeee0630cb2f4bb83c7b18ac09484cecddfe7dd121345a2b224802cfc9", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:51.943286+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p8", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 8, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET\n\n                                                      1st Ind\nBasic ltr fr Hq USAF, 3 Nov 48 to CG, AMC, \"Flying Object Incidents in\n  the United States\"\n\n     6. Although explanation of many of the incidents can be obtained from\nthe investigations described above, there remains a certain number of re-\nports for which no reasonable everyday explanation is available. So far,\nno physical evidence of the existence of the unidentified sightings has\nbeen obtained. Prominent scientists, including Dr. Irving Langmuir of the\nGeneral Electric Company, have been interviewed to determine whether they\ncould advance any reasonable explanation for characteristics exhibited by\nthe objects sighted. In an early interview, Dr. Langmuir indicated that\nthese incidents could be explained, but insufficient data were available\nat that time on which to base definite conclusions. It is planned to have\nanother interview with Dr. Langmuir in the near future to review all the\ndata now available, and it is hoped that he will be able to present some\nopinion as to the nature of many of the unidentified objects, particularly\nthose described as \"balls of light.\"\n\n     7. All information that has been made available to this Headquarters\nindicates that the discs, the cigar shaped objects, and the \"balls of light\"\nare not of domestic origin. Engineering investigation indicates that disc\nor wingless aircraft could support themselves in flight by aerodynamic means.\nIt is probable that the problems of stability and control could also be\nsolved for such aircraft. However, according to current aerodynamic theory\nin this country, aircraft with such configurations would have relatively\npoor climb, altitude and range characteristics with power plants now in\nuse.\n\n     8. The possibility that the reported objects are vehicles from another\nplanet has not been ignored. However, tangible evidence to support con-\nclusions about such a possibility are completely lacking. The occurrence\nof incidents in relation to the approach to the earth of the planets Mercury,\nVenus and Mars have been plotted. A periodic variation in the frequency of\nincidents, which appears to have some relation to the planet approach curves,\nis noted, but it may be purely a coincidence.\n\n     9. Reference is made to \"The Books of Charles Fort\" with an introduc-\ntion by Tiffany Thayer, published 1941, by Henry Holt & Co., New York, N. Y.\nIt appears that similar phenomena have been noted and reported for the past\ncentury or more.\n\n     10. In view of the above, the following conclusions are drawn:\n\n          a. In the majority of cases reported, observers have actually\nsighted some type of flying object which they cannot classify as an air-\ncraft within the limits of their personal experience.\n\n                              3\n\n                                                            T-73017\n\n                             SECRET", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cc95254f5878028267a491c4ac407eb2a6555e25ac0ebc75cbd098bb301f967b", "output_sha256": "0413b38295b0cb3afa9819e0872d2c2f5a26c27b3102e374fabc481bd5f6143e", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:54.714376+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p9", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 9, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET\n\n                                              1st Ind\nBasic ltr fr Hq USAF, 3 Nov 48 to CG, AMC, \"Flying Object Incidents in\n  the United States\"\n\n        b. There is as yet no conclusive proof that unidentified flying\nobjects, other than those which are known to be balloons, are real aircraft.\n\n        c. Although it is obvious that some types of flying objects have\nbeen sighted, the exact nature of those objects cannot be established until\nphysical evidence, such as that which would result from a crash, has been\nobtained.\n\n        11. It is not considered advisable to present to the press information\non those objects which we cannot yet identify or about which we cannot present any reasonable conclusions. In the event that they insist on some\nkind of a statement, it is suggested that they be informed that many of\nthe objects sighted have been identified as weather balloons or astral\nbodies, and that investigation is being pursued to determine reasonable\nexplanations for the others.\n\n        12. A report, summarizing the results obtained from analysis of the\ndata and a technical investigation of the engineering aspects of the objects\ndescribed, is nearly complete, and a copy will be forwarded to your Headquarters in the near future.\n\n        FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                              H. M. McCOY\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Intelligence Department\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                              4\n                           SECRET                              T-73017", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4040051abb7cfcd3ea037472dd6a1c52d19f11a2eb8981b43a46e60d4c71d7a6", "output_sha256": "7244d17aee9dcc8a1d16dba8ed806af8125112214afc6c5b63f290ce997f9f7a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:56.520211+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p10", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 10, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/dw/4544\n        RESTRICTED        12 Nov 48    15 Nov 48\n\nR/L fm Hq USAF, 27 Aug 48, subj:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\nAFOIR-CO-5 (1-10-78)          2nd Ind\n\nDept. of the Air Force, Hq USAF, Washington 25, D. C.\n\nTO:  Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air\n        Force Base, Wright Field, Ohio\n        ATTN:  MCIAXO-3\n\n     1.  Basic letter's reference to the contacting of the Air Transport\nAssociation was with the understanding that such arrangements were to be\nmade, or had been made, by Project SIGN personnel.  This was the decision\nmade as a result of the conference held at this Headquarters 27 July 1948.\nJANAP 146 was forwarded merely as being of possible value in the estab-\nlishment of a direct reporting system by airline pilots.\n\n     2.  It is therefore requested that Project Sign personnel make ar-\nrangements to enlist the services of the Air Transport Association in\norder to develop a system whereby U. S. airline pilots could make flash\nreports of any unusual aerial sightings direct to your Headquarters.\n\n     3.  In this connection it is suggested that the \"Essential Elements\nof Information\" inclosed with 1st Indorsement may prove too detailed for\npractical use by airline pilots in forwarding initial reports to your\nHeadquarters.\n\n                    BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                                        /s/\n                                ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n                                Colonel, USAF\n                                Chief, Collection Branch\n1 Incl:                         Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n  n/c                           Directorate of Intelligence\n     [handwritten: orig]\n\n\nRef:  Ltr fm Hq USAF, 27 Aug 48, subject as above. (Already in file)\n      1st Ind fm Hq AMC, MCIAXO-3, 26 Oct 48, same subject.\n\n\n              [handwritten: .13191 JANAP]\n\n\n\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "88122f305d6f7b2b62711b24421323c5fa3c0593edb0bea32226abb2d963a62e", "output_sha256": "88122f305d6f7b2b62711b24421323c5fa3c0593edb0bea32226abb2d963a62e", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:56:58.969186+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p11", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 11, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt.Col.Garrett/dw/4544\n26 Aug 1948\n\n27 Aug 48\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n                    27 AUG 1948\n\nSUBJECT:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\nTO     :  Commanding General\n          Air Material Command\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Wright Field, Ohio\n          ATTN:  MCI\n\n\n     1.  At the conference in this Headquarters 27 July 1948 on\nsubject project, it was agreed that the Air Transport Association\nwould be contacted in an effort to enlist the cooperation of United\nStates airlines in reporting sightings of unusual aerial phenomena\ndirect to your Command.\n\n     2.  The attached publication JANAP 146, although not specifically\ndeveloped by the Joint Communications-Electronics Committee for the\nreporting of \"flying disc\" sightings, is forwarded with the suggestion\nthat you may wish to consider its use for this purpose by commercial\nairline pilots.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n1 Incl:                    ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n  JANAP 146                Colonel, USAF\n                           Chief, Collection Branch\n                           Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                           Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n                                D\n                               [ILLEGIBLE]\n                              27 AUG 1948\n\nFILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7b060a33233416d2976ae91ccb04f29c031625a0dd0b2c57d7823bcce41a72d8", "output_sha256": "7b060a33233416d2976ae91ccb04f29c031625a0dd0b2c57d7823bcce41a72d8", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:00.538661+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p12", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 12, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\nAMC\nSubject:  \"Project 'Sing'\"\n\n                    1st Ind          MCIAXO-3/RRS/ej\n\nHq AMC Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, 26 Octo 48\n\nTO:  Chief of Staff, United States Air Force, Washington 25, D. C.\n     ATTN:  AFOIR-CO-5\n\n     1.  With reference to paragraph 1 above, the efforts to enlist\nthe cooperation of United States airlines in reporting sightings of\nunusual aerial phenomena directly to this Command are greatly appre-\nciated.\n\n     2.  This Headquarters further requests cooperation in effecting\ndistribution and use by commercial airlines of an \"Essential Elements of\nInformation\" check list, copies of which are inclosed.  This list may\nbe used as a supplement to the publication JANAP 146, developed by the\nJoint Communications-Electronics Committee for the reporting of \"flying\ndisc\" sightings.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                              /s/ W. E. Goll\n                              for H. M. McCOY\n1 Incl:                           Colonel, USAF\n  6 cys EEI form                  Chief, Intelligence Department\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fb8e573af5a0a9f13da9826759f16a2d3835568a58b6f2dd26d0f41f515a6671", "output_sha256": "d77a8f116e49818bd07434f536ef254e5e8997ea0e2810d63f26d8379e92eb67", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:02.027764+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p13", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 13, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "Investigation by United States Air Force of reports on so-called flying saucers has led to the identification of some of these objects as weather balloons and astral bodies. The investigation of such reported incidents is continuing at the Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio.\n\n\n\n\nIncl. 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "04d97c9fb04bd6d7359d8d3faa0ea7f1ffb53b9c7059ab543cc5328a4091a9ee", "output_sha256": "9f8c7d1d6056d8784d91074067d87015238f3f776a4b31969e75d1cffb284986", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:03.009087+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p14", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 14, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "DATE: 8 Nov 48          SECRET\nFROM: OIN\n\n                                    SUSPENSE DATE:        NO.:\n                                      22 Nov 48          [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                          HLS\n                                    FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\n                                         809 Flying\nTYPE: 1st Ind to Gen S Mil Ltr of\nSMRY: 3 Nov 48                            Discs\n\n        FLYING OBJECT INCIDENTS IN THE US. (Cover Sheet\n          fr OIN)\n        Iss\n        DO NOT REMOVE THIS COPY\n\nTO:              TO:              TO:              TO:              TO:\n  OAI              OIN              DI[ILLEGIBLE]                              \nDATE:            DATE:            DATE:            DATE:            DATE:\n  12 Nov 48        11-19-48         1-5-49\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:  FILED (PLACE):           OTHER ACTION:\n\n\n                                                                    HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "90c28ba3dce69ae43475c52ce5d3ae70c3972fae3f446bb781d371a2ee75115a", "output_sha256": "24e51019c9246b42c6c300efbb9241c0c037a0af755c8b8fda1f7f832aaa8115", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:04.392021+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p15", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 15, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\n*                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST                    b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:   Hq. AMC          DATE:   8 Nov 48\n\n                         TYPE: 1st Ind to Gen. C.              SECRET\n                         Mil Ltr of 3 Nov 48\n\nSUMMARY:\n                                                                 SUSPENSE\n\n   Flying Object Incidents in the United States                DATE  22 Nov 48\n                                                               ASGD BY  Col Sibley /ol\n                                                               NO.   OIN =  18078\n\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT   Del'd to AFOIN by Col. McCoy in\n                        person\n\nc.  OAI:              SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n                                                               DATE  11 Nov\n   Would appreciate your\n   verbal comments at                                           NO.    1\n   an early date.\n                    cpc\n              (Use other side this sheet for additional remarks)\n\nd.   TO    BR.    TO              TO    DIV.    TO              TO    DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN          UP             DOWN          UP              DOWN              UP\n\n     OIP-PP                                                      ✓  ASST EXEC  [signature]\n     OIP-FL               ______  AFOIP  ______\n     OIP-SP\n\n     OIR-CO\n     OIR-DD\n     OIR-AA               ______  AFOIR  ______                    ASST EXEC  4/8\n     OIR-SR                                                                   1700 [signature]\n     OIR-RC\n                                                               [signature] EXECUTIVE [signature]\n     OAI-OA\n   ✓ OAI-DA   [initials]      X  W   AFOAI   W              cpc  DIR/INT  [signature]\n     OAI-AE\n     OAI-AF\n     OAI-SV\n\n     PERS\n     M & R\n     B & F            ______  ADMIN  ______\n     CABLE\n\n     .......        ☒  Action                               (Page # 158\n     .......                                                    (343)\n     .......        ✓  Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR ___________      f.  DISPATCH ____________ FILE  /DMZ\n    ACTION ASGD TO __________ DATE _______   DISPATCHED BY  DP    TO\n    SIGNED _________________  DATE _______   DATE DISPATCHED    7-6-49\n\nAFOIN FORM 4\n22 SEP 48                    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.               9-1748.AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5a58d80b4a63fc11fe7d5f6fe8ae822dd4904ebf50df5aea823ea78f559265d1", "output_sha256": "5a58d80b4a63fc11fe7d5f6fe8ae822dd4904ebf50df5aea823ea78f559265d1", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:07.007754+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p16", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 16, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g. TO: Chief D.A.     SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                          DATE  15 Nov\nFor verbal comment to\nChief, OAI o/e 17 NOV.              NO.   2\n                        [signature]\n                            OAI\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nh. TO: General Cabell                          DATE      19 Nov 48\n\n     1.   AFOAI recommends that no statement be released  NO.      3\nto the press on flying object incidents until press demands make such release\nimperative.\n\n     2.   If the statement to the press is required it is recommended that Incl 2\nform the basis of the statement.\n\n     3.   We are prepared for the verbal comments at your convenience.\n\n                                    [signature]\n                                        for\n                                    Gen Moore\n                                              13018", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8df51548752edc640dd336fd48c214da519148f0e6ddab3e49c52e17af29252f", "output_sha256": "8df51548752edc640dd336fd48c214da519148f0e6ddab3e49c52e17af29252f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:08.343783+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p17", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 17, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt.Col.Garrett/ab/4544\n28 Oct. 48\n\nB/L fm Mrs. Ruth Shook, dtd 14 Sep. 48, subj: Request for Information\n    Concerning Strategic Aircraft.\n\nAFOIR-CO-5 (1-10-64)          2nd Ind.          28 OCT 1948\n\nDept. of the Air Force, Hq. USAF, Washington 25, D. C.\n\nTO:  Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson\n         Air Force Base, Wright Field, Ohio.\n     ATTN:  MCI\n\n     Forwarded as a matter pertaining to your Command.\n\nFOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                         ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Collection Branch\n                         Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n      MRS. SHOOK, RUTH\n\n\n\n\n                                          FILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "239c99668c0eeb0a5971deb0ead86eb819d8e9b49712b9b531819fb3d78d7d1d", "output_sha256": "c2ef10697f9b7dcd3fd5bef3b96de840472f570e8ef5dfee2e5f61ec5d9330c7", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:09.894702+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p18", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 18, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "\"C-O-P-Y\"\n\n                                        Hiawassee, Ga.\n                                        Sept. 14, 1948\n\n\nThe War Dept.\nWashington, D. C.\n\nGentlemen,\n\n     Please inform me what those things are that the people in North\nGeorgia have been seeing flying through the sky.\n\n     They are round and long some what like a giant cigar.  They\nhave a motor that sounds like a motorcycle. If they are foreign machine\nyou should know about it.\n\n     If they are American military machines I do not need to know\nabout them.\n\n                              Yours truly,\n\n                              s/  Mrs. Ruth Shook\n\nP.S.  The Atlanta Constitution stated that no one in Atlanta knew\n      what they were.\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Request for information concerning strange aircraft.\n\nAGAO-C 095 Shook\nRuth Mrs. (14 Sep 48)          1st Ind          PRW/wcw/1D-860\n\nAGO, DEPT OF THE ARMY, Washington 25, D. C., 13 October 1948\n\nTO:  Chief of Staff, United States Air Force, Washington 25, D. C.\n\n                         s//E.F. P.\n\n                         E.F. Pegraw", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b7dd12cb006043e54d623bcfb287e17205f63f75d7fdee85ce3468afb7058ed6", "output_sha256": "5fafde2e2c37868cc34929e3bb749aa75a8ed532d450f47785e442b950b2c715", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:11.442092+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p19", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 19, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "DATE:    13 Oct 48                    SUSPENSE DATE:          NO.:\nFROM     AG\n\n                                        FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\n\nTYPE:    1st Ind\n\nSMRY:\n        Request for information concerning strange\n        aircraft.                (Route #1, Bx 27)\n        [REDACTED]B/L fr Mrs. Ruth Shook, Hiawassee, Ga. dtd 14\n        Sep 48.\n                    BKS                 ekp\n\nTO:           TO:           TO:           TO:           TO:\nSPR           OIN\nDATE:         DATE:         DATE:         DATE:         DATE:\n15 Oct 48     21 Oct\n\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:    FILED (PLACE):         OTHER ACTION:\n2nd Ind        CG AMC                            29/10/48\n                                                   