cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5796aff5148682d534168e818b33cc3b30cc47c19cda25069bc21c877683d0c4", "output_sha256": "74a1aadcc5531340910bf98affba61c759e0e1cef33087268109a281903f5f1a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:16.065244+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p22", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 22, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "See LtR-12 Jan 50 (Reas)          AFOIR-CO/Lt.Col.Garrett/as/4544\n                                        27 October 1948\n\n               SECRET\n\n                              280449\n\n                         2 3 OCT 1948\n\nAFOIR-CO\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR THE DIRECTOR OF CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE\n\nSUBJECT:  Unidentified Aerial Phenomena\n\n     1.  The Air Materiel Command is currently engaged in an intelligence investigation of all reported unidentified aerial phenomena.\n\n     2.  To date, no concrete identity of any of the reported objects\nhas been received.  Similarly, the origin of the so-called \"flying\ndiscs\" remains obscure.  The possibility exists that some of the sighted\nobjects are of domestic origin, i.e., unrecognized configurations of\nsome of our latest aeronautical attainments, or that they are objects\nnot readily recognized by the public - test vehicles in various stages\nof development, etc.\n\n     3.  It is requested that your Agency submit to the Directorate of\nIntelligence any available evidence that may come to your attention which\nmight serve to indicate that these objects have a domestic origin.\n\n          FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                         GEORGE D. GARRETT, JR.\n                         Lieutenant Colonel, USAF\n                         Acting Chief, Collection Branch\n                         Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n          1040.9  Central Intel Agency\n\n\n               DISPATCHED BY CIG COURIER\n          OIN NO 335-B   DATE  23 OCT 1948\n                         1155 copy\n\n               SECRET", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0fc9523493b5ce15a911644f6e27483fbd450bab03e9a554c4ae05f4eb9766e0", "output_sha256": "16795be4fdfbef68dfd971cd0669d79e57350ea8a2d542c470ba4934b3d17838", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:18.050443+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p23", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 23, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "[REDACTED]\nDATE: 7 Oct 48                    SUSPENSE DATE:        NO.:\nFROM: AMC, Ohio\n\n                                   FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\n\nTYPE: ltr    T-63070\nSMRY: Project \"SIGN\"\n      1 Incl\n      mjp\n\n\nTO:    OIN     TO:          TO:          TO:          TO:\n\nDATE:          DATE:        DATE:        DATE:        DATE:\n       11 Oct 48\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:   FILED (PLACE):        OTHER ACTION:\n\n                                                           HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fb8fd1b5d279618f4c055b8eb3289c355d2c07fb3fabec2175ee06eea7f1252a", "output_sha256": "fb8fd1b5d279618f4c055b8eb3289c355d2c07fb3fabec2175ee06eea7f1252a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:19.085136+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p24", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 24, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET\n\n                    Headquarters\n               AIR MATERIEL COMMAND\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n               Wright Field, Ohio\n\n                    7 October 1948\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\nTO:       Chief of Staff, USAF\n          Washington 25, D.C.\n          Director of Intelligence\n          Deputy Chief of Staff, Operations\n          ATTN: AFOIR\n\n\n     It is requested that your office forward the attached letter to\nthe Central Intelligence Agency, Washington 25, D.C.\n\n     FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n                              /s/ H.M. McCOY\n                                  Colonel, USAF\n                                  Chief of Intelligence\n\n\n1 Incl\n  Ltr to CIA\n\n\n\n\n                              DECLASSIFIED\n                         E.O. 13526 Sec 3.3\n                         NW 34267\n                         DOC    NARA DATE 5-4-16\n\n\n\n\nSECRET", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2d022bd5818990c40d6a262eb14d76665a3a3dcfd2f17837c19d252ddc1f51dd", "output_sha256": "13ee3cac9303027aeeab633ca6468e6c4524b932c374965ac399d49e46206428", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:20.518264+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p25", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 25, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET\n\nMCIAXO-3                                    MCIAXO-3/SZH/aw\n\n                                            OCT 7  1948\n\n          Central Intelligence Agency\n          Washington, D. C.\n\n\n                    SUBJECT:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\n          Gentlemen:\n\n               This Headquarters is currently engaged in an\n          intelligence investigation of all reported unidentified\n          aerial phenomena.  To date, no concrete evidence\n          as to the exact identity of any of the reported objects\n          has been received.  Similarly, the origin of the so-\n          called \"flying discs\" remains obscure.  The possibility\n          exists that some of the sighted objects are of domestic\n          origin, i. e., unrecognized configurations of some of\n          our latest aeronautical attainments, or that they are\n          objects not readily recognized by the public - test\n          vehicles in various stages of development, etc.\n\n               Where security regulations will permit, it is re-\n          quested that your office submit to Hq, Air Materiel\n          Command, Wright-Patterson AF Base, Wright Fld., Ohio,\n          Attn:  MCIAXO-3, THRU:  Chief of Staff, USAF, Washington,\n          25, D. C., DIRECTOR OF INTEL, Deputy Chief of Staff,\n          Operations, ATTN:  AFOIR, any available evidence which\n          might serve to indicate that these objects have a domestic\n          origin.\n\n               Your cooperation in so doing might greatly assist\n          in identifying our own domestic developments from\n          possible inimical foreign achievements.\n\n                              Very truly yours\n\n\n                              H. M. McCOY\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief of Intelligence\n\n                                                        T-63070-A\n\nSECRET", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a209c618d01e90f75d3c7d220a4bac3c2ea0f3910fcedc13bb157b0750a40730", "output_sha256": "8a09319657385e7e4a270c7b49083c5cba1a71ccd164168627c55646b1ae88c6", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:22.553248+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p26", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 26, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COVER SHEET -                                    L-10-29\n\n*                    *\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                          DATE:\n\n                               TYPE:                        SECRET\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n                                                           SUSPENSE\n\n                                                  DATE   21 Oct 48\n\n            