  Dispatched\n              11-12-48\n              — [handwritten signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3326480835e2620cfe0c99ea27f986696b4ac79f328647ef1a99493bfc868cba", "output_sha256": "acde27bbbf92d2083bce2cdd386b996e2c3066b929c5396302d9b334b016c455", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:45.041053+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p39", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 39, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "19 Oct 48\n\nSubj:   Project \"SIGN\"\n\n                                        EW\n\n             1st Ind                    MCIAXO-3/HWS/dw\n\nHq AMC, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio   OCT 19 1948\n\nTO:  Chief of Staff, United States Air Force, Washington 25, D. C.\n     ATTN:  AFOIR-CO-5 (L-10-1)\n\n     Request to investigate the sighting reported in letter attached\nas Inclosure 1 to basic communication, has been forwarded to Branch\nIntelligence Office, 112th CIC Detachment, New Orleans, Louisiana.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n                                              X over\n1 Incl          /s/ W. R. CLINGERMAN\n  w/d               Colonel, USAF\n                    Actg Chief, Intelligence Department\n\n\n006.9 Flying Discs", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "96365da227de583f0cfb45f9759a634653a13f85ec30b3ec36bc1263818343cb", "output_sha256": "96365da227de583f0cfb45f9759a634653a13f85ec30b3ec36bc1263818343cb", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:57:46.240977+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p40", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 40, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt.Col.Garrett/ab/61067\n6 Oct. 48\n\n7 Oct 48\n\n800.9 Flying Discs\n\nAFOIR-