t": "g.  TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE  ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.   ___________________\n\n\n\n\nh.  TO:                                             DATE  ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.   ___________________\n\n\n\n\n8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4f588e724a8dd7fb917cdd4dcee3e8b77ed84ff76e2a890474481d68a15d6cbd", "output_sha256": "850140203caefcc9e1dca641cdb59859ea4f528f2698e89ce092f744cd744b04", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:58:12.326027+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p56", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 56, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt.Col.Garrett/as/4544\n9 August 1948\n\n\n                                                    9 AUG 1948\n\nAFOIR-CO-5(L-S-31)\n\nSUBJECT: Project \"SIGN\"\n\nTO:      Commanding General\n         Air Materiel Command\n         Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n         Wright Field, Ohio\n         ATTN: MCI\n\n     1. Attached civilian communication is forwarded as a matter\npertaining to your Command.\n\n     2. This letter has been acknowledged by the Adjutant General,\nDepartment of the Army, but not by this Headquarters. It is assumed\nthat your Command will make proper acknowledgement.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                   ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n1 incl                             Colonel, USAF\n  Ltr fr J. Jamnicky               Chief, Collection Branch\n  dtd 9 July 1948 w/2 Incls.      Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n            w/orig                 Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n                    o 95. JAMNICKY, JOHN, JR.\n\n\n\n\nFILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f97df5c7f349fcecf2b468dcbc2a911ab80b378a199b1a291598eae16252796c", "output_sha256": "ef5eb1f86affd11b69fece683adbf9ef5dea7491fb41dc46794d94861892ab0e", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:58:13.884619+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p57", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 57, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COPY\n\n                                        Box 227\n                                        Dravasburg, Pa\n                                        9 July 1948\n\nUS War Department\nWashington, D.C.\n\nTO WHOM IT MAY CONCERN:\n\nDear Sir:\n\n     On the Fourth of July (July 4, 1948) my wife and I were sitting\non a bench on our lawn and we were watching the stars, planes, etc.\nAt 11:15 P.M. D.S.T. we saw something very strange.\n\n     We thought we saw a star moving. There was a light in the sky\nthe same color and size of a star and it was moving. We decided it was\na plane but it made no noise. We soon changed our minds because this\n\"thing\" moved across the sky then stopped for about 8 seconds then\nchanged its course a bit and went straight and stopped again for about\n5 seconds, changed its course a bit and went straight for awhile and\nstopped again this time for at least 15 seconds then it went across the\nsky a little ways and disappeared completely. When this \"thing\" stopped\nin the sky, if you didn't know where it was at, you could not tell it\nfrom a star as the resemblance was identical to a star.\n\n     After reading in the paper on July 8, 1948, about two women seeing\n\"Flying Saucers\" in the day light July 8, I believe I saw a \"Flying\nSaucer\" or something in the night July 4, because I know it was no star\nor an airplane because neither can travel and stop in the air like this\n\"thing\" did. I live about 2½ miles from these women who have seen the\n\"disc\" in the daylight.\n\n     Has the War Department any comments on these strange \"discs?\" They\nare now reported in the heart of the steel industry. \"PITTSBURGH DISTRICT\".\n\n                              Yours\n                              /s/ John Jamnicky, Jr.\n                                  Box 227\n                                  Dravasburg, Pa.\n\n2 Incls.\n  Newspaper Clipping dtd 8 July 48\n  Chart", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "34bd596b685fc250cd147a84990148b509bab5ba8e8e720e93a8a10400865631", "output_sha256": "3b866cf0b61a2642d9e0103f28962c91707efa3f944246ee971831f43c8d49d2", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:58:17.389154+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p58", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 58, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AF HQ - 12 (REV. 10 NOV 1947)\n          •HEADQUARTERS UNITED STATES AIR FORCE\n              ROUTING SLIP\nTO:\n1. OFFICE                                              DATE\n         AFOIP                                          4\n  ATTENTION                                            Aug\n         Lt Col Sheley\n2. OFFICE                                              DATE\n\n  ATTENTION\n\n3. OFFICE                                              DATE\n\n  ATTENTION\n\nFOR:  FOLLOWING  ACTION(S)  AS  CHECKED\n\n  COORDINATION          NOTE AND RETURN          INFORMATION\n  NECESSARY ACTION      RECOMMENDATION           FILE\n  SEE OR PHONE ME       APPROVAL                 SIGNATURE\n\nCOMMENT\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFROM:\nJACKSON M. PHIPPS\nOFFICE                              [ILLEGIBLE]    ROOM NO.\n     Major, USAF\n     Administrative Assistant\nINDIVIDUAL                                        PHONE\n     Air Information Division                      760\n\n          