                      \n\n\n\n                                                                    7-1187,AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5aa1543f9e8aaf95f505c5df7b2041545f94646d9646ce8510c841aa51f70f26", "output_sha256": "0bfcb4111f0ad62cfe260ad4cdb567beb1780e1fa7c2864585a0e0bb9b7cf930", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:00.459808+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p82", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 82, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/jh/4544\n                    2 June 48\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Flying Discs                    2 June 1948\n\nTO:       Commanding General\n          Air Materiel Command\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Dayton, Ohio\n          ATTN:  MCI\n\n     Forwarded as a matter pertaining to your Command.  Request acknowledgement be made to Mr. Bonneville.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                         GEORGE D. GARRETT, JR.\n1 Incl                   Lieutenant Colonel, USAF\n  Ltr frm Wm. Bonneville  Acting Chief, Collection Branch\n  dtd 23 May 48           Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                          Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nmailed\n  6-3-48\n  pes", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0c31e6ad14aa03dac0545b9c5cfbea52fd9ff4bb4d330abfdc19260e84728d84", "output_sha256": "4f7b916fa85354bc19c5ce963191a9f38d78ce6b0b281a216ac7e5c6616539a3", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:01.664904+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p83", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 83, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt/Col.Garrett/as/4544\n            21 May 1948\n\n[REDACTED]\n\nAFOIR-CO-5 (5-61)                    21 May 1948\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Flying Discs\n\nTO:       Commanding General\n          Air Materiel Command\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Dayton, Ohio\n          Attn:  MCI\n\n     Attached is a report of a flying disc sighting by an officer\non duty in the Offensive Air Branch of this Directorate.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n                         ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n                         Colonel, USAF\n1 Incl.                  Chief, Collection Branch\n                         Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[REDACTED]\n\nPLEASE RETURN TO DIR of INTELL.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "113f3f192ba48510b965f61de42e8fc29ed7311e3ca851edcace0852f1defc98", "output_sha256": "113f3f192ba48510b965f61de42e8fc29ed7311e3ca851edcace0852f1defc98", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:02.994273+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p84", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 84, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COPY\n\n                                        4 May 1948\n\nMEMO FOR LT. COL. THOMAS\n\n     The undersigned officer was participating as pilot on a local\nflight on Friday, 30 April 1948, in Navy aircraft, SNJ Buno 90731.  At\napproximately 1015 local time, at an altitude of about 5500 feet, on a\nmagnetic heading of about 180 degrees, just south of Anacostia Naval\nAir Station, an object was sighted ahead to the left and about 1000\nfeet below at a distance of about 1 mile.  The object resembled a\nyellow sphere estimated at 25-40 feet in diameter.  The flight path of the\nobject was in approximately a South to North direction (despite upper\nwind from North Northwest) and apparently followed a constant altitude.\nPilot did not pursue object further because it was entering the\nprohibited flying area, U.S. Capitol, White House Area.\n\n     The object appeared to pilot to be a yellow (or bright colored)\nballoon and attracted attention principally because of its flight path.\nNo external fittings or attachments were observed on the object.  The\nspeed of the object was estimated to about 100 MPH.\n\n                              /s/ Marcus L. Lowe, Jr.\n                                  Lt. Cdr. US Navy", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c222ddbde9283ffbb1df6d1236e548ffdc3dd8c72b13976061e610aa683ffb59", "output_sha256": "78500599ae93f0d14bdaa1d381d008619c0918ded81db948cc4c3431a9d45d07", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:04.549501+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p85", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 85, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET                    5-61\n\n*                    *\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST                    b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:  AFOAI-AE                    DATE:    10 May 48\n\n                                   TYPE:  R/S w/longhand memo\n\nSUMMARY:  Memo from Lt. Commander Lowe for Lt. Colonel\n          Thomas re object sighted on flight South of\n          Anacostia Naval Air Station, 30 April 48.\n\n          (forwarded to Gen Cabell by R/S from Col Walsh,              SUSPENSE\n          AFOAI-AE)\n                                                              DATE _______________\n\n                                                              ASGD BY ____________\n\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT  OIR    11 May 48                      NO. ________________\n\nc.                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n   OIR-CO                                                     DATE _______________\n      Here we go again. Will you send\n      this to AMC  W&E                                        NO. ________________\n\n\n\n                USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.  TO    BR.    TO         TO    DIV.    TO         TO      DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN          UP         DOWN          UP         DOWN               UP\n    _____ OIP-PP  _____\n    _____ OIP-FL  _____  }   _____ AFOIP  _____  }   _____ ASST EXEC _____\n    _____ ADMIN   _____\n                                                                        *\n  X       OIR-CO  [initials]                                _____ ASST EXEC _____\n    _____ OIR-DD  _____  }  W&E  AFOIR  _____  }\n    _____ OIR-AA  _____    11 May\n    _____ OIR-CM  _____                                     _____ EXECUTIVE _____\n    _____ OIR-RC  _____\n\n    _____ OAI-OA  _____                                     _____ DIR/INT  _____\n    _____ OAI-DA  _____\n    _____ OAI-AE  _____  }   _____ AFOAI  _____\n    _____ OAI-AF  _____\n    _____ OAI-SV  _____\n\n    _____ OCI-IS  _____\n    _____ OCI-RR  _____  }   _____ AFOCI  _____\n    _____ OCI-CI  _____\n\n    _____ ....... _____\n    _____ ....... _____       X   Action\n    _____ ....... _____\n    _____ ....... _____       ✓   Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR  12 May      1948  DATE      f.  DISPATCH  mail     FILE\n    ACTION ASGD TO  CDA       1948  DATE          DISPATCHED BY  O/2      TO  AMC\n    SIGNED  Parrett           DATE 21-5          DATE DISPATCHED  5/21/48\n\n                                                                    8-3477,AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0f1e8cfbfce6d1c2aed5f62982978c062d96ca7728132a81c59164d075487942", "output_sha256": "f778616050a87bcd3a29702e09f781d7b475c18a1fdd20172f0d1753645bc562", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:07.840527+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p86", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 86, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g.  TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\nh.  TO:                                             DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\n8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6661618ac931720a9055aa7e767b2d0a809c78e94594cd2344b7c3dd9f0c6b13", "output_sha256": "c796e3c0afe235dd4a201411700e15086a2fa6ed3380ace16ac788a38478e822", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:08.562039+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p87", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 87, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET                AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/6282\n                           12 May 48    18 May 48\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n                                    13 MAY 1948\n\n     SUBJECT:  Flying Discs\n\n     TO:       Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-\n                    Patterson Air Force, Dayton, Ohio\n               ATTN: MCI\n\n          Forwarded for your information.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n     1 Incl.              GEORGE D. GARRETT, JR.\n       ID No. 456982      Lieutenant Colonel, USAF\n       (4 copies)         Acting Chief, Collection Branch —\n                          Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                          Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     mailed\n     5/13/48\n     POS\n\n\n                           SECRET\n\nFILM COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "10dbff460b903fe1de4346ae2d0c89165c33ce72b35faa5da5e80f4eef3f2781", "output_sha256": "a5c720f0e2cb076fd1c00397fd41b4b3f9c9e6136811d60d9be73c6b09c35e04", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:09.968386+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p88", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 88, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544\n6 May 48\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n\nSUBJECT: Flying Discs                    [ 6 MAY 1948 ]\n\nTO:        Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-\n           Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio\n           ATTN:  MCI\n\n          1.  The attached correspondence from Miss Ethel Evans,\nof Wildwood, New Jersey, pertaining to Flying Discs, is\nforwarded for your information.\n\n          2.  Attached herewith is copy of this Headquarters'\ndirect reply to her letter of 23 April.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                   GEORGE D. GARRETT, JR.\n                                   Lieutenant Colonel, USAF\n2 Incls.                           Acting Chief, Collection Branch\n  1 - cy of ltr to                 Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n        Ethel Evans dtd 6 May      Directorate of Intelligence\n  2 - ltr fm Ethel Evans\n        dtd 23 Apr. w/incls.\n\n\n\n\n          Vogt. Evans, Mrs. Ethel\n\n\nFILM COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8071b50341c993e3ba68e01635d64291080eb3a29f697ff034c17f41802f956f", "output_sha256": "5d2ba16d8bd5234ff9262f6b21f98500ead3adbb9362b8c704efb72ed66b29d1", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:11.537877+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p89", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 89, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544 - 6 May 48\nRewrtn:  AFOIR/Col Mallory/mcb/6548 - 10 May 48\n\n\n                                    12 MAY 1948\n\n\nMrs. Ethel Evans\nPost Office Box 119\nWildwood, New Jersey\n\nDear Mrs. Evans:\n\n        Your letter of April 23rd to Mr. Symington, with its\ninclosures, has been referred to this office during his\ntemporary absence and we wish to thank you very much for\nyour patriotic interest.\n\n        We assure you, Mrs. Evans, that rather than being\ntreated lightly, your reports of information concerning\nunusual aerial phenomena have in every case been studied\nby those persons concerned with such matters.\n\n        We sincerely hope that you will continue to send any\nfurther reports of these sightings, should they occur, to\nthe Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\nDayton, Ohio.\n\n                              Very truly yours,\n\n\n\n                         JOEL E. MALLORY\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Acting Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\nCC:  Air Materiel Command", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cee5832c9a4ad7600fa4f2431f74e638a789e267806fbe52a567c1c54dd26b91", "output_sha256": "60655926b41ccc2b9b6d91f8ce09d457972d4d57e2e50a4794605a9b5278e083", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:13.330535+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p90", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 90, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544\n6 May 48\n\n\n                                        May 6, 1948\n\nMiss Ethel Evans\nPost Office Box 119\nWildwood, New Jersey\n\nDear Miss Evans:\n\n     Your letter of April 23rd to Mr. Symington, with\nits inclosures, has been referred to me during his\ntemporary absence, and I wish to thank you very much\nfor your patriotic interest.\n\n     I assure you, Miss Evans, that, rather than being\ntreated lightly, your reports of information concerning\nunusual aerial phenomena have in every case been studied\nby those persons concerned with such matters.\n\n     We sincerely hope that you will continue to send any\nfurther reports of these sightings, should they occur, to\nthe Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\nDayton, Ohio.\n\n                         Very truly yours,\n\n\n\n                         GEORGE D. GARRETT, JR.\n                         Lt. Colonel, USAF\n                         Acting Chief, Collection Branch\n                         Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n                                   rewritten\n\nFILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d77afa669c3a39e1346747eedd4e4123b1b05e69f4767dd1d3937dd52c70fe4d", "output_sha256": "d77afa669c3a39e1346747eedd4e4123b1b05e69f4767dd1d3937dd52c70fe4d", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:15.028085+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p91", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 91, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544\n6 May 48\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\n\nPROBLEM\n\n     1.  To reply direct to a Mrs. Ethel Evans of Wildwood, N. J., who\nwrote direct to Mr. Symington, under date of 23 April, concerning flying\ndiscs.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n     2.  This woman is an old friend.  She has been writing to just about\neverybody in the Government concerning the strange lights she has seen\nover the Jersey Coast.  Her Senator, President Truman, The F.B.I., AMC,\nand various radio commentators have been the objects of her attention\nfor some time.\n\n     3.  Her correspondence with AMC finally reached such a crescendo\nthat an officer was sent down to Wildwood especially to interview her.\nAfter talking with her, it was decided to pursue the matter no farther.\nTo play safe, however, the officer made arrangements with the Coast\nGuard Headquarters in Washington, in coordination with this Directorate,\nto report any unusual aerial phenomena to AMC.  As far as is known,\nnothing has come in from this official source.\n\nACTION\n\n     4.  Attached letter to MRS. Evans thanking her for her interest,\nand attached letter to AMC forwarding the correspondence for their\ninformation.\n\nCOORDINATION\n\n     None", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1284e0b541309992cbbdb4db3d6ede3ded4976aaf8ebbeb57b8c1a43f6b3506d", "output_sha256": "1284e0b541309992cbbdb4db3d6ede3ded4976aaf8ebbeb57b8c1a43f6b3506d", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:18.991654+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p92", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 92, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET                    5-26\n\n                    *                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST              b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                          DATE:  23 apr 48\n   Ethel Evans                 TYPE:  Ltr to Sec a7\n                                       w 5 Incls\nSUMMARY:\n                                                    SUSPENSE\n   Flying Saucers in Vicinity\n   of Wildwood, N.J.                          DATE  14 May 48\n                                             ASGD BY  7/6\n                                                      1432\n                                             NO.  011\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT          6 May 48\n\nc.                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n\n   Suspense DCS/O Tally 5/4                            DATE\n   Date 1400 - 17 May 48\n                                                        NO.\n\n   Secy a7 # 7138\n              USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.  TO   BR.   TO          TO    DIV.    TO              TO    DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN  UP               DOWN          UP               DOWN            UP\n      OIP-PP                                              7/6  ASST EXEC  7/5\n      OIP-FL\n      ADMIN    Gr.\n\n  X   OIR-CO\n      OIR-DD\n      OIR-AA              m/c AFOIR   M/DE               ASST EXEC\n      OIR-CM              3 May       7 May\n      OIR-RC\n                                                          EXECUTIVE\n      OAI-OA\n      OAI-DA                                              DIR/INT\n      OAI-AE              AFOAI\n      OAI-AF\n      OAI-SV\n\n      OCI-IS\n      OCI-RR              AFOCI\n      OCI-CI\n\n      .......\n      .......      X   Action\n      .......\n      .......      ✓   Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR   6  MAY 1948       f.  DISPATCH  7/6     FILE Ethel Evans\n    ACTION ASGD TO   GDB   DATE           DISPATCHED BY 011 1463  TO 19 AMC\n    SIGNED            DATE               DATE DISPATCHED  17 May 48\n\n                                                                        8-3477.AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bc5ba338cfb68543088e80c356c58e81b8dd5c5f4b4b319671b688d299ac6e79", "output_sha256": "bc5ba338cfb68543088e80c356c58e81b8dd5c5f4b4b319671b688d299ac6e79", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:21.427593+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p93", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 93, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g. TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                        DATE ___________________\n\n                                        NO.  ___________________\n\nh. TO:                                  DATE ___________________\n\n                                        NO.  ___________________\n\n8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a068708900169b85bc25b81ddcffc58a99fc246669256505fee40ae5f622b028", "output_sha256": "f25e472d8b6866a14980b7f188a067fe4e58f191c51417f7fc24ee88519741b0", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:22.269572+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p94", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 94, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/jh/4544\n                                        28 Apr 48\n\n           SECRET\n\n\nLtr frm Hq AMC, MCIAXD, dated 13 Apr 48, subject: \"Interrogation of\nHorten Brothers\"\n\nAFOIR-CO-5                    1st Ind.\n                                                    28 APR 1948\nDept. of the Air Force, Hq. USAF, Washington 25, D. C.\n\nTO:  Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force\n     Base, Dayton, Ohio\n     ATTN: MCIAXD\n\n\n     1.  This Headquarters has received no information, as yet, resulting\nfrom interview of subject brothers.\n\n     2.  As soon as received, it will be forwarded to your Headquarters.\n\n         BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                    ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Chief, Collection Branch\n                    Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                    Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n              ↓095. HORTEN, REIMAR\n\n\n\n\n\nReference:  Ltr frm Hq AMC, MCIAXD, dtd 13 Apr 48, subject as above.\n            Ltr frm JIOA, dtd 31 Mar 48, subject: \"German Scientists\n            (Civil), Reimar Horten.\"\n\n\n        [ILLEGIBLE signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6a77d87ca69db404917af3413b1bd9b516a50ba29b01499709bac44ff71fa94d", "output_sha256": "6cf57281f28722b10b221ce0ce3e3df50d4ce9c117fe2ea3b554eb34857763a5", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:24.339252+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p95", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 95, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "HEADQUARTERS\nAIR MATERIEL COMMAND\n\nMCIAXD                                          MCIAXD/HWS/dw\n                                                Wright Field, Dayton, Ohio\n\n                                                Apr 13, 1948\n                                                REFERENCE\n                                                A    4062\n\n          SUBJECT:  Interrogation of Horten Brothers\n\n\n          TO:       Chief of Staff\n                    United States Air Force\n                    Washington 25, D. C.\n                    ATTN:  AFOIR\n\n\n          It is requested that this Headquarters be advised of any\n     information available as a result of the interrogation of the\n     Horten Brothers, referred to in letter, your Headquarters,\n     AFOIR-CO-5, dated 24 February 1948, subject \"Flying Discs\".\n\n               FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                                          /S/ James J. Hansman, Lt. Col. USAF\n                                          for H. M. McCOY\n                                               Colonel, USAF\n                                               Chief of Intelligence", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1a3465fad378453787bd683b171e72f6be914d4fa736723eee84f389376ee672", "output_sha256": "f551e77f3a5239670945cd460d920e439fcfb2e4f373f274ab4f9263ecfcab24", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:26.255928+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p96", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 96, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COPY                    SECRET\n\n                    THE JOINT CHIEFS OF STAFF\n                      Washington 25, D. C.\n\nJoint Intelligence\n Objectives Agency                    31 March 1948\n\nJIOA 1068\n\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR Collection Branch, Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n               Attn:  Directorate of Intelligence\n\nSUBJECT:  German Scientists (Civil), Reimar Horten.\n\n     1.  Reference is made to the recent telephone request of Captain Macken\nthat Dr. Reimar Horten, allocated to the U.K on the U.K. 15th Civil List,\nbe made available to the Department of the Air Force for interview.\n\n     2.  The British Joint Services Mission has agreed to the interview of\nHorten by the Department of the Air Force at some future date.\n\n\n\n                              /S/ BOSQUET N. WEV\n                                  Captain, USN\n                                  Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     S[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6beae6d2471dda3f9ecdf0de977d1b047b1e59e0ce5a21b960ac55a5c88aba34", "output_sha256": "6beae6d2471dda3f9ecdf0de977d1b047b1e59e0ce5a21b960ac55a5c88aba34", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:27.550673+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p97", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 97, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET [REDACTED]\nDATE: 13 Apr 48          SUSPENSE DATE:          NO.:\nFROM: AMC, Wright Fld, Ohio                          261792\n                              FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\nTYPE:   ltr (RN # T-8411-B)\nSMRY:\n\n     Interrogation of Horten Brothers\n                  mft\n\n\n          1st Ind\n\nTO:          TO: AMC     TO:          TO:          TO:\n OIR\nDATE:        DATE: 28 Apr  DATE:        DATE:        DATE:\n14 Apr 48\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:   FILED (PLACE):          OTHER ACTION:\n\n                                                             HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e036c3afa4c4a9aee68ca9b30e191bc76de0594342dfb7e67f9ff534b989eddb", "output_sha256": "e036c3afa4c4a9aee68ca9b30e191bc76de0594342dfb7e67f9ff534b989eddb", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:28.673356+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p98", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 98, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET\n                                                                    A-4062\n        *                    *\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                          DATE:\n                                                              SECRET\n                               TYPE:\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n                                                         SUSPENSE\n\n                                                    DATE   22 April\n\n                                                    ASGD BY   DIR\n\n                                                    NO.    4-259\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT\n\nc.                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n\n                                                    DATE\n\n                                                    NO.\n\n\n\n\n              USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.   TO    BR.    TO            TO    DIV.    TO              TO    DIR/INT    TO\n     DOWN   UP                 DOWN          UP              DOWN              UP\n         OIP-PP\n         OIP-FL                        AFOIP                       ASST EXEC