26750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bbde7a987c68acebff49eb6d476d3b050158890435963107c93efd2d26523ee9", "output_sha256": "bbde7a987c68acebff49eb6d476d3b050158890435963107c93efd2d26523ee9", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:31.889607+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p100", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 100, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/jh/4544\n                    16 Feb 48   24 Feb 48\n\n         SCN\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n                                        24 FEB 1948\n\nSUBJECT:  Flying Discs\n\nTO    :  Commanding General\n          Air Materiel Command\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Dayton, Ohio\n          ATTN:  TSDIN\n\n     1.  Attached, for your information, is copy of Collection Memorandum\nNumber 7, which was forwarded to field collection agencies for action on\nabove subject.\n\n     2.  This Directorate has been advised that contact has been made with\nthe Horton Brothers, and the Assistant Chief of Staff, G-2, of European\nCommand has accordingly been advised by Telecon to use this Memorandum\nas the basis for interrogation.\n\n     3.  The results of this interrogation will be forwarded to your\nHeadquarters as soon as received.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n1 Incl                                C.P. CABELL\n  Col Memo #7                         Major General, U.S.A.F.\n  dtd 21 Jan 48                       Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                                      Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n         SCN", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "45ff865d67da171aa5d3d5c892f7e605ba698d5c73c14a6b992bc38733127cc0", "output_sha256": "fa31ca8566fd955830e330d65cb2812e864da9cf25cb8e49903b3f278541797d", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:33.508619+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p101", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 101, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "MEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM\n\n     1.  To forward to AMC a copy of Collection Memo #7, and advise\naction being taken.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n     2.  Collection Memo #7, outlines our intelligence requirements in the\nfield of unconventional a/c, as they pertain to overseas agencies.\n\n     3.  Of particular interest in this Memo is the desire to contact the\nHorton Bros, designers of a flying disc type a/c.\n\n     4.  Scientific Branch, ID, advises that EUCOM has made contact with\nthe Horton Bros., and this Office has therefore asked ID to instruct the\nG-2 of EUCOM to arrange an interrogation of the Hortons, using Collection\nMemo #7, as the basis for the interrogation.\n\n     5.  Col. McCoy has been advised of this contact and proposed interrogation.  He feels that further possible exploitation of the Hortons should\nawait the results of this first interrogation.\n\nACTION\n\n     6.  Attached letter to AMC advising them of above facts.\n\nCOORDINATION\n\n     7.  Col. McCoy, T-2, AMC", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "451c942b509f63cbaa276cb26ff36df9a683d2fef7149201dd1f87ff4ed441be", "output_sha256": "e231764f12a31109faa879effc485dca8f28dafc824f0713afa82e3f60adfc8b", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:34.941193+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p102", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 102, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          S[ILLEGIBLE] COVER SHEET\n\n                    *                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST                    b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                               DATE:\n                                         16 Feb 48\n    AFOIR-CC-5                      TYPE:  Letter                    S[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n                                                                    SUSPENSE\n            Flying Discs\n                                                        DATE ___________________\n\n                                                        ASGD BY _________________\n\n                                                        NO. ____________________\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT ___________________\n\nc.                      SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n                                                        DATE ___________________\n\n                                                        NO. ____________________\n\n\n\n\n                    USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.  TO    BR.    TO          TO    DIV.    TO              TO      DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN          UP          DOWN          UP              DOWN               UP\n\n_______ OIP-PP ________                                  ________ ASST EXEC ________\n_______ OIP-FL ________  }  ________ AFOIP ________\n_______ ADMIN  ________  }\n\n_______ OIR-CO ________  }                               ________ ASST EXEC ________\n_______ OIR-DD ________  }\n_______ OIR-AA ________  }  ________ AFOIR   X[ILLEGIBLE]\n_______ OIR-CM ________  }                  [ILLEGIBLE]  ________ EXECUTIVE ________\n_______ OIR-RC ________  }\n\n_______ OAI-OA ________  }                               ________ DIR/INT __________\n_______ OAI-DA ________  }\n_______ OAI-AE ________  }  ________ AFOAI ________\n_______ OAI-AF ________  }\n_______ OAI-SV ________  }\n\n_______ OCI-IS ________  }\n_______ OCI-RR ________  }  ________ AFOCI ________\n_______ OCI-CI ________  }\n\n_______ ....... ________\n_______ ....... ________     X   Action\n_______ ....... ________\n_______ ....... ________     ✓   Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR                    f.  DISPATCH  mail      FILE\n    ACTION ASGD TO  GDG      DATE        DISPATCHED BY  OIR    TO  AMC\n    SIGNED  [ILLEGIBLE]      DATE 16 Feb 48   DATE DISPATCHED  2/24/[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                             SECRET\n                                                                   8-3477,AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3446350b4f0dce5d514626a87ae325b30e5d1b9996a25ba4f0d15a6721350965", "output_sha256": "3446350b4f0dce5d514626a87ae325b30e5d1b9996a25ba4f0d15a6721350965", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:37.601469+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p103", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 103, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g.  TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nh.  TO:                                             DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7957f5d200bf89a3b3304741b1cba4b0fba8ac0ba9114db3165d93e2aa5de850", "output_sha256": "7957f5d200bf89a3b3304741b1cba4b0fba8ac0ba9114db3165d93e2aa5de850", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:38.483539+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p104", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 104, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL                    AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544\n                                        28 Apr 48\n\n                                              2-2-73\n                                              3-62\n\nAFOIR-CO-5                                        28 APR 1948\n\nSUBJECT:  Clipping Service for Project \"SIGN\"\n\nTO:       Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson\n            Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio\n          ATTN:  MCI\n\n     1.  Reference is made to your letter dated 15 March 1948, subject\nas above.\n\n     2.  Based on past experiences of other Government intelligence\nagencies which have been contacted, and taking into consideration the\nnecessity for additional handling which would result if another agency\nsubscribes to the service for you, it is recommended that your Head-\nquarters subscribe to the desired service, rather than have the\nservice contracted for you.\n\n     3.  It is suggested that the simplest method to avoid compro-\nmising the Air Force in a program of this kind would be for a civilian\nmember of your Intelligence staff to secure a Post Office box in\nDayton, contract for the service in his own name, and pay the cost by\nmoney order or certified check secured with funds furnished him by\nthe Government.\n\n     4.  Coverage of general domestic newspapers can be obtained\nthrough Consolidated Press Clipping Bureaus, 431 South Dearborn St.,\nChicago, with branches in New York, Kansas City and Minneapolis;\nHenry Romeike, Inc., 220-30 West 19th St., New York, and American\nPress Clipping Service, 119 Nassau St., New York.  Any one of these\nshould give good coverage, but it might be desirable to query each\nof them before making a choice.  Consolidated is probably the largest.\n\n     5.  For coverage of the domestic trade press, American Trade\nPress Clipping Bureau, 15 East 26th St., New York, is recommended.\n\n     6.  The International Press Clipping Bureau, 5 Beekman St.,\nNew York, provides coverage of the foreign press.\n\n     7.  As to rates, Consolidated charges 10¢ a clipping with a\nminimum charge of $10.00 a month.  American Trade Press Clipping\nBureau charges 15¢ a clipping, with a minimum of $12.00 a month.\nThis Office does not have specific rates for the other bureaus, but\nit is believed that the general newspaper clipping charges run about\n\n                         000.76 General\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9c7bf07660237af10893a6450b42d25cb6f6be76220402e1e107b9304c2b050c", "output_sha256": "a3818aa1821a5e605470ce620cb3169f5f24c883c17df50f22b9f71f99568a70", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:42.561699+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p105", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 105, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/lwd/4544\n28 April 48\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\n\nLtr to AMC, subj: Clipping Service for Project \"SIGN\", dtd\n\nthe same, i.e., 10¢ a clipping, with a minimum of $10.00 a month.\nThe general magazine rates are around 15¢ a clipping with a\nminimum of $15.00 a month.\n\n        BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                    ROBERT TAYLOR 3rd\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Chief, Collection Branch\n                    Air Intelligence Requirements Division\n                    Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\nRef: Ltr AMC dtd 15 Mar 48, subj: as above\n\n     and ltr fm AMC dtd 20 Feb 48, subj: Clipping Service\n\n\n\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "85494e5af28ba923cf8a4958dd5632903443f59d938a29eea444c050739505e5", "output_sha256": "85494e5af28ba923cf8a4958dd5632903443f59d938a29eea444c050739505e5", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:43.854776+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p106", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 106, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\n                                          MCIA/JCB/amb\n\nMCIA\n                                          MAR 1 5 1948\n\n          Clipping Service for Project \"SIGN\"\n\n\n          Chief of Staff\n          United States Air Force\n          Washington 25, D. C.\n          ATTN: AFOIR, Lt Col George D. Garrett, Jr.\n\n\n     1. It is believed that the initiation of a clipping service on\nthe subject of flying discs would be of considerable value to this\nCommand relative to the accomplishment of Project \"SIGN\".\n\n     2. The Research Division of Plane Facts Magazine, Dayton, Ohio\nwas contacted in an attempt to negotiate such a contract. This com-\npany has submitted a few courtesy articles which proved highly useful.\nHowever, in view of the factors involved, indications are that such a\ncontract negotiated directly by this Headquarters with a private com-\npany would carry no assurance that the USAF would not be compromised.\n\n     3. It is requested, therefore, that your Headquarters investigate\nthe possibility to contract for this service through some other Govern-\nment agency. This contract should contain the following coverages:\n\n          a. U. S. newspapers\n\n          b. U. S. periodicals\n\n          c. Leading foreign newspapers (including translations)\n\n          d. Leading foreign periodicals (including translations)\n\nThe cost of such a contract would be furnished from the budget of the\nIntelligence Department, this Command.\n\n     FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n\n                              H. M. McCOY\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief of Intelligence\n\n                         CONFIDENTIAL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ce66ed9f9e01d45213c269d539c7ca541d72a6a953a84b3d65b8361d48baa498", "output_sha256": "ce66ed9f9e01d45213c269d539c7ca541d72a6a953a84b3d65b8361d48baa498", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:45.805204+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p107", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 107, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "SECRET\n\n                                                    MCI/JSH/dm\n\nMCI\n                                                    20 February 1948\n\n          Clipping Service\n\n\n               Chief of Staff\n               United States Air Force\n               Washington 25, D. C.\n\n               Attention: Director of Intelligence\n\n\n          1.  Your attention is invited to the attached proposal from\n     the Research Division of PLANE FACTS magazine to furnish this Head-\n     quarters with a clipping service as explained in the attached\n     correspondence.\n\n          2.  This matter was previously discussed informally with your\n     Headquarters and the undersigned was notified that since the respon-\n     sibility for a review of the world press was vested in the CIA, such\n     matters should be referred to that authority.\n\n          3.  The service proposed by PLANE FACTS would be highly\n     desirable in that the material furnished would be organized in a\n     manner that would facilitate processing within this Headquarters\n     with a minimum of delay.  The ability of the PLANE FACTS organization\n     to successfully furnish such a service is, however, unknown to this\n     office, and no attempt has been made to ascertain its capabilities\n     in this direction in view of C.I.A. responsibility.\n\n          4.  Since it is manifestly true that it would be impracticable,\n     if not impossible, for this Headquarters to set up a worldwide coverage\n     of the press and trade journals in the aeronautical field without out-\n     side assistance, it is requested that efforts be made to make necessary\n     arrangements with C.I.A. whereby this service may be furnished this\n     Headquarters.\n\n                    FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n     Incl:                              H. M. McCOY\n       Ltr. 26 Jan 48                  Colonel, USAF\n       w/Incl.                         Chief of Intelligence\n\n\n                    SECRET                              T-4272-A", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1c4617fc0635ab62f0c0c0c1ece91c8e2118e0362cdab5efeeeb6760143ac1c0", "output_sha256": "0e46f36552f80294ce04c2b3b82dde7d06bcc7de1a3dd85d920c6d7f8d375390", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:47.874893+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p108", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 108, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "DATE:   [REDACTED]\nFROM:   15 Mar.48\n        AMC Ohio.\n\n                                    SUSPENSE DATE:          NO.:\n\n                                                            257078\n\n                                    FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\n\n        Ltr.\nTYPE:\nSMRY:\n\n        Clipping Service for Proj.    \"SIGN\"\n\n\nTO:             TO:             TO:             TO:             TO:\n    OIR\nDATE:           DATE:           DATE:           DATE:           DATE:\n    16 March\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:     FILED (PLACE):          OTHER ACTION:\n\n                                                                HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "867e663aa0e2f6cc7b14930bc8c3e6dc68dc38edab362cbb89a7a9e383e57aab", "output_sha256": "88dbed47ea0e242feef0dfa141283b210bbe92995872914822a44750c59bd40b", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T03:59:48.961589+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p109", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 109, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report 