          NO.   ___________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "13030cbdb0cdbcbd17fe1fee46fbfd0993ac78e09077ba71414445dadca9de9f", "output_sha256": "13030cbdb0cdbcbd17fe1fee46fbfd0993ac78e09077ba71414445dadca9de9f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:00:58.823653+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p150", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 150, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "C\nO                    [REDACTED]                    10 Mar 48\nP                                                C\nY                                                P\n                                                 Y\n\nAMC                          2nd Ind              MCIA/JCB/amb\nSubject:  Project \"SIGN\"                          MAR 10 1948\n\nHq, AMC, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio\n\nTO:  Chief of Staff, United States Air Force, Washington 25, D. C.\n     ATTN:  AFOIR\n\n     In accordance with instructions, the 44 reports listed in 1st Ind,\nyour Hq, are returned for your files.\n\n               FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n\n                              A. J. Hemstreet, Jr.\n44 Incls          For         H. M. McCOY  Lt. Col. USAF\nn/c                           Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief of Intelligence\n\n\n     Incls w/d\n     by CIR-DD\n     File W. B. Mickley\n     Maj. USAF\n          JS\n     Original to Classified Files\n     17 Mar 1948\n\n\n\n\n                                        Vx over\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                    [REDACTED]\n                        3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "15ae82b509cb55517a5918b504d8c2d40744c9014d1475cf37548feaef9c5809", "output_sha256": "4385d44fc8bde2e9c262b73ba9a57519ea84e8509f297285e61a546178a6678a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:00.465827+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p151", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 151, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO-2/Maj Tolbert/hrf/6282\n                    wtn 5 Feb 48\n\n                         SECRET\n\nB/L fr Hq, AMC, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio\ndated 23 Jan 48, subj:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\nAFOIR-CO-2                 1st Ind.\n A-2641\n\n                                              12 FEB 1948\nDept. of the Air Force, Hq, USAF, Washington 25, D. C.\n\nTO:  Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air\n     Force Base, Dayton, Ohio  ATTN:  MICA\n\n     1.  Forwarded herewith on a loan basis for a period of thirty (30)\ndays are the following listed documents:\n\n          KO 54851      KO 70820      KO 61960\n          KO 58833      KO 68030      KO 61859\n          KO 56280      KO 66307      KO 64982\n          KO 70007      KO 67141      KO 61895\n          KO 66691      KO 67097      KO 61986\n          KO 68332      KO 66129      KO 63350\n          KO 67999      KO 63300      KO 61681\n          KO 69518      KO 67122      KO 61943\n          KO 73874      KO 66335      KO 62298\n          KO 75893      KO 66115      KO 60556\n          KO 75634      KO 64613      KO 57213\n          KO 61180      KO 62556      KO 57670\n          KO 86615      KO 63570      KO 57652\n          KO 73577      KO 62008      KO 90250\n          KO 70535      KO 63079\n\n     2.  It is requested that any future correspondence pertaining to\nthis request bear reference to Control No. A-2641.\n\n                    BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                              DOUGLASS W. EISEMAN\n                              Lt. Colonel, U.S.A.F.\n44 Incls                      Executive, Air Intelligence Requirements Div.\n  as listed above             Directorate of Intelligence\n\n  Ref:  (1)  AMC 1tr (MCIA) dated 23 Jan 48, subj:  Project \"SIGN\"\n        (2)  Documents on loan from OIR-DD.\n\n                         10 Mar 48\n\n              319.1 Accession List\n              319.21 Dissemination\n\n                         SECRET", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d5c81e0d9c4f7497f828fc91e9ea687eb97abf1a1fc0dea4fcb8ab4ee3398911", "output_sha256": "7c11716ec0806a8fd4aaf7ca5c7164149169f25e81c6f24d3b809e3630236e9d", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:03.296384+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p152", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 152, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nHEADQUARTERS\nAIR MATERIEL COMMAND\n\nIn reply address both\ncommunication and en-\nvelope to Commanding\nGeneral, Air Materiel\nCommand, Attention\nfollowing office symbol:\n\n    MCIA\n\n                                        MCIA/ACL/amb\n                                        Wright Field, Dayton, Ohio\n\n                                        23 January 1948\n\n\n        SUBJECT:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\n        TO:       Chief of Staff\n                  United States Air Force\n                  Washington 25, D. C.\n                  ATTN:  AFOIR, Lt Col George Garrett\n\n\n        1.  In connection with the investigation of flying discs, Project\n\"SIGN\", it is believed that the various unidentified flying objects seen\nover Sweden (so-called \"Swedish Incidents\") might be helpful.  It is our\nunderstanding that a comprehensive file of these incidents accumulated\nduring the past two years is located at your Headquarters.\n\n        2.  It is requested, therefore, that the entire file \"Swedish Incidents\" be forwarded to this office for review as soon as possible.  If\nextra copies are not available, reproduction copies will be made at this\nCommand so that the originals can be promptly returned.\n\n        FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n\n                                        /s/ W. R. Clingerman Col USAF\n                                        for H. M. McCOY\n                                             Colonel, USAF\n                                             Chief of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fbf73091326da559b262238dcd2358b96de8550da32847bbd32c2dd99509ffd7", "output_sha256": "d03e9ccc2844a3bffebd56a1f149cb62df8141382e124f25017dbcac2239455b", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:04.976276+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p153", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 153, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "DATE: 10 Mar 48          S[ILLEGIBLE]          SUSPENSE DATE:          NO.:\nFROM: AMC Ohio                                                          257308\n\n                                                FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n\nTYPE: 2d Ind          T 6618\nSMRY:\n\n          Project SIGN  KO 54851\n          B/Lfr AMC Ohio dtd 23 Jan 48\n          44 Incl: wbg\n\n\nTO:          TO:               TO: [ILLEGIBLE]     TO:          TO:\n             AFOIP[ILLEGIBLE]   [ILLEGIBLE]\nDATE: OIR   DATE:             DATE: [ILLEGIBLE]   DATE:        DATE:\n      11 Mar 48\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:   FILED (PLACE):          OTHER ACTION:\n\n                                                                    HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c1c4e06896f7e18e97a4079fd2de26af496704c82366c7fbe7f6410ebca58484", "output_sha256": "ba863163f39d1feb09bf14f33474a23f21ea9ce0caee858548d3a7ac8b7b5399", "generate