n     _____ OCI-CI _____    }\n\n     _______ ......\n     _______ ......       [X] Action\n     _______ ......\n     _______ ......       [✓] Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR    11 MAR 1948         f.  DISPATCH _________ FILE _____\n    ACTION ASGD TO   GDG    DATE            DISPATCHED BY _______ TO _____\n    SIGNED   Garrett         DATE 12-3-48   DATE DISPATCHED\n\n                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1bc1e6391a6aa240eda6d435f267b730685a66e820151263ac1fbf7a609220d3", "output_sha256": "a4dba90f32616896b10668d8a430b7ddb7bce437303ca0d111790a8e33372943", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:38.740784+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p171", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 171, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g.  TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nh.  TO:                                             DATE ___________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ___________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0a27b369b329cde4325aa5adb4643283f2f6de97b42e645dcc3e4c470b66e763", "output_sha256": "0a27b369b329cde4325aa5adb4643283f2f6de97b42e645dcc3e4c470b66e763", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:39.506448+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p172", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 172, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO-5\n                                          27 Feb 48\n                                                    AFOIR-CO-5\n                                          Lt.Col.Garrett/dk/4544\n                                               25 Feb 48\n                                          See ttu 12 Jou 3 8\n                                               (Resc)\n\nAFOIR-CO-5                    Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs.\"\nCSGID                          HQ. USAF - AFOIR\nAttn: Plans & Collection                              27 FEB 1948\n       Branch                                    Lt.Col.Garrett/dk/4544\n  Lt.Col. Smith\n\n     1. It is Air Force policy not to ignore reports of sightings and phenomena in\nthe atmosphere, but to recognize that part of its mission is to collect, collate,\nevaluate, and act on information of this nature.\n\n     2. In Implementing this policy the Air Materiel Command has been designated\nas the Air Force agency to collect, collate, evaluate, and distribute to interested\n[REDACTED]government agencies and contractors all information concerning sightings and phenomena in the atmosphere which can be construed to be of concern to the national security.\n\n     3. All Air Force installations within and outside Zone of Interior and Alaska\nhave been instructed to report all sightings, or information concerning sightings\nwhich comes to their attention, direct to the Commanding General, Air Materiel Command,\nWright-Patterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, Attn: MCI.\n\n     4. Air Materiel Command has been authorized direct contact with all Air Force\ninstallations whenever required to develop additional information on the flying discs.\n\n     5. It is requested that all Department of the Army installations also be instructed to report such occurrences directly to Air Materiel Command and that they be informed that Air Materiel Command is authorized to contact them direct when necessary\nin connection with such occurrences.\n\n     6. If possible, reports to Air Materiel Command should include the following\n[REDACTED]information:\n\n          a. Location and time of sighting\n          b. Weather at the time\n          c. Names, occupations, and addresses of witnesses\n          d. Photographs of objects, if available\n          e. Object sighted:\n               (1) Number  (4) Color   (7) Maneuverability  (10) Exhaust trail\n               (2) Shape   (5) Speed   (8) Altitude               or not\n               (3) Size    (6) Heading (9) Sound\n\n          g. General remarks\n\n                                               C. P. CABELL\nFOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:          Major Brigadier General, U.S.A.F.\n                                          Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                                          Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n                         [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5b606304037450937fa2636edab2223b19bec2a71c498536708f466b46a03c35", "output_sha256": "6ce4ec29bbd53b78a22fb226b5026177c9c13986cecc62f7d0be5c1ae167cd8b", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:42.300602+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p173", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 173, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/dk/4544\n                                    25 Feb 48\n\n\n\n\n\n                    MEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\n\nPROBLEM\n\n        1.  To request that all Army and Navy installations make any\nreports of \"flying discs\" direct to AMC, Attn: T-2.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n        2.  By letter from Dir/Research & Development, USAF, to CG,\nAMC, dated 30 Dec 47, AMC was assigned responsibility for the collection,\ncollation, evaluation and distribution of all information and intelligence\npertinent to flying discs.\n\n        3.  In accordance with this letter, therefore, and at the verbal\nrequest of Col. McCoy, it is believed desirable that Army and Navy installations be requested to pass all subject reports and information\ndirect to T-2, AMC.\n\nACTION:\n\n        4.  Attached D/F to CSGID and Letter to ONI requesting that they\ninstruct their installations to forward flying discs information to\nT-2, AMC.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n        5.  Col. McCoy, MCI, AMC", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "28d19ed0a0759f8bfacd93bd0849bb0e6072fce1ccc67a5eb190547a0b20d131", "output_sha256": "a1e47b4cf290ebbaf1a3bfa1f7e4abdf91e1fbc18bc4500dad6a55578352742f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:43.893712+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p174", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 174, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO-5\nLt.Col.Garrett/dk/4544\n25 Feb 48\nSee also 17 Jan 50\nResc\n27 FEB 1948\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\nSUBJECT: Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs.\"\n\nTO:     Chief of Naval Intelligence\n        Department of the Navy\n        Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\n     1. It is Air Force policy not to ignore reports of sightings\nand phenomena in the atmosphere, but to recognize that part of its\nmission is to collect, collate, evaluate, and act on information\nof this nature.\n\n     2. In implementing this policy the Air Materiel Command has\nbeen designated as the Air Force agency to collect, collate, eval-\nuate, and distribute to interested government agencies and con-\ntractors all information concerning sightings and phenomena in\nthe atmosphere which can be construed to be of concern to the\nnational security.\n\n     3. All Air Force installations within and outside the Zone\nof Interior and Alaska have been instructed to report all sightings,\nor information concerning sightings which comes to their attention,\ndirect to the Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-\nPatterson Air Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, Attn: MCI.\n\n     4. Air Materiel Command has been authorized direct contact\nwith all Air Force installations whenever required to develop ad-\nditional information on the flying discs.\n\n     5. It is requested that all Department of the Navy installa-\ntions also be instructed to report such occurrences directly to Air\nMateriel Command, and that they be informed that Air Materiel Command\nis authorized to contact them direct when necessary in connection\nwith such occurrences.\n\n     6. If possible, reports to Air Materiel Command should include\nthe following information:\n\n          a. Location and time of sighting\n          b. Weather at the time\n          c. Names, occupations, and addresses of witnesses\n          d. Photographs of objects, if available\n          e. Sketches of object's configuration\n\n\nFILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6b8f2340614ec6cc78b0ecf28bd457c84d023849586fa6c9bb125ae3d054f465", "output_sha256": "5afcd3cb290a04572839ec1ab55bdde91d3279186bb1458787913530467ad078", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:46.589324+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p175", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 175, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\nAFOIR-CO-5 Ltr to Chief of Naval Intelligence, subj: Reporting of Information\n         on \"Flying Discs.\"\n\n         f.  Object sighted:\n\n              (1) Number      (5) Speed              (9) Sound\n              (2) Shape       (6) Heading           (10) Exhaust trail\n              (3) Size        (7) Maneuverability        or not\n              (4) Color       (8) Altitude\n\n         g.  General remarks\n\n     FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                        C. P. CABELL\n                              Brigadier General, U.S.A.F.\n                                        Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                                        Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                      - 2 -\n\n                              RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5dca09d3223d60805162c53c517daecfb5ce7de1f9ccc710668ea0f500959dbb", "output_sha256": "9ab4dafc31214294a4d0aa50eaa57eda4d525cafe00b045372d691426682fdb8", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:47.767119+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p176", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 176, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)                    COVER SHEET\n\n              *                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST                    b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                              DATE:  26 Feb 48\n        AFOIR-CO-5                                                        RESTRICTED\n                                   TYPE:  D/F and Letter\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n        Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs.\"\n                                                                         SUSPENSE\n\n                                                                DATE ___________________\n\n                                                                ASGD BY ________________\n\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT ___________________                       NO. ____________________\n\nc.                          SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n\n                                                                DATE ___________________\n\n                                                                NO. ____________________\n\n\n\n\n                    USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.  TO    BR.    TO              TO    DIV.    TO                   TO    DIR/INT      TO\n    DOWN          UP              DOWN          UP                   DOWN               UP\n         OIP-PP                                                            ASST EXEC ______\n         OIP-FL              __________ AFOIP __________\n         ADMIN\n\n         OIR-CO  [initialed]\n         OIR-DD                                                            ASST EXEC ______\n         OIR-AA              __________ AFOIR  Cfc\n         OIR-CM                                  26 Feb\n         OIR-RC                                                            EXECUTIVE ______\n\n         OAI-OA                                                            DIR/INT _________\n         OAI-DA              __________ AFOAI __________\n         OAI-AE\n         OAI-AF\n         OAI-SV\n\n         OCI-IS\n         OCI-RR              __________ AFOCI __________\n         OCI-CI\n\n         .......\n         .......              X   Action\n         .......\n         .......              ✓   Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D RR _______________          f.  DISPATCH  [ILLEGIBLE]      FILE\n    ACTION ASGD TO    GDG    DATE ________     DISPATCHED BY   S/R    TO  ZSG-1D\n    SIGNED   Garrett           DATE 26 Feb 48  DATE DISPATCHED  2/27/48\n\n                                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "70bef36e0e861fa574ed30f14be413abff525f5924872912b30f89c3a28ad600", "output_sha256": "953a5433bd9d97918b993a80d1b7f3edfcc2f033621c02392d1b48bd13a9311f", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:50.394152+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p177", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 177, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g.  TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                        DATE ________________\n\n                                                        NO.  ________________\n\n\n\n\nh.  TO:                                                 DATE ________________\n\n                                                        NO.  ________________\n\n\n\n\n                                                                    8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b0bdb84c047c4323ebd73b59e119ed19d828188cf809cd88e506c46d72ca0c4e", "output_sha256": "030fd5e74c46782559be497fd70aa0c3912c4e025401f41840d88ca028917a69", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:51.388901+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p178", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 178, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\n                    DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\n               HEADQUARTERS UNITED STATES AIR FORCE\n                           WASHINGTON\n\n                                                    26 February 1948\n\nSUBJECT:   Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs\"\n\nTO:        Commanding General, Caribbean Air Command\n           Commanding General, United States Air Forces in Europe\n           Commanding General, Far East Air Forces\n           Commanding General, Pacific Air Command\n           Commanding General, Air Materiel Command\n\n     1.  It is Air Force policy not to ignore reports of sightings and\nphenomena in the atmosphere but to recognize that part of its mission\nis to collect, collate, evaluate, and act on information of this nature.\n\n     2.  In implementing this policy the Air Materiel Command has been\ndesignated as the Air Force agency to collect, collate, evaluate, and\ndistribute to interested government agencies and contractors all infor-\nmation concerning sightings and phenomena in the atmosphere which can\nbe construed to be of concern to the national security.\n\n     3.  Any information pertaining to the sighting of so-called flying\ndiscs, which is secured by or comes to the attention of any installations\nunder your command, will be forwarded, through channels, to the Command-\ning General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\nDayton, Ohio, Attention:  MCI.\n\n     4.  In observing this procedure for reporting information on flying\ndisc sightings, every effort will be made to include the following items:\n\n          a.  Location and time of sighting.\n\n          b.  Weather at the time.\n\n          c.  Names, occupations and addresses of witnesses.\n\n          d.  Photographs of objects, if available.\n\n          e.  Sketches of object's configuration.\n\n          f.  Object sighted:\n\n               (1) Number          (5) Speed           (9) Sound\n               (2) Shape           (6) Heading        (10) Exhaust trail or\n               (3) Size            (7) Maneuverability      not.\n               (4) Color           (8) Altitude\n\n\n\n\n                              RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e5732e941021bd48b546771a7a746fad11467ff2aa0ed693b25fda96a40f19f3", "output_sha256": "d7da787e30247d4fdc6137d0703b2dff1a9f0cd66680e96a99e5063d3ee91f15", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:53.717850+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p179", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 179, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\nLtr, Hq USAF, dated 26 February 1948, Subj:  Reporting of Information\non \"Flying Discs\"\n\n          g.  General remarks.\n\n     5.  A copy of all reports or summaries of information sent to Air\nMateriel Command in accordance with the above provisions will be for-\nwarded at the same time to this Headquarters, Attention:  Director of\nIntelligence.\n\n     6.  Headquarters, Air Materiel Command, is authorized direct con-\ntact with installations of the addressees of this letter in connection\nwith the development of information on flying discs.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                              C. P. Cabell\n                              C. P. CABELL\n                              Major General, U.S.A.F.\n                              Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED\n     2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c0bdfae50878833306dd7e3f26a3e4664ae680a84e976968b3564f4f31d67794", "output_sha256": "9342953b0fc1d088c5287014313294a4c1e550f397076976c2457457abdf1970", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:54.938396+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p180", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 180, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt Col Garrett/nc/4544\n26 Feb 48\n\nRESTRICTED\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To instruct the overseas air commands to report all flying disc\nsightings direct to AMC.\n\nFACTS & DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  By letter dated 30 December 1947 this Hqs assigned AMC the responsibility for the collection, collation, evaluation, and production of\nintelligence concerning the so-called flying discs.\n\n     3.  It is therefore desirable to instruct that all such occurrences\nwhich come to the attention of installations within the overseas air commands\nbe reported direct to AMC.\n\n     4.  Air Commands within the ZI and Alaska have already been instructed\nto report this information direct to AMC.\n\nACTION:\n\n     5.  Dispatch of attached letter to overseas air commands.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     6.  None.\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a2346a10f05f96a5d16893ff688ae6d6341ae701898e4f8e8951ab31c8f5fc2a", "output_sha256": "c4c292f928501d98921bb43b3afd8ff51f8bbf49f4009bf794b7cd491dfc203a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:56.456623+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p181", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 181, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET                    15 copies\n\n*                    *\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                          DATE:  25 Feb 48\n    AFOIR-CO\n                               TYPE:  Letter (Ditto)\n*\nSUMMARY:\n\n        Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs\"\n                                                            SUSPENSE\n\n                                                   DATE ___________________\n\n                                                   ASGD BY ________________\n\nDATE RECEIVED DIR/INT ___________________          NO. ____________________\n\nc.                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS\n                                                   DATE ___________________\n\n                                                   NO. ____________________\n\n\n\n\n              USE OTHER SIDE THIS SHEET FOR ADDITIONAL REMARKS\n\nd.  TO    BR.    TO          TO    DIV.    TO            TO    DIR/INT    TO\n    DOWN          UP          DOWN          UP            DOWN              UP\n    ______OIP-PP                                          ______ASST EXEC ______\n    ______OIP-FL ______  }   ______AFOIP ______  }\n    ______ADMIN                                           ______ASST EXEC ______\n    ______OIR-CO [initialed]\n    ______OIR-DD          }   ______AFOIR  alc\n    ______OIR-AA                              26 Feb       ______EXECUTIVE ______\n    ______OIR-CM\n    ______OIR-RC                                          ______DIR/INT ______\n\n    ______OAI-OA\n    ______OAI-DA          }   ______AFOAI ______\n    ______OAI-AE\n    ______OAI-AF\n    ______OAI-SV\n\n    ______OCI-IS\n    ______OCI-RR          }   ______AFOCI ______\n    ______OCI-CI\n\n    ______......\n    ______......         X  Action\n    ______......\n    ______......         ✓  Coordination\n\ne.  DATE REC'D BR                    f.  DISPATCH              FILE\n    ACTION ASGD TO  GDG   DATE           DISPATCHED BY OIR-CO to EACH Comd\n    SIGNED  Garrett        DATE 25 Feb 48  DATE DISPATCHED  27 Feb 48\n\n                                                                    S-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6bd7dcc27df8e8bcf68ef42a55ac9ec031cac9dc3b8af9053712bf9dcdfa9333", "output_sha256": "510bf09ddd51f26f610759b96916b3a83275339409811c4cb78713b24a66b856", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:59.094746+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p182", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 182, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "g. TO:                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS - REMARKS (Continued)\n\n                                                    DATE ________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nh. TO:                                              DATE ________________\n\n                                                    NO.  ________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                8-3477, AF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "74dd2557856459fcde8ce34efd39cb4288a480fca735e56bd177a9407a9da917", "output_sha256": "74dd2557856459fcde8ce34efd39cb4288a480fca735e56bd177a9407a9da917", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:01:59.973614+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p183", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 183, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "R E S T R I C T E D\n\n                                        Rescinded\n                                        by ltr 12 Jan\n                                        50 this file\n         DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\n    HEADQUARTERS UNITED STATES AIR FORCE\n               WASHINGTON\n\n                                   26 February 1948\n\n\nSUBJECT:  Reporting of Information on \"Flying Discs\"\n\nTO:       Commanding General, Strategic Air Command\n          Commanding General, Air Defense Command\n          Commanding General, Tactical Air Command\n          Commanding General, Air Training Command\n          Commanding General, Air University\n          Commanding General, Alaskan Air Command\n          Commanding General, Air Transport Command\n          Commanding General, Air Materiel Command\n\n   1.  Reference is made to letter from this Headquarters dated\n6 February 1948, subject as above.\n\n   2.  Paragraph 1 of subject letter is changed to read as follows:\n\n        \"1.  Any information pertaining to the sighting of so-called\n   flying discs, which is secured by or comes to the attention of any\n   installation under your command, will be forwarded direct to the\n   Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air\n   Force Base, Dayton, Ohio, Attention:  MCI.\"\n\n   3.  Hereafter any sightings of flying discs will be reported under\nthe provisions of this letter whether they occur within or outside the\nUnited States and Alaska.\n\n              BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                        C. P. Cabell\n\n                              C. P. CABELL\n                              Major General, U.S.A.F.\n                              Chief, Air Intel. Req. Div.\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n              R E S T R I C T E D\n\n                                              FILM COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8eaef5e6c66872d324514a09b2999555ce255c528b5e51148c235a24f4c4bf2c", "output_sha256": "aba81787a1941a944d348844a1e1c163a73fd955f8a10b4dbf3058369e408e0a", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:02.360907+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p184", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 184, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR -CO/Lt Col Garrett/nc/4544\n              25 Feb 48\n         RESTRICTED\n\n              MEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To change text of Para. 1 of this Headquarters' letter dated\n6 February 1948, subject, \"Reporting of Information on Flying Discs.\"\n\nFACTS & DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  Subject letter, addressed to all air commands in ZI and Alaska,\ninstructed that information on the sightings of \"flying discs\" occurring\nwithin the ZI and Alaska be forwarded direct to Air Materiel Command.\n\n     3.  It is felt that the reporting of information on this subject\nshould not be limited to occurrences within the US and Alaska only, but\nthat all instances, in no matter what part of the world, should be\nreported direct to AMC.\n\n     4.  Accordingly, the necessary correction should be made to basic\nletter.\n\n     5.  A separate letter is being sent to Caribbean Air Command,\nUSAFE, Air Div. US Army Forces Austria, FEAF, Pacific Air Command, and\n1st Air Div.\n\nACTION:\n\n     6.  Dispatch of attached letter to addressees of our letter of\n6 February 1948.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     7.  None required.\n\n\n\n\n         RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e42a1ff8421634418050007fb8cc6754000efc885f29cae037e6e96c1a0532a6", "output_sha256": "5f581cf9abe0d91e64160dae5eb19103c0e38f57fed5cba0d28601da8c98acda", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:04.097719+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p185", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 185, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/jh/4544\n16 Feb 48\n\nAFOIR-CO-5\n\n                                              20 FEB 1948\n\nSUBJECT:  Flying Discs\n\nTO    :  Commanding General\n         Air Materiel Command\n         Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n         Dayton, Ohio\n         ATTN:  TSDIN\n\n\n     Forwarded for your information.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                              DOUGLASS W. EISEMAN\n                              Lt. Colonel, U.S.A.F.\n1 Incl                        Executive, Air Intelligence Requirements Div.\nNewspaper clipping            Directorate of Intelligence", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a2600fcc6485f814a2096eae8006e5ec3f0965eab6728f4de6fcf4f8ecd81d81", "output_sha256": "a2600fcc6485f814a2096eae8006e5ec3f0965eab6728f4de6fcf4f8ecd81d81", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:05.845310+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p186", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 186, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET\n\n              *                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                         DATE:\n  AFOIR-CO-5                    16 Feb 48\n                              TYPE:\n                    