the\nV-1.  This German scientist in all of his calculations showed that their\nV-1 model should be actually getting five times as much range as they were\ngetting in their experiments.\n\n      3.  Dr. Wilkenson apparently had very definite ideas with regard\nto the much-discussed \"meteors\" that have been seen over their country,\nbut Colonel von Schinkel got into a very excited discussion in Swedish\nwith Dr. Wilkenson, which apparently changed his ideas about making\nany statement on the subject.\n\n             *              *              *\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFILED UNDER:  470.  Armament & New Weapons", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5eed4ca032015001112986184277979d9294c90b37cfa2a63ef1cb7844fd5dab", "output_sha256": "eb1201571a3662800bdd77e5f0c33ae4815b0147a231d1fa9693a280eb291e02", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:10.766031+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p189", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 189, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIR-CO/Lt. Col. Garrett/jh/4544\n                                        10 Feb 48\n\n              CONFIDENTIAL\n\nLtr frm AMC MCIA, dtd 4 Feb 48, subject:  \"Project SIGN\"\n\nAFOIR-CO-5                    1st Ind.\n\nDept. of the Air Force, Hq. USAF, Washington 25, D. C.        13 FEB 1948\n\nTO:  Commanding General, Air Materiel Command, Wright-Patterson Air Force\n     Base, Dayton, Ohio\n     ATTN:  TSD-N\n\n\n     1.  No information has been received from field agencies, as yet, in\nconnection with subject guide.\n\n     2.  As such information is received it will be forwarded promptly to\nyour Headquarters.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n                         DOUGLASS W. EISEMAN\n                         Lt. Colonel, U.S.A.F.\n                         Executive, Air Intelligence Requirements Div.\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n              CONFIDENTIAL\n\n                                              FILE COPY - DIRECTORATE OF INTELLIGENCE", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fbf4730c8ddbf19a22a2e4dcbe1aa94ec58d0e14010aca1b5dee3f9ece39b31b", "output_sha256": "fbf4730c8ddbf19a22a2e4dcbe1aa94ec58d0e14010aca1b5dee3f9ece39b31b", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:12.633108+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p190", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 190, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "COPY\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\n\n\nHEADQUARTERS\nAIR MATERIEL COMMAND\n\nMCIA\n                                          MCIA/EHL/amb\n                                          Wright Field, Dayton, Ohio\n                                          4 February 1948\n\nSUBJECT:  Project \"SIGN\"\n\n\nTO:       Chief of Staff\n          United States Air Force\n          Washington 25, D. C.\n          ATTN:  AFOIR, Major Samuel Tolbert\n\n                                               in Co files\n\n     1.  Reference is made to AMC letter dated 7 October 1947, subject:\n\"Flying Discs\" (Project \"SIGN\") pertaining to the distribution of the\nAir Intelligence Guide for Alleged Flying Saucer Type Aircraft.\n\n     2.  It is requested that a follow-up be made to determine the avail-\nability of any pertinent information as a result of this inquiry.  Expe-\nditious action is requested so that these findings may be considered\nin a new guide now being prepared.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                              /S/ W. R. Clingerman Col USAF\n                              for H. M. McCOY\n                                  Colonel, USAF\n                                  Chief of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dd33dcb60dbb03d3babc95175eb66f8836f2022ce2b5b436dc074b60a1f2109a", "output_sha256": "a2ce9d7ef7581b147e4a07e275a3f9a5f04de8485f4c1b6f30745ffd9eed8aa7", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:14.077925+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p191", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 191, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\nDATE: 4 Feb 48                    SUSPENSE DATE:              NO.:\n                                                               248660\nFROM: AMC, Ohio\n      Wright-Patterson              FILE DESIGNATION AND DATE:\n      AFB, Dayton, Ohio\n      ltr\nTYPE:\nSMRY:\n      Project \"SIGN\" (Flying Discs)\n      mjp\n\n\n\n\nTO:          TO:              TO:              TO:              TO:\n   OIR\nDATE: 5 Feb 48  DATE:          DATE:            DATE:            DATE:\n\nREPLIED OR INDORSED TO:    FILED (PLACE):         OTHER ACTION:\n\n                                                                  HQ AAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cd42c20ad21540aee2e216a8430b2d0909ae855954273be372c4bb44b2a11944", "output_sha256": "cd42c20ad21540aee2e216a8430b2d0909ae855954273be372c4bb44b2a11944", "generated_at": "2026-08-08T04:02:15.167805+00:00"}, {"id": "da533c72f476d84f-p192", "card_id": "da533c72f476d84f", "page": 192, "title": "DOW-UAP-D100, Air Materiel Command Report on Unidentified Flying Objects, 1947-1948", "text": "AFOIN-4 (Rev 5 Dec 47)          COVER SHEET          2  62 A  [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                    *                    *\n\na.  RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST  -          b.  CLASSIFICATION:\n\nFROM:                              DATE:\n                                                          [ILLEGIBLE - stamped]\n                 