2142bcebc28d3f2a0c", "output_sha256": "e4c97b1b982464caa8bf8839f4bbb496468b3d648a44602142bcebc28d3f2a0c", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:06.373778+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p17", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 17, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "Indices Search Slip\nFD-160 (Rev. 6-11-56)\n\n                                                          Date\nTO: CHIEF CLERK\nSubject  (B) Jones, Willi\nAliases  J.J.        B-N\n\nAddress                                    Birth Date    Birthplace\n\n     Exact Spelling                    Main Criminal Case Files Only              Restrict to Locality of\n     All References                    Criminal References Only\n     Main Subversive Case Files Only   Main Subversive (If no Main, list all Subversive References)\n     Subversive References Only        Main Criminal (If no Main, list all Criminal References)\nFile & Serial Number        Remarks              File & Serial Number              Remarks\n\n25-0-A-1212(con)\n\n\n\n100-31271-1861-13\n\n\n\n(S) 25-4912*\n\n\n\n(J) [ILLEGIBLE]         1*C      )\n\n          Num if on other name variations\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRequested by                              Squad         Extension     File No.\n\nSearched by\n                                          (date)\nConsolidated by\n                                          (date)\nReviewed by\n                                          (date)\n              File Review Symbols\n  I  - Identical              ? - Not identifiable\n  NI - Not identical          U - Unavailable reference\n\nNW-91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 17", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ef91c4fdbcba087d3b01299208066d716ed49c9ec6b3fe66c81c8c5d8fb7e526", "output_sha256": "9e6f31846cf09638d585508309b3417c70a95e4a022e73c31b993341411137e2", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:07.964141+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p18", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 18, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO    :    SAC, NK (62-0)                    DATE:    11/13/57\n\nFROM  :    SA DONALD H. ROBERTS\n\nSUBJECT:   UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT\n\n          WILLARD JONES, 284 Chestnut Street, Kearny, N. J.,\ntelephone, Kearny 3-0722, telephonically contacted this office\nat 11:25 p.m., 11/12/57, to advise that he had seen an unidentified flying object (UFO) over New York City from 11:15 p.m. to\nthe time of this call.  JONES stated that the UFO had fast\nfluctuating red and blue lights and remained in a stationary\nposition.  JONES stated he was unable to describe the shape\nof the UFO. JONES stated he was using a 7x50 lense in observing\nthe UFO.\n\n          Agent GEORGE H. WERTZ, OSI, was telephonically\nappraised of the above at 11:35 p.m.\n\n                         ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                         HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                         DATE 3/15/15 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nDHR:MCR\n(1)R\n                                             100-36998-10\n                                        SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                        SERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                             NOV 1 3 1957\n                                             FBI NEWARK\n                                             [ILLEGIBLE]\nRec'd 11/[ILLEGIBLE]\nSO.\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 18", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "793867460d9d74f0e54b6b19f7a83e5580cf8d884cc274bd3f9076b395e3299a", "output_sha256": "1461dc2484c3c036a8aefc132e2b49917c2a51b44ca2a4d9419fc6602e6cd066", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:09.833507+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p19", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 19, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO :        SAC, NK (62-0)                    DATE:    11/15/57\n\nFROM :      SA DONALD H. ROBERTS\n\nSUBJECT:    UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT\n\n        At 7:15 p.m., 11/5/57, Mr. MARINO, 29 Windsor Place,\nGlen Ridge, N. J., telephonically advised this office that at\n4:45 p.m., this date, his wife observed an unidentified low\nflying object over Glen Ridge, N. J.  MARINO stated his wife\ndescribed this object as being a brilliant white, cigar shaped\nwith delta wings toward the tail and was unable to hear any\nnoise coming from this object.  According to Mrs. MARINO,\nthis object was flying from the south to the north.\n\n        SA LAWRENCE W. VAN LIERE, OSI, was telephonically\napprized of the above at 7:50 p.m, 11/5/57.\n\n\nDHR:MCR                    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n(1)                        HEREIN IS CLASSIFIED\n                           DATE 5/15/85  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                        100-36998-11\n                              SEARCHED... INDEXED...\n                              SERIALIZED... FILED...\n                                    NOV 15 1957\n                                    FBI - NEWARK\n\nRec'd 11/18/57.\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 19", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5eeb14433ee38b05d690948e82ff0371136f20f4e24ede0e9beb86b60367f783", "output_sha256": "5eeb14433ee38b05d690948e82ff0371136f20f4e24ede0e9beb86b60367f783", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:11.747110+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p20", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 20, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO :     SAC, NEWARK  (100-36998)          DATE:  2/14/58\n\nFROM :   SA RICHARD G. MOHR\n\nSUBJECT:    UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT\n\n          At 1:10 p.m., 2/11/58, Mrs. MARY JANE KACZYNSKI,\n2630 Vauxhall Road, Union, N. J., phone MU 6-0912, telephonically\nadvised this office that at 12:25 p.m., 2/11/58, she observed\nan unidentified flying object from the kitchen window of her\nhome.  She described this UFO as bullet-shaped, silver, no wings,\nflying south at a very high altitude with vapor trail.  She stated\nit flew much higher than commercial aircraft and she heard\nno noise.\n\n          HAROLD PECK, OSI, was notified 4:00 p.m., 2/11/58.\n\n\n\nRGM:AM\n(1)\n[ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\n\n\n\n\n                                        100-36998-12\n                                    SEARCHED   INDEXED\n                                    SERIALIZED\n                                        FEB 1 4 1958\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                                [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:24742114  Page 20", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "60b73a51368bc9d75425ad95c2a2ceea4ad295ca8965c236551c5fedd97c6bd7", "output_sha256": "a2e53919eb4840cb15bcd1b03d119ca1d468196ceea820508a6a49b7f5e43e35", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:13.362768+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p21", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 21, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC, NEWARK                          DATE:  4/14/58\n\nFROM  : SA BILL WILLIAMS                    100 - 36998#\n\nSUBJECT: UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT SIGHTED\n         NEAR PERTH AMBOY BRIDGE ON 4/12/58  ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n         AT ABOUT 3:30 PM.                   HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                             DATE 5/10/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n     Mrs. Edward Barry, 232 Dwight St., Jersey City, phone HE-\n5-0331 telephonically advised on this date that she and her husband\nobserved the subject object which appeared as a flaming rocket\ncoming down from the sky.  They were in their car at the time coming\nhome (North) from the shore on RT. 35 and were passing over a small\nbridge just before going on to the large bridge at Perth Amboy.\n\n\nVan Lean\n   OSI adv.\n      h.\n\n                         [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\n                                        100- 36998-13\n                              SEARCHED  INDEXED\n                              SERIAL    FILED\n                                   1  1000\n                                   FBI- NEWARK\n                                              h.\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114 Page 21", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "76ac4230ad868205f69b31b0a69bb1901bafa9efda205b5e25dc0aee71973dd2", "output_sha256": "d8deb101173d2263398b1e3e8c6e96fc13753362c9ca887c0326899106c22906", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:14.964382+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p22", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 22, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO  :SAC W.G. SIMON                         DATE: 12-14-58\n\n                                    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nFROM :Clerk William P. Nugent        HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                    DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\nSUBJECT: UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT SEEN BY JERSEY CITY\n  P.D. DETECTIVES LANGREHR & SHERRY ON\n  12-14-58, and HERMAN TAUBMAN'S ON\n  SAME DATE; and ALSO THE A.G. DOWER'S.\n\n        The writer was telephonically contacted on this date\nby Det. George Langrehr of the Jersey City P.D., at 12:55 AM.\nDet. Langrehr informed the writer that at 12:43 AM on this date\nhe and his partner, Det. Edward Sherry viewed in the sky the\nexhaust of an object which Det. Langrehr stated traveled at\na speed of 300 or 400 miles an hour at an altitude of 1,000\nto 3,000 feet. He described this object as having an exhaust\nof a brilliant bluish white flame about 40 feet long and he\nstated he saw this object for about 30 seconds. He stated that\nit wasn't a fallen star in his opinion as it traveled in a flight\nmanner. He and Det. Sherry saw this object at Communipaw and\nPacific Ave.'s in Jersey City, while they were in a car traveling\ndue west. They stated this object traveled in a North, Northwest\ndirection. They lost sight of it when it traveled behind some\nbuildings in Jersey City. They stated that Ptl. John Wheamen\nof the same precinct also viewed it. These three officers are\nall attached to the Fourth (4th) Precinct in Jersey City.\nDet. Langrehr resides at 55 Bleecker St., Jersey City, N.J. and\nDet. Sherry resides at 56 Gates Ave., Jersey City, N.J.\n\n        At 1:05 AM, the writer received a phone call from\nMr. Herman Taubman, who stated that he had viewed an object\nwhich he described as a meteorite or comet in the sky above\nWoodbridge, N.J., on Helm Ave., in that city. They stated\n(He and his wife Betty) that they were on a hill above the\nCurtiss-Wright Plant in that city and this object flew over\nthis plant in a left to right direction at a height of 1,000\nto 3,000 feet but he said it traveled at a speed of 10,000 mph.,\nand his wife said it traveled much slower than that speed, that\nthis object was of a tremendous size and that the object had\na bluish-white flame and he saw it for some 30 seconds.\nBesides himself and his wife, he stated the following people\nsaw this object: Doris and Bob Ostroff of Roselle, N.J.; the\nRichard Morgan's of Passaic, N.J. (Mr. Morgan is a lawyer);\nHarold and Janet Packer of Woodbridge, N.J. (Mr. Packer is a\nlawyer); and other witnesses whose names he will give upon\nrequest. Just before he concluded the conversation with the  100-36998-14\nwriter at about 1:05 AM he stated he saw another UFO. He\nstated he saw the first object at 12:13 AM. Mr. Taubman informed    SEARCHED    INDEXED\nthe writer that he resides at 470 Piaget Ave., Clifton, N.J.   SERIALIZED   FILED\n                                                         DEC 1 5 1958\n                                                    FBI - NEWARK\n                                              John Murphy [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 22", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a41477ef269117ef777c299c30eb5df3a6c3657214de614c6d3f18677dc7b987", "output_sha256": "bda231ec6c25321d95132392d5fdee3b51d1d50768905cabcac534ea1f92cd6c", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:19.695220+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p23", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 23, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "The writer telephonically contacted SA John Murphy, who\nis in charge of liaison with other government agencies in the\nNewark office, at 1:10 AM.  The writer wished to know whether he\nshould immediately contact OSI or if SA Murphy should do so.\nSA Murphy told the writer that the procedure as he understood it\nwas to send a letter to the interested agency and not make an\nimmediate contact with the agency at night.  SA Murphy did suggest\nthat the writer inform the Sunday morning duty agent of the\ncontents of this memo and leave it to his discretion as to whether\nOSI should be contacted at that time.\n\n          Mrs. A.G. Dower telephonically contacted the Newark office\nat 1:35 AM on this date.  She informed the writer that she and\nher husband had seen a UFO that had passed over her residence in\na South to North direction; that it had lasted for only two or\nthree seconds; that to her it appeared to be a white hot point of\nlight, with a tail of predominantly orange coloring; that this tail\nwas at least ten times as large as the object; that the tail was\nfan shaped; that it was at an altitude of greater than 3,000 feet;\nthat it was unlike a falling star; and that when they first saw\nthe object it appeared to them that it had burst into flames.\nMrs. Dower advised that she resides at 8 Harvard Terrace, West\nOrange, N.J.\n\nJohn G. Caton, OSI,\nOrange 5-3512 was\ntelephonically advised of\nabove at 8:56 AM\n12/14/58\n     J.P.C.\n\n\nNews reports on radio 12/14/58 revealed\nthe Air Force had received numerous calls\nconcerning above and they had checked\nwith the Hayden Planetarium, N.Y.C.\n     They advised that the UFO were extremely\nbright meteors that were falling and\nwere not any type aircraft.\n     No need to advise Bureau or U.S.A.F.\n                              J.M.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dd777c67a540c6e405f02cf5ecf5d4cb75ef66ad55ab1aff432e387b5c9101da", "output_sha256": "5453257e436658f939e02533057d9c0af9349671f6634d6d61c2cb66f2431403", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:21.848007+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p24", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 24, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC, Newark                                    DATE: 1/3/59\n\nFROM : SA Walter A. Wangenheim\n\nSUBJECT:  UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT SEEN\n          BY WILLIAM KNOERER, 14 STONY\n          BROOK DRIVE, OLDBRIDGE, N.J.\n          TELEPHONE # CLIFFORD 4-6302\n\n                                    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                                    HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                    DATE 5/12/75 BY SP4[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n     Writer telephonically contacted this date by captioned\nindividual at 10:23pm.  This individual stated he and wife\nsaw object, approximately six foot long, orange in color,\nflying in north east direction from the front of his house\nwhich faces in same direction.  Knoerer saw object at about\n4:55pm.  It flew for about five minutes in NE direction then\nreversed its course to a south west direction and flew for\nabout five minutes more before disappearing.\n\n     Knoerer had no idea as to its speed or altitude.  He mentioned\nthat for a couple of minutes in each direction it actually\nappeared to be two objects flying side by side.  He explained\nthat there was a patch of blue sky between both orange objects.\n\n     Knoerer stated he hesitated to report incident for fear\nof sounding foolish but after thinking about it realized\nit should be reported.\n\n     OSI representative Harold N. Peck, Nutley 2-9062 was\nadvised of facts, 10:30pm, same date.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                         100-36998-15\n                              SEARCHED      INDEXED\n                              SERIALIZED    FILED\n                                   [ILLEGIBLE] - [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                                   John Murphy [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 24", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "427d3c7d4e27c4db7af41a959735746678f6139f8ca143ccdf6e6c3ca7b6de3b", "output_sha256": "57f8a6941a2415a1033d06cd0fbb5677dc6d42b6206a0dbf00ce293455525e85", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:23.881299+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p25", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 25, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO : SAC, NEWARK                    DATE: 2-26-59\n\nFROM : Clerk William P. Nugent\n\nSUBJECT: Unidentified Flying Object        62-0-13812\n\n          The writer received a telephone call from Mrs. Robert\nSchrann, at 6:37 PM on this date.  Mrs. Schrann was very nervous\nand subsequently admitted to being scared, as she was the only\none at home and she saw a UFO in the air outside her home.  She\nstated it was a considerable distance from her home and only\ncould identify it as a \"silver object\".  OSI advised at 6:55 PM.\n\n          Mrs. Schrann's address is 65 Shetland Lane, Levittown,\nNew Jersey.\n\n                    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                    HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                    DATE 5/15/85  BY SP6 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n                              100-36998-16\n                    SEARCHED   INDEXED\n                    SERIALIZED   FILED\n                         FEB 27 1959\n                         FBI - NEWARK\n                              [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 25", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "779423991c45e3e4124d8c14320c6f5a509ba4659625a273682e0e511df57f49", "output_sha256": "a0c32826b1467d38d151481becbb5326b78e9ec032368d7f5d131fa3f1b425b9", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:25.660510+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p26", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 26, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC                                    DATE:  4-22-59\n\nFROM  : CLERK WILLIAM P. NUGENT\n\n                              100-36998-X\nSUBJECT:  UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT\n\n     O  The writer was telephonically contacted by Mr. OSCAR R.\nGRAHAM, WHO RESIDES AT 266 NORTH AVE., FANWOOD, N.J., at 10:15 PM\nthis date.  MR. GRAHAM stated that he was viewing a series of lights\nin the air that came out of the Southern Horizon and traveled as fast\nas the satellites sent up by this country.  He stated these lights\nchanged color, and also divided in the air and came together again.\nHe stated he had called the local police and there was a local\npoliceman in his home at the time of his call.  The writer advised\nMr. Johnson that he would furnish his information to the OSI and upon\nthe termination of Mr. Johnson's call, the writer telephonically con-\ntacted Agent BLALOCK of the OSI and informed him of Mr. Johnson's\ncall.  Agent BLALOCK told the writer that he would handle the matter.\n\n          MR. JOHNSON'S TELEPHONE NUMBER IS FANWOOD 2-6756.\n\nBlalock advised          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED          1/00-36998-17\nat 10:20 PM              HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n   wpn-N                 DATE 5/15/15  BY [ILLEGIBLE]SEAR[ILLEGIBLE]  cc\n                                                    APR 2 3 1959\n                                                    FBI - NEWARK\n                                                       [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149  [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 26", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f1bd571f34f503f89d35a8c987ee8fda2c83ec02577280ddea8999b1517089f1", "output_sha256": "f1bd571f34f503f89d35a8c987ee8fda2c83ec02577280ddea8999b1517089f1", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:27.638742+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p27", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 27, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC, NEWARK                                    DATE:  7/6/59\n\nFROM  : GEORGE H CHRISTIAN (CLERK)\n\n                        ✓  62-0-13812\nSUBJECT: REPORT OF UNIDENTIFIED FLYING\n         OBJECT in Sky over Pompton Plains,    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n         N.J., 7/6/59.                         HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                               DATE 5/15/85  BY SP6 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n          At 10:15 pm this date Mr. THOMAS SCALZA, Rt. #23, Pompton Plains, N.J.\ntelephonically contacted this office and reported seeing an Unidentified\nFlying Object in the sky over the general area of his home.\n\n          Information was secured from Mr. SCALZA re the exact location of this\nObject, its distance from him, size and any other distinguishing characteristics\nthat the object had.\n\n          At 10:25 pm the writer contacted Mr. HAROLD N. PECK, 2nd Dist. OSI,\nU.S.A.F. and supplied him with the above information.\n\n\n                                              100-36998-8\n                                         SEARCHED......INDEXED......\n                                         SERIALIZED......FILED......\n                                               JUL - 6 1959\n                                              FBI - NEWARK\n                                                            [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\nNW 91149  [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 27", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ebb371d887cb916432f73a0aceb45edc074946192b5ba566432054585c7879c8", "output_sha256": "014b6cd5250a8e6590b15a02a36d9868ee4351b8138c779b601b4abcda28db15", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:29.466690+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p28", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 28, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO : SAC                                    DATE: 10/28/59\n\nFROM : Clerk William P. Nugent\n\nSUBJECT:    UFO SIGHTED ON 10/28/59          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n            AT APPROXIMATELY 5:40 PM         HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                             DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n          Between 5:40 and 6:45 PM on this date, this office was\nin receipt of some seven calls in regard to captioned matter.  The\nobject sighted was generally described as a very bright object with\na number of twinkling lights around it; was surrounded by a haze or\ncloud like mist; had a vapor trail which dissipated very quickly and\nwhich was of great area in the vicinity of the object.  It is to be\nnoted that the individuals calling claimed to have numerous witnesses\nto this phenomena.  The following is a list of those who contacted\nthe office and the time which they called is noted above the name,\naddress, and telephone number:\n\n                    5:55 PM                  Mr. Ecker called again at 7:25 AM\n                    Mr. Walter Ecker, →  To state that it was not the\n                    P.O. Box 327,            balloon released in Va. that he\n                    Bedminster, N.J.,        reported last night but some other object\n                    Tel. # PE8-1106\n\n\n                    6:01 PM\n                    Mr. Leonard Connors,\n                    210 19th Street,\n                    Surf City, N.J.,\n                    Tel. # HY 4-9333\n\n\n                    6:05 PM\n                    Mr. Martin Arman,\n                    25 Valley St.,\n                    East Orange, N.J. (Business Address)\n                    Tel. # SO 2-8460\n\n\n                    6:10 PM                              100-36998-19\n                    Col. Vernon A Peterson;           SEARCHED.... INDEXED......\n                    Village Road,                     SERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                    Greenwich, N.J. (Phonetic)             OCT 28 1959\n                    Tel. # FR 7-5826                       [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n                    6:45 PM\n                    Mr. Richard Stoner\n                    130 Verton Rd.,\n                    Hamilton Square, N.J. (near Trenton)\n\nNW 911149 [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 28", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d45dc74922cb26da5811a0eed3682cee1d94e6e96a962686486575f8fe8c6a89", "output_sha256": "a1b73862f78f0b5a693ce9c8178b534aa1d8ce7b8de272ba8a1f349a87b0d10d", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:31.974842+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p29", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 29, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "It is to be noted that the above telephone calls were received by the writer.\n\n      SA Gay R. Shahan was in receipt of the following calls:\n\n\n                    5:50 PM\n                    Mr. Arthur D. Lockwood,\n                    561 Oregon Ave.,\n                    Palisades Park, N.J.\n                    Tel. # WH 5-9282\n\n\n                    6:30 PM   Tel. # PI 6-8049\n                    Mrs. Richard La Bonte,\n                    11 Norwood Ave., (Upper Montclair), N.J.\n\n      Mr. PETER C. GREY, OSI duty agent for 10/28/59, was advised of the calls received by the writer and SA Shahan at 6:17 PM. (That is the calls received before that time.) At 6:40 PM, he telephonically contacted the office and requested that any calls received pertaining to this incident should be placed on a list which an OSI representative would pick up or acquire by telephone on 10/29/59.\n\n                    10/29/59- No call was received.\n                              John T. Murphy.\n\n\n\n\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 29", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0f9a127fa0edd72aa0978d9eeefa2a73ed72e8973960d7f0ca90732115d820cb", "output_sha256": "bb731df162d91ba7eec8290730354b66123cc0fd4df11c316cd67e56ab2f00b8", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:33.727064+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p30", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 30, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   :SAC                                    DATE: 1/16/60\n\nFROM :  SA WILLIAM H. ROCKETT\n\nSUBJECT: Unidentified Flying Object\n         Observed 5:45 PM\n         January 16, 1960\n                              ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                              HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                              DATE 5/15/15 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n     At approximately 5:50 PM this date, STEPHEN KLYCE,\n541 W 113 St, N.Y.C., telephonically advised that he is\nthe organist at the First Presbyterian Church, Broad\nSt., Bloomfield, N.J. PI 3-1796.  While at the church\nat about 5:45 PM this date, he and others heard what\nsounded like a roar of a jet.  On going out and looking\nat the sky they saw a bright object in the sky with a\nhazy outline around it.  It appeared to be stationary\nand was east in the direction of N.Y.C.  A plane was\npassing overhead at the same time and the UFO was about\n5,000 feet up in the sky. The UFO disappeared after about\n5 minutes.\n\n          At 6:00 PM, RALPH LAVELLA, 10 Hillcrest Avenue,\nWest Paterson, N.J., telephonically advised that at about\n5:45 PM he had seen a jet plane flying SE, heard an ex-\nplosion, saw an object leave the plane and move in an\neasterly direction.  A bright light emanated from the ob-\nject and after several minutes it appeared to drop from\nthe sky in the vicinity of N.Y.C.\n\n          At 6:03 PM, Agent M.A. SRODA, OSI, Camp Kilmer,\nN.J., KI 5-8286 was telephonically advised of the above\ninformation.\n\n          An anonymous caller furnished similar information\nat 5:47 PM and at 6:27 PM ALBERT DOUGLAS, 202 Morris Avenue,\nSpringfield, N.J., DR 6-3997, advised that at 5:45 PM,\nwhile sitting in his car in a supermarket at Spring-\nfield, N.J., he had observed a vapor trail [ILLEGIBLE] in\nthe Southern sky.  At the end of it there was a bright\nobject travelling at jet speed, then it seemed to stop,\nand remain stationary for 5 minutes and [ILLEGIBLE]\nthen disappeared.\n\n\n                                        100-36998-20\n\n[ILLEGIBLE signature]                   SERIAL CAM\n                                        JAN 15 1960\n                                        FBI - N. WARD\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 30", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "51f39fbe1ce5d41e04f537b67715aab447656d47e1e4152c0f8e80346b46ab57", "output_sha256": "b1332a1b117c43e70c16cd079aa2824d22044d7b3357d3a98ab7b79c9d41a842", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:36.498387+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p31", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 31, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC (100-36998)                    DATE: 2/27/60\n\nFROM : Clerk William P. Nugent\n\nSUBJECT: UFO SIGHTED ON 2/27/60          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n         by S.M. KAPLAN OVER             HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n         BLOOMFIELD, N.J.               DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n          The writer received a telephonic contact from\nMR. S. M. KAPLAN, 19 Alfred Lane, Bloomfield, N.J. [REDACTED]\nat 6:35 PM this date.  He advised a group of neighbors\nand himself had seen a UFO and reported the details\nconcerning it.\n\n          The writer telephonically contacted OSI agent\nLa Belle, the duty man for this date, and advised him\nof the incident.  He stated that he did not want the\ndetails as he would get them first hand from Kaplan,\nthanked the writer, and terminated the conversation.\n\n\n                                    100-36998-21\n                              SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]    INDEXED\n                              SERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE] [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                    FEB 29 1960\n                              [ILLEGIBLE] WARD\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149 [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 21", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "99881b20fca50ea2176e504dd2bf263ead4a2c24f8d3632f671f33b5c4f13e59", "output_sha256": "0342496a2fed5f1f4757228083fbaab84763e2adb124a70bf532ae9cd4666433", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:38.329343+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p32", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 32, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\n3010-104-01\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\nMemorandum\n\nTO   : SAC NEWARK                              DATE: 10/[?]/60\n\nFROM  : IC D. LOUIS BARRA JR.\n\nSUBJECT:  UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT          RFC NO\n          OBSERVED EARLY MORNING         ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n          9/5/60                         HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                         DATE 5/15/85  BY S26b[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n          Alethea Charney, 464 Jefferson Ave. Elizabeth, New\nJersey, telephonically contacted the Newark office on 10/7/60.\n\n          Complainant indicated that she had telephonically\nadvised the Newark office 9/5/60, that she had seen a flying\nsaucer in the early morning.\n\n          On 10/7/60 she received a call from a person who identified\nhimself as a Federal officer, and he indicated that he was\ncoming to see her regarding the information she had concerning\nthe flying saucer.  The caller never kept his appointment with\nher.  Charney desired to know if it had been a FBI agent who had\nmade this call.\n\n          A search of the indices by the writer failed to disclose\nany record of the above mentioned call.  A check with OSI\nNewark, failed to reflect any more light on the problem.\n\n          Charney was contacted and advised, that it was not an FBI\nagent that had contacted her, but it could have been one of\nseveral federal agencies.  She was requested to advise the\nNewark office if she received any more information.  She indicated\nshe would do so.\n\n          The above information is recorded for filing purposes.\n\n\nShe called again\nat 5:00 PM 10/[?]/60\n& stated she had\nbeen recontacted\nby Investigator Gray\nFederal Aviation Agency\nHe made an appointment\nfor a later date\n[ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\n                                    100-36998-22\n                          SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                          SERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                OCT 7  1960\n                              FBI — NEWARK\n                                         4\n\nNW 91149  [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 32", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e5cf17423791e29ea6e663786ea9a50a831a5a97222ba2a60a516634e03f9f62", "output_sha256": "3d198667919b59acac0eeff7cb649ef5c78a838acf8e86e2937ad243fa252564", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:42.573985+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p33", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 33, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\n5010-104\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\nMemorandum\n\nTO   : SAC, NEWARK (62-0)                    DATE: 2/8/61\n\nFROM : SA WILLIAM E. GAGNON\n\n                                    ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nSUBJECT:  JOHN MURPHY               HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n          Information Concerning     DATE 5/15/18  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n        MR. JOHN MURPHY, 1054 Seward Avenue, Westfield,\nNew Jersey, telephone AD 2-6277, telephonically contacted\nthis office on the evening at which time he furnished the\nfollowing information:\n\n          He stated that while driving home in his car last\nSunday, 2/5/61, around 7:00 p.m., he noticed an extremely\nbright object in the sky. He stated that this object, which\nis not a star, appeared to be round in shape and much larger\nthan a star. He stated that this object, which he could not\nfurther describe, appeared to the Northwest of his residence.\n\n          He stated that he saw this same object on Monday\nand Tuesday evenings, and that tonight there were three similar\ntype objects in the sky. He stated that one object appeared\nto be Northwest of his residence; one to the West and the\nother to the North of his residence. He stated that these\nobjects, however, had changed from a round shape to lateral\nshape and appeared to be much like a spectrum.\n\n          He stated that his wife told him he had been drink-\ning and imagining things. He stated that he had his daughter\nwho is a school teacher, his son, his wife and a neighbor out\nlooking at these objects and they had verified his findings.\nHe stated that he didn't understand these objects and for this\nreason wanted to report this matter to this office. He stated\nhe had reported this matter to the Westfield, N.J. Police De-\npartment but they were too busy to check on this because they\nwere shoveling snow. He stated he tried to report the matter\nto Civilian Defense but there was no answer.\n\n          He stated that since he did not understand these\nobjects and he did not know whether they were weather balloons\nor foreign objects, he wanted to report this matter to the FBI\nfor whatever action deemed appropriate.\n\n          No action recommended.          100-36998-23\n(1)\nWEG   Note Telephone directory lists T. G. MURPHY\n      at 1050 SEWARD AVE, WESTFIELD  SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]\n      TEL. AD 2-6277.                              1001\n\n2-10-61                                        FBI — NEWARK\nLuke Dempsey OSI Nwk. alerted\nP.S.\n\nNW 91149\nDocld:34742114  Page 33", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "53dee1b8e51c6572b6e0cdbcea4894de0f1804bd4feaf4fc7be80e5ebab97fce", "output_sha256": "7084c16dd75d47362f12f52fb13c5e2890da89bd3c2c5904dea22b385b52184b", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:45.403989+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p34", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 34, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum · UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO   : SAC, NEWARK                          DATE: 2/6/61\n\nFROM  : SA JAMES R. LAUGHLIN\n\nSUBJECT:  UNSUB; Bright Object in Sky,        ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n          West of Paterson, N.J.              HEREIN [ILLEGIBLE] IFIED\n          7:50pm 2/6/61                       DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                                              DRIVE\n     At 7:50 pm 2/6/61 Mrs. BERNICE ABRAMS, 174 Elmwood Terrace,\nEast Paterson, N.J. telephone SW 6-4442 telephonically contacted the\nwriter at the Paterson Resident Agency.  She advised that there is\na very bright object in the sky west of Paterson, N.J. She said she has\nnever seen this object before and does not believe it is a star since she\nis accustomed to viewing the stars.  Her husband, CARL, got on the phone\nand advised he first saw this object this evening while driving from Newark\non the Garden State Parkway; that first it was west of him and then\nsouth of him.\n\n     They advised they did not know whom to call but felt the Federal\nGovernment should be made aware of this peculiar object in the sky.\n                                        100-36998-34\nLuke Dempry OST NE.              100-36998-34\nadvised 2-10-61 F.L.        SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                            SERIAL [ILLEGIBLE] FILED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                 FEB - 8 1961\n                               FBI — NEWARK\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:24742114  Page 34", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "205df2997ad2186d67411a99e82009fe628d4c89bc61d5e9447f4a30176d80ea", "output_sha256": "6c181fa160366d3ba234e28964c61024f786930e56dd11e9e962805372566aa1", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:47.745224+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p35", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 35, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\n5010-104\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\nMemorandum\n\nTO   :  SAC NEWARK                          DATE:   1/16/61\n\nFROM  :  IC D. LOUIS BARRA JR.\n\nSUBJECT:   UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECTS   ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n           INFORMATION CONCERNING        HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                         DATE 3/15/10 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\nIndex\n        Mrs. George Doarcke, 122 Main Street, Franklin,\nNew Jersey, telephonically contacted the Newark office today.\nShe indicated that she has seen objects in the sky on\nseveral occasions which she was unable to identify.\n\n        Complainant related that she has other information\nshe would like to furnish to a FBI agent, but was unable\nto explain any further on the phone.\n\n        Doarcke was very vague concerning her complaint\nand would not discuss the information she desired to furnish\nthe FBI, while she was on the phone.\n\n        The above data is recorded for information and\nis suggested that a agent contact complainant to determine\nif she has any information of any value to the FBI.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                        100-36998-25\n                                        62-0-15013\n                                        [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                   SEARCHED .... INDEXED ..........\ntransfer to                        SERIALIZED .... LED ..........\n100-36998                               JAN 1 6 1961\n                                        FBI — NEWARK\n                                   R.C. Lee GRC\n                                   (contact Doarcke) $1.ws\n\nNW 91149 [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 35", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9d87cc92bf73ec533029266366e6541d32eb3d7fc1cc21be226192c1ec82c03e", "output_sha256": "ab8100d9ca8dd73d6834d754a13a00603a837aeaa60ba4dda0a0d548cdc7cb30", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:49.715001+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p36", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 36, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\n5010-104\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\nMemorandum\n\nTO  :SAC, NEWARK (62-0-15013)          DATE: 2/14/61\n\nFROM :SA RICHARD C. LEE\n                                        SEARCHED      INDEXED\n                                        SERIALIZED .........FILED\n                                             FEB 15 1961\nSUBJECT: UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECTS        FBI — NEWS\n         INFORMATION CONCERNING\n\n        Re memo of SC. D. Louis Barra Jr. dated 1/16/61 at Newark.\nIndex\n        On 2/13/61 Mrs. George Goarcke, 122 Main St. Franklin, N.J.\nadvised that she had approximately one month ago seen an article in\nthe Newark News concerning unidentified flying objects that were a\nmatter of concern to the U.S. She stated that as a result of this ar-\nticle she recalled that in either 1938 or 1939 she attended the Newark\nArt School and had a teacher by the name of John Grabach, who resided\nat 915 Sanford Ave. Irvington, N.J. Mrs. Goarcke stated that on one\noccasion in 1939 Grabach had requested her to do a drawing of Boulder\nDam which was to be used for purposes of reprinting. She stated that\nshe had never been paid for this drawing and that she has had no contact\nwith Grabach since that time.\n\n        Mrs. Goarcke also stated that she believed that these uniden-\ntified flying objects could be used to obtain pictures of such install-\nations as Boulder Dam which idea occurred to her as a result of the above\nmentioned article in the Newark News. Mrs. Goarcke also stated that in\n1939 Grabach was in sympathy with communism and damned the American Way\nof life.\n\n        Mrs. Goarcke was during the course of the interview inclined\nto wander in her thought process and appeared on occasions to be in a\ndaze. She could not furnish any information other than she believed\n                                        SERIALIZED    FILED\nthat unidentified flying objects could be used to take pictures of\nBoulder Dam.   ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED                FEB 2 0 1961\n               HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED                   FBI - NEWARK\n               DATE 3/15/85  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 36", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3035800e84291b2a9dd5e41cf8b9e0fe4493cc6fa42d2de406acae72f8af5ea9", "output_sha256": "aee7009bdab544711f56fecd40c3e34eec481b9b1dc8b98c8d4689ba89a4eab4", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:52.154631+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p37", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 37, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "STANDARD FORM NO. 64\n\nOffice Memorandum • UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nTO    : SAC, NEWARK (100-36998)                    DATE: 9/13/61\n\nFROM  : SA FRED V. CROWLEY\n        Night Supervisor\n\nSUBJECT: UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n         OBSERVED 8 pm, 9/13/61.             HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                             DATE 9/15/15  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n        From 8:10 pm to 9:00 pm, 9/13/61, the following persons called\nto report that at approximately 8 pm, they had observed a very bright\nobject about midway elevation above the horizon in the sky, slightly\nSouth of East.\n\n        The object appeared to have a reddish or tangerine color and\nincreased in size as if some type of explosion. There was no apparent\nmovement or noise connected.\n\n                WILLIAM BRANDT\n                753 Jersey Ave.,\n                Elizabeth, N.J.\n\n                MIKE HARTTEN\n                Fords, N.J.\n\n                GORDON SCHACHER,\n                Physics Dept.,\n                Rutgers University,\n                New Brunswick, N.J.\n\n        The above calls were reported to Duty Agent PETER MARTIN,\nHqrs. 2d Dist., OSI (IG)USAF, 111 East 16th St., New York, N.Y.,\nOR 7-2800. MARTIN requested that OSI, Newark, be advised through\nliaison, as verification.\n\n                    9/14/61\nabove info. furnished to\nJack Labelle, OSI, Newark.\n                John T. Murphy\n\nFVC\n(1)\n\n                                            100 36998-27\n                                    SEARCHED........INDEXED\n                                    SERIALIZED.......FILED\n                                         SEPT 4 1961\n                                         FBI - NEWARK\n                                         [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 27", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fcc16f6809d291b837074d7a0df8e104bbe2de4c5ce25a21af1b3cdddc940ac1", "output_sha256": "649bf2c67ee059cdef7a209521efa20262bb7e9f508941adaeef2367776a5544", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:54.261313+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p38", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 38, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "NEW JERSEY ASSOCIATION ON\nAERIAL PHENOMENA\n\nSTATE FILTER CENTER #1\n69 HOBART STREET\nHACKENSACK, N.J.\n\nDI. 2-6500\n\nSEPTEMBER 19, 1962\n\n\nDEAR SIRS:\n\n     The New Jersey Association on Aerial Phenomena is extremely interested in the recent sighting of an unidentified flying object by officers Rudloff and Troy. We would appreciate any information available.\n\n\n                                        Sincerely,\n                                        John Nove'\n                                        John Nove', Secretary\n\n\n     ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n     HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n     DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]        100-36998-28\n                                                dcf\n                                        SEP 2 7 1962\n                                        -- NEWARK\n                                            fh\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 38", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a9d0c47356ce337cb3d23913eb272eb710b20330d6d4cf299cc0920ddc401d06", "output_sha256": "b44847c28944aaced31f1f009138f934b52e5fbf29aed27d4f27e84c535d86a5", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:55.428592+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p39", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 39, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\n5010-104-01\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\nMemorandum\n\nTO :    SAC, NEWARK                    DATE:  3/12/64\n\nFROM :  [ILLEGIBLE] SAC, NEW YORK\n\n                                ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                                HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nSUBJECT:   JOHN NOVE              DATE 5/15/85  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n           69 HOBART STREET           36998-25\n           HACKENSACK, NEW JERSEY\n           INFORMATION CONCERNING\n\n          Mr. SAM NOVE telephonically contacted this office\non 3/9/64, in an attempt to obtain an opinion concerning his\nson's membership in an organization.\n\n          Mr. NOVE's son, JOHN, age 16, who attends school\nin Hackensack has joined some type of peace organization\ncontrary to his father's wishes.  This organization has\nbeen given permission to hold meetings in the school and to\nrecruit students.  The organization is sponsoring a students\npeace march from Hackensack to Newark.\n\n          Mr. NOVE was advised of the confidential nature of\nFBI files and that his call would be made a matter of record.\n\n\n\n\n\n2 - Newark                          100-B6998-28a\n1 - New York                    SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                SERIALIZED\nKRS:MAH                             MAR 13 1964\n(3)\n                                [ILLEGIBLE] Jennelly [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                (Info)", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d59e3ba9e0b977c1cd2034d8445f2175b1b5d2dbe5e5262a0cd5dc67ed204c37", "output_sha256": "1b09d7394b77fe510c79f35b91269082fbecae4232f6929b01112a7a78c91c3f", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:57.235944+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p40", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 40, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF POLICE\nWESTWOOD, NEW JERSEY\n\nJOHN C. LINDEMANN, CHIEF\n\nPHONES:\nHEADQUARTERS: NORTH 4-7000\nCHIEF: NORTH 4-7040\nSept. 24, 1962\n\nSpecial Agent, Mc Grail,\nF.B.I. Office,\nP.O. Box #336,\nHackensack, N.J.\n\nDear Sir :-\n\n        Per your request, letter received by this Dept. from N.J.\nAssociation on Aerial Phenomena, State Filter Center # 1, 69 Hobart\nSt., Hackensack, N.J. signed by JOHN NOVE' Secretary, herewith enclosed.\n\n                                Very truly yours,\n\n                                Capt. H.E. Voorhis.\n\n                                Capt. H.E. Voorhis.\n\nach by\n  Mc Grail\n    h.\n\n                                        100-36998-29\n                                    FILED    INDEXED\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE]  [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                    SEP 27 1962\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE] - NEWARK\n                                         h\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE 6/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 40", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f90d30792b4c9fc76c4397e8fa3ddc03b2d5f0e5ca8e06bf3d0f1449d3064f42", "output_sha256": "f90d30792b4c9fc76c4397e8fa3ddc03b2d5f0e5ca8e06bf3d0f1449d3064f42", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:08:58.843997+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p41", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 41, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10          5010-106\nMAY 1962 EDITION\nGSA GEN. REG. NO. 27\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nMemorandum\n\nTO   :        SAC, NEWARK (62-0)              DATE:     3/8/63\n\nFROM :        SA LOUIS F. HIBAN, JR.\n\nSUBJECT:      WILLIAM STOCKS,   No 62 rmv  88-957#\n              45 Kipp Avenue,                    #88ug\n              Lodi, New Jersey      ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n              INFORMATION CONCERNING HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                    DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n          On 3/1/63, the subject telephonically contacted the\nHackensack, New Jersey Resident Agency and advised that he is\nemployed as a guard for a detective agency and last night, he\nobserved flying objects in the air over Lodi, New Jersey.\nSTOCKS believes that these flying objects were flying saucers\nand he would like to furnish this information to the appropriate\nfederal agency.\n\n          STOCKS advised that he observed flying saucers over\nLodi, New Jersey, on 9/15/62 and notified the local police\ndepartment of this event.  STOCKS stated that on this date,\ntwo patrol cars from the Lodi, New Jersey Police Department\narrived at the scene, but they did nothing about this occurrence.\nSTOCKS stated that he has documents and affidavits that he sent\nto the United States Air Force in Washington, D.C., regarding\nthis event.\n\n          At the conclusion of the interview, STOCKS advised\nthat he would contact the United States Air Force in Newark,\nNew Jersey, and advise them of these flying objects he observed\nfor their information and any action they deem appropriate.\n\n          No action is deemed warranted in this matter, and it\nis suggested that the subject's name be indexed inasmuch as\nhe may contact the FBI in the future regarding flying saucers.\n\n\nLFH:mjf  mjb\n(1)\n                                    cl   100-36998-30\n                                        SEARCHED .......... INDEXED\n              S-1                       SERIALIZED .... FILED\n                                             MAR  8 1963\n                                             FBI — NEWARK\n                                                        [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nNW 91149\nDocID:34742114  Page 41", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e29adc11ae144b7633e039a949954ed6c11f1817be8cc829f239e970b9f770da", "output_sha256": "c2cf67c665832e4c3fad00b8f54c3f07bf5e92524a9e9e6131b1296a4c9ca7f8", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:01.386307+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p42", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 42, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "Indices Search Slip\nFD-160 (Rev. 10-1-59)\n\n\n                                                    Date\nTO: CHIEF CLERK\nSubject\n(1) James Mosely\nAliases\n\nAddress                              Birth Date    Birthplace           Race    Sex\n                                                                               □Male\n                                                                               □Female\n\n□  Exact Spelling              □  Main Criminal Case Files Only        □  Restrict to Locality of\n□  All References              □  Criminal References Only\n□  Main Subversive Case Files Only  □  Main Subversive (If no Main, list all Subversive References)\n□  Subversive References Only  □  Main Criminal (If no Main, list all Criminal References)\n\nFile & Serial Number          Remarks          File & Serial Number          Remarks\n\n(1) 100-4284-1A-8\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                              ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                              HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                              DATE 5/15/15  BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n\n\nRequested by                          Squad         Extension     File No.\n\nSearched by\n                              (date)\nConsolidated by\n                              (date)\nReviewed by\n                              (date)\n\n               File Review Symbols\n  I  - Identical              ? - Not identifiable\n  NI - Not identical          U - Unavailable reference\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 42", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2329d74e024e2d035e877583e86336bc475a8c1ccd7cb5f7f2f59c977f653404", "output_sha256": "e0669c8340665cc9a1e0c1a5881e63121807ed6dfc7915cef3d1d4b2357b3e8d", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:02.971539+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p43", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 43, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\nWASHINGTON\n\nOFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\n\n                                        20 February 1963\n\n\nDear Mr. Hoover:\n\n     It has been some length of time since I've written you on a\nsubject of mutual interest---Unidentified Flying Objects.  When I\nlast contacted you, I was then Department of Defense spokesman for\nProject Blue Book, the organization responsible for investigation\nof UFO sightings, a part of our Foreign Technology Division located\nat Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, Ohio.  I turned over my respon-\nsibilities as spokesman to Major Carl Hart of our Division a year\nago last month, when I was moved up to Deputy Chief of the Operations\nBranch, Public Information Division.\n\n     I thought the Bureau might be interested in the inclosed \"burn\"\ncopy of a letter which was printed in the March 1963 issue of \"Saucer\nNews\" (now in its tenth year of publication).  This publication is\nprinted quarterly by the \"Saucer and Unexplained Celestial Events\nResearch Society\"---James W. Mosely, Editor.  It takes a middle-of-\nthe-road editorial policy, printing views of non-believers, believers,\ncontactees, etc., and reviews books on the \"flying saucer\" subject.\n\n     With best wishes, I am,\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              WILLIAM T. COLEMAN, JR.\n                              Major, USAF\n                              Deputy Chief, Operations Branch\n                              Public Information Division\n                              Office of Information\n\nMr. J. Edgar Hoover\nDirector\nFederal Bureau of Investigation\n9th & Pennsylvania Ave., N. W.\nWashington, D. C.\n\n1PS Incl 35 LN 83\n     \"Saucer News\"\n\n                                        cartoon!\n                              The\n                                        SEARCH INDEX\n                              SERIALIZED\n                                        FE 27 1963\n                                        FBI - NEWARK\n                              The cartoon is a bonus item!  C.\n\n                                        100-36998-32\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 43", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7479b6628f08242f702ff827c53537491905c9daf68b7f124cd88ded008c6893", "output_sha256": "e53dc43a9a891ebbf9f30271b39ef0732a656750188458afa66913981c370fee", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:05.270693+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p44", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 44, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "VOLUME 10, NUMBER 1                    STARTING OUR TENTH YEAR                    MARCH\n  (Whole Number 51)                       OF PUBLICATION!                           1963\n\n              SAUCER NEWS\n\n    OFFICIAL PUBLICATION OF THE SAUCER AND UNEXPLAINED CELESTIAL EVENTS RESEARCH SOCIETY\n\nMAILING ADDRESS: P. O. BOX 163, FORT LEE, N. J.                    EDITOR:\nOFFICE: ROOM 1009, 303 FIFTH AVE., NEW YORK, N. Y.                 JAMES W. MOSELEY\nTELEPHONE: MURRAY HILL 6-3743\n\n\n          There has been a delay in the publication of my forthcoming book,\n\"The Second Coming of Christ and Flying Saucers!\" I had plans to have it printed instead of mimeographed. I took it to a printer and he obtained legal advice that didn't recommend its publication. I was told by the attorney that\nthe book was too harshly critical of the U. S. Government, particularly the\nFBI, and that this might bring legal trouble; and that other parts of the manuscript are so controversial that they might cause libel suits. He felt that\nyou might sue me. I tried others, but after reading the manuscript, they would\nnot print it.\n          This meant I had to send out notices to purchasers of the book\nthat I would have to put out a mimeographed edition, and this would not come\nout before March. \"Flying Saucer Review\" turned down my ad, but so far, other\nmagazines plan to publish it in January and February. All will be given a\n                                              chance to order it, and\n                                              all orders will be shipped the same day. The\n                                              book will mean my arrest\n                                              and so I plan to release\n                                              all copies in one day.\n                                              If I were to fill orders\n                                              as they came in, then\n                                              someone on the list\n                                              might be a secret Government agent, or would\n                                              turn it over to the authorities as a book that\n                                              threatens the national\n                                              security of the U.S.;\n                                              and the rest of the copies would be confiscated. This is based on the advice of the attorney who read\nthe manuscript. After getting that advice, I am keeping the contents of the\nbook secret until its release in March. Thus, the Government has no idea just\nwhat I intend to release, until too late! After the orders are shipped in that\none mailing, they can come and arrest me for all I care. My life's mission for\nJesus Christ will have been fulfilled, and my goal accomplished. The truth,\neven if it should violate man-made law, will be sent out to seekers of truth.\n....So I risk personal ruin to get this thing out; but one must make sacrifices in the name of Christ if one is worthy to enter the kingdom of Heaven.\nIn the eyes of the Government, the book will be considered dangerous, but in\nthe eyes of God, it will be considered Truth.\n                         RICHARD OGDEN\n                    P.O. Box 9005, Seattle, Washington\n\n(Editor's Note: We will be looking forward to Mr. Ogden's book with interest\nand avid curiosity, though from the tone of this and other letters he has sent\nus on the subject, we doubt if it will ever be published.)\n\n\nNW 91149  [REDACTED]\nDocId:24742114  Page 44", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1ac19a00e515e178a067b49798e43af05b2ff21452d50f9a4c9e183842976041", "output_sha256": "f1843cd774c615f08b3a9d442a5247081b25b2281ec28bc7ce1802f7ad5f86fc", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:08.716944+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p45", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 45, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "February 26, 1963\n\nMajor William T. Coleman, Jr.\nDeputy Chief, Operations Branch\nPublic Information Division\nOffice of Information\nDepartment of the Air Force\nWashington, D. C.\n\nDear Major:\n\n          Thank you for your letter of February 20th,\n\nwith enclosure.  Your thoughtfulness in writing and furnishing\n\nme a copy of a letter printed in the March, 1963, issue of\n\n\"Saucer News\" is indeed appreciated.\n\n                         Sincerely yours,\n\n                         J. Edgar Hoover\n\n1 - Seattle - Enclosures (2)\n1 - Newark - Enclosures (2)\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE 2/15/85  BY P. [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                              100-36998-33\n\n                    SEARCHED    INDEXED\n                    SERIALIZED\n                         FEB 27 [ILLEGIBLE]\n                         F.B.I. NEWARK\n\nNW 91149\nDocID:34742114  Page 46", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f78095cccdcf018103e4d4b119943d4521afea3193e7f62f46d2c4672ef47122", "output_sha256": "b254d371333e9c767a489dff67c3909dbbf22b555db834a3ed5538c1ac148a50", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:10.894944+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p46", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 46, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "7 Idlewild Lane\n        Matawan, New Jersey\n        January 15, 1964\n\nState of Arizona\nDepartment of Law and Public Safety\nDivision of State Police\nState House\nPhoenix, Arizona\n\nDear Sirs:\n\n        I am a member of the National Investigations\nCommittee on Aerial Phenomena (NICAP), headquarters\nWashington, D.C., and would greatly appreciate your\nanswering the following questions:\n\n        1- Has the United States Air Force compelled\nyou in any way, thru official orders or otherwise, to\nwithhold from the press media and the general public\nany information you might obtain from investigating\nan unidentified flying object sighting reported to\nyou or any county or local police force in the State\nof Arizona?\n\n        2- If the answer to question #1 is in the\nnegative what is the Arizona State Police policy regarding UFO sightings reported to you in releasing\ninformation on said sightings to the press media and\ngeneral public?\n\n        3- Have you investigated any recent UFO reports and, if so, what were the results of those investigations?\n\n        Thank you.\n\n                        Sincerely yours,\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE 5/22/85  BY SP-6bje[ILLEGIBLE]    John Laval\n                        NICAP member\n\n                                        100-36 998-34\n\n                                SEARCHED\nSERIALIZED\n                                FEB 19 1964\n                                FBI - NEWARK\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 46", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8570d4a7a4fc77b5d132b221cdc123c6d6907325395e65521b086e8d4832a9d4", "output_sha256": "b2bbc2844f1dcb0a2f861fb7eb9e70895b8d0124bb8c1516549d5c02d00d35c7", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:13.747150+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p47", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 47, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "UNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE\n\nFEDERAL BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION\n\nIn Reply, Please Refer to\nFile No.\n\n                    Phoenix, Arizona\n\n\n                              February 14, 1964\n\n\n     RE: JOHN LAVAL\n         MEMBER, NATIONAL INVESTIGATIONS\n         COMMITTEE ON AERIAL PHENOMENA\n         INFORMATION CONCERNING\n\n\n          Attached is copy of letter received by\n     the Arizona Highway Patrol from JOHN LAVAL, 7 Idle-\n     wild Lane, Matawan, New Jersey, in which he states\n     he is a member of the above organization the NICAP,\n     Washington, D. C., and requesting information.\n\n\n\n\n          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n          HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n          DATE 5/22/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   100-36998-35\n                         SEARCHED        INDEXED\n                         SERIALIZED\n                                FEB 19 1964\n                               FBI — NEWARK\n\n\nNW 91149 [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 47", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "91138651d1bf3ab0b49a0de804dae985094d6afe0b3f751622233eaf4f7e6ee0", "output_sha256": "91138651d1bf3ab0b49a0de804dae985094d6afe0b3f751622233eaf4f7e6ee0", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:15.198349+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p48", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 48, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "DIRECTOR, FBI                                    2/14/64\n\nSAC, PHOENIX (62-0)\n\nJOHN LAVAL,\nMEMBER, NATIONAL INVESTIGATIONS     ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nCOMMITTEE ON AERIAL PHENOMENA       HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nINFORMATION CONCERNING              DATE 5/29/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nFor the information of the Bureau and possible dissemination, there is enclosed letterhead memorandum concerning communication from the above individual to the Arizona Highway Patrol in Phoenix.\n\nNewark is being furnished copy of letterhead memorandum for information, since LAVAL gave his address as 7 Idlewild Lane, Matawan, New Jersey.\n\n\n2 - Bureau (5) [ILLEGIBLE]\n(1)- Newark (enc 1)  REGISTERED\n1 - Phoenix (62-0)\n\n\nELB-kb\n  (4)\n\n\n\n\n                                        [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                              100-36998-36\n                         SEARCHED    INDEXED\n                         SERIALIZED\n                              FEB 19 1964\n                              FBI — NEWARK\n                                    [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9fbb2865454617040ded3cefc3da4d088215c88e225b17f6b11037d23df147e3", "output_sha256": "755629fa9608494a6ff7f61a3aee51ab3bdcae20b9b77f706720a6828d60391e", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:17.523522+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p49", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 49, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "FD-159 (Rev. 6-29-59)\n\nRECORD OF INFORMATION FURNISHED OTHER AGENCIES\n\nOrally _____________ By Telephone 4/2/64 Written Communication ___________\n          date                        date                                              date\nInformation concerning:\n\n     National Investigations Committee\n     on Aerial Phenomenon\n\nInformation furnished from File, Serial, and Page Number:\n\n          100 - 36998-\n\nInformation furnished was obtained:\n\n     □ during course of Bureau investigation\n\n     □ from informants\n\n     ☒ from complainants or other sources\n\nInformation furnished to:\n\n     Joseph Clark, OSI\n\nRemarks: Was advised there was no\n     derogatory information\n     in file re above.\n\n                              ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                              HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                              DATE 5/15/85 BY SP.6 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                              100-36998-37\n                              SEARCHED ........... INDEXED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                              SERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                    APR 2  1964\n                                    FBI — NEWARK\n\n                              John T. Murphy\n                                    Special Agent\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page:49", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c6f84b99867b131c3d8a921f5eaea1824ec910e5563b808974a1f3a474b55fa7", "output_sha256": "c6f84b99867b131c3d8a921f5eaea1824ec910e5563b808974a1f3a474b55fa7", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:18.964374+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p50", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 50, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "Post Office Box #1158\n Newark, New Jersey  07101\n\n June 8, 1964\n\n\nLt. Col. Robert S. Hermann\nDistrict Commander\nHeadquarters 2nd OSI District (I.G.)\nU. S. Air Force\n111 East 16th Street\nNew York 3, New York\n                              ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n                              HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                              DATE 9/15/15 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\nDear Lt. Col. Hermann:\n\n          On the evening of May 30, 1964, Theodore John\nRubitz, age 13, of 167 West 19th Street, Bayonne, New\nJersey, telephone Federal 9-8738, telephonically advised\nthis office that at about 9:50 PM on May 30, 1964, he was\nwalking along 22nd Street in Bayonne between Avenue A and\nNewark Bay when he observed five unidentified flying objects.\n\n          He described these objects as being round and gray\nin color, flying north to south in a diamond-shaped formation,\nwith the fifth object just in back and to the right of the\nlast object in the diamond.  He stated that they were very\nhigh up, looking like they might be lights but traveled\nacross the sky faster than the speed of a plane and he\nwas certain that these were not just planes or search lights.\nRubitz was unable to further identify these objects.\n\n          Mrs. Theodore Rubitz, mother of Theodore, advised\nthat her son was not given to fanciful stories and that from\nwhat he had told her, she was sure that he had seen the\nobjects described by him.\n\n                                   Very truly yours,\n\n\n                                   [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n                                   R. W. Bachman\n                                   Special Agent in Charge\n\nRegistered Mail\n\n  2-OSI, New York\n  1-Newark (100-36998)\n  GPH:rac\n[ILLEGIBLE] (3)\n[ILLEGIBLE]\n[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                                        100-36998-38\n\nNW 91149 [REDACTED]\nDocId:34742114  Page 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0fecdc1f8c111886fa57f3fccf2e8a6c566ad9b368ad8a70f03fc1bdbc6772f7", "output_sha256": "a064fd310ee42463179ce6b7a4e97bf069bbf359405d85ef819cdad7d3e7b322", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:21.119041+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p51", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 51, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "OPTIONAL FORM NO. 10\nMAY 1962 EDITION\nGSA FPMR (41 CFR) 101-11.6\n\nUNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\n\nMemorandum\n\nTO   : SAC, NEWARK (62-    )                    DATE:7/11/66\n\nFROM : SA JOHN J. CREAMER, JR.\n\nSUBJECT: UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECTS          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n         West Orange, N.J., 7/11/66.          HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n                                              DATE 3/25/85  BY S06 6[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n        At 10:18pm, 7/11/66, NANCY RAUCH, 141 Old Short Hills Rd.,\nWest Orange, NJ., telephone 731-8336, advised that she and her\ngirl friend saw three white objects in the sky at about 10:00PM.\nTwo planes came towards the objects from two opposite directions\nas if they were chasing them. As the planes drew near them, the\nobjects disappeared.\n        RAUCH'S friend is SUSAN SHAW, 18 Maplewood Dr., Livingston,\nN.J.\n\n        Officer Murphy, W.Orange N.J. P.D. was contacted and he advised\nthat there has been no reports of unidentified objects in the area.\n\n        Recommendation: Notify proper authorities.\n\n\n\n\n                                              100-36998-39\n                                         SEARCHED..........INDEXED..........\n                                         SERIALIZED.........FILED..............\n                                                  JUL 1 1 1966\n                                               FBI — NEWARK\n\nJJC/jjc\n(1)\n\n\n\n\n                  Buy U.S. Savings Bonds Regularly on the Payroll Savings Plan\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 51", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4acd04a198dee8f882f20f80a49c894514f21a7258286bd84f2a0dcc0c7d27c9", "output_sha256": "4acd04a198dee8f882f20f80a49c894514f21a7258286bd84f2a0dcc0c7d27c9", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:23.171434+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p52", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 52, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "FD-350 (Rev. 7-16-63)\n\n(Mount Clipping in Space Below)\n\nUFO Sightings\n53\nObjects Seen in Wanaque, Newark\n\nA large shining unidentified flying object hovered over the Wanaque reservoir and was seen by police and more than a dozen residents last night. Another sighting was reported in Newark.\n\nAt about 9:25 p.m., the reservoir police were swamped with phone calls, which reported a mysterious flying object had flown over the Wolf Den Dam and landed in the reservoir in Upper Passaic County.\n\nReservoir Police Sgt. Ben Thompson who investigated radioed back to headquarters reporting that a large object, about the size of an automobile was hovering over the reservoir at a height of about 150 feet.\n\n\"It's lighting up practically the whole southern end of the reservoir\" Thompson told Patrolmen Edward Webster and William Pastor who were at headquarters at the time.\n\nObject Disappears\n\nThompson then turned on the red light atop his police car. The object disappeared.\n\nBoth Webster and Pastor said they saw the object fly off in a northerly direction.\n\n\"It definitely wasn't a plane,\" said Pastor.\n\nPastor explained that the object which flew away at a height of several hundred feet, would sometimes stop and hover in one spot for several seconds and then move off with great speed.\n\n\"Sometimes it would disappear for a second or two and then you could see it again,\" he said, adding:\n\n\"We finally lost sight of it shortly before 10 p.m. It was heading north over the upper end of the reservoir toward New York State.\"\n\nHad Been Seen Before\n\nPastor said the object had been seen several times before but it had not gotten this close to the water recently.\n\nHe said that Air Force officials had taken pictures of the object in January, after it was seen one night by about 50 persons in the area.\n\nHe added that the Air Force officials who investigated the January sightings made no comment on the UFO.\n\nAir Force officials at bases in this state and New York said they knew nothing about UFO reports last night.\n\nNorvel Wilson of 33 Burnet St., Newark, reported his attention was attracted to the sky over his home by a whirring noise which he found hard to describe and spotted what appeared to be a large kite with a string of lights several hundred feet in the air. He said the object disappeared as it headed southward.\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE: 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n(Indicate page, name of newspaper, city and state.)\n\n53\nNEWARK EVENING NEWS,\nNEWARK, N.J.\n\nDate: 10/11/66\nEdition:    WALL ST.\nAuthor:\nEditor: WILLIAM R. CLARK\nTitle:\n\nCharacter:\n   or\nClassification:\nSubmitting Office: NEWARK, N.J.\n\n□ Being Investigated\n\nSEARCHED ...............INDEXED..................\nSERIALIZED/AC.........FILED, A.C. Acr\n         OCT 12 1966\n         FBI — NEWARK\n\n100- 36898-40\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "561ad42369631f76987eb38b399179bd3a90728ba444cd1036bb2c7d82ae2022", "output_sha256": "0ee64bfd7b968489cf719874698559819b8dea10fa4e3e4b1668dd3d7ae9abe9", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:26.191107+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p53", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 53, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "25 Clifton Ave.\nNewark, N.J. 07107\nDec. 10, 1966\n\nF.B.I.,\nFederal Sq.\nNewark, N.J.\n\nDear Sir:\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n     This \"AFSCT\" is definitely a Communist\nOrganization. Of you read the lines I have\nunderlined in red, I'm sure you will agree.\n     Hope something can be done to stop\nthem.\n\n                              Sincerely Yours,\n                              Mrs. M. Stein\n                                   2527\n                              134-\n                              100-[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nClosed\n   K.K.\n\n                    SEARCHED [ILLEGIBLE] INDEXED\n                    SERIALIZED............FILED\n                         DEC 12 1966\n                         FBI — NEWARK\n                              m\n\nNW 91149\nDocId: 34742114  Page 53\n\n                    100-9699 S-41", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b096b260c0ffc8ea1c455ba6dd89705d07e2df2cbcfc71644554d6e344e66d36", "output_sha256": "80e3c1a6741b17e7c8498e412be0d8263137e2780b8e659e8cbeddf3d867baf5", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:27.611316+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p54", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 54, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "Post Office Box 1158\nNewark, New Jersey 07101\nDecember 14, 1966\n\n\nMrs. M. Stein\n25 Clifton Avenue\nNewark, New Jersey 07104\n\nDear Mrs. Stein:\n\n          I have received your letter dated\nDecember 10, 1966, and the enclosure contained\ntherein.\n\n          Thank you for making this publication\navailable.\n\n                    Very truly yours,\n\n\n                    R. W. Bachman\n                    Special Agent in Charge\n\n          ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\n          HEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\n          DATE 5/15/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n1 - Addressee\n1 - Newark\nWVM:aas [ILLEGIBLE]\n  (2)\n\n\n                              100-36995-42\n\n\nSEARCHED___INDEXED [ILLEGIBLE]\nSERIALIZED [ILLEGIBLE] FILED [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "13a5ed930a8b0e58868c881fcb630a41038f78d896311dd70a774725d48b99ce", "output_sha256": "df913d292f3fec087f43bcc132798575d313378d2b4b55267befb1cbac310d01", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:28.729368+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p55", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 55, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "International Flying Saucer\n100-0-R-7516-\n100 ref.\n\nFLYING\nSAUCERS\n\nALL INFORMATION CONTAINED\nHEREIN IS UNCLASSIFIED\nDATE 3/16/85 BY [ILLEGIBLE] Sparley\n\n100-36998 con.\n62 ref.\n\nOfficial Journal of the\nAmalgamated Flying Saucer Clubs of America, Inc.\n\nINTERNATIONAL\n\n[PHOTOGRAPH OF FLYING SAUCER ABOVE TREELINE]\n\nSPECIAL AFSCA THIRD NATIONAL FLYING SAUCER CONVENTION ISSUE\n\nSEARCHED    INDEXED [signature]\nISSUE NO. SERIALIZED [signature] FILED [signature] JULY, 1966    100-36998-4-3    50c\n\nNW 91149\nDocId:34742114  Page 55", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8684fdcb87024b3e1d10daa0bf4ec360500eddb287926e412fc3a109f7074b40", "output_sha256": "5b3e8d333e03a0b30e2cb336b5c57b91b1d9c2faa4a652ae9b5a2c67ac371936", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:09:29.868367+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p56", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 56, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "SPECIAL    AFSCA    CONVENTION    MESSAGE\n\nBRIGHT WORLD IN HANDS OF SAUCER MOVEMENT\n\n(Editor's Note: This special message was received from Master Kalen-Li Retan (head of the planet Korendor, about 400 light years distant) on May 4, 1966 via special directional short-wave radio by Bob Renaud, the young electronic-technician whose remarkable story we printed in issues #18, 19, 20, 21, and 22, which will be continued in our next issue.\n\nSince Bob's initial radio contact in 1961, he has talked with the crew of a spacecraft as he watched them on his special TV screen in his home — and eventually met his contacts in-person; visited their undersea and underground bases on other planets; was taken aboard many of their spaceships; and was actually allowed to pilot two of their small scout craft — one on a short solo flight.)\n\n\"Kalo (Hello), friends. We will get directly to the point of our message to you. Frankly, we are appalled at the state of Earth at present. Despite our continuing warnings and even our actual intervention in some instances, the condition upon your planet grows steadily worse.\n\nOne subject on everyone's lips these days is Vietnam. From a little civil war, it has grown steadily and inexorably into a full scale conflict between the world's three major powers: the United States, the Soviet Union, and Communist China.\n\nMany influential people have used the approach of patriotism and love of God and Country to twist decent human feelings into dangerous channels of thought and action. With their charges of treason and sympathy with the enemy, they have aroused a good portion of the populace to a state of fear, distrust, and hatred of those who seek peace. — Unfortunately, because some unconventional individuals have been associated with the peace movement, that entire operation has been seriously hindered.\n\nYour government is a military puppet, a mere parrot of the monstrosity that is the Military-Industrial complex. Your senators, except for a few, are robots, speaking what they are told to say.\n\nYour President is, unfortunately, a pawn of their needs and demands. We have contacted him several times concerning the state of affairs, and he has said that he could do nothing to change them, for if he were to speak out against the Asian conflict, he would be removed. This is what happened to the late Mr. Kennedy who, in his great humanitarianism, was reluctant to sacrifice his ideals and his visions for the sake of the Military industrial octopus. He paid the supreme penalty for his efforts in behalf of humanity.\n\nMake no mistake. Your government is not in the White House or the Congress. IT IS IN THE PENTAGON, AND IN THE HEADQUARTERS OF THE VAST \"DEFENSE\"-ORIENTED INDUSTRIES. It is THEY, not the President or the Congressmen, who run the United States. The facade government is merely to allay undue alarm or suspicion of the people.\n\nExamine another aspect of the Asian war, the ECONOMIC side. As your Wall Street stock reports just recently, the Dow-Jones average dropped sharply BECAUSE OF A RUMOR THAT NORTH VIETNAM HAD MADE A PEACE BID? Does the staggering implication of this news evade you? Stock prices suffering a heavy loss because of a rumor that peace might come to pass!\n\nThis thought is most distressing. Your economy relies so heavily on war and destruction, that if it were to stop, THE UNITED STATES ECONOMY WOULD SUFFER A MASSIVE DEPRESSION! Your money system would collapse like a house of cards. Millions would be unemployed, sick, hungry and homeless. Tremendous industrial complexes would close their doors.\n\nThe utterly appalling fact is this: WAR IS PROFITABLE. Highly so! Every major conflict has been accompanied by a strong peak in your monetary prosperity. Peace has usually been economically painful.\n\nAfter World War 1, the nation coasted for a while upon the fat put on during the boom of the war years. Then in 1929, the bottom fell out. After the Korean War, in the 1950's came another recession. What comes after Vietnam? No one knows, and no one wants to find out. The war in Vietnam is bringing an unheard-of degree of affluence in the United States. Why kill a good thing by ending the war? The philosophy, in essence, is this: It is economically expedient to send military forces to Vietnam and elsewhere in Asia in order to wage war, because in doing so, the United States' economy is bolstered and maintained at a high level of prosperity; human life is secondary to the preservation of economic well-being!\n\nIt is thus evident that, unless a drastic change is made in the structure of your economy, war will never end because the Military-Industrial complex WON'T LET IT!\n\nMany of you fear Communism. Where did that fear come from, I ask you? From within yourself? No! It was been instilled into you by the Military-Industrial complex. Who controls all your news media? The government and the advertisers. Who, then, is in a position to dictate what shall be printed?\n\nThe Military-Industrial complex, by opinion-control through the use of psycho-politics (brainwashing by controlled news management).\n\nConsider this: In order to survive, a commercial medium, such as a newspaper or magazine, requires a vast amount of advertising revenue. The mere subscription fees will not cover the costs. Thus, they depend for their continued existence upon many large advertisers. What happens, then, when the editor of a certain newspaper decides that he is opposed to the Vietnam policy, and says so in his paper. The advertisers simply say to the editor, \"Either run the type of news we want, or we'll withdraw our advertising.\"\n\nSuch pressures are a fact of life. The newsmen are torn between their higher devotion to Truth, and their less idealistic, but very practical nature. Rather than jeopardize their security and their futures they, of course, submit meekly to power. This we find entirely understandable, and we do not hold them responsible.\n\nWe throw the blame directly on the Military-Industrial complex which, by its underhanded dealing, freedom of press, and economic pressure and retaliation, has crushed the spirit of American journalism and turned it from a dynamic motivating force in American life into a weak-willed, subservient mouthpiece for the power structure. We blame them for the death of journalistic freedom and individuality!\n\nOne more comment on this topic: May I say that a breath of fresh air has come lately from the leaders of the Flying Saucer Movement. It is the system known as Universal Economics. As we have said over and over before, it is the non-money economic system which MUST be applied on your planet before you can start to resolve most of your major problems and thus begin to establish a highly-advanced, non-destructive state of existence on Earth such as we and other advanced planets have enjoyed for so long. INVESTIGATE THIS SYSTEM to evaluate it for its merit — then ACT to apply it! YOUR VERY SURVIVAL AS A CIVILIZATION MAY DEPEND UPON IT!\n\nPerhaps this is an opportune time to clarify a few questions which have been asked about us.\n\nDo we of Korendor work with the other planets in our operations? Yes, we do cooperate with them a great deal. However, our work on Earth is relatively independent of the local planets. We have many times overstepped what is considered to be the limit of interference upheld by Venus, Mars, and other planets. This has caused a good deal of debate and disapproval among the Confederation. It turns out that we of Korendor are basically pragmatic in nature. Although we do respect the laws of self-destiny, we feel also that where stepping in is required to prevent disaster, we exercise our right and our duty.\n\nWe have interfered in such places as the United States, China, Russia, and on a large scale in Vietnam. This has caused no end of consternation in the local Tribunal of Planets. We are sympathetic to their viewpoint, but we do feel that their policy is limited in its capacity to achieve the desired goals. It is quite easy for us to stand on the sidelines and achieve any noticeable results.\n\nAs I have said before, we have infiltrated your planet. We are directly involved in Earth's life. You might feel that you have been invaded — a wrong way of phrasing it, to be sure, but nonetheless factual, since we walk and work amongst you daily!\n\nWe have been asked about our physical appearances. We are humanoid, indistinguishable among yourselves, except that in our natural form we average three to four feet in height. Every other dimension is proportionately scaled, so that photographs of us would not reveal our origin in any way.\n\nWe are able to increase our height while on Earth through a technical process we relate to teleportation. It is concerned with recording the atomic and molecular structures of our bodies, and then reproducing them identically on a larger scale. Differences in our internal structure are adjusted by the computer which controls the reproducer.\n\nOur most common skin color is a little darker than yours. We have varying skin colors which vary as yours do all over the Earth. Usually, however, we would look \"tan\" to you. We are NOT green, blue, or heliotrope, as has been suggested!\n\nConcerning our language: we generally use one of two tongues and we are fairly familiar with a third. On Korendor itself we speak the native language, Korendian. It is similar in many ways to your own languages. Our sister tongue was originally derived from Galingua, one of the two universal tongues. The other is Solex Mal, which is more familiar to us since it is used widely by many long-advanced planets. It is seldom heard now in our sector of space, as Galingua has replaced it almost completely.\n\nUnlike your own, however, the Korendian-Galinguan speech is very melodic, and lacks harsh sibilant sounds, such as \"s\" or \"z\". Some of the sharper sounds like \"c\" and \"k\" are minimized. It is a beautiful language which is very musical and pleasant to hear.\n\nPerhaps you would be surprised to learn that ancient Latin was liberally taken from Galingua. There are many similarities in the two languages. Even modern English has roots on other worlds!\n\nIn concluding my message to you, may I say — people of Earth: open up your minds and your hearts to the world around you. There is so much to be learned, so much to be discovered. Don't waste precious hours and days in bigotry and ignorance, and in senseless fighting and killing. To do so is truly barbaric, and a waste of human life!\n\nAt this stage where you have the very stars almost in your grasp, how irrational and barbaric it is to spend futile hours warring with your brothers. As an old saying on your world puts it: \"As you make your bed, so shall you lie in it.\" The decision does not seem difficult. Here are the alternatives: A world living in peace and justice, with real abundance for all, or a world continuing to reap the bloody harvests that grow from the seeds of hatred and mistrust. If left to their own devices, the majority of mankind will be doomed to a destiny of destruction and annihilation, oblivious to the danger in their actions. They are short-sighted; they care little for the future.\n\nIt is you New Age people, dedicated to the welfare of all mankind, and having the vision and understanding of the ways to build the better world of tomorrow, who are our hope here. You have the future in YOUR hands, if you will but shoulder your responsibilities. The Flying Saucer Movement, as you call it, belongs to you. Support it in every way possible. Help it to grow until it is known throughout your world. Go out into the world and guide the misguided, find the lost, and recover the strays. We are behind you all the way. As we have said many times before, it will take two steps for every one that you take to help yourselves.\n\nThe time has come for nations to \"bury the hatchet\" — to clasp hands, and plunge into the future together — in cooperation toward universal goals.\n\nLook to the heavens and realize that your destiny is not in bleak atomic desolation, but in the magnificent greatness that you can achieve if you will only work for it. Choose the right path and you will soon qualify to join with us in our journeys amongst the stars.\n\nVa i Luce (Go in Light).\" Kalen-Li Retan 3\n\nFLYING SAUCERS INTERNATIONAL\nISSUE NO. 24    JULY, 1966\nOfficial Journal of the\nAmalgamated Flying Saucer Clubs of America, Inc.\nInternational Headquarters: 2004 N. Hoover St., Los Angeles, Calif. 90027, U.S.A.\nDedicated to\nGABRIEL GREEN, Editor    The Physical, Spiritual, and Economic Emancipation of Man    A Non-profit Organization\nHELEN RINK, Asst. Ed.\n\nFLYING SAUCERS INTERNATIONAL (6 issues-$3.00. Membership-$1.00) is published quarterly. Copyright © 1965 by Amalgamated Flying Saucer Clubs of America. All rights reserved. The information presented in \"Flying Saucers International\" does not necessarily represent the views of AFSCA. The number after your name on the address label indicates the issue with which your subscription expires. Subscription renewals will start where the previous one ended, and will be acknowledged only by the new number after your name on future issues. A \"Time to Renew\" notice will be enclosed in the last issue for which you have paid. New subscriptions will start with the last issue published, unless a specific starting issue number is requested. When writing to AFSCA for a reply, enclose a stamped self-addressed envelope. Not responsible for magazines lost in the mail due to subscribers' failure to inform us of their current addresses. Price subject to change. Payment must accompany order. Send cash, check or money order to: AFSCA; 2004 North Hoover St.; Los Angeles, California 90027. Phone: 662-4404.    2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f1f2c93c1e72368ee1741b945e4ce858c81607268e83df18986a8822483481ee", "output_sha256": "79cabe556d5d14449e441a169be7f4a2fac7fdd612af8dd7690b27e487579893", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:10:10.023801+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p57", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 57, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "AFSCA CONVENTION SPEAKERS\n\n1. WAYNE S. AHO: The New Age Foundation, Inc.;\n   8 Smith St.; Seattle, Wash. 98109.\n   Publish: \"The Aquarian Dawn\" (Donation basis).\n2. CARL A. ANDERSON:\n   2522 E. Pearson Ave.; Fullerton, Calif.\n3. ORFEO ANGELUCCI:\n   4160 Verdugo Road; Los Angeles, Calif. 90065.\n4. MICHAEL \"X\" BARTON: Futura Press;\n   2949 Gresham Ave.; Hollywood, Calif. 90038.\n   Phone: 464-0441.\n5. WESLEY BATEMAN: Mental Investigations of New\n   Dimensions (M.I.N.D.); 4916 Franklin Ave.;\n   Hollywood, Calif. 90027. Phone: 661-1731.\n   Publish: \"Prism\" (12 issues--$3.00).\n6. MARIANNE FRANCIS: Solar Light Center;\n   Rt. 2, Box 82; Central Point, Oregon 97501.\n   Publish: \"Starcraft\" (6 issues--$2.00).\n7. DR. DANIEL W. FRY: Understanding, Inc.;\n   P.O. Box 105; Merlin, Oregon 97532.\n   Publish: \"Understanding\" (12 issues--$2.50).\n8. CALVIN C. GIRVIN:\n   6711 Yucca St.; Hollywood, Calif. 90028.\n9. GABRIEL GREEN: Amalgamated Flying Saucer\n   Clubs of America, Inc.; 2004 N. Hoover St.;\n   Los Angeles, Calif. 90027. Phone: 662-4404.\n   Publish: \"Flying Saucers International\"\n   (6 issues--$3.00).\n10. DR. GEORGE KING: The Aetherius Society;\n    6202 Afton Place; Hollywood, Calif. 90028.\n    Publish: \"The Aetherius Society Newsletter\"\n    (Donation basis). Phone: 465-9652.\n\n11. JOHANNES \"HANNO\" MAYBERRY:\n    Unified Research Center, Inc.;\n    P.O. Box 764; Selma, Oregon 97538.\n12. HOWARD MENGER:\n    202 Schumann Drive; Sebastian, Florida 32958.\n13. LAURA MUNDO: The Interplanetary Center;\n    27359 Cranford Lane; Dearborn Heights, Mich.\n    48127. Publish: \"The Interplanetary News\" (Free).\n14. MEL NOEL:\n    2760 Hollyridge Drive; Hollywood, Calif. 90028.\n15. SIDNEY PADRICK:\n    196 Hidden Valley Road; Watsonville, Calif.\n16. CHIEF FRANC STANDING HORSE:\n    AFSCA Unit #9; Rt. 2, Box 194, (27401 Hwy. 74);\n    Ferris, Calif. 92370. Phone: 657-2873.\n17. DR. FRANK E. STRANGES:\n    International Evangelism Crusades, Inc.;\n    P.O. Box 252; Venice, Calif. 90293.\n18. MOLLIE THOMPSON:\n    Linton, Astley Bank, Darwen, Lancs., England.\n19. HOPE TROXELL: School of Thought;\n    P.O. Box 458; Independence, Calif. 93526.\n20. GEORGE W. VAN TASSEL:\n    Ministry of Universal Wisdom, Inc.;\n    P.O. Box 458; Yucca Valley, Calif. 92284.\n    Publish: \"Proceedings\" (Donation basis).\n21. HAL WILCOX:\n    Institute of Parapsychology;\n    871 Gower St.; Hollywood, Calif. 90038.\n    Phone: 469-5438.\n\nSPACE AGE SONGS by Mollie Thompson\n\nTHE COCKEYED BALLAD\n\nThere's a cockeyed feeling in the world today\nThat power politics is here to stay.\nBut China, Russia and the U.S.A.\nBoy—don't let them fool you!\nTake a look at this world of ours,\nJust one mud ball in the sea of stars.\nOther planets have no color-bars,\n'Cause they've got perspective.\nYanks and Ruskies put men into space,\nBut it's all a mad politician's race,\nOne-up-manship in this Year of Grace.\nIt makes you giggle.\nThe population stands and stares,\nWhile men in capsules explore upstairs.\nWhy we can't even manage our own affairs!\nSomebody check—colonization!\nBesides, they've got people on Venus and Mars.\nThey got lads and lasses and ma's and pa's.\nAnd they've got better transport than four-wheel cars.\nHave you ever seen 'em?\nThose Flying Saucers whisking through our skies\nMust take some power to make them rise.\nBut government departments just hide their eyes,\nAnd call them theoretical!\nWith all the lies that they print and shout,\nThe general public's got its work cut out—\nFiguring what it's all about—\nBut just you keep on trying.\nI suppose you know why I'm telling you this,\nSo you won't shriek or shake your fist\nWhen you discover Martians do exist!\nThey're real nice fellows.\nI know, 'cause I met one a week ago!\nHis ship came down for an hour or so.\nHe talked to me, but then he had to go.\nReal interested I was!\nGot brothers on Venus and Saturn, it seems—\nFly their ships on magnetic beams.\nThey wear one piece suits—you can't see any seams;\nBut apart from that—they're just like us!\n\nSPACE-TALK\n\nThe powers that be will tell us we're alone.\nThey'll tell us that in space we are unique;\nOn this little desert island we call Earth\nThe human race is just a kind of freak.\nWhen we send out envoys into space,\nThere'll be a smile upon this planet's face,\n'Cause brother, right out there—I'm telling you,\nThere's another human race; it's very true!\nThey're a very very peaceful crowd,\nFor they just never go to war.\nAnd they cannot interfere,\nThis is by Universal Law.\nThe spaceman's message to us all\nIs based on how to banish fear,\nAnd if we only understand,\nSo we'll find it written here.\nWhile we must rely on war,\nWe never will be happy here.\nWhile this world's economy\nIs based on hardship, strife and fear.\nHow do they live without a war\nIn their lands of milk and honey?\nThey don't need economics,\nBecause they don't use any money!\nThey cannot give us any ships.\nSo we must try and build our own.\nBut they are waiting right out there,\nOh, my friends, we're not alone!\nHow do they go at such great speed,\nAnd vanish then without prediction?\nBecause they use free energy,\nAnd there isn't any friction.\nBrother have you seen their ships?\nSisters have you seen them glow,\nAs they dance and hover in the sky,\nAnd make our fastest jets look slow?\n\n5\n\nThird National Convention\nJULY 3, 1966\n\nAmalgamated Flying Saucer Clubs of America\n\nCENTENNIAL COLISEUM\nLos Angeles, California\n\n[Complex multi-column schedule table with times, rooms, speakers and topics for Friday July 8, Saturday July 9, and Sunday July 10, 1966 - details include multiple speakers and session titles in GOLD ROOM and MAIN HALL]\n\nFOR FURTHER INFORMATION, contact: AFSCA HEADQUARTERS; 2004 N. Hoover St.; Los Angeles, California 90027. Phone: 662-4404.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ed2b2b38cbc063fb0c32fb36f723fd89525cae477f1375edbff749ac55a38656", "output_sha256": "b9d16f7fbc30c798fc111cbe6ac273a9ede2b1141f3b7d463d316868b557e1c3", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:10:23.353589+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p58", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 58, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "GOLDEN GATE\nHandicap—Results    Oakland Tribune    METRO FINAL PM\nESTABLISHED FEBRUARY 21, 1874 · OAKLAND, CALIFORNIA\n\n94 YEAR, NO. 84    8    FRIDAY, MARCH 25, 1966    75¢ DAILY, $3.25 A MONTH\n\nFlying Saucers Are\nPoppin' Up All Over\n\nUFO'S (?) FLASH ACROSS MICHIGAN SKY\nTime exposure, taken by Michigan deputy sheriff...\nNEW PLYMOUTH, TUESDAY, MAY 15, 1966    Price Fourpence\n\nMYSTERY\nOBJECTS\nIN SKY\n\nOne Shot\nBy Man\nIn Maine\n\n[Photo caption: \"Let's see the Air Force beat this one up\"]\n\nThe Christian Science Monitor    Monday, May 9, 1966\n\nFlying swamp gas?\n\nSwamp gas in UFO? The civil defense director of Michigan's Hillsdale County has issued a report challenging an Air Force study which concludes that swamp gas was responsible for two sightings of Unidentified Flying Objects. William Van Horn said that, at the time of the sightings, a light was seen which emitted gas, and changed direction, while no gas was visible. The county civil defense director radiation and burns. Van Horn also obtained this photo of a UFO at a farm near Hillsdale County in late 1965. It comes from UFO files of France.\n\nAir Force UFO\nreport refuted\n\nHILLSDALE, Mich. (UPI)—\n[remainder of article text is too small/illegible to transcribe accurately]\n\nAIRLINER DETOURS\nTO CHASE U.F.O.\n\nOhio Police Trail\nUFO 86 Miles\n\n[Multiple newspaper clippings with various UFO-related headlines]\n\nPortland Oregon Journal\n[date]\n\n40 See 'Flying Saucer'\n\nAsks Probe of Flying Saucers\nFord Says U. S.\nPublic Should\nGet Answers\n\nAnother 'UFO'\nIs Sighted By\nWoman At Elmer\n\n[Various other partially legible article texts]\n\nMarch 28, 1966\n\nNow those flying saucers\ncome to Canadian skies\n\nFIRST UFO SPOTTER\n\n[Photo of man pointing at sign]\n\nBREWER Welcomes\nUFOs\nLANDING SITES AVAILABLE\nSigned... Barry York MAYOR\n\n'Flying saucer' pics on show\n\nOPP Chase\nFirst UFO\n– No Arrest\n\nMichigan\nUFO Lands\nIn Swamp\n\nNEW SAUCER PHOTOS: These remarkable photos of Flying Saucers were taken by Dr. Daniel W. Fry,\nPresident of Understanding, Inc., of P.O. Box 76, Merlin, Oregon 97532. Your editor enlarged them\nfrom the original 16mm color movie film. Spots on the photos are due to the extreme enlargement of\nscratches and dust spots on the film. Of special interest is the fact that the same type of craft was\nphotographed near Merlin, Oregon in a wooded section, and again near Joshua Tree, Calif. on the desert.\n\nNW 3114 [ILLEGIBLE]\nDoc [ILLEGIBLE] Page [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b7105547b3866ed35c2a8d142386d8aae0af160ba799d36c79d87a51b351ac6a", "output_sha256": "0df03970b41500706fd01ce1d3593a6a3ee755154c6d779862f44e60b436959b", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:10:26.404907+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p59", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 59, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "Head Saucerer Believes\nMartians Are Watching Us\n\nWho's in All\nThose Saucers?\n\nBy Harold Scarlett\n\n[Article text about saucers and Martians - partially illegible]\n\nSOMETIMES HE said, he met these\nvisitors individually, sometimes in\nappointments. Three were arranged\nthrough associates of his with the\nperfect tokens.\n\"And once in a while,\" he said, \"they\nwould take me on the plane.\"\nGreen, who lives in Los Angeles, is\nthe head saucerer — the president —\nof the Amalgamated Flying Saucer\nClubs of America.\n\nDuring a recent interview, we had\ncalled Green on the phone to interview\nhim about the alleged rash of flying\nsaucer sightings around the country.\n\"They hope to convince you of their\nexistence and to acquaint you with\nour advanced forms.\nSightings, analysis of sightings and\nfindings, I understand, will become\nmore frequent,\" he said.\nSo far as Green is concerned, they\nwould like...\nWHY DO THEY keep buzzing down\nhere and scaring people?\n\"They feel we've hit a predicament\nwhere we start wrecking the present\ncatastrophe that mankind or will\ndestroy ourselves and perhaps some of\nour systems along with us,\" Green explained.\n\n\"This is one of the primary reasons\nwhy the extraterrestrials started making visitations in 1947, shortly after we\ndeveloped this ability... to destroy.\"\nHe said they are a contact-attempt\ngroup,\" he said, \"meaning that many\nof our members have made actual\n\n[continues]\n\nSAID RUEFULLY, however:\n\"I've seen their ships themselves and\nan economic pinch that has prevented\nme from meeting.\"\nGreen said he runs the saucer clubs\nfrom his home but spends \"about two-\nthirds of my time on the telephone and\non the overhead.\" He said there are\nabout 1,000 major U.S. members\nahead, with a total of about 5,000\nmembers outside the club he said.\nGreen has between 3,000 and 4,000\nnames on his mailing list.\n\"We are a contact-attempt research\ngroup,\" he said, \"meaning that many\nof our members have made actual\n\n[SAUCER OR STRAW HAT, THIS FLEW IN CALIFORNIA LAST AUGUST]\n[Highway Patrolman Photographed It Through His Car Windshield]\n\nFROM PAGE 1—SPOTLIGHT\n\nTHE PHILADELPHIA INQUIRER, SUNDAY MORNING, APRIL 18, 1966\n\nUFO Plays Tag With Deputies in 85-Mile Chase\n\nRAVENNA, O., April 17 (UPI)—Portage county sheriff's head light so bright he couldn't look reported the object, which had Wilkins said the object \"was\n...[article continues about UFO chase with deputies]\n\nA-8 [Los Angeles Times-Examiner] Tuesday, May 17, 1966\n\nMysterious Sky Objects Have Texans in Dither\n\nMINEOLA, Tex., May 17—A brilliant strip of white appeared 35 miles distant at J. W. Henley, a farmer in...\n[Article continues]\n\n1-25-66\n\n---\n\n\"Peking between my hell and the green—I'd hardly\ncall THAT from another planet.\"\n\nFrom B.C., the Post, May 9, 1966\n\nTHE SWAMP GAS IS\nRESTLESS TONIGHT!\n\n[Cartoon illustration]\n\nGABRIEL GREEN\nHead Saucerer\n\n[Article column continues]\n\nBUT GREEN BELIEVED his own\nexplanations...\n\"They're so indignant it's hardly\nbelievable,\" Green said. \"Some of our members have actually\nhad encounters they finally built\nEconomics. The economics part of it is\nwhat I personally am trying to think\nabout.\"\n\n[Article continues about Green hotel and Martians]\n\n\"I feel his hair and it was quite\ncurly and went in a U shape down from\nthe temples to the back of the neck.\"\nGreen said, \"But I rather doubt all\nof our members when their hair, any\nmore than we do.\"\n\"HE SAID THE MARTIAN...\"\n\n---\n\nSaucer\nSighting\nDETROIT,\nMICHIGAN\n\n[Article about Detroit sighting]\n\nFive children were re-\nported sighting of unusual\nflying objects, observers\nfell on...\n[Continues]\n\nNorthwest Precinct police\nstations and three reports\nfrom other...\n\n---\n\nGOLDEN GATE\nHandicap—Results\n\n---\n\nCivil Defense Director\nWatches 'Flying Saucer'\n\nOakland Tribune METRO\nFINAL PM\n\nESTABLISHED FEBRUARY 21, 1874 • OAKLAND, CALIFORNIA\n\n93rd YEAR, NO. 81                    B                    TUESDAY, MARCH 22, 1966                    10¢ DAILY, $2.25 A MONTH\n\n---\n\nEerie 1896 Sighting\n\nBY JIM HAZEWOOD\n...[Article about 1896 sighting continues]\n\n\"That a huge airship has\nbeen reported...\"\n[Article continues]\n\n---\n\n★ GALLUP POLL ★\n\nMore Than 5 Million People\nSay They Saw Flying Saucers\n\nBy GEORGE GALLUP\n[Long article about Gallup Poll on flying saucer sightings]\n\n\"It was very likely...\"\n[Article continues]\n\nS—Nevada State Journal        Tuesday, May 10, 1966\n\n---\n\nSheriff Aides\nChase A UFO;\nWere 'Close'\n\nA Portage County Deputy Sheriff and...\n[Article continues about sheriff chasing UFO]\n\n1-25-66\n\n\"My flying-saucer-sighting time and I'm determined to see one\"\n\n---\n\n87 Coeds\nObserve\n'Object'\n\nBinghamton, N.Y., October 14, 1965 THE SUNDAY PRESS\n\nENCOUNTER WITH A SPACE SHIP\n\n'I Know What I Saw';\nEgg-Shaped Craft\n\nBY KEITH GEORGE\n[Article about egg-shaped craft sighting]\n\nHILLSDALE, Mich. (UPI) —\n...[Article continues]\n\nGARY WILCOX\n\n[Article continues about encounter]\n\n\"I just don't worry about\nit,\" a young farmer said...\n[Continues]\n\n---\n\nTwo In County\nClaim They Saw\n'Glowing' UFO\n\nAt least two Ventura County\nresidents reported seeing a\nWednesday night, shrouded\nand giving off a \"glowing\"\nlight...\n[Article continues]\n\nMrs. Marvin Miller of 24 Juniper St., Ventura told officers\nthe object appeared at about\n11 p.m. Wednesday as she and\nher husband were watching...\n[Continues]\n\nNW_M149\nDoc.ID:474214 Page:09", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "24dda7d490fa3213a70e40e99a5366c6ff21c1e3d89c58b03aac73c2b862d768", "output_sha256": "8888d9d06860ec83f0a957a1ba3ae10e9a3a4aab11e3411c0291357fa2c4c3a0", "generated_at": "2026-09-22T22:10:39.359009+00:00"}, {"id": "df252334c73a9019-p60", "card_id": "df252334c73a9019", "page": 60, "title": "FBI-UAP-D012, Newark Field Office, 1952-1967", "text": "10\n\nWorld Flying Saucer\nBelievers Convene\n2-6-66\n\nNew York Times Service\n\nLOS ANGELES, Calif. —\nThe largest problem of\nimproving communications\nwith the thousands of beings\nfrom outer space who sup-\nposedly visit earth regularly\nwas afforded solemn delib-\neration this weekend at\na special convention of fly-\ning saucer buffs.\n\nAmong the nearly 300 dele-\ngates was a self-professed\n\"intergalactic traveler\"\nnamed Standing Horse, an\nEnglishwoman named Mary\nwho issues mimeographed reports\nof her conversations with\nspace travelers, a man who\nclaimed to record \"psychic\nsightings\" of flying saucers\nand a presidential candidate\ncampaigning on the flying\nsaucer ticket.\n\nTHE SPACE buffs, who\nassembled in a motel estab-\nlishment called the Biar-\nritz, California's much im-\npressed with Thursday's So-\nviet moon shot—were\nawed and confused by\nwhat they regarded as a\nsharp increase in flying\nsaucers.\n\nOne delegate, Marianne\nFrancis, warned that the\nworld was experiencing the\nbeginning of some \"ominous\nchanges\" in the earth's pop-\nulation. But the convention\nchairman, Dr. Frank\nStranges, said the \"interplan-\netary visitors\" were reported\nto be \"angelic creatures\nwhose mission is to help\nmankind.\"\n\nThe delegates were gen-\nerally well groomed, articu-\nlate men and women who\ncould have been at a regular\nPTA meeting. Many were\nfrom organizations whose\nmembers spotted and photo-\ngraphed \"unidentified flying\nobjects\" and claimed to main-\ntain contact with newsrooms\nand space travelers.\n\nNEARLY ALL agreed that\nwhat they call the \"flying\nsaucer movement\" was un-\ndergoing a great expansion.\nTwo delegates announced\nthey were negotiating to rent\nthree radio stations to help\ntransmit their thoughts. Sev-\neral flying saucer magazines\nand pamphlets were available\non sale at the convention.\n\nThese people are enthusi-\nastic and experienced, said\nRiott Green, a serious young\nman who served as secretary\nof the Amalgamated Flying\nSaucer Clubs of America.\n\nFlying Object\nSighted in Illinois\n\nNORMAL, Ill.—UPI—Sev-\neral persons living on the\nsame block today said they\nsaw an unidentified flying\nobject last night.\n\nThe object had four blink-\ning lights, red, white, blue\nand amber, moving south-\neasterly, hovered over a\nnearby street, then moved\nsouthwesterly. The object\nwas seen first by the Merle\nSimpson family, then others.\nThey said it was flat and\nsmall.\n\n2 SOUTH AFRICAN POLICEMEN\nREPORT SIGHTING OF 'SAUCER'\n\nJOHANNESBURG, South Africa—\nSouth Africa police and\nscientists investigated Thursday\na report that a flying saucer-\ntype object had landed on a\nmain highway near Pretoria, the\ncountry's administrative capital.\n\nTwo patrolling police officers\nclaimed they saw a glowing\n\"saucer,\" about 30 feet in di-\nameter, on the Pretoria-Balmoral\nhighway.\n\nOne of them, Koos de Klerk,\nsaid his story appeared in the news. The object resembled a gust\nof light.\n\nTHE BOSTON HERALD, FRIDAY, SEPT. 13, 1965\n\nThe two men claimed that, as\nthey approached the object, it\ntook off silently at great speed\nwith flames shooting out of its\nunderside.\n\nScientists who examined the\nspot where the officers said the\nobject landed are reported to have found burns on a 10-foot\nwide section of the tarred road\nand marks in the gravel and sand\non either side of the highway. The marks\nwere reported slightly\nradioactive.\n\n[Image caption: These flying saucer stories are getting more ridiculous every day.]\n\nBROTHER JUNIPER BY FR. JUSTIN McCARTHY & LEN REINO\n\nPC REPORTS 'I\nSAW 6 FLYING\nSAUCERS.'\nTuesday, May 17, 1966\n\nPOLICE CONSTABLE Donald Cameron made out a report\nlast night and hoped the Chief Constable would believe\nthat he really DID see six flying saucers.\n\nPC Cameron was at home on sick leave when he looked out\na window and saw the objects about 150 feet above ground.\n\"I thought I was seeing things and called my wife,\" he said last night.\n\"We watched them for about 30 seconds before they veered away\ntowards Manchester.\"\n\nPolice Kept Busy\nSpotters Jam Up-County\nRoads for UFO Glimpse\n\nRINGWOOD — If the little\ngreen men from outer space got\nup-county police on the run\nWednesday night, their counter-\nparts caused more trouble Fri-\nday night.\n\nThrongs of the curious ringed\nnormally deserted Wanaque\nReservoir in this small hamlet\nand created what the police\nsay is the first traffic jam in\nthe area in many years — 500\ncars parked along Westbrook\nRoad and Route 23.\n\nRingwood Police Lieutenant\nJack O'Hara said \"We told\n\nAttention Slips\nJan. 15, 1966\n[Newspaper clipping content about UFO spotters]\n\nthose to move on, but they kept\ndriving from one side of the\nroad, so we just had to\ncall in a couple of extra men.\nThey had everything.\nTrailers, binoculars, tele-\nscopes. I was waiting to see one\nof them get out with a geiger\ncounter.\"\n\nO'Hara watched Ringwood\nas its force after spread pub-\nlicity that a woman had iden-\ntified flying objects over the\nreservoir in [Continued on Page 3, Col. 7]\n\n\"It'll be Long Before\n'Saucer' Is Forgotten\nJANUARY 19, 1960\n\nBY PETER A. DYBARCKAS\n[Article content about flying saucers being forgotten]\n\nMany months will pass before\nthe impact of the weird, slim\nobjects which dominated the\nskies above the Wanaque area\nfades into memory.\n\n[Continued article text about UFO sightings, investigations, and various accounts from witnesses and officials]\n\n2 THE WALL STREET JOURNAL\nMonday, December 13, 1965\n\nNew 'Fireball' Raises\nAn Old Question: Do\nFlying Saucers Exist?\n\nCalifornian, Who 'Talks' to Men\nFrom the Stars, Says 'Yes';\nScientists Assault Air Force\n\nBy ELLIOTT CARLISLE\n[Article content about flying saucers debate]\n\n[Multiple newspaper clippings continue with various UFO-related articles]\n\nLondon, Ontario Free Press\n2-26-66\n\n100 Watch UFO\nFlying\nsaucers\nmystery\n\nDisc-Like Object Hovers, Rises\nFor Two Hours East of Kettle Point\n\nBY JIM ETHERINGTON\n[Article content about UFO sighting in Ontario]\n\nBANIA — A revolving ob-\nject, outlined in the sky east\nof Kettle Point last night, was\nwatched for more than two\nhours by about 100 persons.\n\n[Continued article text]\n\nFlying Saucers\nGain Proponent\nNew York Times\n\n[Additional article content]\n\nSTRANGE OBJECT\nOVER MT. WILSON\n\n4-18-66\n\n'Report Them . . . Forget It—\nI Have Enough Credibility Problems As It Is'\n\nUN Watch for Saucers Urged\n\nUNITED NATIONS, N.Y.,\n(AP)—Count Carl Von Iskewken, an employee in the\nU.N. library, proposed today\nthat nations could be es-\ntablished on permanent watch,\nthat members of the United\nNations establish a network\nto observe flying saucers.\n\nHe told a press conference\nhe believes someone in outer\nspace is sending flying\nsaucers on exploratory mis-\nsions to earth.\n\nHe said no radar reports\nhad been obtained on any of\nthe sightings.\n\nIn Michigan, police in two\nplaces in the area, at one\npoint following the objects\nalong the Lake Huron shore.\nOne woman who said the\nobject she saw was a jet.\n\nIn Michigan new reports of\n\nHong Kong China Mail\nFlying\nsaucers\nmystery\n2-3-66\n\nPEOPLE in North Queens-\nland were reported by\nthree separate reports of\nFlying Saucers.\n\nThe first report came from a\n37-year-old banana grower,\nMr. O. Van Huber, who rode his\ntractor to his home along a\ncounty road on his way to his\nown farm. He reported that\nhe said he looked at it through\nbinoculars and could see the\nblue, green and white lights\nof what looked like a disc\nshape.\n\nSheriff Douglas Harvey of\nWashtenaw County and civil\ndefense director William Sny-\nder of Hillsdale County criti-\ncized the Air Force because\nVan Huber said the swamp gas\nexplanation didn't make sense.\nHe said, \"We all\nsaw the thing\"\nand that it was about\nor 300 feet off the ground to\nthe east. Then it slowly began\nto move up.\"\n\nMr. Bressette said it could\nnot have been swamp gas\nwhich is often the proffered\ncause of unidentified flying\nobject sightings in the Lansing\narea last week.\n\n\"This was not the same,\" he\nsaid. \"It was hovering. I've\nnot seen any swamp gas lights\naround here since before the\nwar.\"\n\nMr. Bressette said his broth-\ner, Jeffrey, also reported see-\ning the object. He lives near the\nreservoir for Amherst. \"But our\nAir Force hasn't moved on it.\"\n\nNevertheless, \"we have on file a great num-\nber of reports from pilots who don't want their\nnames used but still want to tell somebody\nwhat they've seen,\" claims J.B. Hartmen, Jr.,\npresident of the Aircraft Owners and Pilots As-\nsociation. \"I am not in a position to draw any\nconclusions myself, but I think we're certainly\ngot a good mystery on our hands.\"\n\nHe said no radar reports\nwere ever obtained on any of\nthe sightings.", "model_id": "cl