3931a06926fdae093a08097af135c1361cd19c84369840ef1deb2294b9", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T13:54:08.504142+00:00"}, {"id": "f85532f0514320be-p112", "card_id": "f85532f0514320be", "page": 112, "title": "65_HS1-834228961_62-HQ-83894_Section_007", "text": "The\nInternational Flying Saucer Bureau\nALBERT K. BENDER\nINTERNATIONAL\nPresident and Editor\n\"All is possible to one who believes\"\nHEADQUARTERS\nMAX KRENGEL\nP. O. BOX 241\nVice-Pres. and Treas.\nBRIDGEPORT 2, CONN.\nALAN C. RIEVMAN\nU. S. A.\nSecretary\nFRED J. BENDER\nHistorian\nGreat Britain Branch\n71 Chedworth Road\nOctober 26, 1952\nHorfield,\nINTERNATIONAL\nBristol 7, England\nCOUNCIL\nROBERT N. WEBSTER\nMr. J. H. Frahm,\nEditor - \"Fate\" Magazine\n949 E. Jefferson Street,\nWILSON \"BOB\" TUCKER\nAuthor - Editor of\nFranklin, Indiana\nScience Newsletter\nDear Mr. Frahm:\nELLIOTT ROCKMORE\nEditor - Publisher\n\"Saucer Review\"\nOnce again I am happy to write to you about\nGEORGE D. FAWCETT\nB and your fine work in helping our organization\nLecturer - Sauceriana\ngrow larger and stronger.\nCollection\nSTANLEY E. CROUCH\nIn your last letter you asked what course of action\nEditor - Science and\nyour club should take in connection with IFSB. I\nCulture Magazine\nwould suggest the following:\nFRANKLIN M. DIETZ\nEditor and Publisher\n\"Science - Fantasy and\n(1.) Appoint a local Chairman of the IFSB in\nScience Fiction\"\nFranklin, Indiana. Also appoint a local\ntreasurer and secretary.\nBRITISH REPRESENTATIVE\n(2.) Hold your meetings at least twice a month,\nE. L. PLUNKETT\nwhere you can discuss saucer happenings and\nRetired Capt. 8th Army\nclub activities. Use a local hall, or better\nyet, hold the meetings at each others homes.\n(3.) If and when you form your own city group, a\ncertain portion of the club membership fee\nmay be retained by you to help your cause.\n(4.) Mr. Dick Campbell, is an International Officer\nin IFSB and should be paid such respect at all\nyour gatherings.\n(5.) We will do any post card printing you desire or\ncards of similar size.\n(6.) You can print your club activities in \"Space\nReview\".\n(7.) Get contributions from your members to help\nyou get formed.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7c9134ee7768c3f2e6661ae59acc1cb0d0cdbd0ea534599d92c1f45db57154a2", "output_sha256": "9443058a10dfa755741a1f7f4b1141657a6744e7158588c0659985413cb839e4", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T13:54:14.315742+00:00"}, {"id": "f85532f0514320be-p113", "card_id": "f85532f0514320be", "page": 113, "title": "65_HS1-834228961_62-HQ-83894_Section_007", "text": "The\nInternational Flying Saucer Bureau\nALBERT K. BENDER\nP. O. BOX 241\n\"All is possible to one who believes\"\nPresident and Editor\nBRIDGEPORT 2, CONN.\nMAX KRENCEL\nU. S. A.\nVice-Pres. and Treas.\nALLAN C. RIEVMAN\nSecretary\n) II (\n(8). Report to IFSB all reports and sightings in\nyour area. However, first put the sightings\nbefore your group and let them judge whether\nthey are authentic or not.\n(9). Keep a record of all club members in your area\nand their activities as far as IFSB is concerned.\n(10). Obtain if possible (merely a suggestion), a tape\nrecorder so that you can send actual voice to\nIFSB headquarters. In this way, I as President,\ncould send messages for you to play at your local\nmeetings. In the future I may even pay your city\na visit and attend one of our meetings.\nThese are all merely suggestions for you to ponder over\nand if you decide to adopt any of them please consult with\nIndiana Representative, Mr. Campbell. After you have\nthis, get in touch with me at once.\nI sincerely hope that these suggestions will help you\nnoting some move as to what your local group will do.\nForever Looking Up,\nalbert K. Bender\nAlbert K. Bender\nPresident\nAKB/BOT", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "