nd as to his residence. When asked where he\nplanned to stay tonight, at least, in order that\nAir Force might interview him if deemed advisable,\nBailey said the writer wanted to know too much and\ndisconnected. Since no specific information was furnished\nand since the call may have been a prank, the Air Force\nwas not advised. Since no identifying information was\nobtained, no attempt was made to check Bureau records.\nRecommendation:\nFile.\nLHM: dmd\nCORDED-102\nINDEXED-102\n62-83894-32\nMAR 10, 1953", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "11b0f0dd01951879776dd01da145e9c19bb65afae2509adc198adee3a345b60b", "output_sha256": "06128051bd22fd3d929a6b329355995f4dae3a5257aebdf1ce1aeea84a0ceda3", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T13:55:24.265213+00:00"}, {"id": "f85532f0514320be-p132", "card_id": "f85532f0514320be", "page": 132, "title": "65_HS1-834228961_62-HQ-83894_Section_007", "text": "This document appears to be severely corrupted or garbled OCR output that does not form coherent English text. It contains:\n\n- Repetitive phrase fragments (\"THE PARTY OF\" repeated many times)\n- Foreign language text (Chinese characters)\n- Random number sequences\n- Repeated words (\"the second\" repeated many times)\n- Nonsensical phrases that don't form grammatical sentences\n- Strings of repeated characters (like \"1111111...\")\n- Fragmented words and incomplete thoughts\n- Mixed language content (Spanish text at the end: \"SECIO ESPIONÁGE\")\n\nThe text is too severely corrupted to determine what the original document was meant to contain. There are no clear OCR errors to fix in the traditional sense (like broken hyphenation or column-detection scrambles) — instead, the entire document appears to be either:\n\n1. A scanning error where multiple pages or documents were overlaid\n2. A corrupted file\n3. Text that has been processed through multiple failed OCR passes\n\nWithout a legible source reference or clearer content structure, I cannot responsibly \"correct\" this text as it would require inventing content rather than fixing OCR recognition errors.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f43b37c8f1b5d08db1000a404447e597e3daa98a1cae7d60f43166f79bdd39c3", "output_sha256": "ac96c5931e2aa4d92005e6c62603b36a73ab3c8e72b60e13c7bf6fa34aff6640", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T13:55:28.341684+00:00"}, {"id": "f85532f0514320be-p133", "card_id": "f85532f0514320be", "page": 133, "title": "65_HS1-834228961_62-HQ-83894_Section_007", "text": "CORDED-102\nMarch 12, 1953\nDate:\nDirector of Special Investigations\nTo:\nThe Inspector General\nDepartment of the Air Force\nThe Pentagon\nWashington 25, D. C.\nJohn Edgar Hoover, Director\nFrom:\nFederal Bureau of Investigation\nFLYING SAUCERS\nSubject:\nAt 9:05 p.m. on March 9, 1953, an individual giving his\nname as John Bailey telephonically contacted this Bureau and advised\nhe had just seen a flying saucer near Bowie, Maryland. Mr. Bailey\nwas vague as to any details in this matter and would not furnish any\ninformation concerning his residence or the place from which he was\nmaking his telephone call. No additional pertinent information in\nthis matter was furnished by Mr. Bailey.\nThe above is being furnished to you for your information and\nassistance in the captioned matter. No investigation is being conducted\nby this Bureau concerning this matter.\nEHM:elk MC\nAPPROPRIATE ACTIVITIES\nINR 12\nAND FIELD OFFICES\nRECEIVED\nADVISED BY ROUTING\nS DEPT\nSLIP(S) OF\n9\nBUREAU\nDATE\nW\n23\nEG. Md\nS. Dis Sile\nTolson\nLadd\nS DEPT\nNichols\nMAILED\nBelmont\nClegg\n'53\nGlavin\nHarbo\nRosen\nTracy\nLaughlin\nMohr\nWinterrowd\nTele. Rm.\nHolloman\nGandy", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "051a8750d