50384\nFACS/ISC/NARS, Conv.\n4/2/84", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "21d00d5c11ca9a923aaa3632431e4f983ac69ec21cc62c1626e7e6bed5affde8", "output_sha256": "21d00d5c11ca9a923aaa3632431e4f983ac69ec21cc62c1626e7e6bed5affde8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:50.053716+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p3", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 3, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Unclassified) Transmittal of FLYOBRPT's\nChief, ATIC, Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio                    19 Dec 52\n\nDeputy Director for Estimates, D/I                    Capt. Smith - AFOIN-2A2\n                                                        75990/AC\n\nForwarded for your action are four inclosures, all on FLYOB's.\n\n4 Incls: (W/orig only)              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   1. Ltr fr Mr. Johnston           Colonel, USAF\n      dtd 10 Dec 52                 Chief, Topical Division\n   2. AF IN 2127                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n      18 Dec 52                     Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n   3. Comment No. 2\n      SCIA dtd 17 Dec 52\n      W/1 incl.\n   4. Comment No. 1\n      CID dtd 12 Dec 52\n      W/1 incl.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n[signature]              [signature]\nAFOIN-2A2               AFOIN-2A\n\n                    v\n               x-3227 ATIC\n\n\n          When incl(s) No. 1, 2, 3, 4\n          is/are withdrawn (or not attached),\n          the Confidential classification\n          of this correspondence will be down-\n          graded to unclassified in\n          accordance with Par 25A, AFR 205-1.\n\n                    31 Jan 1952\n                    DIR/INTI\n                    HQ USAF\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2302f157a22d3a3136109f9b3458cbe310eb9ab3c90b93300942728a2e779bec", "output_sha256": "2302f157a22d3a3136109f9b3458cbe310eb9ab3c90b93300942728a2e779bec", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:51.816054+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p4", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 4, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Capt Smith/AC/75990\n19 December 1952\n\nPublic Information Division\nUnited States Coast Guard\nRoom 1004\n1300 E Street, N. W.\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\nAttn: Mrs. Mary M. Mead\n\nDear Mrs. Mead:\n\nIn compliance with your telephone request of 15 December,\n1952, attached will be found the negative of the photo of\nunidentified objects taken 16 July 1952, at Salem Air Station,\nMassachusetts.\n\nWe sincerely appreciate the cooperation of personnel of\nthe United States Coast Guard in this matter.\n\nYours very truly,\n\nSIGNED\n\nEncl.                   WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Negative           Colonel, USAF\n                        Chief, Topical Division\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n                        ↓\n                        ↓ 062.1 Photographs\n                        ↓ x 095 Mead, Mrs Mary M.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n[signature]              [signature]\nAFOIN-2A               AFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    [circular stamp: OUT DEC 1952]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "42fad1d5fdf15541c3b825d1860a5c51877b74b88926e9210ec1ffada7f462a3", "output_sha256": "f55fddaa2bb45317448e120d1162bc7ce84b63ddceb76738eaf9b261e4532786", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:53.357823+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p5", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 5, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Capt Smith/AC/75990\n19 December 1952\n\n\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To return a photographic negative purported to be\nof \"flying saucers\" taken by a member of the USCG at Salem\nAir Station, Massachusetts, on 16 July 1952.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:                                          M/R\n\n     2.  On 15 December 1952, Mrs. Mead of the Public Information Division of the USCG here in Washington telephoned Captain\nSmith of AFOIN-2A2 and requested return of subject negative.\n\n     3.  Captain Smith contacted Captain Ruppelt of ATIC on\n16 December 1952 by telephone and requested he bring the negative\nto HQ USAF on a staff visit which he was to make on 17-18 December.\n\n     4.  Captain Ruppelt stated that ATIC was finished with\nanalyzing the photograph and that he would bring it with him\nfor return to the USCG.\n\nACTION:\n\n     5.  Subject negative returned by attached letter in compliance with the request of the USCG.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n  AFOIN-2A2, Col. W. H. Smith, Ext. 71016\n  AFOIN-2A,  Col. W. A. Adams, Ext. 74072", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f352c822a23bf60683aae19f496f5426d40052a34e194754b9b0fe4c74da2214", "output_sha256": "37c523b2888621ab576b11b7ba15be3185532ef3e1528c330eccf29dae57e47a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:55.214806+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p6", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 6, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED                    ~~CURITY INFORMATION~~\n\n                                                    1B\n              HEADQUARTERS STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND\n                      OFFUTT AIR FORCE BASE\n                         OMAHA, NEBRASKA\n\nDINC  3 5 0                              3  DEC 1952\n\nSUBJECT:  (Unclassified) FLYOBRPT\n\n\nTO:       Director of Intelligence\n          Headquarters USAF\n          Washington 25, D.C.\n\n\n          The attached Air Intelligence Information Reports are forwarded\nas per instructions AFL 200-5, dated 29 April 1952, subject, FLYOBRPT.\n\n     FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                                        Hal E. Beym\n                                    ~~HAL E. BILYEU~~\n2 Incls: ✓                          MAJOR, USAF\n  1. IR-166-52 (4 cys)              Asst Adj Gen\n  2. IR-167-52 (1 cys)\n                  only 1 cy recd 01A-162\n\n                         9 Dec\n\n                  Incl w/o in AN 132 ✓\n                  Mj Randolfo  COUPON DESIGNATION MADE --------\n                        [circled: 22\n                               2h]\n\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c2a388f9dfe55dc43085cabb8c69a0914a36d142b6375e8061169a563de6bf68", "output_sha256": "3c5d682d04a3599f1aeaefcf14b3938192a4d76a5f0097eda87fa31b334e3047", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:56.769498+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p7", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 7, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "REC'D\n5 DEC 1952\nDIR/INT\nHQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "412e7ac061dc2c724c97842966a9584b2ad94b0103d6c2b97b5e591cf07fb816", "output_sha256": "412e7ac061dc2c724c97842966a9584b2ad94b0103d6c2b97b5e591cf07fb816", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:57.365249+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p8", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 8, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED                    [ILLEGIBLE] INFORMATION\n\n             HEADQUARTERS STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND\n                    OFFUTT AIR FORCE BASE\n                      OMAHA, NEBRASKA\n\n\n     DINC   3 5 0  1                              3  DEC 195[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n     SUBJECT:  (Unclassified) FLYOBRPT\n\n\n     TO:        Director of Intelligence\n               Headquarters USAF\n               Washington 25, D.C.\n\n\n             The attached Air Intelligence Information Reports are forwarded\n     as per instructions AFL 200-5, dated 29 April 1952, subject, FLYOBRPT.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                                        HAL E. BILYEU\n                                        MAJOR, USAF\n     2 Incls:                           Asst Adj Gen\n       1. IR-166-52 (4 cys)\n       2. IR-167-52 (2 cys)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dd37e5f684f5c9e2ddc5a757763e75aebaa097658c032e2841a6974f8b05f7c1", "output_sha256": "dd37e5f684f5c9e2ddc5a757763e75aebaa097658c032e2841a6974f8b05f7c1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:05:58.742841+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p9", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 9, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nw/2 December 1952\n\n\n                    3 Dec 52\n\n\n\n\nGentlemen:\n\n     The Secretary of Defense has asked me to reply to your letter\nof 13 November 1952, file DS, forwarding a report of an observation\nof an unidentified flying object submitted by Mr. Jacques Petitjean\nRoget of Martinique, F. W. I.\n\n     The Air Force has been given primary responsibility for the\nproduction of intelligence on this subject.  We were very pleased\nto receive this report and would appreciate any additional reports\nwhich the Consulate at Martinique is able to furnish us.\n\n     We appreciate your cooperation in this matter.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n                         Secretary of Defense\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\nThe Department of State\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n[signatures]\n                                            OUT\n                                         5 Dec 1952\n                                          DIR/INT\n                                          HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "89f46fd54f800643730d58fa1d2d94e3635ecaa412cd31937f45fb583ceec8ec", "output_sha256": "7d8775cb60b8e105feb222700ca41441fc4113afeec39c4a9ef77c53e458ee60", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:00.451731+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p10", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 10, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\n2 December 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1. To prepare a letter to the Department of State for the Secretary\nof Defense.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2. In a letter dated 13 November 1952, the Department of State\ntransmitted to the Secretary of Defense, a copy of a letter from Mr.\nJacques Petitjean Roget of Martinique, F. W. I. reporting the observation\nof an unidentified flying object. The Department of State requested\ninformation regarding our desire to obtain additional reports of this\nnature.\n\n     3. The Office of the Secretary of Defense instructed the Air Force\nto prepare a direct reply to the Department of State.\n\n     4. The attached reply to the Department of State expresses the\nappreciation of the Air Force for their cooperation in this matter and\nindicates our desire to receive additional reports which they mention\nare available from this area.\n\n     5. Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the\nDaily Staff Digest.\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS:\n\n     6. Approval, signature and forwarding of attached reply.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Smith, Ext. 71016  dthmill\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072  rua", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4a6bc278449c4bd48cb1afa455c962822f8d72084b6a5b1eeb910cf885ac1d6c", "output_sha256": "4a6bc278449c4bd48cb1afa455c962822f8d72084b6a5b1eeb910cf885ac1d6c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:02.035173+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p11", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 11, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "000.9  Flying Discs\n\n322.7  ATIC\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\n\n1 Dec 52\n\n\nFROM   AFOIN-2A2\n\nTO     ATIC\n\n\nDF 1\nSUBJ:  (Confidential)  Background Investigation of Des Vergers, D.S., for\n       Project Blue Book\n\n        1.  The inclosed report was prepared by the Directorate of Special\nInvestigations, this Hq, in compliance with a specific request from this\noffice.  It is for your information and retention.\n\n*                    *                    *                    *\n\n\n\n\nFILED UNDER 383.4  INVESTIGATIONS CIVILIANS", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c4e930da7167690f715db2eedd0ed2343b578f0cd699424c8302c675b815f17f", "output_sha256": "4c128c669d8ebc232b4105048f89eaf6daf20bbcfbf76bc18f79e137f0bf9bd1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:03.054527+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p12", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 12, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nw/28 Nov 52\n\n\n                                    DEC 1  1952\n\n\nMr. Ken W. Purdy\nEditor, True Magazine\nFawcett Building\n67 West 44th Street\nNew York 36, N. Y.\n\nDear Mr. Purdy:\n\n     I appreciated your letter of November 14 forwarding a\n\ncopy of the December issue of your magazine.  Many thanks.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n               This ltr not sent out\n                    File P+R.\n\n\n        x095. True Magazine\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A     AFOIN-2     AFOIN\n\n         BpWHSmith    GBBelksd   Jkmonow    ________\n              BJ\n\n[Sideways text on right margin:] AFOIN Coordination Copy\n[Sideways text on right margin:] 000.9 Flying Saucers", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "666a59ad04c840d5d7eae839c1a1a53b13aaa386a9c0c5bdfe4b2304e31e2d71", "output_sha256": "666a59ad04c840d5d7eae839c1a1a53b13aaa386a9c0c5bdfe4b2304e31e2d71", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:04.372547+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p13", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 13, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\n28 November 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1. To prepare a non-military letter to Mr. Ken W. Purdy, Editor\nof TRUE magazine.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2. By personal letter to General Samford dated 14 November 52, Mr.\nPurdy forwarded a copy of the December issue of TRUE magazine for\nGeneral Samford's perusal since it contained an article on \"flying\nsaucers\" by Donald Keyhoe. Mr. Purdy considered this article to be of\npossible interest.\n\n     3. Mr. Purdy had forwarded in similar fashion a previous issue of\nTRUE which contained another article on the same subject. A reply signed\nby General Samford, expressing his appreciation, was sent to Mr. Purdy.\nA precedence was thereby established.\n\n     4. Attached reply simply expresses appreciation to Mr. Purdy for\nhis latest letter. It is written in the first person from General\nSamford.\n\nRECOMMENDATION:\n\n     5. That the attached reply be signed by General Samford and dis-\npatched to Mr. Purdy.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Smith, Ext. 71016 [ILLEGIBLE]\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 71564 [ILLEGIBLE]\n     AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110 [ILLEGIBLE]\n     AFOIN, Maj Gen Samford, Ext. 55613", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9f575884234dde65f09643bb5890c886f37c9c4a14f90526b849379633c1aef4", "output_sha256": "9f575884234dde65f09643bb5890c886f37c9c4a14f90526b849379633c1aef4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:06.129639+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p14", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 14, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "TRUE\nTHE MAN'S MAGAZINE\n\nFawcett Building  67 West 44th Street  New York 36, N.Y.  MUrray Hill 2-3606\n\n\n\n\n\nNovember 14, 1952\n\n\nMajor General John A. Samford\nDirector of Intelligence\nU.S. Air Force\nWashington 25, D.C.\n\nDear General Samford,\n\n               In view of your kindness in commenting\non TRUE's recent exposure of the flying-saucer \"little men\"\nhoax, I feel that perhaps our latest report on the saucer\nproblem, in the December issue which will appear next\nWednesday, will be of interest to you.\n\n                                        Sincerely,\n\n                                        Ken W. Purdy\n                                        Ken W. Purdy\n                                        EDITOR", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1828f65534089ae134fa1a503b7d7356afa4b1652b8d39207d54a3df1cfd3420", "output_sha256": "26658bc818deea1ce404b35ff166beb250906656ae34f46beefd2b210379ff66", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:07.285018+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p15", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 15, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET                          SUSPENSE\n\nORIGIN OF BASIC                    DATE        TYPE                DATE\n\nSUBJECT                                                          ASSIGNED BY\n\n              Letter of Appreciation                             NUMBER\n\n                                    ROUTING\nInitial \"IN\" column to denote review prior to action. Initial \"OUT\" column to denote review of completed action. (X-for action:\nV- for coordination)\n\nIN    OFFICE      OUT   IN    OFFICE      OUT   IN    OFFICE      OUT   IN    OFFICE      OUT\n      AFOIN                   OIN-1                   OIN-2                   OIN-3\n      OIN-X  S               OIN-1X                  OIN-2X    OOD           OIN-3X\n      OIN-X1\n      OIN-X2\n\n\n      CABLES\nM  1  ILE                                                               SR NAVAL OFF\n      DISPATCH                                                           SR ARMY OFF\nTO:                                                              DATE\n              AFOIN-2X                                                    11 Dec 52\nFROM:                                                            COMMENT NUMBER\n              AFOIN-2A                                                    1\nCOMMENTS (Use reverse, if necessary)\n                                                                AFOIN No.\n        The attached correspondence is transmitted for forwarding to OIN for  938\nsignature and dispatch.\n\n\n                              DCB\n                              DONALD E. BEEBE\n                              Captain, USAF\n                              Executive, AFOIN-2A\n\nTo: AFOIN                                          11 December 52\nFROM: AFOIN-2X                                     Comment 2\n\n              Forwarded for signature.\n\n                                                   veu\n                                                   AFOIN-2X\n\n             M+R                                   #2\n             AFOIN X                               17 Dec 1952\n\n             Answer letter not required - file.\n\n                                                   [ILLEGIBLE] File\n\nAFHQ  FORM  O-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.                D 6616\n     22 JUL 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "931682b08db0d6bb740b68da755a043f9224c4fbb79e141efa50bfb2f98a8f25", "output_sha256": "017db33eb60d824bc7cdc132336d0d221f5528544ccb67054ce0f557628b8d89", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:09.343455+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p16", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 16, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    HEADQUARTERS STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND              467\n                             OFFUTT AIR FORCE BASE\n                               OMAHA, NEBRASKA\n\nDINC  3 5 0  1\n                                                        25 NOV 1952\nSUBJECT:  (Unclassified) FLYOBRPT\n\n\nTO:          Director of Intelligence\n             Headquarters USAF\n             Washington 25, D.C.\n\n\n        The attached Air Intelligence Information Reports are forwarded\nas per instructions AFL 200-5, dated 29 April 1952, subject, FLYOBRPT.\n\n        FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n                              L-31941 Af Intel. Rpt\n\n                                   Hal E. Bilyeu\n3 Incls√                      HAL E. BILYEU\n  1.  IR-162 - 52 (4 cys)     MAJOR, USAF\n  2.  IR-164 - 52 (3 cys)     Asst Adj Gen\n  3.  IR-165 - 52 (3 cys)          COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\n\n                         5 Dec\n\n              And m/e in OINBR\n\n                    Maj. Pandolfo\n\n                         [signature]\n\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0a319be8e06f2d3b1351fe793b88f966e67fa6d1abce54bfb05a50e9f14f4971", "output_sha256": "0a319be8e06f2d3b1351fe793b88f966e67fa6d1abce54bfb05a50e9f14f4971", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:10.952073+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p17", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 17, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "REC'D\n28 NOV 1952\nDIR/INT\nHQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c52ceca09a04d07e4bb279f1936f23ec271ec40ebe015eca3d5324559124a2a9", "output_sha256": "c52ceca09a04d07e4bb279f1936f23ec271ec40ebe015eca3d5324559124a2a9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:11.591892+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p18", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 18, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWrtn 24 Nov 52\n\nAFOIN-2A2\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR: DIRECTOR OF NAVAL INTELLIGENCE\n\n                ATTN: Op322Y5\n\nSUBJECT: Interpretation of Movies of Unidentified Flying Objects\n\n                                              NOV 24 1952\n\n     1. Further to our Memorandum dated 24 October 52, same subject\nas above, it is requested that the inclosed roll of 16 mm Kodachrome\nmovie film be analyzed in the same manner as the film previously for-\nwarded. In addition, a comparison with the latter film would be most\nhelpful.\n\n     2. Background information pertaining to the inclosed film is\ncontained in Incl 2, the official report on this incident.\n\n     3. Your cooperation in satisfying this additional request is\nearnestly solicited. In addition, notification of preliminary results\nof both analyses at the earliest opportunity would be appreciated.\nSuch preliminary data may allow us to complete some of the pending\naction on these films prior to receipt of the final results.\n\n\n2 Incls                          WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. 16 mm Kodachrome movie film (original) Colonel USAF\n  2. Cy of official rept of            Chief, Topical Division\n     Unconventional Acft sighting\n\nHand Carried\n25 Nov 52\nCapt. Bell,\nAFOIN-2A        Xover\n               X 062.2 Motion Pictures\n\nCOORDINATION: AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n[signature]          [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3eccbf8107baf1fab38fa6ff3aeab32624b24a63fc439c4b3a2f19bd72b22d9e", "output_sha256": "9f840eced27a190fc37df51e16aaad3d1e8f171d9a5038a4adeac868b2820900", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:13.929741+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p19", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 19, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                 SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n24-0                                          6 October 1950\n\nSUBJECT:  UNCONVENTIONAL AIRCRAFT\n\n\nTO:       District Commander\n          5th District Office of Special Investigations\n          Wright-Patterson Air Force Base\n          Dayton, Ohio\n\n\n\n          1.  Transmitted under separate cover is approximately fifteen\nfeet of moving picture film taken by Mr. Nicholas Mariana, of 2919\nFirst Avenue North, Great Falls, Montana, who is general manager\nof the Great Falls Baseball Club.\n\n          2.  Mr. Mariana made these pictures on 15 August 1950 between\nthe hours of 11:25 and 11:30 A. M., at Great Falls, Montana.  On\ninterview, he stated that he first sighted the objects while standing\nin the grandstand of the ball park located at 26th Street and Eleventh\nAvenue North, Great Falls, Montana, and that he saw two bright disc\nshaped objects proceeding in a southerly direction at an altitude\nof approximately ten thousand feet and at a distance of about three-\nquarters of a mile in a westerly direction, from the observer's view-\npoint.  Mr. Mariana then stated that he ran downstairs and outside\nto his car from which he obtained his camera and made the pictures\nshown in the film.  From the time of first sighting to the\ncompletion of taking of the pictures, Mr. Mariana estimated consumed\napproximately twenty seconds.  At the time of his taking\nthe pictures, a Miss Virginia Raunig, 112 Second Avenue North,\nGreat Falls, Montana, who is employed as his secretary, was a\nwitness.\n\n          3.  The water tower in instant pictures is located approximately\nseven hundred feet in a southwesterly direction from the point at\nwhich Mr. Mariana stood when taking the pictures and the tower is\napproximately one hundred seventy-five feet in height.\n\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                 SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nIncl 2                                                        COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e83b5d88c01248546f6961619067d837253530779d01e669d6dd5f52e670d09b", "output_sha256": "386b8b0ab6327799228720e895bc03152fe94e61bae71f19db71d70958b91096", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:16.010812+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p20", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 20, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\nC O P Y\n\n24-0                                    6 October 1950\nSUBJECT:  UNCONVENTIONAL AIRCRAFT\n\n        4.  With reference to background information as regards Nicholas\nMariana, he is a graduate of Montana State University, 1938, with a\nBA in journalism.  He was born in Miles City, Montana, in 1912, went\nto Montana State University in 1935 and has, since graduation from\nthat school, resided in Helena from 1940 to 1941 and from 1941 until\nthe present at Great Falls.  During the war, Mr. Mariana served in the\nArmy Air Forces from June 1943 to October 1945, attaining the rank of\nCorporal and was editor of a newspaper, The Northern Dispatch, at\nGreat Falls Air Force Base, at Great Falls, Montana.  Subject has been\nmarried for a period of ten years and has one child, a daughter, three\nyears of age.  Presently Mr. Mariana is employed as general manager of\nthe Great Falls Baseball Club, Great Falls, Montana, and also as a\nradio sports commentator and radio announcer of sporting events.  He\nenjoys an excellent reputation in the local community and is regarded\nas a reliable, trustworthy and honest individual.\n\n        5.  Prior to concluding the interview with Mr. Mariana, he\nwas advised that the film was being forwarded to the Air Material\nCommand because of that agency's interest in anything which would\ncontribute to its fund of technical intelligence data.\n\n\n\n1 Incl.                          JOHN P. BRYNILDSEN\n  Summary of Information         Captain, USAF\n  per provisions of Air          District Commander\n  Intelligence Requirements\n  Memo No. 4.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                        C O P Y", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "31bc1174ed1f4c5b477d47cbde617c5415c11ae4d7b66c5b2b1981b9d8cdb5de", "output_sha256": "9affae272f91eb2272e7cb7ce2d646ad16bad67826efbd8b677bc724a1149585", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:17.970497+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p21", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 21, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n24-0                                              6 October 1950\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:  District Commander, 5th District Office of Special\n                 Investigations, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\n                 Dayton, Ohio\n\nSUBJECT:         UNCONVENTIONAL AIRCRAFT\n\n\n\n        1.  On 5 October 1950, Mr. Mariana advised that the camera\nused by him in the taking of the moving picture film transmitted\nunder separate cover, was a Revere, 16 mm., magazine loading type\nwith an F. 1.9 wide-angle, telephoto lens.  Mr. Mariana stated\nthat the settings used at the time were: shutter opening F.22\nand focal setting, infinity.  Film make and type was Eastman\nKodachrome, daylight type, and speed at which pictures were taken\nwas sixteen frames per second.  Mr. Mariana further advised that\nin operating the camera intaking the pictures, he had \"panned\"\nthe camera slowly from right to left.\n\n        2.  A further check of the records of Base Operations, Great\nFalls Air Force Base, Great Falls, Montana, indicates that an\nF-94 type aircraft, #2503, and F-94 type aircraft, #2502, landed\nat Great Falls Air Force Base at 1133 and 1130 hours (Mountain\nStandard Time) respectively on 15 August 1950.  These aircraft\nwere assigned the 449th Fighter Squadron, Ladd Air Force Base,\nAlaska.  Mr. Mariana stated that almost immediately after taking\nthe motion pictures, two USAF jet type aircraft had flown across\nthe sky east of him, heading in a southerly direction.\n\n\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                SECURITY INFORMATION\n                                                              COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7f7e13fc097b88980b1bb8128881ea08a4a4d02da377aa5d527658df1e3cd82e", "output_sha256": "a72a01d604f8d4b218916d699c6be51a70b77154ac712d979bfb45780f9bcf8d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:19.957864+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p22", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 22, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nC O P Y\n\n\n                              PART II\n\n     1.  15 August 1950\n     2.  Between 1125 and 1130 Mountain Standard Time\n     3.  a. 26th and Eleventh Avenue North, Great Falls, Montana\n     4.  Two objects, initially approximately fifty yards apart.\n     5.  The U. S. Weather Bureau, Gore Field, Great Falls, Montana, which\n         keeps a record of the observable celestial phenomena or planets\n         reports that there were no such phenomena observable on 15 August 1950.\n     6.  Distance of objects from observer:\n         a.  Approximately three-quarters of a mile laterally in a westerly\n             direction.\n         b.  The angle of elevation from the horizon was about thirty-five\n             degrees.\n         c.  The altitude was approximately ten thousand feet.\n     7.  Mr. Mariana states object was in sight to him a total of about\n         twenty seconds and about seven seconds to his secretary, Miss Raunig.\n     8.  Mr. Mariana states that the appearance of the object was:\n         a.  Of a bright clean aluminum surface.\n         b.  disc shape--apparently had depth\n         c.  Objects appeared to be of metal material\n         d.  According to observer, objects were about fifty feet in diameter\n             and three feet in depth.\n         NOTE:  Observer has had occasion to frequently observe USAF C-54's\n                in flight in the local area and states the objects had a\n                diameter about three-quarters of the wing span of a C-54\n                when viewed from the side.\n     9.  Direction of flight:  Objects were moving in a southerly direction.\n     10. Tactics or maneuvers:  Movements of objects were horizontal but\n         slightly erratic as to speed.\n     11. No evidence of exhaust.\n     12. No clouds were observable on that date.\n     13. No lights were observed as being attached to objects.\n     14. a.  No wings observed\n         b.  No aerodynamic list of fuselage observed.\n         c.  No vertical jet observed.\n         d.  Objects, according to observer, definitely had an appearance of\n             a spinning motion; however no rotating cylinder or cone was observed.\n         e.  No aerostatic lifting devices were attached to objects.\n     15. a.  No propeller or jet device observed.\n         b.  No rotor observed.\n         c.  No aerodynamic vanes observed.\n         d.  No visible exhaust or jet openings.\n     16. a.  No fins observed\n         b.  No stabilizers observed.\n     17. No air ducts observed.\n     18. Speed estimated by observer to be approximately two hundred mph.\n     19. No sound; objects had a purported \"whoosh\" sound.\n\n                           CONFIDENTIAL\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                              C O P Y", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "aff6ebcca7a80602157a4d26011d9f738e34be10be835af4c1a6139be77686d5", "output_sha256": "4ccbfcc3f85acd9a0673efde097425988d59073be6e64d14b7de1b61ac51c871", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:22.829938+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p23", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 23, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "C O P Y\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nPART II (Cont'd)\n\n20. Objects vanished from view after about eight seconds, obscured by\n    uprights of water tank which can be noticed in the film.\n\n                        RELATIVE TO OBSERVER\n\n1.  Name of observer:  Nicholas Mariana\n2.  Address:  2919 First Avenue North, Great Falls, Montana\n3.  Occupation:  Baseball club manager.\n4.  Great Falls Baseball\n5.  Pertinent hobbies:  Observer is not an amateur astronomer,\n    pilot or engineer;  however, he has broadcast sporting events and\n    is interested in photography\n6.  Ability to determine color, speed and size of moving objects of\n    observer should be relatively good in view of his experience as a\n    sporting events announcer.\n7.  Reliability of observer:  Enjoys an excellent reputation in the\n    local community and is regarded as a reliable, trustworthy and\n    honest individual.\n8.  Notes relative to observer on sightings in general:  Mr. Mariana\n    stated to the undersigned that he had read numerous newspaper\n    articles on the subject of flying discs and flying saucers and had\n    not attached very much significance to them.  However, Mr. Mariana\n    almost invariably carries a camera in order that he may make\n    \"opportunity pictures\" and had previously thought that if he could\n    see such unconventional aircraft in flight, he would take motion\n    pictures of them.\n    b.  Observer's attention was definitely drawn to objects by their\n        glint of light.\n9.  Witnesses:  Miss Virginia Raunig, 112 Second Avenue North, age 19,\n    employed as a secretary.  Miss Raunig impressed interrogator as\n    being a fairly reliable individual and of good sound judgment.  Miss\n    Raunig confirmed sightings and number of objects and in substance\n    verified Mr. Mariana's statements as regards objects' appearance,\n    shape, speed, sound and direction of flight.\n\n                           GENERAL\n\n1.  Teletype sequences of local weather conditions:  On 4 October 1950,\n    Mr. C. Robert Guern, Chief Weather Observer, U. S. Weather Office,\n    Gore Field, Great Falls, Montana, after first examining the tele-\n    type sequences of local weather conditions, Great Falls area, stated\n    that there were thin scattered clouds, thirty thousand feet, visibility\n    sixty miles, barometric reading, 1013.9 millibars, temperature\n    seventy-seven degrees, dew point, forty-five degrees, altimeter 30.02\n    southwesterly winds, twenty-five miles per hour.  Time of this\n    teletype sequence was 1130 hours, 15 August 1950.\n\n2.  Winds Aloft Report received from Mr. C. Robert Guern, Chief Weather\n    Observer, U. S. Weather Office, Gore Field, Great Falls, Montana,\n    who stated that:\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                                C O P Y", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f5677603a28636e96d29d15448b51c483078544a3b3c7580460ef3313e05419a", "output_sha256": "7582ade97f859aebedbc1f73ab4859180f1ba74bc60e019fa4f5efcbc2a3002c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:25.801559+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p24", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 24, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n          CONFIDENTIAL\n        SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    PART II\n\nWINDS ALOFT REPORT (Cont'd)\n\n  at 0800, surface winds, 290 degrees, 15 miles per hour,\n              4000 feet, 270 degrees, 19 miles per hour,\n              5000 feet, 240 degrees, 25 miles per hour,\n              6000 feet, 250 degrees, 22 miles per hour\n              7000 feet, 270 degrees, 22 miles per hour\n              8000 feet, 270 degrees, 31 miles per hour\n              9000 feet, 260 degrees, 43 miles per hour\n           10,000 feet, 260 degrees, 45 miles per hour\n           12,000 feet, 260 degrees, 42 miles per hour\n           14,000 feet, 260 degrees, 34 miles per hour\n           16,000 feet, 270 degrees, 34 miles per hour\n           18,000 feet, 270 degrees, 33 miles per hour\n           20,000 feet, 270 degrees, 36 miles per hour\n           25,000 feet, 260 degrees, 26 miles per hour\n\n  at 1400 hours, same date, winds aloft readings were:\n\n              surface winds, 230 degrees, 24 miles per hour\n              4000 feet, 240 degrees, 25 miles per hour\n              5000 feet, 250 degrees, 36 miles per hour\n              6000 feet, 250 degrees, 41 miles per hour\n              7000 feet, 250 degrees, 40 miles per hour\n              8000 feet, 250 degrees, 35 miles per hour\n              9000 feet, 260 degrees, 28 miles per hour\n           10,000 feet, 260 degrees, 24 miles per hour\n           12,000 feet, 260 degrees, 30 miles per hour\n           14,000 feet, 260 degrees, 55 miles per hour\n           16,000 feet, 250 degrees, 54 miles per hour\n           18,000 feet, 260 degrees, 36 miles per hour\n           20,000 feet, 260 degrees, 34 miles per hour\n           25,000 feet, 260 degrees, 39 miles per hour\n\nThere were no testing devices nor Raysonde devices sent aloft between\nthe hours of 0800 and 1400 hours, 15 August 1950.  Raysonde\ninstruments were sent aloft at 0900 and 1400 hours, 15 August 1950\nby the U. S. Weather Bureau, Gore Field, Great Falls, Montana.\nMr. Guern further stated that there were no celestial phenomena\nlisted in the U. S. Weather Bureau report for the twenty-four hour\nperiod 0800 hours, 15 August 1950, to 0800 hours, 16 August 1950.\n\n\n          CONFIDENTIAL\n        SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                           COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f46c2502e108e2e80f5443199760c320ec5399ca7162f9b11bef3ff97db8c23", "output_sha256": "57d35bd4103494ea55fac3c0fe36183b2f4dbaff5a75d2c2dc710b8d00214407", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:28.858035+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p25", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 25, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\n21 November 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To prepare a Memorandum for Director of Naval Intelligence.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  A previous Memorandum to Director of Naval Intelligence dated\n24 Oct 52 requested a complete analysis of a roll of movie film depicting 10 unidentified flying objects.  Full details were given as to\nthe type analysis desired.\n\n     3.  Another roll of film showing 2 unidentified flying objects is\nnow available.  Analysis of this film is desired.  Additionally, a comparison with the previous film may prove productive.  The attached\nMemorandum to Director of Naval Intelligence requests that these analyses\nbe made.\n\n     4.  Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the\nDaily Staff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n     5.  Approval, signature and dispatch of attached Memorandum.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Smith, Ext. 71016  W H Smith\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072  DeBukelagt.\n\n\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ec92594c7d084709b5aba33b45889533cc969240a0b864105b7bb78a298e4cab", "output_sha256": "2f3d38d6a37c5a93f3ab6b9fcd4e2767798fdc4059d1adb40d51adb3d7070bf0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:30.402841+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p26", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 26, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2 Maj Fournet/fh/75990/Rm 4B 864\n                                    wrtn 24 Oct 52\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                 SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\n                                              OCT 2 4 1952\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:  Director of Naval Intelligence\n                 Attention:  Op 322Y5\n\nSUBJECT:  Interpretation of Movies of Unidentified Flying Objects\n\n     1.  The attached movies (see Incl. 1) are possibly the best\ndocumentary evidence yet obtained on unidentified flying objects.\nThey have been analyzed by an Air Force photographic laboratory.\nHowever, it is our desire to obtain an independent analysis by a\nseparate laboratory in order that we may better interpret the\nimplications of these data.  For this reason, it is requested\nthat as complete an interpretation as possible be rendered by a\nNavy activity.\n\n     2.  Circumstances surrounding the photography are summarized\nin Inclosure 2.  Additional details were requested by messages\nwhich are included as Inclosures 3 and 5 and were obtained in the\nreplies attached as Inclosures 4 and 6.  With regard to Inclosures\n5 and 6, the final footage of film referred to has been detached\nand returned to CPO Newhouse.  However, it was deduced from this\nportion that Newhouse obtained excellent results while hand-\nholding the camera; there was almost no camera motion evident.\nThis deduction was applied to the analysis of that portion of the\nfilm depicting the motion of the single object which detached itself\nfrom the group as explained in Inclosure 2.\n\n     3.  A list of representative questions for the interpretation\nis attached as Inclosure 7.  These questions are indicative of the\ntype data desired.  Any additional data which can be obtained\nwould be most welcome, particularly as concerns the light intensity\nof the objects, the formations (including three-dimensional renditions,\nif possible), comments regarding the possibility that the images were\ncaused by aircraft and the conditions which must have prevailed for\naircraft to produce such images, etc.\n\n     4.  It was determined from the Naval Observatory, Washington,\nD.C. that the position of the sun at the time and location of the\nphotography was 64.5° elevation and 131° azimuth.\n\n     5.  Your cooperation in satisfying this request at the earliest\npracticable time is earnestly solicited.\n\n          X045, Navy [ILLEGIBLE]     [signed] matthews\n                                        27 oct 52\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                 SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "474a59f602517ec91f0cf277a8b2abb2278c0b6cf42d7aea370c2cb25cca44bf", "output_sha256": "474a59f602517ec91f0cf277a8b2abb2278c0b6cf42d7aea370c2cb25cca44bf", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:33.938966+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p27", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 27, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nMemorandum for:  Director of Naval Intelligence, Attn:  Op 322Y5\n          Subject: Interpretation of Movies of Unidentified\n                   Flying Objects (continued)\n\n\n     6.  For additional data or referral of specific questions,\nColonel W.H. Smith of the Current Intelligence Branch may be\ncontacted direct.  His telephone number is 71016.\n\n\n\n  7 Incls.\n    1.  Movie (along only)         JOHN G. ERIKSEN\n    2.  Cy of ltr fr               Colonel, USAF\n           CPO Newhouse            Chief, Policy & Management Group\n    3.  Cy of AFOIN 57264          Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n    4.  Cy of CAFIN 65202          Directorate of Intelligence\n    5.  Cy of AFOIN 59782\n    6.  Cy of CAFIN 74096\n    7.  List of questions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n\nAFOIN-2A2        AFOIN-2A        AFOIN-2X        AFOIN-2\n\n[signature]      [signature]     [signature]     [signature]\n\n\n                              2\n\n                         CONFIDENTIAL\n                       SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "241f47888d44bfe3bc3d76d2e6f8928d50a4f5364817206099f89332e8002591", "output_sha256": "0d9b5b211960834ef3ecbc77a41486184cfa3a3e2ec9f21a86dce1fe1ca74b11", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:36.435637+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p28", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 28, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    AVIATION SUPPLY DEPOT\n                     NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER\n                    OAKLAND 4, CALIFORNIA\n\nNT 4-28/8310/177283                              11 August 1952\n\nFrom:  Chief Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse, 177283, U.S.N.\nTo:    Commanding Officer, Hill Air Force Base, Ogden, Utah\n\nSubj:  Motion Pictures of Unidentified Objects in Air\n\nEncl:  (1)  One (1) fifty-foot roll of processed 16mm color motion\n             picture film\n\n1.  Enclosure (1) is forwarded herewith for whatever value it may have in con-\nnection with your investigation of the so-called \"Flying Saucers\".  Pertinent\ndata follows:\n\nPlace:     About 7 miles north of Tremonton, Utah on U.S. Highway No. 30S.\n\nTime:      1110 Wednesday 2 July 1952.\n\nCamera:    B&H Automaster, magazine load, 3\" telephotolens, 16 frames per\n           second.  Handheld.\n\nExposure:  First few feet - f:8.  Balance - f:16.  Clear sun, cloudless sky.\n           EKCo Kodachrome film - Daylight.  Exposure was changed with the\n           mistaken idea of darkening the sky to gain greater contrast.  The\n           result was merely general under exposures.\n\nGeneral Background:  Driving from Washington, D.C. to Portland, Oregon, on\n           the morning of 2 July my wife noticed a group of objects in the\n           sky that she could not identify.  She asked me to stop the car and\n           look.  There was a group of about ten or twelve objects - that bore\n           no relation to anything I had seen before - milling about in a\n           rough formation and proceeding in a westerly direction.  I opened\n           the luggage compartment of the car and got my camera out of a suit-\n           case.  Loading it hurriedly, I exposed approximately thirty feet of\n           film.  There was no reference point in the sky and it was impossible\n           for me to make any estimate of speed, size, altitude or distance.\n           Toward the end one of the objects reversed course and proceeded away\n           from the group.  I held the camera still and allowed this single\n           one to cross the field of view, picking it up again and repeating\n           for three or four such passes.  By this time all of the objects\n           had disappeared.  I expended the balance of the film late that\n           afternoon on a mountain somewhere in Idaho.\n\n\n\n                                        /s/\n                                   Delbert C. Newhouse\n\nIncl 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f76505e50d9a1148bb389dbc490e94e44830f820670b09b162b6a6ab4490a6f", "output_sha256": "0b63f6efcd5be4c2638d744098698fad4dcd349e94a3d8726d284587963c8e1b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:39.105258+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p29", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 29, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Copy of TWX No. AFOIN-57264\n\nFrom:  HQ USAF, WASH, DC                    RESTRICTED\n                                           SECURITY INFORMATION\nTo:    CG WADF\n       Hamilton AFB, California\n\nATTN:  DIR OF INTELL.  REPORT OF UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECTS AND INCLOSED MOVIE\nFILM ON SIGHTING 2 JUL 52 NEAR TREMONTON, UTAH RECEIVED THIS HEADQUARTERS 5 SEP\n52 FROM CPO DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE, 177283, USN, STATIONED AT AVIATION SUPPLY\nDEPOT, NAVAL SUPPLY CENTER, OAKLAND, CALIF.  REQUEST NEWHOUSE BE INTERVIEWED\nAS SOON AS PRACTICAL BY AN INTELLIGENCE OFFICER AND THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION\nOBTAINED:\n\n     (1)  ANY SOUND HEARD DURING OBSERVATION?  IF SO, DESCRIBE.\n\n     (2)  ANY EXHAUST TRAILS OR CONTRAILS SEEN AT ANY TIME DURING OBSERVATION?\n          IF SO DESCRIBE.\n\n     (3)  WERE ANY AIRCRAFT, BIRDS, BALLOONS OR OTHER IDENTIFIABLE OBJECTS\n          SEEN IN AIR IMMEDIATELY BEFORE, DURING OR IMMEDIATELY AFTER\n          OBSERVATION?  IF SO, GIVE DETAILS.\n\n     (4)  DID SINGLE OBJECT WHICH DETACHED ITSELF FROM GROUP HEAD IN DIRECTION OPPOSITE TO ORIGINAL COURSE AND DID IT DISAPPEAR FROM VIEW\n          WHILE STILL TRAVELLING IN THIS DIRECTION?\n\n     (5)  AT APPROXIMATELY WHAT ELEVATION AND IN WHAT DIRECTION (BEARING)\n          WAS CAMERA POINTED DURING EXPOSURE OF FILM?\n\n     (6)  WHAT WAS POSITION OF SUN RELATIVE TO OBJECTS AND TO HIM?\n\n     (7)  WHAT WERE WEATHER CONDITIONS?  APPROXIMATE TEMPERATURE? HAZY OR\n          CLEAR? WIND DIRECTION AND SPEED?\n\n     (8)  ANY METEOROLOGICAL ACTIVITY NOTICED DURING THAT DAY?\n\n     (9)  DOES HE HAVE ANY OPINION REGARDING FOLLOWING:\n\n                                          SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nexc 3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d3a75ca8cdaf145b31d75db5bd24000b91e63a7b99a78d33c6dd414ed8613313", "output_sha256": "14ba9ac5aa45bcb200933702adf727b33b6b9204a12c72610d95f67095c82f24", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:41.329813+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p30", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 30, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "(a) WAS LIGHT FROM OBJECTS CAUSED BY REFLECTION OR WERE THEY\n     SOURCE OF LIGHT?\n(b) SHAPE OF OBJECTS?\n(c) WERE THEY ALL APPROXIMATELY THE SAME SHAPE?\n(d) COLOR OF OBJECTS?                    RESTRICTED\n                                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n(e) WERE THEY ALL SAME COLOR?\n(f) TYPE MOTION ATTRIBUTABLE TO OBJECTS, BOTH ABOUT OWN AXES AND\n     AXIS OF FLIGHT PATH?\n(g) DID ALL OBJECTS HAVE SAME TYPE MOTION?\n(h) HOW DID OBJECTS DISAPPEAR FROM VIEW?\n(10) WAS ANY FILTER USED ON CAMERA?\n(11) REMEMBER ANY LANDMARKS AROUND LOCATION WHICH WOULD FACILITATE\n     FINDING IT IN FUTURE?\n(12) KNOW OF ANYONE ELSE WHO SIGHTED OBJECTS?\n(13) EVER SIGHTED UNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECTS BEFORE?  IF SO, OBTAIN\n     DETAILS IAW PAR 7c OF AFL 200-5.\nADDITIONALLY, DESIRE INTERVIEWING OFFICER FURNISH ESTIMATE RELIABILITY AND\nPHOTOGRAPHIC PROFICIENCY OF NEWHOUSE.  AFL 200-5 MAY AID IN CONDUCTING\nINTERVIEW.  REQUEST INFORMATION BE FORWARDED BY ELECTRICAL MEANS AS SOON AS\nAVAILABLE TO ATIC WITH INFORMATION THIS HEADQUARTERS.  IN RESPONSE REPLY\nTO AFOIN-2A2.  Restricted.\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f83e9e30f15d1d91d9f28c2dbdcf5126149ac9004f3a09facabfa1db9ee8c8ae", "output_sha256": "f83e9e30f15d1d91d9f28c2dbdcf5126149ac9004f3a09facabfa1db9ee8c8ae", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:43.157012+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p31", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 31, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\n                    Copy TWX CAFIN 65202  RESTRICTED\n                                        RITY INFORMATION\nR 121650Z ZNJ\n\nFM CG 28TH AD HAFB CALIF\n\nTO CHIEF ATIC WRIGHT-PATTERSON AFB OHIO\n\nINFO CG ADC ENT AFB COLO SPRINGS COLO\n\nUSAF WASHINGTON 25 DC\n\nCG WADF HAFB CALIF\n\nRESTRICTED/9171. ATTN DIR OF INTEL. IN REPLY TO AFOIN-2A2 AND WADF MSG\n\nWDOID 29149 FOL INFO REQ BY HQ USAF HAS BEEN OBTAINED BY INTERVIEW WITH\n\nCPO DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE. 177273, AVN SUP DEP, NAVAL SUP CEN, OAKLAND, CALIF\n\nREGARDING UNIDENTIFIED FLY OBJS AND MOVIE FILM ON SIGHTING 2 JUL 52 NEAR\n\nTREMONTON, UTAH. CPO NEWHOUSE, HIS WIFE, SON AND DAUGHTER WERE ALL INTER-\n\nVIEWED AT THE NEWHOUSE HOME IN BERKELEY, CALIF ON 10 SEP 52 BY DIRECTOR OF\n\nINTELLIGENCE, 28TH AIR DIV (DEF). FOL ANSWERS TO QUESTIONS 1 THRU 13\n\nIN USAF REQUEST ARE SUBMITTED:\n\n1. NO SOUND HEARD DURING OBSERVATION. 2. NO EXHAUST TRAILS OR CONTRAILS\n\nOBSERVED. 3. NO AIRCRAFT, BIRDS, BALLOONS, OR OTHER IDENTIFIABLE OBJECTS\n\nSEEN IN AIR IMMEDIATELY BEFORE, DURING, OR IMMEDIATELY AFTER OBSERVATION.\n\n4. SINGLE OBJECT WHICH DETACHED ITSELF FROM GROUP DID HEAD IN DIRECTION\n\nOPPOSITE ORIGINAL COURSE AND DISAPPEARED FROM VIEW WHILE STILL TRAVELING\n\nIN THIS DIRECTION. 5. CAMERA POINTED AT ESTIMATED 70 DEGREES ELEVATION\n\nAND DESCRIBED AN ARC FROM APPROX DUE EAST TO DUE WEST THEN FROM DUE WEST\n\nTO APPROX 60 DEGREES FROM NORTH IN PHOTOGRAPHING DETACHED OBJ HEADING IN\n\nDIRECTION OPPOSITE ORIGINAL COURSE. 6. SUN WAS APPROX OVERHEAD OF OBSERVER.\n\nOBJECTS WERE AT APPROX 70 DEGREES ABOVE TERRAIN ON A COURSE SEVERAL MILES\n\nFROM OBSERVER. 7. WEATHER CONDITIONS: BRIGHT SUNLIGHT, CLEAR, APPROX 80\n\nDEGREES TEMPERATURE, SLIGHT BREEZE FROM EAST NORTH EAST APPROX 3 TO 5 MPH.\n\n8. NO METEOROLOGICAL ACTIVITY NOTED DURING THAT DAY. 9. OPINION REGARDING\n\nFOLLOWING CIN A. LIGHT FROM OBJECTS CAUSED BY REFLECTION: B. OBJECTS\n\n                    enc 4", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9dbfe5357b30e482aa37b85a334a46553958a295f741932c0b60ace9aad22186", "output_sha256": "20ad67692b35d39c5468f922550653332dc9cdd2f9ccee0321a62c7718cd624e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:45.994156+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p32", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 32, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\nAPPEARED APPROX AS LONG AS THEY WERE WIDE AND THIN. C. APPEARED IDENTICAL\nIN SHAPE. D. 12 TO 14 OBJECTS. E. ALL APPEARED LIGHT COLOR. F. NO\nOPINION. G. APPEARED TO HAVE SAME TYPE OF MOTION EXCEPT FOR ONE OBJECT\nWHICH REVERSED ITS COURSE. H. DISAPPEARED FROM VIEW BY MOVING OUT OF\nRANGE OF EYESIGHT. 10. NO FILTERS USED. 11. ONE LOW HILL 2 OR 3 MILES\nTO RIGHT OF US HWY 30 DASH S WITH OBSERVER FACING NORTH. LOCATED\nAPPROX 10 MILES NORTH TREMONTON, UTAH. 12. OTHER PERSONS SIGHTING OBJECTS\nWERE: MRS. D. C. NEWHOUSE, WIFE; DELBERT C. NEWHOUSE, JR, SON, AGE 14;\nANNE NEWHOUSE, DAUGHTER, AGE 12. WHOLE NEWHOUSE FAMILY INCLUDED IN INTER-\nVIEW. 13. CPO NEWHOUSE AND FAMILY HAVE NEVER SIGHTED UNIDENTIFIED FLYING\nOBJECTS BEFORE. NEWHOUSE STATED THAT HE NEVER BELIEVED HE WOULD JOIN\nRANKS OF THOSE REPORTING SUCH OBJECTS PRIOR TO THIS OBSERVATION. CPO\nNEWHOUSE AND MRS. NEWHOUSE APPEARED TO BE EXTREMELY HONEST AND RELIABLE\nPERSONS. CPO NEWHOUSE STATED HE HAS BEEN IN THE NAVAL SERVICE FOR OVER\n19 YEARS WITH SERVICE AS A COMMISSIONED OFFICER DURING WW 2. NEWHOUSE\nIS GRADUATE OF NAVAL PHOTOGRAPHIC SCHOOL IN 1935 AND CLAIMS OVER 1000\nHOURS IN THE AIR AS A PHOTOGRAPHER ON ACTUAL AERIAL PHOTOGRAPH MISSIONS.\nNEWHOUSE ALSO DOES CONSIDERABLE GROUND PHOTOGRAPHY. IT IS BELIEVED NEWHOUSE\nCOULD BE CLASSIFIED AS AN EXPERT PHOTOGRAPHER.\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nINFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5038ac230b8678212aad4e98b47e231e98e4c20ecc85adc1e4cc11f2a4776152", "output_sha256": "e0f47d3b2d22d5d26915922394e24b1ef37adc900edcfb127f2919c2a20d6a82", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:48.122357+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p33", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 33, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SECURITY INFORMATION\nFROM:  HQ USAF          7 Oct 52    RESTRICTED\n                    ACTION:  ROUTINE  INFO:  ROUTINE\n\nTO:   CG 28th AIRDIV HAMILTON AFB CALIF   CRYPTOPRECAUTION:  NO\n\nINFO:  CHIEF ATIC WRIGHT-PATTERSON AFB OHIO  IDENTIFICATION:  9171\n                                                               CAF IN 65202\n                                                               (12 Sep 52)\n\n                         CLASSIFICATION:  RESTRICTED\n\nFROM:  AFOIN 59782\n\n     ATTENTION:  Director of Intelligence.  Reference your message\n\n9171 dated 12 Sep 52.  Request CPO Newhouse be asked following\n\nadditional question:  Was tripod used to photograph mountain\n\nscene in Idaho which appears on final footage of film in\n\nquestion?  Forward information by electrical means to ATIC with\n\ninformation this headquarters.  In response reply to AFOIN-2A2\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2______________  AFOIN-2A _______________\n\n                    SECURITY CLASSIFICATION:  RESTRICTED  PAGE 1\n\nDRAFTER'S NAME:                RELEASING OFFICER'S SIGNATURE:\n\n  Maj. Dewey J. Fournet         DONALD E BERRE, Captain, USAF\n                                Executive Officer, Topical Division\n                                Deputy Director for Estimates\nAFOIN-2A2                       Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n          TELEPHONE:   75990\n\n\n                         DECLASSIFIED\n\nIncl 5", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cc8c7ab34700fefc09850358178a25ce6c3dfc31a4427933512e6490b7163b6a", "output_sha256": "181134f4d83d4f8f9ee1dfd33730139a30a2885281d3064ea93f64874c95886b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:49.879074+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p34", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 34, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY                    RESTRICTED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\n                         STAFF MESSAGE DIVISION\n\n                         INCOMING CLASSIFIED MESSAGE\n\n                                                    RESTRICTED\n                                                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nCAFIN 74096\n\nFM JWPML/CG 28th AIR DIV (DEF) HAMILTON AFB, CALIF.\n\nTO JEDWP/CHIEF, ATIC WRIGHT-PATTERSON AFB, OHIO\n\nINFO:  JWPHQ/DIRECTOR OF INTELLIGENCE, HQ USAF, WASHINGTON 25, D.C.\n\n\n/RESTRICTED/ 9171 IN REPLY TO AFOIN-2A2 FOLLOWING INFORMATION REQUESTED BY\n\nHQ USAF HAS BEEN OBTAINED BY TELEPHONE CONVERSATION WITH CPO DELBERT C.\n\nNEWHOUSE, 177273, AVN SUP DEP, NAVAL SUP CENTER, OAKLAND, CALIF. REGARDING AN ADDITIONAL QUESTION ABOUT MOVIE FILM ON UNIDENTIFIED OBJECT SIGHTING ON 2 JULY 1952.\n\nQUESTION: \"WAS TRIPOD USED TO PHOTOGRAPH MOUNTAIN SCENE IN IDAHO\n\nWHICH APPEARS ON FINAL FOOTAGE OF FILM IN QUESTION\"?  ANSWER:  NEGATIVE,\n\nENTIRE ROLL OF FILM WAS HANDHELD.\n\n\nINFO:  OIN\n\n\nCAFIN:  74096   (10 Oct 52)\n\n\n\n\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n                              RESTRICTED\n\nEncl 6", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f95dcaa0285d6d6a6a1d79c4b1517d0ccb8bc964fb1e1c2074de85f99fe6806f", "output_sha256": "1fa30bd6d7e7afafdb9fbb33be6e0d67b3d4d6b2c7236dd2d5467c31431f8ddb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:51.705867+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p35", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 35, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SUGGESTED POINTS FOR ANALYSIS\n\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n     The following questions are suggested for guidance regarding the\ngeneral type of analysis desired:\n\n     1.  Are images made by light source or reflection?\n\n     2.  Any indication of what kind of objects could have caused images?\nIs there any bird sufficiently actinic to cause images?  Could they have\nbeen caused by aircraft or balloons?\n\n     3.  What causes impression that some objects at times appear to\nbecome 2 or 3 where there was originally one; or, conversely, 2 or 3 objects\nat times appear to merge into one.\n\n     4.  Do all objects have same characteristics?\n\n          a.  Same apparent shape?\n          b.  Same color?\n          c.  Same relative size?\n          d.  Same general motion?\n\n     5.  What are shape(s), color(s) and relative size(s) of objects?\n\n     6.  To what can the \"fade-in\" and \"fade-out\" of the objects be attributed?\n\n     7.  What type motion is attributable to the objects about their own axis\nas well as about axis of flight path)?\n\n     8.  Is there any acceleration evident in their motion along light\npath axis?\n\n     9.  Can the motion of the camera (panning and joggling) be allowed\nfor sufficiently to permit determination of the angular velocity of objects\nwhich cross the field of view?  (Reference particularly the single object\nwhich crosses field; photographer states that camera was held motionless\nwhile object crossed field of view.)\n\n\nEnc  7\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "79e980a325f6b210c27e352622510fcd344be8e31e6f37558300e21abd1eecf2", "output_sha256": "b6e5f27f523a8d1bf53e5e937a1269e0dc88823d69329b22591eab038a26c991", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:53.558971+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p36", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 36, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n     10.  Determine patterns of flight from position plots for each\nframe, then:\n\n          a.  Is there any recurring pattern in the relative position\n              of the objects?\n          b.  Do they maintain same relative positions in formation during\n              any maneuvers, particularly violent maneuvers?\n          c.  Is relative position maintained coincidental with movement\n              about their axis?\n          d.  If undulating motion is present among a number of objects\n              which are maintaining a semblance of formation, do those\n              objects undulate in phase?  Ditto for tumbling motion?\n          e.  Is there any indication of abrupt changes in direction\n              of flight path through fairly large angles (e.g. 90 degrees\n              or more during interval of 2 or 3 frames)?\n          f.  Do any objects appear to remain motionless at the same time\n              that others move about?\n          g.  Can all objects be accounted for at all times or do some\n              literally disappear while still well within field of view?\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c4ab8102301cb4875a7f42a1511374813c077a052cb7c7633cb77d04674276da", "output_sha256": "31e714de2799b4f00723678cc1d56176bd9aa61df8f4ee6971ccecb41a28aebf", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:54.926184+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p37", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 37, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-1B3/Capt Laidlaw/eeb/77648\n           wrtn 24 Nov 52\n\n\n\n\nChief, Air Technical          Transmittal of Correspondence  24 NOV 1952\nIntelligence Center           Dept of the Air Force\nWright-Patterson AFB          Headquarters USAF              Capt Laidlaw/77648\nOhio                          Washington 25, D.C.            AFOIN-1B3\n\n     Forwarded as a matter pertaining to your Center.\n\n\n\n1 Incl                        /s/\n  Ltr fr I.C. Hoyer,\n  Eugene, Oregon, dtd 10 Nov 52          J. C. McANINCH\n                                         Major,    USAF\n                                         Chief, Documents Branch\n                                         Dissemination Control Division\n                                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n          ✓\n          ✓ x312. Correspondence\n                              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ________\n            x322.7a TIC\n\n\n\n\n                                               OUT\n                                          G 25 NOV 1952\n                                          [ILLEGIBLE]\n\nAFOIN-1B3\nCapt Laidlaw [signature]\nMaj McAninch [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d001eda39644a53b3579c0050f0a4351d65f03f8b5d9ea2831ad53b04ff8b9ec", "output_sha256": "e274b516388a3348df6ba7cf88e3a2e903d837e15358456c2c96c19627dccf26", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:56.408363+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p38", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 38, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 21 November 1952\nMaj Fournet/tmw/75990\n\n(Uncl)\nCorrespondence from Messrs. Oliver Amlie, Harvey S. Gersenfish and Edmond LeRoy.\nExecutive,                                          21 November 1952\nDirectorate of Research and Development, DCS/O\nAttention:  Maj Forsman                                    I\nDeputy Director for Estimates                  Maj Fournet/tmw/75990\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n     1.  Inclosures are forwarded as a matter of primary interest.  No replies have\nbeen made by this office.\n\n     2.  Mr. Amlie submitted a previous letter pertaining to the alleged observation of\na \"flying saucer\".  It was acknowledged by this office.\n\n     3.  Mr. LeRoy corresponded with us a few months ago and claimed to have available some information on flying saucers which would be of interest to the USAF.  Our\nreply to him stated that we found it impossible to contact him personally as he\nrequested.\n\n              x360.2 Research & Development\n                         SIGNED\n\n3 Incls   (w/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Oliver Amlie to                Colonel, USAF\n     Col Adams dtd                         Chief, Topical Division\n     26 Oct 52                             Deputy Director for Estimates\n  2. Diagram of flying saucer              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n     fr Harvey S. Gersenfish\n     Cincinnati 37, Ohio\n     Ltr fr Edmond L. LeRoy to\n     Col Adams dtd\n     11 Oct 52\n\n\n\n\n              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE -------->\n\n\nAFOIN 2A2              AFOIN 2A\n\n[signature]            [signature]\n\n                                           OUT\n                                        G 24 NOV 1952\n                                         [stamp]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6786b6a86ccd3712ec51525d534bceddcc25d0ffd0325bcb228a7d10f5e8be01", "output_sha256": "95125c761d3aca7ab65140a0346b5cabb0d18543fd15377ccb3c9c1db5fc1aad", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:58.567092+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p39", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 39, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\n20 Nov 52\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n                                    NOV 20 1952\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN          Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\n\n     2.  Request preparation of 3rd Ind to Incl 1 acknowledging receipt.\n\n     3.  No reply has been made to Mr. Boutelle.\n\n     4.  Incl 4 is a copy of the reply made by General Bradley's office to Incl 3.\nFurther action is not recommended.\n\n     5.  There were no previous reports from the sources who prepared Incls 5 and 6.\nQuestionnaires were supplied by and returned to this office and constitute the only\nknown record of these observations.\n                                          COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\n                              SIGNED\n\n6 Incls (w/orig only)             WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr 78th Air Base Sqdn    Colonel, USAF\n     Truax Field, Madison, Wis.   Chief, Topical Division\n     dtd 4 Nov 52 w/1st & 2nd Inds.  Deputy Director for Estimates\n  2. Ltr fr Arthur Boutelle,      Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n     Patterson, N.J. dtd 9 Nov 52\n  3. Ltr to Gen Omar Bradley fr\n     Argyrios Kouzas, Thessaloniki,    ✗322.7ATIC\n     Greece dtd 24 Oct 52\n  4. Cy of reply to Mr. Kouzas fr\n     Gen Bradley dtd 29 Oct 52\n  5. Questionnaire submitted by\n     L/C Milton Morris Kaufmann,\n     Falls Church, Va.\n  6. Questionnaire submitted by\n     Mrs. Carol Sprague, Vineland, N.J.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                                              No M/R necessary.\n\n[signatures]\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "435fb2f137d056137a3b484c15327a63d707c7e736051da791dff89831097d29", "output_sha256": "435fb2f137d056137a3b484c15327a63d707c7e736051da791dff89831097d29", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:00.942107+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p40", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 40, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "NOV 2 0 1952\n\nMrs. Rose Marie Holtz\n346 First Street\nNiagara Falls, New York\n\nDear Mrs. Holtz:\n\nYour recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n\nWe appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\nSincerely,\n\nG 24 NOV 1952\nDIR/INT\nHQ USAF\n\nWILLIAM A. ADAMS\nColonel, USAF\nChief, Topical Division\nDeputy Director for Estimates\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION: AFOIN-2A2        AFOIN-2A  DESIGNATION MADE\n\n[ILLEGIBLE signature]          [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n   [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "37b4087151e9626a0f2016d392d2437399dbdc2c53eb240d0c8a2d75ec7de1a6", "output_sha256": "3441373625d48823d049c3f05d0ff4303f5bb25268c9f26f13e6df318bd27b5a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:02.117188+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p41", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 41, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nW/18 November 1952\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n                                                    NOV 18 1952\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN              Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\n\n     2.  A letter of acknowledgement was sent to Mrs. Scott (see Incl 1).  A\nquestionnaire was inclosed for her to complete and mail to you.\n\n     3.  Mr. Zimmerman's letter (Incl 2) was also acknowledged.  He was informed\nthat the data which he supplied would be referred to you.\n\n     4.  Mrs. Zepp submitted the record of her observations (Incl 3) at our in-\nvitation.  A copy of our letter of acknowledgment is attached as Incl 4.\n\n     5.  Incl 6 is a copy of our reply to Mr. Gorman's letter (Incl 5).  These are\nfor your information and require no further action.\n\n                    Z-322 7 At/C\n                         SIGNED\n\n6 Incls (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mrs. Grace Scott,       Colonel, USAF\n     Birmingham, Ala dtd 27 Oct 52  Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Mr. E.C. Zimmerman,     Deputy Director for Estimates\n     Akron, Ohio dtd 30 Oct 52      Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Mrs. C.R. Zepp,\n     Hyattsville, Md dtd 8 Nov 52\n  4. Ltr to Mrs. C.R. Zepp\n  5. Ltr fr Mr. Robert J. Gorman,\n     Chicago, Ill dtd 29 Oct 52\n  6. Cy of ltr to Mr. Gorman,\n     dtd 12 Nov 52\n\n\n                                              OUT\n                                          19 NOV 1952\n\n\n     COORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n          [signature]          [signature]\n               pf", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e417a22ec8a986993a9c64a8b69b8ad2b30a0ddd5019aa001a82dc47f5167596", "output_sha256": "e417a22ec8a986993a9c64a8b69b8ad2b30a0ddd5019aa001a82dc47f5167596", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:05.031016+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p42", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 42, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\n                                        AC/71379\n                                        14 November 1952\n\n\n                                        NOV 17 1952\n\n\nMr. Narval W. Reece\n1578 Van Fandt Road\nCincinnati 31, Ohio\n\nDear Mr. Reece:\n\n        Your letter of 21 October 1952 to the Federal Bureau\nof Investigation was referred to us for attention.\n\n        We have studied the photograph and negative which you\nsubmitted and are happy to advise you that the \"object\"\nwhich appears on the former is a flaw or blemish resulting\nfrom the printing process.  This is confirmed by the absence\nof a similar image on the negative.\n\n        Your action in this matter was most commendable.\n\n        We are returning your negative and photograph as\nrequested.\n\n                                Sincerely,\n\n                                SIGNED\n\n2 Incls. (W/Orig. Only)         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   1.  Photograph                Colonel, USAF\n   2.  Negative                  Chief, Topical Division\n                                Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n        x095. Reece, Mr. Narval W.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A         AFOIN-2A2\n\n\n[ILLEGIBLE signatures]\n\n                                    AFOIN Coordination Copy", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4dc78ab70668fbf2915b58862004bcecd37eedc6254504c200d4c656e222e324", "output_sha256": "51a0bc5f688061fe72639ccb5a7a3c8ec04825d3a73163b9e46bbd0d7eb0a45e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:06.724909+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p43", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 43, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nw/14 Nov 52\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          NOV 17 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN                Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\n\n     2.  Incls 2, 3, 4 and 5 were furnished by the Director of Special Investigations, this Headquarters.  The latter informs that no investigative action is contemplated in regard to Incl 2 and that their files contain no additional information on Incls 3 and 4.  Incl 5 is supplementary to the information on the Townsend Brown Foundation forwarded to you by DF dated 16 Oct 52.\n\n     3.  The movie film referred to in Incls 6 and 7 was duplicated by this office (4 copies).  One copy is attached for your files.  An attempt will be made to have it analyzed by the Navy in conjunction with their analysis of the movies taken 2 July 52 near Tremonton, Utah.\n\n     4.  Your attention is invited to the third paragraph of Incl 9; the original letter is attached as Incl 10.  Further action in this matter is left to your discretion.\n\n     5.  Incl 11 was received over the Associated Press wire on 17 Oct 52 and may be useful in evaluating reports from the area mentioned.\n\n                    X-322-7-ATIC\n\n11 Incls (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   1. Cy of rept of sighting in      Colonel, USAF\n      Chicago on 19 Oct 52           Chief, Topical Division\n   2. Photostat cy of ltr fr         Deputy Director for Estimates\n      Johnnie L. Last, Green Bay,    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n      Wis. dtd 24 Sep 52\n   3. Cy of ltr fr OSI, NY, NY dtd   When incl(s) No. 5\n      20 Oct 52                      is/are withdrawn (or not attached),\n   4. Cy of ltr fr Walter Wrobleski  the Confidential classification\n      Marshall, Tex dtd 13 Oct 52    of this correspondence will be de-\n   5. Photostat cy of Credit info re graded to Restricted in\n      Brown Townsend Foundation dtd 22 Aug 52 (in trip) accordance with Par 25e, AFR 205-1.\n   6. Cy of ltr to CO, 1701st Air Trans Wg, Gt Falls   COORDINATION: AFOIN-2A2\n      AFB, Mont dt 14 Nov 52\n   7. Cy of ltr to Mr. Mariana dtd 14 Nov 52\n   8. 16 mm movie film\n   9. Cy of ltr to Mr. Burgess, Black Mt, N.C.\n  10. Ltr fr Mr. Burgess, Black Mt, N.C. dtd 13 Oct 52\n  11. AP Press Releases\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A\n[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0d2f1cd1d4502c1a5d8610738771397a0a6148ee3ffe35831517089adc4e2f17", "output_sha256": "91467b1879d84bc85cdd006c750d390039c840e5e2720e0363e869598e05aba1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:10.169000+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p44", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 44, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\nAC/71379\n14 November 1952\n\n\n                                        NOV 1 4 1952\n\n\nMrs. C. R. Zepp\n6401 Medwick Drive\nHampshire Knolls\nHyattsville, Maryland\n\nDear Mrs. Zepp:\n\n     We have received your letter of 8 November 1952\nwith the record of observations attached.  We are very\ngrateful to you for making these available to us.\n\n     The records are being sent to our Air Technical\nIntelligence Center at Dayton, Ohio for careful study.\nShould they desire additional information from you,\nthey will correspond directly with you.\n\n     Once again we extend our sincere thanks for your\nassistance.\n\n                         Sincerely,\n\n                         SIGNED\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2A2\n\n\n[signatures]\n\n\n                                        OUT\n                                   6 17 NOV 1952\n                                    DIR/INT\n                                    HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d046be83e4613da9d587beadf4215b374043d232c3702d8e85c9b6b5021c883f", "output_sha256": "38e4b60a78b8fbd7d95f7d6cb72929a8abae4a890f5389d15694b6fc57f4600e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:12.066242+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p45", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 45, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\n          AC/71379\n       10 November 1953\n\n\n                              NOV 12 1952\n\n\nMr. E. C. Zimmerman\n145 S. Firestone Blvd.\nAkron 19, Ohio\n\nDear Mr. Zimmerman:\n\n     I have your letter of 30 October 1952 with its\n\nvery useful data.  It will be forwarded to our Air\n\nTechnical Intelligence Center for use in their analy-\n\nsis of the incident, and I know that they will be\n\nvery pleased to receive it.\n\n     We are most grateful for your splendid efforts\n\non our behalf.          x-095. Zimmerman\n\n                    Sincerely,        C. C. Mo\n\n\n                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Chief, Topical Division\n                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                    Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A     AFOIN-2A2\n\n[signatures]\n\n                                   G 14 NOV 1952\n                                      [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e681a24351a7464aed3aec22227bd3dab5dbdb74dfeb059a156da6157f4667a5", "output_sha256": "e681a24351a7464aed3aec22227bd3dab5dbdb74dfeb059a156da6157f4667a5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:13.412323+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p46", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 46, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\n          AC/71379\n       10 November 1952\n\n\n\n\n\n                                    NOV 1 2 1952\n\n\n\nMrs. Bluford Scott\n732 Eighth Court W.\nBirmingham, Alabama\n\nDear Mrs. Scott:\n\n     In answer to the request in your letter of 27 October 1952,\n\nwe enclose a questionnaire on unidentified flying objects.  When\n\nyou have completed it, place it in the attached envelope and\n\nmail it; no postage is required.\n\n     We appreciate the initiative which you have displayed in\n\nbringing this matter to our attention.\n\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              K- 095  Scott Bluford\n                                                    Mrs\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n2 Incls. (W/original only)\n  1.  Questionnaire\n  2.  Addressed Envelope\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:                                G 14 NOV 1952\n\nAFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2A2\n\n\n[signature]        [signature]\n                    sk", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a7e6447559185f9b3d7f306b34a9b87273655a5e1d1308f4deb1a72c0240dbf4", "output_sha256": "a7e6447559185f9b3d7f306b34a9b87273655a5e1d1308f4deb1a72c0240dbf4", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:14.944819+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p47", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 47, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\nAC/71379\n12 November 1952\n\n\nMr. Robert J. Gorman\nSuite 1468\nFirst National Bank Bldg.\n38 South Dearborn Street\nChicago 3, Illinois\n\nDear Mr. Gorman:\n\n     Your letter of 29 October 1952 to the President has been referred\nto the USAF since, within the Department of Defense, the USAF has\nprimary interest in investigation of \"flying saucer\" reports. It is\ngratifying to receive such expression of interest from public-minded\nindividuals. In your case, we are grateful for the opportunity to\ncorrect a misapprehension.\n\n     The USAF has not prepared any recent report arriving at any conclusions with respect to the existence or nonexistence of \"flying\nsaucers\". It is believed that Mr. Robert S. Allen, in his article\nof September 26, referred to a report prepared for public release by\na private group of civilians. In commenting on this, the USAF stated\nthat the report reflected the conclusions of individuals who were in\nno way connected with the Air Force. We take this opportunity to\nreiterate this to you.\n\n     It is true that the statements of Mr. DesVergers were startling;\nhowever, a thorough investigation of the incident has been conducted\nand it has been determined that the sensational aspects of the original stories carried by the national press agencies were exaggerated.\nFurther, the USAF made no attempt to restrict Mr. DesVergers' discussion or personal exploitation of the alleged incident; this he admitted\nin an Associated Press dispatch datelined West Palm Beach, Florida,\nAugust 27, 1952.\n\n     The Air Force is actively interested in the investigation of\n\"flying saucer\" incidents. No facts have been withheld from the\npublic. The investigators hope to reach some conclusions concerning\nthe existence and source of the objects. To date, sufficient evidence\nis not available to support any firm conclusions. I am confident that\nwhen scientific analysis of available evidence supports a conclusion,\nthe public will be duly informed.\n\n     It is sincerely hoped that these comments will allay your concern\non this subject. The manner in which you have sought an answer to\n\nx 095. Gorman, Mr. Robert", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "280a87ef48db356f9e3320b2c6a18ca431551afe5594ed075fe5914d940b6a9c", "output_sha256": "9dda9db7f405536611ef52383a29705ec28d1863cd4b4f701a9c0a1431c2f271", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:18.309368+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p48", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 48, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "your questions and the interest that you as a citizen have shown\nin this matter is appreciated. If we may be of any further service\nto you, please do not hesitate to write again.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A       AFOIN-2A2\n\n[signature]    [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9db48b9a25d7b6fb67eb570ead7c647a771e189c470848fea9f6baade015f182", "output_sha256": "243f871f939f50c0fe80a8453024463f7f171562da4b74bf0b345c19e889c7c6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:19.215435+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p49", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 49, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY                                    COPY\n\n\n                              October 29, 1952\n\n\nPresident Harry Truman\nWhite House\nWashington, D. C.\n\nDear Mr. President:\n\n        Permit me to take the liberty of writing you on\n\"flying saucers\".\n\n        It is becoming generally known that the Air Force\nhas a report concluding that flying saucers originate from\nsources outside this planet. Articles like that of Robert\nS. Allen, dated Sept. 26th are being photostated and circulated\nprivately. The statements of Mr. DesVergers of West Palm\nBeach, Florida, concerning his flying saucer experience and\nwhat he was told by the military and other incidents have\nconvinced many including myself that the \"saucers\" are real\nand interplanetary.\n\n        I think it is unfortunate that a matter which is\nof such great import must be investigated privately by citizens\nwho would like to and should be permitted to cooperate with\nand analyze with their government and military authorities.\nI think people who are afraid to tell the people of the\npossibilities of the flying saucers should bolster their\nfaith in the people of this country and democracy.\n\n        I hope you unveil the secrecy of the air force\nreport. I also hope you decide that this is not a matter of\nmilitary secrecy and that events concerning flying saucers\nbe made available to the public as they unfold.\n\n\n                         Very truly yours,\n\n\n\n                         Robert J. Gorman\n\nRJG:im\n\n\n\n                              COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3b210de2d2699b5d74401dff12783ea9765faefdc7f7e9c146cf1e5ef7f542b8", "output_sha256": "8f5554444dd68548c698eeaed6a1f16f7e7ee64bc7cc9d9575eb2110a07e5a85", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:20.930990+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p50", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 50, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWrtn 10 Nov 52\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          NOV 12 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN               Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures were received from the Director of Special Investigations, this\nHeadquarters and are for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  A fourth report, file 24-8-41 from OSI DO #17 dated 8 Oct 52 and regarding\nsighting at Tucson, Arizona on 2 Sep 52 by a USAF M/Sgt, was not forwarded since\nyou were indicated as the action addressee by the originator and should have re-\nceived a copy direct.\n\n\n3 Incls (w/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. AIIR, Form 112, dtd 9 Oct 52        Colonel, USAF\n  2. AIIR, Form 112, dtd 15 Oct 52       Chief, Topical Division\n  3. Ltr fr DO #2, dtd 16 Oct 52         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                          Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n                         4-322.7A710\n\n            When incl(s) No. _______________\n            is/are withdrawn (or not attached),\n            the __________ classification\n            of this communication will be down-\n            graded to _________________ in\n            accordance with Par 25e, AFR 205-1.\n\n          COUPON DESIGNATION LINE\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n     [signature]          [signature]\n\n                                              6 14 NOV 1952\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "484d5357fe805a1aaaf5a603a47ba17649802a50abb40147ba89ad5c4c1a21b0", "output_sha256": "74d9aede898f2e68b2c2380d4f71d59088a7cc5efec4643f9096d08db450a09b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:23.018964+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p51", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 51, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n          SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                    AFOIN-2A2\n                                                    Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\n                                                    Wrtn 13 Nov 52\n\n\n                        (Unclassified) Return of Project Blue Book Material\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          NOV 14 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN               Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  The file on the sighting at Austin, Texas on 8 June 52, previously borrowed\nfrom ATIAA-5, is returned herewith.\n\n     2.  The Photographic Division, AFCAG, made a set of color duplicates (enlarged)\nwhich is attached for your retention (Incl 3).  Black and white reproductions previously attached to the file are also included in Incl 3.  In addition, the\nPhotographic Division made a number of black and white enlargements which are\nattached for your retention (Incl 4).\n\n     3.  Based on further analysis, the Photographic Division and this office do not\nagree with the WADC evaluation of parhelions (\"sun dogs\") since the images do not\nappear at the required angle of 22° or 46° nor are they in line horizontally with\nthe sun as would be required for the formation of a parhelion (which would appear at\nthe intersection of the inner or outer halo circles - 22° and 46° respectively -\nwith the parhelic circle; the latter is in a horizontal plane coincidental with the\nposition of the sun).  Additionally, it will be noted in the photographs that the\nimages display a flat portion which appears inverted from the corresponding portion\nof the sun behind the cloud.  Since a parhelion is the result of refraction through\nice crystals, the resulting image would not be inverted.  Instead, it is our opinion\nthat the images are possibly a form of mirage caused by a hot air mass which\ntraveled from left to right across the field of view and acted as a lens.  However,\nthere is a small image in the third photograph of the sequence which, if evaluated\nas another image of the same type, would seemingly eliminate both parhelia and\nmirages from consideration.  This image is located directly above the seventh\ntelephone pole from the right at a vertical distance approximately equal to the\nheight of the pole.  The minute size of this image militates strongly against the\nmirage theory since the hot air mass would have had to turn about 90° and proceed\naway from the camera in order to produce this effect.  Therefore, further analysis\nappears to be justified.  Suggest the consultant astronomer be asked for an opinion.\n\n     4.  Recommend that the original photographs (Incl 2) be returned to the owner\nimmediately as requested in the report covering this incident.\n\n\n4 Incls (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. 8 Jun 52, Austin, Tex           Colonel, USAF\n     Sighting File Folder            Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Envelope containing 4 transparencies  Deputy Director for Estimates\n  3.   \"          \"     color duplicates   Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/I\n  4.   \"          \"     blk & white enlargements\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2             AFOIN-2A    No M/R necessary, self-explanatory.\n               [ILLEGIBLE]           [ILLEGIBLE]    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                    RESTRICTED\n                              SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f397a88521f93c8649e1a61bb15fa54eeb2cda79ca44fa1daa1f2eee6d0e9395", "output_sha256": "b9a710f22f3bfb06588a9345159784b5793cc7db011c983a20ffcd7770f3bde2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:26.310653+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p52", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 52, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Mr. Clyde E. Howard\n2544 3/4 Cudahy\nHuntington Park, California\n\n                                    10 NOV 1952\n\nDear\nMr. Howard:\n        Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n        We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n                                    Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-3A          AFOIN-3A2\n\n[signature]       [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d8aa8d9315890c4a82519de5a7e7004bf5c6b4bf25adabe0b6128dc556bd5516", "output_sha256": "849bb4be2a298982e088b78c83622555c6145050b1e2a5b57ac625662bcfe9aa", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:27.571485+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p53", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 53, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nMaj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\nAC/71379/6 November 1952\n\n(Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\n                                          NOV 7  1952\nChief, Air Technical      Dept. of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center       Headquarters USAF - AFOIN    Maj Fournet/AC/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosed letters are for your information, appropriate action and\nattention.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made by this office.\n\n     3.  Particular attention is invited to inclosure one.  If Ensign Frey is\nto be sent a questionnaire, this should be done as soon as possible since he\nadvises that he will depart from his present location about 25 November 1952.\n\n\n8 Incls. (W/original only)          WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fm Robert H. Frey           Colonel, USAF\n        dtd 27 Oct 52               Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fm Isabel A. Gold           Deputy Director for Estimates\n        dtd 6 Sep 52                Directorate of Intelligence\n  3. Ltr fm Miss Daisy McNeill\n        dtd 20 Oct 52\n  4. Ltr fm Miss Ida E. Valentine\n        dtd 14 Oct 52\n  5. Ltr fm Miss Ida E. Valentine\n        dtd 15 Oct 52\n  6. Ltr fm Robert Koehler\n        dtd 23 Oct 52\n  7. Ltr fm George M. Garrison\n        dtd 22 Oct 52\n  8. Ltr fm Arthur Halsted\n        dtd 17 Oct 52\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A     AFOIN-2A2\n\n[signatures]\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                           SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "af442d3a24e4a387b6a2a75feab202f4554a88bf10d716886db1fe9b161c29b0", "output_sha256": "83e83e40e0dbedf97fca7d30d98477641665b327119a0feecc0aae251779ec0a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:29.569277+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p54", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 54, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/AC/71379\n5 November 1952\n\n\n                                          NOV 7  1952\n\nMr. Walter B. Burgess\nBox 147\nBlack Mountain, North Carolina\n\nDear Mr. Burgess:\n\n     Because the Air Force has been designated the responsibility for the investigation and analysis of \"flying saucers\",\nthe Secretary of Defense referred your letter of 13 October 1952\nto us for consideration.\n\n     We find your proposal extremely edifying and desire to\ncommend you for your great patriotism.  Unfortunately, however,\nwe cannot accept your generous offer at this time since there\nis no provision which allows us to increase our current organization, and your services could not be utilized without some\nprovision of this nature.\n\n     Nonetheless, we are forwarding your letter to our Air Technical Intelligence center at Wright-Patterson Air Force Base,\nOhio, for future reference.  Should they find that your proposal\ncan be entertained in the future, they will contact you direct.\n\n     Your interest and cooperation are a source of great satisfaction to the Air Force, and we hope that future developments\nwill allow reconsideration of your offer to assist us.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n   AFOIN-2a              AFOIN-2A2\n\n   [signature]           [signature]\n                           [initials]\n\n                                         AFOIN-2A2 Coordination Copy", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "07375aab6d2e761730102e696efe33b93d4c64e4f2e849f2f214cd56f3ca2a96", "output_sha256": "7f2f8fb1cc0b8d9a9f050d8f76fe16eae832266b62b16bed0f15c938e71c2bff", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:31.467708+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p55", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 55, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWrtn 4 November 52\nRewrtn 5 November 1952\n\n\n                                    NOV 6  1952\n\n\nMr. Edmond L. LeRoy\n36 Fifth Street\nOld Bridge, New Jersey\n\nDear Mr. LeRoy:\n\n     General Samford sincerely appreciated your letter of\n30 July 1952 and has asked me to convey his thanks to you.\nWe apologize for the long delay in acknowledging its receipt,\nbut we have received such a large volume of correspondence\nfrom many citizens with similar patriotic motivation that we\nhave found it impossible to be as prompt as we would like.\n\n     With respect to your invitation to assist us further, we\nare very appreciative but regret that it will be impossible\nto contact you personally on this matter.\n\n     Thank you very much for your interest and efforts to\nassist us.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n          x095. Le Roy, Mr. Edmond L.\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2       AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                    ___________  ___________", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0f62a67e1ee4b2e07f6282e064557b006b9c4837b6b72f07e618d76473ff3d6b", "output_sha256": "0f62a67e1ee4b2e07f6282e064557b006b9c4837b6b72f07e618d76473ff3d6b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:33.112799+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p56", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 56, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWrtn 5 Nov 52\n\n                                             NOV 5  1952\n\n\n\n\nMrs. C. R. Zepp\n6401 Medwick Drive\nNorth Hampshire Knolls\nMaryland\n\nDear Mrs. Zepp:\n\n     We have a message which you left with our duty officer on\n26 October 1952 concerning strange lights which you have sighted\nover the past few months.  During your conversation you indicated\nthat you had a record of all such observations and would be\nwilling to submit it to a duly authorized individual.\n\n     We are interested in the record and would be very grateful\nif you would submit it to us by mail.  You may address it to:\nDirectorate of Intelligence, Headquarters USAF, Washington 25,\nD. C., ATTN:  AFOIN-2A2.\n\n     Your interest and cooperation are appreciated.\n\n                                   Sincerely,\n\n                              x095. Zepp, Mrs. C. R.\n\n1 Incl                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  self addressed           Colonel, USAF\n  envelope (franked)       Chief, Topical Division\n                           Deputy Director for Estimates\n                           Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2      AFOIN-2A\n\n\n Cal W H [signature]\n    [initials]\n\n                                        OUT\n                                     7 NOV 1952\n                                      DIPRINT\n                                      HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "87adaee7ef1e17608be9f9e0fd1926955d102beb76d4f751bea5b7a9b77184cd", "output_sha256": "87adaee7ef1e17608be9f9e0fd1926955d102beb76d4f751bea5b7a9b77184cd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:34.858308+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p57", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 57, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\n                                                    tmw/71379/6 Nov 52\n\n            RESTRICTED\n         SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n                        (Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept. of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Headquarters USAF - AFOIN     Maj Fournet/tmw/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\n\n     2.  Inclosures 1 and 2 were received from the Directorate of Operations,\nCS/O, this Headquarters.  They state that Mr. Myers' letter and the clipping\nwere referred to them by Congressman J. E. Van Zandt.  Acknowledgments have\nbeen made to Congressman Van Zandt and Mr. Myers.  Director of Legislation and\nLiaison, this Headquarters, has been furnished copies of entire file.\n\n     3.  Request receipt of inclosure 3 be acknowledged by indorsement direct\nto originator.\n\n     4.  Inclosures 4, 5, 6 and 7 were submitted by Miss Mary B. Hayden, an\nintelligence analyst assigned to Headquarters Air Resupply and Communication\nService, Washington, D.C.  A previous memorandum from Miss Hayden was forwarded\nby DF dated 5 June 52.  Acknowledgment has been made by personal contact with\nMiss Hayden.\n\n\n                                    5-322.7 47C\n\nIncls                               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n1.  Ltr fm C.W. Myers               Colonel, USAF\n       dtd 6 October 1952           Chief, Topical Division\n2.  Cy of Newspaper Clipping        Deputy Director for Estimates\n3.  Ltr fm Brooks AFB               Directorate of Intelligence\n       dtd 10 October 1952 (in quad)\n4.  Ltr fm M.B. Hayden\n       dtd 2 October 1952\n5.  Ltr fm M.B. Hayden\n       dtd 3 October 1952\n6.  Ltr fm M.B. Hayden\n       dtd 17 October 1952\n7.  Ltr fm M.B. Hayden\n       dtd 17 October 1952\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2A2\n\n                                        RESTRICTED\n[signatures]                         SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "278438015d3b5d4b401cb30b3cbab4f162b447f65972c02ebef9ca3f7d1dd154", "output_sha256": "6b83f2879de0b36f12ce011a36b085f2f1b7a6ca8a20b1ef4010f4b58d6dc6cf", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:37.459348+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p58", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 58, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Major Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\nAC/4B-864/27 Oct 52\n\n\n                                          30 OCT 1952\n\n\nMr. Gerald W. Harrington\nc/o Edwards and Angell\n15 Westminster Street\nProvidence 3, Rhode Island\n\nDear Mr. Harrington:\n\n     We have received your letter of 9 October 1952 in which\nyou reported the observation of an unidentified flying object.\nIt is presently in the hands of our intelligence analysts for\ntheir study.\n\n     Your action in reporting your observation in detail and\nin determining the ship's position at the time are a source\nof great satisfaction to us.  I would, therefore, like to\nexpress the appreciation of the Air Force for your initiative\nand efforts on our behalf.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n          x095. Harrington, Mr. Gerald W.\n\n                         C. M. YOUNG\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Policy & Management Group\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A     AFOIN-2X     AFOIN-[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n[signatures]  [signatures]  [signatures]  [signatures]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f9d460cc4550fd358e1ab626b1280c35249268c1028866dccb9c0cbf373d463f", "output_sha256": "f9d460cc4550fd358e1ab626b1280c35249268c1028866dccb9c0cbf373d463f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:38.919467+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p59", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 59, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A\nMajor Fournet/AC/71379\n27 October 1952\n\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To prepare a non-military letter to Mr. Gerald W. Harrington\nof Providence, Rhode Island.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  In a letter to the USAF dated 9 Oct 52 Mr. Harrington\ndescribes in detail an observation of an unidentified flying object\nmade aboard the SS Caronia on 5 Oct 52.  The data which he includes\nis somewhat remarkable in that it is very unusual to receive such\ndetails from the ordinary citizen.  He even took the trouble to\nwrite the ship's captain at a later date and obtain the ship's loca-\ntion at the time of the observation.\n\n     3.  A reply to Mr. Harrington is attached.\n\n     4.  Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion\nin the Daily Staff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n     5.  Because of Mr. Harrington's prominent professional position\nand the excellence of his report, it is strongly recommended that the\nattached reply be signed by General Samford.\n\n     6.  Approval, signature and dispatch of attached reply.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2 [signature]\n     AFOIN-2A  [signature]\n     AFOIN-2   [signature]\n     AFOIN", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bc11931097d6823dc9888037795c20f38d65eb17915a5158e2a44e1ee6c20628", "output_sha256": "bc11931097d6823dc9888037795c20f38d65eb17915a5158e2a44e1ee6c20628", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:40.569410+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p60", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 60, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n      RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST                    CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:                         DATE\n                              TYPE\nSUMMARY:                                                              SUSPENSE\n                                                          DATE\n                                                          ASGD BY\n                                                          NO\n                                                          DATE RECD\n                              SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:    AFOIN-2X                                           DATE    27 Oct 52\nFROM:  AFOIN-2A                                          NO.     1\nREM[REDACTED]:\n\n     The attached correspondence is forwarded for coordination and transmittal\n     to OIN for signature and dispatch.\n\n                                        [signature]\n                                        AFOIN-2A\n                                                          AFOIN No.\n                                                           .562\n\nTO:   OIN X                                              29 Oct 52\nFROM: OIN 2X                                             2\n\nIN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE       OUT    IN    OFFICE      OUT\n  /   AFOIN                 AFOIN-2  T.V.        ASST\nX     AFOIN-X              AFOIN-2A  W141        EXEC\n\n      ADMYN                                             ASST\n      M&R                  AFOIN2B                      EXEC       S\n\n      AFOIN-1                                           EXEC.      x [signature]\n                           AFOIN-3\n                                                        AIR/INT\n                                    X  ACTION           COORDINATION\nAction Asgd to:       DATE:            Dispatch\nSigned:               DATE:            File:  /met     Date: 30 Oct 52\n\nAFHQ Form 0-86 Previous Editions of the Form are Obsolete                51 25247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "61ff31b75d3251d24ede9390de44755fd24d7b805a009869b8138ddef3b9f9ab", "output_sha256": "61ff31b75d3251d24ede9390de44755fd24d7b805a009869b8138ddef3b9f9ab", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:42.545259+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p61", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 61, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Major Fournet/AFOIN-2A2\nAC/4B-864/27 Oct 52\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n(Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nATIC          Dept of the Air Force\n              Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2          Major Fournet/71379\n\n1.  Inclosed letter is for your information and retention.\n\n2.  A reply to Mr. Harrington was made by this office.\n\n\n1 Incl (With Original Only)          WELDON H. SMITH\n  Original copy of letter             Colonel, USAF\n  from Mr. Harrington                 Actg, Chief, Topical Division\n                                      Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                      Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n                    x-095. Harrington, Mr.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A\n\n[signature]   [signature]\n\n                         OUT\n                      29 OCT 1952\n                       DIR/INTI\n                       HQ USAF\n\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "82138b624417805cf94c9042f617635fef96ef830958f1ce1b25ccc7ad50f3be", "output_sha256": "82138b624417805cf94c9042f617635fef96ef830958f1ce1b25ccc7ad50f3be", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:44.218088+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p62", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 62, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force        OCT 27 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hqs USAF - AFOIN         Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Reference our DF dated 11 Sep 52, subject: \"Investigation of Incident\nof 1/2 Sep 52 Arlington Va., having possible relation to Project Blue Book\",\nthe inclosed report was received from OSI and is for your information and reten-\ntion.\n\n     2.  It will be noted that the report explains this incident completely.\n\n\n1 Incl: w/orig only                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Rpt fr OSI                           Colonel, USAF\n  dtd 6 Oct 52                         Chief, Topical Intelligence Division\n                                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\n          When incl(s) No. ____1____________________\n          is/are ________________________ in\n          the __ Confidential ____________\n          of this ________________________ in\n          graded to _Restricted____________ in\n          accordance with Par 23c, AFR 205-1.\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "75c9a849774f20fb96108fde843bd3f297066712469dcea4a534f3b5fda63c6e", "output_sha256": "c452f093cc2746806d09feb18c94de6d5cba2ca187754ee661be5ef0c09d62ab", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:45.965591+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p63", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 63, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWatn 22 Oct 52\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force    OCT 23 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hqs USAF-AFOIN  CONFIDENTIAL  Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio                                        SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n     1.  Inclosed report was furnished by OSI and is for your information\nand retention.\n\n     2.  The inconsistencies between the visual description reported by the\nobserver and the attached photograph are obvious, viz. the time reported as\n1000 hours while the photograph was evidently taken at night; the reported\nshape and relative size as compared with the image in the photograph, etc.\n\n     3.  The Photographic Division of AFCAG has evaluated the \"object\" as a\nlight fixture superimposed on the background through double-exposure.\n\n\n1. Incl: (1s dm.)  w/orig. only          WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   Photo cy Spot Intel Rpt                Colonel, USAF\n   dtd 3 Oct 52 w/attchd photo            Chief, Topical Division\n                                          Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                          Directo