db8087398f", "input_sha256": "934957c4b18d3bf3aa31680aaf22e73feb60eac8d3a701af746181cef1e090b0", "output_sha256": "6a335e8e7cfcdcc9037c178d9918d1aae3b76c645d87f514fece048a2a0d5012", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:07:49.415967+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p65", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 65, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A/Col Adams/fh/74072\n                    wrtn 23 Oct 52\n\n\n\n\n\n                    23 October 1952\n\nMr. Leon Davidson\n804 South Irving Street\nArlington 4, Virginia\n\nDear Mr. Davidson:\n\n     The Air Force Press Desk, Office of Public Information,\nDepartment of Defense, has advised my office of your continued\ninterest in reports of unusual observations of aerial objects.\nYour previous correspondence concerning this matter has been\nreviewed and we believe that your requests for additional\ninformation cannot be adequately treated by correspondence.\n\n     May I advise you that we are aware of the responsible\nposition you hold and of the security clearance that has\nbeen granted you in your present capacity.\n\n     We would appreciate an opportunity to discuss your views\nconcerning possible sources of these objects with you on a\npersonal basis. Of course the matter will be treated in complete\nconfidence. Unfortunately the officer most cognizant of our\ninvestigations in this field will be out of town until after 1\nNovember. If you will contact my office, Liberty 5-6700,\nextension 74072, on or after 3 November we will be happy to\narrange a meeting with you at sometime mutually convenient.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n               SIGNED\n               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n               Colonel, USAF\n               Chief, Topical Division\n               Deputy Director for Estimates\n               Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n               X-095 Davidson, Leon\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A\n\n[ILLEGIBLE signatu