s\nto you for your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects.\n\n        Your interest and efforts to assist us are appreciated.\n\n                        Sincerely,\n\n                        SIGNED\n\n                        WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Chief, Topical Division\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2        AFOIN-2A\n\n  x095. Harrold, Mr. I.D.\n                Col W A [Smith]        [R.H. Bake] Capt\n\n                        [initials]\n\nAFOIN COORDINATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3d81fd7d2e6961ea8ebcc4475e9d5fac1cba661223f840c8c2f27f2f9ea868fa", "output_sha256": "7726a426b772a2bed80c975bd63e46e08899f39c96bc960b8200e484a4af77ea", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:06.068196+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p76", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 76, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN 2A2\n                                        Wrtn 21 October 1952\n                                        Maj Fournet/tmw\n                                        Ext 71379\n\n                              OCT 2 8 1952\n\nMr. Edmond L. LeRoy\n36 Fifth Street\nOld Bridge, New York\n\nDear Mr. LeRoy:\n\n     General Samford sincerely appreciated your letter\nof 30 July 1952 and has asked me to convey his thanks\nto you.  We apologize for the long delay in acknowledging its receipt, but we have received such a large\nvolume of correspondence from many citizens with\nsimilar patriotic motivation that we have found it\nimpossible to be as prompt as we would like.\n\n     With regard to your invitation to assist us, we\nare very sorry that we cannot contact you personally\nbecause the situation makes this impossible.  However,\nwe would welcome another letter from you giving your\nideas in detail, and we assure you that they will be\nconsidered very carefully.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              SIGNED\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nNo M/R                   2A2                    2A\n\n                    [signatures]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fe0e560ddd195e870d7afccc681e1fa09333ad68813566d19321622a5fbccbe7", "output_sha256": "c3070cebbd9fc6227b833665737f992e487f6e3ccb5fc16b5b8f1bc6c6b0b381", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:07.661722+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p77", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 77, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 21 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 2 2 1952\n\nMr. E. C. Henthorn\nSuperintendent of Schools\nSarpy County\nPapillion, Nebraska\n\nDear Mr. Henthorn:\n\n     Your letter of 25 July 1952 was referred to us since the\nAir Force is responsible for the \"flying saucer\" investigation.\nWe apologize for the long delay in acknowledging its receipt,\nbut we have received such a large volume of letters from many\ncitizens with similar patriotic motivation that we have found\nit impossible to be as prompt as we would like.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist us and\nassure you that the ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n\n                         Sincerely,\n\n               SIGNED\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2                    AFOIN-2A\n\n              [signature]                    [signature]\n                   [initials]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a6fd3dfb1e0fb201877a119d277b2663cf5dda42d85cec0411ef1a506969b3db", "output_sha256": "a6fd3dfb1e0fb201877a119d277b2663cf5dda42d85cec0411ef1a506969b3db", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:09.140774+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p78", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 78, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\n                                        Wrtn 21 Oct 52\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hqs USAF - AFOIN    Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB                    SECURITY INFORMATION\nOhio                                    [REDACTED]          OCT 2 2 1952\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made by this office. However, Mr.\nFlorsheim was notified by the FBI that his letter was being referred to the USAF.\n\n\n                                        SIGNED\n6 Incls:  (W/orig. only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mrs J. Albers              Colonel, USAF\n       dtd 29 Jul 52                   Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Mr Willy R.P. Brand        Deputy Director for Estimates\n       dtd 8 Jul 52                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Mrs L.S. Black\n       dtd 7 Aug 52 (w/attch.)\n  4. Ltr fr Mr A.B. Florsheim          COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n       dtd 23 Sept 52\n  5. Ltr fr Mr E.B. Allison\n       dtd about 2 Oct 52 w/photo      COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n  6. Ltr fr Mr C.E. Page\n       dtd 3 Oct 52\n\n            √ NO M/R\n\n              X322.7AT1C\n\n        COORDINATION:         AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                         Col W.H. [ILLEGIBLE]         [ILLEGIBLE] Capt.\n\n\n                                              OUT\n                                          6 22 OCT 1952\n                                            DIR/INT\n                                            HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d8a4612de599e8a9daea24d10319bf7ae479ba7daf939b7a6fd5a3161f16ee90", "output_sha256": "d8a4612de599e8a9daea24d10319bf7ae479ba7daf939b7a6fd5a3161f16ee90", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:11.336384+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p79", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 79, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 16 Oct 52\n\n                                        OCT 17 1952\n\nMr. E. L. Lull\nNew Ute Hotel\nSalt Lake City, Utah\n\nDear Mr. Lull:\n\n        We appreciated your letters of 22 and 23 September\n1952 with your additional comments regarding the date in\nquestion.\n\n        Your continued interest and efforts to assist us are\ngreatly appreciated.\n                    COUPON DESIGNATION MADE -----------\n\n                        Sincerely,\n\n                           SIGNED\n\n                        WILLIAM AD ADAMS\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Chief, Topical Division\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n√x095. Lull, E.L.\n\nCOORDINATION:           AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                    Col W. H. Smith         Col Ada\n                        [signature]         [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "860ee531cc6cc555e65f7c804e14b9bdf7442c18ea019750983cb70392c5cd2c", "output_sha256": "860ee531cc6cc555e65f7c804e14b9bdf7442c18ea019750983cb70392c5cd2c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:12.622701+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p80", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 80, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 17 Oct 52\n\nOCT 17 1952\n\n\nMrs. Jessie Bunting\n1520 Phillips Avenue\nGreensboro, North Carolina\n\nDear Mrs. Bunting:\n\nYour recent letter concerning unidentified flying objects has been received by this Headquarters, and the ideas which you submitted are receiving our careful consideration.\n\nWe appreciate your interest and efforts to assist us.\n\nSincerely,\n\n\nWILLIAM A. ADAMS\nColonel, USAF\nChief, Topical Division\nDeputy Director for Estimates\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                [signature]            [signature]\n                    5J", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "705d97d6e782e9dd399d6873050f4964bbc3667e6ca7e04daf7d4badc748bb74", "output_sha256": "d31ef282fe2bf86b2144a7eac268f2a4912c21966c41f6015f2f0d0e12a78681", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:13.774400+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p81", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 81, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 17 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                          OCT 17 1952\n\nMr. Robert Garrison\nBox 48\nBig Stone Gap, Virginia\n\n     Dear Mr. Garrison:\n\n          Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n\n          We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n          [signatures]\n\n000.9 Flying Discs AFOIN-2 COORDINATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f9e8529f5e65bca6adbde2f9ae667c4de24ecbac3f0b764665b08a7b2cb21598", "output_sha256": "ba3a097dfeb2d805216b2eaf282e3923deb71bbe82a4f0f24f309bacb768efb7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:15.082806+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p82", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 82, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 16 Oct 52\n\n(Unclassified) Correspondence from Mr. Anthony Guidry\n\nExecutive,\nDirector of Research & Development, DCS/D\nAttn: Major Foreman\nDeputy Direc. for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O\n\n                                                    OCT 17 1952\n\n     1.  Inclosure is forwarded as a matter of primary interest.\n\n     2.  Other letters from Mr. Guidry dated 3 and 4 October 52\nwere retained since they concerned an alleged sighting of and a\ntheory on \"flying saucers\".\n\n\n                         SIGNED\n\n1 Incl:  (w/orig. only)          WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Ltr fr Mr. Guidry              Colonel, USAF\n  dtd 4 Oct 52                   Chief, Topical Division\n                                 Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                 Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n               NO M/R\n\n\n                                        G 21 OCT 1952\n                                        DIRINT\n                                        HQ USAF\n\nCOORDINATION:       AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n         Col W [Illegible]          RBH for Col Oden\n\n              [Illegible]\n         /x895. Guidry, Mr. Anthony", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "82e7cdffd979cb62c20351a7e2b554cc6c0fb9b80f8a19c07823d0bc327032f0", "output_sha256": "1a444ec71c607bc436f8ddec31f231486ebcbbfcc938b57b4db4478dad4eb933", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:16.708182+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p83", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 83, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 15 Oct 52\nSECRET\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nRESTRICTED\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 1 6 1952\nIntelligence Center          Hqs USAF - AFOIN\nWright-Patterson AFB                                    Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosed report is for your information and retention.  Request acknowledgment of receipt by indorsement to originator.\n\n     2.  The many questionable aspects of the report and the circumstances surrounding it appear to leave little doubt that this was a hoax.\n\n\n\n1 Incl:  (w/orig. only)          SIGNED\n  FlyOb rpt fr ADC               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  dtd 3 Oct 52 (w/3 attachs)     Colonel, USAF\n                                  Chief, Topical Division\n                                  Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                  Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n                    COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ________\n\n                         x3227971C\n\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2                    AFOIN-2A\n\n                   [signature]                    [signature]\n                       Df\n\n\nWhen incl(s) no.  Secret\nis/are             (or not attached),\nthe                [ILLEGIBLE]\nco\nand                Restricted\nAccordance with Par 235, AFR 205-1.\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n                    SECRET\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        OUT\n                                   22 OCT 1952\n                                    DIR/INT\n                                    HQ USAF\n                                     4765", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d0ff6acdb62a1776f4f74acf18282482df7b32654832d2dfc233a2761852857e", "output_sha256": "62ad61cd0340e57b8d99f1ac5575b71845167640acf378e2d70f0b3dbf750f87", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:18.726265+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p84", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 84, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\n                    Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\n                    wrtn 16 Oct 52\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n              (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hqs USAF - AFOIN           Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\nNo replies of any kind have been made by this office.\n\n     2.  A copy of the translation of Mr. Goy's letter (see Incl. 4) was fur-\nnished AFDRD for their information.\n\n\n                              SIGNED\n\n4 Incls: (w/orig. only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mr. D.L. Pefine                Colonel, USAF\n       dtd 23 Sep 52                       Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Card fr C. S. Stultz                  Deputy Director for Estimates\n       dtd 24 Aug 52                       Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Mr. H.L. Peterson\n       dtd 28 Sep 52\n  4. Ltr fr Mr. R. Goy (transla.)\n       dtd 15 Sep 52 (w/attach in dup)\n\n\n                                                    OUT\n                                               G 17 OCT 1952\n                                                 DIRINT\n                                                HQ USAF\nNO M/R               COORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2    AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                              Col WH[ILLEGIBLE]    [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                    bf\n\n\n\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d82d5385b81393c39016ff9634544d2b29518491bac3220c1c026ff93e5b7882", "output_sha256": "d82d5385b81393c39016ff9634544d2b29518491bac3220c1c026ff93e5b7882", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:20.795797+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p85", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 85, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\n                                        Wrtn 16 Oct 52\n\n                                        RESTRICTED\n                                        SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force      OCT 16 1952\nIntelligence Center         Hqs USAF - AFOIN           Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information and retention.  They were supplied\nby the office of Naval Research to OSI.\n\n     2.  OSI states that the Townsend Brown Foundation was brought to their\nattention by Major General V. E. Bertrandias following a visit to the Foundation.\nDuring this visit General Bertrandias saw a model of a \"flying saucer\" and en-\ngaged in conversation with Townsend Brown and other scientists who disclosed\nthat they had been working on the project for 20 to 25 years.\n\n     3.  OSI checked local and national agencies with negative results.  Their\nfiles contain no further pertinent data.\n\n\n\n2 Incls: (w/orig. only)              SIGNED\n 1. Rpt of Off of Nav Research       WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n 2. Dun & Bradstreet credit Rating   Colonel, USAF\n                                     Chief, Topical Division\n                                     Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                     Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n                                              A\n                                           OCT\n          NO M/R                         G 17 OCT 1952\n                                           DIR/INT\n                                           HQ USAF\n\n\n     COORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n          Ore W H Smith          DH Belo Apt.\n\n                  5f\n\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                              SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5f19b328f39065f460f036aa5e1fe090ba713c2924732113c4b559099b34bb40", "output_sha256": "5f19b328f39065f460f036aa5e1fe090ba713c2924732113c4b559099b34bb40", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:22.882088+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p86", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 86, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 15 Oct 52\n\n                                    OCT 16 1952\n\n                        VIA AIR MAIL\n\n\nMr. Nicholas Mariana\n3235 Fifth Avenue South\nGreat Falls, Montana\n\nDear Mr. Mariana:\n\n     You are probably aware of the fact that the Air Force\nis still continuing the investigation and analysis of \"flying\nsaucers\". We are presently attempting to make a comparative\nanalysis of recent sightings against those made in previous\nyears. In this connection, the report of a sighting made by\nyou on 15 August 1950 has aroused our interest. Unfortunately,\nhowever, our duplicate copy of the movies which you took of\nthese objects has been inadvertently misplaced.\n\n     Therefore, we would be most grateful if you would\npermit us to borrow your original movies for study and dupli-\ncation. In so doing you would be rendering us a great\nservice.\n\n     We will have an officer from Great Falls Air Force\nBase contact you about 22 October and, should you consider\nour request favorably, he will obtain the movies and give\nyou a receipt for them. We will then return them as soon\nas possible thereafter.\n\n     Your cooperation and consideration in this matter is\nearnestly solicited!\n\n                                    Sincerely,\n         x-045. Mariana Nicholas\n                    SIGNED\n                                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\nCC: ATIC                            Colonel, USAF\n                                    Chief, Topical Division\n                                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n          COORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n                          Col A. H. Smith          [signature]\n                               58", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a2e12be2c6009e9f743a3ea056402d0f5170bd09b5939a9f6c986a283558a372", "output_sha256": "7bd4d782ad02c800b91bb5a3704463462145a689943c4807fbfc15720bd6992d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:24.788813+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p87", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 87, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SECRET\n                    AFOIN-2A4/Capt Hosford/pal/74735\nSECURITY INFORMATION    W/14 Oct 52\n                                    SECRET\nRESTRICTED                          Auth CS, USAF\n\n\n\n\n               (Restricted) Return of File on Flyobrpt\n\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force      OCT 14 1952\nIntelligence Center         Hqs USAF - AFOIN-2A4    Capt Hosford/pal/74735\nWright-Patterson AFB\nDayton, Ohio\nAttn:  Capt E. J. Ruppelt\n\n        Inclosed is complete file on Flyobrpt classified SECRET which was borrowed\nfrom your office by AFOIN-2A4.\n\n\n\n6 Incls                             WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. General, G F                   Colonel, USAF\n  2. 17 Dec 48 OSI Rpt              Chief, Topical Intelligence Division\n  3. Mscl. Fireball                 Deputy Director for Estimates\n  4. 13 Dec 48 OSI rpt              Directorate of Intelligence\n  5. Hoax\n  6. Briefing\n\n\n\n\n                            X-322.7  ATIC\n\n\n\n\nWhen inclosures No. 1-6 -- (hrs) with-\ndrawn [ILLEGIBLE] and classification\nof  Secret  on this correspondence\nwill be canceled or changed to Restricted\nin accordance with par 9b., AR 380-5.\n\n                                    RESTRICTED\n\n\n                                    SECRET\n[signature]                         SECURITY INFORMATION\nAFOIN-2A4                           AFOIN-2A\nCapt Hosford", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2140757c4e90585ebf8ad99a518ea591c704e3974d204e74473779c5acc3f434", "output_sha256": "f483eb8141c403ec8526b936c1cfa9ef18471513c70a3653b7d9c4c0f33ad3b6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:26.732725+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p88", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 88, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                              AFOIN-2A2\n                                              Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\n                                              Wrtn 13 Oct 52\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 14 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN           Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB                                         Page 2\nOhio\n\n      8.  No replies of any kind have been made to Inclosures 8, 9 and 14.\n\n\n                                    SIGNED\n\n14 Incls:  (W/Orig only)              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Questionnaire fr Mr. Hazelwood   Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 22 Sep 52                    Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Questionnaire fr Mrs. Hazelwood  Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 22 Sep 52                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Questionnaire fr Mr. Dunn\n     dtd 22 Sep 52\n  4. Questionnaire fr Mr. J. Wahl\n     dtd 22 Sep 52\n  5. Questionnaire fr Mr. R.E. Lloyd\n     dtd 22 Sep 52\n  6. Questionnaire fr Mr. J.W. Burke\n     dtd 22 Sep 52\n  7. Questionnaire fr Mr. M.H. Herrall\n     dtd 22 Sep 52\n  8. rpt re flyobs fr ONI dtd\n     16 Sep 52\n  9. Ltr fr Mrs. U. Schacht\n     dtd 11 Sep 52\n 10. Art. fr Fla. newspaper\n     dtd 10 Sep 52 about\n 11. Art. fr Evening Star paper\n     dtd 27 Sep 52\n 12. Questionnaire fr Mr. D.S. Young\n     dtd 27 Sep 52\n 13. Questionnaire fr Mr. D.S. Young\n     dtd late Aug 52\n 14. Photostat ltr fr Mr. C.P. Olivier\n     thru OSI dtd 26 Aug 52\n\n\nNO M/R              COORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                    [signatures]\n\n\n                                    RESTRICTED\n                                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ce3ac9a241d58673988bc1727140179e88dd9deba22b77d082a095ee69763eeb", "output_sha256": "ce3ac9a241d58673988bc1727140179e88dd9deba22b77d082a095ee69763eeb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:29.249901+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p89", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 89, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                        (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical    Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center     Hq USAF - AFOIN          Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  Inclosures 1 through 7 pertain to the same incident as previously\nreported by TWX AFOIN 53311 dated 22 Sep 52.  Four of the witnesses were\ninterviewed in person and a fifth by telephone.  Pertinent comments are in-\ncluded in the questionnaires.\n\n     3.  Inclosures 8 and 9 were received from ONI.\n\n     4.  The article from a Florida newspaper (Incl. 10) was furnished by OSD-OPI.\n\n     5.  The article from the Evening Star (Incl. 11) may be of some assistance\nin evaluating the sighting in the vicinity of Washington about 2000 EDT on 12 Sep 52.\n\n     6.  Inclosure 12 and 13 are from the same source but pertain to different\nsightings.  He has recently advised that he has made two additional observations.\n\n     7.  The letter from Mr. Charles P. Olivier (Incl. 14) was received from OSI.\nHis offer of assistance appears to warrant investigation.\n\n\n                                        OUT\n                                    G 15 OCT 1952\n                                      DIR/INT\n                                      HQ USAF\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fa87687cdcd9b0be75161f33409b901a79d3954205a332ca6cfa0b2d6869778a", "output_sha256": "fa87687cdcd9b0be75161f33409b901a79d3954205a332ca6cfa0b2d6869778a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:31.078153+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p90", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 90, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\n10 Oct 52\n\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified)  Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN          Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosed documents are for your information, appropriate action and\nretention.\n\n     2.  A reply to Mr. Varela (see Incl. 1) was prepared by this office; a copy\nis attached as Incl. 2.  It will be noted that he was requested to forward direct\nto you any data which his group may obtain rather than to this Headquarters as\nindicated in his letter.  Suggest that a few copies of the questionnaire be furnished\nhim for the guidance of his group in collecting information.  If the group consists\nof competent engineers or other technically trained personnel, they may be well\nworth cultivating.\n\n     3.  Suggest you acknowledge the report of LCDR Nelson (see Incl. 3) which,\nalthough a bit old, may prove useful since it concerns a sighting through a\ntelescope.\n\n     4.  No further action is required on Inclosure 4, since this office collaborated with OSD-OPI in the preparation of a reply for signature in the Office of\nthe Chief of Staff.\n\n              x328.7 ATIC\n                          S\n4 Incls: (W/orig. only)              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mr. Varela dtd 28 Aug 52  Colonel, USAF\n  2. Ltr to Mr. Varela dtd 10 Sep 52  Chief, Topical Division\n  3. Memo fr LCDR Nelson w/attach     Deputy Director for Estimates\n  4. Ltr fr Mr. Berridge dtd 30 Jul 52  Directorate of Intelligence\n\n                                          OUT\n                                       6 13 OCT1952\n                                        CARFINT\n                                        HQ USAF\n\nNO M/R\n          COORDINATION:   AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2[ILLEGIBLE]\n\n         Col W O'Neill                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n              [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                          SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "268ba6aae740bf15d613decf1f173cdbff87bd3e7288a6b334849b1ce20af54c", "output_sha256": "2dd31477752eb941e36833bd24787ad2ea5387fb3589f2d50e848ffe1b0b6eab", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:33.539996+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p91", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 91, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71379\nWrtn 13 Oct 52\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Correspondence Re Project Blue\n                    Book from Ralph H. Ballock of Puyallup, Washington\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN\nWright-Patterson AFB                            OCT 13 1952\nOhio                                    Maj Fournet/cmb/71379\n\n     1.  Inclosed letter from Mr. Ballock is forwarded for appropriate action\nsince previous correspondence was also forwarded to you.  Copies of the latter\nwere not retained by this office, therefore precluding the possibility of fur-\nnishing a comprehensive answer to his latest request.\n\n\n                    x302.7 ATIC\n\n1 Incl:  (W/orig. only)              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   Ltr fr Mr. Ballock                Colonel, USAF\n   dtd 19 Sept 52                    Chief, Topical Division\n                                     Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                     Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\nNO M/R      COORDINATION:      AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n             Col W. H. [signature]        D M [signature]\n                    [initials]\n\n\n        COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\n\n                                    OUT\n                               G 18 OCT 1952\n                                 DAFINT\n                                HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7cec8ed904a4d338a034f21eef750e70552cc6292fb94ac6efa1afba4ade27d8", "output_sha256": "7cec8ed904a4d338a034f21eef750e70552cc6292fb94ac6efa1afba4ade27d8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:35.262206+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p92", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 92, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "HEADQUARTERS\n6580TH MISSILE TEST WING\nHolloman Air Force Base, New Mexico\n\nMTHPI                                    10 October 1952\n\nSUBJECT:  Transmittal of Air Intelligence Information Report\n\n\nTO:       Director of Intelligence\n          Headquarters, USAF\n          Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\n     In compliance with Air Force Letter 200-5, Unidentified Flying\nObjects Reporting, dated 29 April 1952, the following Air Intelligence\nInformation Report is submitted for your information.\n\n     FOR THE COMMANDING OFFICER:\n\n\n\n1 Incl:                    WILLIAM F. HARRIS\n  Air Intel Info Rpt (3 cys)   Lt. Col., USAF\n                           Deputy for Personnel\n\n——————————————\n\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "16ead70f276dfab1c55fea9cbd1f5f68f58d7f5b03bc9393efaed730c82b2467", "output_sha256": "c5fb0c793f62010bc29c6cd1fb7133ea220aebdfdb40c2d7b6df143b5389565f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:36.418179+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p93", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 93, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n1B\n\n68DOI 319                    10 OCT 1952      //\n\nSUBJECT:  FLY OB RPT\n\n\nTO:      Commanding General\n         Second Air Force\n         Barksdale Air Force Base, Louisiana\n         Attn:  Director of Intelligence\n\n\n     1.  Herewith, in accordance with par 7e (2), Air Force Letter\n200-5, dated 29 April 1952 is original AF Form 112, plus five (5)\nozalid copies reproduced therefrom, together with inclosures.\n\n     2.  This observation was made by members of the 68th\nBombardment Wing (M) presently stationed at this Base.\n\n               FOR THE COMMANDING OFFICER:\n\n\n\n1 Incl                              MICHAEL M DUBELKO\n  AF Form 112                       Major, USAF\n    (in sextup)                     Adjutant General\n\n        NOTA\n        No action\n           man\n\n                         COUPON DESIGNATION MADE --------", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "368240bd75c67270cabbd05ba3f1f3ffb2a5e037af5ea9d5b35d68089e0a3135", "output_sha256": "9664a746701177b1041fbf9b415dd9720cf59568bce73f117caeaf54356d2cf2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:37.831716+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p94", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 94, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COMBAT DESIGNATION FILE\n\nAdjutant General\n(IN ANSWER)                    Major, AC\nVA ADJ 333                     RICHARD W. DOCKIKO\n3 INCL\n\nSUBJECT: COMBAT INFORMATION\n\n1. (a) Established herein are(?) the(?) procedures\n   in this application for each of members of the USAF.\n\n(b) The following information concerning the procedures\nfor(?) a copy of this(?) application for assignment to\nthe(?) position at if the(?) classification in Training.\n\n        Chief, Records Division(?) USAF\n        Headquarters 7AF JAPAN(?)\n        Office Air Force\nFor    ADJUTANT GENERAL\n\nREFERRED: APPROVED:\n\nGROUP 3/4                    10 OCT 1952\n\n18\n\nCONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\nCONFIDENTIAL ABSOLUTELY\n\nDECLASSIFIED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ce21bb859ecf0508dc63f1291150ddd3b3ca79cef7c34ec7cd43f1a3fbbff509", "output_sha256": "0d6fe8af7daf126b88e5533437655fed39e91fec37ec897b6fc3a5e353c46946", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:38.971511+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p95", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 95, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 19 Sept 1952\n\n                                              OCT 10 1952\n\nMr. Joseph M. Varela\n17832 Fullerfarm Street\nNorthridge, California\n\nDear Mr. Varela:\n\n     We acknowledge, with sincere thanks, the kind offers made\non behalf of your group in your letter of 28 August 1952.  It\nis indeed gratifying to see the cooperation extended the Air\nForce by organizations such as yours in our attempt to evolve\na final solution to the unidentified flying objects problem.\n\n     Since the Air Technical Intelligence Center at Wright-\nPatterson Air Force Base, Ohio is the activity which is respon-\nsible for the investigation and analysis of these reports, we\nare forwarding your letter to them.  For the same reason, we\nwould like to suggest that you forward all data and findings\ndirectly to them rather than to this Headquarters.  In this\nmanner, the information which you supply will be incorporated\ninto the program much more quickly.\n\n     You will probably hear from the Center in the near future.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNo M/R necessary.             X-095, Varela, Joseph M.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2      AFOIN-2A\n\n     Col W H [signature]      [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "199181c59817a63ba9e1214a27c3c8f02cd2ad6bdd5364c9e7508fb829f1203b", "output_sha256": "199181c59817a63ba9e1214a27c3c8f02cd2ad6bdd5364c9e7508fb829f1203b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:40.718678+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p96", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 96, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\n                                        Wrtn 9 Oct 52\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN                    Maj Fournet/dbv/71379\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosed are reproductions of three color transparencies taken by\nMr. Wallace Litwin, an American press photographer, in the vicinity of the Naval\nformation participating in Operation Mainbrace on 20 Sep 52.  The attached copy of\na letter from Mr. F. Richard Anderson of the Metropolitan Sunday Newspapers, Inc.\ndated 2 Oct 52 (see Incl 2) includes all data on this sighting presently available\nthis office.\n\n     2.  The original photographs were returned to Mr. Anderson with a letter ex-\npressing our sincere thanks for his cooperation in making the photographs available\nto us.  The photographs were enlarged by Hq USAF from the original 2½ x 2½ inch\nsize to the present size; the vertical dimension of the copies correspond to the\ncoverage in the original photographs (enlargement ratio 2.25:5).  These are the\nonly copies which were made; none are filed in Headquarters.  An enlarged reversal\nprint of the second transparency is attached (Incl 3); it was made to show that the\nimage is still round.    Photographs are for official use only; not for release.\n\n     3.  A cable to CINCNORTH, with information copy to you, was dispatched 3 Oct\n52 requesting information on balloon releases by ships in the Naval formation.\nMessage number is AFOIN 59530.\n\n     4.  A copy of OPNAV Notice 3820 is attached as Incl 4 for your information and\nretention.\n                    X322.1ATIC\n\n\n4 Incls (w/orig only)                  WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Pkg of 3 photos                   Colonel, USAF\n  2. Cy ltr fr Mr. F.R. Anderson        Chief, Topical Division\n     dtd 2 Oct 52                      Deputy Director for Estimates\n  3. Photo                             Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  4. Cy OPNAV Notice 3820\nNo M/R necessary, self-explanatory.\n\nAFOIN-\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2 W. A. Smith Col AFOIN-2A [signature]\n                [signature]\n\n\n                                                        OUT\n                                                   12 OCT 1952\n\n                                                    DIR/INT\n                                                    HQ USAF\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fa01c0c5c6df5a6a85361aa0acd54cbfd50163a82282e5bd03f9cff480c4f8c3", "output_sha256": "b4122ba19626c89d5f51df4043e5a9161a907c8dca9d93dd0ab9dc40683c00b6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:43.405027+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p97", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 97, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\nOCT 6 1952\n\nMr. Alexander Factor\nP.O. Box 801\nOttawa, Canada\nDear Mr. Factor:\n        General Samford has asked me to convey his thanks\nto you for your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects.\n\n        Your interest and efforts to assist us are appreciated.\n\n                        Sincerely,\n\n                        WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Chief, Topical Division\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:      AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n        [signature]                [signature]\n\n                        OUT\n                G 7 OCT 1952\n                  DR/INT\n                HQ USAF\n\n000.9 Flying Disc AFOIN COORDINATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "98ff8347c9359e138aec1e4ce5179d0f7db91a1188738e215da2d178b9c0d38a", "output_sha256": "aaf646ebafb5e0f8504ed85ec748ef87dce6548062901e68a0f358a1d6564f69", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:44.768222+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p98", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 98, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 1 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                         OCT 3  1952\n\n    Mr. Wayne F. Rusk\n    Box 66\n    Dodson, Montana\n\n    Dear Mr. Rusk:          COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ------------\n\n        We have received your letter of 28 August 1952 in which you enclosed\n    the aluminum foil strips found on your farm.\n\n        Fortunately, these strips do not represent any activity of which\n    we are unaware.  They are known as radar window or chaff and are dropped\n    by our own aircraft.\n\n        Nonetheless, we are grateful for your interest and your efforts to\n    assist us.\n\n                                    Sincerely,\n    x095. Rusk, Mr. Wayne F.\n\n                                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                                    Colonel, USAF\n                                    Chief, Topical Division\n                                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n    NO M/R\n\n                                                        OUT\n                                                    G  7 OCT 1952\n                                                       DIRINT\n                                                       HQ USAF\n\n    COORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n    _Col W.H. [signature]_        _[signature] Capt._\n              #8", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d614bca4b8de6d773623f08192b4b85903155b810bb7f76c0feb3b5bed52d1a9", "output_sha256": "33aab85e549e4bd26b853fe5ab8ae393b87b7adc6c368b4f4668be2bdc09047b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:46.503340+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p99", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 99, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nRewrtn 3 Oct 52\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 3  1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A             Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosure is forwarded for your information and retention.  It concerns\n\"theories and suggestions\" related to the Project.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made by this office.\n\n               x300.7 ATICS\n\n1 Incl (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Photostat cy of ltr to FBI        Colonel, USAF\n  dtd Aug 52 fr Roy Elwell          Chief, Topical Division\n  Roadstown, New Jersey             Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n[Signature]                [Signature]\n\n                                        OUT\n                                    6 7 OCT 1952\n                                      DIRINT\n                                      HQ USAF\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "95a98a61f3e2dbd32eed4cd432f241c71ee0d1ef78eaef10402693c97e69be5a", "output_sha256": "95a98a61f3e2dbd32eed4cd432f241c71ee0d1ef78eaef10402693c97e69be5a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:48.116219+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p100", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 100, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. John J. Phillips\n6047 Baldwin Avenue\nTemple City, California\n\nDear Mr. Phillips:\n\n     The Secretary of the Army has referred your letter of 29 August\n1952 to us for attention.  Although we had already processed yours of\n26 August to us, we were, nonetheless, very happy to receive your\nadditional comments.\n\n     We would like to assure you that the Air Force is not treating\nthe \"flying saucer\" situation lightly.  As recently announced, we are\nconducting a very serious program of intelligence investigation and\nanalysis, and we will continue to give the problem adequate but not\nfrantic attention.  By this time you have most probably received a\nvery detailed questionnaire from the Air Technical Intelligence Center\nwith a request to enter as much detail as you are able to recall about\nthe object which you observed.  This should indicate to you our earnest\nefforts to find a satisfactory solution to the problem.\n\n     We hope that these brief comments have served to reassure you of\nthe Air Force's attitude towards this subject.  We appreciate your\nkeen interest and efforts to assist us.\n\n          Sincerely,\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:     AFOIN2A2     AFOIN-2A\n\n              el WH/mith     D.W. Berkelagt.\n\n              [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0d7ea814a9bdb3e9103c8f6d519d470e51929ec1d3a6f7f52d3d249a97e5a908", "output_sha256": "b482160fdc2121ee1356876dd6e5b84af91348245a5a93df66eb07c986e0942c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:49.798277+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p101", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 101, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "PETERS, Mrs. Rita M.\n\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\n                                        Rewritten 2 Oct 52\n\n\n                                   OCT 3  1952\n\n\nMrs. Rita M. Peters\n750 O'Farrell Street\nSan Francisco 9, California\n\nDear Mrs. Peters:\n\n     We have received your letter of 4 September 1952 with the\ninteresting newspaper clipping attached.\n\n     In order to relieve you of any further worry about the\nnewspaper photographs, we can assure you that they are fakes.\nApparently the newspaper intended them as a form of subtle\nsatire. Unfortunately, however, many such attempts at humor\ncause undue concern among the public, and this appears to be\none of these instances.\n\n     We appreciate your action in sending us the clipping and\nhope that our comments have reassured you.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n     095. Peters, Mrs. Rita M.\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n[signature]                        [signature]\n                                        OUT\n                                     7 OCT 1952\n                                      AFINT\n                                      HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "65c43434703e2727ae6a55c1753a65398995d6faa37cbc9482cd774240bc0319", "output_sha256": "862307be8f71a6651bc00550a180a5d9f046283bd0228b8000474ea55ff53d4c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:51.575649+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p102", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 102, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWrtn 3 October 1952\n\n                                    OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. J. M. Green\n2640 5th Avenue South\nMinneapolis 8, Minnesota\n\nDear Mr. Green:\n\n     Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\nNo M/R necessary.             Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2    AFOIN-2A\n\n[signatures]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "60e8f5bea71ad06e017a8d78873e00bf3639609dbe5fe1eaa38fc57c70ea4831", "output_sha256": "60e8f5bea71ad06e017a8d78873e00bf3639609dbe5fe1eaa38fc57c70ea4831", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:52.811988+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p103", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 103, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. Charlie Williams\nP.O. Box 597\nMackinac Island, Michigan\n  Dear\n    Mr. Williams:\n        Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been forwarded to this Headquarters by\n\nthe addressee since we are responsible for the\n\nprogram.  The ideas which you submitted are receiving\n\nour careful consideration.\n\n        We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist us.\n\n                        Sincerely,\n\n\n                        WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Chief, Topical Division\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:           AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                        [signature]            [signature]\n                          58", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1b0f51287fc99c200eb61b9184f7f86ff110f3a74001bbd77a5eea77dda401a8", "output_sha256": "fab24761f109890eb52e6d7801e8de7860d38c031167788b922c5ce3c9bfc656", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:54.121480+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p104", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 104, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                        OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. A.W. Bacon\n311 Clay Street\nJacksonville, Florida\n                    COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n        Dear\n        Mr. Bacon:\n\n             Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n             We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                                        OUT\n                                     G 7 OCT 1952\n                                       DIR/INT\n                                      HQ USAF\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:         AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                 [signature]              [signature]\n                    25", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d774be5639a8432cd1394d37aa3ea6a591aa3f9526a094dc68bf7ce1dc3f9fd7", "output_sha256": "92a63ea0075426b1c52270fb3098b339ed1f990ef02c1ecf22e461700e94e1fa", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:08:55.539868+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p105", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 105, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 3  1952\n\nMrs. Maynard Wade\nRoute #2\nConvoy, Ohio\n\n          Mrs. Wade:\n\n          Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n          We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n                                          OUT\n                    Sincerely,        G  7  OCT 1952\n                                        DIR/INT\n                                        HQ USAF\n\n                              S\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                        