"Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n\n                                                OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. Jim Jones\n8907A Eager Road\nRichmond Heights 17, Missouri\n   Dear\n      Mr Jones:\n\n          Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n          We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n\n                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Chief, Topical Division\n                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2               AFOIN-2A\n\n              [signature]              [signature]\n                  [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6da724fc7bcfe1749afb955f5cc6a1da979858cf1ac5318a838e00163ff4004b", "output_sha256": "a46d6ff5bbd317112862de16720caf2d1e757dc4e5af554ca8e01d89a4d69806", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:19.503687+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p124", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 124, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fourret/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                         OCT 3  1952\n\nMr. Ben Ari\n21 East 21st Street\nNew York, New York\n\n    Mr. Ari:\n\n        Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n        We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                    S\n                              WILLIAM A. [ILLEGIBLE]AM[ILLEGIBLE]\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Di[ILLEGIBLE]\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nNO M/R\n\n             COORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2      AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                    [ILLEGIBLE signature]        [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n                              48", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d1013fc27b5e4eca0c194cef85b45dc83699c593a2234ad6ce58533c4338a481", "output_sha256": "d1013fc27b5e4eca0c194cef85b45dc83699c593a2234ad6ce58533c4338a481", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:20.830103+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p125", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 125, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWrtn 3 Oct 52\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                          OCT 3  1952\n\nMrs. S. Stechman\n209 6th Street North\nGreat Falls, Montana\n\nDear Mrs. Stechman:\n\n        General Samford has asked me to convey his thanks\n\nto you for your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects.\n\n        Your interest and efforts to assist us are appreciated.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n                                        OUT\n                                    G 7  OCT 1952\n                                      DIR/INT\n                                     HQ USAF\n                                     AFOIN-2A\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2\n\n        Col W.H. Smith                [ILLEGIBLE]\n              [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "51982279e685f89907cb2bfacf3b218f02cea55455c4499b578d87b9fac2280e", "output_sha256": "958cd0e855e001fda753541b1dd1e5ea047bf448a159dde298f64f0acd968774", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:22.404842+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p126", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 126, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWrtn 2 Oct 52\n\n(Restricted) Unidentified Object Which Fell in\nWater Off Okinawa, Nov 50\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 3 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2\nWright-Patterson AFB                                    Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nOhio\n\n    1.  Reference our DF dated 28 August 1952, same subject as above.\n\n    2.  Large scale maps of the area in question were obtained and the correct spot\nlocated.  It will be noted on Incl 1 that the water off the village of Ginama is\nrather deep.  According to Sgt Guzi's sketch, the object would have fallen in at\n[REDACTED] 10 fathoms of water.  A search for the object would entail diving operations at\nthis depth over an area of approximately one-half square mile or more.  For this\nreason it is considered impractical to request an attempt at recovery.\n\n    3.  It is suggested that all documents pertaining to this case be filed in the\nevent that the future status of Project Blue Book warrants a recovery attempt.\n\n    4.  All documents referring to this case are returned herewith.\n\n                    X322.7 ATIC\n\n6 Incls (w/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                                         Colonel, USAF\n1. Map 3727-1 SW, 1:25,000              Chief, Topical Division\n2. Map 3727-111 NE, 1:25,000            Deputy Director for Estimates\n3. Transcript of interview w/Sgt Guzi    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n4. Memo of Sgt Guzi's comments\n5. Hydro Chart Okinawa\n6. Aero Chart Okinawa\n\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n                                              4\n                                         OUT\n                                      6  OCT 1952\n                                         DPAINT\n                                         HQ USAF\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                                              1-6\nCol W H [mitt]         [signature]    When Incl(s) No.          (or not attached),\n                                    [REDACTED] the   Restricted    ification\n                                    of this copy    will be down-\n                                    graded to Unclassified in\nRESTRICTED                          accordance with Par 25s, ANR 205-1.\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "71d24533f6584a87a7094a010dd0498d9a38fd949fec8b83112df76d842f248b", "output_sha256": "64436df7414dd83fc340032cfc27299ebbe50dc91ce0047dc41469dd93482cf0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:25.063203+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p127", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 127, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL AFOIN-2A2\n[REDACTED] Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nSECURITY INFORMATION Wrtn 2 Oct 52\n\n(Restricted) Lab Analysis of Soil Samples Having Possible Relation to\n         Unidentified Flying Objects\n\nCounter Intelligence Division\nDirectorate of Special Investigations, The IG\n                                                    OCT 3  1952\n                                                         1\n                                              Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nTopical Division\nDeputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O\n\n     1.  Reference our R&R dated 5 September 1952, same subject as above.  Recent\ndevelopments have prompted the attachment of increased importance to these samples.\nSpecifically, a deposit seeming to have the same general characteristics and also\nrelated to a flying object incident has been reported from Flat Woods, West Virginia.\n\n     2.  In view of this possible relationship and the necessity for a prompt analysis\nof these two incidents, it is requested that utmost priority be given to the lab\nanalysis of subject samples.\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n   [signature]                         [signature]\n\n                                              OUT\n                                           6 OCT 1952\n                                           DIR/INT\n                                           HQ USAF\n\n\n                         CONFIDENTIAL\n                       SECURITY INFORMATION\n                              1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9e67ce42829787a11a5943013e955474063f3bb91bf663f85347c3c5ff15da84", "output_sha256": "9e67ce42829787a11a5943013e955474063f3bb91bf663f85347c3c5ff15da84", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:26.866687+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p128", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 128, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWrtn 2 Oct 52\n\n(Restricted) Lab Analysis of Soil Samples Having Possible Relation to\n         Unidentified Flying Objects\n\nCounter Intelligence Division\nDirectorate of Special Investigations, The IG\n                                                    OCT 3 1952\n                                                              1\nTopical Division                              Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nDeputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O\n\n     1.  Reference our R&R dated 5 September 1952, same subject as above.  Recent\ndevelopments have prompted the attachment of increased importance to these samples.\nSpecifically, a deposit seeming to have the same general characteristics and also\nrelated to a flying object incident has been reported from Flat Woods, West Virginia.\n\n     2.  In view of this possible relationship and the necessity for a prompt analysis\nof these two incidents, it is requested that utmost priority be given to the lab\nanalysis of subject samples.\n\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\n\n\n                         CONFIDENTIAL\n                      SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                              1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "24335a6e304dec5eafd6f58eed731bedccca3dd5c3f5027148d0a24937b8a2cd", "output_sha256": "c9da888098478a312b43d89b0eed82fd5eb7fbf84d087f5816e19d65863873c9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:28.463318+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p129", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 129, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWrtn 2 Oct 52\n\n(Unclassified) Additional Correspondence from\nRobert Spencer Carr (ref Project Blue Book)\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 2 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2            Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed correspondence from Mr. Carr to the President, with a copy of\nthe reply made by the Director of Legislation and Liaison, is for your information\nand retention.  Further correspondence with Mr. Carr is not necessary.\n\n     2.  It is suggested that these documents be placed in the file with other corres-\npondence from Mr. Carr.\n\n               x322.7 ATIC\n                      8\n\n4 Incls (w/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   1. cc of ltr to Mr. Carr              Colonel, USAF\n      fr SAFLL dtd 22 Aug 52             Chief, Topical Division\n      w/ltr to the Pres. fr              Deputy Director for Estimates\n      Mr. Carr attached                  Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n   2. Article taken fr 24 Sep 49\n      issue of Saturday Evening\n      Post \"Nightmare At Dawn\"\n   3. cc of ltr to Mr. Carr fr           COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n      ATIC dtd 13 May 52 w/note\n      to the Pres. attached              When incl(s) No. 1-4\n   4. Ltr to ATIC fr Mr. Carr            are withdrawn (or not attached),\n      dtd 8 Apr 52                       the Restricted    classification\n                                         of this correspondence will be down-\n                                         graded to Unclassified   in\nNo M/R necessary.                        accordance with Par 253, AFR 205-1.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n[signature]                       [signature]\n                                                    OUT\n                                                 G  6 OCT 1952\n                                                    CARINT\n                                                    HQ USAF\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                           SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ec915f1787d099a7189e6c15c27820159a8b2aa0492d263f690b1b64fe627b68", "output_sha256": "ec915f1787d099a7189e6c15c27820159a8b2aa0492d263f690b1b64fe627b68", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:30.801805+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p130", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 130, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 2 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                    OCT 2  1952\n\nMr. George F. Allcorn\nP.O. Box 555\nKeyes, California\n\n     Dear Mr. Allcorn:\n          Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n          We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNO M/R\n\n          COORDINATION:     AFOIN-2A2        AFOIN-2A\n\n                    [ILLEGIBLE signature]    [ILLEGIBLE signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1129f2cdefed610ed5dd9d40d2337ebe99ed64c32b6cbbbc6057933ac28200bb", "output_sha256": "b943959d84b6df93f9b21a03afb2cdbd2a3072fa72b00a111daade254c2bcd00", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:32.105018+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p131", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 131, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 2 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 2  1952\n\nMrs. Forrest Payne\n222 Twin Oaks Road, Apt. 2\nAkron 13, Ohio\n     Dear Mrs. Payne:\n\n          Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\ncareful consideration.\n\n          We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNO M/R\n\n          COORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                         [signature]          [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e7916f318a4fc440c324e5789470ef03c8be27839d064dc746c735e23385d6c2", "output_sha256": "25e804a64a4bab1908345e2f721d577516b6171c4e6d9dac6ad8041c891317b7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:33.299482+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p132", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 132, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN 2A2\n                                        Maj. Fournet/tmw\n                                        Ext. 75990\n                                        Wrtn, 1 October 52\n\n\nMr. Albert A. Trogdon\nThird and Main Streets\nUnion City, Tennessee\n                                        OCT 2  1952\n\nDear Mr. Trogdon:\n\n     We have received your letter of 7 August 1952\nand have given your ideas careful consideration.\n\n     With regard to your query about a reward, we\nmust advise that we offer no remuneration for the\nmany unsolicited ideas which we receive on the\nsubject of \"flying saucers\", but we are nonetheless\nhappy to accept them as a gesture of patriotism by\nthe writer.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to\nassist us.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNO M/R\n\n     COORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2        AFOIN-2\n\n\n                    [signature]          [signature] Cpt.\n\n                                         OUT\n                                      3  OCT 1952\n                                      [ILLEGIBLE]\n                                      HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4193168a0609ecb3411fbc2b0da547b57705e46da690e42cbdfc81aaf0d2f0c9", "output_sha256": "37295eb7eacfc6516fad15cb97a76a871ee65656322af96d6c4b85bb4b847c40", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:34.881098+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p133", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 133, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWrnt 1 Oct 52\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          OCT 2  1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2              Maj Fournet/dbv/75990\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n   1.  Reference report of sighting Miami, Florida on 29 July 52 and related 16 mm\nmovie film previously forwarded to you.  The inclosed document, obtained from OSD-OPI,\ncontains additional information on this incident.  It is for your information and\nretention.\n\n   2.  Also inclosed for your retention are photostatic copies of selected documents\nin the Marine Corps personnel file on D.S. Des Vergers.  These photostats were supplied\nby the Marine Corps with the understanding that the information therein would not be\ndivulged to anyone who does not require it for intelligence analysis of the incident\nin which Des Vergers was a principal.\n\n\n\n5 Incls (w/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr USMC, Miami, Fla                Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 4 Aug 52 w/attachments          Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Photostat cy of review of           Deputy Director for Estimates\n     discharge of D.S. Des Vergers       Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Photostat cy of ltr fr Board\n     of Review to The Commandant of\n     the MC, 7 Aug 52\n  4. Photostat cy of ltr to Navy\n     Dept fr Fed Reform, Chillicothe,\n     O. dtd 14 Oct 44 re Des Vergers\n  5. Photostat cy of ltr to JAG, Navy\n     fr US Attorney, Southern Dist of\n     Fla dtd 16 Oct 44\n                         ✓ x3227 A T/c\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2             AFOIN-2A\n\n\n        Col W H Smith                  A M Bride Lt.\n           Df\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1adf0403e73576d9c0cb7557f297ba3ce525b7d7b8434a380cfd00325958e542", "output_sha256": "1adf0403e73576d9c0cb7557f297ba3ce525b7d7b8434a380cfd00325958e542", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:37.205514+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p134", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 134, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWrtn 1 Oct 52\n\nChief, Air Technical          (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nIntelligence Center           Dept of the Air Force    OCT 2  1952\nWright-Patterson AFB          Hq USAF - AFOIN          Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  Following receipt of Miss Butcher's memo (Incl. 1) by this office, she\nwas requested to complete a standard questionnaire which was supplied.  Completed\nquestionnaire is attached as Incl. 2.\n\n     3.  Inclosure 3 is questionnaire completed by LCDR Leon B. Blair, USN,\nfollowing his telephonic report of a sighting to this office.\n\n\n3 Incls: (W/orig. only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Memo fr Lucile H. Butcher             Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 11 Aug 52                         Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Questionnaire completed by Miss Butcher  Deputy Director for Estimates\n  3. Questionnaire completed by LCDR Blair    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n                    4/322.7 ATIC\n\n\nNO M/R          COORDINATION:       AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n              Col W H Iminch          [ILLEGIBLE]\n                   DS                      p\n\n              When incl(s) No. 2 & 3\n              were with [ILLEGIBLE] (are not attached),\n              the Restricted [ILLEGIBLE]ation\n              of t[ILLEGIBLE] down-\n              RECLASSIFIED Unclassified in\n              accordi[ILLEGIBLE]\n              [ILLEGIBLE]Y INFORMATION [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "620ffd3d048dfa6ecfe72f834b5fa23a5c37014d2001199988c08de0232e48b6", "output_sha256": "a69187493823b3836af2852ad1996184969cdcece8cd8fe44602f7b7b82299e9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:39.423482+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p135", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 135, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 3 Oct 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 2  1952\n\nMr. Robert H. Branan\n114 Colonial Circle, Apt. 2\nMarietta, Georgia\n\nDear Mr. Branan:\n\n     Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                                        OUT\n                                   G  3  OCT 1952\n                                      DIR/INT\n                                      HQ USAF\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNO M/R\n\n          COORDINATION:     AFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A\n\n                            [ILLEGIBLE]        [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f5dcc7016b3b849be41d5c6b7d6ad46c1271819b6604f8e82e31ce297e9e5f1d", "output_sha256": "f5dcc7016b3b849be41d5c6b7d6ad46c1271819b6604f8e82e31ce297e9e5f1d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:40.699408+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p136", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 136, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-1B2/Maj Pandolfo/jbl/52563\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                OCT 2  1952\n\nAFOIN-1B2\n\nSUBJECT:  Transmittal of AF Form 112\n\nTO:       Commanding General\n          27th Air Division\n          Norton Air Force Base\n          California\n          ATTN:  Director of Intelligence\n\n\n     1.  AF Form 112 referenced on DD Form 95 was not received in this\nHeadquarters.\n\n     2.  Attached as inclosures are DD Form 95 and statement by Captain\nRalph P. Borgeson (2 copies).\n\n     3.  Request AF Form 112 as mentioned be forwarded as soon as possible\nwith inclosures attached.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                              X-210.31 Borgeson, Capt Ralph P\n\n2 Incls                       /JOHN G. GLOVER\n  a/s                         Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Dissemination Branch\n                              Dissemination Control Division\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nWhen inclosure No. 1 and 2 are\nwithdrawn or not attached, the\nclassification on this correspondence\nwill be changed to UNCLASSIFIED in\naccordance with Par. 25e, AFR 205-1.\n\n\nAFOIN-1B2\nMaj Pandolfo\nCol Glover\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2062c397839158b44effc019961c549cc26e83e573c526205ccb02cfade1758a", "output_sha256": "aff99caa853642f25e28f30698bace127ee4568c13bd7dd0357cef0cb7f10361", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:42.689589+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p137", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 137, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n(CLASSIFICATION)\n\nAC FORM 112—PART II\nAPPROVED 1 JUNE 1949\n\nAIR INTELLIGENCE INFORMATION REPORT\n\nFROM (Agency)                          REPORT NO.\n27TH Air Div (Def), Norton AFB, Cal                    PAGE  1  OF  1  PAGES\n\n                                                    #506502\n\nStatement:\n\n     On the 19 August 1952, at approximately 2000 PDST, Algiers took control of\nSwanee Red from Conform at georef position DD 1050, at which time he was given a\nvector of 290°.\n\n     Swanee Red Leader then called Algiers stating that he was steady on 290° and\nthat he had a stranger at one o'clock.  Algiers asked if he could tell what type\nof aircraft it was?  Swanee Red Leader gave a negative reply, but Swanee Red 2\nsaid it could possibly be a Big Photo because it appeared as a large type aircraft.\nAlgiers then instructed Swanee Red to investigate the stranger, also that Algiers\nhad no contact on the stranger as it was in our clutter area, in the vicinity of\nSan Gorgonio Mountain.\n\n     Lt. Otis, Swanee Red Leader, then reported that upon turning into the\nstranger, it appeared to have no tail assembly and showed great acceleration in\nmoving away from them in an easterly direction and disappearing into space.\n\n     Algiers did not make radar pick-up on the unusual sighting at any time.\n\n     Lt. Otis called the controller, (Captain Borgeson), at Algiers after landing\nand described the object as oval at the base and tapered to a heavy center section;\nhe also re-affirmed that it did not have a tail section.\n\n\n\n                              RALPH P. BORGESON\n                              Captain     USAF\n                              Chief Director\n\n\n\n\n\nIncl #2\n\nNOTE  THIS DOCUMENT CONTAINS INFORMATION AFFECTING THE NATIONAL DEFENSE OF THE UNITED STATES WITHIN THE MEANING OF THE ESPIONAGE ACT, 50 U.S.C.—\n        AS AMENDED.  ITS TRANSMISSION OR THE REVELATION OF ITS CONTENTS IN ANY MANNER TO AN UNAUTHORIZED PERSON IS PROHIBITED BY LAW.\n        NOT TO BE REPRODUCED IN WHOLE OR IN PART, BY OTHER THAN UNITED STATES AIR FORCE AGENCIES, EXCEPT BY PERMISSION OF THE DIRECTOR OF\n        INTELLIGENCE, USAF.\n\nRESTRICTED\n(CLASSIFICATION)\n     16—52380-1  ☆  U.S. GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE: 1950—O-918332", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a10e84500e558f8fb8ee9a3ef4750d0662e78382b274571a2a26b3d9833c4a8f", "output_sha256": "b13b4c5f481c72102b6c492d08ea7c363c80d2324480d97df673ba820addd3e8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:45.259249+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p138", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 138, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 30 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    OCT 2  1952\n\nMr. Herbert H. Middleton,\nPresident, John Middleton Inc.,\n233-35 S. Third Street,\nPhiladelphia 6, Pennsylvania.\n\nDear Mr. Middleton:\n\n     We have received your letter of 8 September 1952 in which\nyou reported the observation of unidentified flying objects. We\nhave referred it to our Air Technical Intelligence Center for incorporation into our study on the subject. You will probably receive\na detailed questionnaire from them shortly, and your assistance in\ncompleting it will aid us appreciably.\n\n     We are very grateful for your interest and efforts to assist\nus.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n          L095 Middleton, Herbert H\n\nNO M/R\n\n          COORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n              Col Wilmuth                [ILLEGIBLE]\n                  [ILLEGIBLE]              Col USAF\n\n                                        G 2 OCT 1952\n                                         CURRENT\n                                         HQ [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dbd697afd819e70b3c4cf95a9b0be2892f63ef00b2ea214c5aad8b7f00a7c9ac", "output_sha256": "0eba7ed6bbefaa91ea0b3740f5e708fbf52a23b5903c0642973cf7ef86cef999", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:46.963321+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p139", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 139, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 29 Sept 52\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical    Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center     Hq USAF - AFOIN        OCT 1  1952\nWright-Patterson AFB                           Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nOhio\n\n        1.  Inclosed letter from the Federal Bureau of Investigation to OSI is\nfor your information and retention.\n\n        2.  Except for the reference to a pilotless craft, the description seems\nto fit the Chance-Vought V-173 or XF5U \"Flying Flapjack\".  This is bolstered\nby the mention of Connecticut as the location of manufacture.  It is presumed\nthat Mr. McLaughlin did not obtain his information through direct contact, thus\naccounting for the discrepancies in his story.\n\n\n\n                                    S\n1 Incl:  (W/orig. only)             WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Ltr fr FBI to OSI                 Colonel, USAF\n  dtd 20 Aug 52                     Chief, Topical Division\n                                    Deputy, Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\nNo M/R                                          OUT\n                                            OC 1 OCT 1952\n                                              DIRINT\n                                              HQ USAF\n\n        COORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n              Col WHSmith              MMBerle apt.\n\n              x322.7 a TIC\n\n\n\n\n                                    [REDACTED]\n                                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "50e7090312ba6d321e525c71b5d9786afa793267eb070a2ac89fada097702be9", "output_sha256": "1bf44d2aa00a822274612ead5f7b2e324bfa128feb04c41ee5792d6eb32eceeb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:48.857873+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p140", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 140, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nwrtn 29 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\n\n                                          OCT 1  1952\n\nMr. Henry Baker Reiley\nPublisher, Somerset Daily American\nSomerset, Pennsylvania\n\nDear Mr. Reiley:\n\n     Since Air Force Intelligence is responsible for the investigation and analysis of unidentified flying objects,\nGeneral Vandenberg has referred your letter of 14 September\n1952 to us and requested that we answer your questions.\n\n     Although our analysis of the many sightings which occurred\non the night of 12 September is not yet complete, we have\ntentatively concluded that the object was a meteor.  It will\nbe quite some time before our final analysis is available\nsince much checking and study of the various reports is required.\n\n     In reply to your query \"Are we being invaded\", we are\ninclosing a standard release which gives in some detail our\ncurrent conclusions on the subject of unidentified flying\nobjects plus many other things about which we have been\nqueried often in the recent past.  We trust that it will answer\nyour question satisfactorily and assist you in answering any\nother questions which you may have or may receive from your\nreaders.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and your desire to obtain the\nproper answers directly from us.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n          x-095  Reiley, Henry B\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n1 Incl:                       Colonel, USAF\n  stan. release               Chief, Topical Division\n  re flyobs                   Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nNO M/R\n\nCOORDINATION:     AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n     Col W H Smith          [signature]\n              28", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f7e67c7b281bc2a896453447f7edf31fc47890c06532086a3a6ef37d980f37ea", "output_sha256": "800eac5dee97b153be8e0e94abc82b79f49a7882bf61749fc5dad47882690af2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:50.866390+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p141", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 141, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nWrtn 30 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\n\n                    (Restricted) Report and Samples Pertaining to\n                    Incident vic. Flat Woods, W. Va., 12 Sept 52\nChief, Air Technical    Dept of the Air Force  1 OCT 1952\nIntelligence Center     Hq USAF - AFOIN        Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWright-Patterson\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed report, prepared by Capt. Dale L. Leavitt of the National\nGuard, was obtained from the National Guard Bureau, Washington.  It concerns\nthe sighting of an unidentified flying object which allegedly landed in the\nvicinity of Flat Woods, West Virginia around 1930 EST 12 Sept 52, and the alleged\nobservation of a \"monster\" shortly thereafter in the area in which the flying\nobject supposedly landed, (see Incls 1 and 2).\n\n     2.  Prior to receipt of the inclosed, the only information received on this\nincident was through the press.  The Washington DAILY NEWS advised OSD-OPI of\ncertain information which they had obtained from persons in the locale.  One\ncomment, attributed to Capt. Leavitt, was that the \"skid marks\" along the side of\nthe hill were formed by a greasy deposit which felt like graphite.  This appeared\nto bear a possible relation to the incident of the \"perfect circle\" in Arlington,\nVirginia on 2 Sept 52.  Therefore, Capt. Leavitt was contacted and confirmed this\nstatement.  He was requested to obtain soil and vegetation samples and submit\nthem to this office.\n\n     3.  Samples arrived 29 Sept 52 and show no evidence of a graphite-like deposit.\nThey are attached as Incl 3 for your disposition.\n\n     4.  Some of the principals in this incident were on the TV program \"We The\nPeople\" on 19 Sept 52.  During this program a drawing was shown which was claimed\nto represent a composite of the descriptions of all witnesses.  A rough sketch\nwas made of this drawing and is attached as Incl. 4.  It is vaguely reminiscent of\na character which appeared in a comic strip a few years ago.\n\n     5.  All inclosures are for your retention.\n\n          COUPON x322 7ATIC              OUT\n                                        1 OCT 1952\n                                     SECURITY INFORMATION\n                                        HQ USAF\n4 Incls: (w/orig. only)           WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Capt. D.L. Leavitt    Colonel, USAF\n     re flyob, dtd 17 Sept 52     Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Drawing re uniden. flyob.    Deputy Director for Estimates\n  3. Samples re sighting          Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  4. Sketch re sighting\n\n     MO M/R     COORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n                    [signature]                [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c9b4f3977b6bb7ed4e2df4198fbe9eeb9b4f867ffb1653fec4b39dcac5c23b7b", "output_sha256": "c9b4f3977b6bb7ed4e2df4198fbe9eeb9b4f867ffb1653fec4b39dcac5c23b7b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:53.792188+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p142", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 142, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-X/Lt Col Smith/met/71092/30 Sep 52\n\n                    30 September 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:  MR. PHILCOX - FBI\n\nSUBJECT:  Comments on Article in The NEW YORKER\n\n     1.  A call was made to the Air Technical Intelligence Center,\n1330 this date, (Captain Ruppelt) regarding the attached article.\n\n     2.  ATIC did not in any way indicate to Mr. Lang that the\nFBI has an interest in flying saucers.  Furthermore, Captain\nRuppelt stated that the FBI to his knowledge has never been called\nupon to furnish reports on flying saucers.  ATIC is under the\nimpression that Mr. Lang made the story up or picked it up from\na magazine or newspaper article sometime back that definitely\nwas not associated with their organization.\n\n     3.  ATIC suggests that you check further with Mr. Al Chop,\nOffice of Public Information, and perhaps he can supply you with\nthe information you have requested.\n\n                    x095 Philcox, Mr.\n\n1 Incl: - fnd d'org only          C. M. YOUNG\n  Article fr NEW YORKER,          Colonel, USAF\n  dtd Sept 6, 1952                Chief, Policy & Management Group\n                                  Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n          Handed to Mr. Philcox, 10 Oct '52\n\n\n\n\n                    AFOIN X\n\n\n                    WK Smith Ltcol", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cbd7b6d1fdf3b492b76962619d1e83ab6229ccd9c6c6a098ca393fc1ab684f3e", "output_sha256": "f16cce45335c7a4a4c1cf731319baf50e01fe893fcea585eff331eb80a58e9c3", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:55.538766+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p143", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 143, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET                              SUSPENSE\n\nORIGIN OF BASIC                    DATE         TYPE         DATE\n\nSUBJECT                                                      ASSIGNED BY\n\n                                                             NUMBER\n\n                                        ROUTING\n\nInitial \"IN\" column to denote review prior to action. Initial \"OUT\" column to denote review of completed action. (X-for action:\nV- for coordination)\n\nIN    OFFICE      OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n      AFOIN                   OIN-1             OIN-2                 OIN-3\n      OIN-X    S   M         OIN-1X            OIN-2X                OIN-3X\n      OIN-X1\n      OIN-X2\n\n\n\n      CABLES\nM     FILE    10/1  and                                               SR NAVAL OFF\n      DISPATCH handed to                                              SR ARMY OFF\nTO:   Wt. Philcoy 10/1                                       DATE\n\nFROM:                                                        COMMENT NUMBER\n\nCOMMENTS (Use reverse, if necessary)\n                                                             AFOIN No.\n\n                                                               299\n\nAFHQ    FORM       0-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.                D 6616\n        22 JUL 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4f9559921d15b2c0967f494b54c6abc54f10babca769dfd5c0f6948a74d51dcf", "output_sha256": "e5a455e754cdcf86ee9e26ac8544534f01795135b969964e20ce49e4a6b9d539", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:57.158006+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p144", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 144, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\n                                        wrtn 26 Sept 52\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\n\n\n                        (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force      30 SEP 1952\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN         Maj Fournet/71016/cmb\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\nAll concern sightings of objects.\n\n     2.  The request for a star chart made by Zella L. W. Bowers (see Incl 3)\nhas been extracted and referred to OSD-OPI for compliance.\n\n     3.  The letter from Mrs. Eric C. Johnson (Incl 8) was forwarded by Mr. Clay\nBlair of TIME.  A letter of acknowledgment has been sent Mr. Blair, but no reply\nhas been made to Mrs. Johnson.\n\n     4.  The letter from Marion Leonard (Incl 2) was answered by SAFLL; a copy\nof their reply is also inclosed.  Further correspondence is not mandatory.\n\n     5.  A reply to Mr. Herbert H. Middleton (Incl 10) was made by this office.\n\n\n\n10 Incls: (W/Orig. only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. cy reply fr SAFLL to Mr. Leonard       Colonel, USAF\n        dtd 8 Sept 52                       Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Mr. Leonard                     Deputy Director for Estimates\n        dtd 27 Aug 52                       Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Zella L.W. Bowers\n        dtd 25 Aug 52\n  4. Ltr fr Mr. L.D. Harmon             COUPON DESIGNATION HERE\n        dtd 14 Sept 52\n  5. Ltr fr Mrs. B. Reese\n        dtd 5 Sept 52\n  6. Ltr fr Miss B. Isaac            X322.7ATIC\n        dtd 8 Sept 52 (w/attch.)\n  7. Ltr fr Mrs M. Little\n        dtd 15 Sept 52\n  8. Ltr fr Mrs E.C. Johnson                         30 SEP 1952\n        dtd 19 Aug 52              SECURITY INFORMATION    DIPRINT\n  9. Ltr fr Wilson Strand                               HQ USAF\n        dtd 15 Sept 52\n 10. Ltr fr Mr. H.H. Middleton\n        dtd 8 Sept 52\n                    COORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\nNO M/R\n                              [signature] Col.      [signature] Lt.\n                                   [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "606339ef11bc135ea583388a6c453a0040165db26b88451b3b3fddf425b7cbda", "output_sha256": "4f08918b2d04e323bea714da06deb073740012b2d3659779602fe0f035eb8b44", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:09:59.944724+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p145", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 145, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "(Unclassified) Proposal from John S. Kim\n\nExecutive,\n  Director of Research & Development, DCS/D\n    Attn:  Major Forsman\nXXXXX\nFROM: Deputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O\n\n                                          26 SEP 1952          1\n                                          Maj Fournet/71016/cmb\n\n        1.  Inclosures are forwarded as a matter of primary interest.\n\n        2.  No reply to Mr. Kim has been made by this office.\n\n\n8 Incls:                                      S\n                                          WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. Lovett         Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 11 Aug 52                        Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Pres. Truman        Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 16 Aug 52 (w/attchd ltr copy to Sec. Lovett) Directorate of Intelligence,\n  3. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. Lovett                                    DCS/O\n     dtd 15 Aug 52 (w/attchd info)\n  4. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. Finletter\n     dtd 11 Aug 52 w/attch cy ltr to LI DAILY PRESS\n  5. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. Finletter\n     dtd 16 Aug 52 w/attch. cy Ltr to Sec. Lovett & info.\n  6. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. State Acheson\n     dtd 11 Aug 52, w/cy Ltr to LI DAILY PRESS\n  7. Ltr fr Mr. Kim to Sec. State Acheson\n     dtd 16 Aug 52, w/cy Ltr to Sec. Lovett (cy) & info.\n  8. Cy ltr to Mr. Kim fr Dept State dtd 22 Aug 52\n\nNO M/R              x095. Kim, Mr. J. S.\n\n        COORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2               AFOIN-2A\n\n\n              Col. W.H. [ILLEGIBLE]              [ILLEGIBLE] Capt.\n\n\n                         COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ————", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bd50f7598716e503e26ae4ca695c86251c323b568fa504892cb32cdc64db01cb", "output_sha256": "83a575e21beb611fed557a74beb70764445d05b94b391d25fd59f19b6dca2014", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:02.335223+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p146", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 146, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 24 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nChief, Air Technical          (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nIntelligence Center           Dept of the Air Force        26 SEP 1952\nWright-Patterson AFB          Hq USAF - AFOIN              Maj Fournet/71016/cmb\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosed letters are for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made by this office.\n\n               x 322.7 ATIC\n\n4 Incls: (w/org only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Mrs M. Loduca               Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 28 Jul 52                      Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr A.E. Morra                  Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 13 Jul 52                      Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Mrs M. Walter\n     dtd 9 Aug 52\n  4. Ltr fr V.L. Stewart\n     dtd 28 Jul 52\n\n\n     COUPON DESIGNATION MADE                    OUT\n                                           9 26 SEP 1952\n                                              DIRINT\n                                             HQ USAF\n\nCOORDINATION:              AFOIN-2A2                AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                    Cl WH Smith                [ILLEGIBLE]\n                        DJ\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                       SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3f7317e1e7f30cb3b1f0dd3ba17653fa4666dac4f0197a65e08e760eba12c5d9", "output_sha256": "3f7317e1e7f30cb3b1f0dd3ba17653fa4666dac4f0197a65e08e760eba12c5d9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:04.186506+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p147", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 147, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 25 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/71016/cmb\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                        26 Sep 1952\n\nMiss Anna Summers\n3108 West 55th Street\nChicago, 32, Illinois\n\nDear Miss Summers:\n\n     Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n     Sincerely,\n\n                              OUT\n                         G 26 SEP 1952\n                           DIR/INT\n                           HQ USAF\n\n                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Chief, Topical Division\n                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n               Col W H Smith          [ILLEGIBLE]\n                    B/", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "321581aa1cfe5446d79ef99cc9de7ded9f87e585a36a605a80f5f8df7e8c2331", "output_sha256": "e9718a7d64c22801439e99aa2c84d49734d6fdcd9bb3f3d935c99deb26d168ee", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:05.581662+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p148", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 148, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 25 Sept 52\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/71016/cmb\n\n26 Sep 1952\n\nMiss Annie Louise Givens\nBloomington, Texas\n\nDear Miss Givens:\n\n     Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been received by this Headquarters, and\n\nthe ideas which you submitted are receiving our\n\ncareful consideration.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist\n\nus.\n\n✓\nx095, Givens, Miss Annie Louise     Sincerely,\n\n[STAMP: A OUT G 26 SEP 1952 DIR/INT HQ USAF]\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2                    AFOIN-2A\n\n          Col W. H. Smith                    [ILLEGIBLE]\n                    DJS\n\n[Vertical text on right margin: 000.9 Flying Discs  AFOIN COORDINATION]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "250c48de33831d6d83b00f77dddef7dbf7b3b0f923d35e3ab16e5b45801207da", "output_sha256": "417f25d6b6736ad81487cf515d0a3222aeb015ab2d8c00a5addd9973eaa4315d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:07.064965+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p149", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 149, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\n23 Sept 52\n\n                                          26 Sep 1952\n\nMiss Lois Neuwirth\nMiss Esther Schilling\n328 East Hennepin Avenue\nMinneapolis, Minnesota\n\nDear Misses Neuwirth and Schilling:\n\n     Your letter of 15 September 1952 was referred to us by the National\nSecurity Council.  As they told you in their letter of 17 September 1952,\nwe are responsible for the \"flying saucer\" investigation.\n\n     With regard to your questions about \"flying saucer\" reports, we\nare inclosing a standard release which sets forth the official Air Force\nattitude and philosophy on the subject.  We hope that it will answer your\nquestions satisfactorily.\n\n     The only report we have received of a \"fire-breathing monster\"\nallegedly seen in West Virginia has been through the press.  Because\nthis observation was made at night and under conditions of excitement\nand, furthermore, since the story has died a natural death without\nfurther mention in the press, we discount it entirely.  It has been noted\nin the past that a flurry of \"flying saucer\" reports will stimulate the\nimagination and give rise to many complementary reports evolved through\nassociation.  We are convinced that the report from West Virginia\nrepresents just such a case where the necessary stimulus was provided\nby the meteor sighting reports of the preceding Friday night.\n\n     We hope that these brief comments have provided satisfactory answers\nto your questions.\n        x 095 Neuwirth, Miss Lois\n        x 095, Schilling, Miss [ILLEGIBLE]\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n1 Incl:                            WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  AF standard release              Colonel, USAF\n  re flyobs.                       Chief, Topical Division\n                                   Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                   Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOORDINATION:        AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN\n\n              Col W.H/[ILLEGIBLE]        [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "babf953dd0e8d84a85419f4a7bde3ac7db30185041ab4e91c8842d9283e67493", "output_sha256": "33a96d5d10a4ebc423393ac2a196e80e7fb6fcb9970cfc3a0bb35791d360da33", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:09.230102+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p150", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 150, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 12 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n                                    25 SEP 1952\n\nMr. G. Francis Nauheimer\nDirector, Glare Research Institute\n6537 S. Seeley Avenue\nChicago 36, Illinois\n\nDear Mr. Nauheimer:\n\n     I sincerely appreciated your letter of 29 July 1952\n\nand have referred it to our intelligence analysts for\n\nvery careful consideration of your ideas and suggestions.\n\n     Many thanks for your efforts on our behalf.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\nx095. Nauheimer, Mr. G Francis\n                         s/ JOHN A. SAMFORD\n                         MAJOR GENERAL, USAF\n                         DIRECTOR OF INTELLIGENCE\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A               AFOIN-2        AFOIN\n\n               Col W Wolfe        [signature]             [signature]\n\n\nTo be filed with coordination copy of DF to Chief, Air Technical Intelligence\n  Center, Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio dtd 16 Sep 52 Subj:  (U) Material for\n  Project Blue Book.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8792a3304719036520325e4d34cb2ee0a3d345dd49539bfa94a493c5108c8c6b", "output_sha256": "8792a3304719036520325e4d34cb2ee0a3d345dd49539bfa94a493c5108c8c6b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:10.665243+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p151", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 151, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 12 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n\n                                        25 SEP 1952\n\n\nMr. John M. Hollywood\nCBS Laboratories\n485 Madison Avenue\nNew York 22, New York\n\nDear Mr. Hollywood:\n\n     I sincerely appreciated your letter of 29 July 1952\n\nand have referred it to our intelligence analysts for\n\nvery careful consideration of your ideas and suggestions.\n\n     Many thanks for your efforts on our behalf.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              s/\n                              JOHN A. SAMFORD\n                              MAJOR GENERAL, USAF\n                              DIRECTOR OF INTELLIGENCE\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2     AFOIN\n\n               Col JW Wolfe       [signature]        [signature]\n                                                     H/C Telev?\n\n\nTo be filed with coordination copy of DF to Chief, Air Technical Intelligence\n  Center, Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio dtd 16 Sep 52 Subj:  (U) Material for\n  Project Blue Book.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e99b4bea77ab4fe2f8f3b77335c54ebb3db821a340045f417083bd73094fbf08", "output_sha256": "e99b4bea77ab4fe2f8f3b77335c54ebb3db821a340045f417083bd73094fbf08", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:12.161771+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p152", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 152, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 12 Sept 52\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nAFOIN-2A2\n\n\n25 SEP 1952\n\n\nProfessor John O. Weber\nCollege of Engineering\nThe University of Wisconsin\nMadison 6, Wisconsin\n\nDear Professor Weber:\n\n     I sincerely appreciated your letter of 2 August 1952\n\nand have referred it to our intelligence analysts for\n\nvery careful consideration of your ideas.\n\n     I would be most happy to hear from you further on\n\nthis subject.\n\n     Many thanks for your efforts on our behalf.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n                              s/\n                              JOHN A. SAMFORD\n                              MAJOR GENERAL, USAF\n                              DIRECTOR OF INTELLIGENCE\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2\n\n     Col HW Wolfe          OHBeck Cpt.          GC Tebley     AFOIN\n\n\nTo be filed with coordination copy of DF to Chief, Air Technical Intelligence\n  Center, Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio dtd 16 Sep 52 Subj:  (U) Material for\n  Project Blue Book.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "80b4a68830f5bc335eabf23130588f5e91ab841112d532f9f75ff672e50264f3", "output_sha256": "ba67bf77c0084c46e2ba2fff3d053926daf10bb8f217074e371af26d26d0292a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:13.686460+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p153", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 153, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\nGLARE RESEARCH INSTITUTE\n\nDiscoverer                                    Office of the Director\n                                             6527 SO. Seeley Avenue\nCONTRA BLUE RAYS                             Chicago 36, Illinois\n\n                                             July 29th, 1952\n\n\nMaj. Gen. John Samford,\nHeadquarters G-2, Air Force,\nDepartment of Defense,\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\nDear Sir:-\n\n        Regarding the recent reports of the so called flying saucers, I am quite\nsure that the hoax will be exposed by telling you that this is nothing more than\nthe silver iodide used in artificial rainmaking.  This is especially true if the\nsilver iodide came in contact with radioactive clouds or so called thunderclouds.\n\n        The solution of this hoax is quite simple, if you will check your records\nyou will find that flying saucers were first seen about the time when silver\niodide came into usage for artificial rainmaking.  Again, silver is a reflective\nagency and will reflect all types of light, which accounts for the various hues\nreported by sky gazers.  Again, silver iodide, if radioactive or ionized by an\nelectrical cloud will become fluorescent, which accounts for flyers being unable\nto overtake the so called flying saucers, and their habit of disappearing.\n\n        Of course, we must eliminate such reports of flying saucers as were accountable\nby balloons, foo-fighters, meteorites, and the person who just calls up a newspaper\nwith the hope of getting his name in the papers.  Also to be disqualified are such\nreports as to ascertain that they are interplanetary space ships.  If it were at\nall possible for another planet to send aircraft of any type to our atmosphere,\nit would simply burn up the same as a meteorite and such space ship remains would\nbe found the same as meteorites.  As far as I know, no such wreckage has ever been\nfound.\n\n\n                                        Respectfully yours,\n\n\n                                             s/\n                                        G. Francis Hauheimer,\n                                             Director.\n\n\n\n                                                                    C O P Y\n\nIncl 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c25f3aea942fd7747de3584800914f67137f8e9fb8ad4fdcc7ea5b101b5c9a34", "output_sha256": "6fb2ef533cef5ea58f2b6df2f7b29905ff882f5743c5401827e02ceec145cf15", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:15.868666+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p154", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 154, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    CBS LABORATORIES\n             A Division of Columbia Broadcasting\n                       System, Inc.\n          485 Madison Avenue, New York 22, New York - Plaza 5-2000\n\n\n                                                    August 1, 1952\n\n\n     Major General James A. Samford\n     Chief of Intelligence\n     Pentagon Building\n     Arlington, Virginia\n\n     Dear Sir:\n\n          In connection with \"flying saucer\" newspaper accounts of\n     observations on the search radar system at the Washington\n     National Airport, it occurred to me that the described be-\n     havior could possibly be accounted for in the following manner:\n\n     High power, narrow beam fire control radar systems of the usual\n     type might conceivably, under unusual atmospheric conditions,\n     create enough ionization along points on the beam in the upper\n     atmosphere to allow the return of an appreciable echo to the\n     search radar system from such points.  The apparent motion would\n     be quite haphazard, following whatever the fire control radar\n     operator does in directing the beam.\n\n     This hypothesis is unattractive for several reasons:  Firstly,\n     the power required for such an effect is many times greater\n     than that put out by the usual radar.  Secondly, such echoes\n     would presumably come from ionospheric heights and therefore\n     could not appear at ranges of a few miles from the search radar,\n     as was reported.  Thirdly, it seems unlikely that a coincident\n     visual effect of any conspicuous magnitude would be produced.\n\n     In spite of this, I am offering this suggestion in the belief\n     that if considerable time, money and effort is being devoted to\n     this problem, it might be worthwhile trying the relatively simple\n     experiment of having a powerful fire control radar sweep out\n     certain simple patterns to see if they can be detected on the\n     search radar system, preferably at a time when \"flying saucer\"\n     echoes are being observed.\n\n                                        Very truly yours,\n\n                                        s/\n                                        John M. Hollywood\n                                        Engineer\n\n     JMH/bas                                                    COPY\n\nIncl 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2073c3e42d44b9117c3959cff0c2eb795595181868db24f66d9cf966d007d875", "output_sha256": "2073c3e42d44b9117c3959cff0c2eb795595181868db24f66d9cf966d007d875", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:17.925240+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p155", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 155, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    THE UNIVERSITY OF WISCONSIN\n                       College of Engineering\n                           Madison 6\n\n     Department of\n     Electrical Engineering\n\n                                                August 2, 1952\n\n\n          Maj. Gen. John A. Samford\n          Air Force Director of Intelligence\n          Washington, D. C.\n\n          Dear Sir:\n\n               I should like to present to you what I believe to\n          be a tenable theory as to the origin and nature of the\n          phenomena popularly known as \"flying saucers\".\n\n               It has been amply demonstrated that electro-magnetic\n          radiation of sufficient power density is capable of\n          ionizing gas at low pressure.  Upon deionization, the\n          gas emits radiation of characteristic wave lengths, some\n          of which lie in the visible spectrum.  Further, it is\n          known that radar equipment can detect ionized gas, such as\n          northern lights, or charged water droplets, such as appear\n          in thunderclouds.\n\n               I believe that ionization of disc-shaped segments of\n          air in the upper atmosphere may be caused by beams from a\n          radar transmitter held in a fixed position or slowly traversed,\n          instead of the usual sweeping motion.\n\n               To verify the possibility, I propose in the very near\n          future to conduct an experiment.  A glass sphere containing\n          air at atmosphere pressure will be exposed to radiation of a\n          known wave length and power density.  The pressure in the\n          sphere will then be reduced until ionization occurs.  The\n          screen of a separate radar transmitter-receiver will also\n          be observed to note whether the change in the condition of\n          the air is detectable by radar.\n\n                                            Very truly yours,\n\n                                            s/\n                                            John C. Weber\n                                            Assoc. Prof. of E. E.\n\n     2007 Engineering\n\n                                                              COPY\n\nEncl 3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "087a2b6975287198c864ad29225b4e526ceda5cdde92408041e6de6934e39b90", "output_sha256": "62e72aa67545ac384dbc99bc2baacb1d62c3c03f1126e7fce430002a3545fa28", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:19.913785+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p156", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 156, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/fh/71016\n                                        12 Sep 52 - wrtn 19 Sep 52\n\n\n                        MEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM\n\n     1.  To prepare DF to ATIC and non-military letters to Prof. John C.\nWeber, Mr. John M. Hollywood and Mr. G. Francis Nauheimer.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n     2.  In letters addressed to General Samford, the above-named gentlemen\noffer theories as to the cause of aerial phenomena which they believe may\naccount for unidentified flying object sightings.  It is noteworthy that\nProf. Weber is Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering at the University\nof Wisconsin, Mr. Hollywood is an engineer for the CBS Laboratories, and Mr.\nNauheimer is Director of the Glare Research Institute.\n\n     3.  Since the proposals of Prof. Weber and Mr. Hollywood coincide\nrather closely with the experiments of Mr. Scott of the Engineer Research\nand Development Lab at Fort Belvoir as well as with the ideas of Dr. Possony,\ntheir letters have been reviewed very carefully.  Copies are being maintained\nhere for further study.\n\n     4.  Original letters received from Prof. Weber and Mr. Hollywood will\nbe forwarded to ATIC by DF after signature by D/I of replies.\n\n     5.  Replies to the three gentlemen are attached.  They have been written\nin the first person from General Samford.\n\n     6.  Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the Daily\nStaff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED\n\n     7.  Because of the professional status of the three correspondents,\nit is strongly recommended that General Samford sign the attached replies.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Smith, Ext. 75990  wh/\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072  [signature]\n     AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110    [signature]\n     AFOIN, Maj Gen Samford, Ext 55613  [signature]\n\n\n\n                        RESTRICTED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "38a90c8d1dd549b27f62a4714cb4884c52ba337ab8a3c01bb2e16bc1f1865672", "output_sha256": "db0b0d93cd0fc70797711bd6833dcce9b19a4f68802d40963328f0735ad8cf15", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:22.191117+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p157", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 157, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\nRECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:                    DATE\n                              17 Sep 52\n     AFOIN-2A             TYPE\n                              Ltrs\nSUMMARY:                                                    SUSPENSE\n                                                   DATE\n                                                   ASGD BY\n                                                   NO\n                                                   DATE RECD\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:                                                        DATE\n     AFOIN                                              17 Sep 52\nFROM:                                                      NO.\n     AFOIN-2A                                              1\nREMARKS:\n\n     The attached letters are forwarded for signature by the Director of\n Intelligence.\n\n\n                              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n                                                        AFOIN No.\n                                                          835\n\nIN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE       OUT\n\n  ✓   AFOIN                  AFOIN-2   B            ASST\n [REDACTED]  AFOIN-X               AFOIN-2A  1943         EXEC\n\n\n      ADMIN                                          ASST\n  ✗   M&R                    AFOIN2B               EXEC         S\n\n\n      AFOIN-1                                        EXEC.        ✓  [ILLEGIBLE]\n                             AFOIN-3\n\n                                                     K.\n                                                   AIR/INT      [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                                          X   ACTION        COORDINATION\nAction Asgd to:       DATE:         Dispatch/Km\nSigned:               DATE:         File:              Date:   9/24/1[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nAFHQ Form 0-88 Previous Editions of the Form are Obsolete                51 25247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7892374017dee227a946b352aa143c81b7e2e4fc9104f85a91b0be53c4784485", "output_sha256": "1433976aab37740ef7fb61dd453fc8819183dcbf57db67252637e3b948fd529e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:24.113928+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p158", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 158, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 23 Sept 52\n\n                    (Unclassified) Staff Study on CIRVIS and\n                         FlyObRpt Procedures\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force        SEP 2 5 1952\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN-2            Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Subject staff study is inclosed for your review since it contains revisions\nwhich affect Project Blue Book.\n\n     2.  Request your comments as soon as possible.\n\n\n1 Incl  (with orig only)              /s/ JOHN G. ERIKSEN\n    Staff Study                       Colonel, USAF\n                                      Chief, Policy and Management Group\n         x382.7 ATIC                  Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                      Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2\n\n    Col W H Smith        Col Uma Adams     Col J G Eriksen\n         /s/                                    When Incl No. 1\n                                           is/are withdrawn (or not attached),\n                                           the Confidential classification\n                                           of this correspondence will be down-\n                                           graded to Unclassified in\n                                           accordance with Par 25b, AFR 205-1.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                    OUT\n                                                 25 SEP 1952\n                                                  DIR/INT\n                                                  HQ USAF\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "413f2c3dfb715d263d95eca1f014e86113c0d7650475fa0f418b8e570982d987", "output_sha256": "676152f4837622372427149d3fc458b1d828c1fa14d76c994e695e4a63544769", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:26.008219+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p159", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 159, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\n23 September 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM\n\n1. To submit a Staff Study for coordination and approval.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n2. It has become increasingly apparent over the past few months that certain revisions are required in JANAP 146(B), Communications Instructions for Reporting Vital Intelligence Sightings while Airborne (CIRVIS).\n\n3. For some time there has existed quite a bit of confusion over the responsibility for evaluating CIRVIS reports, particularly the responsibility of this Headquarters. It has been noticed that very few evaluations have been made by field commands and that this Headquarters has been attempting to furnish ADC the required evaluations. However, these efforts are limited in that the information necessary for an evaluation is normally not readily available here, resulting in an inordinate time loss or, more frequently, the transmittal of an evaluation message which states that no further information is available here.\n\n4. Additionally, the number of reports of unidentified flying objects which have been received over CIRVIS channels during the cyclic flurries of such sightings has given rise to some concern that CIRVIS communication channels may at some time be saturated, thereby providing an excellent opportunity for concealing an air attack which may be mounted against this country.\n\n5. The fact that CIRVIS was restricted to airborne reports was also believed questionable.\n\n6. These factors warranted the preparation of a staff study to examine objectively and completely the adequacy of JANAP 146(B). Since certain aspects of unidentified flying objects reporting are inseparably related to CIRVIS, the study required the inclusion of this subject as well.\n\n7. The attached study was prepared for this purpose and is believed to represent a thorough and objective analysis.\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "066bde40e5a1935192cfedfc6be9de65421218533fc8c55d86e9f15d69a09cbc", "output_sha256": "ef809205fbd2e133485287cb1b82e8f7bb8b6643f01319b4e7e55d8d3129b246", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:27.961562+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p160", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 160, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n     8. Since JANAP 146 (B) is an inter-service publication, coordination must be accomplished with the Navy, Army, JIC and JCEC; the latter has been responsible for publication of JANAP 146.\n\n     9. A DF to ATIC, with a copy of the study inclosed, is attached in order to obtain ATIC's coordination.\n\n     10. R&R's to Director of Operations and to Director of Communications, with copies of the study inclosed, are attached to obtain their coordination.\n\n     11. A letter to CG ADC, with 2 copies of the study inclosed, is attached to obtain ADC's coordination.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED\n\n     12. That the attached study be approved.\n\nCOORDINATION\n        AFOIN-2A2, Col Smith, Ext. 75990 w#/\n        AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072 -[handwritten signature]\n        AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110 28 may [handwritten signature]\n        AFOIN-1, B/Gen Ackerman, Ext. 71079\n        AFOIN, Maj Gen Sanford, Ext. 55613\n\n\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "52d0dbe013b60d159989e32f6e4b146da5a35c5a430a3381927acf287ed600e8", "output_sha256": "75f6fdfbf6f4f1de1985debc20c781c3a32290536dd6344c292547ac2480a982", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:29.576990+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p161", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 161, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET                                    SUSPENSE\n\nORIGIN OF BASIC                    DATE         TYPE         DATE\n\nSUBJECT                                                      ASSIGNED BY\n\n                                                             NUMBER\n\n                                        ROUTING\n\nInitial \"IN\" column to denote review prior to action. Initial \"OUT\" column to denote review of completed action. (X-for action:\nV- for coordination)\n\nIN    OFFICE     OUT    IN    OFFICE     OUT    IN    OFFICE     OUT    IN    OFFICE     OUT\n      AFOIN             OIN-1                  OIN-2                  OIN-3\n      OIN-X             OIN-1X                 OIN-2X                 OIN-3X\n      OIN-X1\n      OIN-X2\n\n\n      CABLES\n      FILE                                                            SR NAVAL OFF\n      DISPATCH                                                        SR ARMY OFF\n\nTO:                                                          DATE\n     AFOIN-X2B(M&R)                                          25 Sept 52\nFROM:                                                        COMMENT NUMBER      1\n     AFOIN-2X\nCOMMENTS (Use reverse, if necessary)\n\n\n     Forwarded for dispatch.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAFHQ  FORM       O-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.                D 6616\n      22 JUL 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f5a06e8438e5084b1b85d54cf58c18d6bb727db3fa9942315335d2b7aa9612d2", "output_sha256": "d3b24d997d5aa9e342a88cd5cef0c52b4680aa7d7379d165506aa191efca8a42", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:31.075568+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p162", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 162, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/71016/cmb\n23 Sept 52\n\n[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Restricted) Project Blue Book, Gun Camera Film\nDept of the Air Force\nHq USAF - AFOIN          SEP 23 1952\n                         Maj Fournet/71016\n\nChief, Air Technical\nIntelligence Center\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Returned herewith is gun camera film taken of an unidentified flying\nobject by the 97th FI Squadron.\n\n     2.  Prints were made of four frames by OSD-OPI and declassified by Security\nReview, OSD.  It is understood that a print of two of these frames will be fur-\nnished TRUE magazine in answer to their request.\n\n                              s/ Donald E. Beebe\n                                  for\n1 Incl:  (W/Orig. only)      WILLIAM A. ADAMS\nRoll 16mm film               COLONEL, USAF\n                             Chief, Topical Division\n                             Deputy Director for Estimates\n     x392.7 ATIC             Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n                         When encl(s) No.  1\n                         is/are withdrawn (or not attached),\n                         the    Secret    classification\n                         of [ILLEGIBLE] document will be down-\n                         graded  Restricted    in\n                         accordance with Par 25e, AFR 205-1.\n\nNO M/R\n\nCOORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A               AFOIN\n\n\n   [signature]           [signature] Cpt.\n        [initials]\n\n\n[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                OUT\n                           26 SEP 1952\n                           DIR/INT\n                           HQ USAF\n                             3999", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "57c26d979b6756fa47042c1ee2172918f7103f0a1b3ecffca2377d66cf7c563f", "output_sha256": "4eb35e89fe373ee262964e4aa50497f9b727e02f42b8670447fc9ee8c0edf005", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:33.200740+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p163", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 163, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/cmb/71016\nwrtn 24 Sept 1952\n\nChief, Air Technical\nIntelligence Center\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nDept of the Air Force\nHq USAF - AFOIN\n24 SEP 1952\nMaj Fournet/71016/cmb\n\n1. Inclosure, received from the Director of Special Investigations, is for\nyour information and retention.\n\n1 Incl: (W/orig only)\nMemo fr Off Spec. Inves.\nre flyobs (in dup.)\n\nS\nWILLIAM A. ADAMS\nColonel, USAF\nChief, Topical Division\nDeputy Director for Estimates\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\nCOUPON DESIGNATION MADE __________\n\nA\nOUT\n6 24 SEP 1952\nONFRNT\nHQ USAF\n\nNO M/R\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2\n\n[signatures]\n\nX 322.7 ATIC\n\nWhen Incl No. 1\n[ILLEGIBLE] opy no.\nConfidential\n[ILLEGIBLE]\nUnclassified\naccordance with Par 25c, AFR 205-1,\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "be09accac26d0518cc475f53e1f18c1b4fa7ddda528ffe429f924976ea92204a", "output_sha256": "be09accac26d0518cc475f53e1f18c1b4fa7ddda528ffe429f924976ea92204a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:34.846108+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p164", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 164, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 24 Sept 52\n\n(Unclassified) Design Proposal from Franz Pankofer\n\n                                    SEP 24 1952\nExecutive,\nDirector of Research & Development, DCS/D\nAttn: Major Forsman                              1\nDeputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O    Maj Fournet/71016/cmb\n\n     1.  Inclosed correspondence and model is forwarded as a matter of primary\ninterest.\n\n     2.  No reply to Mr. Pankofer has been made by this office.\n\n               #095, Pankofer, Franz\n\n4 Incls:                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Capt C.B. McKinney        Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 11 Aug 52                    Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Mr. F. Pankofer           Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 20 Jul 52                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Trans. of Incl. 3\n  4. Cardboard model of \"flying saucer\"\n     (hand-carried by Maj Fournet, 18 Sept 52)\n\n          COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\nNO M/R\n\nCOORDINATION:          AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n          Col W.H. Smith              [ILLEGIBLE]\n               [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f7224c489ff4d01ad3f488571de2ac5135d4a433b304417e852595b9e1931a8a", "output_sha256": "f7224c489ff4d01ad3f488571de2ac5135d4a433b304417e852595b9e1931a8a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:36.572529+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p165", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 165, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION                              Wtrn 22 Sept 1952\n\n\n        (Unclassified) Information for Preparation of Reply to Senator Monroney\n\n        Dir of Legislation and Liaison\n        OSAF                                          SEP 23 1952\n        ATTN: Mr. J. O. Crawford\nXXXXX                                               Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nFROM:  Deputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O   AFOIN-2A2\n\n        1.  Correspondence from Mr. Martin V. Walsh and related referrals are returned\n    herewith.\n\n        2.  Since appropriate comments regarding aircraft accidents have been made by\n    [REDACTED] in their reply to Mr. Walsh, it should suffice to confine our reply to the\n    \"flying saucer\" aspects of his theory.  Mr. Walsh's \"theory\" is typical of the many\n    completely amateurish proposals received on the subject, none of which has any\n    scientific basis except the free use of scientific or pseudo-scientific terms.  It\n    is therefore suggested that the reply include a comment, substantially as follows:\n\n            (Unclassified) In its investigation and analysis of the \"flying saucer\"\n        reports, the Air Force has found no evidence whatsoever which would substantiate\n        the proposed theory.  We are grateful, however, for his efforts to assist us.\n\n\n                                    x 095. Monroney, Senator\n\n    1 Incl (w/orig only)\n      Ltr fr CAA dtd 4 Sep 52\n      w/cc ltr to Sen Mike              S/ WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n      Monroney fr Martin V.                Colonel, USAF\n      Walsh dtd 23 Aug 52                  Chief, Policy\n                                           Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                           Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A             AFOIN-2\n\n     al W H Smith                  [ILLEGIBLE]        [ILLEGIBLE]     H/c by\n          5f                                                         Mrs Glover\n                                                                     23 Sep 52\n\n\n                               RESTRICTED\n                            SECURITY INFORMATION\n                                    1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "25f4af48b7905872e09ce58670bab46e35390b6c6dc73f129f3d0cdaf14bc0b3", "output_sha256": "d265619ef52f2be0907f8708c55d36f510b5d67880e32a8337786f48b3e16d46", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:38.955871+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p166", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 166, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET                                    SUSPENSE\n\nORIGIN OF BASIC          DATE        TYPE         DATE\nDept of Commerce - CAA   4 Sept 52   Ltr          22 SEPTEMBER 1952\n\nSUBJECT                                           ASSIGNED BY\n                                                  M.E. SMITH  [ILLEGIBLE]\n   (U) Information for Preparation of Reply to Senator Monroney\n                                                  NUMBER\n                                                  SAFLL 23530 H\n\n                              ROUTING\n\nInitial \"IN\" column to denote review prior to action. Initial \"OUT\" column to denote review of completed action. (X-for action:\nV- for coordination)\n\nIN   OFFICE    OUT   IN   OFFICE   OUT   IN   OFFICE    OUT   IN   OFFICE   OUT\n     AFOIN           OIN.1              OIN-2                 OIN-3\n     OIN-X           OIN-1X        X    OIN-2X               OIN-3X\n     OIN-X1                        X    OIN-2A   [ILLEGIBLE]\n     OIN-X2                        X    OIN-2A2  [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\n     CABLES\nM    FILE                                                     SR NAVAL OFF\nX    DISPATCH [ILLEGIBLE]                                     SR ARMY OFF\n\nTO:                                               DATE\n   AFOIN-2                                        22 September 1952\n\nFROM:                                             COMMENT NUMBER\n   AFOIN-2A                                       1\n\nCOMMENTS (Use reverse, if necessary)\n\n\n   Suspense  SAFLL        R&R for approval and signature.\n\n   Date  23 SEPTEMBER 1952\n\n[ILLEGIBLE]\n\nAFHQ  FORM       0-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.        D 8616\n      22 JUL 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c16f9e11d1de08a36ba23cefa0374f5210b8649c5cd2b1969fd097d7395d2dc7", "output_sha256": "fa72d4c3495200d9ec773e98fdbc8838abeca8c181414b98a975244d475c1014", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:41.989713+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p167", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 167, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                          AFOIN-2A2\n                                          Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\n                                          Wrtn 16 Sept 52\n\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2             SEP 2 2 1952\nWright-Patterson AFB                                    Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information, appropriate action and retention.\nAll concern sightings of objects.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made by this office.\n\n\n                                   6\n\n8 Incls (W/orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr A. Korch                     Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 20 Aug 52                       Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr D. Anda                      Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 4 Sept 52                       Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Mrs M. Cauldren\n     dtd 1 Sept 52                 x322.7 ATIC\n  4. Ltr fr A.R. Bernard\n     dtd 28 Aug 52\n  5. Ltr fr G.O. Stromberg\n     dtd 4 Sept 52\n  6. Ltr fr J.E. O'Brien\n     dtd 29 Jul 52\n  7. Ltr fr D. Dutton &\n     D. Barry, dtd 2 Sept 52\n  8. Ltr fr Mrs Norris Watson\n     dtd 3 Sept 52\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n        CdWHSmith                  GMMerlelgt.\n\n\n                    [REDACTED]\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "93464fc45f0d53ae144aed7abaeaa2b82799a0e2d095da7dc68e7620b5addab9", "output_sha256": "3049cd3f29288ce7051f44b021c7c74b4f5454a6735df6fc9c6eb94e8941172f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:44.116354+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p168", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 168, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\n18 September 1952\n\nAFOIN-2A2\n                                          SEP 2 2 1952\n\nSUBJECT:  Motion Pictures of Unidentified Objects in Air\n\nTO:       Commanding General\n          Ogden Air Materiel Area\n          Hill Air Force Base, Utah\n\n\n     Reference letter from Chief Photographer Delbert C. Newhouse,\n\nU. S. N. dated 11 August 1952, with inclosed movie film, and your\n\nfirst Indorsement dated 28 August 1952.  Receipt is acknowledged.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n     x320.2 AMC               Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n     [signature]                [signature]\n        JB\n\n                                          22 SEP 1952\n                                          DI/INT\n                                          HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "997c43bd5f331a8389104e2cedba020a78034ca3d21d30e15513ce3c1cec6dea", "output_sha256": "997c43bd5f331a8389104e2cedba020a78034ca3d21d30e15513ce3c1cec6dea", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:45.587517+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p169", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 169, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(U) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          SEP 2 2 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A             Maj Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Forwarded for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  The writer has been notified by the Army that her letter was being referred\nto the USAF.  Additional correspondence with Mrs. Evans is not mandatory.\n\n\n1 Incl.                              S\n  Ltr fr Mrs. E. Evans              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  dtd 25 Jul 52                     Colonel, USAF\n                                    Chief, Topical Division\n                                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n\n\n                                         OUT\n                                      G 22 SEP 1952\n                                        DIAINT\n                                        HQ USAF\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A  RESTRICTED\n[signatures]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8f93c04a27e10af668195e9471d57e1ad7946987a1ff26f1d5c92ffe95745aba", "output_sha256": "941ec6be8fb86eaa91c5bcf50b9b39b9fc7835d6d084724ab58f0f0b1d12af69", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:47.371323+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p170", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 170, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 18 Sept 52\n\nSEP 2 2 1952\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2          Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosures are for your information and retention.  All involve theories\nor suggestions related to the Project.\n\n     2.  It will be noted that a reply to Dr. Vinal was made by the Army and a\nreply to Mr. Glasser was made by General Bradley's office.  Further correspondence\nwith these individuals is therefore not mandatory.  However, it is suggested that\nacknowledgment be made to Mr. Talkes (letter attached to Dr. Vinal's).\n\n     3.  Previous correspondence from Mr. Peirce and other documents related to\nhis case were forwarded to you by DF dated 18 Aug 1952.\n\n               v\n          x 322.1 ATIC\n\n4 Incls (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. 1st Ind fr OCSigO dtd           Colonel, USAF\n        28 Aug 52 with bsc ltr       Chief, Topical Division\n        dtd 25 Aug 52 w/Incls        Deputy Director for Estimates\n  2. Ltr fr Mr. T.J.H. Peirce        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n        dtd 26 Aug 52\n  3. CC of ltr fr Mr. J.E. Perry\n        to the FBI dtd 22 Aug 52\n  4. Ltr fr M.M. Glasser dtd 29\n        Aug 52 w/cc of reply to\n        M.M. Glasser w/attachments\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n     [signature]                    [signature]\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e8b246137d8deccd1625a508cf6b1533ab5b6f3992705984fa18c849f8cb184c", "output_sha256": "7b686ae6b2e4061fee9124dae3316aa6996560462357c76a6612537320249bb6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:49.557076+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p171", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 171, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                          AFOIN-2A2\n                                          Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n                                          Wrtn 15 Sept 52\n\n\n              (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force    SEP 19 1952\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN-2        Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are for your information, appropriate action and\nretention.\n\n     2.  Replies to all letters have been prepared.\n\n     3.  Mr. Forney was advised that you would contact Dr. Buttolph for any further\ndetails which you may require.  Request advice of the results of any tests which\nyou may conduct using the sample submitted by Mr. Forney.\n\n\n3 Incls                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr James C. Crockett        Colonel, USAF\n        Col, USA (Ret) dtd 2 Aug 52  Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Charles Forney dtd       Deputy Director for Estimates\n        30 July 52                   Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n  3. Ltr fr Dr. Leopold Heinemann\n        dtd 30 July 52          X322.1 ATIC\n\n\n\n\nNO M/R necessary.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n[signature]                        [signature]\n\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7fe7abc7b384ddc759a37d8aa699f9b5c85af3003a9fa370a8c8a8fbded96c42", "output_sha256": "7fe7abc7b384ddc759a37d8aa699f9b5c85af3003a9fa370a8c8a8fbded96c42", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:51.324003+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p172", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 172, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 16 Sept 1952\n\n\n\n\nColonel James C. Crockett\nDirector of Civil Defense\nTerritory of Alaska\nBox 2747\nJuneau, Alaska\n\nDear Colonel Crockett:\n\n     Your very interesting letter to the Secretary of\nDefense dated 2 August 1952 has been referred to us\nfor consideration.\n\n     We have forwarded it to our Intelligence analysts\nfor very careful study and incorporation into our\nanalysis of \"flying saucers\".\n\n     We are most grateful to you for bringing these\nfacts to our attention.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2     Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n   al W.H. Smith\n      [signature]\n                              [signature]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d251484ea0b9b0f47ce587829bf8be340b2564bb0d88768c13756a94ce63f9c4", "output_sha256": "eaaffddab1c7e2039faf2963c3fea7361cec1720cd4ccc081d0a1782982e7eb1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:52.573176+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p173", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 173, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 16 Sept 52\n\n\n\n\n                                          SEP 1 1952\nMr. Charles Forney\nPresident, Sani-Ray Corporation\nP.O. Box 478\nNorfolk 1, Virginia\n\nDear Mr. Forney:\n\n     General Samford has asked me to convey his gratitude to you for your interesting letter of 30 July 1952.\n\nWe have referred it to our analysts for study and\n\nexperimentation along with instructions to contact\n\nDr. Buttolph for any further details which they may\n\nrequire.\n\n     We sincerely appreciate your efforts on our behalf.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                         WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Topical Division\n                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n        al W.H. Smith                [signature]\n              jf\n\n\n                                        OUT\n                                  G 22 SEP 1952\n                                    DIR/INT\n                                    HQ USAF\n\nAFOIN COORDINATION COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fb6aac17218ea500c8ecc8fbe4e3914c588d8669fb80252ddd89c5883983778b", "output_sha256": "6449a93d0205d94cc3fb88b96c669516fe8f8906d96e8e6d5447c09a25e86cd8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:54.056049+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p174", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 174, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 16 Sep 52\n\n\n                                          SEP 19 1952\n\n\nDr. Leopold Heinemann\n140 West 94th Street\nNew York 25, N. Y.\n\nDear Dr. Heinemann:\n\n     General Samford has asked me to convey his thanks\n\nto you for your interesting letter of 30 July 1952.\n\n     The ideas which you have submitted are sincerely\n\nappreciated and are being given our careful considera-\n\ntion.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n\n\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n[signature]                    [signature]\n\nAFOIN COORDINATION COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f383b9462ef87e29010f1f3352edf63a6f8e3ef690e3887a1808e160462af31c", "output_sha256": "f383b9462ef87e29010f1f3352edf63a6f8e3ef690e3887a1808e160462af31c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:55.437622+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p175", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 175, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n                                        19 Sept 1952\n\n\n              (Restricted) Results of Lab Analysis of Cap\n              Belonging to D. S. DesVergers\n                                        19 SEP 1952\nChief, Air Technical     Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center      Hq USAF - AFOIN-2      Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Report of lab analysis performed by the Federal Bureau of Investigation\non Mr. DesVergers' cap is inclosed for your information and retention.  The cap\nis also returned herewith.\n\n     2.  Since it was necessary to mark and cut the cap for analysis, it is con-\nsidered inadvisable to return it to Mr. DesVergers.  It is believed preferable\nto offer a replacement for it if there existed an agreement that it would be\nreturned.\n\n                              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\n                         S\n2 Incls                       WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Lab rept by FBI          Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 3 Sep 52             Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Cap which was            Deputy Director for Estimates\n     analyzed (w/orig only)   Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n                    X-095. Des Vergers D. S.\n\nNo M/R necessary              When incl(s) No. 1&2\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2      AFOIN-2A    is are withdrawn (or not attached),\n                                          the Confidential classification\n    [signature]               [signature] of this correspondence will be down-\n                                          graded to Restricted        in\n                                          accordance with Par 25a, AFR 205-1.\n\n\n          H/C - by Capt. Mc Govern\n                  (fr ATIC)\n                  19 Sept 52\n\n\n              CONFIDENTIAL\n              SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6f9ca30e87ff41da00c7a91dfbd3f89a2d419fa1fa0069d29059905d71c2ca94", "output_sha256": "8b2c2551f54fe341e140ced7415567b3b5643c03db3cf7777a04a5226032e467", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:10:57.679352+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p176", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 176, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY                    CONFIDENTIAL                    DECLASSIFIED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION              Authority NW 34267\n                         of the                       By  BLT      NARA, Date 7/16/21\n                          FBI\n                       LABORATORY\n                                                          VIA LIAISON\n                    FEDERAL BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION\n                                                       September 3, 1952\nTO:  Directorate of Special Investigations\n     The Inspector General\n     Department of the Air Force          Attention:  Mr. Gilbert R. Levy\n     The Pentagon                                     Chief, Counter Intelligence\n     Washington, D. C.                                                  Division\n\n          Following is the report of the FBI Laboratory giving the results of\n     examinations conducted on evidence received from your office.\n\nRE:  Unidentified Flying Object Allegedly          s/J. Edgar Hoover\n     Sighted by Mr. D. S. Desvergers,             JOHN EDGAR HOOVER, Director\n     West Palm Beach, Florida\n\n                                              Your File No.  24-185\n                                              FBI File No.\n     Examination requested by:  Addressee     Lab. No.      PC-33720 DE\n\n     Reference:                Letter dated 8-26-52\n\n     Examination requested:    Chemical Analyses\n\n     Specimens:\n          Q1   Cap which Mr. Desvergers was wearing at the time of the alleged\n               incident.\n\nRESULTS OF EXAMINATION\n\n          In answer to your specific inquiry, you are advised that the areas\n     surrounding the three burned holes in the cap were examined for any residues\n     which might indicate the nature of the incendiary material causing the burns,\n     but no such residues were found.  Tests conducted on the sweatband of Q1\n     indicate that the residue from a glowing ember used to burn a hole in the cloth\n     was easily dislodged and removed by handling and \"roughing\" the burned area.\n\n          Some observations made during the examination of Q1 may be of interest\n     to you.  The major portion of the top side of the cap bill as well as the area\n     surrounding the yellow and black emblem or insignia and the insignia itself have\n     been subjected to the singeing action of a flame.  It is of interest to note\n     that the singeing on these areas is not at all uniform as might be expected\n     if the cap had been subjected to a single shot of a \"red blob\" of a fire of\n     some kind.  The fact that the front edge of the cap bill is more severely\n     scorched or singed than other portions of the cap suggests that the singeing\n     could not have taken place when Mr. D. S. Desvergers was fired upon from a\n     position almost vertically above him.  When the cap is observed from the front\n     and left edge of the insignia and the fold in the blue cloth in the surrounding\n\n\nEnclosure                          -1-\n                         CONFIDENTIAL  (continued next page)\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n                                                                          COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c1408508bc930750a3a7df27a863f0941e687433bfc5b3678aa9bfa1e143b3e7", "output_sha256": "cf5fb1f0725d8727f5bba3b2b9f43bb3b14741ed3f755951524ed673281f016f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:01.637772+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p177", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 177, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n\nareas are examined, the absence of singeing under the fold suggests the\npossibility that the cap was not being worn on the head when the singeing\ntook place.  It was noted that this fold \"smoothed out\" when the cap was\nplaced on the head.\n\n        As to what might have caused the burned holes in the cap, you are\nadvised that on the cap bill there was noted an area of particular signifi-\ncance which has been circled with a pencil mark.  In this circle is a\nburned area approximately 1/32\" in diameter.  It is believed to be too\nsmall to have been caused singularly and intentionally by Mr. Desvergers.\nThe appearance of the small burned spot suggests the possibility that a small\nglowing ember of some kind, very hot but containing a small amount of heat,\nbecause of its size, fell on the cap bill, causing burns in two of the\nthreads after which the glowing ember cooled off and fell off the cap bill.\n\n        Specimen Q1 is being returned to you herewith.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                    -2-\n\n                          CONFIDENTIAL\n                        SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a0d4d1c25c11d40788d271f2acb4b3f02a6fc4f00839f4fdb18f34c67e237091", "output_sha256": "bc2823edf3548bfe98dafcf87c25f5d1bcdf3a94b50e41683b6aa7810ca5f73c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:03.023353+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p178", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 178, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Unclassified)  Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force  SEP 10 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN              Maj Fournet/fn/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                         AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are for your information, appropriate action and\nretention.\n\n     2.  Each of these letters has been reviewed by this office for possible\napplication to the project.  Replies have been prepared expressing USAF\nappreciation.\n\n     3.  It is believed that the ideas presented by Professor Weber and Mr.\nHollywood warrant your very careful consideration and study.\n\n\n                              S\n3 Incls.                      WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1.  Ltr fr Mr. G. Francis   Colonel, USAF\n      Nauheimer dtd 29 Jul 52  Chief, Topical Division\n  2.  Ltr fr Mr. John M.      Deputy Director for Estimates\n      Hollywood dtd 1 Aug 52   Directorate of Intelligence\n  3.  Ltr fr Prof. John C.\n      Weber dtd 2 Aug 1952\n\n           x 322.7 ATIC\n\n\n\n\n                                         OUT\n                                    G 26 SEP 1952\n                                      DPINT\n                                      HQ USAF\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2       AFOIN-2A        AFOIN-2\n\nW.H. Smith      [signature]      X      RESTRICTED\nCol USAF                                SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e8e9758872d3b7d11d61174b92d87c9d6ce0d15301bb5454a9e4943e1b9e3d35", "output_sha256": "e8e9758872d3b7d11d61174b92d87c9d6ce0d15301bb5454a9e4943e1b9e3d35", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:05.014414+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p179", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 179, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\nGLARE RESEARCH INSTITUTE\n\nDiscoverer                                    Office of the Director\n                                              6527 SO. Seeley Avenue\nCONTRA BLUE RAYS                              Chicago 36, Illinois\n\n                                    July 29th, 1952\n\nMaj. Gen. John Samford,\nHeadquarters G-2, Air Force,\nDepartment of Defense,\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\nDear Sir:-\n\n        Regarding the recent reports of the so called flying saucers, I am quite\nsure that the hoax will be exposed by telling you that this is nothing more than\nthe silver iodide used in artificial rainmaking. This is especially true if the\nsilver iodide came in contact with radioactive clouds or so called thunderclouds.\n\n        The solution of this hoax is quite simple, if you will check your records\nyou will find that flying saucers were first seen about the time when silver\niodide came into usage for artificial rainmaking. Again, silver is a reflective\nagency and will reflect all types of light, which accounts for the various hues\nreported by sky gazers. Again, silver iodide, if radioactive or ionized by an\nelectrical cloud will become fluorescent, which accounts for flyers being unable\nto overtake the so called flying saucers, and their habit of disappearing.\n\n        Of course, we must eliminate such reports of flying saucers as were accountable\nby balloons, foo-fighters, meteorites, and the person who just calls up a newspaper\nwith the hope of getting his name in the papers. Also to be disqualified are such\nreports as to ascertain that they are interplanetary space ships. If it were at\nall possible for another planet to send aircraft of any type to our atmosphere,\nit would simply burn up the same as a meteorite and such space ship remains would\nbe found the same as meteorites. As far as I know, no such wreckage has ever been\nfound.\n\n\n                                    Respectfully yours,\n\n\n                                         s/\n                                    G. Francis Nauheimer,\n                                         Director.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                            C O P Y\n\nIncl 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2d94f790d396fc6a0b50d9808f33240376dc3c555984102b12b04d2c668870ff", "output_sha256": "c8265d856d0f3f6adb8a6fe2317aab76e6f5aadf8af7af198b2422406a353856", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:07.230549+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p180", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 180, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n                    CBS LABORATORIES\n            A Division of Columbia Broadcasting\n                      System, Inc.\n        485 Madison Avenue, New York 22, New York - Plaza 5-2000\n\n\n                                              August 1, 1952\n\n\n     Major General James A. Samford\n     Chief of Intelligence\n     Pentagon Building\n     Arlington, Virginia\n\n     Dear Sir:\n\n          In connection with \"flying saucer\" newspaper accounts of\n     observations on the search radar system at the Washington\n     National Airport, it occurred to me that the described be-\n     havior could possibly be accounted for in the following manner:\n\n     High power, narrow beam fire control radar systems of the usual\n     type might conceivably, under unusual atmospheric conditions,\n     create enough ionization along points on the beam in the upper\n     atmosphere to allow the return of an appreciable echo to the\n     search radar system from such points.  The apparent motion would\n     be quite haphazard, following whatever the fire control radar\n     operator does in directing the beam.\n\n     This hypothesis is unattractive for several reasons:  Firstly,\n     the power required for such an effect is many times greater\n     than that put out by the usual radar.  Secondly, such echoes\n     would presumably come from ionospheric heights and therefore\n     could not appear at ranges of a few miles from the search radar,\n     as was reported.  Thirdly, it seems unlikely that a coincident\n     visual effect of any conspicuous magnitude would be produced.\n\n     In spite of this, I am offering this suggestion in the belief\n     that if considerable time, money and effort is being devoted to\n     this problem, it might be worthwhile trying the relatively simple\n     experiment of having a powerful fire control radar sweep out\n     certain simple patterns to see if they can be detected on the\n     search radar system, preferably at a time when \"flying saucer\"\n     echoes are being observed.\n\n                                        Very truly yours,\n\n                                        s/\n                                        John M. Hollywood\n                                        Engineer\n\n     JMH/bas                                              COPY\n\nIncl 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "e9e535e86b1b43ee08ff2c24215a8fdc4b7546de055aa1e58096b18c37bb4688", "output_sha256": "6a95f7d6a727a305fd79f7c937843bcd041f76f6ee7f19c3b4acc52dfe481bd7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:09.448820+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p181", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 181, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "C O P Y\n\n                    THE UNIVERSITY OF WISCONSIN\n                       College of Engineering\n                            Madison 6\n\n    Department of\n    Electrical Engineering\n\n                                                    August 2, 1952\n\n\n\n\n            Maj. Gen. John A. Samford\n            Air Force Director of Intelligence\n            Washington, D. C.\n\n            Dear Sir:\n\n                    I should like to present to you what I believe to\n            be a tenable theory as to the origin and nature of the\n            phenomena popularly known as \"flying saucers\".\n\n                    It has been amply demonstrated that electro-magnetic\n            radiation of sufficient power density is capable of\n            ionizing gas at low pressure. Upon deionization, the\n            gas emits radiation of characteristic wave lengths, some\n            of which lie in the visible spectrum. Further, it is\n            known that radar equipment can detect ionized gas, such as\n            northern lights, or charged water droplets, such as appear\n            in thunderclouds.\n\n                    I believe that ionization of disc-shaped segments of\n            air in the upper atmosphere may be caused by beams from a\n            radar transmitter held in a fixed position or slowly traversed,\n            instead of the usual sweeping motion.\n\n                    To verify the possibility, I propose in the very near\n            future to conduct an experiment. A glass sphere containing\n            air at atmosphere pressure will be exposed to radiation of a\n            known wave length and power density. The pressure in the\n            sphere will then be reduced until ionization occurs. The\n            screen of a separate radar transmitter-receiver will also\n            be observed to note whether the change in the condition of\n            the air is detectable by radar.\n\n                                                Very truly yours,\n\n                                                    s/\n                                                John C. Weber\n                                                Assoc. Prof. of E. E.\n\n            2007 Engineering\n\n                                                                    C O P Y\n\nIncl 3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ab1ea7bf12a30666e42448e5d5c5229247aaaaae0c9e10e68d567f9551e85c3b", "output_sha256": "ba3bb79353eb6dd54a4b221a0ca779e80a9bae3e83a9cbbba8b326fd1f25414f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:11.781181+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p182", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 182, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "DECLASSIFIED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force     SEP 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN            Maj Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                      AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are forwarded for your information and retention.\nAll concern sightings of unidentified flying objects or \"experiences\" believed\nrelated thereto.\n\n     2.  No acknowledgments or replies have been made by this office.  However,\nit will be noted that the Civil Aeronautics Administration has replied to Pfc.\nHitchcock (Incl 1).\n\n\n22 Incls (w/orig only)              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n   (See Attached Sheet)             Colonel, USAF\n                                    Chief, Topical Division\n                                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n\n        x322.7 ATIC\n              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\n\n\n\nM/R not required.\n\n   COORDINATION:   AFOIN-2A2       AFOIN-2A\n\n        WH/enie/ty           [signature]\n        Col USAF\n\n                                         A\n                                        OUT\n                                    6 22 SEP 1952\n                                      DIPRINT\n                                      HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c4c95e092e2cf9abffcbac5e357a6e71e640c3f78bc99de2a9802a7c0397eaa8", "output_sha256": "86f9da81033f3de64c4f75f7c78d3eeb9fe92a7309358fba0deab71160410ed7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:13.418718+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p183", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 183, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "INCLOSURES\n\n22 Incls\n   1. Ltr to Pfc Hitchcock frm Office of Aviation Information, dtd Aug 20,52,\n      w/ltr frm Pfc Hitchcock, dtd 11 Aug 52.\n   2. Ltr frm R.J. Blackman, dtd 18 Aug 52, Stover, Mo.\n   3. Ltr frm Mansfield W. Williams, dtd 19 Aug 52, to Sec. Finletter, w/Incl.\n   4. Santa Barbara News-Press clipping, dtd Aug 17, 1952, Titled, \"Happy\n      Says He Saw One, Too,\"\n   5. Ltr dtd 16 Aug 52, frm (Mrs. John F) Lucile S. Janssen, Richmond, Calif.\n   6. Ltr dtd 17 Aug 52, frm Henry B. Lee III, Madera Beach, Fla.\n   7. Ltr dtd 17 Aug 52, frm J. Pat Farrell, Austin, Texas.\n   8. Ltr dtd 30 Jul 52, frm Bert Runnell, Northford, Conn.\n   9. Clipping frm \"The Bay City Times\"\n  10. Ltr dtd 11 Aug 52, frm Gerald G. McKelvey, Waynesboro, Penna.\n  11. Ltr dtd 15 Aug 52, frm John Morrissey, K.C. Mo.\n  12. Ltr dtd 20 Aug 52, frm Gore Vidal, Barrytown, N.Y.\n  13. Ltr dtd 20 Aug 52, frm Steve Davis, La Grange, Ill.\n  14. Ltr dtd 22 Aug 52, frm Lloyd Geisness, Alexandria, Minnesota\n  15. Ltr dtd ? frm Robert J. Hummel, Toledo, Ohio\n  16. Ltr dtd 29 Aug 52, frm Seth Pope, Downingtown, Pa.\n  17. Ltr dtd 29 Aug 52, frm Mrs. Bessie Colton Johnson, Detroit, Mich.\n  18. Ltr dtd 28 Aug 52? frm Richard O. Nelson, Laurel, Mont.\n  19. Ltr dtd 26 Aug 52, frm Maj. John J. Phillips., (retd.) Temple City, Calif.\n  20. Ltr dtd 3 Aug 52, frm Barry T. Jensen, Ph.D., Hyattsville, Md.\n  21. Ltr frm Sam Singer, East Chicago, Indiana.\n  22. Ltr dtd 29 Aug 52, frm Roy F. Hall, Capt. U.S. Army, Retd, w/ltr frm\n      Mrs. Cletus Dodd, Dallas, Texas.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "32c74091a738066725c117460e1a84d4aaa081934983d133f1a1df28ccadb270", "output_sha256": "a7196e56b4117282438ee5c929d141a6c7554c50a0524da2d5621da03c23b7f2", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:16.389258+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p184", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 184, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force    SEP 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN          MAJ Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The in