 Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Uncl) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force    SEP 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN           Maj Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                    AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letter with attachments is forwarded for your information\nand retention.\n\n     2.  Reply expressing USAF appreciation has been made by AFOIN-X.\n\n                                    5\n1 Incl.                        WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Ltr dtd 2 Aug 52, frm        Colonel, USAF\n  D. Jesch, Grants Pass, Oregon  Chief, Topical Division\n  w/incls                      Deputy Director for Estimates\n                               Director of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\nM/R not required.\n\nCOORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n  W.H. Fournet                  [ILLEGIBLE]\n  Col USAF                      SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f67c06644d009b3d36a556266cc5f015d86ebe9a680d7c6cbc952a099d0818a7", "output_sha256": "f67c06644d009b3d36a556266cc5f015d86ebe9a680d7c6cbc952a099d0818a7", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:22.514674+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p187", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 187, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 15 Sept 1952\n\n(U) Material for Project Blue Book          SEP 16 1952\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2          Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are for your information and retention.  They were\nreferred to this office by the Adjutant General, US Army.\n\n     2.  Replies have not yet been made to Mr. Mones and Mr. McHaney.  However,\nthe Army notified Mr. Inghram that his letter was being referred to the Air Force,\nand further correspondence with him is therefore not mandatory.\n\n                                    S\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n3. Incls                      Colonel, USAF\n   1. Ltr fr Mr. A.H. Mones   Chief, Topical Division\n      dtd 30 July 1952        Deputy Director for Estimates\n   2. Ltr fr Mr. Orin W. McHaney    Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n      dtd 14 Aug 1952\n   3. Ltr fr Mr. Joseph W. Inghram\n      dtd 5 Aug 1952\n\n\nNo M/R Necessary.\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2               AFOIN-2A\n\n& [signature]               [signature]\n\n                              OUT\n                         6 16 SEP 1952\n                           DIRINT\n                           HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "47cd5d4ea6323e218233c7f751ca18cee58d037af04620129f095cb14fede08a", "output_sha256": "47cd5d4ea6323e218233c7f751ca18cee58d037af04620129f095cb14fede08a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:24.389581+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p188", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 188, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[REDACTED] 8613                    [REDACTED]\n         SECURITY INFORMATION                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force      SEP 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           HQ USAF - AFOIN            Maj Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                     AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n    1.  Inclosures are forwarded for your information, appropriate action and\nretention.\n\n    2.  Request preparation of appropriate indorsements acknowledging receipt.\n\n\n2 Incls.                                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Ltr fr Pinecastle AFB                  Colonel, USAF\n     dtd 23 Jul 52 w/ Inds                  Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Ltr fr Bolling AFB                     Deputy Director for Estimates\n     dtd 14 Aug 52 w/1 Incl                 Directorate of Intelligence\n     ltr, 4th Dist. OSI, dtd\n     4 Aug 52\n\n\n                                       COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n                              ✓\n                              x 322.7 ATIC\n\n\nCOORDINATION:    AFOIN-2A2      AFOIN-2A\n                                                    OUT\n                                                19 SEP 1952\n   [ILLEGIBLE signatures]                         DURANT\n   Col USAF.                                    HQ USAF\n\n\n              [REDACTED] 8613               [REDACTED]\n                                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d27042ed0f9b40b5766c22b4d0e21cb47b30e811301a19f3699e429994c7d020", "output_sha256": "fee004be9d7973b1a14832613e9a3f18de0fd32bed29821701248877b052314d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:26.204809+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p189", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 189, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 13 Sept 52\n\n                    SEP 16 1952\n\nMr. J. W. Pennington\nRoute 1, Box 132\nMobile, Alabama\n\nDear Mr. Pennington:\n\n     Your recent letter concerning unidentified flying objects\nhas been received by this Headquarters, and the ideas which\nyou submitted are receiving our careful consideration.\n\n     We appreciate your interest and efforts to assist us.\nHowever, we don't wish to impose on your generosity any\nfurther and will attempt to render the suggested interpre-\ntations ourselves.  Many thanks, though, for your kind offer\nof additional assistance.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              JOHN T. MATTHEWS, Captain, USAF\n\n                              JOHN J. MORROW\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\nNo M/R necessary.\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A     AFOIN-2\n\n     Col W Wolfe    [signature]  J. Matthews Capt\n\nAFOIN COORDINATION COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "43ed95356f92e1cfe374bf8b7f83d5ae6ab2cbccacc95d0ef459d1f0592899ae", "output_sha256": "7021ef8bca521e244e8a8bf2a7baa439904bb25a28e597808cdfd5be239a0c5c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:27.708939+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p190", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 190, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\nRECORD OF STAFF CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST\nFROM:                    DATE\n        AFOIN-2A2        15 Sept 52\n                         SUBJECT\n                         Non-mil ltr\n\n        Non-mil ltr to Mr. J.W. Pennington,\n        Mobile, Alabama.\n\n                                              SUSPENSE\n                                         DATE\n                                         ACOD BY\n                                         NO\n                                         DATE REC'D\n\n                         SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nTO:     AFOIN-2                                    15 Sept 52\nFROM:   AFOIN-2A                              NO.  1\nREMARKS:                          Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n\n        Ltr for approval and dispatch.\n\n\n                         AFOIN-2A\n\n\n\n\n  OFFICE  OUT   IN    OFFICE    OUT      IN    OFFICE   OUT\n  AFOIN              AFOIN-2   JDm\n  AFOIN-T            AFOIN-2   1363\n                     AFOIN-2A2\n\n\n         ADMIN                            ASS'T\n  X      R & R          AFOIN-2B         EXEC\n\n                                          ASS'T\n                                          EXEC\n\n         AFOIN-2\n                         [ILLEGIBLE]      RECD\n\n                                          AIR/INT\n\n                                    Action    Coordination\nAction Asgd To:          Date:      Dispatch:\n                                    Class. Auth:\nSigned:                  Date:      Prior:        Date:\n\nAFHQ Form 0-06 Previous Editions of this Form are obsolete.          FL 25267\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "8a209804af5c5bb517f416f02df07ab5c9dfc7b4e67b3e6053f7e833ef4216e8", "output_sha256": "2a6fc784ec1a57b3f09d2484b6da9094f78ebd7b6572e436e2beef7de6385002", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:29.477206+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p191", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 191, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2/ Maj Fournet/fh/71016\n                    wrtn 16 Sep 52\n\n\n                    [REDACTED]\n               SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n\n               (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          SEP 16 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN           Maj Fournet/fh/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                         AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n\n     1.  Inclosed correspondence is forwarded for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  Request acknowledgment of receipt by indorsement to basic letter.\n\n\n1 Incl                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Rpt of U/I flyobs,               Colonel, USAF\n  w/2 Incls - statements           Chief, Topical Division\n  re subj.                         Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                   Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n              ✓\n           x322.7 ATIC\n\n\n               COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ___________\n\n\n\n\n                                        OUT\n                                    18 SEP 1952\n                                     CANNET\n                                     HQ USAF\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2                   AFOIN-2A\n\nW H Smith                   [ILLEGIBLE]\nCol USAF\n\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n               SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "33c85e9bf5b514e33b3f91b495d5e09991ddb16a5b831375bdba92fb3bfb5dba", "output_sha256": "33c85e9bf5b514e33b3f91b495d5e09991ddb16a5b831375bdba92fb3bfb5dba", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:31.179855+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p192", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 192, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2 Maj Fournet/fh/71016\n             wrtn 16 Sep 52\n\nAFOIN-2A2                                    16 September 1952\n\n\nMrs. Nellie T. Dull\n Route 3\nStaunton, Virginia\n\nDear Mrs. Dull:\n\n        We wish to assure you that the contents of your letter,\ndated 1 August 1952, were not divulged to anyone outside of\nAir Force Intelligence and that we treat all information such\nas you submitted as strictly confidential. Therefore, the\nconcern expressed in yours of 12 August 1952 is unfounded.\n\n        Mr. Scott's announcement of his theory at about the\nsame time that you corresponded with us was merely a coinci-\ndence. Furthermore, his theory and yours are quite dissimilar.\nThe only thing in common is that you both utilize some aspects\nof electro-magnetism in arriving at your respective conclusions.\n\n        We hope that this information will help dispel any doubt\nwhich you may have concerning the use of the ideas which you\nsubmitted.\n\n                                    Sincerely,\n\nx095. Dull, Mrs. Nellie T.\n              S\n              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n              Colonel, USAF\n              Chief, Topical Division\n              Deputy Director for Estimates\n              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n    [ILLEGIBLE]                   [ILLEGIBLE]\n    Col USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "dddbaef1370d673d58c13b1387294434fd09b74c1ccbe2b6463a1c50b75b4e55", "output_sha256": "dddbaef1370d673d58c13b1387294434fd09b74c1ccbe2b6463a1c50b75b4e55", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:32.856403+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p193", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 193, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\n15 September 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n1. To prepare non-military letter to Mrs. Nellie T. Dull of Staunton,\nVirginia.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n2. On 1 Aug 52 Mrs. Dull wrote in a letter to USAF Intelligence in\nwhich she theorized, in a completely amateurish manner, that electro-\nmagnetism could account for \"flying saucers\". There was absolutely no\ntechnical foundation to her ideas, and, actually, she presented the entire\nthing in the form of a question, viz. \"please let me know if this is the\nanswer.\"\n\n3. A routine reply, thanking her for the suggestion, was dispatched\nby this office 20 August 1952.\n\n4. In a second letter dated 12 Aug 52, Mrs. Dull expresses concern\nthat her ideas were \"stolen\" by Mr. Noel Scott of the Engineer Research\nand Development Lab since the latter announced his ionization theory\nshortly after Mrs. Dull wrote her first letter.\n\n5. Copies of both letters from Mrs. Dull and our reply are\nattached.\n\n6. A reply has been prepared, the contents of which should alleviate\nMrs. Dull's concern.\n\n7. Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the\nDaily Staff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n8. Approval, signature and dispatch of attached letter.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2, Col Wolfe, Ext. 75990 [signature]\nAFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072 [signature]\nAFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "29e904a73740882d99ddaceed6ba48abd96a5375ddf04f1f0785d8c56bb88c1c", "output_sha256": "48eff639691ed6e1f960f18dbfbc5e00055fe219dc5819d06dbbf551a3522298", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:34.781354+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p194", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 194, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 13 Sept 52\n\n                                    SEP 15 1952\n\n\nMiss Florence Easley\n11702 St. Clair\nCleveland, Ohio\n\nDear Miss Easley:\n\n     Your recent telegram concerning unidentified flying\n\nobjects has been referred to this Directorate.\n\n     We are giving your ideas careful consideration and\n\nappreciate your interest and efforts to assist us.\n\n                              Sincerely,\n\n                              JOHN T. MATTHEWS, Captain, USAF\n                              JOHN J. MORROW\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\nNo M/R necessary        F-095. Easley Miss Florence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A        AFOIN-2X\n\n\n          [signature]              [signature]    J Matthews\n                                                  Capt USAF\n\n                                         [stamp: SEP 1952]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fa2def802decd527c73808df3bfe37bf2e513f68ade244fa80fb297b2de4a78a", "output_sha256": "fa2def802decd527c73808df3bfe37bf2e513f68ade244fa80fb297b2de4a78a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:36.162585+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p195", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 195, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\nATTACH TO BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\n\nFROM:        DATE\nAFOIN-2A2         15 September 52\n                  Non-Mil ltr\n                                                    SUSPENSE\nNon-mil ltr to Miss Florence Easley               DATE\nCleveland, Ohio                                    ASGD BY\n                                                   HQ\n                                                   DATE RET'D\n                  SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:          AFOIN-2A                               15 September 1952\nFROM:        AFOIN-2A2                        NO.   1\nREMARKS:                                     Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n                                                   [handwritten initials]\n\n             Ltr for approval and dispatch.\n\n\n\n\n\n  IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n        AFOIN                  AFOIN-[?]  [handwritten]\n        AFOIN-[?]              AFOIN-2[?] [handwritten]\n                               AFOIN-2A2  [handwritten]\n\n        ADMIN                                       ASST\n  X     R & R                  AFOIN-2S            EXEC\n\n                                                   ASST\n                                                   EXEC\n\n                                                   EXEC\n        AFOIN-1\n        AFOIN-[?]              AFOIN[?]\n                                                   AIR/INT\n\n                                          Action        Coordination\nAction Asgd To:            Date:          Dispatched:\nSigned:                    Date:          Filed:         Date:\n\nAFHQ Form 0-60 Previous Editions of this Form Are Obsolete          51-25247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6c75a9de69ddff6e891eba51c10348446f9f54891698df104299c7165fcf07d6", "output_sha256": "9febc8c0e59bae8614cd95894e43ee6824f953210dd1d192a8b40033f0dccdd8", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:38.072680+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p196", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 196, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 13 September 1952\n\n1 Letters\n\n                                        SEP 15 1952\n\nMr. Zed Taylor\n3101 Clinton Drive\nHouston 10, Texas\n\nDear Mr. Taylor:\n\n        Your letter of 5 August 1952 to the Department of the\n\nArmy was referred to us since we are responsible for the\n\n\"flying saucer\" investigation.\n\n        We will be happy to receive any additional information\n\non the subject which you care to volunteer.\n\n        Your interest is appreciated.\n\n        F-095 Taylor, Zed\n        F-095 Elding    Sincerely,\n                        [signature] Gustav F\n                        JOHN T. MATTHEWS, Captain, USAF\n                        JOHN J. MORROW\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence\n\nNo M/R necessary.  Orig ltr to be filed in AFOIN-2A2\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n    [signature]                [signature] 17 SEP 1952\n                                    DIMNT\n                                   HQ USAF\n\nAFOIN-COORDINATION COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2e0dbb2cb3612f95049819957ca23a6d04d0464c3037d2c3cc1a56d44cd4efac", "output_sha256": "2e0dbb2cb3612f95049819957ca23a6d04d0464c3037d2c3cc1a56d44cd4efac", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:39.569263+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p197", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 197, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbf/71016\n13 September 1952\n\n\nSEP 15 1952\n\n\nMr. Gustav F. Ebding\n4125 East 95th Street\nCleveland 5, Ohio\n\nDear Mr. Ebding:\n\n        Your letter of 11 August 1952 to the Department of the\nArmy has been referred to us for attention.\n\n        We will be pleased to receive any information or ideas\nwhich you may have concerning the subject of \"flying saucers\".\n\n        Your interest and efforts to assist us are appreciated.\n\n                    Sincerely,\n\n                    JOHN T. MATTHEWS, Captain, USAF\n\n                    JOHN J. MORROW\n                    Colonel, USAF\n                    Deputy Director for Estimates\n                    Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nNo M/R necessary. Orig ltr to be filed in AFOIN-2A2\n\nCOORDINATION: AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n     Col W Wlfe               [signature]    17 SEP 1952\n\nAFOIN COORDINATION COPY", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "21ffe4764e4948325b2d2918f7a47bc64804e0832cca59734efbea9d2a12a637", "output_sha256": "92d4837a787792d6a5183ddeac1f1ba5c4beff27db7b81027f8af8641bb67793", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:41.081528+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p198", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 198, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\nWRITEUP OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:        AFOIN-2A2          DATE\n                          13 Sept 52\n                     TYPE  Ltrs\n\nLtrs to Mr. Gustav F. Ebding, Cleveland, Ohio          SUSPENSE\n        Mr. Zed Taylor, Houston, Texas          DATE\n        Mr. John Starr Kim, Westbury, N.Y.          AGED BY\n                                                      NO.\n                                                      DATE REC'D\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:          AFOIN-2A                              DATE  15 Sept 52\nFROM:        AFOIN-2A2                             NO.   1\nREMARKS:                              Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n\n             Ltrs for approval and dispatch.\n\n\n\n\n\nIN  OFFICE   OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE   OUT\n     AFOIN                AFOIN-2           jm\n     AFOIN-X              AFOIN-2A\n                          AFOIN-2A2  m                 ASST\n                                                       EXEC\n     ADMIN                                             ASST\nX    R & R               AFOIN-2B   2                  EXEC\n\n                                                       EXEC\n     AFOIN-1\n                          AFOIN-3                      AIR/INT\n\n                                    Action            Coordination\nAction Aged To:           Date:     Dispatch:\nSigned:                   Date:     File:              Date:\n\nAFHQ Form 01-86 Previous Editions of this Form  are obsolete          51 25247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "20fde52a837b907e2d0f687800af13b43f0457d6c786f3564363363daa3b4682", "output_sha256": "64de143a8fec2e254caa87930ff1c80e8ed0e1ce3e8a1addc6d482d20f872eb6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:42.852993+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p199", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 199, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWrtn 15 Sept 1952\n\n\n                                    SEP 15 1952\n\n\nMr. E. L. Lull\nNew Ute Hotel\nSalt Lake City, Utah\n\nDear Mr. Lull:\n\n        Based on the information in your telegram of 29 July\n1952, your book \"Daniel and the Atomic Equations of the\nLoaves\" has been carefully studied and due notice taken\nof your conclusions, particularly that regarding the date\nof 4 October 1954 (presumably revised by your telegram\nto 4 October 1952).  This data is receiving our careful\nconsideration.\n\n        Your efforts on behalf of the U.S. Air Force and of\nour country are indeed appreciated.\n\n                                    Sincerely,\n\n                        JOHN T. MATTHEWS, Captain, USAF\n                        JOHN J. MORROW\n                        Colonel, USAF\n                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                        Directorate of Intelligence\n\n                    X-095, Lull, E. L.\n\n[REDACTED]\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n        [signature]                    [signature]\n\n                                    OUT\n                                 17 SEP 1952\n                                DUTY\n                               HQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1541d694a22acfd6c03b7cd62063732c59db49b640927463ee23b25879eba461", "output_sha256": "1c524ac6a705f7622cd74e104afbda48f7d795a47a46222c36ccaa309098932a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:44.508471+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p200", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 200, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\n          DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\n            STAFF MESSAGE DIVISION\n\n              INCOMING CLEAR MESSAGE\n\n\nSMD A14 1\n\nWU JØ78 NL PD\n\n                    SALT LAKE CITY UTAH JUL 29 1952\n\nINTELLIGENCE UNIT US AIR FORCE\n\nPENTAGON BLDG WASHDC\n\nWITH RESPECT TO THE RECENT HYPERSPACE DEMONSTRATIONS\nOF THE DISC COMPANY IN FREE SPACE IT MAY HAPPEN THAT\nTHE COMPUTATIONS SHOWN IN MY BOOK \"DANIEL AND THE\nATOMIC EQUATIONS OF THE LOAVES\" ARE IN ERROR BY\nABOUT TWO YEARS\n\n          E L LULL NEW UTE HOTEL\n\n                              JUL 30 52 5A\n\n\nACTION: OIN\n\nAF IN: 14051 (30 Jul 52)\n\n\n                        UNCLASSIFIED\n\n                                                    COPY     1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b623a13df1a9a406d6d772f02ba75efc7059943ad13657636bb941c544a14eaa", "output_sha256": "84212fcfe24a504817e49fdfebf7e856dba0bcf178d5518b46fb095326915a28", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:45.927481+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p201", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 201, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\n13 September 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n1. To prepare a non-military letter to Mr. E. L. Lull of Salt\nLake City.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n2. In a telegram to this Directorate dated 29 July 1952 (AF IN\n14051), Mr. Lull states that, based on certain recent data, his\ncalculations in his book \"Daniel and the Atomic Equations of the\nLoaves\" may be in error by about 2 years.\n\n3. A copy of this book was obtained through the Army Library\nfrom the Library of Congress. It is significant that the latter\nclassifies the book as BS (Bible).\n\n4. This analyst must plead innocent to any accusation that he\nis a theologian. Nonetheless, on the assumption that any information regardless of origin or nature may possibly prove helpful\nto Intelligence and applying amateur theology, the book was\nscanned and the following conclusions derived:\n\n a. Mr. Lull, who is an engineer, has attempted to\nestablish a correlation between certain significant dates in history\nand specific passages in the Testaments and the Book of Mormon\nby the use of mathematical analyses.\n\n b. Further, by the same analyses, he arrives at certain\nfuture dates which, by analogy, he concludes are indicative of\nextreme significance to the world. One such date is 4 Oct 54. It\nis implied that a revelation will be made on that date in fulfillment\nof one of Daniel's prophecies in the old Testament and that this\nrevelation will be a joyous rather than a grievous one.\n\n5. It is assumed that Mr. Lull's statement to the effect that his\ncalculations may be in error by about 2 years refers to the 4 Oct 54\nderivation and, further, that the error is positive, i.e. that the date\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "02689457a68adf292531bd70084789b699ca3bd7b6a8285d69946a410219e3d8", "output_sha256": "1a6eb58e301d6cd2a801f442742b51cdcc1a05e67b04a6896714c5dea4ac8fa0", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:48.007240+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p202", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 202, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nshould be 4 Oct 52. This assumption is based on the urgency with\nwhich Mr. Lull informed us of his error (by telegram).\n\n6. It is additionally assumed that Mr. Lull intends that the\naforementioned date be associated with Project Blue Book since:\n\n        a. He states in his telegram that the basis for his belief\nthat he made an error in his original calculations (presumably re\n4 Oct 54) is \"the recent hyperspace demonstrations of the Disc Company\nin free space\".\n\n        b. His telegram was dispatched at the height of the most\nrecent \"flying saucer\" flurry in the press (the date of the telegram is\nthe same as that on which General Samford held a press conference on\nthe subject).\n\n7. Accordingly, a reply to Mr. Lull has been prepared expressing\nappreciation and stating that due notice has been taken of his conclusions.\n\n8. Additionally, this analyst has marked 4 Oct down as a red letter\nday and is eagerly awaiting its arrival since it apparently means that\nthe mystery of the \"flying saucers\" will finally be solved and his toil\ntowards that end will no longer be necessary.\n\n9. Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the\nDaily Staff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n10. Approval and dispatch of attached letter to Mr. Lull.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n   AFOIN-2A2, Col Wolfe, Ext. 75990 [ILLEGIBLE]\n   AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072 [ILLEGIBLE]\n   AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n                        2\n                   RESTRICTED\n                SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "24b36adff5c6085e1b4d16dc5fc80cc0fd824d7b80ed16274f56449e4ada8ecd", "output_sha256": "f7e6ce91afc55454c49d9607857c83f53c74046d0b03aff1adb8c384ef4e07bd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:49.934461+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p203", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 203, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n[ILLEGIBLE] OF BASIL CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST     CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:                    DATE:\n         AFOIN-2A2          15  September 1952\n                            Non-Mil Ltr\n\n         Non-Mil Ltr to Mr. E. L. Lull\n                                                    SUSPENSE:\n                                                    DATE\n                                                    ASGD BY\n                                                    NO.\n                                                    DATE REC'D\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:      AFOIN-2                                DATE  15 September 52\nFROM:    AFOIN-2A                               NO.   1\nREMARKS:                               Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n\n         Ltr for approval and dispatch.\n\n                            AFOIN-2A\n\n| OFFICE  | OUT | IN | OFFICE  |    | IN | OFFICE   | OUT |\n| AFO