    Major, USAF\n   2. IR-134-52 (3cys)              Asst Adj Gen\n   3. IR-135-52 (4cys)\n   4. IR-136-52 (2cys)\n\n                              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ___________\n\n                    17 Sept 52.\n\n             Incl's in OIN-1B2\n                  maj. Randolfo\n\n                       [RP]\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "30f95ed5bdb09ae4255c0027ae19d8c6e21fcfc529caf3b76f820563fb83eab7", "output_sha256": "d371fd5c86530e9d6860d9d0096a7aab1e69ef38bd8baae27ff470bed32a1a96", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:53.622420+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p205", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 205, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[Document appears to be a reverse/bleed-through image of the opposite side of a page]\n\nREC'D\n16 SEP 1952\nDIR/INT\nHQ USAF\n\n[Remainder of text is mirror-reversed bleed-through from reverse side, largely illegible]\n\nAI IN-130-P5 (38-6)\nAI IN-135-S5 (3648)\nAI IN-135-D5 (3648)\nAI IN-P13-P5 (3648)\nFOPIS\n\nTO ALL COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n[Several lines of mirror-reversed/bleed-through text - illegible]\n\nDISTRIBUTION:\nFour Addressees\nTO: DIRECTOR OF INTELLIGENCE\n\nSUBJECT: (RESTRICTED) AIRCRAFT\n\nFROM:\n\nALEXANDER VARNING\nCHIEF AIR FORCE INTEL\nCOMMAND VIA DISTRICT AIRLINE COMMAND", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "bf2862155663a6e6b9e00c4370a332b274b76db7027d8ed3a120ec5c25b74f0c", "output_sha256": "b5704693f8ac5d56e34b17c267f20fd0242373ada53ee47e16f7289de32f7864", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:54.828025+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p206", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 206, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED                    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n              HEADQUARTERS STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND\n                      OFFUTT AIR FORCE BASE\n                         OMAHA, NEBRASKA\n\nDINC\n     3 5 0\nSUBJECT:  (Unclassified) FLYOBRPT                    11 SEP 1952\n\n\nTO:          Director of Intelligence\n             Headquarters USAF\n             Washington 25, D.C.\n\n\n          The attached Air Intelligence Information Reports are forwarded\nas per instructions AFL 200-5, dated 29 April 1952, subject, FLYOBRPT.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                                              Ray P. Stewart\n                                         RAY P. STEWART\n                                         Major, USAF\n2 Incls                                  Asst Adj Gen\n  1. IR-129-52 (3 cys)\n  2. IR-130-52 (2 cys)\n\n\n                                   COUPON DESIGNATION MADE --------\n\n                              17 Sept.\n\n\n                    Onl m/sim on 102\n                              maj Sandolfo\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6753faaff7df3c2478e3488936698ecc23a8f6cabe696016321f849a2be851af", "output_sha256": "3717a5ed035ee478059f75b4bf32a3408bc45ad72b58a29dd692ececc7591e09", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:56.287523+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p207", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 207, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "REC'D\n16 SEP 1952\nDIR/INT\nHO USAF\n\n[Remainder of page contains bleed-through text from reverse side that is mirrored/reversed and not directly transcribable]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4fb706ce73b1c1da855c4ec4d485880c252d304d57bc92fb456176ad79eeadbd", "output_sha256": "4fb706ce73b1c1da855c4ec4d485880c252d304d57bc92fb456176ad79eeadbd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:56.937772+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p208", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 208, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                    Wrtn 10 September 52\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          11 SEP '52\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN             Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB                                         AFOIN-2A2\nOhio\n\n     Attached cable from USAIRA Norway is for your information.  It is the reply to\nour cable AFOIN 56103 dated 19 Aug 52, an information copy of which was addressed\nto you.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\nIncl (w/Orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Cable CAF IN 98951                  Colonel, USAF\n  dtd 22 Aug 52                       Chief, Topical Division\n                                      Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                      Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nCOORDINATION:   AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n        [signature]               [signature]\n\n\nNO M/R NECESSARY.\n\n\n                              K-322.7 ATIC\n\n\n                         When incl→ No. 1\n                         is    with      (not attached),\n                         the Confidential    classification\n                         of this co          be down-\n                         graded to Restricted        in\n                         accordance with AFR 205-1.\n                                      DIR/INT\n                                    HQ USAF\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "1e252b798c77eae108695e0436b2eabac0615baa0bb8ccf3ff3fdf7ac40fedab", "output_sha256": "1e252b798c77eae108695e0436b2eabac0615baa0bb8ccf3ff3fdf7ac40fedab", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:11:58.639679+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p209", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 209, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified) Investigation of Incident of\n                    1/2 Sep 52 Arlington Va. having possible relation to\n                              Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical         Dept of the Air Force          11 SEP 52\n Intelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2      Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosures relate to the investigation of an incident which allegedly\noccurred during the night of 1/2 September 1952, and which has a possible relation\nto Project Blue Book.  The investigation was conducted by this office on 3 and\n4 September 1952.\n\n     2.  Inclosures 1 and 2 give details of the investigation.  A list of samples\nobtained during the investigation and pertinent data on each are included in\nInclosure 3.  These samples have been forwarded to OSI with a request that they\nbe submitted to the FBI for lab analysis.  The results of the analysis will be\nforwarded as soon as they become available.\n\n     3.  Inclosure 4 contains 5 photographic negatives taken of the area in\nquestion at 1430 hours on 4 September 1952.  All shots except the one showing\nthe cap on the ground were taken of the ring in its original state.  The color\nof the deposit was approximately the same as on the preceding evening when\nsamples were taken, but the amount of the deposit appeared to have diminished\nsomewhat.  The shot in which the cap appears on the ground was taken after lime-\nstone had been spread over the original ring in order to provide better definition.\nCare was taken to duplicate the original configuration, both as to shape and density.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n4 Incls: (w/orig. only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1.  Summary of findings.                 Colonel, USAF\n  2.  Sketch of area                       Chief, Topical Division\n  3.  List of samples obtained             Deputy Director for Estimates\n  4.  Photographic negs (5)   to ATIC only Directorate of Intelligence\n\nNo M/R necessary.  (2nd cy of Inclosures (except no. 4) to remain w/hayback cy)\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                      SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6bb7b6af799c5b857c7dbf3919edc7c176b1234d9d3c1ca6c188042d0c377aed", "output_sha256": "6bb7b6af799c5b857c7dbf3919edc7c176b1234d9d3c1ca6c188042d0c377aed", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:00.974606+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p210", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 210, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\n                    HEADQUARTERS\n               6580TH MISSILE TEST WING\n           Holloman Air Force Base, New Mexico\n\nMTHIP                                        10 September 1952\n\nSUBJECT:  Transmittal of Air Intelligence Information Report\n\n\nTO:       Director of Intelligence\n          Headquarters, USAF\n          Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\n     In compliance with Air Force Letter 200-5, Unidentified Flying\nObjects Reporting, dated 29 April 1952, the following Air Intelligence\nInformation Report is submitted for your information.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING OFFICER:\n                              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE -----------\n\n\n                                   [signature] MAJ USAF\n                              WILLIAM F. HARRIS\n1 Incl:                       Lt. Col., USAF\n  Air Intel Info Rpt (3 cys)  Deputy for Personnel\n\n              x 319.1 AF Intelligence Rept\n                        1952 Sept.\n\n\nMclar/pin O 14 1952\n     Maj. Pandolfo\n\n          [signature stamp]\n\n\n0010386\n\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION\n                      RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2dbe504d99a24e88c14558cab8d753284d60fb84bbad2ffc13ff48c1e8a9d89a", "output_sha256": "9604fd55728db8eb3397c59b28c5da118b418dda9fdbaa189e1412528e318476", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:02.332829+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p211", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 211, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "DISPATCHED: HOLLOMAN\nAF BASE, NEW MEXICO\n\n1952 SEP 11 AM 7:47\n\nREC'D\n18 SEP 1952\nDIR/INT\nHQ USAF", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2037c465813e4e2c5695d08f8da93958921bca4672c2a2b19011a04630cf5c39", "output_sha256": "2037c465813e4e2c5695d08f8da93958921bca4672c2a2b19011a04630cf5c39", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:03.038779+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p212", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 212, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "9 Sept 52\n\nAGAO-CCY                    Flying Saucers\nChief of Staff              TAGO                    11 August 1952\nU. S. Air Force                                     Mr. Acker/52267\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\n     1.  Forwarded as a matter of primary interest.\n\n     2.  Writers have been informed of this reference.\n\n     FOR THE ADJUTANT GENERAL:\n\n\n                                        Wm. Q. Williams\n8 Incl                                  Adjutant General\n  1.  Ltr from T. Houritan\n  2.  Ltr 1 Aug 52\n  3.  Ltr 31 Jul 52\n  4.  Ltr 29 Jul 52\n  5.  Ltr from Billy Cooey\n  6.  Ltr 2 Aug 52\n  7.  Ltr 2 Aug 52 from\n      Mr. Schaefer\n  8.  Ltr 1 Aug 52\n\n                                              w/9 September 52\nTO: Chief, Air Technical FROM: Dept of the Air Force Date:        Comment No. 2\n    Intelligence Center       Hq USAF - AFOIN              Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n    Wright Patterson AFB\n    Ohio\n\n     1.  Forwarded for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  Since all letters have been acknowledged by the Army, further correspondence\nis not mandatory.\n\n     3.  Inclosure 4 has been withdrawn and referred to SAF GBI-OPI for reply.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n8 Incls                                  WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Withdrawn Incl 4                       Colonel, USAF\n  NO M/R Necessary                       Chief, Topical Division\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2A   Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                         Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n[signature]                [signature]\n\n                                         RESTRICTED\n                                         SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6605d0f0ea24d011e4df7928dbfb9354d27f5f4021bdf739881e30a6b9ae192e", "output_sha256": "6605d0f0ea24d011e4df7928dbfb9354d27f5f4021bdf739881e30a6b9ae192e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:05.165362+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p213", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 213, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 9 September 1952\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN                Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nOhio                                                          AFOIN-2A2\n\n1.  Inclosed letter is forwarded for your information and retention.\n\n2.  News releases on 18 and 19 August 1952 were scanned for indications that\nwriter attempted to carry out threat of \"exposure\" mentioned in his letter. Nothing\nwas found. Although this is a rather obvious hoax, it would be interesting to\ndetermine what an analysis of his photograph would reveal and, through your clipping\nservice, if any mention of an exhibition is found, perhaps in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania\nnewspapers.\n\n         BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n1 Incl (W/Orig only)                    WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  Ltr dtd 2 Aug 52                      Colonel, USAF\n  (Anonymous)                           Chief, Topical Division\n                                        Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                        Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O\n\n● M/R NECESSARY.\n\n              X322.7a TIC\n\n\nCOORDINATION:   AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A\n\n    Col M Wolfe        [signature]\n\n                                              OUT\n                                          6 11 SEP 1952\n                                          [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2398b5e68461dfb204dfd0d23c58d8e67efbaf5b49ce7dca3a5c07ba2ae8a693", "output_sha256": "2398b5e68461dfb204dfd0d23c58d8e67efbaf5b49ce7dca3a5c07ba2ae8a693", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:06.876148+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p214", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 214, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        AFOIN-2A2\n                                        Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n                                        wrtn 8 Sept 1952\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN                    Maj Fournet/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are forwarded for your information, appropriate\naction and retention.  All concern sightings of unidentified flying objects.\n\n     2.  No acknowledgements or other replies have been made by this office.\n\n     BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                                   JAMES P. BECKETT\n\n23 Incls  (w/orig only)            WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n  (see attached                    Colonel, USAF\n   sheet for listing)              Chief, Policy and Management Group\n                                   Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                   Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2\n\n     [signature]                  [signature]        [signature]\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                       SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "484a595c693a5fb81ca34cd459f7bbea7e8d6c11240b6fc22ebd60bab4e4d89d", "output_sha256": "f007cc56b5458638d858507300cca62e9aed939cb19431559d0f843a468e7ffb", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:08.380928+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p215", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 215, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "1.  Ltr fr C. Raymond Dillon, Capt, CAP, Balaton, Minn. dtd 24 Jul 52\n2.  Ltr fr Jerry Elliott, Roanoke Rapids, N. C. w/Incl dtd 22 Jul 52\n3.  Ltr fr Jerry Elliott, Roanoke Rapids, N. C. w/ Incl dtd 25 Jul 52\n4.  Ltr fr Corliss Cramer, Arlington, Va. dtd 22 July 52\n5.  Anonymous ltr fr Nokomis, Fla. dtd 25 July 52\n6.  Ltr fr Jim Levenburger, Saginaw, Mich. dtd 22 July 1952\n7.  Ltr fr Mrs. H. M. West, Creston, Iowa dtd 22 July 1952\n8.  Ltr fr Betty Marshall, Havertown, Pa dtd 1 Aug 52\n9.  Anonymous ltr fr San Francisco, Calif dtd 29 July 1952\n10. Ltr fr Michael Duffy, Carlin, Nevada dtd 31 July 1952\n11. Ltr fr Dora Yeaton, Portsmouth, N. H. dtd (PM) 29 Jul 52\n12. Ltr fr Doris Clemens, Pandosa, Oregon, dtd 2 Aug 1952\n13. D/F fr TAG w 1 Incl dtd 6 Aug 1952\n14. Ltr fr Monroe J. Kight, Hot Springs, Ark. dtd 3 Aug 52\n15. Ltr fr Silvino R. Castella, New Bedford, Mass dtd 27 Jul 52\n16. Ltr fr William F. O'Connor, No. Hollywood, Calif dtd 23 Jul 52\n17. Ltr fr Mrs. Raymond O. Pratt, Brattleboro, Vermont dtd 6 Aug 52\n18. Ltr fr Richard Little, Elmhurst, Ill. dtd 31 Jul 52\n19. Ltr fr Lucy D. Sanders, Ypsilanti, Mich. dtd 6 Aug 52\n20. Ltr fr Johanie Mittl, Kutztown, Pa. dtd 31 Jul 52\n21. Ltr fr Albert H. Sundahl, (Cpt-Ret.), Spokane, Wash dtd 31 Jul 52\n22. Ltr fr John E. Byrd, Norman, Ark., dtd (PM) 8 Aug 52\n23. Ltr fr Keith W. Johnson, Dallas, Texas dtd 6 Aug 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "ed1f4e9baf20ce3eb2bf51e9392d1a913621d42ce2f6a9ba04dbbd94bdfd81c5", "output_sha256": "ed1f4e9baf20ce3eb2bf51e9392d1a913621d42ce2f6a9ba04dbbd94bdfd81c5", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:11.084913+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p216", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 216, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\n* RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST*        CLASSIFICATION\n\nFROM:                    DATE  8 September 1952\n   AFOIN-2A2             TYPE\n                               D/F\n\n                                                    SUSPENSE\n                                                    DATE\n   (U) Material for Project Blue Book              ASGD BY\n                                                    NO.\n                                                    DATE REC'D\n\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\n                                                    DATE\nTO:   AFOIN-2                                       8 Sept 1952\n                                                    TO.\nFROM: AFOIN-2A                                      1\n                              Maj Bournet/dbv/71016\nREMARKS:                          [signature]\n\n         D/F forwarded for approval, signature and transmission.\n\n                         AFOIN-2A\n\n\nIN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n      AFOIN                 AFOIN-2    B\n      AFOIN-X               AFOIN-2A  [initials]\n                            AFOIN-2A2\n\n                                                    ASST\n                                                    EXEC\n      ADMIS\nX     H & R                AFOIN-3B               ASST\n                                                    EXEC\n\n                                                    EXEC\n      AFOIN-3\n            AFOIN-2                               AIR/INT\n\n\nAction Asgd To:         Date:        Dispatch: [signature] [initials] Coordination\nSigned:                 Date:        File:                  Date:\n\nAFHQ Form 0-86 Previous Editions of this Form are obsolete        52 23247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "aa38996e6758a6d1e11375ab6aecf3740d0ebf0613bce1d5a53ae41f880e2ea6", "output_sha256": "d4e2a5d9a38564b1d9e7ef0d2ba9e4852b9d79aa0a2d3ead52a667150ad23426", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:12.946883+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p217", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 217, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\nwrtn 8 Sep 52\n\n(Unclassified) Suggested Reply to Mr. Berridge (Partial)\n\nAF Press Desk, OSAF-OPI\n\n                                    SEP - 9 1952\nDeputy Director for Estimates, D/I, DCS/O        Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n                                    AFOIN-2A2\n\n     1.  In addition to the usual comments to be incorporated into a reply to\nMr. Berridge by your office, it is suggested that the following paragraph be\nincluded:\n\n     \"The details of the observation which you made were referred to our\nIntelligence analysts for their study and comment.  They have informed me\nthat, although the object could possibly have been a high altitude balloon\nascending through different wind strata, they find it impossible to arrive\nat a definite conclusion.  However, they were happy to receive the\ninformation and to add it to the data from other sightings which they\nprocess and analyze constantly.\"\n\n     2.  It is also recommended that appropriate comments be made regarding\nGeneral Samford's statements during his recent press conference, particularly those\ndealing with current USAF attitude towards the subject and plans for the future.\nStressing his statement about \"adequate but not frantic attention\" should also help.\n\n     3.  Mr. Berridge's letter is returned herewith.\n\n                    x 095, Berridge, Mr. William A\n\n1 Incl                         s/ WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n  Ltr fr Wm. A. Berridge           Colonel, USAF\n  dtd 30 Jul 52                    Chief, Policy and Management Group\n                                   Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                   Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n                              COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\nCOORDINATION:  AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A               AFOIN-2\n\n   Col [signature]    [signature]              [signature]\n\n\n          H/c by Mrs Glover AFOIN-X-B(OHA)\n                             10 Sept 52\n                             10 o'clock A.M.", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "22dc15a32ced9e99e77eed398cd7304365c665f9f37b9bcdc638e31651467f53", "output_sha256": "22dc15a32ced9e99e77eed398cd7304365c665f9f37b9bcdc638e31651467f53", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:15.049339+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p218", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 218, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "AFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dbv/71016\n8 September 1952\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM\n\n     1.  To prepare an R & R to OSAF-OPI.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n     2.  A personal letter from Mr. William A. Berridge to General Vandenberg was\nreferred to OSAF-OPI for preparation of a reply for signature in AFCCS.  In this\nletter Mr. Berridge reports the sighting of an unidentified flying object and comments that he is disturbed over recent public remarks made by D/I personnel on this\nsubject.\n\n     3.  Major Fournet discussed the letter with OSAF-OPI at the latter's request\nand indicated that AFOIN-2A2 would be happy to suggest certain appropriate comments\nwhich could be incorporated into a reply.  It was understood by OPI that AFOIN-2A2\nwas not undertaking the complete reply since it was largely a matter requiring public\nrelations treatment.\n\n     4.  The attached R & R sets forth those comments and suggestions considered\nappropriate from the D/I standpoint.\n\n     5.  Subject matter is not considered suitable for inclusion in the Daily Staff\nDigest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED\n\n     6.  Approval, signature and dispatch of attached R & R.\n\nCORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Wolfe, Ext. 71379 ow\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, Ext. 74072 usa\n     AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, Ext. 71110 uu", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d6fbd5d2aa3620b2bb059d3c8900c9a25f578d02fa2ac49d93bdc4ee8b9b6bde", "output_sha256": "69d94c350c0c123f7c0104109d0ae0065e6af30cd6d9b750675ab680d9c5567f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:16.946276+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p219", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 219, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\nRECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:                    DATE\n                         8 Sept 59\n    AFOIN-2A2            TYPE\n\nSUMMARY\n                                                    SUSPENSE\n                                          DATE  1200  10 SEPTEMBER 1952\n    (U) Suggested Reply to Mr. Berridge (Partial)\n                                          ASGD BY  M.E. SMITH  MES\n                                          NO.      CSS    019285\n                                          DATE REC'D D/I  29 August 1952\n\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:    AFOIN-2                            DATE   8 Sept 52\n\nFROM:  AFOIN-2A                           NO.        1\n\nREMARKS\n                                          Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n\n       R&R submitted for your approval, signature and dispatch.\n\n\n                                    [signature]\n                                    AFOIN-2A  Capt.\n\n\n\n\n          CSS\nSuspense ————\n$    1200  10 SEPTEMBER 1952\n\n               (Use reverse for additional remarks)\n\nIN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n      AFOIN-P·              AFOIN-A\n      P/PL                  AFOIN-V                      ASST\n      P/MIC                 V/AE           ✓             EXEC\n      P/FL                  V/AF\n      AFOIN-C               V/TC\n      C/CC                  AFOIN-T                      ASST\n      C/DD                  T/TP                         EXEC\n      C/AA                  T/TR\n      C/SR                  T/AO\n      C/RC                  T/AV                    EXECUTIVE\n      C/EE                  T/PV\n      ADMIN                 AFOIN-E    B\n X    M&R                   E/EA\n      B&F                   E/PE                    DIR/INT\n      CABLE                 E/CE\n      PERS                  E/WE\n                            E/CI    [initials]    X  Action    1/  Coordination\nACTION ASGD TO         DATE         DISPATCH    [signature]\n\nSIGNED                 DATE         FILE                        DATE\n\nAFHQ   FORM    0-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE        C 3675\n       15 JUL 51", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "18ff8b492100cd60a5873953bf4c8372d10f8494bbc14bb413b5b79d4229c67d", "output_sha256": "18ff8b492100cd60a5873953bf4c8372d10f8494bbc14bb413b5b79d4229c67d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:19.453641+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p220", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 220, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force         9 SEP '52\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2      Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\nOhio\n\n     1.  Inclosed correspondence from CIA with attached sighting report is\nforwarded for your information and retention.\n\n     2.  Request acknowledgment of receipt be made to CIA.  The latter replied\nto Mr Mookian, and, therefore, further correspondence with him is not mandatory.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n1 Incl:  w/orig. only\n  corres. fr CIA                    JAMES P. BECKETT\n  w/attached sighting rpt\n                              WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Policy and Management Group\n                              Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n                    x-095  Mookian, Samuel\n\n                         COUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n\nNo M/R necessary\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n               AFOIN-2A2    AFOIN-2A    AFOIN-2\n\n          [signatures]\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c60a2cc07124888af249342d8045fe7100b20f1fc893ba7131fb6dcf3aaa3fbc", "output_sha256": "d3682e568868de783a40d077f9c12145e46ed16100d847ed400f928d59a55df9", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:21.012409+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p221", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 221, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\nRECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\n\nFROM:                    DATE  8 Sept 52\n  AFOIN-2A2\n                         TYPE  D/F\n\n                                                    SUSPENSE\n(U) Material for Project Blue Book                  DATE\n                                                    ASGD BY\n                                                    NO\n                                                    DATE REC'D\n\n                    SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nTO:  AFOIN-2                                        DATE  8 Sept 52\n\nFROM: AFOIN-2A                                      NO.  1\n\nREMARKS:                                  Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\n\n\n         D/F for approval, signature and dispatch.\n\n                                          AFOIN-2A\n\n\n\n\n  W    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT      IN    OFFICE    OUT\n         AFOIN                AFOIN-2    B\n         AFOIN-1              AFOIN-2A              ASST\n                              AFOIN-2A2             EXEC\n\n\n  X    ADMIN                                        ASST\n       M & R                  AFOIN-2B              EXEC\n\n\n                                                    HREC\n         AFOIN-1\n                              AFOIN-2               AIR/INT\n\n\nAction Asgd To:              Date:      Dispatch:  [signature] [coordination]\nSigned:                      Date:      File:      Date:\n\nAFWQ Form C-86  Previous Editions of this Form are obsolete          51 25247\n20 Nov 50", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "386506fdd4e2ebc4ff33ca6c3eb1f0a389a8722b074867347c0ac370feaed11a", "output_sha256": "69b651ce1d3711178878593803f0d8491d24767133e30d36950910505c6e05ce", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:22.673113+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p222", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 222, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                    (Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical    Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center     Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2        9 SEP 52\nWright-Patterson AFB                               Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nOhio\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are forwarded for your information and retention.\nThey fall in the \"theories and suggestions\" category.\n\n     2.  No replies of any kind have been made.\n\n          BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                         S/ JAMES P. BECKETT\n                         WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n                         Colonel, USAF\n                         Chief, Policy and Management Group\n                         Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                         Directorate of Intelligence\n19 Incls:\n\n  1.  Ltr fr L.G. Newlin          15.  Ltr fr M. Mobley\n      dtd 5 Aug 52                      dtd 7 Aug 52\n  2.  Ltr fr E. Helekal            16.  card fr G.A. Swanson\n      dtd 13 Aug 52, w/attchd            dtd 4 Aug 52\n      article                      17.  Ltr fr F.W. Wood\n  3.  Ltr fr H.W. Michaelson       18.  Ltr fr Dr O.N. Greenberg\n      dtd 3 Aug 52                       dtd 11 Aug 52 rec'd\n  4.  Ltr fr G.A. Thomas           19.  Ltr Mr Park\n      dtd 29 July 52                     dtd 8 Aug 52\n  5.  Ltr fr P.E. Bennick\n      dtd 20 July 52\n  6.  Ltr fr C.S. Keen         X-322.7  ATIC\n      dtd 11 Aug 52\n  7.  Ltr fr Miss E. Mack\n      dtd 1 Aug 52\n  8.  Ltr fr J.P. Bessor\n      dtd 31 Jul 52\n  9.  Ltr fr N. Rothstein\n      dtd 31 Jul 52\n 10.  Ltr fr Mrs W. Schultz\n      dtd 30 Jul 52\n 11.  Ltr fr R. Funk          RESTRICTED\n      dtd 30 Jul 52           SECURITY INFORMATION\n 12.  Ltr fr F.E. Grote\n      dtd 1 Aug 52\n 13.  Ltr fr C. Panzer      Coordination   AFOIN-2A2    AFOIN-2A    AFOIN-2\n      dtd 7 Aug 52\n 14.  Ltr fr B. Hines\n      dtd 8 Aug 52\n\n                    Col [ILLEGIBLE] Wolf         [ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cb49948f93951aead3e1c7ac8f55c0992568a9738cb6b53b1dfca3b61f7d0450", "output_sha256": "d0c1db1287a247efd56466d6d6e723bf05cea3d8bda6380ed898fe34df6164df", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:25.666334+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p223", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 223, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COVER SHEET\n\n         RECORD OF BASIC CORRESPONDENCE OR REQUEST          CLASSIFICATION\nFROM:                              DATE\n    AFOIN-2A2                           5 Sep 52\n                                   TYPE\n                                        D/F\n                                                              SUSPENSE\n (U) Material for Project Blue Book                   DATE\n                                                      ASCD BY\n                                                      NO.\n                                                      DATE REC'D\n\n                          SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS\nTO:  AFOIN-2                                          DATE    5 Sep 52\n\nFROM:        AFOIN-2A                                 NO.   1\n                                               Maj Fournet/dbv/71016\nREMARKS:\n                                                    [signature]\n              D/F for signature and dispatch.\n\n                              AFOIN-2A\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n  AFOIN                  AFOIN-2    B\n  AFOIN-X                AFOIN-2A\n                         AFOIN-2A   N                ASST\n                                                     EXEC\n\n          ADMIN                                      ASST\nX         R & R            AFOIN-2S                  EXEC\n\n                                                     EXEC\n          AFOIN-1\n                                                     AIR/INT\n\n\nAction Asgd To:          Date:        Dispatch:  [signature]  Coordination\nSigned:                  Date:        File:                   Date:\n\nAFHQ Form 0-99 Previous Editions of this Form  are obsolete\n20 Nov 50                                                     51 29347", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d29583572f256d2d64973aa1ab3f5d008b7eea8539d62472a0d194dcfca6bbbd", "output_sha256": "d29583572f256d2d64973aa1ab3f5d008b7eea8539d62472a0d194dcfca6bbbd", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:27.377936+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p224", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 224, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-2A                                          8 September 1952\n\nSUBJECT:  (Restricted) Unidentified Aerial Phenomena, Discussion\n          Conference with ONR Personnel\n\n\nTO:       Chief of Naval Research\n          Department of The Navy\n          Washington 25, D. C.\n\n\n     1.  Reference is made to your letter, ONR:421:FLT:esw, Ser: 21517,\nsubject, \"Unidentified aerial phenomena; request for information\nconcerning,\" dated 15 August 1952, requesting Air Force participation in\na discussion of unidentified aerial phenomena, at a convenient date on\nor after 15 September 1952.\n\n     2.  It is suggested that the discussion be held at 1000 hours on\n17 September in Room 1803, Building T-3, Navy Department.\n\n     3.  In view of the technical nature of the discussions to be held,\nand the desirability of possible attendance by Air Technical Intelligence\nCenter personnel, it is requested that a representative of the Office of\nNaval Research make direct contact with Major D. J. Fournet, USAF,\nRoom 4B-860, Extension 71016, Pentagon, who will represent the Air Force\nin these discussions and is authorized to make any necessary\narrangements.\n\n     4.  Should the date and time for these discussions, as recommended\nin paragraph 2 above, be inconvenient, it is suggested that a date be\nmutually decided upon between your representative and Major Fournet.\n\n                    FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                    x045. Navy/Dept\n                    William A. Adams\nCOUPON DESIGNATION MADE\n                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Topical Division\n                              Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\nAFOIN-2A2                    AFOIN-2A\n\nCol JW Wolfe                 [ILLEGIBLE signature]\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "191e0301d1c82da6e7c4caa8bf6e9563b14b883a6b7443557abd284c02cb423d", "output_sha256": "191e0301d1c82da6e7c4caa8bf6e9563b14b883a6b7443557abd284c02cb423d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:29.434975+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p225", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 225, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nDEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nOFFICE OF NAVAL RESEARCH\nWASHINGTON 25, D. C.\n\n                                                    IN REPLY REFER TO\n                                                    ONR:421:FLT:esw\n                                                    Ser:\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION                                        21517\n\nFrom:  Chief of Naval Research\nTo:    Director of Intelligence                     AUG 15 1952\n       U. S. Air Force\n\nSubj:  Unidentified aerial phenomena; request for information\n       concerning\n\n1.  In view of current widespread interest, it is requested that a brief-\ning be arranged for the purpose of acquainting interested activities within\nthe Office of Naval Research with the latest developments of the investiga-\ntion of unidentified aerial phenomena obtained under Project Blue Book.\nThe meeting would be limited to about a dozen personnel with a definite\n\"need to know\" and an acute scientific interest in this project.  All in\nattendance will be cleared through Secret and are acquainted with the\nbackground of this program having seen the official reports of Project\nBlue Book dated through April 1952.\n\n2.  It is suggested that a question-and-answer type discussion be sched-\nuled for a date on or after 15 September 1952 in Room 1803 of Building\nT-3, Navy Department, Washington, D. C.\n\n3.  The cooperation of the Air Force in making such a briefing possible\nwill be appreciated.\n\n\n                                        C. M. Bolster\n\n                                        C. M. BOLSTER\n\n\n\n\nThis material contains information\naffecting the national defense of the\nUnited States within the meaning of\nthe Espionage Laws, Title 18, U. S.\nC., Sections 793 and 794, the trans-\nmission or revelation of which in any\nmanner to an unauthorized person is\nprohibited by law.\n\n                                                    RESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "7b7218781537e4a9a5d7b9667ce703310e665f7208e0d8cdfb06f5203258ffd2", "output_sha256": "c7ae93f6a1679d164a6d7e1dca9f2030930c539615c21d47486ed24e779fa193", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:31.408866+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p226", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 226, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[Document appears to be photographed/scanned in reverse/mirror image, rendering text largely illegible]\n\nREC'D\n18 AUG 1952\nDIRINT\nHQ USAF\n\n[Remainder of text is mirror-reversed and cannot be reliably transcribed verbatim]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "28cde1cba79a1e1abb9efe8d0556e941f41c15127dea841e72b6543ee2f2145a", "output_sha256": "28cde1cba79a1e1abb9efe8d0556e941f41c15127dea841e72b6543ee2f2145a", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:32.052211+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p227", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 227, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                M/R.\n                                    Maj Fournet/bmo/71016\n                                    AFOIN-2A2\n                                    w/8 September 1952\n\n                        MEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To prepare a letter for the Chief of Naval Research.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  In a letter to the D/I, the CNR requested a briefing and round\ntable discussion for the purpose of acquainting interested members of his\nstaff with the latest developments in Project Blue Book.  It was suggested\nthat the program be held after 15 September 1952 in Room 1803 of\nBuilding T-3, Navy Department.\n\n     3.  The attached letter will inform the CNR that Maj Fournet will\nconduct the program.  A time of 1000 hours on 17 September 1952 is\nsuggested with a request for confirmation.  The CNR is also requested to\ncontact Major Fournet, direct and arrange for the details of the conference.\n\n     4.  Subject matter is not considered suitable for the Daily Staff\nDigest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n     5.  Approval, signature and dispatch of attached letter.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     Col T. W. Wolfe, AFOIN-2A2, Ext 75990 aw\n     Col W. A. Adams, AFOIN-2A, Ext 71564 wac\n     Col J. J. Morrow, AFOIN-2, Ext 71110\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        RESTRICTED\n                      SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4d20e8ea83358abd85d44e0d644c3ee6d0d6813367d03831614c9ebfd1536b10", "output_sha256": "4d20e8ea83358abd85d44e0d644c3ee6d0d6813367d03831614c9ebfd1536b10", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:33.755653+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p228", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 228, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                    8 Sep 52\n\n           (Restricted) Movie Film of Flying Objects Taken\n               2 Jul 52, Vicinity of Tremonton, Utah\n\nChief, Air Technical        Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center         Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2\n                                                    Maj Fournet/fh/\nWright-Patterson AFB                                71016\n\n     1.  Subject film, received this office 5 Sep 52, is inclosed for appropriate\naction.  Duplicate of report submitted by the photographer, CPO Delbert C. Newhouse\n(177283, USN), is inclosed for your information in the event that the copy forwarded\nto you by the IG, Hill AFB, Utah has not been received.\n\n     2.  A message was dispatched to the CG, WADF on 6 Sep 52, with information copy\nto you, requesting that an intelligence officer interview CPO Newhouse and determine\nadditional details of the sighting, if available.\n\n     3.  A message was also dispatched to the CO, Hill AFB, Utah requesting weather\ninformation for the period and vicinity in question.  An information copy was\ndispatched to you.\n\n     4.  It has been ascertained from the Naval Observatory, Washington, D.C. that\nthe position of the sun at the time (1810Z hours, 2 July 52) and the location\n(4145N - 11210W) in question was 64.5° elevation and 131° azimuth.\n\n     5.  Suggest the film be submitted to the WADC Photo Lab for complete analysis\nas soon as possible.  The following are suggested questions for this analysis which,\nif answered, should facilitate evaluation of the incident:\n\n          a.  Are images made by light source or reflection?\n          b.  Any indication of what kind of objects could have caused images?  Is\nthere any bird sufficiently actinic to cause images?  Could they have been caused\nby aircraft or balloons?\n          c.  What causes impression that some objects at times appear to become 2 or\n3 where there was originally one, or, conversely, 2 or 3 objects at times appear to\nmerge into one.\n          d.  Do all objects have same characteristics?\n               (1) Same apparent shape?         x 320.7 ATIC\n               (2) Same color?\n               (3) Same relative size?          x 413.53 Film\n               (4) Same general motion?\n          e.  What are shape(s), color(s) and relative size(s) of objects?\n          f.  To what can the \"fade-in\" and \"fade-out\" of the objects be attributed?\n          g.  What type motion is attributable to the objects (about their own axis\nas well as about axis of flight path)?\n          h.  Is there any acceleration evident in their motion along flight path axis?\n          i.  Can the motion of the camera (panning and joggling) be allowed for\n\nCONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "fd7d323fce6efa2911e6b21d8dd2b09829b8e59bd14b20919c0860507c35b7d9", "output_sha256": "fd10f91e14f6a513d64dc59fb1d466517bbc40b04a2b8ebff1fdeb655e397b35", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:36.684115+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p229", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 229, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nsufficiently to permit determination of the angular velocity of objects\nwhich cross the field of view? (Reference particularly the single object\nwhich crosses field; photographer states that camera was held motionless\nwhile object crossed field of view.)\n\n          j. Determine patterns of flight from position plots for each\nframe, then:\n               (1) Is there any recurring pattern in the relative\n                   position of the objects?\n               (2) Do they maintain same relative positions in formation\n                   during any maneuvers, particularly violent maneuvers?\n               (3) Is relative position maintained coincidental with\n                   movement about their axes?\n               (4) If undulating motion is present among a number of\n                   objects which are maintaining a semblance of formation,\n                   do those objects undulate in phase? Ditto for tumbling\n                   motion?\n               (5) Is there any indication of abrupt changes in direction\n                   of flight path through fairly large angles (e.g. 90° or\n                   more during interval of 2 or 3 frames)?\n               (6) Do any objects appear to remain motionless at the same\n                   time that others move about?\n               (7) Can all objects be accounted for at all times or do\n                   some literally disappear while still well within field\n                   of view?\n\n     6. Although CPO Newhouse did not request that the film be returned\nto him, it is recommended that the final footage (of the mountain scenery) be\nreturned to him immediately and that he be asked if he is willing to accept\na duplicate of the initial footage in lieu of the original. If his reply\nis affirmative, suggest the duplicate be forwarded whenever available.\n\n     7. Request advice of the analytical results as soon as available.\n\n\n2 Incls: (w/orig only)               WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1. Cy of ltr fr CPO Newhouse,       Colonel, USAF\n        dtd 11 Aug 52                 Chief, Topical Division\n  2. Roll of exposed 16mm film.       Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                      Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n\nAFOIN-2A2     AFOIN-2\n\n[ILLEGIBLE signature]     ___________\n\n                         CONFIDENTIAL\n                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "08cbd12ffd3a0d28e415707e6127815eb2bed2b1ce7bef0cc295b1ab35456042", "output_sha256": "08cbd12ffd3a0d28e415707e6127815eb2bed2b1ce7bef0cc295b1ab35456042", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:38.983092+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p230", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 230, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                    6 Sept 52\n\n      (Restricted) Request for Lab Analysis of Samples Having Possible Relation to\nUnidentified Flying Objects.\n      Counter Intelligence Division\n      Directorate of Special Investigation, The IG\n\n      Topical Intelligence Division, Deputy Director for          1\n        Estimates, Directorate of Intelligence, DCS/O     AFOIN-2A 2/Maj Fournet/\n                                                           fh/ 71016\n\n      1.  It is requested that the samples submitted herewith as Exhibits A thru I be\nforwarded to the Federal Bureau of Investigation for lab analysis since they may have\na possible relation to unidentified flying objects.  These samples were removed from\nthe yard of Mr. Charles Walter Storm residing at 102 North Garfield Street, Arlington,\n[REDACTED]\n\n      2.  The circumstances surrounding the incident to which these samples pertain\nare outlined in Inclosures 1 and 2.\n\n      3.  Inclosure 3 gives significant data about each sample.  Exhibits G, H and I\nare submitted for comparison with A thru F because of the possibility that this\nincident represents a prank of some sort involving the use of one or more of these\nmaterials.\n\n\n3 Incls                              WILLIAM A. ADAMS\n  1.  Summary of circumstances       Colonel, USAF\n  2.  Sketch of Area relating to 1   Chief, Topical Intelligence Division\n  3.  List of Exhibits               Deputy Director for Estimates\n  4.  Exhibits A thru I (samples) c/orig   Directorate of Intelligence\n\n                    [ILLEGIBLE] 095 Storm, Charles Walter\n\n\n                              Hand Carried by Maj. Fournet\n                                      6 Sept. 52\n\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\nAFOIN-2A2              AFOIN-2A\n\n[signature]            [signature]\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n                  SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c221931e24eb47321b6e65c370ec982153fd3a0c797c4fee97aabeb4b5ab4991", "output_sha256": "c221931e24eb47321b6e65c370ec982153fd3a0c797c4fee97aabeb4b5ab4991", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:40.982942+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p231", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 231, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SUMMARY OF CIRCUMSTANCES: INVESTIGATION OF POSSIBLE\nUNIDENTIFIED FLYING OBJECT - ARLINGTON, VIRGINIA\n1-2 September 1952\n\n\n1. At 1600 hours on 3 Sep 52, the Directorate of Intelligence,\nHq., USAF received a telephone call from Mr. Walter Storm, 227 18th\nStreet, SE, Washington, D.C. (phone LI 31298) that an unusual circle\nwas found marked on the lawn of his father, Mr. Charles Walter Storm,\non the morning of 2 Sep 52 and that he believed it might bear some\nrelation to the USAF investigation of unidentified flying objects.\n\n2. Major Fournet, of the D/I, called on the elder Mr. Storm at\nhis residence (102 North Garfield Street, Arlington, Va., phone:\nCH 8508) during the evening of 3 Sep 52.\n\n3. The following was found on Mr. Storm's rear lawn (refer to\nsketch in Incl 2):\n\n     a. A circle 18 feet in diameter and nearly perfectly formed\nwas marked on the lawn by a deposit of some unknown gray substance\nwhich was adhering to the grass in clusters of fine globules.\n\n     b. The band of the circle (around the periphery) was an average\nof approximately 6 inches wide.\n\n     c. The deposits in the band were less pronounced and sometimes\nabsent for short distances where depressions or unevenness in the ground\nsurface occurred.\n\n     d. A small evergreen bush was located at a point about 40 inches\ninside the circle and did not appear to have been disturbed in any way nor\nwere any deposits present on or around it.\n\n     e. A clothes line frame located on a central pole overhung the\ncircle somewhat and had been in place (approximately as shown in Incl 2)\non the night in question.\n\n     f. An antenna wire about 40 feet above the ground overhung the\ncircle, exact amount undetermined.\n\n     g. No other vegetation in the area contained any deposits or\nmarks (small trees were present, as close as 6 or 8 feet from the circle).\n\n     h. Three types of fertilizer were stored in covered drums near\nthe garage about 15 feet away from the circle.\n\nRESTRICTED\n\nIncl 1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "303fca9e9d8bceecd02fcf89b0406a011ea0ad7b01db185c3bd810f5f5310763", "output_sha256": "4f7cebc8003530c1faa8e123bf70e296da4de70e0827891d2417938a968c9049", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:43.333043+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p232", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 232, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[REDACTED]\n                                         SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n     4.  Mr. and Mrs. Storm were interviewed and offered the following\ninformation:\n\n          a.  Mr. Storm cut the grass in the area in question around\n1800-1900 hours on 1 Sep 52.  The clippings were left where they fell.\n\n          b.  At 2300 hours on 1 Sep 52, Mr. Storm put his dog in the\nbasement for the night.  (Note:  the dog barks at anyone who comes into\nthe yard, and, until that time had not sounded off).\n\n          c.  (As related to Mr. Storm later by Mrs. Whitehurst, a neighbor\nimmediately in the rear of the Storm residence and adjacent to the lawn in\nquestion.)  Mrs. Whitehurst was awakened at about 0400 hours on 2 Sep 52\nby barking of dog \"which seemed to be in distress\".  She looked out of a\nwindow in the rear of her house but failed to see anything (it was a rather\ndark night).\n\n          d.  Upon going out to his car at 0730 hours 2 Sep 52, Mr. Storm\nnoticed the circle and walked over to examine it.  He describes it as\nhaving at that time a brown, oily-sandy appearance with what seemed to\nbe a very fine granular structure (as though a fine sand mixed with light\noil had been spread to form this ring).  He rubbed some of the substance\nbetween his fingers and found it faintly gritty and definitely oily.  Mrs.\nStorm corroborates this description.\n\n          e.  During mid-afternoon of 2 Sep 52 Mrs. Storm reexamined the ring\nand found that the color had changed to grayish-blue, and it no longer\nappeared to be oily.  However it still felt oily but no longer felt gritty.\nShe detected no odor upon smelling it.\n\n          f.  Upon returning from work at 1700 hours 2 Sep 52, Mr. Storm\nagain examined it with his wife.  He describes the color as purplish-gray;\nMrs. Storm describes the color as bluish-gray.  Both agree that the\nsubstance had begun to form small, closely-packed globules on the blades\nof grass and that it had begun to \"crystallize\".  Mr. Storm states that it\nthen felt slick (like graphite) when rubbed between the fingers; Mrs. Storm\ndescribes it as a powdery feel.\n\n               (NOTE:  There had been no rain since before the evening of\n               1 Sep 52, and there was a hot sun all day on 2 Sep 52.\n               However, there was a heavy rainfall during the night of\n               2/3 Sep 52).\n\n          g.  During the morning of 3 Sep 52, Mr. Storm reexamined it and\n\"was surprised to find it there after so much rain\".  He describes its\nappearance as darker (a slate gray) and still formed in globules on the\ngrass blades.  It still felt about like graphite, perhaps a bit \"thinner\"\nthan the preceding evening.  (Mrs. Storm removed Sample E that morning).\n\n                              2\n                         [REDACTED]\n                      SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b40e21c84a742388cc9dabae0de828e41bb10a3c553b6977c697f3f78d85c739", "output_sha256": "e7aa0d3cf5e9e9d163ec7643788dc28cff05820590d6c6676a5eccbe91ac376e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:46.381618+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p233", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 233, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n     5.  Mr. and Mrs. Whitehurst were not at home and, therefore, were\nnot interviewed.\n\n     6.  Samples of grass, leaves and soil, and of three types of fertilizer\nstored nearby were removed for analysis (see Incls 3 and 4).\n\n     7.  Mr. and Mrs. Storm were very cooperative and appeared to be\ncompletely sincere.  They stated that they have not recently evinced much\ninterest in the subject of unidentified flying objects nor had they\ndiscussed the subject with anyone, thereby eliminating any obvious motive\nfor a practical joke.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED\n3\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b5c626510d6d0b760267d9323703ae1df7e69dbbc89626954c74913287df0114", "output_sha256": "8169df2db7590faa6c6c9e5ab05dcaf9ab7fc4543f78c5e2ca574d75f193392b", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:47.516760+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p234", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 234, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nSKETCH OF AREA: INVESTIGATION OF POSSIBLE UNIDENTIFIED\nFLYING OBJECT - ARLINGTON, VIRGINIA - 1-2 Sept. 1952\n\n\n                    W = 6\"\n\n←——56'——→\n  ←—50'—→\n\n\n\n\n\n                              10'\n\n\n                                        ①\n                                              40\"\n\n\n             B\n\nClothes lines on\nsquare frame &\ncentral pole.\n\n                        Antenna Wire about\n                        40' above ground\n\n\n①  Small evergreen bush 53\"\n   high & max diam 18\"          RESTRICTED\n\n\nIncl 2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "4de8e9ccc9b9c83e78a8effe8f715463fede795054c57df5f44a560fb879e373", "output_sha256": "377166e8512220b9006bf5f0bdeed9d53c46aa1895640954d225f54c3f3f8f6f", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:48.536091+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p235", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 235, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\n                                        ARMY INFORMATION\n\n         List of Exhibits:  Investigation of Possible Unidentified\n                            Flying Object - Arlington, Virginia 1/2 Sep 52\n\n\n   A -  Soil and grass sample from circle (at A on Incl 1)\n   B -  Soil and grass sample from circle diametrically opposite A (at B on Incl 1)\n   C -  Soil & grass samples from center of area within circle\n   D -  Samples of grass from various points around circle\n   E -  Samples of grass from various points around circle\n   F -  Leaves removed from circle near B.\n   G -  Sample of Vigoro fertilizer\n   H -  Sample of other commercial fertilizer\n   I -  Sample of limestone fertilizer (6 years old)\n\n   NOTE:  A,B,C,D and F were obtained at 1930 on 3 Sep 52.\n          E was obtained on the morning of 3 Sep 52.\n          G, H and I were stored in covered drums about 15' from\n          outer edge of circle.\n\n\n\n\n                              RESTRICTED\n                           ARMY INFORMATION\n\nIncl  3", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "3624038b27d48d1da6a36f92df8787cb5f08309cee9de30e49c1360879b6ecaf", "output_sha256": "bc754d5c525c03f0cf13a38f2cbbe5e94e973d2271c7a8acd67d95360d5da9bf", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:49.998777+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p236", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 236, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SECURITY INFORMATION\n\nRESTRICTED\n\nHEADQUARTERS STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND\nOFFUTT AIR FORCE BASE\nOMAHA, NEBRASKA\n\nDINC 350\n                                                    5 SEP 1952\nSUBJECT: (Unclassified) FLYOBRPT\n\n\nTO:       Director of Intelligence\n          Headquarters USAF\n          Washington 25, D.C.\n\n\n        The attached Air Intelligence Information Report is forwarded\nas per instructions AFL 200-5, dated 29 April 1952, subj, FLYOBRPT.\n\n          FOR THE COMMANDING GENERAL:\n\n\n                                        Hal E. Bilyeu\n\n                                    HAL E. BILYEU\n1 Incl                              MAJOR, USAF\nIR-123-52(3cys)                     Asst Adj Gen\n\n\n                        11 Sept 52\n                                    COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ___________\n\n          Incl w/bin O IN-182\n                    Maj. Pandolfo\n                        (PF)\n\n\n\n\nRESTRICTED", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "49e3cd396750c9894c9e07e283318973f0ac848242e803eaf279bcf9b8a82b04", "output_sha256": "f5b866de76fe6e570156128e2aef73cd3ae5a8024855e2b568c1e861a8776794", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:51.394443+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p237", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 237, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[Stamp - top right corner]: REC'D\n9 SEP 1952\nDIR/INTE\nHQ USAF\n\n[Remainder of page shows bleed-through text from reverse side, appearing mirrored/reversed and largely illegible]\n\n[REDACTED - black bar near bottom of page]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "9172bee596a6a59da66a660ce1cbdcecc85c0d4fcb1ae8c9bef902e583325e3d", "output_sha256": "9172bee596a6a59da66a660ce1cbdcecc85c0d4fcb1ae8c9bef902e583325e3d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:52.232866+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p238", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 238, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Conf) Des Verges, Dunham Sanborn, Request for Information about\nCounter Intelligence Division\nDirector of Special Investigations, The IG\n\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O                    Maj Fournet/bps/71016\n                                                       AFOIN-2A2\n                                                       W/5 Sept 52\n\n     1.  Subject was the principal in the alleged sighting of an unidentified\nflying object in the vicinity of West Palm Beach, Florida on the night of\n19 August 1952.  A field investigation of a technical nature has been conducted\nby the Air Technical Intelligence Center, but no conclusive results have yet\nbeen obtained.  However, there are indications of a possible hoax, viz. the results\nof the FBI lab analysis on Des Vergers' cap (ref your R&R to this office dtd\n30 Aug 52) and the actions of Des Vergers subsequent to the alleged sighting.\n\n     2.  A check of subject's Marine Corps personnel records has revealed that\nhe was given a bad conduct discharge 1 November 1944 following his conviction by\na civil court in Florida for violation of National Motor Vehicle Theft Act.  He\nwas sentenced to 2½ years in the Federal Reformatory at Chillicothe, Ohio\n(Reformatory No. 23542-C).  His Marine Corps medical records were negative as\nregards psychiatric indications or treatment.\n\n     3.  It has also been learned, from a source whose reliability cannot be\njudged, that subject may have been confined at one time to a mental institution\nin the state of New York.\n\n     4.  It is therefore requested that the following information be obtained:\n\n          a.  Any records of psycho-neurotic examination and/or treatment while\nconfined to the Federal Reformatory at Chillicothe, Ohio.\n\n          b.  Evidence that he was at one time confined to a mental institution in\nthe state of New York.\n\n\n                              S/ JOHN G. ERIKSEN\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Assistant Deputy Director for Estimates\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\n[REDACTED]\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                   1", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "cb3fe31db3b8727c3933508ce98059ceceefd764ac6cdcb1d1d3163b9eb792b5", "output_sha256": "901c4266ac89e9c5debb69ccb4aa43486cd95c75df13c5ea900b8f6d3b87954e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:54.424321+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p239", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 239, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "Wrtn 2 Sept 52\n\n\"Flying Saucers\"\n                                                    3 SEP 1952\nOffice of Public Information, OSD\nPress Branch, Air Force Desk\n                                                           2\nDeputy Director for Collection and Dissemination    AFOIN-1/Col Cook/sr/56548\nDirectorate of Intelligence\n\n   General Ackerman does not concur in the recommendation contained in paragraph 4,\nComment 1, and accordingly has disapproved it.\n\n\n\n\n                              EUGENE G. COOK\n                              Colonel, USAF\n                              Chief, Policy & Management Group\n                              Deputy Director for Collection\n                                and Dissemination\n                              Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n\n\nNo M/R required\n\nAFOIN-1\n\nCol Cook\n\n\n\nCmt 1 w/orig\n    + green.\n\n\n                              2", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "42b83d13ea599b5e4781f87ad4a33eba303b292e55837167bf8399dcbe80aeee", "output_sha256": "42b83d13ea599b5e4781f87ad4a33eba303b292e55837167bf8399dcbe80aeee", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:55.571059+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p240", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 240, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED (Wrtn AFOIN-1A1/Maj Harlow/71067/ht/26 Aug 52)\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                    Rewrtn 29 Aug 52\n\n\n\n\n            (Unclassified) Unidentified Flying Objects Reporting\n\nAssistant Chief of Staff,    Dept of the Air Force    2- SEP 1952\nG-2, Department of the Army  Hq, USAF                            Col Cook/56548\nWashington 25, D. C.         AFOIN\n\n     1.  Attached for your information and action considered appropriate is a copy of\nAir Force Letter Number 200-5, dated 29 April 1952 which expresses the Air Force in-\nterest in unidentified flying objects and provides for a reporting procedure.\n\n     2.  To assist the Air Force in collecting information on this subject, it would\nbe appreciated if such data as may come to the attention of Army personnel on unidentified flying objects could be reported to the Air Force rapidly and substantially as\noutlined in paragraph 8c and 8e of attached letter.\n\n     3.  Contents of attachment may be used in any manner you desire for the issuance\nof instructions on the reporting of unidentified flying objects.\n\n     4.  The instructions in this communication supersede those contained in AFOIN\nLetter dated 18 September 1950, subject, Reporting of Information on Unconventional\nAircraft, with one inclosure.\n\n     FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n1 Incl (w/orig)          X 321.9 Assistant    s/\nAFL 200-5                Chief of          GEORGE E. PERRY\n                         Staff - G-2       Colonel, USAF\n                                           Chief of Management\n                                           Policy & Management Group\n                                           Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n                                                    OUT\n                                                G 2 SEP 1952\n                                                DIR/INT\n                                               HQ USAF\n\n\nPREVIOUS COORDINATION VALID\n\n\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                       SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "0a08153540c339c74ecc57a43267ca0461935d0188b04aebcea5663b3e592775", "output_sha256": "a0fe5a2e3878adb58599df6f1c3f8b80c4b25e14bbbddabda5995cf2c9200e47", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:57.689174+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p241", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 241, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED          AFOIN-1A1/Maj Harlow/71067/ht\n     SECURITY INFORMATION          Wrtn 26 Aug 52\n\n\n\n\n                    (Unclassified) Unidentified Flying Objects Reporting\n\n\nAssistant Chief of Staff,    Dept of the Air Force\nG-2, Department of the Army  Hq, USAF, AFOIN                    Maj Harlow/71067\nWashington 25, D. C.\n\n     1.  Attached for your information and action considered appropriate, is a copy\nof Air Force Letter Number 200-5, dated 29 April 1952 which expresses the Air Force\ninterest in unidentified flying objects and provides for a reporting procedure.\n\n     2.  To assist the Air Force in collecting information on this subject, it would\nbe appreciated if such data as may come to the attention of Army personnel on unidentified flying objects could be reported to the Air Force rapidly and substantially as\noutlined in paragraph 8c and 8e of attached letter.\n\n     3.  Contents of attachment may be used in any manner you desire for the issuance\nof instructions on the reporting of unidentified flying objects.\n\n     4.  The previous communication from the Air Force on this subject is hereby\nrescinded: Letter AFOIN, Subject: \"Reporting of Information on Unconventional Aircraft,\"\ndated 18 September 1950, with one inclosure.\n\n     FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n\nIncl\n  FL 200-5\n\n\n\n\n                                                        [signature]\n\n\n\n\n                         RESTRICTED\n                      SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n[Routing slip with signatures]\nOFFICE SYMBOL | AFOIN-  | AFOIN-1X | AFOIN-1A | AFOIN-1A1 |          |\nSignature of   |         |          |          | Maj Harlow| Col Bell | Col Walton\nResponsible Off| [sig]   | [sig]    | [sig]    | [sig]     | [sig]    | [sig]\nInitial Ofcr   |         |          |          |           |          |\nCo-ordination  |         |          |          |           |          |", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "383930fc1f08d67bed6120003a5d86d44e52c06584abd4517ee36b1e4c7c7d1f", "output_sha256": "ea1b4e0d0defb1464645130fc65b980d75d669d415d14af2993566377b3582cf", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:12:59.972884+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p242", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 242, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nAFOIN-1A1/Maj Harlow/71067/ht\nWrtn 26 Aug 52\n\nM/R\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To advise the Army and Navy as to the current Air Force interest\nin unidentified flying objects and gain their cooperation in reporting\nsuch data as may become available to Army and Naval personnel.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  In the past, AFOIN has requested that the Army and Navy assist the\nAir Force in the collection of data pertaining to unidentified flying objects.\nOur desires were made known in a letter AFOIN, Subject: \"Reporting of Information on Unconventional Aircraft,\" 18 September 1950 which was signed by\nMajor General Cabell.\n\n     3.  When the latest AF Instructions on this subject were issued on 29\nApril 1952 (AFL 200-5) action to advise the Army and Navy of the existence\nof new instructions was deferred at the request of ATIC pending the development of an \"Observers Questionnaire.\"  This form was to be used as an aid\nin the extraction of information from observers.  General use of this form\nis not contemplated at this time.\n\n     4.  At the working level, the Navy has asked to be informed as to the\ncurrent Air Force desires in this matter soonest.  At levels lower than this\nheadquarters echelons of the Air Force have mis-stated our desires to\nechelons of the Navy.  Instructions on this subject with the Navy presently\nare conflicting and confused.\n\n     5.  Not for inclusion in the Daily Staff Digest.\n\nRECOMMENDATION:\n\n     6.  That D/F to the Army and Memo to the Navy be forwarded, asking\ntheir cooperation in the reporting of unidentified flying objects and\noutline a desirable reporting procedure in accordance with AFL 200-5.\n\nACTION:\n\n     7.  Recommended letters have been prepared.  Request they be signed\nand forwarded.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN- [signature]               AFOIN-1A1, Maj Harlow [signature]\n\n     AFOIN-1X [signature]             Col Bell [signature]\n\n     AFOIN-1A [signature]             Col Walton [signature]\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "058d427db27f022e16d18e99ed0e4897528bf9f359e23622d7e8cf2f43e769cd", "output_sha256": "30e03b93585efcf25fb47068b2b45b763445fc8a1ee49417507c083288ce64a1", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:02.292602+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p243", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 243, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED        AFOIN-1A1/Maj Harlow/71067/ht/26 Aug 52\n              Rewrtn AFOIN-1/Col Cook/sr/56548/29 Aug 52\n    SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                        2- SEP 1952\n\nAFOIN\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:  THE DIRECTOR OF NAVAL INTELLIGENCE\n\nSUBJECT:  (Unclassified) Unidentified Flying Objects Reporting\n\n\n     1.  Attached for your information and action considered appro-\npriate is a copy of Air Force Letter Number 200-5, dated 29 April\n1952 which expresses the Air Force interest in unidentified flying\nobjects and provides for a reporting procedure.\n\n     2.  To assist the Air Force in collecting information on this\nsubject, it would be appreciated if such data as may come to the\nattention of Naval personnel on unidentified flying objects could\nbe reported to the Air Force rapidly and substantially as outlined\nin paragraph 8c and 8e of attached letter.\n\n     3.  Contents of attachment may be used in any manner you desire\nfor the issuance of instructions on the reporting of unidentified\nflying objects.\n\n     4.  The instructions in this communication supersede those con-\ntained in AFOIN Letter dated 18 September 1950, subject, Reporting\nof Information on Unconventional Aircraft, with one inclosure.\n\n               FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                   s/\n1 Incl (w/only)                GEORGE E. PERRY\n    AFL 200-5                  Colonel, USAF\n                               Chief of Management\n                               Policy & Management Group\n                               Directorate of Intelligence\n\nPREVIOUS COORDINATION VALID\n\n\n\n\n                    RESTRICTED\n                    SECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "d75c7b737f76ead3cb57a87d6d48132960fe18b4a338dcfae76b505d451975f7", "output_sha256": "42afd270125cf353dbe225812c023cdc038f1db4ab16b252726865de8be763ad", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:04.209086+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p244", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 244, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED          AFOIN-1A1/Maj Harlow/71067/ht\n     SECURITY INFORMATION          Wrtn 26 Aug 52\n\n\n\n\nAFOIN\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR:   THE DIRECTOR OF NAVAL INTELLIGENCE\n\nSUBJECT:          (Unclassified)  Unidentified Flying Objects Reporting\n\n\n\n     1.  Attached for your information and action considered appropriate,\nis a copy of Air Force Letter Number 200-5, dated 29 April 1952 which\nexpresses the Air Force interest in unidentified flying objects and provides for a reporting procedure.\n\n     2.  To assist the Air Force in collecting information on this\nsubject, it would be appreciated if such data as may come to the attention\nof Naval personnel on unidentified flying objects could be reported to\nthe Air Force rapidly and substantially as outlined in paragraph 8c and\n8e of attached letter.\n\n     3.  Contents of attachment may be used in any manner you desire for\nthe issuance of instructions on the reporting of unidentified flying\nobjects.\n\n     4.  The previous communication from the Air Force on this subject\nis hereby rescinded: Letter AFOIN, Subject: \"Reporting of Information\non Unconventional Aircraft,\" dated 18 September 1950, with one inclosure.\n\n          FOR THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n\n                                        Burton\n\nIncl\n  AFL 200-5\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n             RESTRICTED\n          SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n[ROUTING TABLE]\n| [REDACTED] | AFOIN-4     | AFOIN-1X    | AFOIN-1A        | AFOIN-1A1   |           |            |\n| [REDACTED] | Col Terry   | Col Carr    | Col Fletcher    | Maj Harlow  | Col Bell  | Col Walton?|\n| [REDACTED] | —           | /           |                 | jmh         | LDB       | LDB        |", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "a9232f4238851d7c59dbba196af17ffe8dceb0e2d008d79b5b170761b0511ad0", "output_sha256": "a17f5c3765e2762ede3a9684005acaa3137a4cbb3f80d122e343b1449dea6008", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:06.299523+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p245", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 245, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\nCOVER SHEET\n\n                                                                    SUSPENSE\nORIGIN OF BASIC                              DATE         TYPE      DATE\n  •  •                                       26 Aug 52    M/R\nSUBJECT                                                             ASSIGNED BY\n  (Uncl) Unidentified Flying Objects Reporting\n                                                                    NUMBER\n\n                                    ROUTING\nInitial \"IN\" column to denote review prior to action. Initial \"OUT\" column to denote review of completed action. (X-for action:\nV- for coordination)\n\nIN    OFFICE        OUT    IN    OFFICE      OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT    IN    OFFICE    OUT\n      AFOIN                (3)   OIN-1               OIN-2               OIN-3\nX     OIN-X [ILLEGIBLE]    (2)   OIN-1X              OIN-2X              OIN-3X\n      OIN-X1               (1)   OIN-1A [ILLEGIBLE]\n      OIN-X2\n      OIN-1A1 [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n      CABLES\nM     FILE                                                          SR NAVAL OFF\n      DISPATCH 9/2/52 - [ILLEGIBLE]                                 SR ARMY OFF\n\nTO:                                                                 DATE\n      AFOIN-1 THRU AFOIN-1A and AFOIN-1X                           26 Aug 52\nFROM:                                                               COMMENT NUMBER\n      AFOIN-1A1                                                     1\nCOMMENTS (Use reverse, if necessary)                                Maj Harlow/71067/ht\n\n      For approval and dispatch, D/F to Department of the Army G-2, Memorandum for\nDirector of Naval Intelligence with accompanying M/R for coordination.\n\n                                        ROBERT U. ROSWURM\n                                        Major, USAF\n                                        Executive, Collection Control Branch\n                                        Collection Division\n                                        Directorate of Intelligence\n\n\n3750\n\n                                    RESTRICTED\n                                  SECURITY INFORMATION\n\n                                                                    X-339\n                                                                    8/29\n\nAFHQ  FORM      0-86    PREVIOUS EDITIONS OF THIS FORM ARE OBSOLETE.              D 6616  122\n      22 JUL 52", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "51362bcfcc2858c350dc1d702704ed3b493e7668b632e3b941a3c285eb985281", "output_sha256": "51362bcfcc2858c350dc1d702704ed3b493e7668b632e3b941a3c285eb985281", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:08.557036+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p246", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 246, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "(Unclassified) Material for Project Blue Book\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force          2 SEP 1952\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2A2          Maj Fournet/cmb/71016\nWright-Patterson AFB\n\n     1.  The inclosed letters are for your information, appropriate action and\nretention.\n\n     2.  Each of these letters has been reviewed by this office for possible\napplication to the project.  Replies have been prepared expressing USAF appreciation.\n\n     3.  It will be noted that the basic theme of ionization is present in varying\ndegrees in all these letters, and they are therefore somewhat similar to letters\nreceived from Prof. Weber and Mr. Hollywood and forwarded to you by separate DF.\n\n               BY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n\n                                        JAMES P. BECKETT\n7 Encls:(w/orig DF only)               S/ WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n  1. Ltr fr Mr A.G. Manke                Colonel, USAF\n  2. Ltr fr Mr G. Vondrasek              Chief, Policy and Management Group\n  3. Ltr fr Mr J.O. Luthy                Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n  4. Ltr fr Mr G.F. Kennedy              Directorate of Intelligence\n  5. Ltr fr Mr J. Scott\n  6. Ltr fr Mr W.E. DeLano\n  7. Ltr fr Mr H.H. Sloss\n\n\n               COUPON DESIGNATION MADE ___________\n\n\nNo M/R is necessary\n\n\nCOORDINATION          AFOIN 2A2                    AFOIN -2A          AFOIN-2\n\n\n              D.E. English                  [signatures]\n              Col. USAF\n\n\nx350.05 Projects", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "47611711dcdee12f4d2fa1ae426136d007bb55513fb88673281ab867605d457d", "output_sha256": "336aff9eab335748533e69dfe321676f87cc55af4b259d543e60a514bfe7586e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:10.541777+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p247", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 247, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "SECURITY INFORMATION\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n(Unclassified)  Correspondence Concerning \"Flying Saucers\"\n\nCounter Intelligence Div., Director of Special\n  Investigations, The Inspector General\n                                                    SEP - 2 1952    1\nDeputy Director for Estimates\nDirectorate of Intelligence, DCS/O              Maj Fournet/cj/71016\n                                                AFOIN-2A2\n\n     1.  Inclosure 1 is forwarded for possible investigative action.  Since\nMr. Springer gives no address, it is impossible to correspond with him and ask\nfor additional information.  Therefore, it is requested that steps be taken to\nhave Mr. Springer located and questioned in order to determine (a) the reliability\nof the information in Inclosure 1, (b) the credibility of his informer, one\nSamuel P. Jones, and (c) any additional information which may have a relation to\nthe intelligence investigation and analysis of \"flying saucers\".  If Mr. Springer's\nclaims in his last paragraph have any foundation whatsoever, it could have an\nimportant bearing on the project.\n\n     2.  Inclosure 2 is forwarded for your information and any action considered\nappropriate.  The clipping referred to was not received.\n\n\n2 Incls:\n  1.  Ltr fr H.D. Springer          S/WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n      dtd 31 July 52                Colonel, USAF\n  2.  Ltr fr Anonymous              Chief, Policy and Management Group\n      not dtd                       Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                                    Directorate of Intelligence\n\n        √ x095. Jones, Samuel P.\n        √ x095. Springer, H.D.\n        √ x 350.05 Projects\n\n                                         OUT\n                                      G  3  SEP 1952\n                                        DIR/INT\n                                        HQ USAF\n\nAFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2          AFOIN\n\nCol T.W. Wolfe    Col W.H. Smith      [ILLEGIBLE]      [ILLEGIBLE]\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5888c55edbbc13ae1b8d7d04a58c25575be339dee2e861f7e39c03dde92adc36", "output_sha256": "3de6ffe60db8843e6d10862103f690799bf01b4b30d005afd09151434db40f99", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:12.765454+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p248", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 248, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM\n\n     1.  To prepare R&R to OSI.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION\n\n     2.  In a personal letter to General Samford, Mr. H. D. Springer\nconveys information concerning the activities of one Samuel P. Jones\nwho has professed complete knowledge of the \"flying saucers\".  According\nto Mr. Springer, this Mr. Jones predicted the recent appearance of\nunidentified objects over Washington, D.C. and vicinity some time before\nit occurred.  It is desired to have Mr. Springer contacted to determine\ncertain information bearing on Project Blue Book.\n\n     3.  Another letter of anonymous origin intimates that there is some\nunusual activity on a movie set in California.  It is desired to refer\nthis letter to OSI for any action they consider warranted.\n\n     4.  The R&R will accomplish the referrals mentioned above.\n\n     5.  Subject matter will not be included in the Daily Staff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED\n\n     6.  Approval, signature and forwarding of attached R&R.\n\n\nCOORDINATION\n\n     Col I. W. Wolfe, AFOIN-2A2, Ext. 75990\n     Col W. A. Adams, AFOIN-2A, Ext. 71564\n     Col J. J. Morrow, AFOIN-2, Ext. 71110  [signature]\n\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "70d916106aa5ef1d3ceffb1cf35fd643566e67f4197916d702ac7b3fd0847db8", "output_sha256": "fecf7d3789a5af0b76af2ea08766afd63c815a29295791dcb3fd1010e6d7036c", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:14.438862+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p249", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 249, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "July 31, 1952\n\nMajor General John Sanford\nWar Department\nWashington, D.C.\n\nSir:\n\n     General Sanford everybody is talking about the flying saucers\nI don't know how I ever got enough nerve to write you but I think it\nis my turn now to put in my nickels worth.\n\n     As one serviceman to another I think I can talk frank with you.\nI think I know the man who is responsible for the flying saucers, it\nis a long story but I will try to make it as brief as possible.\n\n     In 1929 at an inventor's meeting in Long Beach in the Rainbow Pier\nI met a man who called himself, at that time, Samuel P. Jones he had a\nmotor that everyone thought was a fake. He would explain it to you but\nno one would believe him but me. So as a dumb cluck I tried to give\nthe man a helping hand, he said that this motor could be made in any\nsize or horsepower, could be put in ships, locomotives, cars and\nairplanes. At that time I knew a doctor in Long Beach who had a\nclinic and a yacht, I took this Jones to this doctor thinking that this\ndoctor might finance him for a motor for his yacht. After the doctor talked\nto the man awhile, the doctor didn't believe him, though he was nuts, so\nthen I forgot all about this man Jones until World War II. I met this\nsame man in the South Pacific and he was a Skipper in the Army Transport\nService. Then after seeing him again and knowing the position he held\nI took it for granted that he must be pretty smart, not nuts. I became\nvery friendly with this man we chummed together for a couple of years\nin the South Pacific and every once in awhile he would talk about his\ninvention. I asked him if this invention was so good why is it that the\nGovernment wouldn't take it. This is what he told me, that he had tried\nto get the Government to take it and they laughed at him and he finally\ngot an interview with President Roosevelt and the President told him that\nat that time he also had an idea before Congress that if it didn't work\nout they would all go to the insane asylum. He also told him that his\nidea was a thousand years ahead of time.\n\n     Later in 1947 I got a letter from this Jones asking me to come to him,\nwhich I did, in Havre, Montana he had a plane that I would call built with\nthis motor, this was the most damnable looking plane I have ever seen. It\nwas made like a saucer, about 17 feet in diameter and it would fly through\nthe air with a control made from the base of a telephone. This I saw with\nmy own eyes. He said that it would fly so fast through the air that the\nair would melt, and I asked him \"how fast will it go\", he said actually he\ndidn't know but would figure it made a speed of 3 to 4000 miles per hour.\n\n2nd#", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "2baed6166099c074a8b50dae6914e2e05d32ab1c1a488761dda69419ed5f1bf4", "output_sha256": "aba5a86470b2feff7f68fec0b373aabb75a00a56b2e0aeebfb16585cc6f059ed", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:17.248040+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p250", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 250, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "C O P Y\n\nMajor General John Sanford                    July 31, 1952\n                                               Page 2\n\n\n        Again, I asked him why he didn't do something about it and he said\nit was impossible.  I also asked him why he didn't patent this machine and\nhe gave me many reasons, that each and every part about the machine had already\nbeen invented and it would take a millionaire to procure the patent rights\nto this invention.  I also asked him wasn't he afraid that someone would\nsteal it from him and he told me that the public was funny that they couldn't\nsee no further than the nose on their face and that if you had a secret that\nyou wanted to keep to tell everybody and nobody would believe you.\n\n        About three months later I received a letter from this man telling me\nthat he was ready to make a test, a few days later was the first time I\nheard about the flying saucers.  Since that time I have received many letters\nfrom this man Jones.  About three weeks ago I received a letter from him again\ntelling me that over Baltimore, Washington, Alexandria Virginia, etc., that\nhe was going to let the whole world know that his invention was possible.\nThen I went to the American Broadcasting Company, a couple of newspapers\nand tried to tell them this story.  They wouldn't even listen to me and it\nhas happened again.  If this man Jones is not the inventor of the flying\nsaucer how is it that he knows two or three weeks ahead of time when they are\ngoing to fly?  I think that if you will find this man Jones, I know you will\nget this fantastic story straightened out.  His address I do not know but he\nwrites me to my box in Detroit, Michigan and I receive a letter maybe two\nor three weeks later.  When I saw the plane or whatever you want to call it,\nin the air, it would go so fast you would hardly see it.  It was round like\na saucer, had a tail like a plane, and when it would sway (as I would say)\nin the air sometimes it would look like a pencil, sometimes like an egg, and\nagain it would look like a balloon so you take it from here.  Use your own\njudgment, you have my permission to do anything you want with this letter.\nMy name is H. D. Springer, I have no permanent address but I live in Detroit,\nI am going back east tonight at 9 o'clock P.M.\n\n                                        Sincerely yours,\n\n\n\n                                        H. D. SPRINGER", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "5babbc141b8952db53df96c9ff67fcd1eda8d093c2bcb89cf3cdb17a8fd08d67", "output_sha256": "59d22b060099e688f0fbcdc0e176002e4680b7a8e22edb96067a8a05f267df34", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:19.644099+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p251", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 251, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "COPY\n\nMAJOR GENERAL JOHN A SAMFORD\n\nINTELLIGENCE DIRECTOR\n\nUS AIRFORCE\n\nWASHINGTON D C\n\nDEAR SIRS:\n\n     I AM ENCLOSING A NEWSPAPER CLIPPING APROPOS TO\n\nMY LETTER.\n\n     YOUR SO CALLED FLYING SAUCERS HAVE BEEN SIGHTED IN NUMBERS\n\nCLOSE TO PEBBLE BEACH CAL. GOLF COURSE.  THIS INFORMATION I RECEIVED FROM A\n\nSTAR MEMBER OF PAT AND MIKE MOVIE CAST ON WHICH GOLF COURSE THE MOVIE\n\nIS IN PRODUCTION.\n\n     MY INFORMANT WAS ALARMED ABOUT THIS PHENOMENA AS ON CLOSER LOOK\n\nTHEY RESEMBLE MIDGET ATOM BOMBS WITH THEIR FAMILIAR UMBRELLA FORMATION.  I ALSO LEARNED THIS BIT OF INFORMATION.  ONE OF THE WARNER BROS.\n\nSOLD STOCK TO SOMEONE LATER IDENTIFIED AS A CONVICT.  HE SAID QUOTE\n\n\"I DIDN'T KNOW WHO I WAS SELLING TO.\"  THIS MR WARNER WAS ALSO THERE.\n\nI WAS ALSO TOLD THERE ARE THIRTY ESCAPED CONVICTS OCCUPYING\n\nHOUSES SURROUNDING THIS GOLF COURSE.  A MACHINE GUN IS MOUNTED TO STRATEGICALLY GUARD GATE.\n\n     OBVIOUSLY ONE OF YOUR ATOM BOMB CRIMINALS IS ON THE LOOSE.\n\n     THESE PEOPLE FEAR THEY WILL NOT BE ABLE TO LEAVE THIS MOVIE\n\nLOCATION AND ARE ALL SECRETLY WORRIED.\n\n     I WAS GIVEN THE IMPRESSION THAT AT LEAST ONE OF THESE CONVICTS\n\nIS CRIMINALLY INSANE.  YOU MAY NOT KNOW THAT IT TAKES SOMETIMES AS\n\nLONG AS FOUR YEARS TO COMPLETE A PICTURE IN ORDER TO GET ENOUGH TO DISTRIBUTE ALL OVER THE WORLD.\n\n     I WAS TOLD TO NOTIFY THE POLICE.  I THINK IT WILL TAKE SOMETHING BIGGER\n\nTHAN POLICE ACTION TO SOLVE THIS.\n\nIncl #2\n                                        I MUST SIGN MYSELF AN NY  US", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "b918e83a2f9c486c1ae4cdb8105ee6298ec41fa3d2cb9a6b1cd869a3451d0763", "output_sha256": "e6fa7198c5227e3cd005c3c69f4665ee3dc6e17791344c7d1ccc4af43cff6d8e", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:22.151870+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p252", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 252, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\n1. Sept 52\n\n(Restricted) Unidentified object which fell in\nwater off Okinawa, Nov 50\n\nChief, Air Technical          Dept of the Air Force\nIntelligence Center           Hq USAF - AFOIN-2a2                   Maj Fournet/fh/\nWright-Patterson AFB                                                  71016\nOhio\n\n1.  Reference recent report of interview with T/Sgt Emery Guzi of WADC re-\ngarding above subject, an attempt has been made to determine the feasibility of\nrequesting an investigation by the military authorities on Okinawa.  A hydro-\ngraphic chart of the area (Incl. 1) was obtained in order to study the soundings.\nHowever, a question arose over the exact location.  On the aeronautical chart\n(Incl. 2), Sgt Guzi indicated the location at the northernmost point of the island\n(Hedo-misaki or Hedo Saki), but on checking his sketch against Inclosure 1, it\nappears more probable that the location was actually Oku since there is a lagoon\nthere about 1 mile wide and a native village at the southern edge of the lagoon,\nwhich seems to check with his sketch.\n\n2.  Request Sgt Guzi be reinterrogated, using Inclosure 1, to determine the\nmost probable location in question.  In addition an attempt should be made to pin-\npoint the exact location at which object entered water.\n\n3.  If it transpires that the lagoon at Oku is the proper location, it will\nprobably be feasible to investigate since the water is very shallow.  Should it\nbe at Hedo Saki, however, the depth of the water will probably prohibit an inves-\ntigation.\n\n4.  Request return of Inclosures 1 and 2 with reply.\n\nBY COMMAND OF THE CHIEF OF STAFF:\n\n                              [signature] Malone Capt USAF\n                    for  WILLIAM W. WILCOX\n2 Incls: (w/orig only)        Colonel, USAF\n   1. Hydro cht Okinawa        Chief, Policy and Management Group\n   2. Aero cht Okinawa         Office, Deputy Director for Estimates\n                               Directorate of Intelligence\n\nCy 2 Incls\nmust be returned\n     DSB\n\nRESTRICTED\nSECURITY INFORMATION\n\nM/R is attached\nCOORDINATION:     AFOIN-2A2          AFOIN-2A          AFOIN-2\n\n                  [signature]        [signature]       [signature]\n                                     Malone Capt", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "f587301da8975972d32421c8e33b9822ca07809be09cc46ccbaa0e9626691833", "output_sha256": "5a3ebd3562d9f71ba2a2025c5b26e5c1c269ceebd101cab348ec7392ab546be6", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:25.254118+00:00"}, {"id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f-p253", "card_id": "fec5b139eb7b0a4f", "page": 253, "title": "DOW-UAP-D105, U.S. Air Force Flying Discs File, 1952", "text": "RESTRICTED\nSECU\n\nAFOIN-2A2\nMaj Fournet/dmb/71016\nWrtn 25 Aug 52\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD\n\nPROBLEM:\n\n     1.  To prepare DF to ATIC.\n\nFACTS AND DISCUSSION:\n\n     2.  T/Sgt Emery Guzi, assigned to WADC at W-P AFB, recently appeared\nin person before Project Blue Book personnel at ATIC and volunteered in-\nformation concerning the sighting of an u/i flyob on Okinawa in Nov 50.\nHe stated that the object had fallen into the sea.\n\n     3.  Sgt Guzi pointed out the approximate location on a map and drew\na large scale sketch of the area.\n\n     4.  This information was forwarded to AFOIN-2A2 for the purpose of\ndetermining the feasibility of an attempt to recover or otherwise locate\nand examine the object.\n\n     5.  A hydrographic chart of the area was obtained to determine the\nsoundings and thereby judge the feasibility of an investigation.  However,\nit was found that the data reported by Sgt Guzi did not tally with the\nhydrographic chart.  ATIC is therefore being requested to reinterrogate\nSgt Guzi in order to resolve these differences.  The attached DF will\naccomplish this.\n\n     6.  Subject matter will not be suitable for inclusion in the Daily\nStaff Digest.\n\nACTION RECOMMENDED:\n\n     7.  Approval, signature and dispatch of attached DF.\n\nCOORDINATION:\n\n     AFOIN-2A2, Col Wolfe, 75990\n     AFOIN-2A, Col Adams, 71564\n     AFOIN-2, Col Morrow, 71110\n\n\nRESTRICTED\n/ RESTRICTED\nSECURITY IN[ILLEGIBLE]", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "238ddd77a5c74ea15a7da3d352f24c846e52208715f8ddaac81a097c8b483c30", "output_sha256": "10725708505fb8c11df709b480c75881e9b9e021c51376e1f04ecc8ae33fb13d", "generated_at": "2026-09-19T18:13:27.286286+00:00"}, {"id": "ff30c985595153f3-p1", "card_id": "ff30c985595153f3", "page": 1, "title": "State Department UAP Cable 003, Tbilisi, Georgia, October 30, 2001", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\n                              UNCLASSIFIED\n\n\n\n\n                              CONFIDENTIAL\n\n\n\n\nMRN:                01 MOSCOW 13169\nDate/DTG:           Oct 30, 2001 / 300000Z Oct 01\nFrom:               AMEMBASSY MOSCOW\nAction:             WASHDC, SECSTATE ROUTINE\nE.O.:               Unknown\nTAGS:               PREL, MARR, KCFE, UN, OSCE, GG, RS\nReference:          (A) MOSCOW 13072 (B) TBILISI 3087\nSubject:            UFOS OVER GEORGIA: STRANGE ENCOUNTERS OF AN MFA KIND\n\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL  PTQ6889\n\nPAGE 01   MOSCOW 13169 01 OF 02 301754Z\nACTION IO-00\n\nINFO LOG-00  NP-00  AID-00  ACQ-00  CIAE-00  DOEE-00  DOTE-00\n  SRPP-00  DS-00  EB-00  EUR-00  OIGO-00  FAAE-00  FBIE-00\n  VC-00  H-01  TEDE-00  INR-00  LAB-01  L-00  VCE-00\n  MOFM-05  MOF-03  M-00  AC-01  DCP-01  NRRC-00  NSAE-00\n  NSCE-00  OIC-02  OMB-01  PA-00  PC-01  PM-00  PRS-00\n  ACE-00  P-00  SCT-00  SP-00  SS-00  TRSE-00  T-00\n  USIE-00  SA-00  BBG-00  SNIS-00  NISC-00  SSD-00  PMB-00\n  DSCC-00  PRM-00  DRL-02  G-00  NFAT-00  SAS-00  SWCI-00\n  /018W\n          -------------------3782F8 301754Z /38\nP 301741Z OCT 01\nFM AMEMBASSY MOSCOW\nTO SECSTATE WASHDC PRIORITY 1142\nINFO AMEMBASSY TBILISI PRIORITY\nUSMISSION USUN NEW YORK PRIORITY\nMOSCOW POLITICAL COLLECTIVE\nAMEMBASSY BAKU\nAMEMBASSY YEREVAN\nUSMISSION USOSCE\nSECDEF WASHDC\nJOINT STAFF WASHDC\n\nCONFIDENTIAL SECTION 01 OF 02 MOSCOW 13169\n\nE.O. 12958: DECL: 10/29/21\nTAGS: PREL, MARR, KCFE, UN, OSCE, GG, RS\nSUBJECT: UFOS OVER GEORGIA: STRANGE ENCOUNTERS OF AN MFA KIND\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n\nPAGE 02   MOSCOW 13169 01 OF 02 301754Z\n\nDeclassified in Full / Release in Full\nJohn Powers, Acting-Director\nUS Department of State\n2/25/2026\n\n\nCONFIDENTIAL                                        UNCLASSIFIED                                    Page 1 of 5", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "6a9f990ff38d9eb228576f6b6736e5f35157f7c7f1b40ca428b74cc35cf489ae", "output_sha256": "01895f05f2af09a5e680f1445e858df5f771d658ecd314196858409d8adc9cf9", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T15:34:24.589431+00:00"}, {"id": "ff30c985595153f3-p2", "card_id": "ff30c985595153f3", "page": 2, "title": "State Department UAP Cable 003, Tbilisi, Georgia, October 30, 2001", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL                    UNCLASSIFIED\n\n\n\n\n\nKIND\n\nCLASSIFIED BY POLMINCOUNS GEORGE KROL.  REASON 1.5 (B/D).\n\nREF:  (A) MOSCOW 13072  (B) TBILISI 3087\n\n1.  (∅) SUMMARY:  DEPUTY FOREIGN MINISTER MAMEDOV TOLD\nAMBASSADOR VERSHBOW OCTOBER 30 THAT ACCORDING TO THE\nRUSSIAN MINISTRY OF DEFENSE, NO RUSSIAN PLANES FLEW OVER OR\nBOMBED POSITIONS IN THE KODORI GORGE OCTOBER 28-29, DESPITE\nGEORGIAN ACCUSATIONS TO THE CONTRARY.  MFA GEORGIA DESK\nCHIEF TEREOKEN ECHOED MAMEDOV'S STATEMENT.  TEREOKEN\nFURTHER CONFIRMED THAT ONE RAILWAY CAR FULL OF RUSSIAN\nMILITARY EQUIPMENT LEFT GUDAUTA BASE AND ENTERED RUSSIA\nOCTOBER 29 (REF A) AND THAT TWO OTHER RAILWAY CARS ARE\nLOADED AND AWAITING ABKHAZ PERMISSION TO LEAVE FOR RUSSIA.\nTHERE ARE NO PLANS TO WITHDRAW PERSONNEL UNTIL TBILISI\nAGREES THAT APPROXIMATELY 340 RUSSIAN \"GUARDS\" CAN REMAIN\nAT GUDAUTA.  TEREOKEN SAID THAT ABKHAZ AUTHORITIES WOULD\nNOT ALLOW ANY OUTSIDE OBSERVERS TO WITNESS THE WITHDRAWAL.\nTEREOKEN TERMED GEORGIAN PARLIAMENTARY SPEAKER ZVANIA'S\nOCTOBER 25-28 VISIT TO MOSCOW POSITIVE IN TONE BUT EMPTY OF\nRESULTS.  ACCORDING TO THE GEORGIAN EMBASSY, ZVANIA AND\nRUSSIAN DUMA SPEAKER SELEZNEV AGREED THAT BOTH SIDES SHOULD\nAVOID RECRIMINATIONS.  TEREOKEN DENIED MEDIA REPORTS THAT\nDEFENSE MINISTER SERGEY IVANOV WAS PLANNING TO VISIT\nTBILISI SOON BUT DID NOT RULE OUT A VISIT COMPLETELY.  END\nSUMMARY\n\n2.  (∅) ON OCTOBER 30, DURING A PREVIOUSLY SCHEDULED\nMEETING, AMBASSADOR VERSHBOW RAISED REFTEL B REPORTS\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n\nPAGE 03   MOSCOW  13169  01 OF 02  301754Z\nALLEGING RUSSIAN PLANES HAD VIOLATED GEORGIAN AIRSPACE AND\nBOMBED AREAS OF THE KODORI GORGE.  THE AMBASSADOR STRESSED\nTHAT SUCH INCIDENTS, IF TRUE, AND IF CONTINUED, COULD BE\nDISASTROUS FOR U.S.-RUSSIAN RELATIONS AND SPOIL THE\nUPCOMING SUMMIT MEETING OF OUR PRESIDENTS IN THE U.S.\nMAMEDOV AGREED THAT SUCH INCIDENTS WOULD HAVE A NEGATIVE\nEFFECT ON THE SUMMIT, BUT QUOTED THE RUSSIAN MINISTRY OF\nDEFENSE AS CATEGORICALLY DENYING THAT RUSSIAN PLANES WERE\nINVOLVED IN ANY INCIDENTS IN GEORGIAN AIRSPACE.\n\n3.  (∅) MFA GEORGIA DESK CHIEF TEREOKEN, ECHOING MAMEDOV'S\nCLAIMS, DENIED TO US OCTOBER 30 REPORTS OF RUSSIAN PLANES\nBOMBING KODORI GORGE IN ABKHAZIA.  HE ALSO DENIED THAT\nTHERE WERE ANY RUSSIAN VIOLATIONS OF GEORGIAN AIRSPACE,\nSAYING THAT THERE HAD BEEN NO RUSSIAN PLANES FLYING NEAR\nTHE AREA ON EITHER OCTOBER 28 OR 29.  ACCORDING TO\nTEREOKEN, THERE WERE CREDIBLE REPORTS OF ABKHAZ HELICOPTERS\nBOMBING THE AREAS \"WHERE THE TERRORISTS WERE\" BUT THAT\nREPORTS OF PLANES IN THE AREA MIGHT AS WELL HAVE BEEN ABOUT\n\"UFOS.\"  MOSCOW, HE EXPLAINED, DOES NOT HAVE THE TECHNICAL\nCAPABILITY TO DETERMINE WHETHER THERE WERE FOREIGN PLANES\nIN THE REGION.  UNDERSCORING THAT HE \"WAS NOT ACCUSING\n\nCONFIDENTIAL                    UNCLASSIFIED                              Page 2 of 5", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "prompt_sha256": "a59e30285339eb18324e5a8552f80926750818af40043cd98315ffdb8087398f", "input_sha256": "c1a2b66ddb65cf90d9d6be8fa7db4342be4cc895d86ff7317140e91cc1791171", "output_sha256": "6c1485d092633df8aabeb5716cecb217a5d3c68ab7051c212b1ac032248b1202", "generated_at": "2026-05-25T15:34:28.852303+00:00"}, {"id": "ff30c985595153f3-p3", "card_id": "ff30c985595153f3", "page": 3, "title": "State Department UAP Cable 003, Tbilisi, Georgia, October 30, 2001", "text": "CONFIDENTIAL                    UNCLASSIFIED\n\n\n\n\nANYONE,\" TEREOKEN ADDED THAT IT WAS POSSIBLE THAT \"ANY\nSIDE\" HAD SENT PLANES OVER KODORI.\n\n4. (U) ASKED ABOUT PLANS TO WITHDRAW FROM GUDAUTA (REF\nA), TEREOKEN CONFIRMED THAT ONE TRAINLOAD OF MILITARY\nEQUIPMENT HAD DEPARTED THE BASE AND HAD ENTERED RUSSIA THE\nMORNING OF OCTOBER 29.  TWO MORE TRAINS HAVE BEEN LOADED\nAND ARE AWAITING PERMISSION FROM ABKHAZ AUTHORITIES TO MOVE\nTO RUSSIA.  MEMBERS OF THE RUSSIAN GENERAL STAFF ARE IN\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n\nPAGE 04      MOSCOW 13169  01 OF 02  301754Z\nSUKHUMI TO COORDINATE THESE MOVES.\n\n5. (U) WE ASKED WHY OUTSIDE OBSERVERS HAD NOT BEEN INVITED\nTO INSPECT THE WITHDRAWALS.  TEREOKEN CLAIMED THAT THE\nABKHAZ AUTHORITIES LIKELY WOULD NOT TOLERATE THE PRESENCE\nOF OUTSIDERS GIVEN THE TENSE SITUATION WITH TBILISI.  THE\nRUSSIANS, HE ADDED, HAD NO TIME TO INVITE OUTSIDE OBSERVERS\nBECAUSE \"WE DIDN'T KNOW UNTIL THE LAST MINUTE\" THAT THE\nWITHDRAWAL OF ONE TRAINLOAD OF EQUIPMENT WOULD PROCEED.  WE\nARGUED THAT MOSCOW NOW HAS TIME IF IT HAS ALREADY LOADED\nTWO OTHER TRAINS BUT IS WAITING FOR ABKHAZ PERMISSION TO\nWITHDRAW.  THE LACK OF TRANSPARENCY MIGHT RAISE QUESTIONS\nABOUT THE GOR'S INTENTIONS, WE NOTED.  WE ASKED ABOUT PLANS\nTO WITHDRAW TROOPS.  TEREOKEN SAID THAT APPROXIMATELY 600\nRUSSIAN PERSONNEL REMAIN AT GUDAUTA.  MOSCOW CONTINUES TO\nINSIST ON KEEPING ABOUT 340 THERE AS \"GUARDS.\"  TBILISI, HE\nNOTED, CONTINUES TO WANT A MUCH LOWER FIGURE.\n\n6. (U) WE ASKED TEREOKEN ABOUT GEORGIAN PARLIAMENTARY\nSPEAKER ZURAB ZVANIA'S VISIT TO MOSCOW LAST WEEK.  HE\nCONFIRMED THAT THE TONE OF ZVANIA'S VISIT WAS POSITIVE.  HE\nNOTED, HOWEVER, THAT THE VISIT \"HAD NO PRACTICAL OUTCOME.\"\nTHE GEORGIAN EMBASSY TOLD US OCTOBER 26 THAT GEORGIAN\nZVANIA'S VISIT WAS GOING WELL (NOTE:  ZVANIA DEPARTED\nMOSCOW OCTOBER 28).  ACCORDING TO GEORGIAN POLCOUNS\nCHKHEIDZE, ZVANIA AND RUSSIAN DUMA SPEAKER GENNADIY\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL\n\n                    CONFIDENTIAL  PTQ6891\n\nPAGE 01      MOSCOW 13169  02 OF 02  301754Z\nACTION IO-00\n\nINFO LOG-00  NP-00   AID-00  ACQ-00  CIAE-00  